27:47-07:00","id":495707,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> These are the other characters needed to post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:27:12-07:00","id":497132,"title":"","content":"Is it strictly a mechanical reason for this disinclination? Would you think them too weak, too strong, or too much of a headache?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:38:00-07:00","id":497664,"title":"","content":"They are not really balanced for player characters, and not really the sort of thing one buys the way one buys disciplines or contracts anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:58:45-07:00","id":499275,"title":"","content":"Session two. Preparation and meeting the passengers.<br /> <br /> <i>Session II</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 1 May 1920<br /> <br /> Today was a productive and informative day. I learned that Wolfram had no experience with bladed weapons of any kind. Dacian has some, but not a lot. He endeavored to teach our German companion how to use a sword. I resisted adding my own comments to their efforts at training. Dacian was having Wolfram do some simple exercises first before doing anything actually combat related with the blades. You have to get used to the weight first before you try to use it. I am not schooled in a formal fighting style. I know how to use a bayonet to good effect. It is not pretty but it works. Before I was transferred to working as a sniper I had several opportunities to use my bayonet.<br /> <br /> We also learned today that Alla can fight, and rather well at that. I was not expecting a Russian noblewoman to be proficient in combat, but I am not one to judge. The surprise was a welcome one. Tatiana of course can fight, and the two of us sparred, changing forms as we went. I will admit that I missed that kind of fighting. My prey lately have been men or troublesome minor spirits. Fighting with Tatiana was a chance to go all out. I rather enjoyed myself. After a little while Alla asked if she could join us. Tatiana and I looked at each other, skeptical, but then Alla informed us that she has her own powers for combat and assured us that she would be fine. We took her at her word and included her in the fight. She was right. She could keep up, and did. I have to wonder if all Kindred are as martially proficient as she is, or if she is the exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> Dervala was also a bit of a surprise. She is familiar with using knives. She is pretty good with them, and joined Wolfram and Dacian in their practice. I think she said something about having older brothers, which explains some things. If they are protective and practical they would have taught her to use weapons suited to her physical capabilities. The knives suited her. I wish I could have seen more of their practice, but I was busy with my own and I wouldn\u2019t have traded it.<br /> <br /> While some of us were sparring Lizette was apparently working on a duplicate Golden Eagle to act as a decoy when or if we found the original. I thought it looked rather impressive. She also had worked on a bomb that could be hidden and brought onto the train. Some people objected to this but I saw the practicality of it. If things should go horribly wrong, then it would be a good idea to have something like that with us. She assured us that it was something to be used only in an emergency. I was ready to move on after that, but some people still argued. Eventually arguments wound down and Lizette produced a fairly large stuffed bear to hide the explosives in. I thought it was clever. I\u2019m sure with her height Lizette could pretend to be a young girl, and no one is going to take a toy away from a young girl.<br /> <br /> Lizette also demonstrated for us her skill with a chainsaw. I was a little surprised at first by the unconventional weapon, but it seemed to fit the petite builder well. It certainly looked like it could cut down a tree with ease, which meant that it would be more than effective against physical beings. She went on a bit about wanting to be able to set it ablaze so it would be even more terrifying. I brought up the concern that the fuel the machine ran on might ignite if she were to light it on fire, but she did not seem to share my worry. I will trust her in this for now. She certainly seems to know what she is doing around machines.<br /> <br /> Later, after the practice and chainsaw demonstrations I sought out Wolfram to talk to him about his spirit companion. I was curious exactly how he came to be Ridden by a spirit in the first place. Turns out it was something of a bargain. Wolfram lay dying and his Geist offered to bring him back to health if he would play host to the spirit. There is apparently a gain for the host. They acquire some supernatural abilities and are rather hard to actually kill. Wolfram said that one of his abilities was to be able to hide objects within himself. I\u2019m not sure how that works exactly. It cannot be literal. It must be some function of the spirit that hides the item.<br /> <br /> Wolfram assured me that the Geist does not control him in anyway. He said that it was a mutual arrangement. The spirit gets to live vicariously through their host, and the host gains effective immortality and powers. I have seen bargains struck with spirits before and this deal with the Geist seems a little unbalanced. The host seems to gain more than the Geist does. I wonder if there is something that Wolfram is not saying or if there is something that he doesn\u2019t know. I will keep an eye on him to make sure that he is not being unduly affected by the Geist or controlled in any way. I like Wolfram, but if he becomes a threat to the group I will put him down.<br /> <br /> ********<br /> <br /> 3 May 1920<br /> <br /> We are on the train now. We have paired up and picked our cabins. I am rooming with Wolfram. We smuggled Alla onto the train by putting her in a trunk and then Tatiana carried it on board. I\u2019m not sure how Alla managed to fit herself into the trunk, but she did. It seemed the easiest way to get her onto the train and still avoid the sunlight. This will be something to keep in mind for future ventures. She is limited to operating at night which means that we will have to plan around that. I am fine with working at night. A good number of my jobs are carried out in the dark. It better hides me and my activities. There will however likely be some things that must take place during the day. Perhaps we can keep the trunk for just such an eventuality. I wonder if a heavy coat or cloak would be suitable to keeping our Lady Kindred from burning? I will have to ask her next time I get a chance.<br /> <br /> The question of Alla\u2019s sensitivity to sunlight reminds me that I should speak to the rest of the group and see if they possess any weaknesses that I should be aware of. Stories of Fae folk mention weaknesses to cold iron or church bells and such things. I do not know if our contingent of Fae have any such prohibitions or not. It would not be good to find out in the middle of a fight, or some important task that they have a weakness and are incapacitated. The same goes for Wolfram. Can he be bound like spirits can, or can something be done to the Geist to hurt the host? He is not as of yet a front line combatant, but he may be called into that capacity and this would be good to know.<br /> <br /> Tatiana and I should be up front about our susceptibility to silver as well. It is not a very common thing to make weapons out of pure silver, but I will not dismiss such a thing out of hand. I was given the opportunity to hold a sliver knife so I would know what it felt like. I will admit that it hurt quite a bit. I can imagine what it would feel like to be wounded by such a weapon. The silver plated knife hurt as well, but I could tell the difference. It was a matter of intensity. Dietrich always says that we should be prepared for any eventuality. It is a very practical mindset. I agree.<br /> <br /> ********<br /> <br /> This evening we walked through the train cars trying to find the Golden Eagle or some clue to its whereabouts. I suggested that we split up and go individually or in pairs to talk to people or search cars. It did not make sense to be seen entering as such a large and varied group. It would raise suspicions. Why would average people be traveling with obvious nobility? Plus our group is rather diverse. Like tends to call to like, and we defy that.<br /> <br /> Tatiana stayed to the side and watched people. I believe she was mainly paying attention to a man that was doing the same thing. He piqued my interest as well, but it would be too suspicious if we both kept an eye on him. The others split up and talked to various people or groups of people. I believe Alla wanted to talk to the mother/daughter pair. Dervala was going to talk to the other pair of young ladies that were talking quietly to themselves. I\u2019m not sure who the others were planning on conversing with. I figured that all of us in the same car might get crowded, so I took the opportunity to look around in the other cars on the train. I did not break into anyone else\u2019s sleeping cars, but may do that next.<br /> <br /> I did not find anything of note while looking by myself. Later Dacian joined me and we went to look in the baggage car. I am not familiar with how to pick a lock, but the dark man is more than capable. I believe the others had been drawn into a game of Bridge with the other passengers so we left them to it.<br /> <br /> Dacian and I searched everyone\u2019s luggage and found some interesting things. The mother/daughter pair are supposedly on vacation yet they have no bags in the luggage car. It is possible that they are keeping them in their sleeper car, but there is not a lot of room for any good sized bags in them. William (the British man who likes card games and talking) has a shotgun, a revolver and ammunition in his bags. The telling thing is that some of the ammunition in his bag is for a weapon that is not present. This means that he is likely carrying it on his person or it is in his sleeping car. We just keep a close eye on him. Guns are dangerous.<br /> <br /> Ewan (the Scottish stand alone man) has a couple of bags, but no Eagle within them. It might be in his sleeper car. We will check there next. Christina\u2019s (the woman traveling to collect important family paper work) luggage had a special lock on it, that Dacian picked with ease, and inside she has expensive jewelry and a functional dagger. It seems the lock is just to protect her valuables. Suzie (the young lady from the United States) has what looks like costumes, make-up and wigs to be used in disguises packed in her bags. It makes me wonder if the appearance she wears now is her real one or not and why she feels the need to hide her identity. Vera and Gloria (two young ladies from Austria) have occult materials such as carved bones, divination equipment and what looks like a ritual staff.<br /> <br /> After the Bridge game we exchanged information. Apparently Dervala can sense what a person\u2019s utmost desire is and found that the two occult ladies want very much to find out who has the Eagle. Also, Tatiana sensed something magical being cast at Lizette during the Bridge game. It did not appear to be harmful to the young Fae lady, so we are guessing that it was something used to cheat in the game. This power seemed to have come from our two occult ladies. It would be interesting to know what other abilities they have, but to ask them would reveal too much about ourselves and our abilities. I find that it is best to be underestimated.<br /> <br /> There is likely additional information that can be gathered by looking in people\u2019s sleeping cars as well as further conversations with pretty much everyone. Each person that I listed seems to have something of note going on. Whether or not it\u2019s connected to the Golden Eagle is another story. We do not have enough information as of yet. We will attempt to gather more and I will keep track of our progress.<br /> <br /> ********<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> So, you can run as fast as a train, hm, volchonok?<br /> <br /> What? No, the tall woman is not my mate. We are sharing dens for safety. She is a very good choice to guard the approach with me - she fights well.<br /> <br /> No, not with her teeth. Her fists merely, but her powers as a Kindred fortify her. The others... well, they were attempting augment their lack of proper weaponry with the sword, and that was less than impressive.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, they are not pups. Wolfram claims to have some skill with firearms - yes, yes, human things - and Dearbhail is not unskilled with a knife. Lizette seems similarly comfortable, but her choice to wield the chainsaw is odd.<br /> <br /> Chainsaws are another human thing, very loud. Very destructive too, but it requires gasoline to be anything other than an unwieldy club however.<br /> <br /> Bah, I should know better than to say \u2018human\u2019 and expect you to listen. We have found our prey, yes, but it is not so simple.<br /> <br /> Hush, it is not. He has a thing, a powerful thing, that is our true goal. And there are other hunters that we must discover.<br /> <br /> No, not Uratha. At least, none that we have seen so far. I do not know what the others have found, but one of the young women, at least, has some magical powers. She used them to cheat at cards, so either she is quite foolish, or it may simply indicate she has resources to spend trivially.<br /> <br /> There are many options, volchonok, that do not involve what you suggest. I myself shall do nothing as of yet however. Do not growl at me so. This path is much more well known by my fellows in this. They lead the hunt for now, with words and politeness and sneaking. Marek and Dacian spent much of the evening away. I presume they were breaking into the baggage car, and possibly others.<br /> <br /> Because that is the most obvious place to hide this Golden Eagle. We would be remiss in not making some effort to exclude that obvious answers.<br /> <br /> You are still not to chase our songbird. She and the others spoke with our fellow passengers, and played cards. They did not speak with our prey directly - much of the evening had passed before he was identified.<br /> <br /> Silly volchonok. I had no knowledge of his scent. Clearly. The others did not speak with him as he was playing it as I did, standing aloof, watching. He could not resist the English spy\u2019s persistent entreaties to play cards however. That one is another to be after the Eagle, likely. Definitely some sort of spy. Dacian will speak with him more, in Bucharest.<br /> <br /> Yes, speak with.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we cannot simply kill them all and run off into the darkness. Not tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 1 May 1920 - Morning<br /> <br /> No one entered my dreams last night. Well at least not of their own accord. Pity.<br /> <br /> Today we prepare for our great adventure. I do not know what to think of this.<br /> <br /> 1 May 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> Marek and Tatiana spared today. Tatiana was in wolf form for most of the fights. Alla joined in, but I\u2019m not sure if it was to practice or attempt to put on a show. She is stronger than she looks. Lizette built a sizable bomb, just in case as she says. I assisted her in hiding it in a large bear doll. I believe they call them Teddy Bears now. Something about an American hunter, but it makes no sense to me.<br /> <br /> I assisted Wolfram after he mentioned the need to learn the arts of swordsmanship. I tutored him with my own rudimentary skills until Dervala come upon us. She is perhaps the most skilled with a blade of anyone. Lizette mentioned using a flaming chainsaw, which is simply horrifying to consider, but otherwise, Dervala is the most competent.<br /> <br /> Afterward, there was discussion of a more specific nature as to what we could do. I admitted that I could move without leaving tracks or by changing my tracks and also make it easier to move about unseen. Dervala sings, though I suspect she is capable of more. No one pressed the issue so we let it go. Wolfram and Marek track and/or hunt ghosts and spirits respectively. Tatiana hunts humans. She did not elaborate and as I believe I still fall into that category, I felt no need to ask for clarification. Fenric is apparently there solely to make a spectacle, while Alla seems well versed in traversing the social gauntlet, as it were. Lizette is an actual inventor and seems incredibly well versed in the newest advances (and possibly some which are still undiscovered) which science has to offer. We are quite a collection, so to speak, indeed.<br /> <br /> 2 May 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> The trip into Vienna was uneventful, though the destruction left by the war was shocking. It seems that mine was not the only village utterly erased during the conflict. I grew morose and said little as we made our way into the larger city. I can only imagine how the desolation left by the Armies of the Sable Scales would look. Sleep will be a welcome escape from the constant reminders of the devastation war machines leave in their wake.<br /> <br /> 3 May 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> I have not had the chance to update earlier, though the stationary provided on the train is rather lovely. We boarded just after brunch and found our sleeping compartments. Fenric seemed completely boggled by my desire to spend time in the dark without shoes. Separately, we mingled as gently as possible so as not to draw undue suspicions. I sat just beyond a couple speaking of travel, but soon I allowed myself to be drawn into a conversation with William Forsyth and his American acquaintance, Suzy. William seemed to be on assignment from Britain while Suzy was traveling the world while she could. Though my curiosity was piqued, I decided to withdraw when William began trying to casually pull everyone into a game of Bridge.<br /> <br /> Marek and I used the opportunity to enter a fortuitously unsecured baggage car and search the bounty of readily available information about our traveling companions. Or in the case of the conservative mother and daughter, lack of information. We overheard Alla speaking with the pair as they discussed traveling on vacation. Unless they are keeping all their belongings in their sleeping car, I question their presence. However they were not so easily painted as our targets. When we entered, I used my Warlock\u2019s Gaze but found the car bare of any magical items. So we moved to search the old fashioned way. Marek is very helpful in assisting in such efforts. I continue to wonder what kind of courier he is. William\u2019s belongings included a polished shotgun, a well maintained revolver, and ammunition. While I am no expert in firearms, the cartridges for the shotgun and pistol were easily matched, though the rounds for a third undiscovered weapon was concerning. None of us noticed any signs that William was armed in the social car, so hopefully that means his sleeper is well appointed. Ewan Brandon, our intended mark, is a Scotsman who keeps to himself. This fact alone made him suspicious. But his lack of anything interesting, not least the Golden Eagle, in his bags after our previous findings were a stark contrast. Lizette and Wolfram spoke with a Christina, who was travelling to Turkey to finalize some sort of family paperwork. That charade crumbled when I found a specially crafted lock to secure her baggage. I could hear Marek blink in surprise as I simply opened that lock as if I had the key. And were I a common thief, or perhaps on less important business, I would have been thrilled at what I found. Christina had a treasure trove of jewelry as well as a quite functional dagger. Suzy the supposed American, had multiple costumes as well as wigs and disguise kits, which led us to wonder what she really looks like? Lastly we found various crafted bones, divination tools, and even what may be a ritual staff in the Austrian pair\u2019s baggage.<br /> <br /> The Austrian women were easily identified later as Vera and Gloria. They had some magic about them which Tatiana observed was cast on Lizette during the Bridge game. I could not tell that anything had changed by looking, but then we believe it may have been simply to cheat at cards. We reconvened after the Bridge matches to compare notes. Dervala has some Spring Contracts and used them to learn that Vera and Gloria were absolutely trying to find the Golden Eagle. Marek and I were planning to examine the sleeping cars next anyway, but after these revelations, it seems like a requirement.<br /> <br /> Also a trip to the dining car soon would not be unwelcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> It is May Day. We spent the day at Jamal\u2019s residence. I have prepared several items for our journey.<br /> <br /> -A replica of the Golden Eagle, which we can replace the original with. It is based on sketches and a photo, but I am hopeful it will work. Even if we don\u2019t use it now, it may be useful in the future.<br /> <br /> -A bomb powerful enough to bisect a train car and devastate much of it. With a timer. For Mayhem.<br /> <br /> -A teddy bear I can fit the bomb inside of (With help from Dacian).<br /> <br /> The group had little to say about the replica. Dearbh\u00e1il and Wolfram had concerns about the bomb. They just don\u2019t appreciate mayhem like I do. Of course I am not planning to use it. I mean, you load a pistol when you step outside\u2026you are not hoping to use the pistol, but you are prepared to. Similar, then, with a timed high explosive device. You don\u2019t step on the train expecting to use a timed high explosive device (for mayhem) or hoping to (for purposes of this example) but as with our hypothetical pistoleer, one needs be prepared to. For mayhem.<br /> <br /> I also showed off my chainsaw. Such potential these things have. Excellent tools, excellent weapons. I discussed some ideas about igniting the blade, possibly spraying a target with gasoline then igniting the blade so the target bursts into flames while being sawed. It should be noted this is an excellent deterrent. Few really want to charge a person with a chainsaw, fewer if it is on fire, and fewer still if you just sawed someone in half in front of them. I am in the Leaden Mirror after all; fear is my chief weapon. Then surprise I suppose. But eh.<br /> <br /> There was also discussion of using the Hedge to escape if the bomb was set. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> While I was exercising my genius, most of the others were sparring. Tatiana was quite keen on it. Probably a Werewolf thing. Alla apparently joined later. I think I heard something about Dearbh\u00e1il and a knife, but that can\u2019t be right. I think Dacian perhaps wisely decided to let, as they say, Werewolves be Werewolves, but I am sure Wolfram sparred some. Or at least I assume. Actually I sort of hate I missed that. German steel vs. a Werewolf is probably something to see.<br /> <br /> Did not flirt with Dearbh\u00e1il, too nervous. Not sure why. It\u2019s not like women are scarier than men, right? I am not afraid of men especially hot ones. I mean she is Spring Court for crying out loud. Prudes don\u2019t last long among the Antler Crowned. Oh well.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a good workday. Hopefully the boys enjoyed beating each other up.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3<sup>rd</sup> May 1920<br /> <br /> It would probably help to date these damn things. Last one was 1<sup>st</sup> May, one before that was 30<sup>th</sup> April.<br /> <br /> We are on the train. No mayhem yet. Dearbh\u00e1il and I settled into our room. She felt a little out of place with the crew. I tried to reassure her best I could. She is one of the most charming women I have ever met. Surely we can find something for her to do. Also a talented singer, and possibly with Spring Contracts healer. I am not of the Emerald Court, but I hear they have some useful desire detection and manipulation abilities. We do. With fear I mean.<br /> <br /> I also asked if she fancied anyone. She did not say so. I am surprised; I mean we have several rather handsome fellows among us. And me of course. And the vampire, but she is scary. Also, as mentioned, Spring Court.<br /> <br /> We met a number of other passengers. I met the most charming Austrian woman named Christina Esterh\u00e1zy. She has the sort of eyes you dive into and swim around in until the whirlpool draws you so deep you are lost. I was, once or twice. She is traveling to Istanbul to get some items related to her family\u2019s holdings. Documents or something. Noble stuff. Wolfram, being noble, talked to her too.<br /> <br /> She seemed really nice, though Dacian said everyone is up to something. You know, after looking through their luggage.<br /> <br /> This Brit named William Forsyth drew everyone into a big game of bridge. Bridge is something I learned after traveling to Paris. It is not my favorite game, but a good social lubricant. He seemed especially keen to draw in our target, Ewan Brandon, who was sitting in the common car being antisocial. I counted to twenty in my head and when Wolfram had not asked Christina to be his partner I asked her. She seemed charmed. Unfortunately, I think she merely finds me amusing. Wolfram paired with Dearbh\u00e1il, and a pair of Theosophists present stuck together. Christina and I got the Theosophists first and we were trounced. Tatiana told me they used some kind of power on Christina and I, so maybe psychic stuff, Theosophists are always going on about that. Then we switched and barely won against the Brits while the Theosophists clobbered our teammates.<br /> <br /> I learned nothing of Ewan, despite William\u2019s apparent desire to get more from him. Dearbh\u00e1il confirmed the Theosophical girls are seeking the Eagle. A mother and daughter pair did not remain for bridge so I really know nothing of them, but Alla spoke to them. William was chumming with a girl named Suzy from America, though according to Dacian she had disguise stuff in her trunk in the back and William had weapons among other things.<br /> <br /> Fun trip so far! Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session II</i><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a great deal of additional information to add to their accounts. Amusedly, it was only Wolfram\u2019s player who had a more than minor knowledge of Bridge. I had some knowledge but had to get him to confirm a few things. We used the game playing system in Winter Masques, with some hijinx.<br /> <br /> There is little else to add. Warlock\u2019s Gaze used by Dacian is from Contracts of Spellbound Autumn in Lords of Summer.<br /> <br /> Some (hopefully) intriguing personalities. Let\u2019s see what happens. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-01-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T06:10:24-07:00","id":501624,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying it so far but due to the large cast I anticipate that it could get hard to follow all the events. Would you consider writing a short blurb at the start of each session as a framing device? Something like Session 2, in which our cast duplicate a relic, board a train and play bridge. Just an idea, for now things are fine but if travel is going to be part of this game or if the cast split up this could be tricky.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, how have you found juggling the large cast with the various powers? Did you veto any character suggestions or encourage certain characters to take certain traits at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:47:11-07:00","id":501957,"title":"","content":"Well Gravitas Man, there was this one player that (mostly) jokingly kept suggesting the idea of Rasputin as either a Changeling (Oh don't get me started on what my fetch did while I was in Arcadia...) or a Geist. But as the party was heavy on Russian PCs it was deemed a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:18:19-07:00","id":502078,"title":"","content":"I'll see what I can do. The game does have one more player than usual, and one player has a ghoul (Mostly to give her someone to control while the Vampire is sleeping). I will see what I can do for clarity though. Some accounts are going to have a good deal more information. Merak and Dacian are more inclined to more complete recaps than Lizette or Tatiana.<br /> <br /> In this case, the size of the cast made me more inclined to run a game with slightly more specific goals...a bit more narrative and less sandbox than some others. It will still have some sandboxy stuff because that is where my biggest strength as a GM is. The actual cast is, as I say above, only one player higher so it does not feel very different than my usual six player groups. This is my first crossover game as more than a one shot (I have run two crossover one shots) so it is certainly intimidating. Fortunately, given my GMing style that is more given to the whole group pitching in on the game, there is less me needing to control them and more everyone looking at how to have the best game possible. I really did not try to have any PCs have specific traits. I was up for working with what they wanted to make. We had four players considering Changelings, but I did not want 4/7 to be Changelings as I, running a different Changeling game, did not want to have &quot;Changeling and a bit of other stuff.&quot; Fortunately, one player had a strong non-Changeling concept as well. That was it honestly; I did not veto any suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:54:18-07:00","id":509968,"title":"","content":"Such a cool story so far. The start (Jamal's hosted gathering) reminds me of Agatha Christie's &quot;And then there were none (Ten little indians)&quot; book (and perhaps Shirley Jackson's &quot;The haunting of Hill House&quot;). Very interesting characters, only Tatiana needs a little more description in my opinion. We'll know more about her soon, I'm sure. I'm waiting for the next AP's installment. <br /> <br /> I would like to see mixed within the text some rolls to make the reading more 'game-y' but of course it's not easy, I'm not expecting to see that. Have you ever thought of recording (and publishing) these sessions' audio? Or what about going live over hangouts or something? That would instantly set you all to fame and stardom <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for publishing this AP! Keep up the good gaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2738-onirim","name":"Onirim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T13:58:25-07:00","id":510166,"title":"","content":"Hey there. First off, thanks for giving feedback! I always appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Do you have any specific questions on Tatiana? I am sure I or her player could answer. Her player is pretty consistent with journals, so you should keep seeing hers as a perspective.<br /> <br /> The hardest thing with mechanics is most of us don't make many notes about them, and my games are often lower on the mechanics end of things. Most games do have several rolls every session, but not as many as some games do. I hate to ask this again, but I as I am trying to get better with these, is there anything specific you are looking for mechanics-wise? I can try and see what I can add in.<br /> <br /> I can ask my players about the audio, but I expect them to not go for it. We were asked that with <i>Balance of Shadows </i>and got a near unanimous no, and 5/7 are or were in that game. Of course, it came up almost five years ago. Part of the issue is several of us are pottymouths, and a couple are not crazy about their real names being thrown around.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how the hangouts thing would work. If it required audio same issue as above. If not maybe if a player wanted to keep an eye on it, I would not be able to as my brain is too full.<br /> <br /> Sorry I could not be more helpful. :-/ It was good hearing from you though and I am glad you are reading. Appreciate the feedback. Feel free to ask more questions I can halfass answering. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:08:31-07:00","id":515846,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to move forward into the past. Time rushes forward like an oncoming train, as the older of readers are all too aware. This train in our story remains safely in the past. However, little else seems safe on the train. Though it appears as first that things might yet be simpler than they seem, the hunters soon become the hunted, yet even so they ready to spring a trap.<br /> <br /> <i>Session III</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 4 May 1920<br /> <br /> Dervala and most of the others have decided to take a walk in town to see the sights. Dacian left with William and Suzie, while the others went on their own. They even managed to talk Ewan into accompanying them. I\u2019m sure Dervala turned on the charm. I stayed behind to keep an eye on our things as well as observe anyone who stayed behind. The Occultists stayed, as well as Gerta and her daughter. The later stayed in their room which made breaking into Ewan\u2019s room all but impossible for me. They left their door open and I am not the quietest thief, even with Dacian\u2019s lockpicks. I don\u2019t have a lot of practice. So, I skipped his room in favor of looking through Suzie\u2019s. Her room was rather mundane. There were a few items of clothing in a suitcase, but for the most part it didn\u2019t look like she was staying there. I have an idea of who she is staying with though\u2026our intrepid young William. <br /> <br /> Early in the afternoon the urban explorers returned. Tatiana took Dervala off to talk to her. Dervala for her part looked upset about something. A short while later Fenric gathered me and Wolfram to meet up with the others. Apparently Dervala had discovered something and needed to share it, privately.<br /> <br /> During their lunch Dervala used one of her Fae powers to \u201cread\u201d Ewan, and discovered that this whole thing is a test. He was there to make sure that acquiring the Eagle on our parts was met with a certain level of challenge. He is to make it difficult for us, and if we do not find this task to be hard enough he is to eliminate us, or those of us that thought it was too easy. To my mind this does not make for a very good test. One must have subjects, and killing them off because the task was too easy seems counterproductive. It does provide a certain amount of incentive to draw things out though.<br /> <br /> Dacian gave us some interesting information as well. Apparently during their walk, when Suzie was feeding the ducks, William approached Dacian and began sharing some of this observations and secrets. I do not know why he would do such a thing unless he was expecting something in return, but he did give us some interesting insights. He said that Suzie is not an American. She does a good impersonation, but something of her real accent comes through. He was wondering if Dacian had picked up on it. After listening to her speak later he agreed that she is not American. She has apparently spent last night with William. He however suspected she was up to something and set up a trick with coins to let him know if someone had been going through his things. She did. He pretended to sleep through the racket, but she was not idly looking, she was searching for something. Our guess, the Eagle. William also admitted that in Vienna someone broke into his hotel room. He suspected it was Suzie, hence the trap set in his sleeping car on the train.<br /> <br /> Lizette also offered an observation of our Scottish traveling companion. She said that being up close to him she could feel, for lack of a better word, that he is not entirely human. She said that he feels more like a combination of machine and magic than a person. Something like her teapot attendant. Dervala confirmed that he does not have desires the way a human would, giving further credence to his otherworldliness. I did not have as much to report as the others did, but told them what little I had found and observed. We decided as a group to wait until dinner time to investigate Ewan\u2019s room.<br /> <br /> While we waited Wolfram demonstrated how he can hide an object within himself. It was disconcerting to say the least. Lizette worked on a music box for Dervala. I think she has something of a crush on our songstress. It is rather endearing. <br /> <br /> Tatiana for her part paced and did calisthenics. I recognized some of them from my time in the army and decided to find out a little bit more about my fellow Uratha. So, I asked questions. I found out that she had been in the Russian army. She was supposed to go to the front and serve with her brother, but then the unpleasantness at the palace happened and that changed things. She was there when it happened. As soon as she was able she started towards the front, where her brother was stationed, but she was too late. He had been killed in battle. I think she blames the Bolsheviks for this. If they hadn\u2019t attacked when they did she might have been able to help her brother, or at least be there for him as he died. I know that I would want to be there for my brother if he had to die. I will do anything in my power to keep him alive and happy if it is at all possible. She told me about her family, so I told her about mine. I told her about being able to serve with Andel and how we were wounded and discharged. I also shared some of my own frustrations with the Bolsheviks. They impeded the Czech army, demanded weapons as payment for crossing their lands. It became ridiculous. Later they would attack us when we marched through. I\u2019m not sure of the reasons, I just know I started to really hate hearing their name.<br /> <br /> During this time Dacian also tried out some of his own Fae abilities to see if anyone else on his train is a supernatural being, like us. Turns out that Ewan, Gerta and Suzie are all supernatural creatures. Suzie was being concealed magically, but he was able to pierce the protections to see the magic in her. He could not tell what kind of being they were, just that they were magical in some way. The others were not magically concealed in any way. Either they can\u2019t hide themselves in that way or they have no desire to hide. If it is the former then they may not know that others can search for magical beings or they just assume most people won\u2019t \u201clook.\u201d If it is the later, that is worrying. If they choose not to hide themselves they either have a way to explain it away, or they may reveal themselves without any qualms. That could get dangerous depending on what they are.<br /> <br /> Dacian and Wolfram left to go check out Ewan\u2019s room while everyone was eating or otherwise engaged. They were not gone long when Gerta decided to go back to her room. Fenric, ever the gentleman, offered to escort her back and started making small talk all the while. His voice was pitched slightly higher than normal, which I\u2019m assuming is to give our companions time to hide or get away. The ruse worked and the two men were able to get into Ewan\u2019s room before Gerta got to hers. They didn\u2019t find anything interesting, just clothes and toiletries. No Eagle. It was not a complete loss however. They did discover that within the past few hours something magical had been worked on the doorframe. There was speculation on the parts of our Fae friends that it might have been a doorway to what they call the Hedge. It is by no means definitive, so we are keeping our minds open to other possibilities. <br /> <br /> Later Dacian and I decided to take a closer look at Williams\u2019s room while Fenric and Dervala distracted the people in the dining car with conversation and an impromptu song or two. Dervala is very good. I found what had to be a clever trap involving coins and a drawer. It made a great deal of noise and we decided to make our search quick in case someone had heard the racket. I will admit that I felt rather embarrassed at the whole thing, but Dacian did not point out the error, and for that I am grateful. In our quick search we found ether and other medical supplies as well as some small bags of powders. I tried tasting the powders to see if I could identify them or not, but I could not. That was the second time I failed my companions this night.<br /> <br /> Next we broke into Christina\u2019s room. We were only in there for a couple minutes when I heard someone trying to sneak up on the room. I\u2019m not sure how Dacian didn\u2019t hear it. It must have just under human hearing, but not below mine. I\u2019ve discovered that Fae though they may be the three changelings have human hearing. So, we decided to hide from the individual walking up. We both climbed up and hid ourselves along the top corners of the room, Dacian provided extra coverage by extending the shadows over us. That is a useful ability. I will have to inquire about that later. <br /> <br /> The person that opened the door was not the room\u2019s occupant, but Gerta instead. Rather, Gerta as a bladed monster. She had a metallic human shaped body, but had blades of iron and silver coming off of her in several directions. These blades also seemed to rotate and move around on her form. Her eyes glowed red as she looked around and said \u201cCome out, come out wherever you are. Grandma knows you\u2019re there.\u201d The voice was metallic and there was a grinding sound, but it was recognizable as Gerta\u2019s. She searched, but didn\u2019t seem to see us though she did look around closely. Frustrated at not finding us she used her bladed hand to stab through the bed several times. The blade cut through the mattress, bed frame and the floor as if it were made of butter. I had considered attacking the monster, but was uncertain that Dacian would be able to hold his own against such a beast. The silver blades would have caused considerable damage to me, and it certainly looked like she knew how to use them. Part of me thinks I should have attacked it despite my misgivings. It didn\u2019t take any effort to hide its true form which means that it has nothing to lose. And creatures of that strength with nothing to lose are very dangerous. <br /> <br /> After the creature left the room we managed to sneak out and we made our way back to the rest of the group in the entertainment car. Apparently everyone had moved there to hear Dervala sing. We told them of the monster that is Gerta. Wolfram said that he had heard of such creatures and that they were usually created for a specific purpose. This one seemed rather well adapted to killing Uratha, and perhaps Fae kind? I need to ask if they are indeed susceptible to cold iron. If that is what those blades are made of then Dacian and the ladies may be in danger.<br /> A short while later Christina came up to Wolfram and in a panic told him that someone had been in her room and had stabbed the bed with large blades. Wolfram and Dacian, being gentlemen, offered to go with her to take a look. Wolfram got a glimpse of what the monster can do and was impressed and perhaps a little intimidated. Wolfram and some others helped Christina move her things to another room, this one in our car. While he did so, Wolfram sensed a malevolent presence among the young ladies things. And he spotted an amulet that could very well be the source. Christina was doing her best to keep the amulet hidden, so either she knows that it is a dark magical item, or she thinks that it is just worth a lot.<br /> <br /> While Wolfram and Dacian were helping the young lady move I discussed things with Tatiana. We both agreed that we would need to do something very soon. The monster revealing itself knowingly is a bad sign. It has no further need to hide and if we are not careful it may harm innocents. I am not one to condone meaningless collateral damage if I can help it. The plan that we came up with is to have Tatiana lure the monster into the baggage car by changing to her Urshal form in from of it. We will have that car rigged with a shaped explosive that will create an exit for Tatiana and the other bomb that we put in the stuffed bear. Our hope is that the monster will react to the explosives the same way mortal men do and die. I am not convinced that this plan will go exactly the way we want it to though. I don\u2019t know why, but something just tells me that things will not go exactly to plan. I will not hesitate a second time to attack the monster if need arises. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes volchonok I am done pacing.<br /> <br /> Watch your tongue. I am still in no temper for insolent cubs.<br /> <br /> You are lucky you are a spirit. My teeth are sharp from disuse.<br /> <br /> It is none of your concern who I mate with. Besides, now is not the time for mating, it is time for the hunt.<br /> <br /> I did walk with our pretty bird today, yes. As did our prey and many others.<br /> <br /> So you were spying, eh, you insolent volchonok. Yes, she did accept my offering of food. And yes, she touched our prey rather a lot. She is much less enamored of him now.<br /> <br /> Because he is working for Jamal, and this is just, as she says, a bloody test. We are to get the Golden Eagle, once we have \u2018overcome adversity\u2019. She does not care for such trickery. I will enjoy watching her speak with Jamal once we have ended our hunt.<br /> <br /> True, I also do not care for trickery. But I am getting paid to retrieve this thing, I do not care much whose man guards it. Or whose woman.<br /> <br /> No, Dearbhail will not let me throw him out of the train, unless he tries to kill her. I might dangle him out a little. The Eagle is not on his car nor in his baggage, so we will require him alive and answering questions, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> I am preparing for a chase, yes. Gerta, the old woman, is in actuality some monstrous creature of metal. Once the public cars are empty, I will taunt her into chasing me.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it is a small silly human place to run, but that will be to her disadvantage as well. And my fellows are quite good at laying traps. Lizette is able to prevent her from calling on her allies, whether that is Suzie or Ewan.<br /> <br /> The American woman. She is some sort of supernatural thing, we do not know what. But she has been following our prey as well, and spying on the spy.<br /> <br /> I do not know. Marek and Dacian will be on guard against such things. Wolfram will be on top of the meal car, so as to trigger the explosion that will create an escape route, and then the larger bomb which will destroy the baggage car and Gerta with it.<br /> <br /> Alla will be distracting the guard in our car.<br /> <br /> There is a guard in our car because the room of the noblewoman was attacked by Gerta, though she does not know it was her. She rests within our car.<br /> <br /> I do not know. I think it is Wolfram\u2019s fault? The damage to her room was considerable. Marek has said the monster Gerta turns into is covered in blades, some made of silver, yet still sharp enough to slice through metal. Wolfram says he knows of creatures made to fulfill specific roles and hers is certainly clear.<br /> <br /> Bored of metal monsters already volchonok? Or bothered by the silver? Yes, yes, there were new smells. A man with a large mustache and another younger man joined us at this last stop.<br /> <br /> I do not know. They are probably also after the Eagle, but we will retrieve it first.<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok. Soon we will be the ones with the Eagle and it will be time to run properly. But not tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 4th May 1920<br /> <br /> Today has been an emotional rollercoaster.<br /> <br /> Went out to lunch with Dearbh\u00e1il, Wolfram, Tatiana, Fenric, and, oddly enough, Ewan Brandon. Dearbh\u00e1il worked a while at getting Ewan to talk. He said little, really, other than about his work and being followed by Suzy. Tatiana seemed irritated at the attention Ewan was getting from Dearbh\u00e1il. Fell in love a little more with Dearbh\u00e1il. Need to not do that unless she is amicable to such things. I sadly lack the charm to tempt her too much regardless.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il used her Spring Court Contracts on Ewan and was upset at the response. It dampened her mood a bit, though Wolfram cheered her up. Wolfram and I have a similar taste in women. I actually like Wolfram, though, and he seems to respect me. I hope this does not come between us. If we also have similar taste in men it could get bad.<br /> <br /> I got an odd feeling as I interacted with Ewan he was machine like, like a golem or something. I did not say anything about it till we got back. I think it comes from my time doing research in THOTH. They are all crazy with Hedge Golems. But Ewan is not a Hedge Golem.<br /> <br /> Discussed matters after return. Dearbh\u00e1il believes this is all a test by M. Ruhadze. At the time I agreed. Decided to make the switch of Golden Eagles at dinner nonetheless. Discussed several methods including making a display of the fake to throw people off. Dacian found out William was apparently a cad of some sort, though his behavior is, in my experience, not uncommon between men as I understand it. Dearbh\u00e1il went to practice, and I got some materials and spent a couple hours working on a music box for her. She liked it.<br /> <br /> Dinner hit a snag as Wolfram and Dacian were unable to locate the Golden Eagle in Ewan\u2019s car. Also, Greta made things a bit difficult for them. I did not, at the time, understand the significance. Dearbh\u00e1il spoke about Christina Esterh\u00e1zy. Was she trying to reflect my attentions away from herself? Christina did look at me and smile, though I should not have considered it. Dearbh\u00e1il did make me half crazy with tension though, and seemed to enjoy it, but not in a cruel way.<br /> <br /> We moved onto the playroom, and Dearbh\u00e1il sang. She is wonderful. Fenric introduced her and was oddly mesmerizing. I sat with Christina, who scratched my back a little. It was nice. She got up once briefly between songs but it was okay. I was in my own little world, thinking about my spinning flamethrower tank idea when Marek and Dacian returned to the room. Wolfram got up to talk to them, while I rested.<br /> <br /> See the idea is the tank has a pair of tubes that can fire flammable material while they spin at high speed. The idea is the arc is such that the flames go over the tank in sort of a protective field and it can be driven into infantry, or you know bad guys. Also a giant buzzsaw blade around the furthest outside makes it harder to get onto the tank since one risks being sawed if they can\u2019t jump high enough or they miss. The heat from the flamethrows can be used, also, with an internal teapot system so those inside can have tea. A small slit over the teapot releases the steam. It\u2019s ingenious, really. <br /> <br /> But my reverie was broken when Christina returned and went to Wolfram, looking upset. They returned from where Marek and Dacian came, and Dacian followed. I followed as well. It turned out something had broken into Christiana\u2019s sleeper and damaged the bed there. She was very upset. I immediately volunteered to protect her, but she quickly refused, speaking as if I was made of porcelain. She spoke of me as if I was a child, not an adult, much less a woman. I realized I could get angry or cry, so I got angry. Not that she noticed. She was, admittedly, frightened and I cannot blame her for not noticing my response. So Wolfram took her to the conductor while I returned to the car with my head held high. Relatively speaking. Love is poorly understood outside France it seems.<br /> <br /> If I am being honest with myself, Dearbh\u00e1il probably does not take me seriously either in such a way.<br /> <br /> Christina got a guard, and moved to our car, and we discussed what was actually going on. Gerta is some kind of killer machine, with forked blades for hands, glowing red eyes, and spikes rotating across her body. She is cruel and enjoys the hunt for her prey, and she had weaponized silver and iron, plus she carved through the bottom of the train car like it was not there. Does Ewan have these capabilities as well? I suspect his are different, but I cannot say what they are.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I have to admit that is excellently terror inducing, but why the lack of saws? Saws add functionality and stalking potential. A machine-woman with rotating saw blades could carve through doors or tanks, even walls, to get at her prey, and the movement and sound would be quite terrifying. Of course, the sound could get in the way so of course some non-saw weapons are required, but seriously, if I were going to build an ultimate terror machine I would at least give her glorified barbecue forks some extra capabilities. Talk about wasted potential.<br /> <br /> However, we now have a plan (Mayhem) that I like (Mayhem) and has some possibility for real Mayhem (Huzzah!). If Greta is stalking us we need to deal with it sooner rather than later. We agreed to have Tatiana lure Greta into the baggage car in the rear and detonate the explosive there that I had created. I whipped up a smaller explosive for Wolfram to set off to make a hole Tatiana can escape through before the bomb goes off (assumedly). My part of the plan is to hinder Greta\u2019s ability to communicate and set off the bomb. There should be a lot of Mayhem. I hope.<br /> <br /> Oh well, no sense putting off blowing up a train.<br /> <br /> (Mayhem)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 4 May 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> We stopped in Budapest this morning.<br /> <br /> I was slightly nervous given the actions of the Romanian army. It had only been about two months since the military withdrew, and then only after seizing \u201cwar reparations\u201d from the locals. I did not mention these concerns as I had no wish to darken my companions\u2019 opinions of Romania unnecessarily, though I personally found those actions deplorable.<br /> <br /> After brunch, Dervala organized an excursion. Sadly I had already agreed to accompany William and Suzy on our own stroll. Marek assumed, rightly, that I had an available set of lockpicks to borrow, though it was no more welcome a question. Apparently werewolves have little use for conversational delicacy. I believe the Uratha could gain more use from them than I could, at least for now.<br /> <br /> I met William and Suzy in the train station before we wandered the nearby park. As Suzy rather awkwardly left our company to feed ducks by the pond, William began confusing some unusual information to me. It seems good William suspects Suzy of deception and rightly so. At least according to his sensibilities. To begin, he asked if Suzy\u2019s accent seemed odd to me. She had spoken only briefly in my presence, but I am not an expert on American accents. The Englishman regaled me with rather scandalous details of a romantic incident between himself and our \u201cAmerican\u201d associate. Afterwards, he feigned sleep to observe her activities. His suspicions proved true as Suzy searched his room, even tripping the \u201ccoin trap\u201d he left in the drawer. She froze when he continued the ruse by \u201calmost waking,\u201d then she carefully returned to bed. He noted that she did nothing with the coins, so money was not what she was after. I asked why he decided to confide his concerns in me? He noted that as a handsome gentleman, I might attract Suzy\u2019s attention as well and he wanted to be sure I knew what I was getting into.<br /> <br /> We stood from the bench, met Suzy by the water, and continued our walk. William engaged Suzy such that she had to speak in my presence. At the very edges of her speech, and only because I knew to listen, I detected the faintest hint of a Yugoslav accent, though I could not determine any regional distinctions. Otherwise we enjoyed our minor excursion without incident. If Suzy was aware she had been found out, she gave no indication. We returned to the station unmolested and boarded easily.<br /> <br /> Fenric and Wolfram gathered all of our disparate motley for an exchange of information. Our Fairest positively seethed as though she had joined the Crimson Court. When she seemed composed enough, she explained that we were tricked. While on her walk with Ewan Brandon, and most of the rest of our travelling companions, she used her Spring Court Contracts. The business man provided her with quite a bit of information without ever telling her a thing. The task Jamaal set us upon is nothing more than a \u201cbloody test.\u201d We are the only ones who could retrieve the Golden Eagle, though it could only be through adversity. Anyone who felt the too at ease with their part was to be killed out of hand. Though it seems that Ewan has a few secrets of his own. Not only does Mr. Brandon not have desires, but Lizette claimed that he felt like a machine to her. She referenced Golems but I have never had the opportunity to try and steal one, so I am uneducated on the subject. Truly I will be forced to expand my education through my peers, as a matter of career advancement.<br /> <br /> 4 May 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> Two new faces joined us at dinner, though they were not immediately talkative. Given our previous discussions, I decided to confirm a few identities. Seizing the opportunity, I greeted Ewan as I entered the dining car with a welcome handshake. My gamble paid off and my Warlock\u2019s Gaze proved he, Gerta, and Suzy were all somehow more than they appeared. Interestingly, Suzy was concealed but I overcame her defenses. Christina seemed nervous but I could not determine of what. The rest of the passengers had no reaction to our presence other than to greet us. Dervala teased both Wolfram and Lizette about something I later learned was Christina\u2019s attentions. But that is the way of the Fairest, I suppose.<br /> <br /> For my part, I affected a rather convincing grimace and excused myself with apologies shortly after the soup was served. Wolfram came along as the good man he is to ensure one who is ill makes it to their quarters. We hurriedly enacted our plan to search the sleeping cars sharing an amused glance between us.<br /> <br /> We managed to hide in Ewan\u2019s quarters just as Fenric and Gerta entered the car, however. The amusement wore off due to how close we came to be discovered. I had to rather unkindly shove the former pilot in and hold the door to hide our presence. Once I knew we were hidden, I used my Keening to save my Glamour. There was no sign of the Golden Eagle, however some form of magic effect had been used on the door within a few hours. After carefully searching the room manually, we waited for Gerta to leave before returning to the dining car. I missed the salad, but coffee was being served so I could more easily \u201csettle my stomach.\u201d Just as the sponge cake arrived, Gerta left and Dervala decided to sing. I really should travel like this more often.<br /> <br /> 4 May 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> There are monsters among us beyond the pale of anything I have encountered this side of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> After Dervala\u2019s performance, we dispersed as we may. Marek invited me to visit a few rooms while the others spent time in the social car. He was apparently not very successful with my lock picks earlier. Marek is surprisingly quiet when he wishes. We entered William\u2019s quarters first. Sadly, I did not think to warn the werewolf of the coin trap. It was quite loud in the otherwise silent car. Outside of that surprise, we found a jar of ether, multiple unlabeled powders, and a rather sturdy set of handcuffs. While interesting, there was nothing useful to us immediately so we moved on. Christina\u2019s room was never fully investigated as almost immediately after we entered the room, Marek sensed someone coming toward us in the hallway. I pressed myself against the wall of the quarters and held myself above the floor between the wall and ceiling. As I did so, I also pulled shadows around me. I grabbed Marek as he struggled to do as I had done. Just as we were secure and hidden, the door burst in and metal monster stood waiting to destroy us. It had multiple blades, some silver, some iron, others of unknown steels, as well as horrific red eyes which filled the room with their damning glow. We soon realized this beast was Gerta as her metallic voice mocked and chided us to \u201ccome to Grandma.\u201d She could not find us thanks to my Contracts of Darkness and eventually grew bored, as she stabbed Christina\u2019s bed before leaving. My senses strained, I could tell she returned to her room and waited there with the door open. Thankfully, we could escape via the other direction. Our ability to stealthily move saved us from a very unwanted battle.<br /> <br /> We calmed ourselves then returned to the social car. I gave Wolfram a look and he came over to make sure we were alright. I related my tale to the Sin-Eater and finished just as Christina approached with a concerned look on her face. Someone had been in her room and she asked if Wolfram, and myself by association, would take a look. We observed the scene and it was more disturbing than I had realized and I was suddenly very happy to know Lizette possessed a bomb. With the electrics on and without need of watching my back, we could tell the stab marks went through the floor of the car. With that bit of information, Wolfram took Christina to the Conductor while I gathered the others.<br /> <br /> After several ideas failed during a verbal set through, we settled on something unconventional. Lizette would make a smaller bomb capable of only blowing a hole in the side of the car. The real bomb would be placed such that all the car would be destroyed, along with anyone inside. Wolfram would be in contact with the car to coordinate the smaller explosion and to disable any way to escape from inside the car. Tatiana would lure Gerta into the baggage car thusly rigged to explode, where Wolfram would cause the car to seal, then blow the smaller explosive for the werewolf to escape. Before Gerta could follow, the main bomb would detonate and we would be free of the beast.<br /> <i><br /> End Session III</i><br /> <br /> The information on Mr. Brandon came from using the first Fleeting Spring Contract. I described the feelings Dearbh\u00e1il has as more like \u201corders\u201d than \u201cfeelings\u201d that Brandon was to carry out.<br /> <br /> [The PCs] must receive the Golden Eagle<br /> No one else bust receive the Golden Eagle.<br /> The PCs must not know they are to receive it, and any who suspect it must be killed.<br /> <br /> The suspicion, all but confirmed by Ms. Durst, is that the PCs face Angels. The question is who is an Angel and who, if anyone, is a Demon. OOC suspicion falls on the American Suzy to be a Demon. Is she? Well\u2026<br /> <br /> There was chatter as to who was getting more \u201cpoints\u201d with Dearbh\u00e1il. At least by Tatiana and Alla\u2019s players. Tatiana got \u201cpoints\u201d for having her eating place selected, Lizette got a couple \u201cpoints\u201d for sitting next to Dearbh\u00e1il, Ewan for the fact she kept chatting with him, and Wolfram for the fact she walked away with him briefly. Then Tatiana lost a bunch for suggesting they throw Gerta from the train and Lizette gained a bunch for giving Dearbh\u00e1il the music box. All of this OOC, of course. It was rather funny<br /> <br /> Of course, no one else IC knew that Dearbh\u00e1il kissed Wolfram while they had stepped away, which took him rather by surprise. So at the end of that session he was ahead, I guess?<br /> <br /> The next session finishes this leg of the story. There is combat, and half the group nearly gets killed. Much excitement. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:27:35-07:00","id":533955,"title":"","content":"Time for the climax of our first story. Our heroes battle Angels, Demons, and Psychics but come up one Golden Eagle stronger<br /> <br /> <i>Session IV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 5 May 1920<br /> <br /> It is done. We retrieved the Eagle and defeated the monster. It was of course not as simple as that, but it is accurate. The trap we laid for the monster worked for the most part. The explosive created an exit for Tatiana, but as she was getting out the monster stabbed my fellow Uratha through the side with silver blades. Tatiana made it out but within moments she jumped from the train. I could tell from the look on her face that she was in a good deal of pain and she was starting to frenzy. Having had that happen myself I understood why she flung herself from the moving train. She would be a danger to the rest of us if she stayed, so she removed herself from the equation.<br /> <br /> The second explosive went off like it should and flung the bladed monster a good distance away. I took note of approximately where it landed then jumped off the train myself to go after Tatiana. I figured that she would want to personally deal with Gerta, so I hopped off and waited the fifteen or so minutes it would take her to calm down before tracking down my friend.<br /> <br /> I found Tatiana easily. Her scent is distinctive, but there was also a lot of blood and that is one of the easiest things to track. I followed the scent right to her and helped her bandage her wounds using my shirt. That bitch got her good and I did not bother to hide the growl that came from my throat. I stayed composed though and offered to lead Tatiana to the monster. She smiled and we headed out.<br /> <br /> It was easy to find the monster. It was unconscious, which while less sporting, was better for us. I stood back and let Tatiana step forward and rip the monsters throat out. Apparently instead of blood this thing had motor oil in it and Tatiana spat it out with disgust written on her face. That could not have tasted pleasant.<br /> <br /> After the monster was dealt with we headed back to the train, which had stopped in light of the explosion. We integrated ourselves with the milling people and compared notes quickly. Dervala asked Tatiana and I if we were okay, and we assured her that we\u2019d be fine. I do not know if she was completely satisfied with that answer, but we do heal quickly. Silver inflicted wounds take longer to heal, so Tatiana will be at less than full strength for a little while, but she will be okay. Tatiana and I noticed pretty quickly that Lizette was not among us and we, along with Dervala, decided to head back on the train and look for our wayward comrade. I believe Dacian may have come along too, but I lost track of him.<br /> <br /> We found Lizette engaged in combat with a now electrified monster version of Suzie. We knew that she was supernatural in some way and now we know what. Or at least we know what form we takes, but we are still not sure what exactly she was.<br /> <br /> Lizette was attacking Suzie with a hammer, and Suzie was doing her level best to hurt Lizette by shocking with electricity. Suzie had the Eagle and was trying with some amount of success to kill Lizette. Our slight friend was not doing well when we arrived. Tatiana and I rushed forward and attacked the electric creature. Tatiana went for her legs, trying to sweep them. She got a decent shock and was knocked out. I attacked, also going for her legs, and was also wounded for my trouble. The monster then attacked me in return and I felt the same sharp burn of electricity as before. It was not a pleasant experience.<br /> <br /> Lizette used our distraction to grab the Eagle and drop the hammer that she\u2019d been using as a weapon. I grabbed the hammer, thinking it might make a good insulator from the electricity.<br /> <br /> Though sheer force of will Tatiana came around and got back up again. Though she knew she would only end up hurting herself, she attacked the creature one more time. The attack was successful and the monster that was Suzie fell apart. Literally. Into many pieces of junk. I\u2019m not sure if that is what is supposed to have happened, but it makes cleaning up the \u201cbody\u201d much easier.<br /> <br /> Tatiana was knocked out again from the electricity and I carried her back to her room and laid her on her bunk. I figured it would only be a short time until she woke up again, but figured out of sight was better, and the bunk would be more comfortable than the floor.<br /> <br /> Dervala fussed over Lizette, who was not looking very good, but seemed to be in a considerably better mood than she had been. We gathered the group together and Wolfram hid the Eagle within himself so it would be secure. We then agreed to hide the duplicate Eagle among the Theosophists things. They may not know it is a fake and stop looking for it. Gloria at least will have a hazy memory of what happened. She was also in the room that Lizette and the monster (what Lizette called a golem) had been in, but she was already unconscious on the floor when we arrived. It looked like she\u2019d been knocked out by a blunt object. We assumed correctly that it was Lizette and her hammer that did that.<br /> <br /> We agreed to continue traveling on the train until we get to Bucharest. From there we will find alternative transportation to Malta and meet up with Jamal. It had been suggested that we just walk, but some of the others did not seem too keen on the idea. Tatiana was all for walking, but I am glad we decided to stay on the train. She is still badly hurt and the rest will do her some good.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7 May 1920<br /> <br /> We met up with Jamal. Dervala initially confronted Jamal about the fact that acquiring the Eagle had been a test and she admitted that she wasn\u2019t sure if it had been his doing or not. He defended himself by saying that if it had been a test on his part then the Fae members of our party would have felt the promise break. But it had not broken, so that goes a long way to proving that Jamal did not have anything to do with the test.<br /> <br /> We described the monsters that were Gerta and Suzie and he seemed to know about them, or things like them. He said that he had heard of a powerful entity that strives to change history, and that this test and the monsters was their handiwork. He called Suzie a rogue caretaker of reality and he warned us that our plans and those of the caretakers might clash. I am not sure what these \u201ccaretakers\u201d are, but I do know that they are dangerous. They appear to have different powers between them, at least the two that we came across did. I believe that Ewan is one of these caretakers, though whether or not he is \u201crogue\u201d is another question entirely. I saw him turn into a swarm of small mechanical wasps, so I have some small insight into his powers. I am fairly certain that the small size of the wasps would do nothing to dampen their effectiveness in a fight.<br /> <br /> Jamal also showed us how to use the Eagle. We each needed to put a drop or two of blood and a few hairs in a compartment. We are now bound to the Eagle and it to us. I think it will be a useful thing to have, but I will reserve final judgement until more time has passed.<br /> <br /> <br /> 8 May 1920<br /> <br /> We are a pack. When Tatiana brought up the idea of becoming a pack with our traveling companions I nodded and she mentioned the idea to the others. They all seemed interested in the idea, which I\u2019ll admit was good to hear. I have grown to enjoy the company of this motley group. I did mention to Tatiana and will have to bring up with the group the idea of bargaining with a spirit to gain a totem for our pack. I shall have to ask the others what kind of spirit would best represent all of us, then go about finding it. I am confident we will be successful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, I am injured.<br /> <br /> No! No, stop that. You do not need to lick the wound, Marek and Dearbhail have cleaned it already. And you certainly do not need to remove the bandages with your claws.<br /> <br /> No, I am not angered with you. It was just painful.<br /> <br /> Because, silly volchonok, the metal monster had silver blades, remember?<br /> <br /> I did hunt without you, yes, but do not pretend you did not keep your distance on purpose when you smelt the Kuruth.<br /> <br /> I jumped off the train because I did not want to harm the others. I have grown fond of them.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, volchonok. Perhaps they will become pack. We did hunt well.<br /> <br /> It is true, the hunt is finished. Marek found me shortly after I came back to myself, and knew which way the explosion blew the metal monster. It was child\u2019s play to track her down, and finish the kill, for all of her silvered flesh and oil for blood. The Eagle...<br /> <br /> Yes, impatient volchonok, I also smell of burning. I was about to say, the small one, LIzette, found the Eagle, and tussled with another metal monster, the not-American Suzie. We were lucky to find her when we did, as she had some power over electricity. It was like biting fire, but Marek and I finished her as well.<br /> <br /> I will introduce you to that human thing next time we come across an electric fence. You may mark our territory there, and see how you like it.<br /> <br /> We travel to Malta now. I do not like being so close together on the train, with those who might be enemies. The others did not wish to walk to the city however.<br /> <br /> I agree. Bah. It would serve us well, the moonlight above and the earth beneath our paws and space to be free. Even humans such as these are foolish.<br /> <br /> Oh volchonok, I am in no shape for it and there is still danger. I will not leave my comrades to run tonight.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Ah volchonok! I heal quickly, but not that quickly, not with these wounds. You must be careful awhile yet.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is exciting. We are a pack now. It is a good thing. There is also the protection of the Eagle, such as it may be.<br /> <br /> Heh, yes, the songbird\u2019s feathers were ruffled, though not as much as I expected. For the best. I am in no shape to teach him a lesson for her. It was not Jamal who set this test however - his promise would have been broken as soon as Gerta\u2019s silver pierced my flesh, and the fairy creatures would know.<br /> <br /> We do not know. Jamal spoke of \u2018Caretakers of Reality\u2019, creatures who influence the course of history.<br /> <br /> I do not know if it is merely human history. They are attempting to use Marek and I, so perhaps it is broader than that.<br /> <br /> Do spirits have history? Perhaps I should ask Marek.<br /> <br /> There is nothing for now. We stand guard, pay attention to the strange things in our lives and watch each other\u2019s backs. Alla spoke of purchasing a castle for our use, for our territory.<br /> <br /> A castle is better than a city. Lizette would have us in Paris.<br /> <br /> Yes, a human place, full of many many humans. It would be useful, for some of us, it is true...<br /> <br /> Well, we will not. It will be a castle not in a city. Perhaps near a town. I could bring Elena there. She would be safer.<br /> <br /> No, you still may not chase the songbird.<br /> <br /> Because I say so.<br /> <br /> Of course, you are most gracious, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok. Tonight... tonight we will run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 5 May 1920 - Early Morning<br /> <br /> The night proved far more exciting than we could have imagined. Hopefully Tatiana and Lizette will recover quickly for us to speak of it fondly.<br /> <br /> After our planning session, the others looked to me to distract the guard outside Christina\u2019s door. I had no idea of the man\u2019s ability but I knew of a way to remove him from the area. I left Dervala in my room with the door open and the lights out then slipped down the hall. The guard had no idea why the lights in the car suddenly went dark. That the darkness then seemed to close in and surround him did nothing to reassure the man. Once I was confident he could not identify me through the darkness, I moved from my hidden corner and slowly crawled along the floor of the car as though I were climbing a steep wall. My intentions were to drive the man into a dark room with Dervala, a not unpleasant event. However the guard was more dedicated than I expected. Being a gentleman, he knocked on Christina\u2019s door before slipping inside and closing the door behind him. I joined Dervala and closed my door.<br /> <br /> I peered out my door after we heard what sounded like a large dog and a suit of armor running down the hall. Unfortunately I did my job too well and I could only see my darkness. Just after I closed my door, I heard a strange metallic buzzing move by. I looked out again quickly to see a swarm of what seemed to be metal hornets following the others. Lizette came running by then so I assumed all was well.<br /> <br /> Moments later, the train shook from the explosion. I went back to the doorway and noticed Lizette knocking on Christina\u2019s door. They spoke as the train began an emergency stop. I realized that this would be the perfect time to rob the train due to the chaos which would ensure. However, I was attempting to entertain Dervala and did not want the random things the others brought. We exited the train while the conductor, engineer, and several carmen stared in disbelief at the detached and mangled car ripped free from the train as a whole. William was outside as well and asked if I had seen or spoken with Suzy. No one had since before the explosion. Lizette was also missing given William and Christina were together as were Mr. Brandon and one of the Theosophists, Marek and Tatiana, and my Emerald Court companion. Though Tatiana looked as though she was in pain, she and Marek moved to find Lizette.<br /> <br /> I remained behind, in theory I told myself to waylay Ewan in case he decided to investigate the missing guests. But if I am honest with myself, I doubt I would have been any help with any sort of conflict. And given the state Lizette, Marek, and Tatiana were in when they I felt rather guilty for not at least making things harder for our targets. Collectively, we gathered our belongings and left the train while still in range of Bucharest. We leave for Tr\u03afpolis on the next train on our way back to Malta. I believe Dervala will be fully prepared to face Jamal about our \u201ctest\u201d by then.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7 May 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> My dreams remain sorely uninterrupted as we found ourselves back safely in Malta. The smell of the spices in the market is incredible. I may never tire of it.<br /> <br /> I am however concerned as Dervala seems to be building her case against Jamal and these is feeding an unhealthy aggression in Tatiana. I have given Marek several concerned glances, but he has been looking deeply into nothing, so I assume he is dealing with spirits. Hopefully he is not simply ignoring me.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7 May 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> Dervala did not unleash her wrath upon Jamal, though she did lay out our situation and made it very clear she did not appreciate \u201ctests.\u201d For his part, Jamal was very understanding and assured us that he was not involved, as the Lost among us would have felt the oath break. As this didn\u2019t happen, the Irish rage washed away. Jamal is no fool, but neither is he unprepared. The creatures Lizette refers to as golems are the servants of some controlling entity which, like our \u201ctest,\u201d changes the flow of events or sometimes history. Something about caretakers of reality. Suzy was a rogue agent among these caretakers but to what end, we could not be sure.<br /> <br /> Once trust had been reestablished, Jamal showed us how to use the Golden Eagle. Each of us placed a few drops of blood and a small clipping of hair into a compartment within the piece. Once it was done, the Eagle closed. We all waited a moment, sharing confused glances, before I asked if that was it. Jamal approached and confirmed that we were finished.<br /> <br /> We are apparently now bound to the Golden Eagle. Disappointingly, I feel no different.<br /> <br /> <br /> 8 May 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> We are a strange motley, but it works for us. The werewolves apparently felt the same as Tatiana gathered us together and requested that we form a pack. It was an honor to be considered as family among our strong and proud Uratha. And truth be told, it was good to have a family again. There is some talk of binding a spirit to us as a totem guide. I am unsure as to how this works, but I will stand with my brothers and sisters as we learn together.<br /> <br /> There is also talk, from Alla and Fenric, of purchasing a castle to hold as our own. Marek and Tatiana speak of territory, but the safety of such a structure, both within and without, is incredible. My father would be so proud and so sickly envious. It is good to have a family again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 5th May 1920<br /> <br /> \u201cWithout a hitch\u201d would be rather overstatement, but we completed our objective.<br /> <br /> -Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian distracted the guard in our car outside Christina\u2019s room. I believe Dacian mostly used his Darkling Contracts. The guard was inside when he needed to be.<br /> <br /> -Tatiana successfully lured Gerta to the back car. Issue was Gerta\u2019s daughter. I neutralized her gun and managed to take her out with a hammer, being careful not to kill her, but as a result I only got a brief use of Contracts of Entropy to render Gerta unable to call for help.<br /> <br /> -In back car, Tatiana managed to not die long enough for the bomb to go off. Issue was Gerta got a hit in on Tatiana that injured her badly and made her go into a rage. She managed to throw herself off the train as it was starting. I am unsure of the logic behind this but have been told it is a \u201cWerewolf Thing.\u201d Wolfram managed to set off the bomb, injuring Gerta badly enough that she was unable to pursue and Marek and Tatiana managed to put her down.<br /> <br /> Note: Not enough explosives. Sure I took out a train car, but Gerta survived, if briefly and was knocked into a coma. The next time I fight one of these golems, I need more explosives. I can get more explosives. So many more explosives. Hee hee hee.<br /> <br /> -As the train slowed, removed Gerta\u2019s daughter (name forgotten) from the train so she could not accuse us of anything. I am sure she survived. Maybe.<br /> <br /> -Went to check on Christina, be sure she was okay.<br /> <br /> -Once the train was stopped, went to see if Ewan had left the item in his car. Was told something about hornets. I saw Brandon outside so made my move. Issue was Gloria Eberhard and Suzy Jenkins also made moves for it. I saw Gloria not Suzy. Note to self, trying to sneak up on a psychic is unwise. Gloria tossed me with her mind but I managed to knock her out. Then Suzy blindsided me. Suzy was some sort of electrical golem.<br /> <br /> After being shocked a few times Tatiana, Marek, and Dearbh\u00e1il noticed I was missing and came to help. I don\u2019t remember things too clearly at that point as I had been shocked several times. Suzy had the Golden Eagle, and was going to try to escape when the werewolves arrived. Tatiana hit her and collapsed from being shocked. Marek seemed badly hurt as she turned on him. However, the Werewolves intelligently aimed for her legs and knocked her down, and I seized the moment to grab the Golden Eagle and jump out the window, I left my hammer for Marek, who took the golem down.<br /> <br /> Marek, Tatiana and I were not in very good shape. But we acquired the Golden Eagle. Wolfram stored it inside his ghost body or whatever for safe keeping. Tonight we leave Bucharest and return to Malta.<br /> <br /> I spoke to Christina some and we exchanged contact information. I intend to write to her immediately after this is over. I think there may have been a spark there. If nothing else, she seems terribly concerned for my safety.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7th May 1920<br /> <br /> Did some design work for the fire spinning tank. Fire spinning tank is good talk. Hard part is powering the sawblades. Need to work on some designs.<br /> <br /> Spoke with Wolfram about Christina. Acknowledged we were both interested in her, and discussed the situation like adults. We each will continue to communicate our interest, and not do anything uncivilized to sabotage each other. Germans being as fond of duels as they are, I am glad it went that way, but not surprised; Wolfram has never seemed hot headed. He is, sadly, handsome and gentlemanly, whereas I am short and loud, so I fear he has the advantage.<br /> <br /> Meeting with Jamal completed. He said the golems sometimes appear to affect the course of history, and more powerful forces than himself or Gaspard were at work. He recommended proceeding carefully as someone might try to manipulate us into changing history.<br /> <br /> Ha! Lizette \u00c9toile is already a woman who changes history!<br /> <br /> <br /> 8th May 1920<br /> <br /> It looks like Tatiana will be adding us to a \u201cpack\u201d which is meaningful from a Werewolf perspective. We are looking at possibly setting up a group residence where we can work together. I hope for something close to Paris.<br /> <br /> Wrote to Christina. She will get it when she returns to Vienna. Depending on how good she is at reading between the lines, she my find the contents rather exciting\u2026.<br /> <br /> My love life is, I have decided, a bit dull. I should do something about it. Maybe after everyone decides where to set up.<br /> <br /> Assuming I don\u2019t get distracted by the tank.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session IV</i><br /> <br /> So victory, and stuff!<br /> <br /> Ewan is a Psychopomp Angel, while Gerta was a Destroyer, her \u201cDaughter\u201d a Cultist, and Suzy a Psychopomp Saboteur Demon. The disguise stuff was part of her Cover. Gloria is just a Psychic.<br /> <br /> For her part Lizette is far less talented with a hammer than Chainsaw, but it is silent and non lethal, which made losing the specialty and fighting finesse worth it to her, given she could boost her skill with Artifice. She avoided taking lighting damage because she was using a weapon. Was kind of sad Alla did not get into that throwdown, being all but immune to the Electricity.<br /> <br /> Tatiana took most of her health as aggravated damage from Gerta. This left her being repeated KO\u2019d every time she hit Suzy because of her Demonic Form powers. Gerta was not quite killed by Lizette\u2019s bomb but was well into her aggravated wounds and unconscious. Tatiana threw herself off the train to deal with her death rage away from the people aboard.<br /> <br /> Afterward, there was a break in game of well over a month and a half. The next part begins June 21st of 1920 in Vienna and concerns Christina Esterh\u00e1zy and her amulet, among other things. That story will not be about GMC stuff...but soime Vampire and Werewolf stuff at least. This coming \u201coff week\u201d Friday will have downtime journals; we have one (Tatiana) currently, and another player has threatened to have one as well.<br /> <br /> Will see you in a few days. Comments and Questions welcome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-30-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T23:08:58-07:00","id":542304,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week for Golden Eagle, but seems a good time to put up some journals covering what people are getting up to during the downtime. We more or less wrapped the last story at May 7th, 1920 and start the new one June 21st, 1920, so a month and a couple weeks past. Some players did downtime journals to cover character activities during this time, so here we go. These are short ficts not covering in game activity, except Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s discusses the previous storyline.<br /> <br /> <i>Downtime I<br /> </i><br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 15 May 1920<br /> <br /> Reznik got another job the other day. I completed it last night. The man was not a good person. During the war he profited by conning people out of hard earned money and left families homeless or destitute for no other reason other than greed. He tried to run. They all try. He did not succeed. I tracked him as a wolf through the woods. He thought that by hiding in the hills I would be unable to find him. I will give him credit, he knew the woods well. He may have eluded someone else, but not me. My spirit companion urged me to just tear the man\u2019s throat out. I won\u2019t say I wasn\u2019t tempted, but Reznik\u2019s kills have to be distinguishable from Marek\u2019s. If my employer should see the state of the corpse, as is sometimes insisted, then he\u2019d wonder at the wounds. I did want this kill to be a little more personal, so I used my knife to cut his throat. Not as satisfying, but effective nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder at my choice of tribe. You would think I should be one of the Iron Masters since they hunt man, but that is Reznik\u2019s favored prey and I try to keep him separate from myself. I created Reznik as a way to keep my more illicit activities separate from myself so they cannot be traced back to me or mine. This was all before I became Uratha though. So now my favored prey are troublesome spirits. I have not had as much opportunity of late to pursue that but I will make time. I did come across a spirit of death while searching for an appropriate totem spirit. The death spirit was haunting, for lack of a better word, a small town in Russia. I\u2019m assuming the spirit was created during the war and followed someone home. There had been a rash of people getting angry and giving into their rage over small quarrels. I will admit it was satisfying to see the look on its face when it went insubstantial and I hit him anyway. He tried to run too, but I made my next attack count and he didn\u2019t get far.<br /> <br /> <br /> 30 May 1920<br /> <br /> I found a spirit willing to be our totem. She is a spirit of protection which boded well. She seemed interested in my offer and was curious to meet the others. I could not introduce her to everyone, but she at least insisted on meeting Tatiana. I left a message for Tatiana at our territory in France and she met up with us shortly after. I believe the spirit was suitably impressed with her. Ochran\u0144y, as I\u2019ve taken to calling the spirit, can see to the heart of a person and deemed the both of us worthy. Tatiana and I both have family that we keep safe, no matter the means. I think Ochran\u0144y appreciated that. So she agreed to be our totem on a provisional basis until she meets the others. I think she\u2019ll stay though. She seemed quite amused by Tatiana and my spirit companions, and by my naming of her. She laughed at me when I asked if I could call her Ochran\u0144y, since it is the Czech word for protective, but she agreed since the non-Uratha members of our pack cannot pronounce First Tongue. As for Tatiana\u2019s spirit companion, she calls hers volchonok (wolf cub) which is apt. I call mine D\u0115de\u010dek (grandfather). D\u0115de\u010dek has seen Volchonok and seems amused by his antics as well. But then wolf pups are playful by nature.<br /> <br /> The next time we get together as a pack we will do the ritual to bind Ochran\u0144y to us. I\u2019ve never done this myself, but I learned how to do it from Alexej. I just need to make sure that the bargain is fair to the spirit and to us and then actually bind it. I hope none of the others have a problem with blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> 5 June 1920<br /> <br /> Got another job for Reznik. This one is for a couple. A man and his wife have been seemingly generous in their community and have taken in several war orphans to live on their farm. It was suspected that not all was right there, and it was confirmed not long ago that they beat the children and force them to work the farm. There are about a dozen children ranging in age from 5 years to 15 years. I\u2019m not sure what made them think that this was a good idea. Maybe they wanted free labor to work the farm and figured kids would be the way to go. Most of the children are older, but there are a couple young ones too. The couple, the Deuderman\u2019s fled once it was discovered by the authorities what was going on at the farm. I was in the town making a delivery, which was my cover so I could investigate. Early in the day I arranged to go near the farm so I could see the children. I saw firsthand their injuries and living conditions. <br /> <br /> Late in the evening I went back by the farm house, but this time to get a scent to track the famer and his wife by. I thought everyone was asleep as all the lights were off, so I went in Dalu form. One little boy was awake and saw me. He was quiet for a moment but did not seem frightened. He had a black eye and some other bruises showing on his arms. He asked if I was going to find the Deuderman\u2019s. I said yes. He then asked if I was going to kill them. I saw no reason to lie to the child, so I said yes. He said, \u201cgood.\u201d I smiled. He asked who I was and I told that I was a spirit who protected little children from evil people. He asked why I did not help him when his parents were killed. That was harder to answer. I told him that because of the war there were so many children to help that I can\u2019t get to everyone. He seemed to accept that answer. He then asked if our meeting should be kept secret. I told him that some people were afraid of my kind, so it would be best to not mention anything. He smiled and said that he understood. He wished me good luck and I left.<br /> <br /> Throughout the whole conversation with the boy something was trying to make itself known. I figured it out right before I left. He kid is wolf-blooded. I do not know if he\u2019ll become Uratha one day, but he is a child of the wolf or moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7 June 1920<br /> <br /> I found the Deuderman\u2019s. They were not hard to track. The husband sweat like a pig and didn\u2019t smell much better. The woman was sick I think, and had a very distinct scent. Easy to track. When I found them they begged and pleaded. They even offered me money. I had to laugh at that. All of my contracts as Reznik are paid, but I would have done this one for free. My laugh was perhaps not the most comforting sound they heard so the husband pulled out a gun. I shifted form and attacked. Before I could finish him off the husband got a couple good shots in, but by that point it didn\u2019t matter. I used the extra energy to heal the wounds faster, which again, was not a comforting sight. At least not for the wife. She ran. I found her. Turns out she had a gun too. She managed to get a shot off. It was a good one, but not good enough. The bullet grazed my forehead. Things were blurred for a moment, but I recovered fast enough. She didn\u2019t make it two steps after that. When I went back to collect my payment for the job I told Hans that I left the bodies in the woods for the wolves. He seemed satisfied. I know I was.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 June 1920<br /> <br /> I have been using my connections as a courier to find homes for the children that I orphaned once again. Not that they minded their keepers suddenly disappearing, but they did need homes. I told the authorities in the town that I heard what happened and wanted to do my civic duty to help. Not a complete lie, but I\u2019m not doing this for any civic duty. I\u2019m doing this because they are children and while not necessarily helpless, they nonetheless need help. I am in a position to do so.<br /> <br /> I also plan on heading home to visit father and Andel. I can see if anyone at home would like to adopt a child. There are one or two Czech children, a few German, a couple Russian. Quite the mix. I didn\u2019t ask how the farmer and his wife gathered children from all over, but I suppose if they were sent away from home to get away from the war that might account for some of it.<br /> <br /> I will head home tonight. I think I will make good time. I plan to run for a good bit of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 13 June 1920<br /> <br /> I managed to make good time getting home. I was not all that far to begin with, but getting a ride from one of Han\u2019s men also helped. They drove me as far as the border to Czechoslovakia and I ran the rest of the way. I spent the evening catching up with Andel and father, even cousin Josef. Andel shared with me the good news that he was recently married to his sweetheart Lenka. I knew that he\u2019d been courting her, but hadn\u2019t given her much thought. She was not family and could have been a passing fling. But apparently it was not a temporary infatuation. They were married last week. Andel sent me a letter, but it will not have arrived at my mail location yet. I congratulated the happy couple and hugged the bride. I also got her scent, so I will be able to track her if needs be. She is now family and if she is ever in trouble I want to be able to find her. She did not notice, which is for the best.<br /> <br /> We talked into the night and I told my family about the farmer and his wife abusing adoped children. I mentioned that I had agreed to help them find homes and that some of the children where Czech. I thought they should come home. Lenka became quite animated when I mentioned this. She confided in us that her sister and husband had been trying for some time to have children but were unable to. They desperately wanted to have kids. There were two children that I knew for sure were Czech. Kv\u0115ta and Dominik. Kv\u0115ta is 5 years old, Dominik is 12. I told Lenka that I wanted to meet her sister and her sister\u2019s husband before I gave them any further information. She agreed and told me that she thought what I was doing was sweet. I answered that they were children and needed help. I did not mention that I would do nothing of the sort for adults. <br /> <br /> <br /> 14 June 1920<br /> <br /> I met Denisa and Erik today. They seemed like decent people. They were a bit curious as to how I became involved in the whole situation. I explained that I\u2019m a courier and had made a delivery to the town that the farm was located in. I said that I happened to be there when one of the children, a little girl of 8, managed to sneak out and get to town. I saw the girl run to the police station and overhead some of what was going on. There is no way she can verify that, so the lie was easy to spin. I said that other party\u2019s took care of the farmer and his wife and I offered to help with the children since I have connections in several countries. Some of that was true. The last part anyway. I gave them the contact information for the town\u2019s police so Denisa and Erik can contact them about meeting the kids. Hopefully something good will come of all this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Tatiana slunk around the edges of the small tract of land, checking that the perimeter was secure and that she hadn\u2019t been followed. When both had been established to her satisfaction she returned to her human form and approached the house via the path, singing loudly and off-key.<br /> <br /> Two missiles in the shape of young boys launched themselves at the Uratha, yelling \u201cMama, mama, it\u2019s Tanya, Tanya is here!\u201d Their mother came to the door and leaned against its frame, smiling slightly as she watched Tatiana gather them up, tossing each one into the air before gathering them up, one in each arm.<br /> <br /> Tatiana kissed them both on the top of their heads. \u201cHello boys. Have you been good, while I was away?\u201d<br /> <br /> Pyotr, the older boy, nodded and the younger boy, Aleksandr, gave an enthusiastic \u201cYes!\u201d, smiling widely and only giving a short glance to the pack that presents came from.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould your mother say this also?\u201d<br /> <br /> They both looked sheepish. The younger one looked back at his mother, then his brother, then his aunt. The older one looked anywhere but those places. Their mother looked amused.<br /> <br /> Tatiana set them both down and knelt to be at their eye level. \u201cListen well boys - you are young, and failure is how we learn. If we were born knowing what to do always, then being a youngling would be exceedingly boring. But it is not alright to lie about it. Yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> They nodded gravely. \u201cYes. We did try to be good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were mostly good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat I believe.\u201d Tatiana tousled their hair and slung her pack off her back. Rifling through it, she found a pair of sweets and a bag of marbles. \u201cTo share,\u201d she warned.<br /> <br /> They ran off, tussling a little over who got which sweet. Tatiana stood up, putting her pack over one shoulder, and strode towards the woman in the doorway.<br /> <br /> Elena gave an exasperated sigh. \u201cTanya, they have not had dinner yet. You will ruin their appetite.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a dismissive noise. \u201cNonsense. They are growing boys, there is no end to their appetite. They will run themselves hungry again in moments. I have other gifts - a book and a tin horse - for when it is a quieter time. A gift for you as well.\u201d She glanced around before she moved in close and kissed her deeply.<br /> <br /> \u201cA gift for me, or for you?\u201d A loving smile took the sting out of her words. She pulled away from the embrace. \u201cIt is a time until dinner. You can chop more wood, until then. I was going to ask Anton to help, but since you are here, you can do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnton, eh? You would ask Anton over to your house to chop wood for you, huh? Well then. I will leave you a stack to fill your yard because that,\u201d she drew a finger down the side of Elena\u2019s face, \u201cwill not happen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana had been running all day but still managed to make the wood chopping look easy. She glanced up frequently to smile at the kitchen window she knew Elena was watching from. Eventually the woman of the house took pity on her, and beckoned her inside. Elena handed her a glass of water, but then put a hand on her chest as she tried to come into the house. \u201cWash first. You want to set a good example for the boys, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana gave the smaller woman a long suffering look, but went to wash up. The boys were paragons of manners and full of stories for their often absent aunt. After dinner she helped them with their chores, and presented their other gifts, agreeing to read them some from the book before bed.<br /> <br /> Once the children were asleep, Tatiana pounced on Elena and carried her off the her room. They made love quickly and hungrily, then again slowly, rediscovering each other and every aspect of each other\u2019s bodies. After, Elena stretched out against her lover\u2019s strong frame and Tatiana drew lazy circles around her lover\u2019s navel.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose you will be leaving in the morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana\u2019s hand stopped for a moment. \u201cI... have a few days, if you do not mind me staying.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTruly?\u201d Elena turned around to search the other woman\u2019s face. \u201cI never mind you being here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana gave her a fierce smile and kissed her forehead. \u201cGood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe boys would like it if you were here more often.\u201d A pause. \u201cAs would I.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could not support you properly, if I were stayed here. And it would not be safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d Elena sighed and turned around again, settling against Tatiana.<br /> <br /> Tatiana was silent for a moment, resting her chin on Elena\u2019s head. \u201cElena, I...\u201d She stopped. \u201cIt is...\u201d She took a deep breath and let it out noisily, ruffling Elena\u2019s hair. \u201cThe Whites are losing. The Bolshevik's power grows stronger every day, and there is nothing I can do to stop it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena responded without conviction. \u201cThen stop fighting. If it is what is to be, let it. There are other things to live for, other people...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... yes. I said this because... this job I took last. It was not for the Whites, or even against the Bolsheviks. It was for money. A lot of money. So much that there would be enough for you and the boys, and it could also be used to buy supplies and weapons. But giving it to the Whites would be pouring grain into a silo infested with mice, useless. So it is all for you.\u201d Elena moved to speak and Tatiana raised a finger to her lips. \u201cThat is all still not important. The people I worked with, they are good people. We made a good team. There are other things we can do, jobs along the same lines, personal concerns, a patron. It is good work and will provide plenty for all of us, whatever you need, even schooling for the boys.\u201d<br /> <br /> They lay in silence for awhile, before Elena spoke again. \u201cThat sounds wonderful, I suppose. But... where is the other shoe? Why is this so difficult for you to say?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana ran her hands over Elena\u2019s hips. \u201cThey... they wish to work out of France, near Paris. With things being as they are, I could not argue for Russia.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstandable. And?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd... would you, you and the boys, could you come with me? This time, or next time? There is a village, near where I will live. I will not be there always, but often, and France has beautiful countryside. And it will be safer.\u201d Tatiana was still, waiting.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you expect us to uproot and and leave everything behind, to be with you?\u201d Elena asked drily.<br /> <br /> \u201c...yes.\u201d Tatiana\u2019s shoulders slumped slightly. \u201cIt is too much to ask. I am sorry. I will be able to visit more often, still, and...\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena stopped her with a kiss. \u201cOf course we will come with you. Family is more important than places and things, and you are family.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana stayed a week. On the morning she left, she stopped Elena before they left her room. With two fingers under the shorter woman\u2019s chin, Tatiana tilted Elena\u2019s head up and kissed her. Tatiana smiled cockily. \u201cThat is what you want, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d Elena\u2019s smile was slight, but no less loving.<br /> <br /> \u201cI will be back in,\u201d Tatiana calculated in her head a moment, \u201ca month, it should be. Everything will be set.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. We will be waiting.\u201d Tatiana kissed her again and Elena laughed slightly and pushed her towards the door.\u201d Go! Leave quickly and return to us the sooner.\u201d<br /> <br /> The boys were waiting just outside the house. Aleksandr wailed and latched onto Tatiana\u2019s leg when he saw her pack and the older one pouted and crossed his arms. \u201cYou\u2019re leaving again?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly for a short time, Pyotr. Sasha, come now.\u201d She tried to peel Aleksandr from her legs without wrenching his arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou say that every time and then you\u2019re gone forever. You stayed for so long, I thought you were home for good.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana looked at Elena, who shrugged and nodded. She finally got the small boy away from her legs and picked him , settling him on her hip as she knelt down next to Pyotr. \u201cIt will be a month until the next time I am here, and then you three will come to live very near me. But I must leave now, to prepare a place.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pyotr looked at her, eyes wide and Aleksandr spoke for them, his wailing forgotten. \u201cReally?\u201d She nodded. \u201cReally really?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReally truly. Now, you two be good, and help your mother prepare.\u201d Aleksandr held tight to her neck, only letting go when she reached her full height, landing with an \u2018oof\u2019.<br /> <br /> He ran towards his mother. \u201cMama, mama, how can I help?\u201d Elena picked up the reaching Aleksandr and held her hand out for Pyotr.<br /> <br /> \u201cGoodbye Tanya. Travel safely, and think of us often.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGoodbye boys. Goodbye Elena. Take good care of my brother\u2019s sons and I will return soon.\u201d Their eyes said more, but Tatiana\u2019s gaze lingered for only a moment before she turned and trudged off towards Paris.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> May 1920<br /> <br /> Paris had many opportunities for a Darkling with political curiosities and a very particular set of skills. The continued Peace Conference was exciting for Dacian to slip into and also served to help finalize his understanding of the French language.<br /> <br /> In late May, Alexander of Greece, the so called \u201cPuppet King\u201d and his wife were found out to be in Paris. Dacian couldn\u2019t resist the temptation to test his skills yet again. The king was a handsome man in his mid-twenties and Aspasia his loving wife. That the regent of Greece had married a commoner was a scandal for most, but Dacian was intrigued. The dinner party Dacian invited himself to proved to be a delightful evening. Neither of his hosts could place why the Romanian was in attendance, but it was later agreed that his presence was enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Such were the ways the Darkling spent his time while Alla, his vampire companion closed a deal on acquiring Ch\u00e2teau de Chantilly. It was an enjoyable way to hone and increase his skills with his Contracts of Smoke and Darkness. He was also able to learn a useful Goblin contract to defend against future deceptions.<br /> <br /> June 1920<br /> <br /> With an entire castle and grounds to explore, Dacian was not able to travel to Versailles to witness the signing of the Treaty of Trianon, but quietly applauded the sudden expansion of Romanian territories. Given that his French was now passable, Dacian began learning Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s native Irish while still perfecting his German. Through conversations with Wolfram and various German treaty delegations, this was coming along, but still not acceptable by Dacian\u2019s standards.<br /> <br /> When Wolfram received a call from Lady Esterh\u00e1zy, Dacian was both please for his German companion and disappointed for Lizette. Though that was found to be unnecessary as Christina called to request both of their assistance. Because they were a motley, a pack, a family; the rest of the Cabal of the Golden Eagle immediately agreed to travel to Vienna as well.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> My Dear Janos,<br /> <br /> It has been too long, my friend! My travels are keeping me away from your lovely village, but I think of it fondly. While I have not gained the success I once had on the stage, I am on my way. It keeps me very busy, but that is what I want. It is such a delight to sing for others and see their faces alight with joy and hope. It does my heart good and keeps me from focusing on the life my fetch stole from me. I heard she left the stage to marry an English nobleman! How appalling! Enough unpleasantness though - I write to tell you about my most recent invitation.<br /> <br /> I was in Florence when I was contacted by an agent of a wealthy merchant in Milan that wished for me to perform at his home for a small house party. When I arrived it was a great surprise to see one of our own - a lovely green skinned woman of tiny stature. She hails from France and is quite enchanting with her delight at creating the most imaginative tools of destruction - a flaming chainsaw ... who would ever consider such a thing? Apparently dear Lizette. But she is also capable of creating great beauty. She designed and constructed the most lovely music box for me. It is an exquisite gift - I quite treasure it.<br /> <br /> But I'm going off on a tangent aren't I? I am lucky you are used to my rambles and probably expect them by now. <br /> <br /> The house party was more like a business meeting and our host was most interested in the services the other guests brought to the table. He wanted us - yes, me included! - to acquire a device of curious origin. Apparently through his research he found that I and the other guests had a connection to the device and would be able to utilize it's intriguing capabilities - though truly I do not wish to test this theory.<br /> <br /> We entered into a pact - if we would acquire the device and allow him to study it if it were ever used then we could have it. And he promised as part of the bargain to never seek to harm us - that is an important detail as during our adventure I found evidence that made me believe he played us false. My ire was cooled when we returned successful &amp; our pact still intact. I'm being intentionally vague - a fact I know will annoy you to know end, but it is for our safety I not get too specific about our adventure. I should tell you all about my new motley though!<br /> <br /> I have already shared a little about Lizette, a very sweet woman who has her eye focused on a coolly beautiful woman from Vienna. Her interest for this woman is shared by another of our motley, Wolfram. He isn't one of the Lost however, he is something different, a Geist, which is something I'm not entirely certain I understand. But he is a very kind man, and quick to lend aid when requested. I quite like him and hope he and Lizette can come to some arrangement regarding their Viennese woman. <br /> <br /> Dacian is one of the Lost, a darkling, and more than a little charming. He is, as one of the others so bluntly states, a thief, and quite a good one I gather. But he also strikes me as a very honorable man. I have nothing to fear from him, though I have yet to spend much time with him so I do not know how I can help him achieve his desires. No I have not tried to determine the desires of my motley yet. It seemed rude to invade their privacy like that upon our first meeting. I should dig a bit deeper though - I would like to make them happy if at all possible.<br /> <br /> Though I may not try very hard with Fenric. It is uncharitable of me, but he makes me somewhat nervous...as if I could wake one morning and find him watching me. Fenric is the manservant for Alla, a Russian noblewoman that is also a showman...as well as a vampire. I'm not entirely certain how she is able to hide her nature, though I'm sure Fenric takes care of many details so she doesn't risk exposure. <br /> <br /> That leaves the last two members of our motley and I must admit I am drawn to them. They fascinate me as they are werewolves! Tatiana is a rough and tumble sort of girl, she does like a good dust-up. Oh if she could have met my brothers in their youth...such a friendship they would have had! She seems like the loyal sort, I believe she may be devoted to me already in her own way. She was very intent on doing that which would make me happy on our adventure. Marek is the final member of our motley and oh, Janos, he - like Dacian - is quite fit! Blond hair - tousled just so - light eyes...yes, he is the light while Dacian is the dark and I do so enjoy looking at the both of them!<br /> <br /> Lizette asked me if I fancied anyone in our group while we traveled and I am ashamed to say I could not answer. I enjoy looking at them all (except Fenric, bless him) but I have not yet decided if I would like more than just looking. Sometimes that is enough is it not? Perhaps I will change my mind once I know what they desire.<br /> <br /> With our adventure behind us, we've chosen to stay together and set up a sort of freehold of our own near Paris. I have been invited to perform in a few venues in the city and I can't help but be delighted. This will be a good place for us, I am certain. But before we truly settle in we have responsibilities. Wolfram &amp; Lizette\u2019s Viennese beauty has asked them for assistance and of course we are all going to help in any way we can. And of course I have a couple of bookings for while we are there - how could I not? It's Vienna!<br /> <br /> I shall write again as soon as I can. Do tell me how things fare in your village, I miss you dearly my friend!<br /> <br /> Sith agus Sl\u00e1inte 'bha!<br /> Dearbh\u00e1il<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <u><br /> Artifact report to The Holy Order of the Third Hour: The Golden Eagle</u><br /> <br /> For: Jean-Marc of the Scales<br /> <br /> From: Lizette \u00c9toile, Knight of the Third Hour of the Leaden Mirror<br /> <br /> Access Level: \u201cIf you try and touch it you will draw back a stump. If anything happens to make it disappear I\u2019ll cut you in half with a chainsaw before I even start looking for it\u201d<br /> <br /> Report: The Golden Eagle is an artifact of unknown origin. The physical thing appears to be about 35 centimeters tall, weighs 35 kilograms, and appears to be made of gold and brass. It has hinges well hidden along the left side, and can be opened right to left, revealing seven small chambers on the inside, and a network of gears made of brass, gold, silver, copper, and yet unidentified metals.<br /> <br /> The effects of the Golden Eagle are alleged to be immortality, aging suppression, and the ability to return from the dead, if hair and blood of a subject are placed in one of the small compartments on the inside. These effects are unproven. It registers as magical and non-hidden to Kenning.<br /> <br /> Does not confer immunity to damage. Respiration, Food, and Water are still required while connected.<br /> <br /> How it works is yet to be determined. Copper wires link all seven compartments, and the gears turn in perpetual motion. It has no apparent power source. It has no Mien, and limited testing suggests it is not from the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Potentially connected to it are three Biomechanical beings, one possessed it, one tried to steal it, and one tried to kill us for investigating. Remains of the one who tried to steal it have been turned over to the Order for study. According to an advisor, one Jamal Ruhadze, they come from an unseen force directing the course of history. The one trying to steal it is apparently a rogue agent. I lack any concrete information, but I can report they have some shapeshifting abilities as well as the ability to produce weapons seemingly from nowhere, and create an electrical current that forms a defensive barrier. Also, that hurts like a fiend when it shocks you.<br /> <br /> Recommendation: Further testing is ongoing. Will report when effects have been observed. Several subjects, of the Kind and otherwise are connected.<br /> <br /> Order Commentary: Goddamn Gremlins. Maybe we can find it after she blows herself up.<br /> <br /> <i>End Downtime I</i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal of commentary needed.<br /> <br /> The PCs decided to set up in a Ch\u00e2teau outside Paris in Chantilly, after looking over a number of options. They will of course be cut off from it over a period late game, but are aware of this OOC. Hypothetically the next storyline, which takes place in Paris, will feature the location more.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian both referenced the start of the next story, which takes place in Vienna and concerns some of the NPCs met on the train. Nothing in that story will be God-Machine oriented; I have to change it up every so often, you know. And we will have those journals in just a week; I have Tatiana and Lizette already.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T00:24:52-07:00","id":542346,"title":"","content":"I know she loved her brother, but was his death a relief on some level then?<br /> <br /> Not that she wouldn't kill you on the spot for suggesting it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T00:46:44-07:00","id":543597,"title":"","content":"It is true - directly or indirectly because of her brother's death, Tatiana has everything she's ever really wanted - the love of her life and, with two kids that might as well be her own, both by blood and raising, a family, not to mention a purpose and focus for her life and temper. She's not unaware of the idea either - her displaced guilt is no small part of her rage against the Bolsheviks.<br /> <br /> But yes, she would eviscerate almost anyone who brought up the fact that she benefited from his death in her presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1471-levinserra","name":"LevinSerra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1471_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T22:26:17-07:00","id":552556,"title":"","content":"We began a new story last time. It is late June in Vienna, 1920, and our group has come at the request of one of the NPCs from the train. A necklace has been stolen, but there are many complications. Let\u2019s check on our group and what they have determined.\\<br /> <br /> <i>Session V</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 21 June 1920<br /> <br /> Things seem to get more interesting when we come together as a pack. A few days ago Wolfram and Lizette contacted the rest of us. Apparently, Christina, the girl they are both sweet on, has been robbed of a valuable necklace. Normally I wouldn\u2019t have thought this worth our time, but Wolfram says that the amulet that is missing has some powerful dark magic on it and could be dangerous. So, we agreed to meet up and go to Vienna. To draw less attention to ourselves we arrived in pairs, as if we were couples. Wolfram arrived with Lizette, presumably with her as his daughter. She does child impersonations rather well. Tatiana arrived with Dacian. Alla arrived with Fenric and I arrived with Dearbhail. I looked at the register as she wrote her name and discovered the correct spelling. Must be an Irish thing, because what she wrote is not how her name is pronounced. At least I am spelling it correctly now.<br /> <br /> After we checked in Tatiana and I explained to the rest of the pack about the difference between the Uratha and the Pure. There are two Pure tribes that have a good measure of power in this city. They are the Ivory Claws and the Fire Touched. We know that the leader of the Ivory Claws is a man named Wolfgang Von Eggenberg. From the rumors that we\u2019ve heard he looks to be in his late 20\u2019s or early 30\u2019s but is actually over 90 years old. Tatiana said something about it might be fun to piss on peoples shoes while we\u2019re in town. I think she wanted to start a fight with the Pure. I warned her that if we did that, it would lead to a spectacular yet very short fight with Wolfgang. The man has got to be incredibly powerful, and has who knows how many men supporting him. It would be foolish to court such disaster. I believe I got my point across though. No pissing on anyone\u2019s shoes.<br /> <br /> <br /> 23 June 1920<br /> <br /> Tonight was the night that we planned to talk to Christina. Before we did that however, Tatiana and I contacted Krieger, the leader of the Uratha in town and expressed an interest in introducing ourselves. It is after all his territory, it would not be proper to enter unannounced. So, we met him at a caf\u00e9 in town. He seemed to be a rather straightforward man, which I can appreciate. He did warn us to stay away from a certain museum for the near future as there was going to be a confrontation there soon. Apparently there is a locus inside the building and Krieger wants the place for the Uratha, but currently it is the Pure that have control of it. Krieger\u2019s plan is to take the Museum by force and take control of the locus. It is not likely that they will hold the place for long, but hopefully it will be for long enough to accomplish what they want to do. There may also be something we can help them with later if we are still in town. We told him that we were in town to help a friend, and did not have a set date that we\u2019d be leaving.<br /> <br /> Krieger was familiar with Christina, and more importantly one of the young ladies suitors. Apparently there is a Pure named Gunnar Hoenburg that has been courting Christina. This only matters so much, but it could lead to possible confrontation on our part with the Pure. We were warned that even some of the spirits in town support the Pure and report anything they see to their allies. I will admit that the spirits being on the side of the enemy poses some possible problems. We will need to be careful and pay close attention to our surroundings and everything in them.<br /> <br /> Krieger also warned us to stay away from Wolfgang Von Eggenberg. I was right in my assumption that the man is very dangerous and a noteworthy foe. It did not sound like we would come away from a confrontation with him as the victors. It was good to get confirmation.<br /> <br /> We met Christina at her house for dinner and to investigate the theft of her necklace. She explained that her family had fallen on hard times financially and her brother was trying to make some money to pay off debts. He acquired the necklace that has gone missing, presumably with the intent on selling it for a good bit of money. Unfortunately Christina made the mistake of wearing the necklace to a party and it was gone the next day. Someone spotted it and decided it should be theirs. <br /> <br /> Supposedly the necklace was secured in a locked box in a locked room. Marlene, Christina\u2019s Lady\u2019s companion, has the only key and it was not taken. Normally Marlene would be a suspect, but after talking to her we don\u2019t think she had anything to do with it. Dacian also used a fae ability to see if the ladies were lying when we asked them about the theft. The only lie that he found was when Marlene said that she had not worn the necklace.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t think either of the young ladies want that necklace far from them at all. They both seemed to get this kind of glazed look in their eyes when they spoke of the necklace. Wolfram said that the necklace is magical, so it is likely having some sort of influence over the young ladies. They seem very keen on keeping the necklace. If it is found Christina\u2019s brother is going to have a hard time selling it given how much his sister seems tied to it.<br /> <br /> Christina took us to take a look at the box where the necklace had been kept. There were no marks on the door or the lock on the box to indicate that the locks had been picked. If they were picked, it was done by someone with very good tools and very good skill. There may be some supernatural abilities that would allow someone to steal things easier, but we weren\u2019t sure if such a thing was used or not. The abilities that Dacian knows about don\u2019t leave a trace behind. Whoever it was did not have a way to cover their scent though, so that eliminates a fae, or at least tells us that he does not have the same abilities that Dacian does. <br /> <br /> One idea that was suggested was that someone had made a copy of the key and left the original behind. To do that would take time, so it is not likely that the thief would have time to take a mold of the key, make a copy, then steal the necklace.<br /> <br /> After we investigated the room and the box all we could in front of witnesses we asked if we could speak in private. Christina escorted us to the garden. We discussed our ideas and what we needed to do next. Tatiana and I suggested that we use our Uratha abilities to see if we can find a scent trail for the thief and either track them or eliminate suspects. Lizette also told us that she had revealed her fae form to Christina some time back. She gave permission for Christina to tell Marlene, which explains the smirks and curious looks the young lady was giving Lizette when we first arrived.<br /> <br /> We returned to the house and the others distracted Christina and Marlene, Tatiana and I went back to the room where the necklace had been, changed forms and continued our investigation. We caught the scents of Christina, Marlene, some other household staff and one stranger. We could tell right off that the stranger was not a werewolf, so it was likely not Gunnar, though the man had expressed an interest in the necklace when he saw it. We tracked the scent down the hallway to Christina\u2019s room, then Marlene\u2019s then back down the hallway to the jewelry room. <br /> <br /> So, we know who is not the thief, but are no closer to determining who is the thief. Right now our plan is to have Lizette make a replica of the necklace to fool the brother, and anyone else, from knowing that it is missing. The plan is also to have Lizette handle the box that the necklace was kept in and use one of her fae abilities to see if she can get an image of the amulet itself and perhaps the one that took it. The later would be a great boon in our favor. Our resident tinkerer seems to be rather talented so I\u2019m sure what she comes up with will be a suitable replacement for our missing evil amulet.<br /> <br /> Like I mentioned before, interesting things happen when the pack is together. I suppose the situation with the Pure would be happening in this city regardless of our presence, but it is interesting that it is tied in some small way to the missing necklace. There also happens to be something big going on very soon involving both tribes of Pure in the area, the Ivory Claws and the Fire Touched. We do not have much information on the Fire Touched as of yet, but we do know who the leader of the Ivory Claws is, and to avoid him if at all possible. I will relate more as soon as I know more. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Ah, volchonok. It is good to see you survived the journey. Have the Pure bothered you yet?<br /> <br /> No, I have not changed my human fur to hide from the Pure. The humans would not care for my Russian uniform, here in Vienna.<br /> <br /> Since when do you care so about human things? It is because many people lost many things in the war, and people wearing a Russian uniform did some of the taking from these here.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is foolish. Are you nervous, volchonok, that with a pack of many humans and my Elena soon to be nearby, that I will forget how foolish human things can be? Do you search for reasons for me to turn from them?<br /> <br /> A change of subject, eh? Very well volchonok. Marek and I have met with the Hunter, Krieger, it is true. We have not encountered any of the Pure. This is good. Marek has forbidden me from pissing on their shoes.<br /> <br /> Well, would you like it is I marked your paws as my territory?<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think so. The others worry too much over the Pure. So long as we are not stupid, we will be fine and they will be no danger. Even if we are a little stupid, they will be distracted, Krieger says. Something about a museum.<br /> <br /> A museum is a human thing, a building full of old things, and pretty things. Boring.<br /> <br /> No, not pretty things like our songbird. Pretty like pictures, or statues.<br /> <br /> I did say it was boring. Listen, you volchonok - stay away from the Pure Eggenberg. That will be a glorious fight, but Marek is likely correct, a short one should it happen now. He is a powerful creature, and I do not want him making a pet of you.<br /> <br /> Oh, there will be fighting. Krieger perhaps has some task we could assist with and whoever took the necklace is unlikely to give it over willingly.<br /> <br /> The reason we are here, silly volchonok. The woman from the train that caught Lizette and Wolfram\u2019s fancy, she obtained an amulet with dark magic on it. It was supposed to restore her family\u2019s fortune.<br /> <br /> By being sold, I suppose. Not that she is inclined to, even should we find it. She and her maid are both obsessed with the thing.<br /> <br /> If we knew who took it, I would right now be threatening them until they gave it back. I do have the thief\u2019s scent, so I know who it is not - the servants, the lady, a werewolf. They are quite good at picking locks, Dacian says, with either magic or much much money. Not his magic, he says, or else I would not have been able to follow the scent back through the maid\u2019s room, then the lady\u2019s room, then to where they came into the hall.<br /> <br /> Come now volchonok. No, he is not my mate. Not everyone I den with is my mate. It is to be less conspicuous that we have such quarters. Now, Marek and our songbird might yet mate. She does enjoy looking at him.<br /> <br /> No, you are still not allowed to chase her.<br /> <br /> Because he is not a silly volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is also because he leads the pack and because a mate who is also in my pack would come between me and Elena and that will not happen.<br /> <br /> No, she will not be in my pack.<br /> <br /> Because I have said so.<br /> <br /> You think so, eh? Leave me be, if that is how silly a volchonok you are, there will be no running tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 21 June 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> We arrived in Vienna at different times due several concerns. First, a rival coalition of werewolves which collectively call themselves the Pure, are in control of the city. The Uratha are not only unwelcome but are actively hunted if exposed. What sort of egotistical dictator would lead such a pogrom against another group of their own is beyond me. However the Uratha are not ones to simply bare their throats, so to speak, and are waging a series of calculated strikes to weaken the stranglehold the Pure have over Vienna. Second and ironically, Alla\u2019s Invictus vampires are experiencing the same incursion into their domain as the Pure. A group known as the Carthians are mirroring the Uratha\u2019s tactics for what seems to be similar reasons. Both the Pure and Invictus supported and backed the nobility, which suffered significant losses in power after the war. Each were apparently surprised when the \u201cpeasants\u201d refused to return to their position of stepping stones.<br /> <br /> I admit I enjoy my expensive tastes, however I also do not burden those which begin with nothing. Coming from a minor noble family, I can say that most nobility would be hard pressed to truthfully say the same. But I am not here to judge.<br /> <br /> Finally, I brought a third concern to the attention of our cabal. If we were identified as a group by these caretakers of reality, it would perhaps be best if we were not so easily recognized in the future. The same concern was shared with the Theosophists from the train, which were conveniently based in Vienna. Dodging political infighting between both werewolves and vampires was one thing; avoiding reality golems and unseen psychics was quite another. As such, I recommended that we move in multiple smaller groups. The cabal was broken into couples so that no one was left alone and to appear as uninteresting as possible. Tatiana and I shared a room as did Alla and Fenric. Wolfram and Lizette, who disguised herself as a child, shared a room. And finally Dearbh\u00e1il and Marek were left staring at each other with some very interesting tension between them. I was disappointed that I needed no Glamour. I suspect that if this boarding strategy holds, I will not be at a loss for some time. I was actually surprised as Tatiana chose to stay with me. It was assumed by all that she and Marek would share lodging, but she would hear nothing of it.<br /> <br /> I spent an hour out of the sunlight, without my shoes, and relaxed while Tatiana stared at me strangely. Dearbh\u00e1il and I were made aware of a burlesque house called Gem\u00fctlichkeit maintained by the local Spring Court, but I decided it would be best not to learn of such delights this early in the day. Especially not when there was another meeting in the evening.<br /> <br /> 21 June 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> We are about to call upon Lady Christina Esterh\u00e1zy for dinner and more information on the assistance she requested. Dearbh\u00e1il learned that the Summer Court will assume leadership on 23 June and there will be a party of some form that evening. Marek determined that there would be a pack rite that evening as well. The conclusion of which should strengthen our personal resolve and allow us to heal wounds more quickly. To say I am excited is an understatement. I will get to witness magics of the Uratha firsthand before experiencing the effects before or possibly after enjoying the hospitality of the Summer Court. But now, we must away least Tatiana grow angry with my \u201cwasting time.\u201d<br /> <br /> 21 June 1920 - Late Night<br /> <br /> Wolfram suspected the necklace involved dark magics and based on the two individuals which have been in contact with it, so do I. But I am getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> Right away Marlena, the Lady\u2019s Maid, seemed to know something about Lizette. I was unsure of the connection, but it was definitely there. After a bit of pleasantries, Christina lost a bit of her happy demeanor and explained why we were invited. Her uncle served as an Austrian commander in the Great War. Because of the treaties and restitutions imposed, the family coffers were empty which had left them low staffed. To attempt to restore a portion of the family fortune, her brother stole a valuable piece of jewelry to sell. It was this necklace which Wolfram spotted while we were travelling together. It was quickly obvious that Christina, though sound in mind in other matters, was completely obsessed with this piece. She has no desire or intention of selling it and wants it returned before Gunter, her brother, arrives home. The situation was very simple on the surface as Marlena was the obvious thief, given the necklace was left in her care while Christina was not admiring it. But as I mentioned, it was only simple on the surface. Both the jewelry box and the key were still present and only a man named Gunnar Hohenburg had seen the necklace other than the remaining staff. Marlena openly disliked the werewolf, as he was one of two Marek had warned us about. Tatiana spoke up to voice her disapproval of him as well, a touch I believe was best left in her mind. That a member of the Pure had been within the Esterh\u00e1zy estate and seen the relic was troubling. That Gunter seemed to enjoy the idea of marrying his sister to the man was more so. As we pieced information together, I noticed that Marlena\u2019s eyes shared her Lady\u2019s obsessive gleam in reference to the necklace.<br /> <br /> I requested to observe the jewelry box and investigate with Marek and Tatiana. I found myself looking through the halls as we walked, planning how I would enter to steal such piece. Getting into the estate would be of no consequence for me. The room in which the necklace was kept however had no windows and the door locked. Secure for not having been built for such things. The jewelry box was locked when we arrived but Marlena turned to retrieve the key. With but a moment\u2019s flinch, I excused \u201cmy mistake\u201d as the box was actually open. There was no sign of tampering of any kind. The thief either had the key, used some form of magic, was a Lurker with helpful fingers for such things, or had incredibly expensive and functional lock picks. I used my Goblin Contract while interviewing everyone and found that only Marlena lied, and then only when asked if she had ever worn the necklace. Oddly, when we mentioned something of the occult in relation to Christina, Marlena forgot herself and openly mocked the idea. She believed her Lady to be ignorant of such things.The necklace had been gone for less than a week so it couldn\u2019t have gotten far, especially given the strange addiction it caused. We excused ourselves into the garden to discuss the situation.<br /> <br /> After I confirmed with our Uratha pack mates that we were unobserved, I listed the common powers for a relic of this sort to the others. Often the higher self was penalized for following the path of virtue while acts of vice richly rewarded user. Truly monstrous acts could even help the user gain greater understanding in some ability or knowledge. Physical contact seemed very unwise and the description we received from Marlena was concerning. The pendant was a smooth, black metal of unknown origin holding a large crimson gem in the center. The necklace itself was a chain made of silver, though if the pendant is of a strange metal, the chain may also be more exotic. Not that our Uratha pack mates would enjoy the more \u201cmundane\u201d effects, but it seems strange to mix the two, unless there is a magical reasoning with which I am presently unfamiliar. It is my professional opinion that such relics should be hidden away from the world until such time as I am paid to retrieve it or destroyed where it can harm no one. I believe the cabal is in agreement with at least one of those options.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 21st June 1920<br /> <br /> Problem: Christina\u2019s amulet has been stolen. Bad enough that anyone would steal from a lady like her, but this was a magic amulet, also. And making things worse is her brother wishes to sell it to help restore some of the family fortunes. The matter is complicated by the fact Christina seems to have a fixation on it. This does not make it harder to find, but adds complications when it is found.<br /> <br /> I am not a detective. I am, however, a genius. My genius can certainly help with this. If I can design a plane that flies upside down to give more room for the automatic mounted on the top-turned-bottom, I can find a piece of jewelry!<br /> <br /> The obvious suspect is Marlene Vogl, her companion. Also influenced by the Amulet, she had the key at all times to the jewelry box it was stolen from. Talking to her she seems disinclined to do so. Also, Marek and Tatiana believed they detected another scent besides hers or the servants in the room.<br /> <br /> Second suspect we worked out is Gunnar Hohemberg, suitor for Christina\u2019s hand, owner of a huge mustache, and a Werewolf. Gunnar is with a rival Court of Werewolves known as \u201cThe Pure\u201d and a member of a Tribe called the Ivory Claws. Gunnar has been in the house and commented on the amulet. However, his scent was not in the room in which it was kept, and the mystery scent was not that of a Werewolf. Given the pride of the Pure, Marek and Tatiana doubt a non-Pure would be used to remove the amulet.<br /> <br /> Given the Ivory Claws name, and connection to Nobility, I assume they are connected to elephants. I wonder if they may even have secret Wereelaphant forms. It makes sense they would disguise as Werewolves, but wolves lack Nobility, all doing their part for the pack, so Wereelephants must substitute themselves somewhere, and this seems obvious. Also, given they dislike most other Werewolves, maybe they teamed up with some who are unlikely to discover they are elephants. The name is clearly a Tell. We should examine this possibility. Perhaps bring an end to their charade.<br /> <br /> I digress. Both obvious suspects out of the way, it falls to us to fan out a bit and comb for information.<br /> <br /> A major issue keeps this from being open and shut in addition to not having a suspect, which is merely a temporary setback. Wolfram insists, and I do not doubt him, that the amulet itself is sinister in nature. It is agreed upon by us that Christina and Marlene have shown evidence of it\u2019s control, and Marlene\u2019s behavior has shown it not only has created a fixation but is altering her behavior. Well, unless she has always had sex with servants in valuables rooms, which I suspect is not the case given her continued job having as a Lady\u2019s companion. <br /> <br /> That said, since discovering I was interested in Christina, Marlene has been giving me the eye. She has done nothing inappropriate, but was very disappointed I was not staying in the house. This could be evidence she is given to playing around, evidence the amulet is still affecting her, or, of course, evidence she is aware that the French are the finest lovers on earth or evidence she is a simply sapiophile and drawn to my genius like a moth to a flame. I shall have to seek an objective answer.<br /> <br /> After all, fire is strangely attractive.<br /> <br /> What was I talking about? Ah yes. The plan. The plan of course, involves me building something, not for mayhem this time, but to make people thing the amulet is recovered. Unfortunately, jewel forgery is not my forte\u2026it seems better for, say, Dacian. However, I have a cunning plan. I\u2019ve checked my notes on the Contract of Animation, and I think if I handle the jewelry box I can get a strong vision of what is inside. I also can, perhaps, create an image of those who have touched it, including the perpetrator of the crime, perhaps.<br /> <br /> So, the plan is I will call on Lady Esterh\u00e1zy early tomorrow and ask to view the box. I can tell her truthfully I intend to use my faerie abilities to see what I can find, since she is aware of my nature. Once I have the information, I report it to the motley and set about making the duplicate. Possibly with Dacian\u2019s help.<br /> <br /> See? Genius can solve everything.<br /> <br /> Also, Mayhem.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session V</i><br /> <br /> One thing that may be difficult to follow is Alla\u2019s player pretty much played Fenric that session. The idea was Alla would join the others after nightfall but that did not actually happen.<br /> Some work was put into capturing Austria after the war. The interwar period had clashes between Communists, Fascists, and Nazis, and I wanted to set up some for that with this story. The Pure I intend to use as villains for this element and the recurring Vienna setting in particular, as the Ivory Claws and Fire Touched look to the Austrofascists as they look to maintain their hunting grounds in Vienna, and ultimately the split with the Nazi rise that pits the tribes against each other even as the Uratha make more and more headway. It seemed interesting, and gives Vienna and element of danger to our Uratha.<br /> <br /> Ironically Alla, who is Invictus, finds herself on the other side of the left/right schism as the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum work to keep out the influence of the Carthians and other Covenants to a lesser degree. The conflicts will parallel the Werewolf conflicts with the PC\u2019s faction on the opposite side of the divide<br /> <br /> Should be interesting.<br /> <br /> There was some covering of downtime and discussion of systems, so for the most part we just had the two major scenes, with Krieger and with Christina. The latter was fairly long, though, with a fair amount of discussion.<br /> <br /> I plan to have something for you next week, then journals as usual next time. Vampire masterminds, plots by the pure, and a Changeling burlesque house await next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T02:25:58-07:00","id":561731,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week, but I wanted to post some information for Golden Eagle<br /> <br /> The Below is a general breakdown of how it works. The Players have seen this information but the characters, of course, have only a vague idea.<br /> <br /> <b>The Golden Eagle</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Golden Eagle has three major effects, slowed aging, limited regeneration and resurrection.<br /> <br /> Most Characters age 1 year for every 5 while linked to the Golden Eagle. Werewolves and Changelings, who age slower anyway, only age 1 year per 10, before taking into account any other slowing aging effects. This has no effect on Vampires or Ghouls. These in frequent intimate physical contact (particularly lovers) age slightly slower, but not to the same extent.<br /> <br /> A character that loses a limb or other part such as an eye can hold it on and have it reattach, even if it normally would not be able to do so, so long as they can find whatever limb they lost. If they limb or part cannot be recovered, they can use the Golden Eagle adding to the blood sample (and spending a permanent Willpower) and grow a replacement that is human looking to normal vision, but to Angels, Demons, or those with Unseen Sense: God Machine looks to be golden and mechanical. It may also be under the control of the God-Machine\u2026.<br /> <br /> Vampires regenerate limbs anyway, but this effect does extend to their ghouls. Changelings enjoy the basic regenerative features, but the golden limbs don\u2019t seem to mesh well with them; they only remain attached for 10-Wyrd years, after which the whole process (and another Willpower) must be done again. Natural regeneration or healing powers are not stymied by the above, and function normally and can forestall the need for either effect.<br /> <br /> The Golden Eagle has the following effects if a character protected by it is killed. This does not interfere with a Sin-Eaters restorative powers in any way; a Sin-Eater can choose to raise themselves early, bypassing any negative effects from the Eagle but suffering those tied to being a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> The Golden Eagle can raise the dead, if already tied to it. The body remains dead for a time equal to 11-Integrity/Humanity/Harmony/Charity/Synergy days, then resurrects at the end of that time. The body is restored at the Golden Eagle\u2019s location or the body\u2019s, as determined (in world) by the Eagle and (out of world) by the player. It can only raise a body at it if it is currently in the world, not inside a Sin-Eater or a Demon\u2019s temporal space.<br /> <br /> Bodies raised at their current location have as much fuel points as it had when it died, and zero willpower. Bodies reformed at the eagle have 0 fuel stats and 0 willpower. Sin-Eaters raised by the Eagle who died in a way resonating with their threshold immediately gain 5 Plasm, otherwise it stays the same.<br /> <br /> A character with 8+ in their integrity stat does raise with some inspired feeling, and may roll Resolve + Composure (+Psyche, if a Sin-Eater) and gains temporary willpower equal to the result (added to 0, as they always come back with 0). This applies in Reverse to Werewolves, who only get this effect if they rise with 3 or less Harmony, not 8 or more.<br /> <br /> Characters with 6- in their integrity stat wake with horrified feelings or terror. They must roll Resolve + Composure (+Psyche, if a Sin-Eater) or lose a permanent Willpower point. Changelings must make a Clarity check and Vampires a Humanity check or risk losing a point of that as well, while Werewolves make a Harmony check against physical. Sin-Eaters do not make an Integrity check. Note for Werewolves, it is 5 or higher Harmony, not 6 or less.<br /> <br /> If Integrity is 7 (4 for Werewolves) nothing good or bad happens beyond the fuel stat loss.<br /> <br /> A given individual can remain in connection with the Golden Eagle for 33 years (total, regardless of if consecutive) with no ill effects, minus 1 year per death (not counting self-resurrections for Sin-Eaters). After that an attached a person does not regain Willpower from sleeping due to nightmares involving the impending dissolution of their soul, and Sin-Eaters gain a penalty to Vanitas use equal to the number of years (rounded up) since their protection wore off. The slowed aging and regeneration still apply, but if they die during this time a loud shriek can be heard and they do not return. After a number of years equal to their integrity stat after protection is lifted, they simply die in a large flash of light when a loud shriek. A person can disconnect themselves from the Golden Eagle at any time, even after protection has worn off.<br /> <br /> As a final note, Angels can sense the location of the Golden Eagle if nearby, and the God Machine itself is aware of it\u2019s location. So long as anyone is attached to it, Demons can sense its resonance. Note neither Angels nor Demons automatically know what they are sensing.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Overall, this was to facilitate a game going over the course of almost thirty years, and putting PCs in somewhat more action oriented situations than is typical for my games. I wanted to give some reason to shy away less from danger than is necessarily sane. None of this has come up, but you have seen the system.<br /> <br /> The investigation continues! I have journals from Tatiana and Lizette, and hope to have more. See you in a week. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T00:27:42-07:00","id":570019,"title":"","content":"Vienna. Alla visits the ancient vampires of Austria, clinging not only to lost Hapsburg glory but Rome itself. Kindred considered by themselves part of a Sect long gone and a city they had never visited. But from the decedent bloodlines or Rome plots stir. The Werewolves do a ritual to protect their packmates and the innocent and the Fae meet the Spring Queen on the final days of her 1920 reign. Wolfram moves to counter his rivals schemes for Christina. The PCs walk through the bones of the old world.<br /> <br /> No Marek this time. I\u2019d refer his usual readers to Dacian. His player should be back to journaling soon, their vacation means a break in the journaling.<br /> <i><br /> Session VI</i><br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> So, volchonok, did our rite meet with your approval? If you keep making of yourself a nuisance, Ochranny will give you a smack and you will regret it.<br /> <br /> Why were you not part of the ritual? Because you have no Kuruth to chain, and you are too much of a nuisance to walk a protective circle.<br /> <br /> Marek calmed me just fine by himself. That was the point. If he could not with his will alone, he could scarcely hope to chain my rage, and if he could chain mine, his would follow.<br /> <br /> The little one was grumpy because there was a nuisancy volchonok...<br /> <br /> I am sorry, volchonok. No, you are not a nuisance, not really. Though you should probably treat Ochranny with more respect. Still, you are my volchonok. You will hunt with me to harness the cycle?<br /> <br /> Calm volchonok, calm. Yes, you may hunt with me, and we will make it the best hunt.<br /> <br /> Heh, you are a clever volchonok. No, Lizette was not grumpy because of you, since she could not see you. She was grumpy, I believe, because it was dawn. She still got the most sleep of all of us, so I do not know what she was grumbling at.<br /> <br /> She did not go with the rest of us to the fairy place.<br /> <br /> Why yes, she did go with the ones who smell of death for their meeting. They wished to look more but not too intimidating, so I myself did not go. But she did not join us even when they did.<br /> <br /> Why would she? Oh, you know, human things.<br /> <br /> Oh no, volchonok, you would be bored.<br /> <br /> Just a room full of women pretty like our bird. That is all.<br /> <br /> No, they were merely very pretty, not exceedingly beautiful. Still, it was quite enjoyable<br /> <br /> Why do you care so what Lizette, Wolfram and Alla were doing, volchonok?<br /> <br /> Ah I see. The magical necklace is too much of a human thing to be an interesting hunt, but finding a wayward vampire child who consumes flesh interests you, eh? You know what would make this hunt easier, volchonok?<br /> <br /> I see by you ignoring me that you do. Human things. Human things would make this hunt easier. Knowing about streets and alleys and rooftops and automobiles. It is an old trail true - it would have been quite difficult. But it was impossible, here in the city. I will get better at it though. My pack quite likes places like this.<br /> <br /> Alla cannot join the hunt in the day. She is a vampire, you know this. Fenric came instead. It is he who found as close as we have to a trail, a place the quarry gets clothes. Wolfram was... looking at books, something about the necklace.<br /> <br /> No, it is good. Human thing or no, we must move quickly in regards to Christina. The Ivory Claw tried to send a letter to her brother, asking to have her as a mate. Marek and Dacian stole it, but he will only be waiting so long before he takes her anyway.<br /> <br /> Because, silly volchonok, he is Pure, and should have nothing that he wants. And because Wolfram wants her for a mate.<br /> <br /> He is very prepared to fight for her. With guns, but still. It is better to fight as one is strongest, after all. I believe Lizette will be making silver bullets even.<br /> <br /> He will not shoot me, or Marek, so why should I care?<br /> <br /> He is not Claimed, he is something else, Marek has said and he knows these things. It is not for volchonoks to decide.<br /> <br /> I too think Lizette wants Christina for a mate but... it is a human thing. Yes, a very stupid human thing, volchonok. She cannot marry her, and so cannot take her as a mate officially, or keep her away from the Pure. She was not at her house just to mate though, she used fairy magic to find what the thief looks like.<br /> <br /> Light colors. Pale skin, blonde hair, yellow eyes. Like Lizette\u2019s. It was a woman.<br /> <br /> That is all. It was magic, it cannot give a smell. It is perhaps a vampire though, or from them. One of Alla\u2019s kind told her there was one gathering artifacts of this sort.<br /> <br /> The thought occurred. I will consult with Marek, but we hunt for many things,and surely one at least is worthy of the Siskur Dah.<br /> <br /> Soon, volchonok. Tomorrow we will hunt Lady Summer and steal her power. But not today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 21 June 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> Around 8:00, Wolfram, Alla, and Fenric went to meet the Prince of Vienna. The werewolves were asked not to accompany as that could be considered a show of power, to arrive with two such bodyguards. How it could be anything other is beyond me, but that was apparently not the desire of our vampire. For their part, Marek and Tatiana were not insulted but did invite Dearbh\u00e1il and myself to join them for a mystic rite at dawn. The sheer excitement the Fairest and I shared was palatable.We changed to be more comfortable in Gem\u00fctlichkeit. Our Uratha companions would be more than welcome there, Dearbh\u00e1il and I would make sure of that. That Dearbh\u00e1il took both their hands and playfully pleaded with them may have decided things for both. We eventually found Lizette to invite her as well. She was drawing plans for what looked to be an enormous teapot modified to include weaponry. The Wizened stumbled through trying to politely turn us down as she was not a terribly social creature.<br /> <br /> She was rescued by the return of Wolfram. The irony of the situation was not lost on me, but I deferred my amusement. Alla received a second and mysterious invitation to meet another powerful vampire and wished for us to know of her whereabouts. Dearbh\u00e1il and I would have been more interested in meeting this strange vampire with Alla, had she not mentioned that she didn\u2019t think he would wish to keep us, but she was unsure. We wished her well in her meeting. However, Lizette jumped at the opportunity to help protect Alla from this strangely large vampire. Something about eating people was mentioned as more of a question? Vampires are strange.<br /> <br /> We finally arrived at Gem\u00fctlichkeit around 9:00. Unsurprisingly, the seat of the Spring Court was warm and inviting. Our werewolf companions marked their territory at a table which was out of the way and yet held a clear view of nearly all the floor. A waitress which Tatiana observed for possibly a moment too long delivered a bottle of quality Russian vodka based on the scent I caught on the way by. I spotted Queen Sophie just after we entered and she graced me with her lovely smile. I chose to mingle with the local courtiers a bit, as it will never hurt to have friendly contacts, before requesting an audience with the Queen. Sophie nearly blushed at how formal I was, but I soon had her much more comfortable with my presence. I believe my name will be well received in Viennese Courts for some time. Dearbh\u00e1il joined the revelry after she felt I had acquired an adequate amount of attention. She truly is quite selfless as Fairest go. My feathered friend convinced Queen Sophie to connect us with the local Autumn Court as well. They would likely have information about powerful relics and how to dispose of them, plus we could take Lizette to something less uncomfortable for her.<br /> <br /> Gem\u00fctlichkeit proved enjoyable for all but as dawn comes early, we returned to the hotel around 11:00. I do hope we can continue to experience the joys of all our cabal as a group. Lizette and Wolfram seemed none the worse for their visit, if perhaps with a bit wider eyes than they left. I must learn tomorrow what was so interesting.<br /> <br /> 22 June 1920 - Early<br /> <br /> If only each morning could start this way, I would not even regret waking before dawn. All, save Alla for obvious reasons, gathered in the fleeing twilight outside of Vienna. As the Uratha and Ochran\u0144y, our totem, collected their ritual equipment, Dearbh\u00e1il prepared us for the day. She warmly took my face and kissed me on either cheek. Fenric only received a warm smile, but he was affected similarly. While she moved on to the others, I was awash in Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s potent magic. Her use of our Court Contracts was useful as well. Once we were all similarly refreshed and awed by Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s charity and beauty respectively, the rite began.<br /> <br /> I focused on every detail I could detect as the Uratha took their positions. The rite was meant to \u201cchain their rage\u201d to help protect the pack and themselves from the bestial fury within. The four main themes I determined were Rage, Calm, Binding, and Dawn. As the first rays of light struck the ritual area, Tatiana symbolized the inner rage of the werewolf. Marek circled Tatiana while binding her hands with a chain made of iron and bone. Marek was the symbol of calm, which is not at all surprising, though I was intrigued by the chain. Tatiana is of the Iron Master tribe, while Marek is a Bone Shadow. The sympathetic connections had to be very strong given the usage. With the obvious symbol of binding, I looked on straining to see the slightest glimmer of our totem. In a wider circle, we were told that Ochran\u0144y moved in the opposite revolution from Marek, protecting the rest of the pack from the rage within should something go wrong. The rite was as beautiful as it was powerful. All to keep others safe from the unbridled wrath within each Uratha. The assembly was speechless; whether through fatigue, ignorance, or appreciation of the display before us was not readily apparent.<br /> <br /> I think I will retire to my room, perhaps attempt to discuss the finer points of the ritual with Tatiana. Or perhaps I will not ask the Uratha what she did with her rage and instead review the map of the grounds for possible improvements.<br /> <br /> 22 June 1920 - After Lunch<br /> <br /> While I do not enjoy being commonly referred to as a thief, I know where my skills lie. When a flustered Wolfram returned from a meeting with Christina\u2019s Lady\u2019s maid, he asked if I could steal a letter being sent to Christina\u2019s brother. Apparently Hohenburg rudely accelerated his intentions with Christina by placing a letter in the post asking Gunter to instruct his sister to accept an upcoming proposal to marry. In the time I have known Wolfram, I have not seen him display such distress as his perceived helplessness. I did not allow him to humble himself toward me further, wordlessly grabbing a random courier\u2019s bag and leaving. At the end of the hall, I turned to find Marek accompanying me. Silently nodding to each other, we continued on to the Post Office.<br /> <br /> Entering the building as though I was judging every brick, I announced myself the courier of an unnamed Romanian noble. The postmen immediately believed my ruse. I noted there was nothing supernatural present as we were given the full tour of the premises on the way to the Postmaster\u2019s Office. He gave me an abundance of assurances that any package my patron might send would be in the very best hands. Marek was immediately accepted as my protector so after we left, I sent him back in to distract the front office. The Uratha stormed back in demanding (in a much thicker than usual Czech-tinted German) a trinket that was mysteriously missing from my bag when we left the building. His size and accent were more than enough to grab the attention of all present, making it much easier for me to slip back in. I used my abilities to guarantee no one could easily follow me, laughed my way past the single locked door barring my path, and grabbed the letter from the outgoing box. I ran back out just as easily and after another tense moment, Marek exited as well. The post was scheduled to leave by 2:00 pm. We returned to the hotel before lunch was brought into the main dining room. I left the unopened and uncreased envelope at Wolfram\u2019s place at the table. I thought he might enjoy the present.<br /> <br /> Wolfram has since left to research what the relic could be in the storied libraries of Vienna. I hope to do something similar through the help of the Autumn Court, once I have been accepted as an ally.<br /> <br /> 22 June 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> Our Sin-Eater returned with only slightly more answers than questions. Wolfram asked Marek and myself to assist him in deciphering the subtext of his library findings on what we learned was known as the Eye of Iblis. That I was included in this scholarly work was flattering as I am fully aware that the other men are greatly my superior, but I contributed nonetheless. After the three of us poured over the notes, consulted tomes and each other, then cross referenced various religious, folk, and historical accounts, we were certain of the following:<br /> <br /> The Eye of Iblis aids in the command of some creatures, likely spirits, while worn<br /> <br /> Encourages acts of atrocity for what amounts to good luck while still wearing the necklace<br /> <br /> Increases the possibility of madness and/or debased actions<br /> <br /> The observed obsession comes not simply from touching the piece but from wearing it<br /> <br /> Theoretically enhances the use of certain hedge magics, notably those dealing with spirits<br /> <br /> Any effect on the supernatural, such as ourselves, is unknown<br /> <br /> Is fairly old as it was possessed by Pashas of the Ottoman Empire for some time before the Great War<br /> <br /> After considering the information and description of the piece, I determined that dislodging the gem would likely break the magic without losing value as exotic jewelry. With jeweler\u2019s tools, I or Lizette could mark the gem around the edges with \u201coccult\u201d symbols to increase the value to some if they are unaware or unconcerned about magic.<br /> <br /> While we three understudies of the occult toiled over old knowledge, Lizette was busy gathering new information. Using her own Contracts, the Wizened learned the thief was a woman with striking yellow eyes, pale skin, and blonde hair. Sadly, we had no ideas as to who this woman might be, though I suspected Hohenberg recruited one of the Pure. This is entirely speculation, of course. Once that was disseminated among the cabal, our small engineer discussed making Wolfram silver weaponry as it seems he may encounter Pure resistance to him proposing to Christina. While most minds fall to silver daggers, it was determined that bullets make the better option. I will likely liberate silverware from several of the numerous fine dining establishments given the Pure must keep close watch on the local silversmiths. Lizette can happily melt my bounty into ammunition. But before I start such an endeavor, we must prepare for Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s performance tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 22nd June 1920<br /> <br /> Well. I have now gotten love letters from two women, and kissed one. Well, one of the love letters spent a bit more time asking me not to kill her potential husband than on affections, but they were there. Okay, not kill. I already said I would not do that. Not take away to faerie, or turn into a frog, or horse, or something. Still, I\u2019ll take it. Marlene\u2019s letter expressed she was curious about my \u201ctastes,\u201d and curious about some things she heard about the French and their\u2026talents. While it was not unseemly, her intentions and interest were clear.<br /> <br /> Okay, more (less?) important things. Herr Hohemberg has attempted to speed up the clock, trying to have a letter sent to Gunter asking permission to propose now with his backing. Marlene tipped us off, and suggested Wolfram put a move on Christina and begin making his own case as a match. She got a kiss for that. Even got to decide where it went. Meanwhile Marek and Dacian absconded with the letter.<br /> <br /> There was talk of blowing up the post office. Enough to get a gal all giddy, especially as Wolfram, who tends to only want to use huge amounts of explosives where necessary, was for it. Obviously he quickly altered it to no loss of life, which is understandable; the postal workers are not our enemy and don\u2019t mean us harm, so I was okay with them leaving. Still, this deal was getting worse all the time. We discussed ways to draw them out, then moved onto a very localized explosion in the mail room, then a fire, then Wolfram decided he did not want possibly valuable letters destroyed so smoke bomb, than no explosion. Bah.<br /> <br /> I need to work on some sort of shaped charges that can eliminate a portion of a structure while keeping the rest intact. If I had something that could blow, say, inward or something, I bet I could have used it. Well, at least until Wolfram decided not to destroy letters.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my visit to Madame Esterh\u00e1zy\u2019s home was not for for skirt chasing at all. Actually, the real reason was to use my Contracts of Animation to examine the box. It took a couple tries, but I did get the face of the thief, which was somewhat unusual though I don\u2019t think she was fae. Still, there are not many yellow-eyed women, besides yours truly, so that should help, maybe?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m doing this backwards, maybe sideways. Following the last journal entry, Alla had gone to meet the lead Vampire of her Court, and got an invitation by a mysterious stranger, one Maximillian Nostras. Which sounds like a made up name to me. As this vampire was a complete stranger, she wanted some backup, but Werewolves might be a bit too threatening, since they are not the hardest supernatural creatures to detect but each one is a juggernaut. Alla made a comment about keeping Dearbh\u00e1il, so she backed down, and Dacian did too, which apparently surprised Alla. Someone had to girl the hell up, and that person was of course the Frenchwoman, yours truly.<br /> <br /> The meeting went fine. Maximillian Nostras is an enormous man, a member of a group called the Macellarius. Most of the conversation was him being side about the Prince, a lady named Magdalena, and a member of a rival lineage called the Eupraxus. He suggested she and some of her hangers on, members of another group called Gorgons who were part of the \u201cCircle of the Crone\u201d might have the necklace. Apparently the Eupraxus are some sort of Vampire nobility, but this one was very new. I am not sure what \u201cnew\u201d means to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Maximillian was eager to ingratiate himself to Alla. He offered her that information for free, and even asked her about doing him a favor which would put him in some debt to her. I confess some suspicion about the large man\u2019s goals. Also, of course, vampires are scary as hell. I try to avoid them when possible, and have a handy flamethrower when not.<br /> <br /> The next morning I watched the Werewolves do a ritual to control their anger, with the sunrise. I was not going to be up for sunrise, but that is how it goes. First sunrise I may have seen since the war. Not sure.<br /> <br /> Anyway, then was Marlene with the letters, me going to the house to examine the box, and the whole post office thing. Wolfram took some time to research the amulet, which is called the Eye of Iblis, which is a Muslim thing apparently from the Ottoman Empire. It makes you stronger if you do bad stuff, but is addictive, or at least makes you disinclined to part with it. Also, some stuff about controlling beings of \u201cSmokeless Fire.\u201d Spirits maybe? Elemental Lost? Bah makes my head hurt. I have my thing\u2026Wolfram, Marek and Dacian will figure out that part, I am sure.<br /> <br /> Oh, some discussion of weapons, with Dacian taking silver cutlery and cheese knives and such, to make for silver bullets or weapons. Silver weapons are not too effective, but that issue does not extend to bullets. I was thinking about a way to have a silver toothed chain saw as well. Sadly I did not keep silver around as it seemed\u2026antagonistic given the Werewolves. But we need to have a way to fight Werewolves if we are not werewolves. Silver bullets and a silver toothed chainsaw could work. You can\u2019t just kill them with a silver cheese knife.<br /> <br /> Tonight should be interesting. Dearbh\u00e1il is performing. Wolfram will be taking Christina there. Marlene\u2019s letter suggested we meet in private while her mistress was away, but when I saw her at the house she seemed somewhat disinclined. Not that I was trying to initiate shenanigans really beyond rewarding her I had work to do. She could go to the concert then after all, maybe, though given Dearbh\u00e1il really seems to dislike her maybe not.<br /> <br /> But honestly right now I need to get back to this duplicate regardless. While it won\u2019t be needed if some of Dacian\u2019s ideas work out, we may need it, and I would prefer to potentially have it if we need it. Hmmm, I wonder if I can make it explode\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VI</i><br /> <br /> The lack of journals from some quarters is unfortunate, but unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Alla had met Prince Lukas Dorn of the Invictus Ventrue and Bishop Magdalena Herzog, Daeva of the Lancea et Sanctum. She was warned about Carthians, Belial\u2019s Brood, and others in the more bohemian districts. She was met by a messenger for Maximillian Nostras, Ventrue of the Invictus and the Macellarius line. That meeting included Maximillian being almost creepily friendly, warning many ended up in a bond to Magdalena, and pointed her to a recently created Daeva of the Eupraxus line, Lisbet Eupraxus. She had fallen in with a \u201cbad lot\u201d but Maximillian claimed there were no Belial\u2019s Brood but Circle of the Crone, including members of the Gorgon Bloodline. He suggested they had an interest in occult objects, and could well have taken it. He stressed she owed him nothing for the information, as he claimed he sought to build a rapport of Bonhomie. He did suggest his grandchilde had gone rouge, and if she wanted to him a favor she could deal with him. The grandchilde was not, however, his responsibility, he stressed.<br /> <br /> There was some humor that Dearbh\u00e1il made a big deal of hating Marlene Vogl, Christina\u2019s Companion. Marlene actually came to her for help, suggesting perhaps she and her mistress should not receive the necklace back. She also attempted to discuss Lizette, but lost her nerve. In the end, Dearbh\u00e1il softened her view of her after that.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest was covered above. I realize it is a lot and some journals are spotty. If you have comments or questions let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:58:52-07:00","id":585810,"title":"","content":"Last session was a bit of a rough one. Marek\u2019s player had to miss, and Taitiana\u2019s player had to leave about a half hour into it. Still, we got some good play in and got an action scene. This sessions covers the evening before the Solstice, Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concert.<br /> <br /> Thus Tatiana \u2018s journal does not really cover the session, for the most part, though the Changelings do.<br /> <i><br /> Session VII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I am snarly. Why do you bother me?<br /> <br /> No, we are still to hunt Lady Summer. After all, I missed out on all the fun to scout the hunting ground. I will not make it worthless by snarling too much to perform one of my sacred duties.<br /> <br /> All of the fun. It was a glorious fight, I am told, though Dacian has much flash to him, and it is not as if our pack is truly a fighting sort.<br /> <br /> Heh, volchonok, you think any of them could stand against the Pure? No, it was communists and vampires. Excellent prey.<br /> <br /> You think human things do not make excellent prey? You have attached yourself to the wrong Uratha then.<br /> <br /> Come now, you deny that our communists hunts have not been good hunts? That it is unworthy, to face down a pack of men with their Causes and their shouting and their impudence...<br /> <br /> I have lost you again... they also threatened our songbird.<br /> <br /> Aha! That has your attention. It was maybe not so much threatened, but they did make her angry. She yelled at them quite fiercely, I am told. That would have been sight, volchonok. Even if it turned out there was no fight. They interrupted her singing, you see.<br /> <br /> No, the others do not think that is why they were there. At the same time, the vampires I mentioned earlier, creatures like our Alla, but a different tribe, attacked a different vampire. And we did not like this? I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> Well, of course I would not like them doing this if I wanted to have a fight with them, silly volchonok, but the others did not.<br /> <br /> Wolfram is a clever man, and knew he could win no such thing. This tribe of vampires, they are supposed to be very good in a brawl and at changing their forms. It would be a wonderful fight. It is unfortunate that this vampire we are hunting is not one of these Gangrels. But I am distracted. Wolfram, he made it obvious that they were not humans, by shooting them in the face and having them not fall over, as humans are wont to do.<br /> <br /> They have rules, somewhat like us. The herd must not know, yes?<br /> <br /> I believe that with the shooting, and the rules, and Dacian blinding them somehow and our songbird\u2019s yelling, they ran.<br /> <br /> I know, volchonok, I know. It is a sad ending. Perhaps we will fight them again.<br /> <br /> In my other skin? What do you mean?<br /> <br /> The new clothes that Dacian wants for me? You think fancy clothes will stop me from being able to fight?<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, they are human clothes. I always wear human clothes, when I am in human form.<br /> <br /> Change is not so bad, little one. Listen, volchonok. You stand downwind of your prey on a hunt, you blend in with your surroundings and you move silently. Here in the city, it is just another hunt, and these clothes are what will blend in, better than \u2018my skin\u2019. That is all.<br /> <br /> You do not have to blend in at fancy parties, silly volchonok.<br /> <br /> What is wrong with you, volchonok? Fretting and grumbling about our summer hunt, and hunting humans, and wearing different clothes. I have done these things before without this sulking. It is the city?<br /> <br /> Ah, yes. Do not worry volchonok, I will not lose sight of the spirit world merely because we have business in this place of humans. You know this. You will always be my volchonok. And tonight we will run, with our pack, and hunt Lady Summer. You will see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 22 June 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> I mentioned in my last entry that we must prepare for Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s performance. As I have not yet seen Tatiana wear anything other than her uniform, I suggested (delicately) that we investigate the tailors of Vienna. I knew that she would not stand for anything too fragile or elegant. Thus I chose a more discreet tailor to properly measure and prepare a masculine suit. Tatiana\u2019s subtle curves were appreciated without being emphasized. The hand stitching should hold up, providing she gives at least moderate care, to a fair amount of wear. It was a handsome fit in the end. I paid to make sure the ensemble was completed before we had to leave to support and enjoy Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s efforts.<br /> <br /> 23 June 1920 - Dawn<br /> <br /> The cabal has had an exciting and eventful evening. Our Uratha were not present, as Marek pulled Tatiana to scout their ritual space for tonight. Thus my purchases today were in vain. I am certain our Iron Master will resent missing the festivities at the opera however. ...I never thought I could say that about Tatiana.<br /> <br /> Regardless, when we arrived, we found our seats were well appointed indeed. Christina and Wolfram shared a box while Lizette, Alla, Fenric, and myself shared an adjacent box. I was using my time to practice my forgery. It is not an art in which I excel, but could be incredibly useful in the future. I believe Lizette was working on some form of clothing design. When our Minstrel took the stage all other pursuits were put aside. Though I had had the pleasure of hearing Dearbh\u00e1il sing in the past, knowing the tongue in which she sang added considerable depth to the experience. While we sat in our box, I noticed one of the Theosophists in attendance as well. Her presence was not immediately alarming, though it did serve to remind me of the tenuous situation in which we find ourselves. I would hesitate to claim we are beset upon all sides, as we have as yet not made our presence known. We came to intermission and I noticed Lizette seemed to slump against the back of her oversized seat. Alla left without comment, and I refreshed my drink.<br /> <br /> I returned just as Dearbh\u00e1il took the stage. Her hauntingly beautiful voice filled the hall once again, but only for a few moments before dissonance arose from near the entryway of the wide opera house. A voice cried out, \u201cFirst St. Petersburg, now Vienna!\u201d Tracing the source of the interruption, a brawl of some form tore away from the doors to reveal four gun waving Communists. The upstarts fought with six men from the opera, who struck soundly with batons to restore order for Dearbh\u00e1il. The Fairest ceased her performance as if the note had been severed from her throat. Replacing her melodious song came her Irish temper. Incensed that her opening night was rudely interrupted, Dearbh\u00e1il roared from the stage at the offenders. One left immediately, though his associates were not so lucky. The men from the opera were quite skilled with their batons, though the gunshot which rang from Wolfram\u2019s box finished one as another ran away. The fourth was possibly the least lucky as I struck him blind before the gunshot. He could only hear the terror of the audience and the deathrattle from the ground next to him. Though it was perhaps missed given how liberally the batons were used. A shriek from the other side of the opera house drew our attention to three large men advancing menacingly on a group of women. A chair lay rended asunder by why blade I could not tell. Wolfram seemed to immediately understand the situation and fired his pistol once again. His aim was true, striking one of the men in the face. I flinched as I was not prepared for the horrific scene that never came. I would learn afterwards the men were vampires of the Gangrel clan. These vampires either instigated the Communist attack or were incredibly lucky in their opportunism. Either way, things were not going as they intended. The women were withdrawing and the men, suddenly without targets and the center of attention, seemed to want to run away. I tried to strike one blind as I had with the Communists, but nothing happened. I am unsure if vampires are immune to my abilities, though I suspect I am simply too unskilled to perform under duress. The three Gangrel forced their way through the now hostile crowd and jumped out the window to escape.<br /> <br /> Our Fairest, never one to back away from a challenge, addressed the crowd directly and frankly, calming the situation by taking back the attention of the audience. Dearbh\u00e1il made clear that tonight was for everyone, as no one had come away unchanged or untouched by the Great War and in this, we were all as one. The tense applause grew into a standing ovation as she then launched into a heartfelt version of the Austrian national anthem. With that hurdle cleared, the audience was firmly under Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s spell. Unfortunately, the tenor of the evening left our Fairest quite low. She returned to the hotel with little conversation and no evidence of her usual joie de vivre. This left most of the cabal is lesser spirits.<br /> <br /> I realized immediately that I would need a distraction. And given previous discussions with Lizette regarding arms production, I had the perfect distraction. After taking my time to choose my targets, I spent the rest of the night acquiring the purest of silver from five very richly decorated homes. The Pure may tighten patrols in those neighborhoods, but tonight I have a ritual to attend and tomorrow night I will move on to my next target. Vienna has a number of vastly overstated churches. But now I must fall blissfully into the clutches of sleep.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 23nd June 1920<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concert tonight saw a major interruption. It was dealt with, but I fear she may be a bit crestfallen. I will need to check on her later today when I can catch up and make sure her spirit is still well.<br /> <br /> Her concert was good; Dacian, Alla, Fenric and I sat in one private box, while Wolfram and Christina were in a second. The Werewolves were scouting a ritual area. The first half went well, overall. Her performance was, as always, majestic.<br /> <br /> I closed my eyes and dozed a bit in the intermission. Alla had gotten up, and I was thinking of how she wears those gigantic hats, and with that and her hair were she not so afraid of fire I could have a hidden flamethrower in there. She could simply look down at an opponent, squeeze an air bladder and douse them in flame. I am given to understand vampires do poorly with fire, so it probably would not work. Tatiana does not wear silly hats, and Dearbh\u00e1il\u2026actually Dearbh\u00e1il might work.<br /> <br /> Especially after what happened next.<br /> <br /> As I say through the intermission all was well, afterwards a group of Communist agitators broke into the concert. I have seen their sort in Paris, but Paris is considerably more stable than Vienna. The security was dealing with them when Dearbh\u00e1il began to address them. She (I think) used her Spring Court magic on two of them to make them want to flee, while one was struck blind (by Dacian, I assume.) The fourth one Wolfram stood up and shot dead with his pistol, which took me off guard. I was on my way down to deal with them (or steal their stuff while they were thrown out) so the crack of his shot took me off guard.<br /> <br /> Then apparently conflict between some Vampires broke out. According to Alla, some were of a group called the Gangrel and members of the Carthian organization hostile to her organization. Wolfram shot at them too with considerably less effect. I knew Vampires were scary, but despite taking a direct shot to the face he looked almost unhurt. Dacian began using his magic as well, though, and blinding them. Fairly useful, that. They wound up fleeing through the window. All did not fill us on too much, but I believe the woman was Lizbet Eupraxus. I did not get the best look at her but my eyes are sharp.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian seemed to be able to get a read on the situations quickly, possibly due to their Spring magic. I should really try and learn some Autumnal magic. If nothing else knowing fears can be effective in combat. It\u2019s also worth noting that Vampires neither need weapons (they can apparently grow claws that can shred a seat) but are fairly unphased by them. This is troublesome. I need to get to work on some sort of personal flamethrower, or ability to store sunlight.<br /> <br /> As it stood I was able to bring in a few weapons, a pistol, a knife and a grenade, but did not wind up using any as the pistol would have only added to the chaos (also, I am not as good a shot as Wolfram and have no real experience shooting into fisticuffs.) There was just no bringing in a chainsaw. This is the second time I have been in a situation where blood was shed I could not get to my chainsaw. I need work on finding a good way to keep it handy.<br /> <br /> Anyway Dearbh\u00e1il managed to salvage the evening, and gave a rousing speech to everyone. While I think the revolutionaries did managed to spread some fear, she helped to undo much of it. Dearbh\u00e1il is a most impressive woman.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Christina were rather a flutter with each other, which was bothering me. But Christina is not the only woman to show me any interest. I decided to leave she and Wolfram alone and pursue other options for the evening when the show ended.<br /> <br /> I went to the Esterh\u00e1zy estate, and tapped on Marlene\u2019s window. She was surprised to see me, and nervously made apologies for not meeting that night. I kissed her, wrapped myself around her, and pushed her on the bed.<br /> <br /> Marlene was amazingly soft. Her mouth, her hands, her skin, her neck. Everything was soft and warm. Her letter said she wanted to be ravished, and by God she was ravished. I will never forget the sweet smell of her neck and bosom.<br /> <br /> Before first light, I departed the German maiden\u2019s boudoir. Marlene gave me a very personal token, and suggested given Wolfram\u2019s interest in Christina perhaps I should cast my eyes to a different woman. I told her we would see, but I did not wish for either of us to be spoken for\u2026particularly given it would be much worse for her if she were. Her family has expectations, after all. But we will see. She has a lot of thinking to do.<br /> <br /> Maybe she would like a flamethrower hat?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VII</i><br /> <br /> The scene with Tatiana and Dacian shopping was covered in broad strokes with some RP. That was unfortunately all she was up for that evening.<br /> <br /> Alla and Wolfram both engaged in Social Maneuvering. Wolfram had previously opened a number of Christina\u2019s doors (ahem) and used the opportunity to boost his Impression high enough to roll per hour, which lead to him seducing her successfully. His intentions are, however, honorable; he still hopes to marry her, but he has given himself a bargaining chip if Gunnar makes a play.<br /> <br /> Alla was working on seducing Vera during the intermission, the Theosophist she started on and who did not get pummeled with a hammer. Vera was making resistance rolls (she is older, and Alla\u2019s attempt is same-sex), so despite her having also started on the train during the last story, she got some success but not like Wolfram (also, she only spoke to her during intermission really). Lizette was not really the aggressor in her encounter, needing only to pass a simple roll to get Marlene to do what she wanted to do anyway.<br /> <br /> The combat, such as it was, was quick. Wolfram\u2019s skill with firearms was boosted by his Industrial Caul, which helped him one shot one attacker with his pistol. He hit one of the Gangrel but did only a small amount of damage. Lizette attempted to close but did not make it to either confrontation before it was essentially over. She had a gun but nowhere near the skill needed to shoot into melee without stopping to activate contracts. Dearbh\u00e1il attempted to intercede but her total lack of Intimidation skill interfered.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il did, however, roll remarkably well on her performance, and to get Glamour, and Lizette and Dacian had little trouble topping off. She also did well with her Fleeting Spring uses of Cupid\u2019s Eye.<br /> <br /> Well it was fun, and Vienna\u2019s instability, the general fears of the city at the time have been shown. But there was something about a necklace, right? More when we return (with the Uratha) to tonight\u2019s session, and report in two weeks.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:51:32-07:00","id":603257,"title":"","content":"<br /> The Solstice has arrived! The team takes a break from stalking and skulking to celebrate! More is learned of the local fae, and hookups happen for some of those who did not do so the night before.<br /> <br /> Journals from the usual suspects. Marek is back with journals for three sessions to make up for lost time. So his is longer and touches on earlier plots, then has the newest session. Geez, is it already\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session VIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 21 June 1920 (Evening)<br /> <br /> This evening was just as interesting as the day. Tatiana and I put the finishing touches on the Chain Rage rite that we\u2019ve been planning. I finished the bone and metal chains not long ago, which was the last material piece that we needed. The rest is just planning the ritual to appease the spirits and gain their aid in the rite. This will be to bind our rage should we need it in the future. I thought it a good precaution to take since we might become very dangerous to innocents around us should the Rage take over.<br /> <br /> While we were doing that, and other things, Alla, Fenric and Wolfram were paying their respects to the local vampire Prince. Apparently this went well. The Prince did warn Alla that she should be mindful of her appearance while in town and to hide the fact that she is a Russian noble. The resident Communists do not like nobles, no matter where they are from. There is also another faction of vampires called the Carthians that have set themselves against the faction that Alla is a part of, the Invictis. I\u2019m not sure of all the political minutia, but I know a possible threat when I hear one. Alla could be in danger from the Communists or these Carthians in town. So we will just need to keep an eye out for them, and to have Alla tone down her apparel while in Vienna to keep a lower profile.<br /> <br /> After the meeting with the Prince the trio came back and gathered up Lizette to go meet with another vampire named Maximillian who might be sympathetic towards Alla and her situation. He might be an ally to draw aid from if the need should arise. It was discussed whether or not Tatiana or I should accompany the group, but everyone felt like it would be seen as too hostile an act and may negatively affect the initial meeting. So for the sake of politics Tatiana and I agreed to stay behind. Though the group was not without defenses. Alla is formidable in her own right, Wolfram is good with his pistol, and Lizette brought a bomb in her purse. Always the pragmatist that one.<br /> <br /> The meeting with Maximillian seemed to go well. He gave them information about a woman, of the Eupraxus bloodline (apparently they are part of the Invictis faction) who is interested in arcane objects. Alla told Maximillian that we are looking for the stolen necklace and that it was evil and possibly dangerous. Hence him bringing up the Eupraxus woman. Perhaps if we can track her down we can see if she knows were the necklace is or if she stole it herself. This information was not free however. Not entirely. Maximillian asked Alla and the group to look into the whereabouts of his \u201cgrandchild\u201d who has become a danger to the vampire community. The bloodline that they are a part of doesn\u2019t just drink blood, they eat human flesh, and this \u201cgrandchild\u201d has become too noticeable in his activities. Maximillian asked if our group might look into finding this person and removing him from the equation. I can understand where he\u2019s coming from. It is very important for Uratha to keep the secret of our existence just that, secret. People finding out, that are not bound to a pack, could become problematic for us. The same is true for the vampires. Mortals finding out about them could cause trouble down the line. It is good to be a myth.<br /> <br /> While all of that was going on Dearbhail pleaded and cajoled in that way that only she can do to get Tatiana and I to join her at a Burlesque house. It worked. Tatiana is smitten with our songstress but doesn\u2019t seem inclined to act on that. As far as the Burlesque house went, the fae did a lot of socializing and may have an \u201cin\u201d as far as acquiring information about the necklace goes. Dearbhail talked to the Queen about the cursed necklace and she said that she would put Dearbhail in contact with someone from the \u201cAutumn Court.\u201d From what I\u2019ve picked up about Fae politics, there are four seasonal courts. Each one comes to power in their own season. So right now the Summer Queen is in charge. She was one of the people that Dearbhail and Dacian spent a good deal of time talking to. Each court also seems to have their own talents. Apparently the Autumn court is known for its association with fear and it\u2019s work with the occult. Perhaps they can provide some information.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 22 June 1920<br /> <br /> At dawn this morning we performed the Chain Rage rite with the rest of the pack. Tatiana and I used the bone and metal chain that I\u2019d made to bind our hands together to represent that the binding of the Rage. Metal and bone link to represent the two tribes present, and also for man and for nature. We tried to make this rite as strong as we could. Doing it now during the new moon lent me some strength, plus we also included our packs Totem, Ochranny. She seemed happy to help us in this endeavor. After binding our hands Tatiana and I took on our roles. Tatiana represented \u2018rage\u2019 and I represented \u2018calm.\u2019 She did well portraying anger and rage. She snarled and snapped, while I quietly intimidated her into calming down. I will admit that I called on a bit of Reznik to pull off being intimidating while being calm. If there is one thing that Reznik is, it\u2019s calm. <br /> <br /> So, Ochranny walked a protective circle around me and Tatiana, while the rest of our pack walked a wider circle around all of us. It thought it went well. Ochranny seemed to approve, and the chains I made now seem to hum with a quiet power. It\u2019s not really something you can hear, well, the humans can\u2019t hear it. It\u2019s more a sense of power than a tangible sound. Reminds me of the fetish I made for my rifle. After all of that Dearbhail used some of her fae magic to help take away our fatigue. It worked rather well, and made me feel refreshed. The rest of the day seemed just a bit brighter because of it.<br /> <br /> Later in the day there was a big thing about a letter that Gunnar has sent to Christina\u2019s brother asking for her hand in marriage. We received this information from Marlena. Apparently his servants talked to her servants, or something along those lines. And since Gunnar marrying Christina would interfere with Wolfram\u2019s plans and put Christina in danger we decided to do something about it. <br /> <br /> Marlena also confided in Dearbhail that she did not want her mistress to get the necklace back. She admitted that she knew it has some sort of influence over her and she was afraid of what it might do. Just from the difficulty she had in telling us this information we could tell that it has a strong hold indeed. It made Marlena feel physically ill to even suggest keeping it away. Wolfram decided to look into this more fully by seeing what he could find at the University of Vienna\u2019s library.<br /> <br /> Before he left though, Wolfram asked Dacian and I to look into this letter business. We agreed. We had discussed it as a group, and many suggestions were made as to how we could go about getting the letter. Unfortunately most of Lizette\u2019s ideas involved fire. We managed to talk Wolfram out of that option. Dacian and I are good at going unseen if we want so we said we\u2019d use means other than fire to get the letter. We ended up using subterfuge. Dacian posed as Romanian nobility and I his employee, perhaps servant, and we toured the post office. We found were the letter was likely to be and then we left. I came back a short while later saying that something had been taken from my employer\u2019s bag and wanted it returned. I did my best to physically intimidate the clerks at the front so they\u2019d pay sole attention to me and not mind the man sneaking back in. I may not be the most physically imposing figure, but if you get close enough to someone and project the right emotion in your eyes it will do a lot towards scaring someone. I just imagined that the clerk was Reznik\u2019s last target and it was not hard to project the desire to do bodily harm. I was nearing the end of things I\u2019d thought up to say, when I saw a shadow flit past me and out the door. Having seen Dacian leave, I left the clerk with a final warning and stormed out appropriately angry.<br /> <br /> After appropriating the letter we went back to the hotel to meet up with the others. By that time Wolfram had returned and had indeed found out something about the necklace. Apparently it is called the Eye of Iblis. This was either an angel who was not overly fond of humans or one of the first genies. Whoever this Iblis was, they are no friend to man. The necklace apparently carries with it a curse that encourages the wearer to give in to their baser desires and vices. It, as we\u2019ve seen, has some sort of hold over those that have it and quite literally makes the person sick if they try and get rid of it. It is also possible that it could strengthen hedge magic, but we\u2019re not going to try that out. If it twists your actions so you do things that you would not normally do, I\u2019m a little wary about what it would do to a magic user\u2019s use of magic. We\u2019re also not sure if it would even affect us, since the lot of us could be considered \u201csupernatural creatures.\u201d I don\u2019t have any plans to find out though, and neither do the rest of the pack. <br /> <br /> Alla and Tatiana were also busy while Wolfram, Dacian and I were out. They investigated this Maximillian\u2019s \u201cgrandchild.\u201d They started at his old hideout, but were unable to follow a trail. It was too old and too cold to follow. <br /> <br /> And while all that was going on, Lizette went to Christina\u2019s house to use her power to take a closer look at the box that held the necklace. She said that she got an impression or image of the thief. It was a woman of slight build, with pale skin, blonde hair and yellow eyes. I despaired at hearing the first part since that could fit so many people in this city. The latter however, unless she has a way to conceal her eyes without being obvious, will make her that much easier to find.<br /> <br /> After all that was done with it was decided that while Tatiana and I scouted out a location for our Solstice rite, the others would go to the auditorium and listen to Dearbhail\u2019s performance. Our scouting went well and after a pretty lengthy search we found the perfect place to hold the Solstice ritual. It\u2019s a natural clearing in the woods, a good distance away from town, and without too many low hanging tree branches nearby. So, we headed back, happy with our find.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for our pack mates, their evening was not quite so calm. The performance started off well, Dearbhail singing beautifully, when it was suddenly interrupted by Communists wielding guns. I\u2019m not sure of all that happened or the order that it happened in, but I do know that at one point Wolfram shot a man square in the face. One would think this would pretty effectively end a man. Not in this case. The individual in question just seemed to get mad and shrug it off like it was a fist rather than a bullet that hit him. Our pack-mates later learned that this man was a vampire of the gangrel clan. Something along those lines. Several people were injured, communist and auditorium staff alike, but only one person died. Another man that Wolfram had shot earlier in the brawl. And none of our pack-mates came to harm, which is the important part. I\u2019m not inclined to be overly concerned when strangers fight or kill each other, but when such activities involve my pack or my family I do care. Anyone who hurts my pack will be dealt with.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> <br /> 23 June 1920<br /> <br /> The day started innocently enough. Wolfram wanted to send a letter of his own to Christina\u2019s brother, but we also wanted to make sure that a letter from Gunnar went out as well. So, some of us helped write the letter from Wolfram to the brother while the rest of us helped compose a letter from Gunnar. Not that we were going to be polite or in any way proper in this letter. It just had to look like it came from Gunnar, which is where Dacian came in. Apparently he had been practicing his forgery skills using the original letter from Gunnar that he and I intercepted. So he used his skills to create a new letter that would go out in its stead. Seems a bit overly complicated to me, but I suppose it makes sense. If Gunnar makes some mention of a letter that he send and nothing arrives then it might be suspect. But if a letter does arrive and it puts Christina\u2019s brother off of Gunnar altogether than more the better for us.<br /> <br /> Later, while our fae friends went to yet another one of their celebrations, this one for the new season, Tatiana and I met with Krieger. The gist of what we talked about is that Gunnar is going to be meeting with a Pure woman from Germany in the next day or so. They will be discussing the shipment of spiritually charged items into the area. Of course I was interested in this. Who knows what kind of items they might bring in and what use they will be to us. A lot of relics or talens can be used by Uratha or humans alike, so I was interested to find out what kinds of things they plan on transporting to Vienna. <br /> <br /> Our plan so far is to spy on them and see when they plan to meet. If the meeting will happen soon enough, we will attack the tradeoff of goods. We will take down who we can, but right now we intend to leave the German Pure alive. If she can report back to her people in Germany that Vienna is not as secure or safe as they\u2019d like it then they may decide to sever ties with this area. That would be good for the local Uratha, so we\u2019re going to try and make that happen. I don\u2019t know why I\u2019m being so altruistic, though I suppose I can look at it in terms of what our pack can gain from this venture. We have the possibility of getting our hands on the spiritual items, which is good for us.<br /> <br /> We may also decide to include other members of our pack in the spying and/or attack. We will need to be careful while watching the Pure as they have the assistance of several spirits in the area, and if they see us they will report our whereabouts. I believe Wolfram may be of assistance with this. I will have to ask him if he can see spirits when they are incorporeal. As for the actual attack the others have abilities that will not be known to the Pure. They keep with their own, so they will not have an adequate defense against Dacian\u2019s ability to cause blindness for example.<br /> <br /> After our meeting with Krieger we met back up with the rest of our pack to do the Solstice rite at dusk. We all went to the clearing we had made in the woods earlier and lit a bonfire. This time Tatiana led the rite. After the fire was lit Tatiana loped off to bring back a kill for the ceremony. During the short time we waited I could see the interest and excitement on the faces of the rest of the pack. They had been a part of one pack rite so far and within a short time were getting to see another. I know that Dacian and Wolfram were particularly interested. Dacian is just curious about everything, and Wolfram is particularly interested in anything spiritual. Dearbhail in particular was rather hyper and very affectionate.<br /> <br /> Tatiana came back after only about an hour with a deer. It looked like a fine buck and I thought it boded well for the ceremony. Dedecek and Ochranny looked on with approval. Tatiana laid the animal down and proceeded to cut out its heart with her knife. She took a bite and handed it to me. I took a bite and offered it to Wolfram. Much to my surprise, though I suppose I shouldn\u2019t have been, he accepted and took a bite. This prompted the rest of the pack to do the same. All save Alla. I am not certain that she can actually eat animal flesh, so she abstained. Fenric took a bite in her place though. I must say that I was proud of my pack in that moment. I could see the hesitation and no small about of distaste cross many of their faces, but they all participated regardless.<br /> <br /> Once we had all eaten of the kill Tatiana brought back. She dipped one hand in the animal\u2019s blood and the other in ash from the fire and marked each of our foreheads, saying \u201cBy the blood that sustains us and the earth that enriches us, we regain our strength.\u201d Then in reverse order she wiped the marks from our foreheads and said, \u201cWe bear these marks on our hearts and return to the waking world unwanting. I felt refreshed after the ritual was over, and could tell that everyone else felt it too. I felt that Tatiana\u2019s words were especially meaningful. <br /> <br /> After the Soltice ritual Dacian invited the rest of us to go to the Summer Court\u2019s own Solstice celebration. I believe that we were all still energized from the rite, so we all agreed. Tatiana wore a nice suit of clothes that Dacian had a tailor make for her the other day. Dacian himself wore something nice, but not overly formal. I wore the best clothes I had, which doesn\u2019t really stand up to the others, but it\u2019s what I had. I did not think to get more clothes for special occasions. Dearbhail wore a peasant dress in a purple that matched her wings. I thought the effect was rather lovely.<br /> <br /> In the beginning Tatiana continued our discussion on the Pure and what we were going to do about them. We decided that we were going to call Siskur-da on discrediting the Pure in the area by way of disrupting Gunnar\u2019s exchange of items with the outside Pure. This will fulfill our spiritual obligation to call down a hunt on something/one, and will be particularly satisfying. I have not called Siskur-da on anyone in a while, so it will be good to be on a proper hunt again. For the most part I do not make a ritual hunt out of any of Reznik\u2019s targets, so while I have hunted those people it was not the same as the Siskur-da. <br /> <br /> After we had our conversation we decided to split up and go our separate ways. Tatiana wanted to try and entice a young lady to her bed, but does not speak German, so Dacian and Dearbhail in turns helped our young Russian fine a match. I thought they both looked rather happy when they left the room. Dacian found a young lady to spend some time with and left shortly after. I myself had not been planning on tempting anyone to my bed, but such is the way of things, my plans got changed. Later in the evening Dearbhail apparently decided that I looked unhappy. I tried to assure her that I was having a good time but she didn\u2019t seem to believe me. She coaxed me into dancing, which I will admit was fun. I have not been dancing in a long time. I felt a bit rusty in the beginning, but towards the end of the evening I was remembering my steps more confidently.<br /> <br /> I suppose it was the giddy feeling left from dancing and the good wine that flowed abundantly, but I in a spur of the moment decided to flirt with Dearbhail. She has flirted enough times with me, and decided suddenly that I wanted to flirt back. I was probably not the most suave, I will admit to being rather rusty at wooing young ladies as well as dancing with them. But despite my clumsy attempts Dearbhail seemed happy and willing to accompany me back to the hotel. I will say that her mood is infectious and she probably saw me smile more tonight that I have in a long time. She is truly a delight to be with.<br /> <br /> <br /> 24 June 1920<br /> <br /> This morning the pack talked about what kind of weapons we could make out of silver to any future fights with the Pure. Tatiana and I told of our planned attack on Gunnar and our possible desire for their help. Apparently the other night while we were looking for the proper place for the Solstice rite, Dacian was out the acquiring quite a bit of silver. He robbed at least five houses with the intention of getting enough silver for Lizette to make silver bullets, coated knives etc\u2026 for the pack. I believe that we agreed on several bullets for Wolfram, a pair of silver (brass) knuckles for Alla, and pairs of coated knives for Dearbhail and Dacian. I never thought I would be encouraging the creation of silver weapons, but I trust my pack with them. I will also admit to being curious at how well Lizette will do in the creation of said weapons. We\u2019ll see how they come out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Do you feel better, volchonok, now that we have hunted and brought our proper prey back to the pack?<br /> <br /> It did go well, did it not? I did not truly expect the non-Uratha to consume the meat and blood of the kill. It was a pleasant surprise, even with the Fenric grimacing so.<br /> <br /> It is true, Alla did not. I do not believe she can.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we do hunt a vampire that consumes human flesh. This is a special quality of their tribe, I believe, and Alla is not of the same one.<br /> <br /> Still and all, the rite to harness the changing of the season went well. And the rest of the night also. Our songbird was almost as giddy as a foolish volchonok and this was before we went to the fairy celebration. Well, before we who were not fairies went. She and Dacian and Lizette had been earlier, while we met with Krieger.<br /> <br /> No, just because she is excitable as a foolish volchonok does not mean foolish volchonoks can chase her. Especially not after she helped me gain the attentions of a lovely woman of fire at the celebration. Besides, if our alpha did not choose to pursue her, he is a hard hearted man and I do not understand him.<br /> <br /> Aha, they danced together did they? And left at the same time? Did you find me after all that to gossip like an old woman?<br /> <br /> No, I should have guessed. You found me to pester me about the Siskur-Dah and merely got distracted by our songbird, eh volchonok? Yes, Marek and I did discuss the Siskur-Dah. We will perform the rite tomorrow.<br /> <br /> He will be ritemaster.<br /> <br /> I will learn it. I do not need to be lectured by silly volchonoks to know that a werewolf must Hunt. I will likely learn it soon, Marek has promised, but we Hunt for the Pure\u2019s downfall. It will be good to be able to fight their spirits properly regardless of where they stand.<br /> <br /> I do not Hunt silly volchonoks, so no, you do not need to worry. Unless you have turned to the Pure?<br /> <br /> I did not think so. And yes, this is to do with Gunnar. Krieger believes the Ivory Claw will move against Wolfram, given time to learn of his intent, so we move first.<br /> <br /> He may soon. We have sent off two letters to her brother. One from Wolfram stating this intent, the other supposedly from Gunnar. The last is nothing but insulting. That was fun to help Lizette and Dacian write.<br /> <br /> We do not Hunt him directly for the good of the Uratha as a whole. If we do this properly, the Pure from elsewhere will believe the city unsafe for their kind. A German Pure, Ilsa, brings a shipment of some kind of spirit artifacts. She comes tomorrow night, to meet with the Ivory Claw, to arrange their delivery. If this delivery is soon, we will steal them and let her escape, to tell of the Vienna Pure\u2019s weakness. If not, tomorrow night we will interrupt this meeting, to kill him and have her escape.<br /> <br /> Krieger had a photograph. She is very pretty.<br /> <br /> I know the Oath of the Moon. Besides, she is Pure. Still, it will make it easier to allow her to escape.<br /> <br /> Impudent volchonok! I went off with a beautiful fairy because she was beautiful and for the pleasure of it. This Ilsa has nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> No volchonok. We will be in the city a while yet, you must be patient. Besides, we have hunted already tonight.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 23 June 1920 - Brunch<br /> <br /> Were I to have simply slept away the day, I suspect Tatiana would have found unpleasant ways to roust me. Given I returned with a large sack of silver, I believe she instead found other uses for her time. When I finally returned to the sun-filled dining room, I found brunch being served as well as Wolfram penning a letter to G\u00fcnter Esterh\u00e1zy. His honorable intentions to marry Lady Christina were noted. When I sat for toast, I politely requested stationary which matched that used by Gunner Hohenberg. Lizette and Tatiana assisted in forging a most impolite message to Lord Esterh\u00e1zy regarding his sister and particulars about her which should never be considered in such a rude fashion. Herr Hohenberg should truly learn to keep such thoughts and wishes to himself. I sealed the letter as the previously absconded one had been and requested the hotel make sure it reach the Post Office in time to make the air mail delivery today.<br /> <br /> I believe Gunner Hohenberg will find my shadow war with him will continue for as long as he poses a threat to Wolfram and Christina. Or if he interferes with any of the rest of my cabal for that matter. Now I believe I will enjoy the remainder of this saure L\u00fcngerl.<br /> <br /> 23 June 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> For a celebration meant to welcome the Solstice and the coming of the Summer King, it appeared to be a very desirous occasion. Perhaps it was only so to my perceptions, but it was enjoyable regardless. Lizette came and fairly quickly found other members of the Knights of the Third Hour. Also quite a few people that were interested in her.<br /> <br /> We separated to meet the various others as we would. I mingled lightly until I found the contests. A large Shadowsoul Fairest wore Hedgespun plate mail so dark, I was almost afraid. This Gyula the Black was easily the most skilled swordsman in attendance. He dominated the lists. I sighed heavily as I past the fencing list field. My abilities are still too untested. I did locate a fencing instructor in Paris, but have not spent much time learning as yet. It was such a romantic vision to see such skill and precision with steel. I continued around until I came upon a well groomed Butts. There a Chimera Windwing Beast which rightly called himself Lionwing excelled. The Bowman showed me that while fencing is an honorable gentleman\u2019s style, archery is demure, distanced, and deadly. Pulling myself away from my growing infatuation with Lionwing and his movements, I spotted the incoming monarch himself. Octavian, the Summer King, was a Fireheart Elemental with a presence to match his Seeming. In all, I knew that the rest of the cabal would enjoy such an event, so when we ventured back to the hotel, I made sure to inform the others. No sense in making conflicting plans after all.<br /> <br /> 23 June 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> Tatiana and Marek were prepared when we arrived in a different forest clearing beyond the edge of Vienna. This one showed signs of recent activity at all points. All the leaves and various underbrush had been removed, leaving a soft earthen floor. A downed tree served as a buffet, covered as it was with a feast of traditional Russian food. The ritual area was notably larger than before as a large bonfire licked and pulsed from the center. We made merry and cavorted in our woodland court for a time until Tatiana solemnly stood and walked into the woods. Marek raised a hand when we started call after her. She disappeared into the darkness with only the soft rustle of leaves to prove she was anything more than a forest shadow. We continued with our own celebration of the solstice, albeit slightly lessened without our Iron Master. She returned after an hour dragging a stag and looking pleased. Back at our clearing, Tatiana used Marek\u2019s hunting knife to carve a large section of the hind shank. The Uratha then came to each of us in turn offering the meat of her kill. Marek, of course, took the first bite. Alla looked sad as she declined, but Fenric \u201cbravely\u201d stumbled forward as his mistress shuffled him to the fore. Tatiana looked somewhat disappointed when the small man grimaced through his tiny bite. Wolfram came next and he surprised us all with not only his willingness but his enthusiasm for the ritual. He and I share that particular interest in the occult and unlike most of the cabal, we relish the experience. At that point, Lizette jumped up to be next. I\u2019m not sure if it was to prove herself worthy or to not be surpassed by Wolfram. Dearbh\u00e1il and I stepped forward before Tatiana could turn to us. We each tore into the blue offering with reverence to our task, eliciting a nod of approval from the Iron Master. After we had all partaken of the sacrifice, Tatiana reached into the edge of the bonfire and took up a hand full of soot. Using both hands, she marked our foreheads with blood and ash. She recited her ceremony regarding the blood and the earth giving us strength then wiped the marks off in opposite order. Tatiana proclaimed that our hearts now bore the marks and we would return to the waking world unwanting. As her ritual ended, I felt my confidence surge within. I was a bit confused about returning to the waking world as I was not aware we were in a Dreamscape, but I assumed it was more metaphor than magic.<br /> <br /> With the ritual complete, we collected our belongings and returned to the hotel. Several of us changed and cleaned away the evidence of our ritual before I gathered the cabal to return to the Summer Court inauguration. I selected an emerald outfit which was comfortable but reflected a bit more than just the color of my Court. Dearbh\u00e1il wore a peasant gown which seemed impossibly beautiful upon her form while the green and purple accented her wings. Lizette did return with us, though the interest she generated earlier did not subside this evening. The Wizened is peculiar in that multiple parties (both male and female) showed immediate interest, while she managed to be mostly polite in declining. I am unaware of the severity of her relationships to this point, but I did not think she was spoken for. But I seem to have wandered off topic. I mingled more freely and feel as though I may have engaged the entirety of the Summer Court before the evening was through. I eventually signaled Dearbh\u00e1il and Lizette so that we could all greet the incoming King. Octavian was very gracious, tolerating our Goblin\u2019s pyromaniacal tendencies with interest. Surprisingly, Lizette also managed to convince the Summer monarch to attend Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s next performance. That can only serve to raise her standing among all the Courts.<br /> <br /> Once we took our leave of Octavian, the cabal began to pair off. Dearbh\u00e1il and I separately helped Tatiana overcome the language barrier. Given she sauntered off with two Summer Courtiers at once, I\u2019d say her lack of German wasn\u2019t an issue. Lizette took her leave of us, while Wolfram and Christina politely disappeared. When I happened upon a Summer lady, Dearbh\u00e1il and Marek had just started the amusing game of talking. I knew the Fairest was interested so I left with my companion before the dancing started. The Treasured Shadowsoul left the hotel before I got her name, but I do hope I see her again. It was rare to find such beauty in darkness when also not in Darkness.<br /> <br /> 24 June 1920 - Breakfast<br /> <br /> We often command the hotel dining room when we meet and such was the case this morning. When we were sure there were no prying ears, we discussed plans for the evening. The local Pure, represented by none other than our least favorite Ivory Claw, expect a shipment of spiritual relics to arrive from the German Pure tonight. A woman from Berlin should be accompanying these tools and she seems to be responsible for judging the Pure of Vienna. Or at least, that is the notion upon which we are basing all our planning. If the shipment arrives with the German, then our goal is to finish Hohenberg while allowing her to escape. If the shipment is soon, then we shall wait to steal them, allow the German to escape, and then kill Hohenberg. The ultimate goal will be to convince the German Pure that Vienna is not as stable and under control as they believed. Given the resources needed to keep their shadow war going with the Uratha, cutting Vienna off from German assistance would deeply weaken the Ivory Claws. Thus endearing the cabal to the local Uratha as they strike down the Pure. Removing Hohenberg is merely a perk to assist Wolfram in his romance of Christina. Everyone wins, except the Pure.<br /> <br /> Lizette has already used over the half the silver I acquired in the making of bullets for Marek, more bullets for Wolfram, a pair of knuckledusters for Alla, and matching pairs of daggers for both Dearbh\u00e1il and myself. With our plans and Lizette\u2019s armaments in place, I believe we are prepared as we can be for whatever happens tonight.<br /> <br /> If I make no other entries into these shadowed pages, you will know, dear reader, that I was mistaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 24th September 1920<br /> <br /> Yesterday was a fun diversion, but I have work to do.<br /> <br /> After getting back from seeing Marlene I rested a bit, and in the early afternoon attended the Solstice gathering on the fairground, where the Spring Queen Sophie turned over rulership to the Summer King Octavian. There was jousting, archery, fencing and other events; handled in a manner I can only call \u201cRidiculously German.\u201d As much fun as it is to watch people wave around medieval weapons in the 20th Century, I searched out more scientific minds at the gathering, specifically other Knights of the Third Hour. They understand we are living in the future, not the past.<br /> <br /> It is not, perhaps, surprising given the recent unpleasantness that some were less receptive to my weapons building plans. They did helpfully point out that war is illegal now. I pointed out the Kindly Ones are still out there, and given the option I would prefer to run them down with a flamethrowing tank. We need not assault each other with such things. Also a surprisingly overwhelming number of Knights were men. Okay, maybe not too surprising.<br /> <br /> I did have some ideas for shoes with rocket thrusts which can double as flamethrowing assault footwear. They did have to admit my ideas were innovative.<br /> <br /> Having sufficiently impressed them with my genius, I met the others for the Werewolves\u2019 Solstice party. Tatiana did a hunt and returned with a deer that she and Marek took a bite of, and invited us to. Alla seemed disinclined, but when Wolfram did hell if I wasn\u2019t going to girl the hell up and do it too. Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il also did at that point, or they would have lost face. I manage to put down my sketch work long enough for the ritual, which had a bonfire and Tatiana doing a recital of ritual. Did you know she is the only one in our group who does not speak German? Strange. We all speak English and French, but she does not speak German. I would think if anyone wouldn\u2019t I wouldn\u2019t, since most of the German I heard involved a lot of screaming. Anyway.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s weird, is what I am saying.<br /> <br /> So, we returned to the party, and a decided chunk of the group decided it was time for hookups. I had taken care of my libido the previous night, and frankly could use a good night sleep, but I did hang around a bit, talk to Octavian with Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il, and make sure he knew where to find me if he needed flamethrowing tanks or streetcars with rotating blades and blowtorches. Actually, I don\u2019t think I mentioned that. See it seems it would be more useful on the back anyway, or even, EVEN, a way to leave a trail of smoke or oil which could make it difficult on a pursuer to drive or even see. Of course, smoke would make it harder to fire out the back with your built in machine gun or flamethrower, but then if you have a good enough flamethrower aiming is just a suggestion anyway and\u2026what was I talking about?<br /> <br /> Oh right, rereading helps. So after meeting Octavian, I did some general socializing (most of the other Knights went to bed. I am all about responsibility but there is no need to be boring. A lot of Wizened are crabby anyway) and made sure people knew where to go for their flamethrowing footwear or tank or plane needs, then decided to head back. Wolfram had wanted to discuss a matter, he said. Dearbh\u00e1il was all over the place and in a very good mood. She had been all night, which pleased me. She needed a boost after her concert was interrupted. Marek seemed interested in picking her up, but I left before they did. I was going to go eavesdrop see if they were having sex, but Wolfram distracted me. Marek is cute, Dearbh\u00e1il is cute, would be good all around I think. I wonder if either were virgins. Tatiana and Dacian also would up seducing or being seduced at the party\u2026I think Dearbh\u00e1il helped Tatiana a bit. I was right about her liking women. I am just not sure if she also likes men? I guess? Man I am too curious for my own good. One\u2019s friend\u2019s love lives are interesting, though.<br /> <br /> I did show off my idea for a box with four chainsaw blades that could be swung in a circle on a reinforced cable, but people seemed more interested in my accent and plans for the evening than PROGRESS. Ahem. Chainsaw flails are totally progress. Anyway.<br /> <br /> Wolfram wanted to be sure there were no issues between us about Christina. I won\u2019t, and didn\u2019t, pretend I was not disappointed. However, the fact is she is in a stage where she needs to be at least openly courting, because she is a noble, and frankly, nobles suck. Even though the nobility has been (rightfully) ousted, they have to go on like nothing happened and they did not lose all their power at some point. Ironically, this means the hypothetically powerful women of the nobility at this point have less power over their own lives than middle class women, but the men have the real power and essential ownership\u2026what am I talking about again? Zut!<br /> <br /> The point is having a nobility is bad and people need to be exploded\u2026wait.<br /> <br /> The point is having a nobility is bad and it should be shut down. There.<br /> <br /> Anyway. It\u2019s a good thing we got rid of our nobility, even if it was a bit decapitation happy, because at least it is better than being immolated. I mean I think. You know it\u2019s over right away\u2026<br /> <br /> Focus.<br /> <br /> Right right, Wolfram is a decent guy, despite being a noble (certainly not his upbringing, I mean the nobility has\u2026alright, okay, see above) and wanted to be sure I was okay, did not hate him, did not want to duel (I assume, he is also German) or anything like that. While he did not demonstrate anything approaching a willingness to back down\u2026he is also my friend. We get along well. Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re clearly misinterprets his behavior. But she always was a suspicious type, always willing to defend my honor. Kind of makes me wish I had some.<br /> <br /> Oh boy this is a rough morning for me. Okay summarize. I confirmed with Wolfram that I was not angry with him, he is my friend and I care. Having an adventure with Christina would be wonderful, and I would enjoy it, but not to the point of wanting her to stay single when it might mean she is forced to marry some mangy Werewolf (not that all Werewolves are mangy. I mean Tatiana maybe a little but just a little and I have not seen any sign of it from Marek. To be fair I have not from Gunnar but anyone with a mustache like that is trying to hide something. Maybe it is the mange, maybe it is the lycanthropy. I mean to be fair\u2026)<br /> <br /> CRAP<br /> <br /> Okay, just summarizing now<br /> <br /> Today, Morning<br /> <br /> Discussed with Motley, items required for forging for evening surveillance on the Ivory Claws. Hopefully not needed, but preparation is always important. Items include:<br /> <br /> -24 bullets that are silver, 12 in 9mm for Wolfram\u2019s Lugar and 12 in 7.65mm for my Star 14.<br /> <br /> -4 Knife coatings that are silver, two for Dacian two for Dearbh\u00e1il. They will not retain the blade for more than one solid hit that danger for the Werewolves due to the limitations to the medium. At least, not without some special Lizette cooking we don\u2019t have time for right now. I had some ide\u2026NO.<br /> <br /> -A pair of fighting knuckles that are silver for Alla.<br /> <br /> This will lose us just below half of our collected silver from Dacian, but it should have us well armed.<br /> <br /> I have wasted enough time. It is time to work.<br /> <br /> Done.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VIII</i><br /> <br /> Oh Lizette, a little off subject today\u2026<br /> <br /> The Players designed the Solstice rite, which was cool.<br /> <br /> The German Ivory Claws Pure, Ilsa, is designed as a long term antagonist. I drew aside the veil a moment to note I would like to keep her alive for the late game, possibly build romantic tension if someone wanted to. We discussed how the players would like to see a meeting and potential ambush play out, and they were interested in having that happen and willing to hold off a bit. So we are going to go with what seems most fun for us.<br /> <br /> Mostly IC stuff past that. Worked out a semi-coherant system for how to use the silver Dacian took in his crime wave. No idea how realistic it is.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed. Next time is the Meeting to be spied on, Siskur-da ritual, and a concert. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:12:47-07:00","id":613898,"title":"","content":"So, some of the players were talking, and we wondered if people had theories about who was playing which characters in the various WoD games I have up. So I figured we would offer a chance at discussion of it. In order to protect identities of players, I have not been in a habit of confirming links between players between games. But if you are curious and follow more than one game you can ask. Anything else you ask about will be up to the players if they want to answer. But I will confirm or deny common links between characters if you ask.<br /> <br /> Some facts<br /> <br /> In the four New WoD and one Classic WoD games there are 13 different players. 2 are/were in all five games. 1 is in four games, 4 are in three games, and 6 are only in one game each, at least of WoD games.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rather you be nice\u2026I don\u2019t want to hear \u201cI think player A plays X and Y because they suck\u201d or anything, I am proud of my players. A number of them will be peering in to enjoy this too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any theories I would enjoy hearing them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T00:36:23-07:00","id":620964,"title":"","content":"1920 Vienna: Our heroes take part in a Siskur-dah rite, watch a concert, and observe a meeting. And get up to a few things on their own. Dacian lacks a journal this time due to family stuff demanding his attention\u2026he hopes to cover both sessions next time.<br /> <i><br /> Session IX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 24 June 1920<br /> <br /> After our discussion about silver weapons Tatiana and I asked Lizette if she would be able to make a wooden mask for the Siskur-dah rite that we\u2019re going to perform today. She agreed readily enough and asked what we\u2019d like a mask of. I explained that it needed to represent the Pure, so I suggested making it resemble Gunnar. We are kind of using him to represent the Pure in Vienna since it is specifically him that we plan to attack later. So, while Lizette went to work on the mask and the silver weapons I worked on grinding up one of the long bones from the deer Tatiana took down for the Solstice rite. I will use the bone dust today for the Siskur-dah rite. I plan on using as much of the animal as I can for rites and charms. I am also planning on making charms for the rest of the pack. I will use some of the bone and carve something appropriate to each person, or perhaps just something for luck. I haven\u2019t decided yet.<br /> <br /> During our discussion this morning we also made plans for spying on Gunnar and his German ally later tonight. Only a few of us are actually going to be present for the Pure\u2019s meeting, since some of our group are not quite as stealthy as others. Plus a larger group has the possibility of attracting more attention. Wolfram mentioned that he could use one of his abilities to separate his spirit from his body and go with us to spy on the Pure. He would be invisible to the spirits that work for the Pure since they are in slightly different places in the spirit world. The only thing about this power is that he must set himself alight to activate it. It will appear that his body has been charred while his spirit is away and he will be whole and healed when his spirit returns. He assured us that he would be fine, but said that he would need someone there to put out the fire once he signaled them to. The plan was for Wolfram to set himself on fire in the bathtub so the shower could be quickly turned on to put him out. Fenric volunteered to be the one to douse him. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> I think the Siskur-dah ritual went well. The rest of the pack was present, but only Tatiana, volchonok, Dedecek, Ochranny and I participated. Tatiana and volchonok represented the Pure, while the rest of us \u201chunted\u201d them. The whole thing was silent to represent our intentions of being stealthy during our attack on the Pure. I used the bone dust I ground up earlier to make a line down the center of my face. I also carried my rifle, but did not use it. I do plan on using it during the actual attack, but did not feel the need to use it during the rite. I acted out hunting down Tatiana and in the end cut my hand and grabbed the wooden mask that Tatiana work with my injured hand in order to leave a bloody smear across the face of it. I felt that the rite went well. It was not overly long, but I got the distinct impression that the spirits approved.<br /> <br /> That evening we all dressed in our best and went to Dearbhail\u2019s concert. I was told that the security for this performance was much higher than it was for the last one. Probably just in case the Communists try anything violent again, they\u2019ll be prepared to better stop them.<br /> <br /> While at the concert we noticed several people, some of which were not good in my opinion. We noticed Gloria, the Theosophist in the crowd as well as the Vampire Prince and his second in command. Alla talked to the Lancea Sanctum woman. They seemed to get along, and the other woman was fairly flirty. That was evident even from where I sat. Wolfram pointed out the four or five other vampires that were in the crowd. He told us about Maximillian\u2019s warning concerning the Lancea Sanctum woman and her penchant for \u201cblood bonding\u201d people to her. I\u2019m not sure how this blood bond works, but it does not sound like something I want to see happen to Alla. Blood is a powerful component in many rites and can be used against someone if you know how. The same goes for true names. If you know the name of someone that gives you a certain amount of power over that person. That is one of the reasons I don\u2019t use my actual name when I take on those side jobs.<br /> <br /> We did our best to leave the concert unobtrusively but ended up being spotted by Gloria as we left. I believe that she followed us to the hotel where Wolfram was going to do his own ritual and the rest of us were going to change. Tatiana headed straight for the caf\u00e9 we agreed upon as a rendezvous point to wait for us. Lizette, Dacian and I changed into dark clothing. Lizette actually put on a skin tight suit with a hood. It was rather conspicuous in its design if you ask me, but she said it was her sneaking clothes. I do not believe we were followed when we left the hotel.<br /> <br /> We made it to the Gentleman\u2019s club where the Pure were going to have their meeting. We went into an alley and found a second story window that looked like a good ingress point. Wolfram just walked through the wall and went upstairs. Dacian on the other hand scaled up the wall and opened the window. He tied a rope so the rest of us could climb up after him. I think we did an admirable job climbing. It wasn\u2019t the easiest way in, but it provided us with less possibilities of being spotted by someone in the club.<br /> <br /> We listened in on the meeting between Gunnar and Ilsa. The young lady expressed an interest in dropping off the items in a crypt nearby. Gunnar voiced his dissatisfaction with this plan, but Ilsa was adamant. Apparently Gunnar and the other Ivory Claws in Vienna have an understanding that they don\u2019t do anything in a crypt or graveyard because of the possibility of tainting any such actions with the aspect of death. He was vocal about not desecrating a crypt, while she obviously took pleasure in his discomfort. She said that the goods would be on a train arriving in two days and that she would wire the information to him as to when and where the items would arrive and he told her where to send the message to.<br /> <br /> It should not be hard to disrupt their working relationship or trust in one another. Ilsa already does not have a high opinion of Gunnar and his people based on the way she was talking to him and the fact that she explicitly set up the place to bring the items as somewhere that would make Gunnar uncomfortable. Gunnar in return was not very polite with Ilsa during their conversation. <br /> <br /> Ilsa did bring a couple of what I can only describe as National Pride spirits to the meeting. They did not seem to spot us and left with Ilsa. We met up with the others after they left. We went back out the way we came in.<br /> <br /> From what I can tell the Gentleman\u2019s club is not a front for the Pure. It does seem to be a location that they frequent, but it is not a place to hide their activities.<br /> <br /> Also as mentioned is seems that the Ivory Claws have an aversion to dealing with anything related to death. They generally do not deal with ghosts at all, which might be something in our favor. We have at least two people in our group, myself included, that can see and talk to ghosts. We may be able to recruit a ghost to keep an eye on the Pure for us when they go to the cemetary.<br /> <br /> Wolfram suggested that he could go to the tomb that Ilsa had mentioned and take a look around to familiarize himself with the area and any ghosts nearby. Dacian offered to go along since he can literally blend in with the shadows. Tatiana and I would leave too distinct a scent, so we agreed that we should not go. Apparently Dacian can also completely mask his scent, so the Pure will not even know that he was there. Handy skill, that.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail warned Alla that the Lancea Sanctum woman\u2019s main desire tonight was to drink her blood and for Alla to drink her blood. Alla explained the blood bonding that would occur from such an action and Dearbhail became upset. She really did not like the idea of the other woman doing that to Alla. She looked at me and Tatiana and asked if we could do anything about that. Who says that our sweet and happy songbird cannot be blood-thirsty as well? Tatiana suggested killing the Lancea Sanctum woman and making it look like the Pure did it. I suggested that any action should be taken as we\u2019re leaving Vienna, but we will need to discuss this further before anything is done. I do not want to make things difficult politically for Alla and Fenric in this town.<br /> <br /> Frustrated at not being able to do anything earlier, Tatiana suggested that we go hunt for Maximillian\u2019s wayward \u201cgrandchild.\u201d Alla agreed to go and I said that I would be happy to hunt with them. Tracking people in a city is distinctly harder than tracking someone in the forest. There are so many more scents that overlap and cover others in the city. Tatiana has his scent though, so if we are close to him we will be to find our quarry. This may mean going to known communist hangouts and looking for his scent, but we will find him. It will be good to hunt alongside my pack mates. I usually hunt alone as Reznik, so this will be a nice change. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What are you doing here volchonok? That is a place of the Pure\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Pure have gone. Even so.<br /> <br /> Oh, you think I cannot keep watch alone, do you volchonok?<br /> <br /> When did you become such a grandmother? I will not run off and do something stupid, merely because our plan is working to our best advantage, even if it does mean that I will not wet my claws tonight. I did not even muddy up his precious gilt carriage. Or invite her and her fascism spirits for coffee.<br /> <br /> I am being snappish? I, volchonok? I would show you snappish if we were not at a cafe across from Pure territory.<br /> <br /> A wise choice, volchonok. No, Wolfram, Dacian and Fenric have not gone off to do something stupid either. The artifacts are to be taken to a crypt in two days time. Dacian and Wolfram have gone to see if they can convince any ghosts there to be allies. Fenric guards Wolfram\u2019s body at a hotel.<br /> <br /> That is what you get, staying to watch a songbird sing rather than paying attention.<br /> <br /> Yes, I did tell you to stay. Did you at least watch over the woman Gloria?<br /> <br /> The Theosophist, who Lizette hit with her hammer to get the Golden Eagle? The who noticed us leave?<br /> <br /> Bah, you are a foolish volchonok. Yes, back to Wolfram. He has separated his spirit from his body, to be scentless and see spirits. His body rests in Fenric\u2019s car,as I said. Dacian used fairy magic to become scentless himself.<br /> <br /> We go vampire hunting. Probably the flesh eating one. I have his scent, it should only be a short time marching through Communist Vienna to find it again. And the other quarry requires preparation.<br /> <br /> Ah, yes. Dearbhail arrived back before you. You saw the woman Alla sat with? She is Magdalena, a vampire who apparently goes around enslaving other vampires with mind controlling blood, or some such. This displeases our songbird.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it will not do. And it will help us accomplish our Hunt. If we can lead the vampires to believe the Pure killed this Magdalena, it will do much to weaken their hold on Vienna, surely.<br /> <br /> Are you not done bouncing around about that, volchonok? Yes, it was a good rite. Did you enjoy being a foolish Pure servant instead of a foolish volchonok?<br /> <br /> It was fun, yes, to pretend to be some kind of arrogant ignorant failure of a werewolf. It is also good to be on the Hunt again.<br /> <br /> That again, volchonok?<br /> <br /> No, I am not becoming snappish again. And no, I will not go running off into the night alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 24th June 1920<br /> <br /> Thus far, successful endeavors. I managed to get all my work done on the weapons that are silver in approximately one standard hour. As usual, I work far faster when left alone and unobserved. I am far from the only member of The Holy Order of the Third Hour with such capabilities, so they had facilities to work with for those with our\u2026quirks. I believe they refer to it as the Boon of the Brownie.<br /> <br /> I stopped out at a caf\u00e9 for a light lunch and some glamour after. Apparently a woman of my height carrying such a large backpack draws some attention, but people certainly move out of my way, perhaps because the pack towers over my head.<br /> <br /> I intended a nap before the evening\u2019s work, but attended the Werewolves\u2019 rituals. It was a different sort of ritual this time\u2026different from the angry one or the hunting one. This one was to hunt better, which seems like it would have been more handy before the hunting one, not that Tatiana seemed to need help, but just seems more practical. I don\u2019t really understand their rituals. I mean, they are entertaining, but they clearly hold great significance to them that they don\u2019t to me. But then, they also never attend mass, either of them, so they are clearly going in a different direction. Of course, I am just sort of assuming the rituals are similar to mass, I don\u2019t really know. I mostly just know Russians are never Catholic. I sort of thought Czechs were, but they are near Germany, which isn\u2019t, so maybe not. I guess maybe he is Lutheran? I never asked. Dacian never attended mass either. I mean Dearbh\u00e1il does, of course. The Irish are Catholics, right? I would hate to be the only Catholic here. That is a scary thought.<br /> <br /> Maybe Marek is Orthodox like the Russians.<br /> <br /> I had this idea for a grappling pack at the ritual. Basically it fires a pressurized grappling hook and rope at a triangulated target and uses a small thruster to propel you up as it recoils the rope, allowing swift ascent. No useful if you can fly but who can these days. I hope they don\u2019t think I am rude to sketch at these rituals. I mean, I do at mass.<br /> <br /> Afterward, I took a short nap, while Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re insisted on standing guard. I am not sure why, I am sure Wolfram would have kept me safe. I did warn him about waking me up\u2026since sleeping in the burned out remains of my town, being woken from a deep slumber by German men usually means I go for the eyes, which would be frankly unfortunate in Wolfram\u2019s specific case.<br /> <br /> Evening came, and with it Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s show and our planned espionage. The show was lovely\u2026 Dearbh\u00e1il was slow to warm up but when she hit her stride she did excellently. I wore my red gown, which I made recently and had not shown to my motley before I put it on tonight. I fall out of it less than the wine color, and had not cleaned the one I wore a couple nights ago. Anyway, the show; only wrinkle was I saw Gloria, the woman I beat in the head with a hammer, in the audience, but she did not cause any trouble. Oh, and Alla went and sat with some Vampire woman. I don\u2019t really know, I avoid Vampires, not really wanting to be one.<br /> <br /> The trip was good overall. I met Wolfram, Marek, Fenric and Dacian at the hotel, and changed into my stealth suit, a Lizette \u00c9toile original design, which Dacian took a somewhat lecherous interest in. We fanned out from the room to head to the Noble\u2019s club where the meeting was to take place.<br /> <br /> So\u2026Wolfram needed to set himself on fire and burn up for a projection power to work. That is frankly the most disturbing catch I have ever heard of. I mean there are plenty of good reasons to be on fire, but so you can lay down and burn up is not one of them, even if you un burn later. Okay, maybe not plenty of good reasons, but plenty of reasons. I mean, people rarely mug people on fire, or assault them in the street. People are likely to get out of your way in the queue. I have never been proselytized to while on fire, nor have I seen anyone who has. And no matter how brave someone is, when someone on fire runs directly at them, they tend to run.<br /> <br /> As I think of it, maybe being on fire does have useful applications. This requires more study. Not being afraid of being on fire removes some limitations of fire as a weapon. Of course, there is the burning. That will need to be dealt with, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so we went to this Gentleman\u2019s Club, and like any other trip to a Gentleman\u2019s Club I have ever taken (which is never, but you have to start somewhere) I brought a big enough bomb to level it. The club practically cried out to be reduced to rubble. Not literally, that would be a sign of insanity, but you could almost feel the Smugness wafting from it. I mean, when I say almost, I don\u2019t really mean almost as in on the edge but there is an implication. Regardless, I brought a bomb.<br /> <br /> I climbed the wall behind Dacian (given his ogling I did not feel like having him behind me) and slipped inside. I was glad I did not have the experimental light reflecting mirrors system (LRM) for invisibility, as it would have made me incredibly obvious if it did not work, and it didn\u2019t. Eavesdropping on the meeting was simple. The two Werewolves met and did some verbal sparring. Mostly the German, Ilsa, taunting the Austrian, Gunner, who seemed to have a burst of pomposity which all but cried out for a burst of fiery doom, but I stayed my hand. We needed information. Ilsa angered him by saying she would drop off the items at a crypt, which angered him. I took nobles taunting notes.<br /> <br /> After, we slipped out. We had our information, and were well pleased. I slipped back into the hotel and changed into some less form fitting clothing. Rather than put lady red back on I wore one of my work outfits. I had considered going to see Marlene, but the others were not taking the night off so hell if I would be.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Dacian are going to scout the crypt. Wolfram hopes to meet a useful ghost, and Dacian wishes to ensure access and have a look around. Alla, Tatiana and Marek are off to look for Vampires, specifically this Macellarius one. They plan to hit \u201cCommunist Vienna\u201d as Tatiana keeps calling it. I am sure there is something productive I could get up to\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026or destructive.<br /> <i><br /> End Session IX</i><br /> <br /> The rite was well described game, and was a pretty good scene. Kudos to Marek and Tatiana\u2019s players who actually took the time to work out this (and previous) rites.<br /> <br /> Lizette, with Brownie\u2019s Boon, is a building machine. She got the mask and ammunition made in no time flat.<br /> <br /> On leaving the theater, all everyone (well, everyone but Dearbh\u00e1il) had to do was score one success on a Stealth check to sneak out past Gloria. Given the enrapturing concert that was all it took, but Wolfram failed, and so Gloria got a roll and got a success. His player has been suitably shamed.<br /> <br /> What was more hilarious, though, was everyone got out and, except Tatiana, made Stealth and Perception rolls. What happened was everyone Stealthed well enough that Gloria could not find them\u2026but Gloria Stealthed well enough that they also lost track of her. It was funny.<br /> <br /> We debating the \u2018wavelength\u201d for the Elemental Oracles projection with the edition change. In Balance of Shadows we\u2019ve been using it so it only sees/interacts with Ghosts, but I let the group discuss how they wanted to handle it in Golden Eagle. It was deemed more crossover friendly to let it interact with whatever is in Twilight, so we went with that. Balance of Shadows is, of course, unchanged.<br /> <br /> If you read this and other game journals, note the comments above about guessing about common players. We are curious what you think. Though comments and questions of other sorts are welcome as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T09:43:35-07:00","id":624445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=613898#post613898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, some of the players were talking, and we wondered if people had theories about who was playing which characters in the various WoD games I have up. So I figured we would offer a chance at discussion of it. In order to protect identities of players, I have not been in a habit of confirming links between players between games. But if you are curious and follow more than one game you can ask. Anything else you ask about will be up to the players if they want to answer. But I will confirm or deny common links between characters if you ask.<br /> <br /> Some facts<br /> <br /> In the four New WoD and one Classic WoD games there are 13 different players. 2 are/were in all five games. 1 is in four games, 4 are in three games, and 6 are only in one game each, at least of WoD games.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rather you be nice\u2026I don\u2019t want to hear \u201cI think player A plays X and Y because they suck\u201d or anything, I am proud of my players. A number of them will be peering in to enjoy this too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any theories I would enjoy hearing them!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I started doing this kinda of thinking after Malibu Dream House started (at that point I was only reading Balance of Shadows), but then I decided I didn't want to know. I don't want the characters to blend with each other in my mind just cause I know it's the same player. I think I will want to know after the games are done, then it will be interesting to put the connections together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T10:06:06-07:00","id":624458,"title":"","content":"That's cool. I understand that approach as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T23:41:02-07:00","id":636731,"title":"","content":"Just caught up!<br /> Nice time period and locations to explore, and a wonderful cast of characters.<br /> I'm a bit surprised at the lack of Mages among the PCs, given how easy they are to involve in crossovers, but I'm even more surprised to be interested by the Forsaken. They actually made me pick up the book again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T01:16:48-07:00","id":636805,"title":"","content":"Anteros: Glad you enjoyed the characters. I gave people fairly free reign with what to pick...Beast was not yet at a point that they were options, but everything else was. One player seriously considered a Demon, but I am pretty happy with what we got. And yea, the Forsaken are pretty neat. I suspect a reason for the lack Mages is none of the players were very familiar with <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>, and they can seem pretty daunting compared to, say, Changelings or Werewolves. I do appreciate the feedback! I am sure the players enjoy hearing you like the characters!<br /> <br /> Talking to ghosts, shooting at Werewolves, seducing nobles, and hunting vampires. All in a day\u2019s work for the crew of Golden Eagle. Note the opening of Lizette\u2019s journal is rather racy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session X</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 24 June 1920<br /> <br /> Today has continued to be an eventful day. Dacian and Wolfram went ahead to the Hollenberg crypt so they could check it and the surrounding area out. See if there were any ghosts or spirits worth mentioning etc\u2026 Tatiana, Dearbhail and I went to the different cafes to get drinks and try and see if Tatiana could pick up Gustov\u2019s scent. Dearbhail got several drinks bought for her over the course of the evening and we didn\u2019t stand out from the crowd. Dearbhail enjoyed the attention and we all took advantage of anonymity. Eventually Tatiana caught the scent she was looking for and we tracked Gustov to an old building that was damaged in the riots. <br /> <br /> Gustov himself had blood down the front of his shirt, not his own, and was looking less than completely sane. I attacked the crazy vampire, but before I could step back again he grabbed me. He has quite the grip, I will say that. Tatiana attacked him and managed to do a bit more damage than I did. She is a very effective combatant. Even Dearbhail tried to tackle Gustov. I was glad that he already had a grip on me at that point so he was unable to grab Dearbhail. She is not weak, but she is more delicate than I am when it comes to shrugging off injury, and I did not want to see her hurt.<br /> <br /> After a few moments I was able to break free of Gustov\u2019s hold and got away. It wasn\u2019t long after that I heard other vampires coming in fast, in animal form. I am given to understand that these are the Gangrel clan. Those that can assume the form of an animal. There were five of them coming and we did not know if they were coming to attack or aid Gustov so we decided that a tactical retreat was in order. Tatiana had gotten a taste of his blood and would be able to find him no matter where he went, so we had no worries about losing him.<br /> <br /> As we left I saw at least one of the, in the form of an eagle, abruptly change course and head away from the building. Not sure what the others did, but at least one of them thought it better to run than to engage us in a fight. I\u2019m not sure of our odds if we had tried to face them all at once tonight. As much as I\u2019d like to claim otherwise I do not think that things would have gone well for us. I am a pragmatist. I will say that Tatiana agreed with the suggestion of leaving, so I do not think I was too far off. There was also Dearbhail to take into account. She is not a combatant and I would not see her injured.<br /> <br /> We arrived back at the hotel to find a note from Christina, or perhaps Marlene, asking us as a group to come to her house. There was a second note from Lizette asking for us to bring her pistol and the silver bullets she made for it. Dearbhail gathered up the weapon and we headed over to find out what was so urgent.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, there had been a werewolf prowling around the grounds earlier this evening. Lizette warned it off by shooting it with a rifle. The round was not silver so it did not do any lasting damage, but it still hurts to get shot no matter the composition of the bullet, so he or she left. Tatiana did not recognize the scent, but I did. It was someone from the club. I could not give you a description of the person, but I\u2019ll know them if I see them.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Dacian told the rest of us what they had been doing tonight. Turns out that there was a ghost in the crypt. His name is Franz Ludwig Von Hollenberg. He has apparently appointed himself the protector of the family crypts as a way to preserve his name and make amends for his less than noble death. I believe he tripped over a lover or his wife while intoxicated and fell down the stairs, breaking his neck. The others discussed the fact that the Pure plan to store items in the Hollenberg family crypt, but that Wolfram and Dacian plan to take care of it. I believe assuring the ghost that we only had the family\u2019s best interests at heart shown us in a favorable light. So we should have his cooperation.<br /> <br /> I think that Dacia also managed to talk Franz Ludwig into giving him fencing lessons. At least the shadowy man broke into a store and stole a pair of decent quality blades for that purpose. Should be interesting at the very least. Ghost fencing lessons. I don\u2019t think that is something that has ever crossed my mind, and I\u2019ve seen and done a lot of interesting things in my lifetime.<br /> <br /> In order to explain why a wolf showing up on the property was not a good thing, Wolfram explained to Christina and Marlene about Gunnar being a Pure and what his intentions were. This led to a discussion about the rest of us, specifically what we are. He must have explained things well because the two ladies treated us the same as they have in the past. There was no suspicion or wariness in their behavior. We had talked about revealing our natures to the ladies earlier and decided it was a good idea, especially if Wolfram was going to continue to court Christina. There are things about us that will come up or be revealed, so it is best to get it out in the open so there are no surprises later on.<br /> <br /> It was decided that we would set a watch for the rest of the night, just in case the werewolf came back. As the rest of us had been awake all day, Alla volunteered to stand watch. Hopefully it will be uneventful.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 25 June 1920<br /> <br /> This morning Tatiana brought up the idea of hunting Gustov during the day, while he slept. I thought this was a good idea as it would keep other vampires from interfering since they would be asleep as well. I do not think that Christina and Marlene were quite prepared to hear such conversation over a meal. Dearbhail stepped in with a distraction for the ladies while the rest of us discussed our options. In the end it was decided that Wolfram and Dearbhail would stay behind with the ladies while Tatiana would go into the area and scare off anyone that was hanging around. Dacian would scout ahead and make sure that there were no innocents in the building. There were a couple of homeless people in the alley, but Tatiana quickly convinced them to relocate.<br /> <br /> After that Tatiana told Lizette exactly where Gustov was sleeping and the slight fae woman snuck in and placed the bomb where it would do the most damage. Once she was out of the building she set off the bomb. Gustov was not happy to say the least, if his roar was any indication. The rest of us attacked as the opportunity arose. Lizette hit him with her flame-thrower, which she had stashed in a backpack and brought with her. Tatiana and I attacked with claws and teeth. I got a taste of his blood this time as well and have to agree with Tatiana that it tastes different than human blood. There is just something to it that makes it more appealing. This is probably not a good thing. Alla did explain to us about blood bonding, and it made me wonder if non-vampires can be bound by their blood as well. Something to ask Alla when she wakes up tonight.<br /> <br /> Lizette was not the only one to use fire as a weapon. Dacian had a Molotov cocktail in hand and deftly snuck it into the pocket of Gustov\u2019s jacket. I\u2019ve seen people pick pockets to take things, but rarely have I seen someone sneak something into a pocket. It worked though and once the cocktail exploded Gustov fell unconscious. Fenric explained that Gustov was in something called Torpor and that he could now be killed, which we did by removing his head from his body. He promptly disintegrated into bones and Fenric took Gustov\u2019s skull to give to Alla to present as a trophy for killing the rogue vampire. This would be the proof for Maximillian that Gustov was in fact dead.<br /> <br /> Once that was done we left as quickly as we could so as to not get caught by the authorities who came to investigate the fire. It would not have been wise to be caught at the scene. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> There, are you satisfied now volchonok? We have had our proper fight. I told you this would be better.<br /> <br /> Last night was a good hunt the whole way through, volchonok, none of your \u2018until\u2019s. Only a few hours to catch the scent of a dead man in a crowded space. It helped that many rushed to buy our songbird drink after I got the first. They came in close, bringing their scent to me.<br /> <br /> I surrendered nothing. We had where he nested and I had the taste of his blood. It was a heady thing, headier than most. It makes me wonder if all vampires taste that way...<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, when five of those Gangrel vampires made their approach, we fell back. When you see the hunters snare in the brush, you do not wait for it to tighten around your leg so that you have to gnaw it off. Not unless you stood to gain somehow.<br /> <br /> There was nothing to gain! Nothing that was not gained this morning, when the sun\u2019s rays kept the Gangrel asleep. Besides, this way allowed Lizette to blow something up, and use her flamethrower. She was restless, last night. It is good to have something allowable to destroy.<br /> <br /> Of course, she did not alone. I must be allowed to destroy things as well, and Marek and Dacian did their part. The explosion when Dacian slipped the Molotov cocktail into his pocket was spectacular.<br /> <br /> I do not believe the Gangrel and this Maximilian are on speaking terms. So the Gangrels will not know when Fenric presents the skull as proof. But yes, we will perhaps have to deal with these hunters. They have disrupted our activities twice now. But there are better situations, and better times.<br /> <br /> Indeed, volchonok, you are thinking now. Last night was not a better time, as the Pure were threatening the pack\u2019s mates while we were avoiding the snare. It is good Lizette was there, and shot so well. It is also probably good that she did not have the silver bullets. It gives less away.<br /> <br /> No, it was not Gunnar himself, nor was it Ilsa. I presume still that Gunnar sent them. Troubling questions are raised otherwise, as to why they came here.<br /> <br /> No, silly volchonok, their spirit creatures could not have followed Wolfram. The wolf arrived at Christina\u2019s before he did. He contacted the ghosts at the crypt last night, do you not recall? I understand this has gained us an ally for our Hunt, one skilled with a blade, if a bit clumsy with drink and mistresses. Presumably less of an issue now that he is dead.<br /> <br /> No volchonok, we do not run with this ally tonight. Tonight we prepare. Tomorrow, we Hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans<br /> </b><br /> 24th June 1920<br /> <br /> It turned out my last minute decision to visit Marlene would be important.<br /> <br /> The festivities, to that point, had gone well. Marlene was more than happy to invite me into her room, and I had unfastened her gown and pulled it down to pin her arms and expose her breasts (note to self, this definitely gets the desired reaction from Marlene. Do it again) when I noticed (somehow) movement from the window behind her across the lawn. I told her to get down and leapt over to the window. It was a white wolf sniffing around the front door.<br /> <br /> I asked Marlene for the largest gun she could give me, and she gave me a Mannlicher, as I did not have the Star 14 with bullets that are silver on hand. Once I had the Mannlicher, I told her to wake Christina before the gunfire did. I am pretty sure she was not fast enough. After spending a moment whispering to the rifle, to use my Contracts of Artifice and Animation, I fired a shot and hit the wolf directly in the head. It being a Werewolf, looked back and saw the Mannlicher sticking out of the window and fled. I doubt it was injured for long.<br /> <br /> I told Marlene to call the hotel and be sure a note was sent to the room with Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re. I then stood guard until Wolfram and Fenric arrived. I briefed them (giving Wolfram a paper thin lie about why I was there but enough to protect Marlene\u2019s reputation.) Wolfram took charge and saw to Christina and Marlene (who was keeping me plied with tea.) Then Dacian arrived with a pair of swords, and the others got there soon after. Dearbh\u00e1il kindly brought my Star 14 and my bullets that are silver, which made me feel better about if the Werewolf returned to discuss my shooting him in the side of the face.<br /> <br /> The Mannlicher was a powerful rifle, but as I had observed in the past problematic for me to use. I can set it up for a sitting or reclined fire position but it is too long to be wieldy. Of course building some upper body strength will help, but at the same time I feel maybe some sort of harness would help too. It seems difficult to simply have a standing one, but I bet I could wire something so I could do it. Hmmmm. Anyway.<br /> <br /> We decided to remain at the house, with Alla standing guard. By now, Wolfram had made Christina and Marlene aware of the particulars of our group. I had other things to deal with so I was in and out and I did not catch everything. I know Christina chalked up a lot to me being a Faerie. It may have lulled her into a false sense of security. I need to have a long discussion with her about all this. Wolfram was rather thorough, I hope. I don\u2019t think I could explain Vampires anyway without her wanting to kill Alla. \u201cVampires drink people\u2019s blood and turn them into more Vampires. Sometimes, one bites you and makes you an obese Vampire apparently.\u201d No, that does not sound like an explanation that would help Alla.<br /> <br /> He did have to be reminded not to try to sneak off with Christina, while I also had to let Marlene know she was not going to be compromised further this evening. Unfortunately, given her obvious favoritism of me keeping me plied with tea and Cognac, I cannot imagine anyone missed her increased interest.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019ll sleep now, alone, and discuss how to further deal with the situation when I awake. My brain it needs to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25th June 1920<br /> <br /> My brain seems disinclined to stick to the projects that she is assigned. I woke up from a dream of the previous evening\u2019s tableau only with the roles reversed and Christina also present due to thudding in one of the other rooms. I don\u2019t know by whom but I am not happy with them whoever they are.<br /> <br /> At breakfast Tatiana was\u2026herself\u2026and surged forward with all the bluster I suppose I should expect. She wanted to hunt the cannibal vampire, and put things very bluntly in front of Christina and Marlene that, as nobles (and ex-nobles), they did not seem quite prepared to hear. Dearbh\u00e1il stepped in quickly to sort of distract them, though Tatiana seemed undaunted. She (Tatiana) was keen on killing him during the day, after the previous attempt turned into a Carthian ambush using him as a lure. We made a plan, with Dacian, Fenric, Tatiana, Marek and I moving to slay the vampire, and Wolfram and Dearbh\u00e1il staying back and standing guard. Alla was, of course, asleep. I am still scared of Vampires.<br /> <br /> We swung by the hotel, and I reassured Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re all was well, as well as picked up the flamethrower for me and a couple Molotov cocktails for Fenric and Dacian.<br /> <br /> The Flamethrower is a fascinating invention. For sheer terror, nothing beats wading in flinging fire everywhere. No one likes being on fire. Well, maybe if there was a good reason. And I had time to prepare. And I could impress someone.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is somewhat indiscriminant and can set the whole building on fire\u2026but really, if you can\u2019t handle being in a burning building you should not be out killing people, much less setting them on fire. And they are never happy about the burning building either. Maybe we should practice escaping a burning building so I can set a building on fire and they can escape without being hurt. Sounds like a good team building exercise. Hopefully they are not afraid of a little fire. By little I mean building. Which is not little. Usually. Unless it is a little building. But that would not be\u2026I am off subject.<br /> <br /> Tatiana effortlessly hunted the Vampire down. I blew up the damaged building it was in but did distressingly little to it, and it seemed to heal rapidly. While the Werewolves fought it I waited then when they moved away a moment I cut loose with the flamethrower. That seemed to do it in. Even Vampires can only walk around as a bonfire for so long.<br /> <br /> Now that that is done, we move onto dealing with this Pure menace and who knows? Someday maybe even the necklace we actually came here for. I am beginning to get tired of all the German.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session X</i><br /> <br /> Session 10 already!<br /> <br /> The Gangrel were Carthians, hoping to kill some Invictus when they came after beast ridden Kindred. Gustav himself was not Carthians, or anything really anymore. The fight was a good workout for our Uratha practicing vs. something dangerous but not yet fighting Pure (that will probably be next session, but we will see).<br /> <br /> Of course, we will have to see how far Dearbh\u00e1il is willing to push toward fighting Magdalene. That could make the story take a turn.<br /> <br /> As a note, Franz Ludwig was a hit. His various tales of staring at his mistress\u2019s bosom at mass, or tripping on his drunk mistress while drunk himself and falling down the stairs was amusing, and he kept referring to Frater Hans, his teacher, and a lot of babbling about witchcraft. He only vaguely understands what is going on, but the conversation had people in stitches.<br /> <br /> As a second note, yes, Lizette had a distraction penalty to her Perception check to notice the wolf out the window.<br /> <br /> We are winding up the Vienna leg of the story. What I told my players before this upcoming session is 2-4 session in Vienna then we jump to 1922 Paris as the jazz age hits Europe. It should be fun.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T09:56:44-07:00","id":637118,"title":"","content":"How aware of the supernatural are Christina and Marlene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T12:32:28-07:00","id":637264,"title":"","content":"When they met Christina in session 2, she was completely unaware of the supernatural, beyond folk tales. In session 5, Lizette directly expressed romantic interest in her and Enchanted her, so she could see the Changelings actual forms, and essentially told her she was Faerie. She gave her relatively little info beyond that, less than she should have, but Christina could see faerie forms. Christina told her companion, who believed Christina was naive and that Lizette was simply a short lesbian spinning a tale. Christina realized Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il were also Faerie that session (while less educated than Christina, Marlene is close to her own brother and knows more than a proper lady probably should). In session seven, Lizette and Marlene slept together and Lizette enchanted her, so she could also see the green skin, yellow eyes, and pointy ears, since Marlene was...romantically may be too strong a word....physically interested in Lizette (who represents guilt free sex with no chance of pregnancy or virginity loss in her mind) and Lizette strongly feels anyone she is involved with should see her as she really is. Lizette does not really understand breaking points.<br /> <br /> In session 10, with the whole Werewolf thing, Wolfram gave a &quot;basic&quot; crash course on the fact that in addition to the Faerie there were the two Werewolves, Vampire, and himself as a Sin-Eater. This was relatively basic, as Wolfram is well versed in the Occult but not real sure of some specifics. He knows Werewolves don't get their power from Satan and they don't infect other people, he knows Alla is unlikely to start a Vampire outbreak, but is short of specifics. He told Christina and Marlene what he knew. I don't think they know about the Eagle. They have no real awareness of things like the fact the Changelings were Taken or who Father Wolf was.<br /> <br /> Christina Esterh\u00e1zy is highly intelligent and strong willed (Intelligence, Resolve, Composure 4 each) and fairly well educated for an Austrian Noblewoman (Academics 3). She is figuring stuff out. Marlene is a bit above average in most of those categories but is Academics 0, being kept ignorant so her future husband could decide how educated he wanted his wife to be. She is, however, more aware of the darker side of the world in a non-supernatural sense, having essentially lost everything and only remaining in noble circles as her friend's companion.<br /> <br /> Does that answer pretty well?<br /> <br /> ETA: As a side note, both Christina and Marlene were included as potential love interests, Christina especially. Both are bisexual, though Christina had no real idea of what homosexual interest was and even when Lizette expressed it assumed it was a weird Faerie thing of her not fully understanding how humans work until around session 8 or 9. Christina was designed as a harder nut to crack for same sex interest, while Marlene was, by design, very prone to a same sex affair but is unlikely to want a permanent arrangement, being very afraid of becoming an old maid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-23-2015, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T17:02:01-07:00","id":637544,"title":"","content":"Very complete answer, thank you!<br /> Are changelings sterile in this game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T22:46:12-07:00","id":637728,"title":"","content":"No, on the same basis as MDH, Changelings (outside Arcadia) are slightly less fertile than normal but can have children. As in CtL, these Children are mostly normal, possibly with a special sense for Glamour","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T23:01:58-07:00","id":653528,"title":"","content":"t\u2019s time to return to Vienna 1920. This chapter of our story rushes toward a climax, and along the way a duel challenge is laid, a meeting with vampires takes place and a second meeting is arranged. The Conspiracy looks at having their goals in the Imperial City Achieved.<br /> <br /> Note Dacian covers like three sessions in his journal, though each are brief. But the bulk of it covers past events.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 25 June 1920<br /> <br /> After we got back from taking care of Gustov, we found that Wolfram had been sent a letter from none other than Gunnar. Apparently the Pure invited Wolfram to come to the Gentleman\u2019s club to talk early this evening. This prompted a good deal of discussion within the pack. Several people were of the opinion that Gentlemanly honor would be upheld and Wolfram would be safe. That they would not dare hurt Wolfram since it was known that he would be a guest there. Christina seemed to firmly believe this. Some argued that the Pure may not have a reason to abide by that particular code and would use it as an excuse to take our friend out of the picture. Tatiana was the main proponent of the later idea. I will admit that I agreed with her. Just because he follows tradition when it comes to Christina, and actually asked her brother for her hand in marriage, doesn\u2019t mean that Gunnar will follow other aspects of that same nebulous Gentleman\u2019s code of conduct.<br /> <br /> Once it was decided that Wolfram should go, there was discussion about whether or not he should go alone or have someone go with him, seen or unseen. Dacian suggested that he could sneak in and be there in the shadows in case Wolfram needed assistance. It might be a good idea in other places but not, in my opinion, in a place full of werewolves. If they heard him or smelt him they would become angry and might have a perceived reason to retaliate. It was also suggested that Dacian go in as Wolfram\u2019s manservant. This would get our shadowy compatriot inside the building, but he would not be in the same room and would be heavily watched by the staff. I argued against Dacian going in. Saying that we should not try and be covert on this because it had too much potential to backfire.<br /> <br /> In the end we decided to let Wolfram go to the club by himself and Dacian, Tatiana and I would be at a nearby caf\u00e9. Should he need help, and I would know, we would be able to assist. Rude or not, we would invite ourselves in. Dearbhail then brought up the idea that this whole meeting might be a distraction so that someone could be sent to collect Christina. I suggested that the ladies go shopping, somewhere nice and public. Gunnar and/or the Pure are far less likely to try anything in a crowded public place. There would be repercussions if they were seen taking her against her will.<br /> <br /> Because we had free time between then and Wolfram\u2019s meeting, Tatiana asked if I\u2019d like to spar. I agreed and we went out to the backyard where we would have privacy. Dearbhail, Christina and Marelene decided to watch. I have to give them credit. None of them excused themselves early in fright. Two Uratha fighting in our more animalistic forms tends to inspire a good deal of fear and trepidation in non-werewolves, so it was impressive that they seemed unaffected. <br /> <br /> Tatiana for her part gave as good as she got in the fight. I did my best to keep up with her, and can say that we ended that match in a draw. I know that will not be the case every time. She is the better fighter when it comes to hand to hand, but then she is not as good with a rifle as I am. I am looking forward to using those skills tomorrow night. I prefer attacking from the shadows and hitting the target before they even have a chance to react. Some may say that it\u2019s not very sporting to do things that way, but I don\u2019t attack for sport. I attack to kill.<br /> <br /> The evening came quickly and at the appointed time Wolfram made his way to the Gentleman\u2019s club. Dacian, Tatiana and I went to the caf\u00e9 nearby and ordered our drinks. A relatively short time later Wolfram emerged from the club looking amused. We all went back to the hotel before talking. Apparently Gunnar was very conceited and went on and on about bloodlines and divine right and all manner of bullshit. Wolfram did not take this lying down and gave as good as he got back, poking holes in Gunnar\u2019s lineage and fa\u00e7ade. I will admit that it was probably amusing to watch. I am sorry that I could not witness it. If Tatiana had been there I\u2019m fairly certain that Gunnar would not be standing right now. She has only held off \u201cpissing on his shoes\u201d this long because I asked her to. His insulting of Wolfram would probably have hit a nerve and she would react accordingly. I can\u2019t say that I\u2019d blame her. Wolfram though found the whole thing to be funny, even the fact that Gunnar called him out for a duel the day after tomorrow. Or maybe especially the fact that Gunnar called him out. I mean, Wolfram has already come back from the dead once, and is now connected to the Golden Eagle, so it\u2019s not likely that death will take the second time around either should he lose. This is if Gunnar survives tomorrow night. I\u2019m not planning on letting him live though, but we\u2019ll see what happens. <br /> <br /> When talk came around the impending ambush tomorrow night Dacian asked Lizette about the possibility of making a fragmentation device that would have silver as the projectile. He thought that it might make a good weapon against the Pure. Lizette was unsure that the idea would work since silver is such a soft metal. She was afraid that it would melt too much in the heat of the explosion. I myself was not too keen on the idea, just because it could go badly wrong. I would not want to get hit by it, nor would I want the enemy to figure out the same idea and use it against me or mine at a later date. It was a clever idea, I\u2019ll give Dacian that, but unfortunately not the most feasible technically or tactically.<br /> <br /> Despite our talk of the ambush tomorrow, Christina seemed fixated on the duel between Wolfram and Gunnar. We hinted that there would likely be nothing to worry about, but her concern remained. We didn\u2019t flat out say that we plan on killing Gunnar tomorrow so there should be nothing to worry about, but we tried to insinuate that there\u2019d be no problem. I think the others feared that saying it so plainly would have been inappropriate. Well, Tatiana probably wasn\u2019t against being so bold. I suppose just coming out and saying it could be considered upsetting. My own reactions are not the same as others so I tend to try and emulate what others are doing in order to \u201cget it right.\u201d<br /> <br /> Later when Alla woke she came out of her bedroom holding the skull, which had been placed near her bed by Fenric, and asked whose it was. She was told that it was Gustov\u2019s and she immediately brightened up. She went around and gave everyone hugs. It was kind of amusing to watch people\u2019s responses to her delighted reaction. After the hugs were done she said that she wanted to go meet with Maximillian and present the skull to him. Tatiana asked if it would be appropriate for the two of us (Uratha) to accompany her since we were involved in the hunt. She said that it should be fine and the three of us joined Fenric and Dacian to go meet the obese vampire. <br /> <br /> Maximillian is an interesting individual. He came across as very confident and sure of himself. He didn\u2019t overly exert his authority over anyone but has a decent amount of power, both supernatural and political. He also showed no fear in our presence, which was interesting. Most people that can sense the wolf within us would tend to shy away from two of us in one place. <br /> <br /> Alla presented the skull to Maximillian, who was impressed. He offered to hold a Salon for Alla and invite the Eupraxus girl, Lisbette so Alla could question her about the necklace that was stolen from Christina. Our vampire pack mate accepted this as payment for the favor of removing Gustov as a threat.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Dearbhail was teaching Christina and Marlene how to fight with a knife. I believe that Wolfram joined in to learn as well. He is familiar with guns, but not so much with blades. I think all of us agreed that it would be a good idea for the ladies to learn how to defend themselves if they should need to. Wolfram stressed that he would keep his lady love safe to the best of his ability, but wanted her to be safe on her own should something delay him. I just think it\u2019s just prudent for everyone to learn how to defend themselves. The violence has not ended since the war stopped. Things are still in flux and there are opportunistic people out there that will take advantage of those they perceive as weak if they can. The ladies protested at first that they would have no need to use a knife since the rest of us would protect them, but they eventually saw reason and acquiesced. <br /> <br /> After the meeting with Maximillian, Dacian gathered up the pair of swords he acquired and went to go meet the ghost for fencing lessons. I\u2019d be interested in seeing that, but if I went to the cemetery then the Pure would be able to find my scent and the ambush would not work. So I will need to content myself with hearing how the lessons went from Dacian himself.<br /> <br /> As for myself, I am preparing myself for the ambush tomorrow night. I sparred with Tatiana earlier, which helped ease off some of the tension. This evening I have been going over in my mind all that I know about the Pure and Gunnar himself in order to better anticipate how the fight will go. I do not expect it to be easy but I believe that we will succeed. Our pack has abilities that they know nothing of, and may not be able to combat. In that regard, we have the advantage. We also have surprise on our side, and I plan to make the most of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Hush you. I have told you we Hunt tomorrow. There is a timing to these things.<br /> <br /> Will you call me a coward too, volchonok?<br /> <br /> Because I counseled him not to go to that foolish meeting, Wolfram, with Gunnar. The club may not be the Pure\u2019s den, but it is his ground, his place. These people rely too much on this gentleman\u2019s honor foolishness. One does not do this, one does not do that. Bah. He is a prideful Pure above else, and Wolfram challenges him, in his city.<br /> <br /> No, nothing came of it. Because nothing bad happened does not mean it was not foolish.<br /> <br /> The songbird and Christina did have an excellent idea, to have Wolfram disappear quite publicly from the club. It would still have been a risk, but there would have been something to gain. But since he cannot disappear, if he is to marry properly, there was nothing to be gained but to tweak Gunnar\u2019s nose.<br /> <br /> Yes, his nose was tweaked, and yes, it would have been good to see, distractible volchonok. The Pure has challenged our Wolfram to a duel, to be held the morning after tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> It is true, yes, there will likely be no duel. And Dacian has plans that we shall hide the body, and he shall go through Gunnar\u2019s things, so that it appears he ran in fear of the duel. More noble foolishness, but it will possibly weaken his Pure relatives and packmates, so this will prove of some benefit, I suppose.<br /> <br /> For once I agree with you, oh so reasonable volchonok. Human foolishness. At least I had company, sitting in that coffee shop again. Not our songbird - she was escorting Christina and Marlena, in case the entire meeting was a ploy, and not simply noble whimsy.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, you are a wise volchonok, and you know many things. You followed them, yes? Did you also watch them practice fighting while I met the vampire?<br /> <br /> Of course you did. You would not have liked it there anyway. It was much small talk and politicking. Though I do rather like this Maximilian. He acknowledged our strength, without being afraid. I wonder if his blood is as sweet as his grandchild\u2019s...<br /> <br /> Bah, you are one to ask about purposes, volchonok. He will assist us in meeting this Lizbet, the vampire who might have the necklace.<br /> <br /> A salon? Something of this sort. Lizette and Alla go shopping for it this night. It will be in some nights time... 3, I believe. Tomorrow night is the Hunt, the next night, I do not know, and then this salon.<br /> <br /> And then, volchonok? Well, if Lizbet gives over the necklace, then we leave, I suppose.<br /> <br /> For Paris. To run together in our own territory, as is proper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 24 June 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> My hunger for occult knowledge continues to be sated. Tatiana and Marek led us to a different area outside of Vienna. This time it was to make sure we were not inside the territory of another. This ritual was for something incredibly important to the Uratha. It was referred to only as the Siskur-Dah. The purpose of this sacred hunt was to discredit the Pure of Vienna.<br /> <br /> We have several options, and indeed several plans by which to achieve this goal. However the Siskur-Dah ritual was not the subtle machinations of a plotting cabal. Lizette carved a wooden mask which parodied Gunner for use in the ritual. Tatiana wore the mask and began strutting around the ritual area much like a peacock. Marek wore his rifle though it was obviously for show. Our totem and the Uratha\u2019s companion spirits were also involved, I learned later. No sound was made as this was to be an assassination. The spirits assisted Marek in stalking their prey, as he tracked from the shadows. At length, Marek lept from his vantage point with an outstretched hand, symbolizing the reach of our cabal. The strike left a bloody splash upon the mask before Tatiana fell back stiffly.<br /> <br /> With the ritual slaying of Gunner complete, we returned to the hotel to change and prepare for another performance at the Opera. Dearbh\u00e1il did not disappoint, of course. The security tonight was higher, which I\u2019m sure offered some small reassurance to our Fairest. In attendance, we spotted Gloria the Theosophist, though she did not seem to notice us at first. Given Lizette\u2019s aggressive hammering on the train, it was for the best that we remained unnoticed. Additionally, Wolfram noted two sets of vampires. A man and a woman, each with a small compliment of bodyguards. Alla chose to visit the lady though I am unsure how their meeting went. I should also note that Lizette\u2019s abilities as a seamstress are amazing. The crimson gown she wore defied her child-like frame and proved she was definitely a mature woman. It was less revealing perhaps than the merlot dress from the last performance, but who am I to complain about presentation of beauty?<br /> <br /> Lizette, Fenric, Marek, and I accompanied Wolfram to a hotel unofficially known for its discretion near the gentlemen\u2019s club to which Herr Hohenberg belongs. There we changed from our opera attire into more appropriate garments for illegal entry. Lizette emerged from a side room wearing a sable outfit which left me staring. My usually even calm demeanor must have been compromised as Lizette took one look at me before leaving the room awkwardly. Tatiana waited in a cafe down the street, where she had a vantage of the club but not too close to give herself away. Wolfram and Fenric remained in the hotel as he had to light himself on fire to become insubstantial. Fenric was to watch over the body and also turn on the shower to end the burning. I removed any trace of my passing and made it harder to be noticed before grabbing my rope and slinking out and across the street. With the help of the rope, I scaled the wall and found a carelessly unlocked window on the second floor. Once I was inside and secured the rope, I was followed by the others. Wolfram apparently just walked through the wall as if he were indeed a ghost. Needing to be perfectly stealthy, I turned invisible and further expanded my ability to move silently. Then we moved in.<br /> <br /> A woman from Germany, by her accent, spoke with Gunner about a shipment of relics to aid the Pure of Vienna. The two obviously disliked each other as they spoke in barbs. Ilsa was aware that she held the upper hand and was intentionally condescending toward Gunner. In turn, Hohenberg was as rude as he could get away with regarding her femininity and lack of breeding. A noble without a sword can always find a way to fall upon a blade, if led to believe they are superior to those around them. Gunner was no exception. I am pleased to note Wolfram is above such foolish delusion. At length, we learned that these relics would arrive in two days and be delivered to a crypt. This is apparently more than slightly distasteful to the Ivory Claws, which is precisely why Ilsa suggested it. The details would be wired later, though we learned both the location the wire would arrive as well as the crypt in question.<br /> <br /> Now I have managed to grasp a bit of the Contracts of Shade and Spirit so I can see and hear Wolfram while in this form. Together we form a rather potent information gathering team. Now that I have written this and sent it back with Marek, I will accompany our Bound to the crypt where we can investigate the best way to ambush the meeting of the Pure.<br /> <br /> <br /> 24 June 1920 - Late<br /> <br /> Tonight has been most informative.<br /> <br /> With my newfound ability to see into Twilight, I accompanied a ghostly Wolfram to a cemetery that was obviously reserved for the high-born. While my spectral associate had little issues, I had to pick the lock of the outer gate, sneak past the guard, and then best a most formidable lock on the crypt entrance. Between my skill and my Contracts, I gained entry without alerting the guard.<br /> <br /> However I found myself standing in a lightless tomb. I could sense the echoes of horrors I heard but never saw slithering past and lumbering through the Apothic Reaches closing in upon me. But before I could tumble down that mental spiral, Wolfram flooded the entire crypt with his ghost flame. Once I could see, I found that my breath had caught in my throat and I once again began to breathe.<br /> <br /> We were surrounded by jewelry and valuables beyond measure, though none were of any magical significance. While disappointing, it was for the best. As we moved among the dead, a soldier from another time awoke and climbed from his casket. Speaking in a thick German that I could only barely recognize, Franz Ludwig Hollenberg asked us to leave. Thinking quickly and assuming the bearing of a true noble, Wolfram addressed Herr Hollenberg and convinced him of the infiltration of \u201cwitches\u201d into his fair bloodline. As Hollenberg still wished to serve his family, even in death, he resolved to assist us when these fiends defiled his family\u2019s resting place. That Hollenberg believed werewolves were servants of Satan not withstanding, he apparently felt a debt was owed to his family. Possibly related to an accident involving quantities of alcohol, a mistress, and treacherous stairways. Wolfram seemed to understand and commiserated, though I have no idea if he knew what was happening or simply held to his role exquisitely. Once Franz Ludwig was committed to assisting us in ridding his family of \u201cthe witches\u201d and their \u201cunclean charms,\u201d I inquired as to his willingness to instruct me in the ways of the blade. His soldier\u2019s uniform spoke of at least some training and it seemed he had little else to do with his time. Happily, the ghost agreed to give me a few lessons if I could but bring him a sword. Wolfram thankfully remained unmoved as I assured Franz Ludwig that I would acquire blades for both of us. We took our leave after that and I returned with Wolfram to reclaim his body.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25 June 1920 - Early<br /> <br /> Leaving Wolfram and Fenric to return to the others, I ventured out around eleven o\u2019clock in search of a quality blacksmith. Instead, I found Vienna does not keep their smiths in the open, but presents the wares in storefronts. The lock was of no consequence but the shopkeeper living upstairs might have been. As it happens, I left two swords heavier than I arrived and no one realized I had ever entered.<br /> <br /> I returned a slightly roundabout way to the hotel to find Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re holding a note. It read in French, \u201cLizette needs you at Christina\u2019s.\u201d Beneath, a second line in French read, \u201cWolfram and Fenric are already there.\u201d I thanked the teapot, which whistled steam at me in response, and headed back to the street. I considered my options, but decided to casually hail a carriage. My latest acquisitions were carefully wrapped in polishing cloths, so I simply brought them with me. I was less able to keep track, but I do not believe I was followed. I arrived unmolested and quickly learned that while Wolfram and I searched the crypt, a large white wolf was spotted stalking the grounds. Lizette was already in hand to spot the wolf, curiously from Marlena\u2019s bedroom window. Acting quickly, Lizette sent for a gun which was a bold move considering we assumed it was a werewolf. The assumption was confirmed when Lizette informed us that she shot the beast in the head with the provided Mannlicher, a rifle which stood far taller than Lizette. The wolf was wounded, but shook off the wound then looked up at the window from whence the shot came. As the Mannlicher\u2019s crosshairs were already aligned for another shot, the wolf abandoned his investigation and fled the scene. Marek sniffed the air and determined it was not Gunner, but another werewolf which frequented the gentlemen\u2019s club. I find that when Marek speaks, it is as though the world pauses for a moment as there was occasion for him to make sound. Like me, he is often silent but I don\u2019t believe the world is as concerned when I speak. Intriguing. The remainder of our cabal arrived not long after, bringing our cache of silver bullets and assorted weaponry. I assumed another call was placed to Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re. With our entirely force assembled, Christina rushed around with Marlena to prepare more rooms.<br /> <br /> As we were not so unconcerned as to think the matter closed, watches were decided. Alla took first watch, as she would have more problems after dawn and there rest of the cabal would benefit from sleep. I took second watch, and as my duties as sentry are at an end, I have penned this entry. Now I will enjoy the comfort of this warm bed.<br /> <br /> 25 June 1920 - Breakfast<br /> <br /> Sleep enveloped me much like dusk covers the land in darkness. I awakened sooner than I would like, but the smells of freshly baked bread roused me, as they often do. Coffee joined the scents as I prepared for the day. I arrived to breakfast without keeping anyone waiting, which would be rude as we are guests here.<br /> <br /> Plans were discussed once we confirmed that no other issues occurred. Fenric noted that Alla would gain much praise if she could present some proof of killing a rogue vampire to the mysteriously large Maximilian. Tatiana heartily supported this idea through her enjoyment of eggs. Though Christina paled a bit, Marlena spoke some quiet reassurances to her and the conversations continued. As Tatiana apparently already had this vampire\u2019s scent, she was more than ready to hunt. That word has such a deeper meaning when the Uratha say it. You can hear it as if there is a world of secrets buzzing just out of earshot each time the word is spoken. But I digress. Once Tatiana picked up the scent we would move in. I would scout the area to locate and remove any innocents before Lizette would plant an explosive to level the building. After that, we simply find something to take back as proof.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25 June 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> Never once has Alla or Fenric claimed that any vampire would be simple to deal with. After today, I fully understand why.<br /> <br /> We moved through the less affluent sections of Vienna into a part of the city I was unaware even existed. Poor was an understatement. Buildings showed signs of conflict far more recent than the war and I believe someone mentioned this was the Communist part of Vienna. Tatiana led us to a building that had been bombed at one point, but was mostly still intact. I concealed my tracks and made it more difficult for others to notice me before slipping inside. I believe Tatiana may have menaced some vagabonds while I was inside, but I found no one else. The Iron Master\u2019s ability to track astounded me as she simply motioned Lizette forward with a few instructions and our little munitions expert walked almost on top of the sleeping vampire. Given that we set an incendiary device next to him, in the full light of day, I assumed that this would be over before it began. The roar that followed the explosion was savage and terrifying. Lizette handed Fenric and I a Molotov cocktail each before strapping herself into her own personal flamethrower.<br /> <br /> The building suffered further damage from the explosion and of course was still burning, when the vampire burst from the rubble. Though on fire, this Gustov looked surprisingly unharmed given the sun, the flames, the explosion, the crushing rubble. I believe my point is made. Fenric and I glanced at one another before lighting our bombs. Tatiana, ever prepared for a fight, leapt into the fray and bit down on his leg to reduce his chance to escape. Marek used a similar tactic before they both moved aside. Gustov turned to see a gout of flame engulf him as Lizette finally utilized one of her inventions. The vampire ignited in a way that can only be compared to a bonfire, yet was still more than willing to attack. Seizing my opportunity I crept upon the very distracted vampire and slipped my cocktail into his tattered clothing, quickly enough not to be burned myself. I then ran for cover. Just as I reached the section of wall still standing enough to duck behind, Gustov exploded. Flames shot past and around me as the wall crumbled away above me. However, once those flames subsided, the fight was over. Gustov lay face down in a burning heap. Fenric examined the body from a distance and noted that this is what vampires call torpor and that if we wished to do so, now would be the time to kill him. I was shocked that the vampire was still not finished. But when the head was severed from the smoldering body, it fell to ashes and bone. I scrounged a sack from where the vagabonds had been, and we carried the partly damaged skull back to Christina\u2019s for Alla.<br /> <br /> Given the explosions and our obvious soot-stained participation of same, we did not tarry from returning to the Esterh\u00e1zy estate. We arrived as the bells struck two o\u2019clock to find both Christina and Marlena in a bit of excited chatter. One of Hohenberg\u2019s men delivered an \u201cinvitation\u201d to Wolfram to meet Gunnar at the gentlemen\u2019s club. It was immediately agreed, by all but Tatiana, that this was a posturing attempt to push Wolfram out of the contest for Christina\u2019s hand. Tatiana, a bit more pragmatic, stated it was clearly a trap. Also, and I cannot overstate this point enough, that what a noble must and should do have no bearing on what a werewolf will do. Any such thought is ridiculous and dangerously na\u00efve thinking. While I agreed, having seen firsthand everything short of the werewolf portion of the statement come true, I was also not oblivious to the seconds counting down before Christina swooned. Tatiana\u2019s statement contradicted almost every aspect of the Esterh\u00e1zy world view, and there were only minor attempts from the rest of us to the contrary. Once Marlena stabilized her mistress, we decided not to let Tatiana address the subject of nobility again for a while. Beyond that, she, Marek, and I would have coffee in a caf\u00e9 nearby in case of trouble and Wolfram would indeed walk into the wolf\u2019s den.<br /> <br /> I am unsure of the outcome, but as I finish this entry, I plan to take a nap in this lightless room, my shoes neatly placed at the foot of the bed. After an hour (or more depending on the nap), I will be as prepared as I can be to possibly lay siege to a Pure stronghold. Were it not for the safety of my cabal, I could never have imagined ever writing that line before this moment.<br /> <br /> Courage, it seems, stems from having something to lose or someone to miss.<br /> <br /> 25 June 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> I accompanied my Uratha cabal mates to the designated coffee shop. I carried a small travel bag containing my rope and a roll of dynamite, courtesy of Lizette. It was enough explosives, based on our Wizened\u2019s calculations, to level the entire building as well as anyone left inside. The fuse was set for me to have roughly 10 seconds before the blast. I have very few things dear to me left in this world. Those in my cabal are the first on that list. Any harm that befalls them will be met with dire consequences.<br /> <br /> We enjoyed our coffee for a time before Wolfram returned unmarred. He even asked me, as we were leaving to be his second! I accepted without hesitation, but I was surprised at the insinuation. When I was a boy, that generally meant that a duel was coming. But even I was aware the Archduke had outlawed such things among the nobles three years ago. Something about preserving the nobility. I remember thinking when I learned of it, that it was to save the nobility from itself. But that was a year before my Return, so I was still grappling with all the changes in the world. Now, I again concerned Tatiana\u2019s stance and nodded to myself.<br /> <br /> When we returned to Christina\u2019s, Wolfram explained the situation to the cabal and our hosts. Not only did Hohenberg challenge our Bound to a duel one day after his relics were to arrive, but he also threatened Wolfram\u2019s entire family. My grip upon my chair tightened until I heard a slight creak from the antique wood. Christina\u2019s concern pulled me from my darkened thoughts as she felt Wolfram must accept even though it was dangerous. Marlena looked almost intoxicated with excitement. Thankfully, Alla saved us from another lesson in the passing of the nobility. She entered carrying Gustav\u2019s skull, which shocked Christina into silence, and prompted a change in subject.<br /> <br /> Dinner involved discussing a visit to Maximilian and the lack of necessity for me to acquire any more silver. I believe Wolfram also discussed what we all actually are with Christina and Marlena. This will be difficult for them at first, but ultimately it is for the best. Perhaps it will also hasten Christina\u2019s acceptance of how the world truly is and not how she has always been assured it must be.<br /> <br /> Now I must change to go, against Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s wishes, to meet a vampire.<br /> <br /> 25 June 1920 - Late<br /> <br /> Marek, Tatiana, Fenric, and I accompanied Alla to present the trophy to Maximilian. We met in a large room, which hinted at opulence, but the open space seemed to suggest past fortunes. At the center of the room sat a massive man behind an equally impressive desk. Our host was gracious in a way as he acknowledged he owed Alla a boon. It was determined that he would hold a salon in payment. One in which the vampire suspected of collecting magical artifacts would be in attendance. From there, the meeting turned more into a social gathering. Maximilian greeted each of us, seemingly as equals, though he clearly thought he had an upper hand somehow. Not that I wished him any ill, but I noted that the pair of Uratha did not seem to cause any unease.<br /> <br /> Eventually we took our leave, parting on good terms and without incident. I have penned this short entry, and now plan to visit Franz Ludwig for that lesson in swordsmanship.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 25th June 1920<br /> <br /> Upon returning to Christina\u2019s residence from dropping off the equipment, we discovered that Gunnar had sent a letter to Wolfram\u2026at Christina\u2019s house\u2026insisting at a visit at his club at five on the clock. This lead to a great deal of discussion. Should he take an escort? Would it make him look weak? Strong? Christina kept pushing that a man of his peerage cannot simply be kidnapped or murdered in a club he was known to be visiting so he should be safe. Tatiana kept countering that ultimately it was competition for mates and the Pure would stoop to that level if they felt they had to. I thought both points of view had merit. Dacian felt somewhat put off I think about the discussion of his subtlety.<br /> <br /> Christina had an undertone of excitement. It flickered behind her eyes and kept her hands busy, much like mine tend to stay. I am not positive what it was, but I have my suspicions. Marlene passed me a letter pleading me to spend the night in her boudoir, claiming our interruption was distracting and addling her. It all created an\u2026undercurrent.<br /> <br /> In the end, the plan made was that Wolfram will go himself to meet Gunnar, but Dacian, Tatiana, and Marek would be there in case an extraction was needed. In order to protect Christina, she, Marlene, Dearbh\u00e1il and I would shop. I hope it is a good bonding moment.<br /> <br /> An incident with Dacian and the daggers that are silver made me wonder about what the best thing for defense for Christina and Marlene. I don\u2019t think they can handle chainsaws, which is a shame as I would love to make them personalized chainsaws. I could put their initials on them. But I don\u2019t think they would like it. Shame.<br /> <br /> But this is the 20th century and a lady needs her superweapon. We can\u2019t be depending on men to protect us. Maybe a flamethrower would work. I just don\u2019t want them to catch fire. Maybe a teapot to ride on which sprays hot tea? Time to switch to my planning notebook\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> (later)<br /> <br /> Wolfram\u2019s trip was a success. It could be best summarized as \u201cA lot of noble bullshit happened and now he has been challenged to a duel his opponent will probably not survive to see.\u201d I went shopping with Dearbh\u00e1il Christina and Marlene. No clothes for me (really, I always end up making my own) but a good trip overall. That excitement I mentioned was very much still there.<br /> <br /> But back to the whole babbling about ones noble family and dueling\u2026these nobles are weighing on my nerves. I mean, I really like Christina, Marlene and Wolfram. I really do. I would sleep with any of them under the right circumstances, and I won\u2019t sleep with just anyone. I consider them all friends. But their fretting about bloodlines, family honor, propriety (not personal, but noble) and all this stuff\u2026I think we in France had the right idea about to handle the nobility broadly speaking. And it was all I could do to stifle the urge to remind them of the year. I guess they can\u2019t help it. They were raised noble and don\u2019t really understand the real world.<br /> <br /> And Wolfram and Gunnar and their manly honor and duels\u2026honor died on the battlefield of Verdun. It is so archaic, so nineteenth century\u2026what year is it again? Why twenty years into this bold new century? Sometimes I wonder if they even know.<br /> <br /> I should note that Christina is still getting used to us discussing our powers. Wolfram\u2019s discussion of his ability to have guns inside himself prompted a comment about difficulty getting used to it, and various other comments seemed to take her off guard as well, including the note Dearbh\u00e1il can rouse us as if we slept a full night, or Dacian\u2019s casual discussion of being able to become invisible. Still she handled it well, even handled watching the werewolves spar outside human form well. She did ask me to stop discussing blowing up the club.<br /> <br /> The immediate threat has ended, so it looks like a quiet evening. Alla, Dacian, Marek and Tatiana went to give the head (what century is this again?) of the fallen vampire to Maximillian (who hopefully won\u2019t eat it) and trade it for a favor of arranging a vampire salon to talk to Lizbet. Dearbh\u00e1il trained Christina, Marlene and, comically, Wolfram in the hand to hand. As for me, while we discussed making more bullets that are silver I wound up not. We discussed making some for the Mannlicher, which everyone seemed rather amused by my saying out loud, but wound up, again, not. I did make an incendiary device for Wolfram\u2019s ghost powers. Making a device specifically to burn up my friends sits poorly with me, even if I understand this will not cause him harm in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Alla took me out to show me some gowns she wanted duplicates of and provide me with money for material. They will be purchased on the morrow. She will have them by the salon.<br /> <br /> As I considered bedding down, Marlene came to me with an issue with some of the houses new electrical systems. My dubiousness that anything regarding that would be in her bedroom was strong, and well justified. Still, she made the trouble up to me, and I fell asleep beside her. I am no Dacian, but slipping back to my rooms was simple enough, and I am prepared to work on the gown until such time as it is the time to set werewolves aflame.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <i><br /> End Session XI</i><br /> <br /> I honestly wish I wrote down all the stuff Gunnar said, but it was based on a light set of notes and a lot of ad-libbing, though my players insist I killed it. Gunnar began with a rambling story of the Battle of Vienna in 1683 and the friendship of Hohemberg and Esterh\u00e1zy commanders in the battle, and tradition, and an offhanded remark of something his late aunt, Sophie the Duchess of Hohemberg who he broadly described as married to the heir to the throne of Austria, Hungary, Bohemia, etc. I had Wolfram make a politics roll to accurately correct him that as she was a wife in a morganatic marriage she was not to truly be those things. By the end, he was challenged to a duel. And the snobbery continued.<br /> <br /> The long of the short of it was men with impressive mustaches sniping each other. As I say, I hate I did not record it.<br /> <br /> With the sparring Werewolves, the roll to resist Lunacy was not hard for Christina, who has very high both Resolve and Composure (4 in each). Somewhat harder for Marlene, who has 2 and 3. She spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> Dacian\u2019s lessons were not played out.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. If I missed something and you have a question let me know. Next session was much shorter than usual, but should still have some journals. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T14:40:04-07:00","id":656934,"title":"","content":"Finally caught up with the journals! Between school starting, getting an internship set up, and Shadowrun: Hong Kong. I've let them slip a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:44:06-07:00","id":657047,"title":"","content":"Good to have you back! ^_^ It's an exciting time in the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T01:37:33-07:00","id":669342,"title":"","content":"We had a short session last time, as we could not start arriving until usual start time due to family obligations of the hosts. Also, this had them tired and we had another player unusually tired. This lead to a short session. Still, we have three journals for you. No Tatiana as her player did not feel she (Tatiana) had much to add but grousing. Here are journals from the usual suspects however, enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 June 1920<br /> <br /> I have a moment or two before we have to leave so I will record what has happened so far. Dearbhail, Dacian and Lizette met with the Autumn courts leader, Mercutio, to discuss the necklace. Apparently the Autumn King says that the necklace sounds like a cursed item. He was not aware of anyone in their court having such a cursed object in their possession though. He also recommended that if and when we find this necklace that we quarantine it to keep its influence or curse from spreading further. In addition he offered the services of his people to see what they could do to render the necklace safe once it is found. I thought the idea had merit. I was also fully in support of just destroying the thing. There was some debate among the others whether or not we should \u201cdamage\u201d or change the necklace enough to make the magical qualities of it fail, or if we should just have Lizette make a duplicate and use that to give to Christina\u2019s brother.<br /> <br /> I am all for destroying the damn thing, like I said. Though I\u2019m not sure if the brother plans to sell the necklace because it\u2019s pretty or because it is a magical artifact. If it is due to the later, then the duplicate might not work. It all depends I suppose on whether or not Gunter or his buyer(s) can sense the magic on it or not. And if I recall correctly the brother did not want his sister to wear the necklace. This could mean that he did know it was cursed and didn\u2019t want it to affect her. Or it could also meant that he didn\u2019t want people know that he was trying to sell jewels to keep his family afloat. Regardless I doubt the others will agree to give him a functioning cursed necklace back to the man regardless of his intentions, whether they are good or not.<br /> <br /> Mercutio also warned our three Fae friends about interacting with the vampires in town. He is of the opinion that they are dangerous and should be avoided. I agree that they are dangerous, and could cause all manner of problems if they so desired, but I don\u2019t think that they are an immediate threat. We have Alla on our side and she is adept at playing the vampire political game. At least so far as we\u2019ve seen.<br /> <br /> Because Dearbhail was so worried about the vampires, Lizette tried to calm her down by reminding our songstress of her fully functional flame thrower. I think there was a fairly heated, no pun intended, discussion about this as they were walking back to the hotel. It was what they were discussing when they walked in the door. Lizette was assuring Dearbhail that she would not set any friends on fire unless specifically asked to by said friend, and that she had practices in mind for keeping the rest of us free of the fire. I\u2019m assuming that she means she will make sure to aim away from the rest of us and only ignite someone if they specifically ask her to, like Wolfram has once in the past.<br /> <br /> After the meeting this morning and everyone had reconvened at the hotel the discussion of who was going to go to the Salon hosted by the vampires was brought up. I believe that Alla, Fenric, Tatiana, Dacian, Lizette, Wolfram and myself will be going. I am still unsure of Dearbhail. She seemed rather nervous about the whole idea. It was also mentioned that we should be appropriately attired to go to this thing. For Dacian I think this was just an excuse to get a new suit. I actually needed something nice to wear. I have a dressier suit of clothes, but it is not up to the standards that I\u2019m sure will be expected. Lizette had made a suit for Tataina a couple of days ago, so she offered to make one for me and Dacian if we would go with her to pick out fabric and show her which style of suit we\u2019d like. I chose a fairly simple suit and a dark grey fabric. Dacian went a little fancier than I did with his. So, we took our purchased cloth back to the hotel and in about an hour we had two very well made suits courtesy of Lizette. She is a truly gifted woman to be able to craft weapons and elegant clothing with the same amount of haste and ease. My own creations seem so simple next to hers. Though to be fair, I have only crafted charms or items to use in a ritual so far. I have a ways to go yet before I\u2019m considered proficient. <br /> <br /> Once we were altogether there was some discussion about what our plan for this evening was. We debated ambushing them at the train station, at the crypt, or both places. We figured that they would have people at both places and we didn\u2019t really want to fight the whole lot of them at once. Splitting up was seen as a good idea until it was brought up that Ilsa and Gunner would be in different areas and the whole point was to make sure that Ilsa saw how ineffective Gunnar was in this whole affair. So, I think the plan that we have settled on is to have Wolfram go incorporeal and spy on the train station to get an idea of the number of people and how many boxes or containers they have with them. While he is spying, Lizette will drive his body towards the rest of us who will be at or near the crypt. Tatiana and I will need to stay out of sense range. The others probably should too, except for maybe Dacian who can mask his presence, including smell. <br /> <br /> Once back together, or as soon as Wolfram was done gathering intel, he will go back to his body and tell us what to expect. We will then wait on the rest to come or even up the field a bit before they arrive and ambush the new arrivals. Honestly it would be nice to have more information now to make our planning a little easier, but we must work with what we have, and right now that\u2019s not much. I personally think we need to solidify our plan a little more and come up with a couple of contingency plans that we can enact if things go badly. I as a matter of practice I never assume that things will go to plan. If I have a contingency in place then when or if things go wrong I can seamlessly move into the alternate plan.<br /> <br /> I have, since the war, never assumed that I would make it out of any particular mission alive. Even the simple ones. I have learned all too well how bad things can get in a very short period of time. In this instance we will be fighting at least two, maybe more, werewolves and who knows how many humans. I plan on taking down as many as I can and still walk away, but I do not assume that I will be walking away. Some people may call me a pessimist, but I prefer to see myself as a realist. The world is harsh and there are no second chances to make a different choice. I do not automatically assume that I will die either, I just prefer not to be surprised if I do. Of course in my case death won\u2019t be permanent. Won\u2019t that be a surprise?<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should tell them about Reznik? They are pack after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> I have spent a good day working on getting ready for the next couple of nights. I have made a gown for Alla and suits for both Marek and Dacian. What would have taken a lesser woman hours only took me thirty minutes each. This is because I am awesome. Sure, another Lost with the Boon of the Brownie could make it with such speed, but not, dare I say, with such style!<br /> <br /> In the afternoon Dearbh\u00e1il, Dacian and I went to town and met the Autumn King at the Autumn Court, a second theater, more traditional than Burlesque. Mercutio is some sort of darkness Elemental with a tragedy mask over his face. I\u2019ve never seen an Elemental King before, though heard of such for the Winter Court. His bodyguard Siegfried is an Ogre, probably a Bloodbrute.<br /> <br /> As have the others, Mercutio made a point of being polite, finding out our business and discussing options. In the end, he could tell us little we did not already know. Messing with cursed relics is dangerous, we should not do it without care. He was more the \u201cpolitical\u201d Autumn King, so while his Occult knowledge was broad he wished to consult other Courtiers. He offered to examine it or have them examine it.<br /> <br /> He was not interested in examining my flamethrower, nor with equipping his court (or the Changelings at large in Vienna) with such items. I suspect, being an Elemental tied to darkness, he clearly fears things that bring such light. A pity. Of course the Summer King did not want them either. Perhaps I should have brought chainsaws. I am sure Mercutio would haven found use for them.<br /> <br /> Mercutio also threw in a warning that Dearbh\u00e1il rather latched onto about the Vampires. Namely, to be wary of them. I don\u2019t know why everyone is not terrified of vampires. You have a human and Vampire, they go off alone, and you have two vampires. It seems like their ascendancy is inevitable. Dearbh\u00e1il was more worried about Alla and a Vampire who wore a habit named Magdalena if I recall correctly. Maximillian warned she was prone to blood bonding and Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s desire reading concurred. That and what to do about the Salon rather dominated the walk home.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il does not seem to understand my protocols for setting friends on fire. Setting friends on fire is not a thing done without reason and prior consultation. It is rude to simply take a flamethrower to a person, especially if that person is a friend of yours. We discussed using the flamethrower to help Alla as needed. I would, of course, apply it with care.<br /> <br /> En route back I let it slip I may not have been alone minding my own business when the werewolf was spotted. I know Dearbh\u00e1il caught on; I need to talk to her before she constructs any sort of bizarre narrative in her head.<br /> <br /> We met back as a group (sans Alla) to discuss making our move tonight with the Werewolf elimination plan. After a good deal of debate I think the idea is I will drive with Wolfram\u2019s projection to the train station and observe the size of the group moving to take the items to their car. Dacian will scout the mausoleum for the size of the group there. Wolfram will jump to his body near the rest of the team who will be near enough for Dacian to arrive quickly and we will set tasks as needed. Foremost will be the determination of whether we can handle the group together or need to work separately. I will have my star with the bullets that are silver, my chainsaw my flamethrower, and enough explosive to level the mausoleum. Everything a gal needs to feel secure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 26 July 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> The morning was devoted to our own endeavors today. Tomorrow there is a duel and tonight there is an ambush upon the Pure. No one could find a reason to be terribly formal under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> I took a pear and a bit of strudel as I moved through at one point, but otherwise found that relaxing in my room, contemplating my swords and the state of Twilight were the best uses of my time.<br /> <br /> During Lunch, Lizette mentioned going shopping for fabrics to make a dress Alla had seen while they went window shopping. Marek and I accompanied our tiny seamstress and I find a few new fashions I quite liked as well. Glancing about the tailors\u2019 supply, I picked up enough material for both Marek and I to have new suits made. That I paid for them was I believe somewhat of a relief to Lizette and Marek. Likely for different reasons. When we returned, it was time to visit the Autumn King. Now we shall learn what the Autumn Court of Vienna holds in store for us.<br /> <br /> 26 July 1920 - Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> Lizette accompanied us to ensure that the two Spring Courtiers were properly received. We arrived at the old theatre near Gem\u00fctlichkeit at the appointed time. Dearbh\u00e1il knocked and a large yellow eye peer around the slightly opened door. A deep voice rumbled that the theatre was closed. Undaunted, our Fairest expressively pouted and countered that we were invited. Also how much she loved theatres. The door opened a bit more and then we were allowed inside with a rushed apology for not realizing who we (she) were. The large grey skinned Ogre introduced himself as Siegfried and led us inside. A billowing pillar of darkness stood wearing a tragedy mask at center stage. Mercutio was a Darkness Elemental who proved very charming to us. When I described him as such, Tatiana grew terse, however I simply meant that he was willing to help us recover (and destroy if needs be) the Eye of Iblis. Additionally he was more than happy to get the word out that such a piece was in Vienna to the rest of the Autumn Court. He suggested that there may be an expert on such things but Mercutio\u2019s faith in this person\u2019s social graces had faltered. Lizette volunteered to be a liaison as the Changeling in question apparently has issues with the Spring Court. I can\u2019t imagine anyone treating Dearbh\u00e1il poorly simply because of her Court, but I suppose stranger things have happened.<br /> <br /> I went from out meeting to change and stand for Lizette to take my measurements. She truly is amazing with the creation of anything. The suit was completed in less than half an hour and was a far better quality than any article I had ever commissioned from a normal tailor. I could tell as I stood by the mirror, it would be very helpful in any persuasive endeavors I may have in the future. I can not say enough about the quality. The stitching could hold a mainsail on the Sea of Slashing Squalls and yet the fit was infinitely superior to my most expensive attire.<br /> <br /> Now I believe Dearbh\u00e1il and I are going to make a bit of a show in the Bohemian district for Glamour. After that, we will begin our preparations for the ambush on the Pure.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XII</i><br /> <br /> Entirely an RPing session. We did not want to get into the whole thing with the heist with tired people and the late start, so decided to start with that the next time. So the session was really the Autumn Court meeting, discussion en route home, and planning the heist.<br /> <br /> Hopefully next session will be back to normal. Will see you in two weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/