"content":"I was thinking visual and musical style along with that 90s low budget kind of intro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T01:39:17-07:00","id":672998,"title":"","content":"That's<i> Balance of Shadows</i> for me. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> in my head is a 40s era opening in black and white with swelling and dramatic music. Malibu Dream House would be swelling and theatrical, while <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> would be hard boiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:46:14-07:00","id":673274,"title":"","content":"I can dig it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:33:50-07:00","id":675678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=672998#post672998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's<i> Balance of Shadows</i> for me. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> in my head is a 40s era opening in black and white with swelling and dramatic music. Malibu Dream House would be swelling and theatrical, while <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> would be hard boiled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want intros for all of them now. That would be awesome. If I had time I'd do it myself, but I am far to busy, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T16:41:33-07:00","id":677021,"title":"","content":"We talked about the idea one opening for BoS was pale hands (Clearly Natalie's) playing <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-Xm7s9eGxU\" target=\"_blank\">Gymnopedie</a> by Sati on the piano interspersed with shots of the house and PC as the opening, and closing credits playing on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YX_kez_xwJs\" target=\"_blank\">Smaller God</a> by Darling Violetta playing. Those are the two pieces that, independent of any character I associate with that game. NTDA has <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=El8VSMamtpw\" target=\"_blank\">Philter (In Viaggio Attraverso L'Australia)</a> by Fantastic Plastic Machine and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kj7PGkYX1xk\" target=\"_blank\">Stylo</a> by the Gorillaz but not specific plan for opening. This game I don't have a soundtrack for, but if left to my own devices I would use a lot of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/ScottBradleeLovesYa/videos\" target=\"_blank\">Postmodern Jukebox</a> to provide music. Seriously, check out the Seven Nation Army cover there. I keep threatening to use the Soundtrack to <i>Cat's Meow</i> with it. or maybe <i>Miss Fisher's Murder Mysteries</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T00:32:38-07:00","id":686640,"title":"","content":"New Journals! Tatiana\u2019s player had to miss due to family crisis. As she is heavily combat focused, we decided to say the shipment had been delayed to the next night, and just roleplay the intervening time. It went well, we got some good RP in, and the characters got to test their mettle against each other in friendly contests.<br /> <br /> No Tatiana, but an extra Dearbh\u00e1il this time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 June 1920 (evening)<br /> <br /> Well, that was disappointing. The shipment of goods coming into town was delayed, so in turn our ambush of said goods was delayed. The train should be coming in tomorrow, along with our quarry. So, we had free time to kill this evening. Lizette took Dearbhail aside to have a private conversation. I\u2019m not sure what it was about but they both came back in good spirits so I\u2019m assuming everything is okay. While the two ladies had their chat Dacian and Wolfram decided to spar with swords in preparation for our ambush tomorrow night. They both did well and fought with skill. It seems that Dacian\u2019s lessons with the ghost are bearing fruit after a short time. That is good.<br /> <br /> Once the ladies came back Lizette it seemed did not want to be left out of the sparring so she challenged the two men to fight. Dacian stepped back, content to watch, and Wolfram accepted. Neither one wanted to lose so they both made good use of their own particular skills and magicks to aid them in their fight. They were exceptionally well balanced and fought really well. I can only hope that their skill from tonight is just as bright tomorrow evening.<br /> <br /> They fought twice, both times going full tilt. Wolfram won the first match and Lizette won the second by a slim margin. After they were done sparring. The slight inventor asked if anyone else wanted to have a go at it. Dacian indicated that he was fine where he was, so I said that I\u2019d spar against her. I will admit that I am not as practiced with a sword as I am with a rifle or my claws, but I do have some skill. I knew from the onset that I would not win the fight. Lizette\u2019s fae abilities were still partially animating her sword and I have no magicks that will aid me with a blade. The fight was fun and exhilarating though, so I did not mind her beating me. I did find it amusing that Lizette apparently found it necessary to cut several buttons off of my shirt as we sparred. It was her way of giving the others a show, Dearbhail seemed to like the view, and to prove Lizette\u2019s superior skill in a non-lethal way. In the end I conceded the fight and gave Lizette a bow.<br /> <br /> It seemed to be an ongoing theme for the evening and after the match with I sparred with Dacian. I did manage to best the other man, but I think that had to do more with his inexperience with a blade than my superior skill. Still it was fun and informative for both of us. He tends to leave his left side exposed more than he realizes. I pointed this out and showed him how would remedy the oversight. I suggested that he talk to Wolfram or his ghostly mentor for other suggestions as well.<br /> <br /> Throughout this whole thing Dearbhail, Christina and Marelene seemed to be enjoying themselves just watching the rest of us fight. It was rather blatant, and a bit daring on their parts, but I don\u2019t think anyone really minded having an audience. If men can get away with looking at women in such a way then it\u2019s only fair that they get a chance to look at us with the same expression.<br /> <br /> After everyone was done swinging sharp steel at one another Lizette came up with another challenge. She brought out her pistol and asked if anyone would like to have a contest shooting at targets. I smiled and said that I\u2019d take that challenge. Wolfram also volunteered to shoot with his Luger. So, while someone was busy setting up the targets I went to get my rifle. I will admit that it was fun, if a bit quaint, to be shooting at paper targets rather than people. It is certainly a different feeling. On the plus side, the paper targets are not constantly moving this way and that as they go about doing their daily actions. Or running if they\u2019ve caught wind that I\u2019m after them. Moving targets are harder to hit, but infinitely more satisfying. So, while the paper targets were a bit pedestrian I did have fun. Maybe it was because I was distracted by thoughts of my usual targets, but I did not win this little contest. Wolfram actually did. Not by much, but enough to concede the point. I will give him this, Wolfram is a talented solider, and I am glad to have him on my side. Lizette was also rather skilled with her pistol. I\u2019m not sure if she was using her fae abilities or natural talent to accomplish this. To be fair, I don\u2019t know if Wolfram was using any of his abilities either. Regardless, as long as they are this accurate tomorrow during the fight with the Pure then I will be content.<br /> <br /> I believe while we were sparring that Alla went out on the town looking for shows or performances that she might attend. I think she was in the mood for entertainment and to feed. I realize that it should probably bother me that she feeds off the blood of unsuspecting mortals, but it really doesn\u2019t. Even if she took enough to kill someone I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d be bothered all that much. They are not pack, not family and therefore I don\u2019t really feel overly concerned one way or another about them. This is a failing on my part, I know that. My mother tried to help me feel empathy for others, but it only ever extended so far before my capacity to care reached its limits. I will admit that the number of people that I hold in regard has increased quite a bit since becoming a part of this pack. If Wolfram has any say in the matter then Christina will be part of the pack soon enough, and by extension Marlene. My brother also got married, and so his dear wife has become part of the family. If our little group keeps growing as it has been then they may make a compassionate man out of me yet.<br /> <br /> 27 June 1920<br /> <br /> It is a new day. Everyone slept a little later than usual due to our martial contests last night, but as we did not have anything pressing on our schedule for this morning it was fine. During breakfast conversation turned to some of our abilities and Lizette mentioned that she can increase the accuracy or efficiency of different kinds of weapons. She offered to aid some of us with our chosen weapons, but could not do it for everyone. It would take a good deal out of her to do just a couple and we need her at full strength and capacity tonight. With this in mind she used her fae magicks on Alla\u2019s silver knuckles and my rifle. We will both be attacking with silver and we are both proven combatants. I would have suggested doing it with Tatiana\u2019s claws, but I don\u2019t think the power works on natural weapons like that. I do not mind gaining an advantage with my rifle though so I will not complain.<br /> <br /> The only task left to us until tonight is to keep ourselves occupied until then. I am well familiar that waiting for the fight is usually more nerve-wracking than the actual fighting is. Battle goes by too fast to do anything but attack, defend and dodge. All we can to do now is finalize our plans and wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 26 July 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> While I am in no way racing to meet my doom, I did find myself disappointed when we learned the train from Berlin was delayed. There would be no ambush tonight.<br /> <br /> To take the edge off and get more practice in, I moved to the inner courtyard of the Esterh\u00e1zy estate with my blades. Wolfram asked if I would mind an opponent. This immediately summoned the ladies. Dearbh\u00e1il, Lizette, Christina, and Marlena all came to bear witness. Wolfram called our match a draw, but he was being gracious. Lizette whispered something to her blade, threw her jacket over her shoulder like a matador, and strutted like a peacock out to us. I knew the attention of the observing ladies was more the goal of any further competition just as I knew cheating would soon commence. Thus I bowed out as Lizette tossed down her jacket and crossed blades with Wolfram.<br /> <br /> They looked majestic as their steel clashed with palatable power imbuing each thrust and parry. Each participant took one contest and looked magnificent, even in defeat. Out of respect for the proper spirit of competition, the two bowed and moved in separate directions. Lizette offered to spar with both Marek and myself. I again declined on the basis of dignity. I did smile as Marek joined the Wizened when I thought of how the playing field would be leveled when I held some command with the Contract of Blades. Dearbh\u00e1il was quite attentive to this match though from my vantage, Marek was finished before he began. I had to wonder what Lizette\u2019s skill would look like without the benefit of her Contracts? When the buttons flew from Marek\u2019s shirt exposing his toned chest, Dearbh\u00e1il barely muffled a giggle. Lizette was gracious enough to offer to repair the damage she had caused to the shirt. I again remembered how wonderful the Parisian could be.<br /> <br /> As the Wizened left with Marlena and Wolfram with Christina, I offered to spar with Marek as I knew I could receive an honest match. The Uratha accepted and did not disappoint. I was bested but with some effect. We shook hands with warm smiles in the end. He even offered a few points for me to be aware of. I apparently leave my left side open when I advance. It is good to learn this in friendly competition rather than deadly combat.<br /> <br /> Now I shall try to still my tense nerves. Tomorrow shall be less friendly.<br /> <br /> 27 July 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> Much of last night\u2019s joviality burned away with the morning mists.<br /> <br /> We joined together for a late lunch and most of us have since found ways of relaxing before our train arrives. While I still do not share in Tatiana\u2019s seeming hunger for battle, I will be happy when it has come to an end. I will be more pleased to see all of my cabal standing when the smoke clears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> My Dear Janos,<br /> Vienna is still a wonderful city though I do not believe the residents entirely believe the world has changed as much as it has. Despite the change in the noble class\u2019s stature in Vienna they still believe they have the upper hand. Of course the noble\u2019s involved are werewolves \u2013 a mad faction of the werewolves known as the Pure. I don\u2019t entirely understand exactly what they hope to gain but they are the enemies of my dear wolves Marek and Tatiana. \u2013 I have to wonder if it would bother them that I refer to them in such a manner. It seems terribly affectionate to me, but my brothers always said I was a bit \u201coff\u201d in what I find to be appropriate.<br /> <br /> I hope you get to meet them at some point in time. Oh! Perhaps you can come to the wedding! Not my wedding of course \u2013 but Wolfram\u2019s. I feel sure they\u2019ll be announcing a date soon. I am afraid I let the secret of his plan to ask for his lady\u2019s hand out before he had the opportunity to talk to her. I was ever so embarrassed. Stop laughing! I am quite aware I tend to speak before I think sometimes. But Wolfram was kind and did not get upset with me. I think Lady Christina\u2019s delight in his intentions made up for my indiscreet conversation. So, as I was saying, I\u2019m sure a date will be announced soon. It would be a lovely time to visit our new home in France. You would like Lizette &amp; Dacian and I think Tatiana would enjoy a drinking contest with you. She could give you a challenge I\u2019m sure!<br /> <br /> I should not avoid my purpose for writing any longer. I am concerned, my friend. One of the tasks we\u2019ve undertaken in Vienna has shown me that I could be a liability to my motley and I do not want to put them at risk. A few days ago we were tracking a vampire\u2019s whereabouts. Well, Tatiana, Marek, and Dacian were. I was along because I thought it would be nice to spend time with them and as we\u2019ve observed with Alla, vampires are not active during the day. We didn\u2019t believe there would be any danger but we were mistaken. The vampire was quite terrifying and somehow I seem to have alerted it to our presence &amp; he attacked.<br /> <br /> The others defended against him admirably but more vampires were coming so we had to leave quickly. I did attempt to help defend against the vampire \u2013 but despite the lessons in fighting my brothers gave me as a child \u2013 I was very ineffectual. The others do not see me in this way, I believe they are very gracious to acknowledge that my talents do not lie on a battlefield. But I feel as if I could be a distraction if I cannot defend myself properly. I do not believe I could, or wish to, become a warrior \u2013 but I would like to make a proper showing of it if someone were to attack me.<br /> <br /> It is possible I will have to deal with an attack in the coming hours \u2013 I am sure it will be fine, I won\u2019t be among the fighters but nearby just in case they are in need of healing. I am quite please to know I can assist in such a manner. But my martial skills must be improved! My dear friend, may I come to you once our time in Vienna is done for training? I will not make the trip until I hear from you. I would like to keep this from the others simply so they do not try to discourage me. I do not believe they would disapprove but I do not know if they would understand why I feel I must do this.<br /> <br /> Last night as our plans were changed at the last minute my friends engaged in contests of skill and sparring. It was enlightening (and thrilling) to observe them. Wolfram is a soldier \u2013 his martial prowess makes sense. Marek\u2019s abilities are of no surprise. I believe he fought in the Great War, but even if he did not, he carries himself as a warrior as does Tatiana. Dacian, with his lithe frame and quick actions also has skill \u2013 which he is improving on with the aid of a mentor or teacher. Lizette is a Wizened \u2013 she has the capability to make her weapons work even better than they should in the first place. Alla was not with us last night, but I do not worry for her safety. She is a vampire \u2013 so far I have met no vampire that cannot handle violence.<br /> <br /> Speaking of vampires \u2013 we are going to a salon hosted by one of them in a day or two. I am not happy about this but as the rest of my motley is going I don\u2019t feel that I can stay away. One of the vampires is interested in binding Alla to her after all and we cannot allow that to happen. It is also possible that we can find out where the necklace Christina asked us to find may be hidden or at least a clue to point us in the right direction. She\u2019s terribly concerned about getting it back though her companion wishes it would never return as it is cursed. Christina\u2019s brother asked her to keep it until he has a buyer for it. He\u2019s looking to boost the family fortune and in this situation it appears he was unaware of the cursed nature of the necklace. Or he has no regard for his sister\u2019s safety and if that is the case he should be beaten within an inch of his life. It is the brother\u2019s duty to look out for his sister just as she looks out for him.<br /> <br /> Did I not tell you there would be adventures when I started traveling and building my reputation once more? Are you terribly jealous that you didn\u2019t come with me now? I only jest, dear one, I know you are meant for your blacksmith shop. You are a steady presence in my life though we are so far apart. Please say you\u2019ll allow me to visit once more. I look forward to hearing from you soon.<br /> <br /> Sith agus Sl\u00e1inte 'bha!<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019 Plans</b><br /> <br /> So we got all ready to go, and everything got forestalled. I am sure it will be fine; I hope the others are not too anxious. We got some extra practice sparring and exhibition matches, however.<br /> <br /> Before then, I spoke to Dearbh\u00e1il. I wanted to clarify that I was not engaged with an affair with a specific person, and did not want her looking too closely into my partners, for the sake of my partners themselves. I wanted to shield their dignity. I also dropped hints I am experimenting with women more generally, but I detected no interest. Ah well. Overall it was a success. She stressed she wanted me to be happy. She claimed she was always happy. I hope she was telling the truth.<br /> <br /> We joined the others, and Wolfram and Dacian were doing some sparring. I noticed Christina and Marlene watching, and saw Dearbh\u00e1il sit to watch and make daisy chains. I decided as much fun as the boys were having, I could add a little challenge to their evening. I enhanced the usability of a sword nearby and sashayed over and challenged Wolfram, saying I would show him how we did it in France. No half measures.<br /> <br /> I had seen boys in Paris practice swordplay, the showy style some indulged in involved a hand on a hip and a lot of motion. I was pretty sure I could fake that. As a Wizened, I am quick, and the sword sought to serve me. I entered with my coat over my shoulder, but dropped it one handed as I moved out to spar. I am pretty sure I even got the en garde stance right. I was something to see.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was quick to challenge. I quickly realized even as I had ensorcelled my blade, he called upon his grave-borne vigor to bring power behind his sword. Our initial exchange favored him, not by a huge margin but the victor was obvious. I pushed more power into my blade, and challenged him to a rematch. The rematch favored me as he was, I think, unprepared for how much I wanted to win. Honestly, so was I. When I saw just how intensely my sword struck under my command I\u2026sort of took it easy. Humiliating Wolfram was never the goal, and, honestly, if he wanted to match again he would have been more prepared. It looked closer than it was, but I was the clear victor.<br /> <br /> I challenged Dacian and Marek. Dacian demurred, but Marek stepped in. I think he was also somewhat unprepared for the magic behind my weapon. But then, claws, teeth and rifles are more his specialty. I maintained enough control to cut several buttons on his shirt and expose his chest, to Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s delight. I felt good about the win\u2026and quietly promised to repair the shirt.<br /> <br /> Marek and Wolfram had a turn, which went to the German. Feeling confidant I suggested a test of skill with firearms. I glamoured my pistol well up, and Wolfram and Marek took up the challenge. It seems I was a bit overconfident, as I tied the sniper and Wolfram managed to slightly outfire us both. I did not actually want him to look bad so I suppose it was good.<br /> <br /> Now, I had to ask myself, why did I indulge in the rowdy play with the boys? Why did I indulge in something so archaic as sword fighting? Aiming for a nonmoving target? I am a woman of the future, of the twentieth century. Swords were getting behind the times in the sixteenth century. But ultimately, it was play. It was impressing the other ladies. It was showing the boys that girl or not, I could stand side by side with them. That\u2019s why I did it.<br /> <br /> The rather intense carnality later that night was not such a bad reason either.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> The initial sparring with Dacian and Wolfram was just contested rolls, but once Lizette got involved she and Wolfram upped the ante. He used his Industrial Caul and channeled Plasm through his keystone sword, while Lizette involved Contracts of Artifice and Animation to double buff her sword and gun. While she initially only went with Artifice, when Wolfram won the first round she activated Animation as well. She used both (I think) on her gun, while Wolfram used his stored Lugar from his Caul which gave it a bonus. Not the best use of fuel before a big fight, but Lizette at least restored the 9 (!) glamour she used before the combat.<br /> <br /> The duel with Wolfram and Lizette was both described as showing off for the ladies and flirting with each other. They have odd ways of flirting.<br /> <br /> She used Artifice to buff Alla and Marek\u2019s weapons the next day. She pushed for the exceptional success, and while she was able to regain glamour, she was short a couple willpower for the battle. Still the bonuses made Alla and Marek quite potent in the battle.<br /> <br /> Alla did some hunting to top her Vitae off.<br /> <br /> That covers it. We had the big battle tonight, and it was the whole session. One Vampire, one ghoul, six Werewolves, Five Wolf-Blooded, Three Changelings, one Sin-Eater, one Ghost, and three Spirits all were in a huge battle in the cemetery in the shadow of a Cathedral. Marek one shots a Werewolf! Lizette cuts a man in half with a chainsaw! Wolfram and Gunnar have a duel! You simply must come and read it. See you then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T19:52:05-07:00","id":687776,"title":"","content":"Somehow, I kind of feel sorry for Lizette that Dearbh\u00e1il doesn't appear to have any interest in her (or indeed even notice her attraction).<br /> It was interesting to learn more about Marek's psyche. lt somewhat looks like he's recovering from some sort antisocial disorder thanks to the pack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T22:56:52-07:00","id":687962,"title":"","content":"Lizette is certainly attracted to Dearbh\u00e1il but is not really shattered at her lack of interest. Did kind of hurt her pride, and MAY have had something to do with her ostentatious display with the sparring. Still much of her ego comes from her intellect and skill at mechanics.<br /> <br /> Marek is something of a sociopath, and his learning to care about more than his brother is something the player very much wants to explore. Sort of part of this is he has the attention of most of the party who like men to one degree or another, but his player probably expected that when that actor was chosen to be him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-06-2015, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T00:02:07-07:00","id":704430,"title":"","content":"After much planning, we move to the battle. This session was all prep and combat, so when the journals focus on it that\u2019s because, well, that is mostly what happened.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 27 June 1920<br /> Tonight was satisfying. We planned that I would go to a high point on the outside of the Catholic church near the edge of the graveyard and snipe the Pure with my rifle, Tatiana would take care of the spirits, Lizette was armed with her chainsaw and was also going for the Pure. Wolfram was going to go after Gunnar and Alla will keep the Pure\u2019s attention on her so they won\u2019t shred our pack-mates. Dearbhail was going to stay to the outskirts of the fight and support us with her healing abilities if needed. Dacian had planned on hiding out on top of the crypt, invisibly, and blinding and otherwise hindering anyone that needed it. Good plan. It even mostly went the way we expected it to. Before the fight began we did several things to prepare. We asked Ochranny for her blessings, as well as using gifts of our own to increase the skill and durability of several of our number. <br /> <br /> We did pretty much exactly as we\u2019d planned. Tatiana took on the spirits. There were three of them. A Pain spirit and two spirits of Protection. They worked well together to cause us problems and to heal and protect their charges. Tatiana though was not to be deterred. She fought tirelessly to take down the spirits that the Pure had brought with them. She was the only one that could do it since I was in my perch. I felt a little bad that I could not help my fellow Uratha, but I did some good from my vantage point. There are several threats that were eliminated due to my position and choice of weapon. Tatiana also took on Ilsa herself during part of the fight. The Pure woman perceived that Tatiana was a threat and decided to attack her. She did not leave much of a mark though. Tatiana ended up chasing the other werewolf off at the end of the fight. She wasn\u2019t actually going to engage the Pure since we wanted Ilsa to get away, but the other woman didn\u2019t need to know that. That part of the plan worked out rather well if I do say so myself.<br /> <br /> Alla played her part and played it well. She set out to be a distraction for the Pure and she succeeded. She used her silver knuckles to good effect, even gaining the attention of Ilsa herself. Though I suppose the thing that gained her attention the most was when Alla picked up the statue of the angel and threw it at Ilsa. That was definitely a good way to gain someone\u2019s attention if you ask me. Though pounding one\u2019s minions flat with knuckles made of silver worked rather well too.<br /> <br /> Wolfram afforded himself well tonight against Gunnar. The two were perhaps not the most evenly matched if you just looked at their physical capabilities, but Wolfram had a few tricks up his sleeve tonight. He seemed able to soak up as much damage as Gunnar could dish out with little real affect. I don\u2019t know how many times I thought for sure that Wolfram was going to fall, and he just shrugged it off like it was a mosquito bite. Some of it was Ochranny\u2019s blessing, some of it was his own Spirit\u2019s gifts.<br /> <br /> Dacian managed to stay hidden for most of the fight on top of the Crypt. I saw him strike at least one man with a gun blind. The man decided to forgo shooting and pulled out his knife instead. As soon as I saw what happened to him I knew that he wasn\u2019t going to last long in the fight. It was just a matter of time. I think Dacian also spread fear to some of the men, because at least one of Ilsa\u2019s mortal followers made a beeline for one of the trucks. Maybe it\u2019s just that I never leave witnesses, or maybe I wasn\u2019t sure if he was going to go for the truck that had the artifacts in it, but I took him out with a single head shot. I will admit that I had a satisfying time tonight. Every man I shot died in short order.<br /> <br /> Lizette for her part started off with a silver loaded pistol, but ended up demonstrating in graphic detail exactly what a chainsaw will do to human or Uratha flesh. It is rather impressive I will say. Rather messy, but very impressive. There is also the intimidation factor to work in. This unfortunately led several of the mortal gunman to take aim at the slight inventor. They were intimidated by her choice of weapon I think. Lizette was shot twice in short order and fell to the ground after the second round. I will admit that I grew worried when I saw her go down. I have become rather fond of the Fae woman and did not want to lose her company so soon. Thankfully she managed to get back up, still wielding her chainsaw and nearly cut one of the gunman in half from hip to chin. <br /> <br /> Even Wolfram\u2019s ghostly teacher, Franz helped to fight off the gunman. He engaged and killed one of the gunman himself. Not that I didn\u2019t think him capable, I just wasn\u2019t sure if ghosts retained their fighting ability or if it faded with time. He seemed to handle himself just fine for a spirit.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail used her Fae magicks to heal those that needed it and even chided Dacian for shielding himself from sight after he\u2019d been shot by a gunman. He had become visible to use one of his powers and one of the human henchmen took offense at this and did his best to kill our shadowy packmate. At that moment I had two targets that both needed to die, but could only shoot one of them at a time. A gunman was about to go after Lizette and the one that had shot Dacian once already was lining up a second shot to take him out. In the end I gambled that Lizette and her chainsaw would be able to kill her combatant before the unfortunate man had a chance to act. I wasn\u2019t as certain about the man on Dacian, so I took him out with a single shot as well. I should probably mention my work as Reznik to the others. After tonight\u2019s showing it will not be a surprise.<br /> <br /> In the end I took out three men with three shots. The first to go down was the tall Pure man that came with Ilsa. Our plan had been to take out the Pure first and so he was my first target. Lizette and I were to focus our attention on him until he went down. Well, one shot with a silver bullet did that just fine. The second was the man running, and the third was Dacian\u2019s attacker. After that first shot though I thought I felt something start to shift inside me, but it stopped. Nothing physical really, it was just a feeling. Brief, then gone just as quickly. It happened only with the first shot, so I am thinking that it has something to do with using silver weapons against another werewolf. I had been warned about using silver weapons, and I knew that something might happen, but it was the best way to ensure that our targets didn\u2019t just brush off the damage as if it were nothing.<br /> <br /> So, the quick version of events is thus. We engaged with the enemy, taking care not to hit Ilsa with anything silver. The other Pure could rage if they wanted to, and one did, but we did not want her to fall into the Rage. We wanted her to run. The fighting was fast and brutal all around and several of our number were wounded. Lizette and Dacian most of all. In the end they enemy had all fallen and we made a show of harrying Ilsa in the direction we wanted her to go. She jumped into one of the cars and drove off as fast as she could. Unfortunately for her, Lizette used her Fae abilities to wreak havoc on the vehicles brakes. Ilsa crashed the car and was thrown out of it, pretty badly wounded. It probably didn\u2019t help the fleeing woman that Wolfram also used his powers to set her on fire while she was driving away. It helped us plenty. It just didn\u2019t help her. In the end we made a show of trying to catch up to her and \u201cfailing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Once the excitement was over Dearbhail healed those that needed it. I don\u2019t think she was able to get rid of all of their wounds, but she greatly reduced their severity. We then discussed what we were going to do with all the bodies we had lying around. We could not leave them in the graveyard for the authorities to find. That would lead to too many questions, but we had to do something with them. All the gunfire would draw the police, there was no question about that. In the end we agreed to let Dearbhail open a doorway to some place she called the \u201cHedge.\u201d We threw the bodies in that place and then shut the door behind us.<br /> <br /> The last thing we needed to do was to dispose of the vehicles, or at least some of them. We took the truck that had the items we were looking for to a parking lot on Christina\u2019s property. The one that Lizette \u201ctinkered\u201d with was in flames. The others we just left where they were. It\u2019ll be a mystery for the authorities to figure out, but it shouldn\u2019t be traceable back to us.<br /> <br /> Now we just need to make it look like Gunnar has run off to avoid his duel with Wolfram in the morning. I believe Dacian was planning on breaking into Gunnar\u2019s place and hastily packing a bag and leaving, making it obvious that he had run off. A body would cause too many questions, but just his absence allows those curious about his whereabouts to use their imagination. And the imagination of the community is better than any lie we could come up with. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, yes, my brother, it was an excellent fight. One to howl of and celebrate, to be sure. But work is not yet done, so we will howl later.<br /> <br /> Indeed, volchonok, they were as pups before a rabid bear. They growl and snarl but they can do nothing. We had every advantage, even in their own home. 4 werewolves to two and it was no contest for us.<br /> <br /> Heh, yes, volchonok, I was there, remember? You are an excitable one. I did see Marek end the worthless Pure lackey to Gunnar with a single bullet to the head. He has much skill with the gun. I fear the Pure Wolfblooded would have made of with the relics had he not stopped him. Fenric was on hand, of course. He could have slowed him down enough. Probably.<br /> <br /> It is not so unbelievable. His mistress is quite skilled. Surely you saw her destroy the other werewolf lackey with a single punch? Silver laced, yes, but even so. She even took a hit from Ilsa with nothing but bruises to show.<br /> <br /> That is unkind, volchonok. Wolfram would have killed his rival much quicker had it been a proper duel, without the interference of the purity spirits and their healing. Wolfram is to be commended for his bravery, to be certain, even if his wisdom was lacking in this instance. It is not many men who could stand against a werewolf and destroy him, and come out largely unscathed.<br /> <br /> I got to the purity spirit as quickly as I could, foolish volchonok. The pain spirit was much more dangerous, and Wolfram was not truly in danger, not yet. It only took a pair of bites to rip its armored shell to pieces, spikes and all, no matter how much it made my blood burn. The blessing of our totem was still appreciated.<br /> <br /> Yes, Ochranny\u2019s blessings were upon us. It definitely helped Alla take Ilsa\u2019s hit, and Lizette probably would have fallen, had our totem not been with her.<br /> <br /> Oh, you noticed, did you, volchonok? I thought you might have ignored her use of such a human thing.<br /> <br /> This is true - it is difficult to ignore a chainsaw wielded in such a way. I did not even have to lend her my Gift, though I did Alla. Fairy magics are strong. The Prussian Wolfblooded stood no chance. Well, their rifles gave them some chance. Their fear as she closed almost did her in, but it was not enough, especially since our songbird\u2019s fairy healing magic is also powerful.<br /> <br /> Our thief is a more subtle man. I believe he cursed our foes with blindness and fear. At least, one of the rifleman decided to abandon his military firing discipline and draw a knife. It did him not much good against Lizette\u2019s chainsaw.<br /> <br /> Our songbird was upset at Dacian because he used his magics to disappear when he got wounded.<br /> <br /> Yes, it did mean that he did not get hurt further, but she told him not to. She is not always reasonable about these things. She wished to do more in combat, rather than after.<br /> <br /> Of course we let Ilsa go. This was the plan, yes? To spread news of the defeat of the Pure in Vienna. Foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> I believe this was Lizette? She has powers to make \u2018human things\u2019 break. It would be a great coincidence if the car merely broke down.<br /> <br /> Of course I harried her away, it could not be obvious that she was to escape. Besides, I believe that Wolfram and Dacian had some anger to express. If I could throw fireballs and silver daggers at a fleeing Pure, I would probably do so after winning a fight.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, it is not the time to run. Now that the bodies have been left in the fairy lands, we must prepare the deception regarding Wolfram\u2019s duel, prepare for this vampire salon, and speak with Krieger concerning what was done this night. There is no time for running now.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 27 June 1920 - Early Evening<br /> <br /> We have made our plans and now we prepare ourselves and our abilities. The cabal has been divided into our respective teams and a sense of deep calm has settled over us. I choose to believe it is a sign. We will strike decisively or we will quite literally fall to the wolves.<br /> <br /> 27 June 1920 - Late<br /> <br /> I was to be a noble, in a nearly forgotten life. I was a servant for a lifetime best left in shadows. For a time, I was used as a distraction to gain the trust of Gentry before attacks were launched. When I was betrayed and abandoned, I fought my way through the Hedge and found myself given another chance at life. I fancied myself as an artisan of my chosen craft. But tonight I have been the Terror out of Sight, the Harrier of Hope, and the Promise of Death. Though I am not yet finished, I shall start again.<br /> <br /> I began my insurgence by masking any trace of my passing before reaching the crypt. Once my scent was hidden, I moved around freely verifying we were not ourselves walking into a trap. Once I satisfied my suspicions, I let the others know the crypt was clear. While we awaited Lizette and Wolfram\u2019s arrival, I scuttled around the top of the crypt in a very well hidden vantage. After a time, I heard Lizette\u2019s motorcar sliding to a halt at the rendezvous point. I knew our prey was close behind. I made detecting me or anything else harder and hid myself even more deeply in the stone. I made sure I could see ghosts so I could communicate with our chivalrous spectre if the need arose and then I saw the first arrival. Three vehicles from separate directions arrived in total. The first was apparently Gunnar\u2019s men. A footman drove the other four men dressed in what I recognized as noble uniforms. Gunnar arrived next, oddly alone, in his own car. Lastly, Ilsa arrived in the cargo truck with two other men. One was notably tall, the other short. It was rather odd. They both carried themselves with the same cocksure attitude as Ilsa so I assumed they were addition Pure of Berlin.<br /> <br /> While they were carefully stepping through their political dance, Lizette ran through with the information that Ilsa\u2019s greatest fear is to be forced into marriage against her will. I couldn\u2019t see how this was relevant currently, as I certainly couldn\u2019t preside over a service. Given that could have alerted our targets however, I prepared to strike from my hidden nook. The four noblemen each took a rifle from the trunk. Their practiced lockstep movements suggested military training, if the rifles did not. Indeed, the assembled group came to investigate the crypt with precision and confidence. We waited until the advantage of surprise offset their numbers. Marek opened fire from an adjacent mausoleum, killing the taller werewolf next to Ilsa. I was startled as I did not expect a werewolf to die so easily. Tatiana leapt from her hiding place in dire wolf or Urshal form to bite at Gunnar\u2019s car. I am told there was a spirit there. I assume this is the case and not some kind of battle madness. Nevertheless, Alla popped up and threw a challenging swing at the shorter werewolf. Her silver knuckledusters missed, though our vampire definitely had all the attention from her opponent. One of the riflemen opened fire on Wolfram, who was charging, pistol drawn for Gunnar. Our Bound never flinched as the wound seemed to softly billow white smoke. Alla\u2019s opponent shifted to his dire wolf form as Wolfram shot Gunnar in the heart. The Pure did not fall, but was grievously wounded. The next rifleman shot Wolfram as well, but the fiery armor only I could see deflected the bullet. I was frightened at how quickly everything was happening but pushed through the fear. I was finally able to strike then, blinding one of the riflemen with Murkblur. I would not see another unanswered shot fired at Wolfram. Just as one threat was temporarily removed, another rose. In fact, Gunnar rose to nearly nine feet as his body seemed to reject the damage Wolfram had inflicted. The wound closed as fur tore through the skin. Gunnar lashed out with his feral claws, no thought to strategy, only survival fueling his attack. Wolfram would have been torn to ribbons were he a lesser man. But his armor did not dull the full power of the blow. Fortunately, his death magic protected him and though he smoked like a campfire, he stood strong. Dearbh\u00e1il screamed a curse so potent in her Irish tongue that even Gunnar was affected. I was surprised such horrible words could come from such a lovely voice. Another shot rang out but the bullet ricocheted from Wolfram\u2019s back into a statue. The damage to the cemetery angel was enough to rouse our final combatant from his slumber.<br /> <br /> The distance peel of gunfire explained the sudden collapse of the footman Fenric was chasing to the cargo truck. This was obviously a human as his corpse littered the ground in a wide radius from the body. Tatiana was still mauling the unseen spirit at the cars. For just a moment, we all seemed to slow as Alla threw a punch so devastating, she killed her opponent before his broken body could even strike the ground. The dire wolf shrank back into the shorter man just as the horrible sound of Lizette\u2019s chainsaw broke the stillness. The Wizened charged from cover, weapon ahead, herself growling. The riflemen with the sight to do so, turned their barrels toward the Gremlin. One fired a terrible round into Lizette just as Wolfram shot Gunnar at point blank. The werewolf was deeply wounded as was Lizette, who received a second shot from the other rifleman. I had to do something and fear was the first thought I had. Using my Contracts, I instilled the creeping dread of darkness rising in the rifleman nearest to me. That I shouted from the underside of the crypt awning, where I was until then invisible, made me more of a target than I intended. So much blood came next. It was a blur of fury and gunfire. I remember Dearbh\u00e1il screaming, seeing Franz Ludwig advance on the men firing at Lizette, and then pain. The fourth rifleman spotted me before I could again turn invisible. His bullet drank deeply of my blood. I stumbled down from the crypt and coughed up more blood.<br /> <br /> I looked my murderer in the eye as his finger tightened on the trigger. The shot I heard seemed wrong however. Then I realized Marek had saved me. As the rifleman\u2019s body fell limply forward, I spotted the Bone Shadow abseiling down the side of the mausoleum. From the corner of my eye, Tatiana had moved on to a different empty space to attack. Alla struck Ilsa with another piece of the statuary before the nightmarish gurgling of the rifleman cut down by Lizette\u2019s chainsaw momentarily drowned out the other nearby sounds of battle. A flurry of combat surrounded me on all sides. I could not see for sure where all the enemy gunmen were and I knew I could not take another wound like I carried already. I watched Wolfram fire a third round into the werewolf before I vanished. Dearbh\u00e1il screamed again but I could not see why. I knew I couldn\u2019t stay hidden long so I found cover for when I reappeared. From my vantage, I saw Fenric climb into the cargo truck to protect our prize. Then I turned to see Franz Ludwig run another of the riflemen through.<br /> <br /> I heard Tatiana savaging another piece of air before Lizette\u2019s chainsaw sang a gruesome duet with one of the dwindling riflemen. Franz Ludwig held Ilsa at bay while the duel continued, though I took the time to tear a piece of white cloth from my undershirt. I tied it to the pommel of my dagger. I intended to slip up behind the shewolf and tie the silver to her tail. As amusing as that would have been, Gunnar was finally overcome by his wounds with Wolfram\u2019s fourth silver bullet. Ilsa, realising she was outnumbered, out maneuvered, out gunned, and out of luck, shifted to her Dalu form and make a break for Gunnar\u2019s car.<br /> <br /> Before she could drive away, I hurled one of my silver daggers such that it embedded into the door next to her. Wolfram summoned an orb of flame into his palm before hurling it at Ilsa as she drove frantically away. She shrieked as burns appeared on her flesh. Lizette stopped then and simply blew a kiss after the werewolf. I felt a subtle shift in the Wyrd and Gunnar\u2019s car careened off the road. Ilsa was thrown from the wreckage due to her reckless driving. Marek and Dearbh\u00e1il fell in with rest of the cabal behind a bloody Lizette as she began to walk menacingly toward Ilsa, chainsaw at the ready. The plan was to allow her to escape, though I cannot say Lizette would have stopped if she were able to reach her quarry. And we could not let her believe she was spared. As the werewolf turned to look over her shoulder, she saw the complete assemblage of our group walking toward, with, but also oblivious to, our varying degrees of injury. I can only imagine what a terrifying image it must have been, if only based on her expression. At that point, the only Pure survivor from the ambush bolted into the night.<br /> <br /> I turned to the others with a smile that faded quickly as Dearbh\u00e1il began swatting me for disappearing. In my pain, I could do little but pull away and look pitifully confused at the insane Fairest. In the process of her browbeating me for making it hard for her to heal me, she lessened most of my wounds, then hugged me. I believe she may have been distraught at how wounded several of us were and felt somewhat responsible. Since then we have gathered the bodies (and anything useful from them) and thrown them into the Hedge. And if that horrible sound from the forest is any indication, Lizette found the last rifleman.<br /> <br /> Now we must go and make sure Gunnar\u2019s home looks as though he left in a hurry to escape his duel with Wolfram tomorrow. With that, I will become the Silver Conspirator and my job for the evening will be complete. The relics will return with us and after Gunnar is humiliated tomorrow, I can set about indexing and identifying what our bounty can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Okay, that\u2019s out of the way, now focus, girl.<br /> <br /> Through the power of my Glamour, I was able to do well in the fight. I was also able to observe a variety of supernatural creatures in action.<br /> <br /> Alla, as a Vampire, withstood a couple direct attacks from a Werewolf. Even Ilsa was not able to slow her down much. She killed a Werewolf with a single blow using silver, enhanced by my glamour. She is a silken tiger.<br /> <br /> Vampires are frighteningly resilient. Only Wolfram shrugged off damage like she did. Her strength is clearly greater than it appeared\u2026Alla was able to throw a stone statue at Ilsa as well as, as noted, kill a Werewolf with a silver assisted haymaker. Vampires continue to frighten me with their power.<br /> <br /> Marek had noted he was an excellent shot, and this proved his boast was not without teeth. He killed a Werewolf in a single shot, and another two human defenders with a single shot each. His lethal accuracy was\u2026impressive, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Tatiana, unsurprisingly, was more hands on and visceral. She targeted Spirits, so to me she appeared to be shadowboxing. She evidently took three down. Two of them with a single blow each. I lack knowledge of Spirits to know how impressive this is, but I feel a certainty I would not want to have a strike from her against me.<br /> <br /> One thing I discovered was the claim silver is lethal to werewolves was no empty claim. Only Gunnar withstood more than a single shot, and he had spirits helping him. There is still no questioning their lethality, however. I hope we do not have to fight more Werewolves soon.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il healed. And hexed a little. Her Spring Court magic proved most helpful in lessening my injuries. She kept her head through the fight, though, which is good.<br /> <br /> Dacian started off using the Contracts of Smoke, but ceased at some point to taunt the mortals. He was hurt badly. His talents as a thief far outstrip his talents as a warrior, and I hope he takes more care for his safety next time.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was a juggernaut, as much as Alla, shrugging off rifle shots and werewolf claws, smoke pouring from his injuries. He was very impressive. I doubt I was the only lady who noticed. And like Alla, he was barely scratched when the fight was over despite the concerted effort to take him down. He also made Ilsa burst into flames.<br /> <br /> Just based on Wolfram, Sin-Eaters are powerful and implacable foes. He claimed some ability to shrug off man made attacks, and it served him well. I am unsure if this salient ability is special to him or common to Sin-Eaters. I know his ability to unleash ectoplasm fog and shrug off injuries is not uncommon. I can see now high explosives, set off from a remote location, are the way to fight them.<br /> <br /> I could not get a good idea of the Spirits or Ghosts, as only Franz Ludwig actually appeared and he fought like a human. I did not see the others but Tatiana shredded them easily. I suppose this could be said of most things she attacks, however.<br /> <br /> But the mission was a success, and I have learned much. I have a better idea of more supernatural creatures capabilities should they need to be dealt with, and I have cultivated a strong appreciation for the fact the rest of the Motley is on my side.<br /> <br /> Also, Mayhem was wrought. It was glorious.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIV</i><br /> <br /> That was pretty crazy. Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> Several people got an extra health level from the totem, including Marek, Tatiana, and Lizette. Dacian got defense. Lizette buffed the weaker willed allies with the third level of Contracts of Entropy, as well as her uses of Contracts of Artifice ahead of time to boost others weapons (and Artifice and Animation on her own). Dearbh\u00e1il used some Hearth on the enemies when not healing her allies. There was a lot of prep time, and it was used well.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed Requiem vampires are tough. Alla easily shrugged off incoming rifle fire even with just a couple levels of Resilience.<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws were dangerous, but well tanked by Tatiana, Alla and Wolfram. Especially given one one killed in a single shot in the first action of the fight by Marek. The humans were Wolf Blooded, hence their immunity to Werewolf hijinx.<br /> <br /> I implemented the Distractions hack from Armory Reloaded, allowing Changelings to Spend a Glamour to boost their Defense by their Wyrd against a single attack by an enemy who was not of the Wyrd themselves or enchanted. While useful, Lizette and Dacian took heavy damage compared to the Kindred and Bound shrugging damage off. Chainsaw damage is insane, by the way. Changelings also had the option of taking an action to try and harvest glamour at a small penalty, which Lizette did for fear in order to replenish her reserves burned though in buffing herself and others.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where Dacian finds himself alone and in danger in hostile territory and tempers flare as Christina intuits her companion has been with Lizette. Join us!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T06:29:25-07:00","id":704786,"title":"","content":"Very impressive battle ! It really showed how fragile Changelings are compared to other supernaturals, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 10-17-2015, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T00:30:39-07:00","id":706438,"title":"","content":"Somewhat. I mean Lizette took two direct shots with a rifle, six health levels before adding dice for hit successes. Use of Distractions meant she took less since I let it apply to ranged attacks. But Lizette is hard to hit normally...remember she took on a psychic then when she went down a demon who had ambush in rapid succession and had the demon badly hurt using only a claw hammer. Lizette has taken a lot of damage, but she is also pretty fearless, which means her actions are not always as...tactically sound. Also, as may have been conveyed, she is trying to demonstrate badassery.<br /> <br /> Dacian, well, I am sure his player felt revealing himself to rifleman and making the atmosphere a bit spookier seemed a good idea at the time. His PCs have a history of...interesting decisions in combat when occasionally silence the table.<br /> <br /> However, you are correct in that it was not just tactics. Sin-Eaters and 2nd edition vampires, especially ones heavily invested in physical disciplines like Alla (not min/maxed, 2 Celerity, 2 Resilience 1 Vigor as well as her 2 Majesty). Marek is more fragile, but Marek, unlike Liz or Dacian, remained hidden. Changelings are finesse creatures for the most part, though an Ogre jacking his strength to 12 or 15 hurts like hell when he punches you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-18-2015, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T01:05:53-07:00","id":710130,"title":"","content":"I would also point out that when making characters we knew the party had two werewolves so combat wasn't a primary for any of the Changelings. Because I expected there would be some werewolf enemies along the way and since it suited the Firebrand Templar I did give Wolfram Caul and Shroud with an eye toward survivability. I honestly didn't realize how much Industrial Caul would end up enhancing his pistol and thus also making him decent at offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T18:26:06-07:00","id":716598,"title":"","content":"Safe to say Wolfram was running on fumes by the end of the fight. Good fight though. I love it when a plan comes together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:54:44-07:00","id":720523,"title":"","content":"Yes and no Omenseer. He still had about half his plasm (he went in mostly full) and thanks to the armor granted by his powers he only took one level of damage beyond what he could bulwark (which ended up being the bonus level the pack's totem gave him). He could have gone another couple of rounds at least without counting the Fairest ready to heal. He also had a few more silver bullets in his Luger. So he had fight left in him, but had things gone longer he'd have been taking real damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:54:50-07:00","id":742973,"title":"","content":"In the aftermath of the combat at the Cemetery, our heroes seek to tie up loose ends and get back to the investigation for the necklace. But strange luck follows, as Lizette finds her affections coveted, and Dacian grows bold after many successful thefts.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 27 June 1920<br /> <br /> Dacian headed over to Gunnar\u2019s place to leave \u201cevidence\u201d of the man fleeing and the rest of us headed back to Christina\u2019s house. Of course Marlene and Christina fussed over Lizette as soon a she walked in the door. She had elected not to change her clothes before she walked in and still showed evidence of having been hurt. Wolfram had Fenric run in and get him a change of clothes before he walked in the door. I do not believe that he wanted to worry the woman he intends to marry. The rest of us walked in as is, but did not gain much attention, regardless the state of our clothing. Though we were not aiming for such. <br /> <br /> A strange look passed over Christina\u2019s face when Marlene was tending to Lizette. The other woman stammered and left the room quickly. I\u2019m not sure what was going on, but it seemed that Dearbhail did and took the other woman aside to talk. Before they left however Christina offered us food or drink. Despite the circumstances she refused to be a bad hostess. Tatiana said that she would like food, specifically meat. I agreed and nodded my assent as well. It was Dearbhail that came back and gave Tatiana and I a portion of ham. We split the meat and the bone. Cracking the bone reminded me that it\u2019s been too long since I\u2019ve actually just hunted as a wolf. I believe that Tatiana is closer to that side of herself than I am, or sometimes if feels like that. Sometime I\u2019m going to have to let go of being Marek and just let myself run.<br /> <br /> I believe that there are some lingering feelings for Lizette in Christina\u2019s heart and she\u2019s having a hard time with them. Propriety would say that she should not pursue them, but I think she wants to do otherwise. Wolfram is aware of all this, but I don\u2019t think Christina has picked up on his feelings on the matter. I overhead Dearbhail tell him that he should talk to Christina about her feelings towards our slight inventor. Life is too short to not act on your feelings. I realize that society may frown upon the emotions going on between those three, but I don\u2019t. They should enjoy it as Dearbhail would say. Of course I have not been one to be too overly concerned with how society views people\u2019s behaviors. I do my best to mimic the reactions of those around me, but sometimes I just don\u2019t get it right and I can\u2019t find it within myself to get too overly concerned about it. I suppose that will be something that I need to work on in the future.<br /> <br /> Not long after we\u2019d gotten back to the house I got the sudden feeling that Dacian was wounded and in trouble. I told Tatiana and the others that Dacian needed help and we took off. Tatiana and I ran in wolf form towards Gunnar\u2019s house. Some of the others followed in a car. We had almost reached Dacian when suddenly all senses of him ended. They just stopped like he wasn\u2019t in the world anymore. Even dead someone gives off a scent, so I knew he wasn\u2019t dead. At least not yet. Then a few minutes later I was able to sense him again, but this time he was much closer to us. Then suddenly Dacian comes stumbling out of the woods in front of us. It seems that he had made his way through the Fae realm to get to us. <br /> <br /> Dacian was not in good shape. Tatiana and I stabilized his wounds so he wasn\u2019t actively bleeding out in front of us. A few moments later Dearbhail, Alla and Wolfram were able to catch up to where we were. Dearbhail opened a gate into the Hedge place to escape the Pain Spirit that was still pursuing Dacian. The spirit had placed a Mark on Dacian which would allow it to track him wherever he went, but it only worked if you stayed in the mortal world. They could not track him to the Fae lands, so we stayed there for about two hours or so until I could feel the Mark dissolve. In that time Tatiana and I protected the rest of the pack while Dearbhail healed Dacian to the best of her abilities. <br /> <br /> Apparently the negative attention that Dacian gained he brought on himself by stealing a sword of Gunnar\u2019s that had been hidden in the man\u2019s room. Dacian argued that if it was important then Gunnar would not have left without it, but was not aware until it was too late that it was being guarded by several spirits. He opted to keep a hold of the blade as he ran. Unfortunately the spirits wounded him several times as he fled so his blood was left behind. He can be tracked by that if the Pure have a desire to do so.<br /> <br /> And the sprits can tell the other Pure what happened, so our plan of making it look like Gunnar just up and ran away has been hindered. While we waited for the Mark to dissolve we talked about the plan for the morning when Wolfram must meet for the duel. We of course know that Gunner will not be showing up, but it would look suspicious if we acted on that knowledge. So, Wolfram must show up expecting to duel. The problem with our plan was that originally Dacian was going to be Wolfram\u2019s Second, but he is rather badly wounded and Dearbhail can only do so much right now to heal him. We argued back and forth about whether he should go or if we should another person in his place. That in and of itself might also be suspicious. So we agreed that Dacian would still go as Wolfram\u2019s Second, but would mask the scent of his blood with large amounts of cologne. <br /> <br /> While we were in the Hedge Wolfram took the opportunity to look more closely at the sword that Dacian had acquired. As soon as he started to draw it from its scabbard Alla growled and told him to put it away, now. Apparently this sword is specifically designed to kill Vampires and weaken them more than an ordinary sword would do already. Alla said that she had the feeling that whoever was holding the drawn blade was a personal threat to her. We agreed to leave the blade sheathed unless absolutely necessary. We also discussed what weapons we would bring to the Salon. Technically it would not be polite to go armed, so some people are going to have Wolfram hold onto their weapons and conceal them within himself. He is going to do this for his own weapon and for Lizette\u2019s flame thrower. Tatiana and I are our own weapons.<br /> <br /> Before we headed home Dearbhail made a point of thanking me and Tatiana for protecting the rest of them and saving Dacian. A nod seemed to suffice as a response. I will admit that I was a little confused by her reaction. I appreciate the sentiment and all, but she is pack, as are the rest of them. Of course we\u2019re going to protect them. We protect our own. And if I wasn\u2019t taking my own advice, and not pissing on anyone\u2019s shoes, I\u2019d be hunting down the spirits that hurt Dacian and utterly destroying them. I am still tempted to hunt them down, but am not sure if those particular spirits worked for Gunnar alone, or if they are loyal to all the Pure in Vienna. I have no wish to go toe to toe with Wolfgang just yet. From what I\u2019ve been told he would tear us to shreds before we made any significant impact on his health. Despite that, I know that if I asked her to Tatiana would join me on a hunt for those spirits, or even Wolfgang himself. I must be careful what I say.<br /> <br /> <br /> 28 June 1920<br /> <br /> Today has gone by rather fast. Wolfram, Dacian and Lizette as their driver showed up for the dual. Wolfgang was there waiting and informed our people that there was an attack on Gunnar last night and that he fears his acquaintance is dead. He excused Wolfram from the dual since he did not have anything personal against our German noble. Dacian offered his condolences for the loss of his friend. Wolfgang apparently did not seem overly upset by the possible death of Gunnar and did not really seem to reply to Dacian\u2019s words. Wolfgang turned to leave and our people did the same.<br /> <br /> The only thing interesting that really happened was Marlene brought in a telegram from Christina\u2019s brother. It just said that he would be coming home and would arrive in two days time. Most of us took the opportunity to sleep then. There wasn\u2019t much in the way of time for sleeping last night, and since we are planning on being up late tonight we took our rest where we could get it. Wolfram I believe stayed up to talk to Christina. I can understand that there might be some tension when her brother arrives home. There are several guests staying in their house that he does not know, one of which is the man currently courting his sister. I am unsure if Christina had an opportunity to tell her brother about the rest of us. It should be an interesting meeting if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Once we were all awake we went over what our plans concerning this Vampire Salon were. It seems that this Salon is open to the Invictus and Lancea Sanctum groups. Alla is a part of the Invictus group. The woman that wants to make a bond of blood with Alla is part of the Lancea Sanctun group. I will have to keep an eye out for her. It was also brought up that we should play nice with the one called Lisbette. It is likely that she is the one that has the necklace that we are looking for and we will want her in a receptive mood if we are to retrieve it from her tonight or at a later date. It was stated that we should do the same for all the Vampires present. We also agreed that Tatiana and I would be in Dalu form for the Salon. It would make a strong impression on those present without being overly confrontational or threatening. I am not opposed to making a show of force on behalf of our pack. Vampires seem to be a predatory group. They will understand it for what it is.<br /> <br /> After talk of the Salon some of us, Wolfram, Dacian, Lizette and myself, took a closer look at the items that we acquired from the Pure. This is what we found\u2026<br /> <br /> Notes on Items found in crates:<br /> <br /> Four unique items<br /> <br /> Cup of Life. Can hold essence within itself. Seems to be able to hold about three times its strength in essence. This will be useful to Tatiana and myself at the very least.<br /> <br /> Mirror. Will allow you to scry on someone if you cut yourself and drop blood on it. The downside is that it will summon a spirit to the location of your target, or your location. This spirit cannot be seen. I am not sure if the downside of this item will make it prohibitive to use or not. There is no telling if the spirit summoned will be friendly or not, and what kind of damage they may do while present. Are they specifically attracted to the caster or the target, or do they just show up in the vicinity and then go on their own way? Questions that need answering before we use this thing.<br /> <br /> Spirit Lure. When worn by an individual that person will seem like the perfect target/object/thing for any spirit that is nearby. If they desire fear or pain that person will seem the perfect person for their needs. This might be an interesting way to lure in a spirit if one happens to be our prey.<br /> <br /> Bowl. This will allow you to take any object you want into the Shadow. You just need to destroy the object (edible or otherwise) put it in the bowl and consume it. This for example would allow you to take a handgun into Shadow. I do not believe that this will be all that good to use. I\u2019m not sure if the consumption of such inedible objects would hurt you or if there is some magic that would protect you from the effects of actually consuming pieces of a gun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Calm yourself, volchonok.<br /> <br /> I mean it. You must calm yourself. What is...?<br /> <br /> Ah. Yes. Well, next time there is an emergency I will be sure to inform you ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is foolish, that is the point...<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not blaming you. It was perfectly reasonable to become bored with the strangeness of women and it was not as if I could share the ham bone with you, as I did with Marek.<br /> <br /> It was an emergency, as I said. Our magpie of a thief found the wrong shiny thing and alerted Gunnar\u2019s spirits.<br /> <br /> The shiny thing? A vampire killing sword. Useful, I suppose, except that its mere presence angers Alla.<br /> <br /> No, not like silver for us. It steals their energy and incites their inner Beast.<br /> <br /> Just because Gunnar is dead, it does not mean his spirits abandon their post. It was a pain spirit, as the thief described it, and two spirits which impaled him with rough knives of wood. They also put some kind of mark on him.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that is why we disappeared, to escape the mark.<br /> <br /> To the other place. The... hedge, I believe the fairies call it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, volchonok. It is full of green things and interesting smells. You would probably like it. But if we do take you along next time, you must stay close.<br /> <br /> Of course, you are the bravest volchonok I know. But it is a place designed to confound the senses, and only a fairy may leave easily.<br /> <br /> Oh do not think so, volchonok. Dacian has paid for his transgression. Only the blessing of Ochranny keeps it from showing on his face. He was barely alive when I found him.<br /> <br /> Of course our songbird healed him. She was quite put out when I ordered her to open a gate to the other place before she did so. Then again, she could not hear the call of the mark.<br /> <br /> Even fairy magics can do little for wounds as severe as that.<br /> <br /> What? No, Dacian is not sick. The stench is because he bled all over a Pure\u2019s territory. He does not want Wolfgang to be able to sniff him out, so he has used magic to hide his scent and masks its lack with unpleasantness.<br /> <br /> Yes, they go to the duel that will not be. I go to sleep.<br /> <br /> I am in this chair, volchonok, in case I am needed, again. A bed, especially the bed here, is too decadent, too difficult to wake from. I will sleep fine here and wake the easier for it.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means I will be awake this night, but not for running, volchonok. Tonight is the salon of the vampires.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, volchonok. Perhaps we will run after.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 28 July 1920 - Afternoon<br /> <br /> I am not ashamed of my failure, as I am mostly without such a frailty. Though I suppose disappointed is a better description. I have discovered weaknesses in myself that I will endeavor to correct. However this bit of inner reflection tells nothing of my actions.<br /> <br /> I ventured to Gunnar\u2019s estate and found it was as predictable as he. Heavily guarded and secure in its ability to keep the outside out. I prepared as I would for any other entry, taking care to conceal myself and exploit the natural powers of the Darkness. I did move very slowly while climbing the fence to avoid the guard\u2019s notice, but I scuttled up the wall without reserve. The locked window eased open to my skilled fingers.<br /> <br /> I quickly went about my mission: Make Gunnar look like a coward for fleeing his coming duel. In this, I succeeded without question. Even I would have believed he left in a hurry. Before I left, I used my Kenning to make sure there was nothing special I missed. Surely a magical item would be important enough to take if leaving in a rush. I found a most intriguing sword and scabbard which was most definitely magical. As I took the hilt into my hand, I was struck by a sense of wrongness. I turned to find a feminine figure reaching for me. It was at that point I realized what was wrong. A spirit of pain closed in upon me. The woman\u2019s face was drawn open at the mouth by jagged fish hooks and her corpus seemed to suggest she was sentenced to an Iron Maiden. Those brief moments of understanding were my undoing. The spirit\u2019s fingertips turned into talon-like fish hooks as I was suddenly wracked with pain and another sensation I could not comprehend at that moment. I\u2019m told it was only the blessing of Ochranny which allowed me to withstand such an assault. Moving more on instinct than strategy, I dove for the window and ran down the wall, holding the rope to keep my head above feet. The Iron Maiden above screamed as she threw herself from the window in pursuit. Two more spirits, which in my haze of pain seemed like animate tree people, leapt from the treeline and launched stakes of white ash into my chest. My vision dimmed as my feet hit the ground, but as I coughed lifeblood on my lips, I thought of Marek and Wolfram. I had already failed the Uratha by being spotted. However, if I were to die here, Wolfram would surely be disgraced. With what little of my dwindling strength remained, I stumbled forward. The Iron Maiden was not so impaired as she rushed for me. Desperate not to leave a corpse on the estate, I flung open a door into the Hedge and scrambled like a lame hare through the two columns. The spirit of pain pulled up short of the door and I realized she was waiting for her compatriots to come and finish what they began. I ran to distance myself from the portal and to find another closer to my friends. If I were to die, I wanted to at least leave a body for them. Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s conscience would not allow her to rest if she thought I had been Taken again. As the blood from my chest covered my slowing feet, I glimpsed a low door with Marek and Tatiana running toward me. They were both in Urhan form and were searching with their unconquerable smell. I crawled through the portal, which was actually a hole in a tree trunk before I collapsed. Tatiana became more human and made the bleeding stop before shifting to her Urshal form, lifting me in her jaws, and running. Unfortunately, the pain of such movement overcame me and I fell into blackness.<br /> <br /> When I awoke, I was surrounded by all but Lizette in a very different part of the Hedge than I left. I was no longer impaled, my chest was bandaged, and I could move with somewhat less pain than before. Dearbh\u00e1il was immediately over me and refreshing me with her Spring magics as soon as they noticed my awareness. We discussed our options after I recounted my failure. While no mortal authorities will have evidence of the truth, my blood spilled on the estate will guarantee the Pure will know Gunnar is not simply missing. Plus the spirits can report what they saw, which causes more problems for the cabal as a whole. Our plans were shattered. For a very small positive, Wolfram examined the sword while I was indisposed. It apparently is very effective at killing vampires. So much so that even the sight of the drawn weapon enrages the monster which drives them. I believe Alla referred to it as the Beast. Either way, she snarled at Wolfram when he attempted to unsheath the blade. We waited until Marek could no longer sense the spirit mark the Iron Maiden used to track me before I opened a new door out of the Hedge. It was less than an hour until we were due to arrive at the duel. Also that meant Alla had a similar amount of time before sunrise.<br /> <br /> We returned to the Esterh\u00e1zy estate to change and plan. I slipped past Christina and Marlena to investigate Gunter\u2019s room. There I found cologne which would help me mask any scent, but also mask no scent. Wolfram and Lizette had to suffer along with me during the ride to meet Archduke Eggenberg as I was not immune to the strong scent. The Archduke immediately wrinkled his nose as I opened the door to the car. We approached and were informed Gunnar was missing and believed to be dead. Eggenberg gave Wolfram the option to fight him if he must, but there was no reason to engage that particular werewolf. I apologized to him at the mention of the loss of a friend, but he seemed mostly indifferent. We returned home where I happily bathed and then found comfort in sleep.<br /> <br /> We rejoined Alla in her room to plan for the salon. Several weapons would be stored within Wolfram but we would not go armed to the this gathering. The Uratha would be in attendance and stay in Dalu form, both as a precaution and to send a clear message of power. For my part, I hope to only impress and observe as I am still in no condition to face any further confrontations. Marek, Wolfram, Lizette, and I then moved on to classifying the relics.<br /> <br /> There were several small artifacts which fell into a few categories, but the four pieces that struck me were the cup, the mirror, the lure, and the bowl. We have not yet learned the name of more than the Cup of Life and the Spirit Lure, but the uses of those four are most interesting.<br /> <br /> The Cup of Life can hold the essence of power used by Uratha. I have no idea how to measure this essence, but by Marek\u2019s reaction, I would suspect it is great.<br /> <br /> The mirror allows its user to scry upon another by feeding it a small quantity of blood. My understanding was that the blood must come from the user, though I have not had time to investigate that further. Additionally, use of the mirror summons an unseen spirit either to the target\u2019s location or the user\u2019s. We are unsure how much, if any, hindrance this spirit could be.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Lure is a small charm worn to make any spirit nearby find the wearer the perfect target for their needs, no matter what that may be. I can think of three spirits this could be useful for, but that is not relevant to the object.<br /> <br /> The bowl will allow the user to bring items into the Shadow. I was unaware this was an issue, but Marek seemed vexed by this proposition. To use the bowl, the user must destroy the object, place it in the bowl, and consume the remains. Given Lizette\u2019s talent with creation, I can imagine a large number of wooden constructs going into the bowl. It is not so hard to consume ashes when sprinkled over food.<br /> <br /> Now I think I will go and bathe again. I can still smell the cologne.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 28 June 1920<br /> <br /> With great alacrity, things became more complicated.<br /> <br /> After our return from the battle, I, unlike Wolfram, decided to wear my valor a bit more on my sleeve and not change before arrival. As such Christina and Marlene were all over me to see if I was okay when I arrived.<br /> <br /> Christina, unexpectedly, saw Marlene\u2019s fondness and worry\u2026and recognized it for what it was. Now Christina had told me before that she was hoping to marry Wolfram and that nothing between us should make him unhappy. She did so while flattering me more than my practical mind required\u2026though I enjoyed it anyway. I had thus ceased my wooing of the girl\u2026after all she was looking for something more serious than I was, and I had assignations with Marlene, who was looking for something as serious as I was\u2026namely, safe and fun sex with no pregnancy or even virginity loss (on her part, a bit late for me).<br /> <br /> So imagine my surprise when I see Christina\u2019s eyes darken with rage. She whirled around and gave Marlene a glare that terrified the poor girl, leaving her retreating rapidly from the room. Had I been more prepared I probably could have replenished my glamour store on the fear she caused but, sadly, I was too shocked. She caught herself after, and intended to go after her after fetching Tatiana some meat. Dearbh\u00e1il pursued her, and then brought Tatiana the food herself. I believe Dearbh\u00e1il had a conversation with her, and I am embarrassed and intrigued to consider what the two of them could have been discussing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Alla quizzed me on which was \u201cbetter.\u201d I said nothing, of course. A lady\u2019s dignity must be protected, after all. Besides, I have kissed both but nothing more with Christina.<br /> <br /> Still, Christina had, politely, carefully, and kindly let me down that she had chosen Wolfram, so it was a great surprise to see jealousy flare up so intensely, but the light of the jealousy scorched the room.<br /> <br /> I needed time to think after. While I was in my room Christina came to speak. She assured me that I was not to worry, she meant what she said about Wolfram and she had simply had a \u201cmoment of weakness.\u201d She assured me I was still her \u201cFaerie Princess\u201d and that she cared but that this would not continue.<br /> <br /> It was rude of me, in retrospect, to kiss her at that point, but her eyes told me to do it, and she gave no resistance, and kissed me in return. However, after our third, she quickly excused herself. I heard voices; she had found the others it seemed.<br /> <br /> Also, I may have unconsciously loosened some of her clothing. Maybe that was part of why she withdrew.<br /> <br /> Dacian had gotten injured, and the Werewolves had tracked him down. His mission to make Gunnar seem like had fled had failed, and the Ivory Claws were onto him. He had escaped, however, with help from the Werewolves and Dearbh\u00e1il, as they had to hide in the Hedge awhile. He managed to make the duel along with us, and as we had hoped Archduke von Eggenberg dropped the duel, though it was less \u201cGunnar\u2019s shameful disappearance\u201d and more \u201cGunner was kidnapped and was probably dead.\u201d If he suspected Wolfram, he did not show it.<br /> <br /> With them safe and my head swimming from kissing Christina, I went and slept.<br /> <br /> When I woke, we met in a windowless room so Alla could attend to discuss the Salon. I sort of posed for Christina and Marlene\u2019s arrival and got the desired result when they saw me. I also saw things were smooth between Christina and Wolfram, which was good; I revel somewhat in her attention but do not seek to interfere with Wolfram\u2019s love life. They joined us, and Marlene kept me plied with Cognac.<br /> <br /> In the end, we will all attend, well all the Motley, and leave things to Alla. I am fine with that. I am however nervous about arriving unarmed, so I stored a flamethrower inside Wolfram. He is right handy that way. I hope it will not be needed, but then it is wise to be prepared.<br /> <br /> I was thinking for situations like close quarters firefights or vampire salons a flamethrower with three different barrels to spray fire in sort of three streams might be effective. It makes it harder for the undead to flank you without being set alight. It might be nice to focus all three into one direction heavily, but why would one really want low power beams ever? Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I lack time to prepare and build a three pronged flamethrower not because of lack of genius (there is no lack of genius) but because before roasting the undead with it requires field tests, and fast as I am blueprinting, gathering materials, building, testing, and prepping a device for scorching a room full of vampires and stinky cheeses is more than I have time for. Sadly.<br /> <br /> I mean I assume there will be stinky cheeses or this salon will be a waste of my time. Who has salons without stinky cheeses? Vampires, I guess, with their blood drinking and making people vampires. I don\u2019t want them to make me a vampire. I am flammable enough as is; I can\u2019t afford to be more flammable. Well, usually. Probably.<br /> <br /> I need more smooches.<br /> <br /> Okay, well, I\u2019ve rambled enough. Now is the time for action! Roast, er, talk to some vampires, get the jewelry, replace the jewelry with a fake, and get back to Paris. I miss her already.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XV</i><br /> <br /> Neither Dacian\u2019s discovery nor the confrontation over Lizette were actually planned. I made an Empathy roll for Christina when Lizette came in showing signs of injury to have her notice Marlene. As for Dacian, he got a bit bold after his success carrying his mission out and explored the house, where he was set upon by the Spirit. Werewolves having Spirits. Crazy.<br /> <br /> Honestly I think most of expected Dacian to die off and not be part of the end of the story, but he managed to survive, barely. I was rather glad of the Golden Eagle conceit at that point.<br /> <br /> Dacian covered his scent (again) with Smoke, but as his scentlessness would have been noticeable used cologne to cover and Darkness to make the overpoweringness of the distraction moreso.<br /> <br /> I think the players will be really glad to go up against something besides Werewolves. Their senses were giving the PCs fits, and the Spirits part they were unprepared for. Of course, all this was deliberate. I want them to fear Werewolves sense and minions as well as their claws. I suspect I have nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> Well, that covers that. We are on the d\u00e9nouement as the PCs go to the Salon, either for a quick wrap to the story or a whole new leg. I am sure you are as curious as I am. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the