"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:43:09-08:00","id":758778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=758314#post758314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is true. Lizette is adorable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mayhem!<span style=\"font-size:8px\"> Mayhem!</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:01:34-08:00","id":759588,"title":"","content":"Some of the feedback I get on the forums are from PMs or discussions outside the forum threads where the games are discussed. A number of them can be applied pretty broadly to my games, so I paraphrased some and put some info down here to \u201cdraw back the curtain\u201d as it were as I thought some would be of interest to some readers. Add your own if you wish, as always.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of female characters in your games. Like, most of them. Is this on purpose?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. Some of it is deliberate. Media is all about men, and many TV shows, movies, books and, honestly, role-playing campaigns have few females that are often lovers, prizes, victims or relatives. I try to make women who fit every conceivable role, but have many male characters too.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I just come up with female characters more easily, and since I cull pictures from the internet which provide inspiration for PCs, the fact that I have way more female pictures means I get inspired for female characters more often. That is not deliberate, just the way it turns out.<br /> <br /> <b>How about LGBTQ characters? Same?</b><br /> <br /> Most NPCs are actually Herosexual. With a few exceptions such as Maximillian Nostras or Gunnar Hohemberg, most NPCs orientation is such that they would be interested in PCs interested in them. Those with exceptions are NPCs whose concept defines their sexuality, and they are rare. Then sometimes as I see them in action NPCs seem to make good couples or drift together. I have no bias to create gay or straight couples this way. It just happens. However, see above that women outnumber men. I am proud, however, of the queer representation in my games.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because an NPC could fall for a PC of either sex does not mean they are equally easy to woo. Christina Esterh\u00e1zy could go either way but is easier for men, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>No gay male relationships with PCs, but there are several lesbians\u2026</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t tell my players what orientation to make their PCs. If a male character wants to have a relationship with a male NPC that\u2019s fine (it even happened in my <i>Masquerade</i> game) but it is what the players want.<br /> <br /> <b>You have less Trans characters than I expected.</b><br /> <br /> Yea, not so impressive regarding those numbers. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is my only current game with no Trans characters so far.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of, um, sex in your game. Is everyone okay with it?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. I will speak plainly. Sex for me is way more interesting than violence. I\u2019d be more interested in seeing a PC having a torrid affair than a gunfight. This does not mean my games are without action; <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has a setting conceit allowing for more danger and daring-do since the conceit prevents a PC revolving door. There is more action there than other games. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has more action than <i>Balance of Shadows</i> or <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, because it is spy-noir, while <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is part noir, part mystery, part pulp. But yes, relationships are a huge thing.<br /> <br /> My players know this, and new players are told before they join. No player has to play romantic relationships, straight or queer.<br /> <br /> For the record, we almost always fade to black unless there is a good reason not to, and sex is only rolled if something besides having a good time is going on, such as getting a foe vulnerable, staying awake so the PC can rummage through their partners stuff, staying awake so their partner can\u2019t rummage through theirs, impressing a countess, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>So everyone has pictures, can I see a picture of [NPC]?</b><br /> <br /> Probably. If it is a picture culled from the internet and you want to see an NPC, I will show it unless I am using the picture with particular permission of the photographer or model, in which case no because they have not given me permission for that.<br /> <br /> <b>How many of your players are women/lesbian/bisexual/giraffes/etc</b><br /> <br /> I am not going to give out too much information on my players. I will say every game linked in my sig has a mix of male and female and straight and LGBTQ players. Most games hover somewhere close to 50/50 male female, or one more of one or the other. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is the exception, with many more women than men. . I will tell you, if you have read about a female PC having relationships with female NPCs in these games and assumed they are being played by a guy you will be wrong much more often than not.<br /> <br /> <b>Do Players plan their PCs relationships before the game starts?</b><br /> <br /> Not usually. Sometimes they have an idea getting together is likely. In discussing concepts we guessed there would eventually be romantic tension between Wolfram and Lizette, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>What genre would you call your games</b><br /> <br /> Mystery/Supernatural Drama. <i>Balance of Shadows</i> has ghost story elements. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has noir and spy elements, and <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has noir, pulp, and mystery. <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is more pure mystery-drama.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I play in your game?</b><br /> <br /> Probably not. If you live in North Carolina we can discuss it, but even then probably not. My games are almost all full.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time where our heroes recover the necklace and a certain vampire gets several PCs wrapped around her finger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-06-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T15:22:51-08:00","id":765182,"title":"","content":"This chapter is winding up. Lets explore the penultimate session of 1920 Vienna for our group.<br /> <i><br /> Session XVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 28 June 1920<br /> <br /> The Salon was interesting, I\u2019ll give it that. We arrived \u201cfashionably late\u201d as Alla wanted. Our entrance was quite a bit more extravagant that anything I have ever or will ever want to do, but I had agreed that it would be good to make a strong impression on the local Vampires. Wolfram drove the car, a Silver Ghost, through the front doors, literally. Dacian and Fenric had opened the doors and Wolfram pulled the car through into the foyer. Tatiana and I hopped out of the car, again flashier than I would usually prefer, and Dacian helped Alla out of the car. The others paired up and we all entered the Salon. Before we split up though Lizette let us all know that a yellow-eyed woman that was socializing with Lizbet\u2019s people was the woman that stole the necklace in the first place.<br /> <br /> I think Maximillian was amused by the entrance but perhaps not overly pleased by it. He did allow the eccentricity though and smiled throughout. He even introduced Alla as his good and kind friend. I believe he was referring to the favor that we did for him the other night. I\u2019m not sure if the events of that night are public knowledge or not. He did in his own way acknowledge the service that Alla performed for him in his introduction though.<br /> <br /> What we was able to find out about some of the guests is this. The yellow-eyed woman is associated with Lizbet\u2019s group. Her name is Constancia. Lisbette is in turn connected to but not directly a part of the Circle of the Crone. From the quick explanation I got it sounds like they are a small but noteworthy pagan group. Theodora is a part of this Circle. Apparently she is also part of a Bloodline, which sounds like a family lineage of sorts that is descended from Medusa. So all the members of this line are known for having live snakes or snake imagery on them at all times. Theodora was no exception. She had live snakes moving underneath her clothes. I saw the movement under her sleeves. I will say that it was interesting and a little disconcerting. <br /> <br /> After Alla had learned what she could from Maximillian he introduced her to Lizbet. Tatiana had stayed with Alla as a guard of sorts. I followed but at more of a distance, and Dacian was on Alla\u2019s arm. Alla introduced the rest of us to Lizbet and then they started making small talk. Eventually they came around to the subject of occult objects. Our pack-mate is certainly a social butterfly but sometimes she is about as blunt as a brick wall. Tonight was such a night. She just flat out asked Lizbet if she knew about the Eye of Iblis. Theodora, who was with Lizbet, knew what it looked like and if I\u2019m not mistaken it looked like Lizbet became noticeably nervous. I\u2019m not sure if the others picked up on that or not, but it seemed obvious to me. At the same time the Eye of Iblis was brought up, Constancia (the yellow-eyed woman) turned her attention to our group. <br /> <br /> Theodora suggested that if the Eye was recovered then the Lancea Sanctum might try and acquire it for themselves. I believe that they would want to study or possibly destroy it. It was suggested that Alla meet up with Theodora and Lizbet later this evening at 4:00am at Lizbet\u2019s house. Alla asked if she could bring the rest of us and the other woman\u2019s reply was only if she could bring her friends as well. I was not keen on meeting at someone else\u2019s territory. Alla it seems felt the same way and asked if it would be possible to meet on neutral ground. Lizbet said no. She would brook no argument and left after it seemed there was no more to say.<br /> <br /> Once Lizbet and Theodora had left Constancia made her way over to Alla and the others and introduced herself as the Princess of Evil. She offered to help us track down the Eye of Iblis for a favor to be paid back at a later time in Paris. It seems that Constancia also has property in Paris and would prefer to have us owe her later and collect there since it is a mutual location for both of us. Alla agreed to this, and they agreed to talk about a meeting later. Dacian then asked Constancia to dance. I was not really surprised that he did that. He is rather good at appealing to others good graces and tonight was no exception. I believe that Tatiana was a little annoyed by his actions though. If given the chance I believe she would have asked the golden-eyed woman to dance.<br /> <br /> After the dance was done Constancia went back to talk to Theodora. They began arguing in Greek. Constancia seemed to show her teeth an awful lot during the conversation. The whole display brought home the predatory nature of the Vampires. They put on a nice veneer of polite society but underneath it all they are animals like us. They can\u2019t escape it, though they try. We embrace the predator within. We let it free to run and play and hunt. I do not think that the Vampires do that. Not to the same extent anyway. They do feed, they just don\u2019t kill. I suppose I can understand the reason behind their discretions though. Unchecked their kind would cause problems for the human population.<br /> <br /> A short while later Constancia came back and told Alla that everything had been taken care of and that she would meet us later to give us the necklace. We agree that neutral ground is preferred and came up with the idea of meeting at one of Dearbhail\u2019s performances. We set the performance at the same Theater as before and arranged a time. After Constancia left we discussed living arrangements. We agreed that we should move back to the hotel since Christina\u2019s brother is coming back and it would look odd for his sister to be hosting so many people without a chaperone. Ridiculous if you ask me, but that is what I believe is expected. Alla will move her stuff back later this evening and the rest of us will move in the morning.<br /> <br /> We also discussed what we were going to do about the necklace once we got it back. Dacian\u2019s idea was that we should sell it back to Theodora. That way Christina\u2019s family would gain some income and the necklace would go to someone that understands what it can do and how to take care of it. I myself am not so certain that selling it back to Theodora would be such a good idea. Theodora had it in the first place before Constancia somehow stole it. I think Theodora will want to retrieve the necklace, but not part with any money for it. I rankled me earlier when Constancia offered to get the necklace in exchange for a favor when she is the one that stole it in the first place. Now Dacian wants to do the same thing to Theodora. In essence we\u2019d be selling her back her own necklace. At least I\u2019m pretty sure that she sees it as hers. <br /> <br /> I will admit to being curious how Constancia got the necklace back. She did not leave the Salon, and yet with no communication with anyone that I could see, she acquired the necklace from wherever Theodora had it stashed. That would be a useful skill to learn. Despite my curiosity however I do not plan on asking Constancia how she did it. I have a feeling that she would not answer with a straightforward answer anyway.<br /> <br /> While we were discussing said necklace a note arrived from Maximillian warning us that if we had the necklace then we should conceal it immediately. This caused us some concern and Tatiana immediately used a gift to see if there was any sort of magic being used upon the grounds. There was. Tatiana and I immediately changed into wolf form and patrolled the grounds until we came across our quarry. There were a number of snakes moving around on the edge of the property. As this is unusual behavior for such animals we proceeded to chase them off and scatter them. We did not attack them since that might call for retaliation. It was obvious who sent the snakes and as much as I like a good fight, it was unnecessary to start one with Theodora at this point in time. <br /> <br /> After the excitement was over Alla went back to the hotel so she could avoid trying to make it there during the daytime tomorrow. Most everyone else went to sleep. Wolfram and Lizette stayed awake and talked. I believe they were keeping an eye on things just in case anything else came up. I thought that their caution was a good idea and kept watch myself. I turned to my wolf form and patrolled the grounds outside. Dedecek stood watch with me. There is only so much that a spirit could do if there was trouble, but I\u2019m sure that wry old man would find a way. Come to think of it, I\u2019ve never seen him materialize. I wonder if he can. Maybe I\u2019ll ask him at some point.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 29 June 1920<br /> <br /> Today Tatiana and I met up with Krieger. We felt it only fair that since we hunted on his territory that we should let him know how we fared and to share with him a portion of the spoils. We gave him a couple of the smaller unknown items that were in the crate. We kept the ones that I had written about earlier. It was after all our prize. We are sharing it since it was taken on his land. We probably could have gotten away with not presenting any gifts, and initially Tatiana was of this opinion. I explained to her why it was appropriate to bestow some of the takings on our host and she eventually agreed that it was only right. Krieger was in turn generous to us and let us refill our essence at the locus that is within his place. It was a much welcome surprise, and one that we both took advantage of.<br /> <br /> This evening we met at the theater for Dearbhail\u2019s concert and for the rendezvous with Constancia. We were not the only ones that came to the performance. Apparently Maximillian was also in the mood for music as he also came to the theater.<br /> <br /> The whole lot of us came to the theater, but only a smaller handful including Alla, Dacian and Tatiana actually met with Constancia. The yellow eyed woman came as promised and sat down to make small talk for a bit before settling into our business. As the ladies were talking Wolfram said that he noticed another woman that looked just like Constancia standing nearer the wall and watching wherever the yellow eyed woman\u2019s back was turned. They could have been twins, but the second woman did not have the same unique eye color. She also read as \u201cdead\u201d to Wolfram\u2019s power though, so she could be a vampire or something else. She wasn\u2019t quite right to be a ghost.<br /> <br /> So, after the pleasantries were over Constancia pulled a velvet bag out and handed it over to Alla. Our socialite looked inside and smiled. Constancia seemed happy with the transaction as a whole, and said that it was good to have fate on our side. She admitted that she was happy to be able to return the necklace to us after having been the one to steal it in the first place. I will admit that it was convenient to have the woman that stole the necklace be the one to return it to us, but I\u2019m not so sure it was fate. I acknowledge that I have seen and experienced several strange things in my life, and I\u2019m not all that old. In a relatively short time I have discovered that there are ghosts and spirits walking the world in a kind of twilight. There are vampires and werewolves roaming the land, and I can count myself as one of the later. There are Fae men and woman wandering everywhere and I can count three of their number my friends and pack. So, everything considered, I suppose I shouldn\u2019t dismiss her comment out of hand. It could have some truth to it. I guess time will tell. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, you did very well.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the red banded snake fled from you with great speed. You are an excellent hunter.<br /> <br /> We harried the snakes because they were sent by the vampire Theodora. They were part of some magic that searched Christina\u2019s house for the necklace.<br /> <br /> She is the one who stole the necklace. Well, she had it stolen.<br /> <br /> By Constancia, another vampire, the yellow eyed woman that Lizette saw in her vision. Lizette did not do her beauty justice when she described her.<br /> <br /> No, I did not, impertinent volchonok. Dacian danced with her though. And I will see her again, it is for certain.<br /> <br /> She will be in Paris. We owe her a boon, as she has stolen the necklace back for us.<br /> <br /> Bah. I will be enamored of who I please. You listen too much to the songbird\u2019s fears of vampires. This Constancia, she is a smug creature of grace and confidence. She is almost Russian even - her name is Greek, and that is what she speaks with her mentor Theodora, but she has lived in St. Petersburg, and regrets the fall of our homeland as I do.<br /> <br /> Yes, Elena will be in Paris as well. That is not your concern.<br /> <br /> Volchonok...<br /> <br /> You are wise to change the subject. Yes, we do have the necklace now. Constancia - do not look at me like that volchonok - brought it to us at Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concert after having stolen it, apparently, while she was still at the salon. If that is true, and it seems so, it is quite a feat. But it was, according to Constancia, her purpose in the city, to steal it from Christina and then give it back by way of us. Theodora is very unhappy with her.<br /> <br /> We have not decided. Dacian thinks to sell it back to Theodora, since Christina\u2019s brother\u2019s intent was to sell it and she, at least, will not accidentally fall under its curse. Dearbh\u00e1il wishes to destroy it, I believe, but is concerned with the state of Wolfram\u2019s suit, should these noble matters go poorly.<br /> <br /> For once, volchonok, I agree with you. Boring human things.<br /> <br /> I do not know if there will be more werewolf things. Once the necklace is dealt with, we will return home, and werewolves have nothing to do with this necklace, it seems. Since we have informed Krieger of what has happened, as well as shared in our kill with him, we have no further business with him, for now, either.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we will go to Berlin. We are good at putting the Pure in their place, no? And since the military is much more reasonable, and better off, than the nobility, the Uratha there have even more need for us.<br /> <br /> Not right now, foolish volchonok. We finish this first, then we move Elena to Paris, then perhaps Berlin, or perhaps not.<br /> <br /> I have told you... no, we did not move dens because we are leaving now. We wait for the brother and to ensure the necklace is disposed of properly, however we decide properly is. We moved dens because of foolish human things. Christina and Wolfram are not lawfully mates yet, so they may not den together.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that is backwards.<br /> <br /> It does make much more sense to run swiftly in the cool night air. That is a thing we will do soon. Not tonight, but soon.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 28 July 1920 - Evening<br /> <br /> The potential for Maximilian\u2019s Salon inspired Alla like few other things since we have known the vampire. She concocted what amounts to a circus entrance to the party tonight. I have no idea how the vampires will react but I doubt in any other formal court we would receive another invitation.<br /> <br /> The Uratha will be going in Dulo form and acting as bodyguards. Marek agreed that making at least a moderate show of power would be good for our standing among the vampires of Vienna. The Changelings will be escorts. Wolfram will be a chauffeur. Having spent time as a servant, I was originally most unamused by this plan. But it became clear by the end, Alla must surely be mocking the standing conventions of etiquette.<br /> <br /> My understanding of \u201cThe Plan\u201d is as follows:<br /> Wolfram will drive a Silver Ghost with all of us aboard (I have no idea where Alla acquired this vehicle)<br /> Fenric will open the main doors to the event and announce his mistress\u2019 arrival<br /> Dearbh\u00e1il will sing melodiously as Wolfram drives into the Foyer<br /> Marek and Tatiana will acrobatically leave the vehicle<br /> I will escort Alla, along with the werewolves<br /> Fenric will escort Dearbh\u00e1il<br /> Wolfram will escort Lizette<br /> <br /> If somersaulting werewolves and minstrelling faeries aren\u2019t going to make a memorable entrance, I have obviously been missing the wrong vampiric parties.<br /> <br /> 29 July 1920 - Early<br /> <br /> We drove through the front doors fashionably late so all the esteemed guests would be sure to bear witness to our arrival. And what an arrival it was. It lacked only a calliope and fireworks from being a carnival show. In spite of this, Maximilian greeted Alla and associates warmly, even referring to her as his good and kind friend on several occasions. Lizette, ever watchful, noted before we dispersed that the yellow-eyed woman which stole the Eye of Iblis was talking to Lizbet. That put up our guard. But after, or perhaps because of, our rather elaborate entrance, I was in the mood to flaunt tradition. Not at the expense of our host however as he was most gracious indeed.<br /> <br /> Maximilian introduced Alla to Lizbet, who was somehow associated with the Circle of the Crone, which began a most spiralling conversation. Alla, never quite following social convention, asked Lizbet directly if she knew of the Eye of Iblis. Theodora, a companion which had remained silent until then, gave a convincingly vague description of the necklace. Lizbet looked somewhat nervous at that point, though the yellow-eyed woman did turn to look in our direction at the mention of the cursed relic. Theodora, now obviously in control of the conversation (perhaps for the best), wistfully noted that the Lancea et Sanctum would be very interested in such a relic, though I could not tell if she meant for study or destruction. It was obvious that she was hiding something though it became more sinister when Theodora suggested that Alla meet around 4:00 this morning at Lizbet\u2019s home. That she come alone was only inferred until Theodora refused Alla\u2019s gentle request for a neutral meeting area.<br /> <br /> After Lizbet was led away by Theodora, the yellow-eyed woman approached us with a feral smile. She introduced herself as Constancia, the Princess of Evil. It sounded like a Gentry title, but Alla plowed along, asking how she received such a station. Once we moved beyond such \u201cpleasantries,\u201d Constancia noted that she could assist us in retrieving the Eye of Iblis for a favor. It seems, coincidentally of course, that the Princess keeps a haven in Paris and would collect her boon back home. Alla agreed and a meeting on neutral ground was set for a future time, yet to be determined. Before anything else could transpire, I decided I had remained confined by mores and expectations long enough. With a smile of my own, I asked if Constancia would care to make the rest of the assemblage envious? Her fangs made the crooked grin all the more striking as she took my hand and I led her to the center of the salon. We indeed danced as a pair longer than would be acceptable in most places before she split away and returned to Theodora.<br /> <br /> A rather toothy and energetic, if quiet, argument took place in what I believe to be Greek. Lizbet walked though I don\u2019t know precisely what else happened as I noticed then as I turned that Tatiana seemed unpleased with me. As that is not pleasant for a multitude of reasons, I tried to make less of a showing after that. I was unsure if my extravagant behavior upset the Uratha or something more subtle, but I had little reason to find out.<br /> <br /> Constancia raised her voice slightly, now in German once again, noting something to the effect that, \u201cit was done.\u201d With that, she walked away. All the vampires with the Circle of the Crone seemed angry, though Theodora stormed off in a different direction, dragging Lizbet. With that, I noted to the others that perhaps we should take our leave as well. I graciously thanked Maximilian for his unrivaled hospitality then assisted Wolfram in backing the Silver Ghost from the Foyer. Constancia met us out front, noting that everything was taken care of. We arranged for Dearbh\u00e1il to have another performance so the exchange could take place in the neutral opera house. Then we loaded up the Ghost and started back for the Esterh\u00e1zy estate.<br /> <br /> I refused to allow the conversation of what we would do with the necklace until we arrived at Christina\u2019s. I did not wish to take the chance that we could be overheard by vampiric spies. Once we were safely away from such concerns, I eagerly pointed out that we could now get the necklace back then arrange to sell it to Theodora, as there was obviously a desire there. The others raised a legitimate concern that the vampire may just kill Gunter and take the necklace, but surely we could somehow intervene. Before I could continue my argument, a message arrived for Alla from Maximilian. It stated that if we indeed held the necklace, we should conceal it immediately. Tatiana took that as a clear and present threat so used some form of Uratha ritual to detect magic within the territory. Startlingly, she found it instantly. The werewolves changed to their Urhan forms and rushed outside. They returned after roughly fifteen minutes, having scared aware a strange nest of snakes before the discovered effect ended.<br /> <br /> Alla, not a friend of dawn, gathered her things so she and Fenric could return to the hotel tonight. With Gunter\u2019s return imminent, the rest of us will do likewise in the morning. Given the possible danger to Christina and Marlene however, Wolfram, Lizette, and Marek decided to stand watch. I retrieved the vampire killing sword, for which I almost gave my life, and found an unoccupied chaise. If another scan should come, I intended for the caster to realize their mistake. Now I shall enjoy the comfort of this pillow.<br /> <br /> <br /> 29 July 1920 - Night<br /> <br /> We spent most of the morning removing our belongings and returning the Esterh\u00e1zy estate to form. Then we returned to the hotel and prepared for this evening.<br /> <br /> I managed to make no real impression at all on the good people in the cafe I selected in an attempt to harvest Glamour. This dampened my spirits somewhat. But I contented myself with the knowledge I would see Constancia again.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concert was another great success given the packed house. Her voice was truly a thing of beauty. There were no otherworldly interruptions, though Maximilian and Constancia arrived separately. No issues occurred so Tatiana and I accompanied Alla with little expectation of violence. Constancia was very happy to make the trade. Though something she said struck me deeply. During the exchange, she noted that it was good to work with Fate and that she knew the necklace \u201cwas supposed to come back to us.\u201d<br /> <br /> I have doubts as to the coincidences involved in our \u201cgood luck\u201d in retrieving the Golden Eagle and now the cursed Eye of Iblis. I hesitate to suggest that cursed items are drawn to us, as we have not experienced tragedy regarding the Eagle. However luck is certainly not lending itself to our actions.<br /> <br /> What could be manipulating events which have so thoroughly entwined us? I shall not dwell on this thought alone. I fear that delusions of Keepers, which are possibly more frightening than Keepers that are truly there, will drive me to madness. I am of no use to my cabal if I cannot force myself from the safety found beneath my bed. I sleep now. Atop my pillow.<br /> <br /> Any Keepers here must face Tatiana this night ...and that gives me a sense of peace.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 28 June 1920<br /> <br /> I am not, it seems, a socialite. Scientist, yes. Soldier, sometimes. Craftswoman, without compare. Partisan, when necessary. Lover, when possible. But socialite, not so much.<br /> <br /> Alla arrived in the back of a Silver Ghost, driven by Wolfram, with the Werewolves flanking her in near human form, and Dearbh\u00e1il singing as I rode with her and Wolfram in the front. Fenric announced us. Dacian also got a door, and waited inside to take Alla\u2019s hand. Wolfram took mine. We left the car on the floor.<br /> <br /> It seemed terribly rude to drive a car into Maximillian\u2019s house. Well, I guess it was his house. Someone\u2019s house. A car should not be in someone\u2019s house. Usually. Of course a car in a house could be useful, actually. A small, one-person vehicle, agile, able to take corners quickly, sort of like a plane but on the ground. What might be ideal is a gun mounted on the middle that spins, and the car moves in the direction of the gun, and operator facing, letting it turn quickly so it can weave room to room in an agile fashion. Possibly releasing fire on the ground behind it. Well, that would not work if it changed direction. Perhaps it needs a flamethrower. But on which side? Perhaps every side! Multi-directional flamethrower. And saw blades of course for clearing hallways and people hiding in bedrooms. Of course. Yes that might be useful.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve lost the plot. Something about the party. Ah yes, Lizette the socialite that is not.<br /> <br /> In truth, I spent most of the Salon watching the Vampires glide across the room. It felt, to me, not unlike swimming in an ocean with sharks, hoping none notice, hoping they do not want to make a meal of me. Feeling a twinge of nervousness when one looks toward me. For a woman who fears nothing, I felt like quite the coward.<br /> <br /> Apart from Constancia Lampros, none showed anything obviously Vampiric. The woman called Theodora, who people kept calling a \u201cGorgon\u201d (I question that she was either ugly or a mythological creature) had pet snakes under her clothes, but nothing more. It almost was like a human party with slightly-too-perfect people. Also a bit pale. Not that I can cast stones for people who see my Mask.<br /> <br /> In the end, Alla had to choose between the intense and powerful Theodora and the seductive and charming Constancia. It did not prove a difficult decision. Alla made her pact with Constancia.<br /> <br /> Dacian then proceeded to dance with Constancia. Perhaps he does not realize vampires are dangerous and could make him one of their number? I think they are terrifying myself. All a Werewolf can do is kill me. Can the Eagle prevent my transformation into one of the living dead? Actually, that is a good question. I mean, it does bring one back. I don\u2019t want to be bitten by a vampire to find out though. I like the sun too much. I mean, I don\u2019t really like the sun, but without it the earth gets cold. And while that is a nice idea in the heat of late June, not having the sun would actually be terrible.<br /> <br /> Okay, I got off track. What I mean is not having the sun would be bad. No, wait.<br /> <br /> What I mean is turning into a vampire is bad because then I would have trouble with my flamethrowers. Yes, that is it. I think.<br /> <br /> Was I talking about flamethrowers\u2026no\u2026okay\u2026ah, Dacian danced\u2026right. Okay. Back on track.<br /> <br /> We came back to the house, and Christina was there (of course) and eager to get her necklace (of course). She was disappointed we did not have it but hid it well\u2026the need began to affect her, though, and Marlene took her to bed.<br /> <br /> Maximillian sent word if we had the necklace to conceal it, but we did not. Apparently Theodora was searching. Marek and Tatiana found some snakes apparently tied the ritual in the lawn and chased them off.<br /> <br /> Alla returned to the hotel with Fenric, and Wolfram and I decided to guard just in case Theodora tried something direct. We had a long talk about Christina. Wolfram does not wish to interfere in anything between Christina and I, so long as I don\u2019t do anything to interfere with his marriage plans. I reiterated I did not wish to. The idea of tempting the bride to be of so noble a man as Wolfram bothers me, and while I can be bohemian at times his laissiez-faire attitude toward the whole thing seemed strange. Perhaps it is a Protestant thing. I told him we would see, and to bring things on a better track, I helped Wolfram a bit in learning his prayers. It will be important when he converts after all.<br /> <br /> Wolfram is handsome, charming, open-minded, intelligent, daring, heroic. I really wish he was not German. But then, as he plans to marry a different lady, perhaps it is best he is.<br /> <br /> <br /> 29 June 1920<br /> <br /> As of tomorrow, I will have known the others two full months. How odd it is that we have already come to rely upon each other so much.<br /> <br /> Today was mostly preparing. We moved back to the hotel in preparation for Gunter\u2019s arrival. No doubt the Ivory Claws are in too much disarray to do much now. We will be on guard, however. Tatiana and Marek met with their contact, and all seems well.<br /> <br /> I got a note from Christina, requesting I speak to her tonight in her room. She intends to \u201cclear the air\u201d regarding anything between us. In her bedroom. In secret. At night. If I am lucky, she will only try to sweet talk me into giving her the necklace. I am seriously considering not going.<br /> <br /> The handoff was almost anticlimactic. Dearbh\u00e1il had a concert, and we were on time. Maximillian was there, curiously. Or perhaps he just liked Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s voice. Constancia Lampros arrived, handed Alla the necklace wrapped in velvet, and slipped out. She made enigmatic comments about fate putting it in our hands, which is the second time that has happened. I am suspicious of this. Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s singing was heavenly, but worries about Constantia\u2019s parting words weighed on me, but less than one other question:<br /> <br /> Do I go see Christina?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVI</i><br /> <br /> Pssssh do you actually doubt you are going to go Lizette? C\u2019mon now\u2026<br /> <br /> There is fate again. \u201cIt\u2019s good to have fate on your side\u201d Constancia commented, noting it was difficult when it was the other way around. <br /> <br /> The consensus is Constancia is a Hollow Mekhet, given the duplicate, but they do not know for sure.<br /> <br /> I am low on time. Next session will complete the 1920 Vienna leg of Golden Eagle, and we move ahead to 1922 Paris. The Roaring 20s are in full swing now; grab your dancing shoes and some wine\u2026no prohibition on that side of the pond. See you in two weeks, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T19:34:14-08:00","id":765295,"title":"","content":"The gears turn and perhaps a metallic screech can be heard echoing in the distance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T22:42:11-08:00","id":765361,"title":"","content":"Something like that. Probably Lizette's fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:48:06-08:00","id":776749,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the d\u00e9nouement of 1920 Vienna. Gunter arrives to meet the group, having set events in motion that lead to much of this story.<br /> <br /> Note while the Werewolf journals cover in game events, Lizette\u2019s a short fiction covering an encounter that happened at the very beginning of the session. I would be remiss in not mentioning too that Lizette\u2019s journal is not safe reading for work as it contains erotic elements.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 30 June 1920<br /> <br /> Well today was interesting all around. It started off with the pack discussing what we were going to do with the necklace and the duplicate. At first we talked about giving the duplicate necklace to Gunter since it seemed unlikely that he would be able to tell the difference between the real and the fake. Lizette did an exceptional job copying the Eye of Iblis, so much so that I couldn\u2019t really tell them apart. We figured that even if he sold the duplicate to someone that could tell that it wasn\u2019t magical, he could say that he was sold a fake and didn\u2019t know it. I had insisted early on in the conversation that Gunter not be given the real one because we did not know his intentions, or his potential buyers. Someone that he sold it to could use it to bad ends and we\u2019d be responsible in a way. <br /> <br /> While we were making our plans Marlene came by and we talked with her about our excuse for being here. We decided that the best thing would be to say that Christina had a bad feeling when she held the necklace and called her friend, Wolfram, who is knowledgeable about the occult. The rest of us just came to be supportive of our friend. And since we did not want Christina to hold the necklace again, for her safety, we came up with the idea that she gave it to us to hold onto because of the bad feelings it gave her. This would explain why we had it and his sister did not.<br /> <br /> Later we received a note from Gunter inviting the lot of us to dinner. We all tried to dress appropriately, some of us were more successful than others. Wolfram looked very posh in his suit, which was the point. He wanted to make a good impression on Gunter from the start. I figured he was going to have no problems with initial impressions. Dearbhail also dressed very nicely for the dinner. She was rather fetching. The rest of us dressed nicely as well, mostly in suits, though Lizette chose to wear her leather jacket and slacks ensemble. Wolfram did not say anything against the outfit so neither did I. The dinner tonight was Wolfram\u2019s show, just like the Salon was Alla\u2019s. The rest of us followed Wolfram\u2019s lead in the manner of dress and etiquette. <br /> <br /> When we first met Gunter I noticed Dearbhail looking intently at Gunter for a moment before breaking out into a radiant smile. As is her habit, I assumed that she was reading his desires and found them acceptable. I later found out that I was correct in that matter. His main desire at the time was to find out what kind of man Wolfram was and what his intentions were towards his sister.<br /> <br /> During the dinner Gunter thanked all of us for helping his family and keeping an eye out for Christina while he was away. He then talked with each of us in turn asking where we\u2019re from and how we\u2019re finding Vienna. For my part I told him what region of Czechoslovakia I was from and about the hills and valleys of my home. I compared the countryside of my home to different places that I\u2019ve traveled as a courier. And in turn I asked what some of the places that Gunter has traveled to are. He said that he\u2019d been to Russia, Germany, and Dalmacia, which I believe is now Italy. Apparently his family used to have some holdings in Dalmacia and he is eager to try and get them back. Through all of this I made sure to only speak of places that I\u2019ve been to as Marek and not mention anywhere else that I may have traveled no matter how beautiful. It would not do to have Gunter get suspicious of me or my activities. He is a clever man and is not to be underestimated. <br /> <br /> After dinner we separated along gender lines and the women went to one room to talk, while the men when to another. We were offered brandy and cigars, which were both good. I noticed that Dacian palmed an extra cigar for later, or for one of the ladies. My guess is Tatiana. We then made more small talk about our homes and the recovery effort after the war. Thankfully the war did not touch Czechoslovakia all that much so there wasn\u2019t much to do. The people on the other hand need time to get over the war, but the countryside itself was spared the ravages of war, much to my joy. <br /> <br /> Once the small talk was done Gunter asked to speak privately with Wolfram. He agreed readily enough and the two of them went outside in the garden to talk. I stayed somewhat near the door and listened in. I did not feel bad in the least about listening in on my pack-mates conversation. We do not know Gunter very well, and I wanted to make sure that if anything were to go wrong and Wolfram were to be in danger that I would be able to react quickly. Not that Wolfram cannot take care of himself, but again we did not know Gunter or his capabilities. So, I listened. They spoke about the necklace and it was revealed that Gunter did in fact know that it was magical and very dangerous. Hence his warning to Christina not to wear it. I find that unless given a reason, warnings like this are not usually adhered to. He did have a couple of potential buyers lined up and was in the process of deciding which one to actually sell the Eye of Iblis to. His intention was to sell it to someone that did not have bad intentions. Wolfram then explained that he was holding onto the necklace due to its evil aura. He did not want it to be anywhere near Christina. He did not mention that Gunter\u2019s sister had already tried it on once, he just emphasized how dangerous it was and how it was safer if kept away from the ladies. Gunter agreed and said that they would speak more of the artifact tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Then Gunter surprised Wolfram, and myself for that matter, and flat out asked him about his involvement or knowledge of his part in Gunnar\u2019s death. Wolfram decided then to be honest and told Gunter that the situation was not of his making but that he did what he had to in order to resolve the problem. And in just as vague a way Gunter said that he was happy that his sister found someone that will do what needed to be done in order to keep her safe. It was never said outright, but Gunter was impressed that Wolfram was willing to kill to keep Christina safe. I am not sure why they just didn\u2019t say outright what they meant instead of using vague terms to say things. They both knew what they were talking about. There was no need to hide their actions or intentions. This may be part of that whole Noble code or etiquette. To not speak of \u201cdistasteful\u201d things in plain terms. It seems silly to me. There would be far less room for misunderstanding if they just spoke in plain words. In the end though I guess it did not matter here. They were both on the same page, so to speak, and seemed to get along well.<br /> <br /> After the business of the necklace and Gunnar\u2019s death was taken care of Wolfram asked Gunter for his blessing before he asked for Christina\u2019s hand in marriage. Again, it was all very formal, but amicable. Gunter gave his blessing and the two men made their way back into the house. As they were walking in Dacian got a strange look on his face for just a moment and I made a note to myself to ask him later what he had discovered. I assumed he had used one of his Fae powers and learned something unexpected. Dacian looked between Gunter and the ring on his finger a couple of times before relaxing marginally. The ring didn\u2019t look significant to me, but there was something about it that bothered Dacian. Whatever it was left him a bit tense.<br /> <br /> Once Gunter and Wolfram came back inside we decided to rejoin the ladies, who apparently had been playing some version of Blind Man\u2019s Bluff. They seemed to have enjoyed themselves though I could tell that Tatiana was not happy to have been told to stay with the ladies. She would much rather be a part of the action than be given a sideline role. Granted I didn\u2019t do much more than listen to a conversation and nothing that was said before would be considered inappropriate for her to have heard. I guess it\u2019s just more of the Noble etiquette coming up that says that certain activities, such as brandy and cigars are only for men. Not sure why, but we went along with it for now. If we were not actively trying to make a good impression on Gunter I would have insisted that people be allowed to do as they pleased rather than what society dictated was correct. After we\u2019d rejoined the ladies Wolfram asked to speak to Christina and they went off to a corner of the room to talk. Tatiana and I could hear what was being said just fine, but I suppose the distance gave the illusion of privacy. So, Wolfram proposed to Christina in what I suppose is a romantic way, and she said yes. I do not know how long their engagement will last before they actually get married, but it is now official that Christina will become part of the pack. <br /> <br /> After we got back to the hotel we all talked about what had been said and discovered. Wolfram told us about his private conversation with Gunter and how the other man knows that he was involved in Gunnar\u2019s death. He also told us that Gunter knows that the necklace is magical and his intentions regarding the artifact. I was not initially pleased with Wolfram\u2019s promise to return the original necklace to Gunter just because we do not know him well, but the deal was struck and it would be hard to go back on it now. I can only hope that he was telling the truth about wanting to sell it to someone whose intention was to contain it rather than use it.<br /> <br /> Dacian also told us what he\u2019d discovered about Gunter. He said that when Gunter came back in the house he used a power on the other man to see if there was anything magical or otherwise about him. Apparently both the man and his nondescript ring are magical in some way. We know that his is not a Vampire or a Sin-Eater since Wolfram would have detected that right off. He is not Fae. He has no \u201cmask\u201d to hide elfin features. We also know that he is not Uratha or Pure because Tatiana and I would have discovered that as soon as we met him. It was also said that Gunter does not \u201cread\u201d the same way as those things on the train that we fought a while back. So they are not \u2018guardians of fate,\u201d or some such monster. The question remains. What is he?<br /> <br /> 1 July 1920<br /> <br /> Today there was another meeting with Gunter. It was supposed to be just Wolfram and Gunter, but Dacian hid himself in the room before the other two men arrived. Tatiana and I waited a respectable distance away from the room but well within range to hear what was being said just in case there should be trouble. They spoke of Gunter\u2019s intentions with the necklace and that he had a buyer that specifically wanted to contain the relic and not use it and they spoke of themselves, or more specifically about their abilities. Wolfram asked, again delicately, what kind of creature Gunter was. He said that he felt that it was good to be up front about such things when dealing with others so closely. Gunter said that he had been found as a child to have skills and was sent to a special tutor to learn how to use his abilities. I suppose the best way to say it is that he has skill in magic. Wolfram then admitted that he had died and had come back to life. Gunter said that he had known of others like our German friend that have had the same experience. Wolfram also admitted that others that he was with also have abilities. Gunter admitted that he noticed and that some of us were more obvious than others. The matter was pretty much dropped after that so I\u2019m not sure which of us Gunter has figured out. <br /> <br /> After they\u2019d cleared the air somewhat and spoke of the necklace and Gunter\u2019s intentions with it, Wolfram pulled out the actual necklace and gave it to Gunter. Wolfram admitted that we had made a duplicate to be on the safe side and offered it to Gunter as well in case he wanted to try and sell it to both parties that he had in mind. Gunter did not want to sow that kind of chaos and said that he would sell the necklace to the more conservative of the potential buyers. We had agreed that this would be acceptable so Wolfram gave the Eye of Iblis to Gunter.<br /> <br /> Later, after dinner, we discussed what we were going to be doing once we left Vienna. We agreed that we would split up for a while, but frequent our home in Paris. I told the others that if I am ever out working and they need to contact me and they cannot find me by my usual name, that they can look for me under the name of Reznik. I told them that if all else failed that Jamal might be able to help them find me if I was out on a job. I believe that they all had an idea of the sort of work that I do as Reznik, especially after I told them that Jamal could find me. They know that he is involved in the more questionable side of things, and has resources. There was no condemnation or accusatory looks for which I was glad. I am not ashamed of my work as Reznik, but I did not want there to be tension in the pack. But they all took things in stride which I\u2019ll admit was a relief.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I am packing.<br /> <br /> This time, yes, we are leaving today. For home. For Paris.<br /> <br /> No, we do not take Christina with us.<br /> <br /> Yes, she is to become pack. The promises have been exchanged. But she is not to join him in his den for a time.<br /> <br /> Human foolishness.<br /> <br /> Are you still harping on that volchonok? I have told you, Blind Man\u2019s Bluff is not foolishness, it is a game and it is enjoyable if you do not have the senses to overcome a blindfold. Or if you enjoy being close to beautiful women.<br /> <br /> Bah, no, we did not stop when the men arrived because we did not want to be close to them. It would have been a good reason, but instead it was because Christina was embarrassed.<br /> <br /> Oh, volchonok, that I cannot answer. Why she should be embarrassed, why we should separate, why Wolfram and Christina must have privacy where we may watch, why only the men are allowed brandy and cigars is truly human foolishness. It was good of Dacian to steal me a cigar, at least.<br /> <br /> From what was said, I believe Gunter went to school to become magical, so he is human, so he may be foolish.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that is why we gave him the necklace even though we said we would not. Also, he promised it was to be sold to someone who intended to keep it safe.<br /> <br /> No, he told this to Wolfram alone. At least, I don\u2019t think he said it at dinner. I was not always paying attention, especially when he spoke over much of noble politics.<br /> <br /> I do not know why out alpha scolded me with his eyes. It was not that - I was paying attention at the time, because Gunter was speaking of Wolfram and Christina\u2019s engagement. I even congratulated Wolfram with a slap on the back.<br /> <br /> Well, no, volchonok, he did not exactly speak of the engagement then, but humans often do not say what they mean. He had invited Wolfram there, intended to speak with him privately, and spoke of what was best for Christina. This was obviously Wolfram.<br /> <br /> Certainly better than Gunnar. Wolfram has said Gunter knows Wolfram is the one who killed him.<br /> <br /> I was not there to ask. He is not foolish enough to be bothered over much, at least.<br /> <br /> Oh, you tire of asking me questions I have no answers to, eh, impertinent volchonok? What would you do instead then?<br /> <br /> Of course you would. Well, volchonok, I am packed. Let us run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b><b>Happiness on the Horizon</b></b><br /> <br /> Christina Esterh\u00e1zy had almost decided her visitor would not be coming when she heard the tap at the window. Christina was a proud noble, on the cusp of being engaged, and she had invited that woman to her room. They had kissed a couple nights before, and her head had been in a fog since.<br /> <br /> The tapping came.<br /> <br /> She let in her small green friend. Lizette \u00c9toile wore her bomber jacket, boots, a wide belt, and goggles; a tough combination that was softened by her gentle features. She landed remarkably quietly from climbing in the windowsill, then quickly found a chair and sat down, sprawling out with her arm over the side of the chair and legs further apart than a lady should. Christina trembled.<br /> <br /> \u201cLizette\u2026my Fairy Princess\u2026this is getting out of control. I\u2026should not have invited you here, but I wanted to clear the air\u2026.\u201d Christina started.<br /> <br /> \u201cOui? Than that is what I want too. To work out what is to be between us,\u201d the Gremlin leaned back. Her accent always seemed a bit thicker in their private conversations, Christina noticed. \u201cI want happiness for you and for Wolfram. And also for myself. I am not here to take you from him. Indeed, I want to assure you I will not be getting between you and he.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026good,\u201d Christina breathed. Was she disappointed? The tension did not leave the air.<br /> <br /> \u201cI also know that he has no trouble with what is between us. The attraction\u2026the intensity. I am here also spend the night\u2026seeing to it that it is resolved.\u201d<br /> <br /> Christina froze. \u201cI am\u2026not sure\u2026that is a good idea, my dear\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette smiled, admiring the sheer nightgown Christina was wrapped in. Her eyes rose to Christina\u2019s, which much like the last time they kissed, seemed to call to her. \u201cPerhaps not. But we can but follow our heart in this life.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat my heart tells me right now and what I should do are different.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette smirked and rose from her chair. \u201cYou may ask me to leave, mademoiselle, and I will do so,\u201d She took a step toward Christina, who took a step back feeling her bed behind her. \u201cIf you do not\u2026well,\u201d Lizette sauntered up to Christina, who sat down, trembling. The Wizened quickly climbed onto the bed, straddling Christina\u2019s lap, looking into her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you want me to leave, ch\u00e9rie, you need only ask\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, Lizette, I don\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette pulled Christina into a kiss. It was intense, passionate, the way Lizette always kissed. Christina felt dizzy, and lay back on the bed, as Lizette straddled her waist. Looking up, Christina saw Lizette\u2019s eyes blaze golden. The smaller woman pulled off her belt with a crack, and tossed it and her coat onto the floor.<br /> <br /> Christina\u2019s final inner voice telling her not to do this was silent, her restraint shattered. Her eyes locked with Lizette\u2019s as the slight Changeling opened Christina\u2019s nightgown, and Christina maneuvered her arms out of it. Lizette\u2019s hands found their way to her chest as Christina put her own hands under Lizette\u2019s shirt and growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome to me, Fairy Princess!\u201d<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Movement woke Christina. Movement and the sudden departure of the warm ball against her chest. Christina whimpered disapproval then opened her eyes. The sky was turning lighter as Lizette slid off of her bed.<br /> <br /> \u201cDarling?\u201d Christina croaked.<br /> <br /> Lizette tuned, looking first over her shoulder then turning to face the noblewoman as she saw her partner was awake, \u201cMon amour?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a silence. The sky got lighter.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026that happened. We just\u2026I didn\u2019t dream it.\u201d Christina was unsure if she was overjoyed or horrified.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay, Ma petite?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026depends of if Wolfram would still want to marry me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette placed her hands, palm down, on the bed a looked at her lover. The darkness outside lightened a bit more. The scant light caught Lizette\u2019s golden eyes. Despite the intensity of the look, Christina could not help but see Lizette almost struggled to keep her balance. She must be standing on the frame. \u201cI expect you to marry Wolfram. I would not have spent the night with you if I thought you wouldn\u2019t. He told you himself, did he not, that this was okay? To try out the attraction\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLizette! We made love! That wasn\u2019t \u2018trying out\u2019 anything!\u201d<br /> <br /> A long pause. \u201cC\u2019est vrai.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat wasn\u2019t\u2026what you and Marlene did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNon, it was not, my dear.\u201d<br /> <br /> Christina laid her head back and closed her eyes. Lizette leaned forward.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, what happened was not mere sex. Yes, it was intense and yes, our feelings for each other have not lessened. At least mine have not for you. But I will not get in Wolfram\u2019s way, even if it means never seeing either of you again. And he will still marry you. Had I even a sliver of doubt I would not be here.\u201d Her voice was gentle, now, her accent less prominent. It almost sounded maternal.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy Fairy Princess\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI always will be,\u201d Lizette looked out the window behind her and back. Grays and blues were becoming greens. \u201cI need to go. Will you be okay my sweet? Know nothing has changed between you and the man you love.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about your feelings?\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette looked sad. It did not suit her face, Christina decided, to look sad. \u201cI will find love that won\u2019t interfere in my best friend\u2019s happiness. I have every confidence I can. I will be okay. I promise. \u201c<br /> <br /> Christina reached out and took her hand. \u201cI love you, you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette squeezed her hand, and smiled. Her eyes were wet. \u201cOui. But today, your brother returns. Today, one way or another, you and Wolfram take a step toward you new life. And I will cheer you on. I will always be close. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> Christina smiled. \u201cOkay.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette dressed. As the first rays of sunlight fell upon her petite lover, Christina could swear that Lizette was posing just to show herself off. All too soon she was done.<br /> <br /> \u201cI must return, my dear. Greet your brother. No doubt tonight he and Wolfram will talk. Be ready. Let me not be in the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> Christina smiled, \u201cAs you say. Farewell\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette smiled. \u201cAu revoir,\u201d and slipped out the window. The sun was rising. It was the dawn of a new day.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026My Fairy Princess.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> This was largely a roleplaying session. Dacian used his Kenning to \u201ccheck\u201d Gunter. There were general social rolls all around for Socializing. Overall, the tone was laid back.<br /> <br /> As Gunter, I asked each PC in turn to tell me about themselves, to talk of where they had been and how they felt about Vienna. I only got the \u201cdeer in headlights\u201d from a few players. ^_^<br /> <br /> Tatiana\u2019s player suggested Blind Man\u2019s Bluff, but I was assured Tatiana didn\u2019t. Lizette stood on a chair when playing standing up. Beats charades, I suppose. <br /> <br /> Next time it\u2019s April 1922 and the jazz age is in full swing. Join us for tales from the group\u2019s home base in Paris. But in the meantime, nearly two years is a long time, and next Friday I will have downtime journals and stories from some PCs about their activities. Currently, I have a pair of stories from Tatiana and a journal from Lizette. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T20:02:53-08:00","id":780334,"title":"","content":"Its been two years.<br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s been , like, a week, but in game it has been two years. It is 1922, and a lot has happened since the group left Vienna, the conflict for Christina Esterh\u00e1zy\u2019s affections won (in theory) and complicated (totally) and Vampiric allies and enemies made.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the off week, and some of the group has some stories covering their activities before we resume in April 1922. None of this happened at table, but it is part of the storyline. Lizette has a general journal, Marek covers a specific series of events, and there are two stories about Tatiana and her family. Let\u2019s take advantage of this chance to see what the group got up to.<br /> <br /> <i>Downtime </i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 21 August 1920<br /> <br /> I went home to visit my brother Andel today and found out that his wife\u2019s sister Denisa and her husband adopted one of the Czech children that I freed a while back. They decided to adopt the little girl Kv\u011bta. I will admit that I was happy to hear the news. Kv\u0115ta deserves to have a caring family and she is young enough to get over what was done to her. If she had been older the damage might have been more permanent. But despite all her hardships the little girl seems to be adapting well to her new family and was happy to see me. She of course does not know all that I did to free her from those despicable people. She only knows that I am the one that introduced her future parents to the right people so that they could adopt her. That is enough. Denisa and Erik seem like caring parents. They appear to truly love the little girl and I am happy to see it. Though if they should fail that child retribution will be swift and unpleasant.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9 November 1921<br /> <br /> My brother Andel welcomed his first baby into the world today. I am happy to say that I was visiting when the baby was delivered. It turned out to be a mere fluke of luck, but I am happy nonetheless. The little girl, Darkja was born to Lenka at 4 o\u2019clock in the morning to a happy mother and father. I have never seen my brother quite so happy since we were children and it was good to see. I had despaired that my brother would not experience anything that would bring him such joy since the war. He has been at least a little depressed every time I have seen him, even after he married Lenka. The war did my brother no favors, but it appears that the little Darkja has. I haven\u2019t seen his face light up in such a long time. I was happy to see it. I will admit that I was happy for him and for the little girl. My brother is a caring soul and I think that this will continue to do him some good. I believe that I will stay on a few days before I move on.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 January 1922<br /> <br /> I am being hunted. I will admit that this is a new experience for me since the war has ended. I\u2019m not sure who is after me, but I have found tracks belonging to someone else and I have sensed their presence. I do not know if they wish me good or ill. I suppose I should go out and try to meet them and see what their intentions are. What can it hurt to ask?<br /> <br /> <br /> January 1922<br /> <br /> I do not know the date. It is still close to the middle of the month. I am not doing well. I thought that there was someone following me. I was right. He has been tracking me and I have been doing my best to avoid him. It has not worked so well thus far. Whoever he is, he is informed. He knows of what I am or at least has been armed with the right kind of weapon. I knew I was being followed, but like the idiot that I am I thought that I had more time. The other day, I think, he found me. I knew that he had found me when pain blossomed in my leg. I had been shot, and it was with a silver bullet. I know what it feels like to be shot, and I know what silver feels like. This was silver. It hurt. A lot. I tried to brush it off and flee deeper into the forest, but I think he continued to follow me. It is I admit rather disconcerting to be on the other side of the gun. I have done my best to bandage my wound, but since it was made with silver, it is going to take some time to heal. I do not know how long. I am only semi-aware of how much damage was done in the first place. If only I had a safe place to hole up and see to my wounds. But I am in the middle of a forest in Germany and I don\u2019t have any safe places near here. I will have to make due with what I have.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> January 1922<br /> <br /> My would-be killer is intent on finishing the job. I have tried to run, but it is becoming more and more difficult. He managed to get another shot in. It hit me in the arm, high up. Silver again. I have resisted the urge to go into a frenzy so far, but I do not know how long it will last. I think that the chain Tatiana and I created has helped me keep things in check so far, but I don\u2019t know how much longer I can hold out.<br /> <br /> This bastard has tracked me tirelessly for the past several days. I do not know how many. The days are blurring together, but he was waiting for me. I know that much. My killer started to harass me a few days ago and hit me twice now. I know he was expecting to have killed me by now, but I am nothing if not tenacious. I was able to keep the beast under control and I tried to find my attacker. I found tracks, but after a relatively short period of time they were obscured and I could not continue on the trail. When I find the bastard I\u2019m going to make sure that his last moments on this earth are painful.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> January 1922 ?<br /> <br /> He found me again. Hit me a couple more times. One grazed my head. I stumbled and he fired again. He was getting closer with each shot. He was going to finish me off. The last shot went through my chest, high and to the right. It hit my lung I think. Breathing after that was hard and I coughed up blood. In that moment I was preparing to die. I knew that I would come back, but I will admit that dying is not pleasant. My clarity lasted for a moment or two longer and then vanished. In that instant I went into a rage. I do not remember what happened, but I have a pretty good idea given what I found. My would-be killer was about a hundred meters from where I woke up on the forest floor. I tracked the bloody path back and found the body. Or at least what was left of it. From what I could tell he was not very old. He had blond hair and blue eyes. His features other than that were ruined, and his chest was shredded. I\u2019ll admit that I was angry about being shot at and wanted to kill the one responsible, but if I had a choice I would not have gone this far. I have only raged once before this and that was when I discovered what I was. I am not happy to have lost control like that, though I understand intellectually that sometimes we have no choice but to let the beast out.<br /> <br /> After I\u2019d finished looking over the shooter I looked for his weapon. I found it a few meters away. It was a decent sniper rifle so I took it and the ammunition I found. He only had a couple of silver rounds left, but there were some traditional lead rounds in the pouch as well. There was also a photograph of me. No name on it, just the picture.<br /> <br /> I washed as much blood off as I could in a nearby stream and then bound my wounds as best I could with shreds from his shirt. What I could find that wasn\u2019t soiled anyway. I made sure I had his scent so I could find his camp. He might have supplies that I could use.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> February 1922<br /> <br /> I found the man\u2019s camp and made it my own. I was only there for about a day when I in turn was found by a local Uratha pack. The man that found me called himself Adalwolf, which given its meaning of \u201cNoble Wolf\u201d is not likely his given name. It is too much of a coincidence. Anyway\u2026I was found by Adalwolf when I was collecting water. He started to confront me in a hostile fashion, I\u2019m assuming he thought the scent of blood was from something I\u2019d hunted, but then he stopped. He seemed to notice that the blood was mine and he changed his approach. I explained to him in general terms what happened and how I found myself to be in his packs territory. I could not explain to him who sent the shooter, much to his chagrin. I\u2019m assuming that he wanted to know if there was going to be a further threat to his pack. I showed him the picture I found in the young man\u2019s pocket. It was of me. He was specifically after me and knew where to find me. Seeing as he was dead he did not know about Adalwolf\u2019s pack. So it was unlikely that anyone would be after them. He seemed to calm down after that.<br /> <br /> He invited me to stay with his pack for a little while, until I had healed a little more. I gratefully accepted the invitation and told him that I would owe him a favor in the future. I packed up the shooter\u2019s gear and took it with me. I am not one to turn down free equipment, especially if it is fairly won. When we got back to their cabin I was greeted by another man, Griswold and a woman, Tresa. They looked to their alpha and he told them that he had invited me to stay given my circumstances. After that they were friendlier. Tresa had been a nurse in the Great War and helped to clean out my wounds and bandage them in a more professional manner. I will admit that I slept a lot in the beginning. When I woke in the woods I was close to death, I am pretty sure. Adalwolf helped me to walk back under my own power, which I appreciated. I didn\u2019t pass out until after introductions had been made and Tresa saw to my injuries.<br /> <br /> The pack that helped me was understandably wary of me at first, but they obviously had the advantage of me if it had come to a fight. I was in no condition to fight anyone. After a little while they seemed to get used to my presence and accepted me as a guest. I promised them that I would help to hunt for the pack as payment for their kindness, and I did, as much as I could. In the beginning I was not able to run anything down myself, but I helped get water and dig tubers where they could be found. Griswold still ate vegetables, the other two only ate meat.<br /> <br /> After some weeks had passed the worst of my wounds were well on the way to being mended. I stopped coughing up blood some time ago, and I have been very happy about that. The other wounds were nothing compared to that. Once my chest was sufficiently mended I was able to help with the actual hunting. I did what I could to bring down deer and help them cure and store the meat in case food became scarce.<br /> <br /> As it turns out Griswold is a Bone Shadow as well. We have spent several nights talking about spirits and the making of fetishes. I am still a novice at making items that I can actually catch or coerce spirits into, so I asked Griswold if he would teach me. He agreed readily enough and started to show me how to go about gathering the right materials, the right way to put them together, what shapes and symbols hold the most power, and in the end how to craft the right kind of agreement with the spirit you desire to be in the fetish. The trick is finding out what the spirit really wants and to work with that, but sometimes they are not so forthcoming and you have to tease it out of them. I will admit that this is not one of my strong points but it is something that I will work on. I get along well enough with Dedecek and Tatiana\u2019s wolf pup on the occasions we\u2019ve interacted. He is so young and vibrant while Dedecek is older and much more calm. It\u2019s like night and day with those two. Now I just need to learn how to make connections with spirits other than those I already know.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 4 March 1922<br /> <br /> I will be leaving Adalwolf\u2019s pack tomorrow morning. They have been more than generous in helping me heal and teaching me things that I did not know. I know that what scant hunting I have done since recovering is not enough to make up my debt to them, so I have promised them a favor owed. I have told them how to find me in France and who to ask if I\u2019m not there. I have also let them know that my pack is somewhat unique, so if they come searching for me and find Wolfram or one of the Fae they will not be surprised. My pack can find me if the need should arise.<br /> <br /> My only real concern in leaving this safe place is that I do not know if there will be anyone else hunting me. I will admit that I have had my fill of being the hunted for one lifetime. I fully understand that I will not always be the hunter, but I prefer not to be the prey. I will assume that there is someone still out there and plan accordingly. I do not know if my would-be killer was after me or Reznik. I don\u2019t know who sent him or why. There are too many unknowns for me to be comfortable, yet I cannot stay here forever. I have a life and I am intent on getting back to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> <u>Going Home</u><br /> <br /> Elena looked back at boys. They were still sleeping in the backseat, so she spared a glance at the long road behind them. It was true, what she\u2019d said. Family is more important than places or things. But Livny had been home for a long time. It was more difficult than she let on to simply leave it behind for some town in France.<br /> <br /> She did not let on, because that town in France was where family was. It was where Tatiana would be. A slight smile crossed her face as she looked at the woman in the driver\u2019s seat. Driving a car was not a thing that showed off her muscular form, but somehow she still managed to imbue it with her usual grace and barely restrained power.<br /> <br /> She was favoring her left shoulder. The macho woman was usually better at hiding such things, but the unfamiliar motions involved in driving occasionally surprised her out of her usual bravado. Elena idly wondered if there would be more scars for her to find when they stopped for the night.<br /> <br /> Tatiana noticed her watching and smiled broadly at her, though her eyes only left the road for a moment. She stretched her left arm, rotating it, ending with it near Elena\u2019s thigh, palm up. Elena placed her own hand in Tatiana\u2019s and held tightly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Where the Heart Is</u><br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il recognized the drab uniform after a moment's confusion. She had thought the werewolves were off on business. She smiled and almost called out to her friend Tatiana when she realized the off-key whistling she was hearing was coming from her. She cocked her head inquisitively, and followed behind her quietly, feeling quite adventurous.<br /> <br /> She didn't follow her into the grocery store, feeling too obvious, so she missed the easy exchange between the werewolf and the baker.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy hello Tatiana. Back to the Chateau already? I can gather up your usual in a jiffy.\u201d The baker looked confused.<br /> <br /> Tatiana smiled. \u201cAm I that predictable? No, I have come for your pastries. Two of those, please.\u201d She pointed at the pain aux raisins.<br /> <br /> The baker raised an eyebrow. \u201cThe boys' favorite, eh? Will I have an angry Elena in here again, requesting that I stop selling you so many sweets?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana looked somewhat sheepishly at the floor. \u201cBut it is Sasha's birthday. Every boy deserves sweets on his birthday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that so?\u201d A pair of apple tarts made their way onto the counter by the pain aux raisins. \u201cI do believe you are right.\u201d Tatiana reached into a pocket for another note and the baker stopped her. \u201cA birthday present.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana smiled at him, and tucked the pastries carefully into her bag. A quick stop at the greengrocer later, and she continued down the street, munching on an apple, 3 more in her bag. Dearbhail followed her again, her curiosity only peaked by the wide, relaxed smile that spread across the werewolf's face, an unusual sight.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail's eyes widened as Tatiana was greeted at a house by two young boys, about 4 and 6 years old, who were definitely related to her. She stared intently at the tall woman for a moment before a brilliant smile spread across her face and she barely managed to keep from clapping. The Changeling hid around the corner, in the direction Tatiana would have to go to go home.<br /> <br /> \u201cTanya, Tanya!\u201d the boys yelled in chorus as they ran over to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cBoys.\u201d She smiled as they stopped just in front of her, their eyes wide.<br /> <br /> Aleksandr broke the silence first. \u201cDo you know what day it is?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm...\u201d Tatiana made a show of thinking hard. \u201cSaturday?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo...\u201d Aleksandr's face contorted.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am pretty sure it is Saturday.\u201d Tatiana kept a straight face.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, yes, it is Saturday.\u201d The small boy looked at her pleadingly. \u201cBut what else, Tanya?\u201d She thought some more. \u201cIt's my birthday!\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana smacked her forehead with her palm. \u201cOf course! Little Sasha's birthday. You are... 2? 3?\u201d<br /> <br /> Pyotr smirked as Aleksandr stomped his foot. \u201cI'm 4! You're pulling my leg.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana lifted the boy up easily and placed him on her shoulder, giving his leg a tug once he was seated. \u201cPerhaps I am pulling your leg a little. Of course you are four. Of course it is your birthday. Has it been a good one?\u201d<br /> <br /> The young boy nodded and began to tell her all about it, speaking quickly enough that he stumbled over his words in parts. She carried him inside, set him down at a seat and pulled up a chair for herself, without him stopping for a single word in edgewise.<br /> <br /> When he finally paused, she reached into her bag, pulling out the pastries. Both boys' smiles grew as Tatiana winked at them. They jumped when their mother sighed loudly behind them. \u201cSweets again, Tanya?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana looked innocently up at her. \u201cThey have been good boys, no? I have not brought them sweets for months, I have apples as well. And it is Sasha's birthday...\u201d She stood, moving over to take Elena's hand.<br /> <br /> Elena chuckled quietly. \u201cThis once, it is alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan we eat them now momma?\u201d Aleksandr asked.<br /> <br /> Elena looked at Tatiana as if to say, 'see?' and then sighed. \u201cYes, dears. You may have one of them each. The other we will save for after dinner, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> The two women left the boys to their pastries. Shutting the door to the kitchen behind them, Tatiana pounced on Elena, wrapping her arms around her and burying her face in the shorter woman's hair. \u201cI have missed you, my heart.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow quickly you are spoiled.\u201d Elena leaned back into the other woman, turning her head to rest her cheek on her chest. \u201cIt has been two weeks only.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTwo weeks too long,\u201d Tatiana murmured into her hair. She sighed. \u201cI must leave tonight. It is only because of Sasha's birthday that I left things as they were. I will be back, not tomorrow probably, but the day after.\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena moved away to look up at the werewolf. \u201cCan you stay for dinner?\u201d Tatiana shook her head no. The shorter woman sighed. \u201cVery well. It will mean much to Sasha that you have come.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena reached up to touch Tatiana's cheek. \u201cAlways, my love.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il sat patiently, waiting for her friend to leave the house. After about an hour, she heard the boisterous boys come out of the house, the rambunctious voice of her friend accompanying them. The boys called out to her in Russian, waving from the edge of the property, a woman who was probably their mother standing behind them. Tatiana's eyes lingered on the woman, until she turned the corner where Dearbh\u00e1il waited.<br /> <br /> \u201cTatiana! This is wonderful!\u201d The bubbly Changeling took both of the werewolf's hands.<br /> <br /> Tatiana looked stricken. \u201cDearbh\u00e1il. What are you doing here? What...?\u201d She looked around nervously, and herded the Changeling away from the house, moving quickly enough Dearbh\u00e1il had difficulty keeping up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI saw you in the market and you seemed so happy, and then when I saw you go into that house, I simply had to know what you were after, and it's so wonderful! I so love it when my friends are in love!\u201d Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s happiness was undimmed. \u201cWho is she? A childhood sweetheart? She's from Russia, right? And those boys, they look so much like you! Are they yours? Family? They are wonderfully behaved and so darling.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana smiled despite herself, then stopped and sighed. \u201cI will tell you, but you must promise me that you will not interfere and not tell the others.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il was taken aback. \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do not want them involved in... in the things we do. The supernatural. They do not know what I am, they do not know that things like me, or you, or Alla, or Wolfram exist. They are safer that way, innocent. I do not want to drag them into that world, our world.\u201d Tatiana looked wistfully at her hands, and back towards the house.<br /> <br /> \u201cSurely you can protect them,\u201d Dearbh\u00e1il said earnestly.<br /> <br /> Tatiana nodded. \u201cAnd that is what I am doing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il sighed. \u201cI mean, if they lived in the Chateau. And... if the boys are family... couldn't they be, you know, werewolves?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are safer as innocents, not involved in our pack business. Yes, the boys are family, and perhaps they will become Uratha. But they are not now.\u201d Tatiana was steadfast.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, fine, if that's what you think is best. I won't tell anyone, and I won't interfere.\u201d Dearbh\u00e1il paused, an anticipatory smile growing on her lips. \u201cSo... who are they?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana rolled her eyes. \u201cThe boys are the sons of my brother. My twin brother. Elena, she was married to my brother. They are her sons too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dearbhail gasped. \u201cHow romantic! Supporting the family of your brother after he was gone, falling in love \u2013 I can just imagine it.\u201d Her eyes sparkled as she clasped Tatiana's hands.<br /> <br /> Tatiana chuckled, smirking a little. \u201cSomething like that. I am glad you are pleased.\u201d<br /> <br /> The winged Changeling put her arm in Tatiana's and began walking. \u201cYou have the whole walk back to the Chateau. Tell me everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 2 April 1922<br /> <br /> I sometimes look back on my old journal from the summer of 1920 and think about how much those days changed everything.<br /> <br /> Now here we are at the Chateau de Chantilly, the eight of us rather filling out the house. I have almost reached the point where Fenric does not annoy me. The Werewolves come and go frequently\u2026Marek goes off doing stuff I am better off not knowing about while Tatiana goes to the village regularly. Dacian and Alla have their politics. Dearbh\u00e1il brightens things for us for long stretches, but even she travels. I have made a single trip to Ireland with her. Actually, I guess we all travel a lot, which, well, a lot of us doing that already is part of how we got involved in all this in the first place.<br /> <br /> Christina has a long-term room at the Plaza Ath\u00e9n\u00e9e. She goes between there and her home in Vienna a great deal. She and Wolfram will marry soon, in about a month. My feelings on the subject remain mixed. Indeed I am quite pleased she and Wolfram are happy, I told him that summer I would not sabotage his happiness and indeed I remain a woman of my word. And she is legitimately taken with him. He is most dashing, and tall\u2026things I am not.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Christina and I have been spending time in private\u2026passionate time, for the same two years. She has become a more modern woman, cutting her hair into a bob much like I do, and she has also embraced some more modern modes of dress. We walk in Paris and people think we are longtime friends, window-shopping some and looking out over bridges.<br /> <br /> It would be a lie to say we are not in love. But it would be denial to say she does not feel the same, if not more, for Wolfram. He knows what is going on. I enjoy my time with Christina, but she needs a husband, something I simply cannot be. I am a woman, even if I occasionally wish for just a moment I was a man in her company.<br /> <br /> I have not, however, been lonely. Even beyond our affair, her Companion Marlene Vogl and I have had some fun as well. Love is\u2026not really what is between us, but she is a fun and very adventurous woman, and like her mistress she has had flirtations with the modern world. However, finding a husband is important to her, so she maintains her once noble bearing as much as she can. It suits her.<br /> <br /> I also have my eye on someone else. Clara Bellerose is an attractive aspiring poetess I have met at Natalie Barney\u2019s socials. I was born in a small village far from the city, and spent my adolescence as a mechanic in Arcadia and fighting the German army, so I feel very undereducated. A Salon run by a woman of intelligence who gathers people from all the various humanities together is quite nice in and of itself, but the sheer number of lesbian affairs going on is staggering. I would think it the plot of a lurid novel were I not there. I suspect the lovely Miss Bellerose is curious about such things. She may learn, especially once Christina and Wolfram make things official.<br /> <br /> The way things are going, I am hoping that relationships such as the Sapphic relationships I see there (and relationships between men, too) will be publicly accepted in the next twenty years. This is the future, after all.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and I have a plane. Actually I\u2019ve constructed a pair of planes after extensive study of aircraft, after arranging for a hanger and menacing people into keeping away. The larger, slower plan can carry five passengers, pilot included. The other just the two, for Wolfram and I, and has it set up for duel synchronized Vickers machine guns ready to go. I am working on the best way to enhance speed, and have a speed boost system attached to the engine that remains sadly largely untested at the moment as it might become explosive but I am sure we will sort it out.<br /> <br /> Only one engine has exploded so far but I still managed to convince the engine to work long enough for the plane to land properly. Frankly I am not sure what everyone was so upset about. It exceeded two hundred kilometers per hour before it exploded! Progress!<br /> <br /> People are far less sanguine about putting a pair of Vickers on my Cadillac Sedan. I am not sure why, an armored bulletproof car with a pair of Vickers mounted on it makes the streets safer, assuming I am driving. The caltrops and oil slick is largely experimental but I am optimistic. I know it works, anyway. I mean, at what price personal defense? Christina likes it. She says it is a pretty green. So there.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> We really could have used that in Vienna. Ah well.<br /> <br /> For personal safety, a lady can\u2019t be too careful, and that is why I use a Thompson M-1. It fires over 700 rounds per minute, and has a variation of the \u201cAnnihilator\u201d 100 round drum magazine. I am working on modifying it to hold even more ammunition easily but I am not quite there yet. Still, it is an absolute marvel to use and load, easy to switch to semi-automatic or fully automatic, and is a stylish matte black that goes with almost any outfit.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem is recoil. I weigh around sixteen kilograms. It\u2019s an issue. But I am dealing with it. Bracing myself helps, and I am working on boots that will eject spikes from behind the heel into the ground to make my position firmer. Also, helpful when kicking out knees.<br /> <br /> For a sidearm I have put my Star aside for a Colt M1911. It\u2019s pretty impressive, but damn heavy. It works for some outfits but not others. It\u2019s concealability is useful for avoiding having to match too closely, but it lacks the mystique of the Thompson and the ability to put so many bullets in the air I can hardly resist cackling with glee.<br /> <br /> In continuing my \u201cmodern\u201d look, I have adopted a bob, short skirt, and galoshes whenever possible. I have not lost my taste for long coats, and I jump between men\u2019s hats and women\u2019s. I never travel without my monocle, in case any dolls nearby catch my eye and need a hint. Men, I find, never need a hint. Bless them.<br /> <br /> Flamethrowers really don\u2019t work with any of my current eveningwear, which is kind of upsetting. Chainsaws don\u2019t either, but I have actually made more improvements to my chainsaw to make it lighter weight and even less likely to gunk up from intestines or viscera. Also green. Sadly nothing touches the Thompson for matching outfits.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also come a long way in preparing explosives, but Wolfram says I ought not write much about that down.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve traveled to some\u2026I went to Ireland with Dearbh\u00e1il and have been to Spain. I have not been able to make myself go to Germany yet. Frankly, I don\u2019t trust myself. After Verdun, I still don\u2019t trust Germans. Broadly speaking, anyway\u2026Wolfram is an unusual case. I recognize that this is illogical and that the flaw is clearly with me, but it is there.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and I do go flying frequently. We have gone together and separately to Vienna, and traveled over a good deal of Southern Europe. Not far over the Mediterranean yet, but I am still looking at flight ranges. I do hope to visit everyone\u2019s home city eventually. Well, those of us whose home cities are not burned out husks anyway.<br /> <br /> Such freedom in the air! It is certainly a major bonding thing for us. Wolfram is probably my best friend right now. Which only makes the whole Christina thing more awkward.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a quiet life, but I am getting stir-crazy. Just dusting off the old journal again has my blood pumping a bit. A gremlin needs her excitement. I wonder what things are in store?<br /> <br /> <i>End Downtime</i><br /> <br /> Well then. Clashing Marek\u2019s story of survival with Tatiana\u2019s endearing stories of family was amusing. And of course Lizette is, well, Lizette. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> We hit the ground running next session, with vampires, flappers, archaeologists, nobles, <i>Nosferatu the Vampyre</i>, and stubborn reporters. Join us, won\u2019t you? Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T02:01:00-08:00","id":784013,"title":"","content":"Time to return to the Jazz Age. It is April 1922, and events are beginning to unfold in Paris. Let\u2019s check up on our adventurers.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 23 April 1922<br /> <br /> Today has been a rather eventful day. As such, I did not get the chance to ask the others if they have had anyone hunting them. I will make an effort to ask when we are all together again.<br /> <br /> So, yesterday evening Alla was summoned to a function being held by the vampire\u2019s Prince of Paris. He called a big meeting to talk to all of the kindred in the area about some artifacts that were recently and the publicity surrounding it. Apparently two archaeologists, which are under the Prince\u2019s protection, have brought to town three artifacts from ancient Egypt. Their construction is somewhat interesting as is their history. It was speculated that they are related to kindred history as well, and could be connected to certain clans and such.<br /> <br /> Three people were chosen, each from a different group, to lay down protections on the artifacts so no one person or group can steal the items and get away unscathed. It sounds rather paranoid to me, but apparently enough groups of vampires are against the others that theft is a very real threat. So, there are magical shields and whatnot being put on the items and the Prince is having the archaeologists and others study the items to see if more can be found out about their history, use and power, if any.<br /> <br /> The artifacts being brought in was not a quiet affair and the press is keenly interested in finding out more about the relics. Related to this increase in reporters, the vampires that were present were warned against getting caught on film since they don\u2019t show up very well and it would be a breach of their laws if someone noticed the aberration in the photographs. There is in particular one reporter named Greta Hess that is very, and I do mean very, interested in finding out all she can about the artifacts and getting that information out to the public. She was spotted and duly distracted by Fenric at the museum that the meeting was held in.<br /> <br /> Wolfram did mention that he knew who Greta was. Apparently hers is a fairly well known, and rich, German noble family. She is the eldest, but because of tradition will not inherit the family business. Her younger brother will do that. From what Wolfram says she sounds like a formidable young woman.<br /> <br /> Anyway\u2026the two archaeologists that are studying the artifacts are Dr. Nathan Henshaw, an up and coming archaeologist. He is supposed to be intelligent and well spoken. The other is a young woman, young looking anyway, named Dana Barlow. Apparently she is so good at what she does that if she\u2019d been born a man she would be one of the foremost academics in the field. Tradition being what it is says that because she\u2019s a woman she can\u2019t be considered in that way. Sometimes I find that what is considered socially acceptable is not very acceptable. I find it confusing. Why disregard someone\u2019s knowledge because of their gender? It is not physical prowess alone that gives people power. Look at me. Tatiana could probably pull me limb from limb, but she deferred to me when we met. I have not been accustomed to following others even when I was in the army. I was given my own discretion as to who my targets would be and it was a system that worked very well.<br /> <br /> The relics themselves I will admit hold my interest as well. They apparently seem to contain arcane technology in much the same what that the Golden Eagle does. Could they have been made by the same group/culture? These pieces are supposed to be ancient and yet they seem to have more modern technology within them than would normally be found in that time. Who built them and for what purpose?<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> In order to find out more about the artifacts and what was going on Wolfram left his calling card at the hotel that Dana Barlow was staying at. We arranged to meet her this evening. Wolfram, Dacian and I went to meet her at the hotel and we walked to a restaurant nearby. Unfortunately we were followed to and into the restaurant by Greta. I am not sure what the acceptable way to get her to stop following us would be. Threatening her will only harden her resolve to see and report on the relics. Killing her would only draw undue attention to the city and possibly to us. Trying to reason with her did not work, so I\u2019m not sure what other options we have.<br /> <br /> So, we talked this evening about the relics and how Dana believes that the artifacts are from an earlier period, but were tinkered with by the Egyptians. There is also supposedly a connection to a long dead pharaoh whose name has been obliterated from the records. He is simply known as the Black Pharaoh. Dana also wants to use a device called a w\u0101s, which is an ancient Egyptian kind of wand, to see if she can figure out what the items do and if they have any sort of power inherent in them. It seems that this wand also has the same sort of technology that the Eagle does. She also told us that she knew of some Arabic people following her and the artifacts. She did not know what their intentions are, but they seem to be keeping some distance. I will have to keep an eye out and see if I spot any of these individuals. They should stand out somewhat from the most of Paris\u2019 denizens.<br /> <br /> In the end we learned a bit more about the relics and something more about our intrepid archaeologist. Dana, according to Wolfram, is not aging. We postulated that she is perhaps a ghoul, like Fenric. His aging was stopped as soon as he entered into Alla\u2019s service as a ghoul. I believe that he drinks her blood and essentially gains long life and something of her powers. But, Wolfram can \u201csee\u201d an individual aging, or when they died if they are a ghost. It\u2019s like a timer of sorts. Only hers is stopped. Dacian also did something he calls Kenning to see if she was magical, and she certainly was. As was her belt. This did not answer any questions since Fenric shows up to Dacian as a magical being as well, so Dana could be like Fenric. She may be something completely different, but if she is it\u2019s not immediately apparent what she is.<br /> <br /> As we left the restaurant we tried to leave discreetly while Dacian intercepted Greta. I believe that I was more successful than Wolfram was in the end. Dacian did succeed in keeping Greta from following us however, so that worked at least. He struck up a conversation with the young lady and discovered just how determined she was to find out about the relics and to report on it to the general public. As I said before. We are not going to dissuade her from her investigation. She has got to be the most determined reporter that I\u2019ve ever met. As admirable a trait as determination is, she is going to get herself killed if she\u2019s not careful. Unfortunately for her I do not see her being careful.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening we all met up to watch the movie \u201cNosferatu.\u201d Alla even got Lizette to fly her into Paris from our chateau. That woman likes to make an entrance. In any case the movie was not exactly accurate, but entertaining all the same. It\u2019s probably a good thing that it has details wrong about the vampires. They, I\u2019m sure, would not like it for mortals to have a true understanding of them or even know that they actually exist. After the movie Alla was approached by a gentleman by the name of Harlow that she\u2019d met previously and who produces plays. He wanted to see if she\u2019d like to be involved in a particular production that he is working on at the moment. It is apparently an adaptation of the story of Orpheus and it involves the queen of the maenads, Agrippa. Interesting thing is, earlier this evening Alla met a kindred woman named Agrippa, who is of Greek origin. Coincidence? Probably not. The producer of this play found some old religious text and adapted it into his play. Alla said that she was planning on talking to Constancia, who was embraced, I believe is the correct term, by Agrippa. She wants to confirm whether or not Agrippa is the woman mentioned in the ancient texts and if she would have a problem with Alla being a part of this production.<br /> <br /> After the movie the pack discussed what we had found out about the relics, the determined reporter and plays based on ancient vampires. We decided to split up and explore our two main concerns, the play and further conversation with Dana Barlow. Wolfram was going to take Christina back to the hotel as she was still scared from the movie. I did not find the movie all that frightening. I have to remind myself though that Christina, and most people for that matter, have not had my life experiences. I do not find it scary because I have seen and experienced worse already. I guess it puts things in perspective.<br /> <br /> So, after our talk Lizette, Dacian and I went to go talk to Dana again, this time at her hotel. Lizette got her room number from the front desk attendant and she and I headed upstairs. Dacian said that he was going to go up the outside of the hotel and have a look around on the roof and around her window for anything suspicious. I knocked on Dana\u2019s door and heard the telltale sound of a gun being cocked. Not a sound you ever forget. I let Dana know who I was and that I had brought an associate to talk to her about our earlier discussion. Dana opened the door after a moment and I saw her put a shotgun down within easy reach. She offered us scotch and we started talking. I left most of the discussion to Lizette since it was more technical information that we were after on this trip. Lizette dropped some terms and Dana understood them, which I take to mean that the artifacts were similar in design to the Golden Eagle. They were both trying to charm information out of the other. It was interesting to watch, but made me glad that I wasn\u2019t trying to chime in. I am far too blunt to do the subtle dance of words that those two were doing. After things wound down I made our excuses and said that we should leave but that we\u2019d see her at the viewing for the artifacts. Lizette did what I can only describe as a swagger as she left. I simply said goodnight and we left.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> The last part of the evening, while Lizette and I were visiting Dana, Alla and Tatiana went to the museum to find Agrippa and have a talk with her about the play. They arrived at the museum to find the guard unconscious near the door and a cup on the floor nearby. It appears that someone drugged the guard, but the odd thing is that they did not take his keys. They were still on his belt. So the ladies went to the door and found that the lock had been picked. The keys would have been easier, but perhaps more noticeable if missing? As it was, it might have been assumed that the guard simply fell asleep while on his shift. It wasn\u2019t the most professionally done charade, but it wasn\u2019t bad. From what I heard, at this point, Alla challenged Tatiana\u2019s tracking ability. Tatiana promptly shifted forms and proceeded to lead Alla straight to an open air vent where they found Greta Hess. And though he\u2019s seen the change before, Fenric didn\u2019t do so well and became quite startled. Soon after finding the open air vent Marisa and Constancia came out and joined the search for the intruder. They got Greta out of the vent and Tatiana picked her up and carried her towards the door. She told the reporter to stay away from the museum and motioned for her to leave. She did leave this time, but I have a feeling that she is going to disregard Tatiana\u2019s order and come back.<br /> <br /> After Greta left, Alla went to speak with Agrippa about the play, the playwright, and the book it was all based on. It appeared that Agrippa took things well and did not see overly put out by the idea of a play featuring her namesake and Alla playing said part. She did seem interested in reading the play though, and possibly the book that the playwright used as his source material. I have to admit that I\u2019d be curious to read anything that someone had written about me or someone that could be me. I have secrets that I\u2019d rather not get out, as I\u2019m sure Agrippa does as well. I know what I would do to keep my secrets, and I have a feeling that Agrippa would be less sociable than I would be about keeping them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Stop that volchonok, it is unkind.<br /> <br /> Yes, the small man makes amusing faces when he is terrified. It is still unkind, and he is pack.<br /> <br /> I... who has been teaching you to argue with me volchonok? Have you been speaking with Ochranny? Perhaps it was unkind to change in front of him without warning, but Alla questioned my ability to track.<br /> <br /> It was easy, of course, tracking a single young human in a museum full of vampires. It is good we found her, I believe that other vampire, the friend of Constancia, would have been less gentle.<br /> <br /> Holding her above my head was gentle. I did not even attempt to frighten her. Perhaps I will have to tomorrow - she needs to leave this be - but I did not there. I did not even bite her to get her taste to follow.<br /> <br /> We were there because Alla\u2019s writer friend had a book stolen for him to write a play from, and Constancia\u2019s Sire has the same name as a character in this book, and they both have yellow eyes.<br /> <br /> It is a religious book, an old religion, and Agrippa, Constancia\u2019s Sire, is old and it was possibly a secret book from her religion, and she would kill writer and actors for it. She is not stable, apparently, and Alla thought it would be best if we brought it to her ahead of time, and perhaps head off problems.<br /> <br /> Of course I went to speak with Constancia. I do not care what this Agrippa thinks, so I certainly did not go to speak with her.<br /> <br /> The others were speaking with Dana Barlowe, the archeologist woman. Lizette wanted to see if she knew things about magical machines, and Marek had met with her earlier, so he introduced her. I believe Dacien was lurking about on the roofs.<br /> <br /> This archeologist found artifacts which are machines like the Golden Eagle perhaps. We are going to guard her in exchange for being able to look at these artifacts.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was sleeping with Christina. She was frightened of the show and wished his presence to feel safe.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it would be more convenient for that if she denned with us.<br /> <br /> Yes, I would be able to sleep with Elena more if she denned with us.<br /> <br /> Because I do not want foolish volchonoks giving the boys ideas.<br /> <br /> No, I would rather foolish songbirds not give the boys ideas either, but that is not your concern. You stayed with the songbird tonight, yes? Has she gone back again?<br /> <br /> Very well. No, I do not know why she did not want to see the movie. Because it was about vampires, perhaps? She does not like vampires.<br /> <br /> It was quite a good movie. Very German. I do not know if Dearbh\u00e1il would have liked it anyways.<br /> <br /> Perhaps. Next time you shall have to come see one of these films, volchonok. Perhaps you will appreciate one human thing.<br /> <br /> It has been a long night, volchonok. And there is much to do tomorrow. We have had much time for running recently. But not tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 23rd April 1922<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just like old times! It looked like a normal day but we are knee deep in Adventure!<br /> <br /> It was Sunday and the start of a frankly emotionally taxing week, with Wolfram and Christina getting married soon. I am trying really hard to be happy for them and not resentful or sad or anything and it is really hard. I need to put on a bright face and never communicate that it hurts to see them marrying each other. In another life, I could have had a wonderful relationship with either, maybe even settled down. God, I am crying thinking about it. Lizette does not cry!<br /> <br /> Also, I think Christina is pregnant. That is a, pardon my language, fucking punch in the face. I mean I actually feel sick from jealousy. Sometimes I wonder of which. It\u2019s these times I hate being a twisted little freak.<br /> <br /> Okay, stopped crying. This is not a sad entry. I can continue. I don\u2019t feel anything. I am a powerful and resilient adventuress. I don\u2019t feel bad when my friends get together. I do not feel sad. I do not feel sad. I do not feel sad. Okay.<br /> <br /> But\u2026BUT\u2026tonight was awesome DESPITE them being all lovey-dovey, because I got to flirt with outrageously beautiful women and work on building weapons. Dulled the pain for awhile.<br /> <br /> Earlier in the day was working on the car. Got my mind off things anyway. As I did not need to be anywhere until that night, it seemed a good time to look at attaching the hidden flamethrower to the car. Now, as if cars are not explosive enough, the tank can be a liability, so a real trick is knowing where to place it, and how to do so without compromising the flamethrower itself. Now, obviously the flamethrower is more or less anti-personnel, especially anti-whoever the poor slob is trying to get into my car, so I have to consider placing it so it can dissuade people trying to board, the best way possible to dissuade someone from doing something like that: Setting them on fire.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> I tried a few locations and had some ideas but the tank is still an issue. Work for another day.<br /> <br /> From there was prepping the plane. I needed to work on the booster for the engine but not tonight. Tatiana, Dacian, and Marek had ridden up to Paris earlier, and Dearbh\u00e1il was not going, so it was just Alla, Fenric and I headed up for the movie. The planes are in good shape and I must say I am rather proud of them.<br /> <br /> According to the agreement, I flew Alla out to see <i>Nosferatu le Vampire</i> in time to arrive about 7:30, and smuggled her inside. She was quite pleased the opening night went so well, and brought in an actor from the film as well as a pianist. The fear glamour was positively delicious. I think the Autumn Court could really be on to something here\u2026who would have thought they would make so many fear movies? I mean <i>Le Cabinet du Docteur Caligari</i> was scary too, but wow <i>Nosferatu</i> was chilling. This could be a very good thing for the Leaden Mirror to explore.<br /> <br /> We saw various people on the way out. Alla was sidelined by her friend Harlow from Vienna, a traveling entertainer. They discussed a play he was working on, which she believed might reference a particular local Vampire, Agrippa. For my part, Clara was there (I had missed her in the audience) and came up to gush over me. I am not sure she had seen me in my jacket, gloves, and goggles and she was super nervous. She also tried to pick me up again. Being small does not mean I want to be picked up, even by someone as cute as Clara. Well\u2026not where anyone can see me. I scolded her lightly, but Clara is button cute so hard to stay mad at.<br /> <br /> Of course Christina and Marlene found my discomfort hilarious.<br /> <br /> With everything done, we split up as several of us had tasks to do. Wolfram and Christina went off to\u2026well the less said the better. Let it pass, Lizette. Alla and Tatiana ventured to speak to this Agrippa. The end result of that was Agrippa is not going to kill anyone over the play, but seemed terribly amused. She\u2026also may not have been being totally honest. She is Connie\u2019s Sire, and I can only wonder how similar they are. I like Connie, but I trust her less even than most vampires. Tatiana got to hang out with her, though, so I am sure she was thrilled. I wonder if Dacian was jealous.<br /> <br /> So, complicated story, a Dr. Nathan Hinshaw and his assistant Dana Barlowe uncovered some unusual relics in Egypt. These relics apparently had a similar techno-magical feel to the Golden Eagle, and were associated with a particular nameless pharaoh. They have come to Paris, invited essentially by the vampire Prince so that some vampire mystics can study them. They have apparently layered traps. Weird, but acceptable. Wolfram contacted the pair, and Dana responded. Wolfram, Marek, and Dacian met with her and she laid out her theories, noted she had been being followed but shook off her pursuers in Rome, and had just recently arrived. She was willing to trade protection for access to the artifacts, and Wolfram rather charmed her, because of course he did. She has been followed there by a German reporter, Greta Hess, who is from money but being a woman does not stand to inherit her fathers business. Greta was apparently also at the museum last night, where Alla and Fenric met her. She even turned up at the museum tonight and was tossed out by Tatiana. Those Germans are always showing up where they are not wanted.<br /> <br /> I know of Miss Barlowe. She has been an unapologetic adventuress for thirty years. She has been paired, romantically and otherwise, with several explorers, and famous and infamous men, and even a few ladies, based on what I hear at the salons. She even has two children. She is the sort of woman I aspire to be. Attractive, dead shot with a gun, brilliant, knowledgeable\u2026 she can even fly a plane. But I bet she can\u2019t build as good a flamethrower automobile attachment as I can, nor build it as fast. Still, a bit of hero worship there on my part.<br /> <br /> So the three of us arrived. Dacian elected to spy through the window because Darkling. Darklings are weird. That left Marek and myself, which given Marek\u2019s stoicism left all the flirting\u2026er talking for me to do. Marek introduced us, and I began asking about her work, using my knowledge from the Order to show I understood the sort of techno-magic they used. She was amused at first, but quickly was impressed. Being me, and in the presence of such a woman (in her nightgown) I started flirting, and she started flirting back! As the conversation went on (and we all had some scotch) I began to consider that I might end up staying the night. Eye contact was more intense, and she has let the gown reveal a leg. I was frankly fine with that. Miss Barlowe is the sort of woman I don\u2019t mind being a bedpost notch for.<br /> <br /> She had been asking leadingly if someone would be \u201cguarding her door\u201d just in case in a voice that was beginning to purr when Marek noted that we needed to be on our way. I was needed to fly the plane back, of course. I can\u2019t say I wasn\u2019t disappointed, but I also knew Marek was right and we could not necessarily trust her yet, however much I hope she turns out to be one of the good guys. Also, that whole flying the plane thing. And, well, the fact I was perhaps a bit too eager to jump in a nice warm bed with someone after watching Christina and Wolfram nuzzling and laughing, and eventually slipping away. Seven more days. Christ I need some Cognac.<br /> <br /> Now I am warmer. How often does one meet cute adventuresses anyway? I am not some kind of slut, right? It\u2019s not an unusual thing, and she smelled good. And smiled a lot, at me, and no I am not going to mope again.<br /> <br /> We met back and I flew us home. Dacian was a bit delayed, presumably making sure he was leaving Dana safe. What a day. I need another drink.<br /> <br /> The<span style=\"font-size:8px\">rumnol</span><br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il was largely absent as her player felt a bit under the weather so went to bed after the first hour or so.<br /> <br /> Greta was fun to play. Every time she was caught, she would point at her (hatless) head and firmly say \u201cpress\u201d, then realize her hat with press tag was not on, and she would go fetch it. She could be a competent and helpful ally on the inside in Germany, or an implacable foe. Clara was also fun to play, as I got to be as adorable as possible with motions I have often seen from silent movies. Note by picked up Lizette meant lifted up not seduced. Clara clashed with cocksure Greta and cunning, capable Dana, but it was deliberate. I wanted to show women of the 20s trying to claim their own place, but not vilify men\u2026which is part of why while Dana was the wiser of the pair, Nathan was still portrayed as intelligent, capable, and far from a buffoon he saw the value in Dana\u2019s wisdom and experience. Nathan wasn\u2019t the stereotype of the man taking credit for what the woman did, even with society trying to press him to. His role was small, but will expand next time.<br /> <br /> Constancia and Alla were joined by partner in mischief Marissa Sangiovanni, who was new to the session but well known to Alla at the start of the story. She wound up feeding on Greta after Fenric distracted her with Majesty. For his part, Prince Etienne made it known Paris would be soon full of cameras and even minor attention from humans would be punished severely. The initial meeting also had the first appearance of Agrippa, but she was not yet known to Alla. It may be worth noting that both Agrippa and Constancia have wine-gold eyes, a trait Maenads in my games have often had. Lizette\u2019s gold eyes are wholly unrelated (but still vaguely bestial)<br /> <br /> Also, poor Fenric did not handle the Werewolf change well.<br /> <br /> Poor Marek missed some overtones. Christina was spooked by the movie but that was\u2026not why she wanted Wolfram back at the hotel. Similarly, Marek did not quite catch how thick the sexual tension between Dana and Lizette got. Note the player got them, but Marek is not good with people. Both Marek and Lizette were unaware Dacian showed at Dana\u2019s door after they left\u2026but Dacian\u2019s evasive comments and describing what he had seen her doing when she thought she was alone shot any seduction attempt rather firmly in the foot. I am\u2026unsure why the player chose to do that.<br /> <br /> As for Harlow \u201cvon Hoddenberg\u201d, he had previously appeared while Alla was hunting in Vienna, though his role was small then, it was to set up for his appearance now.<br /> <br /> Christina has not said she is pregnant, but she has made it clear the Wedding must not get pushed back and is nervous of any delay. She also has referenced having a \u2018good feeling\u201d about her wedding night so\u2026yea she is pregnant.<br /> <br /> On the next off-week, I will be putting up a short handout I wrote on the early 20s, Paris, how groups some PCs belong to (women, LGBTs) were affected, and a supernatural view of the Paris of the Jazz Age. Check it out then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-19-2015, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T03:24:50-08:00","id":784039,"title":"","content":"So, Egyptian relics. I'd think for sure Mummies are due to make an appearance, if they items themselves weren't giving off the God-Machine vibe.<br /> <br /> Dana is &quot;non-aging&quot;? Blue-Book, or something from a main gameline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T12:42:00-08:00","id":784293,"title":"","content":"There will be &quot;A&quot; Mummy, but I don't expect the PCs to interact with them much. Whether they even know the person is a Mummy will depend on if they interact with Wolfram or Alla (Wolfram can just spot dead people, Alla would notice no heartbeat) The big Mummy story comes later <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you are correct about the God Machine vibe.<br /> <br /> As for Dana, that is a bit of a spoiler. You can guess here of course, but if you want to know my answer I will PM what her deal is to you. Your call.<br /> It may come out tonight's session, or it may not come out at all.<br /> <br /> Thanks much for the comments! I love hearing from you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T23:31:23-08:00","id":789132,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week for Golden Eagle, but I remembered I wrote a short thing for the PCs as we got closer to the break to get them thinking about what sort of stuff they would be up to over almost two years. The end result was a (very) general introduction to the 1920s in Europe\u2026nothing too specific, but as I say very very general.<br /> <br /> In covering things I tried to hit groups whose stories were less well known but represented in the group, such as women and LGBTs. I also had a (fictional, of course) brief conversation about \u201ctypes\u201d of supernaturals represented by the PCs.<br /> <br /> And I also lecture a bit. Sorry.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The Roaring 20s have fully hit Europe. Bobbed hair is not unusual, especially in the west. The stereotypical flapper dresses, with less adhering to the body and more leg showing, has caused wigs to be initially flipped and are now all over. Similarly, the (what is now called) \u201cGatsby Look\u201d is popular with the menfolk, as men value \u201cmodern\u201d suits over those before the great war. More than any time previously, there is an intense gap between the old and the young. And the young are on fire.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s not just Fashion. Flappers demand the right to vote, to take whatever job they qualify for. They march in and apply for jobs not specifically listed as being for women and ask men what their problem is. And women\u2019s voting is breaking out everywhere. Germany and the United Kingdom in 1918. Austria allowed it in 1919. Czechoslovakia allowed it in 1920. The Italians haven\u2019t yet but it will clearly be any year now. France and Belgim are nowhere close, and women are hopping mad about that and constantly pushing for it.<br /> <br /> By this time Jazz has exploded into Europe. The popular songs sound very different. It\u2019s a year before the Charleston hit, but dancing, performing, the very done is different. Women move on stage in all sorts of ways. This is less a surprise for the French PCs than for German, Russian or Austrian, but it\u2019s still a major shift. Dearbh\u00e1il likely recalls totally different types of music less than a year ago, but this is what people want to hear. Music has always echoed all over Paris, but never like now.<br /> <br /> Of course, no Prohibition here.<br /> <br /> Women are taking all kinds of advantage of freedom they did not have before the war, and its happening at an astonishing rate. Walking alone on the street won\u2019t likely the questions about where one\u2019s father or husband is\u2026maybe from some old fool, but no one a gal has time for.<br /> <br /> In Europe (unlike America) we are at a high water mark for gay acceptance we would need see the like again of till the 1990s and have not seen over much of the continent since the fall of Rome. Movies, non pornographic ones, are being made in Germany and France discussing stuff like coming out for men or men who become involved with couples, and gay men have their own magazines in the United Kingdom (not Ireland, of course, it\u2019s banned) France, and Germany. Germany and France even have magazines for queer women. Minor queer subplots appear in more mainstream films or stories, which are often not translated to English\u2026.a mysterious siren may have an old female lover she mentions offhandedly, or good friends may be involved with each other. This does not mean there were not vicious attacks on gays and lesbians, but never had it been so publicly acknowledged or discussed, and it would be about 50 years after WWII that it would be again, as Homosexuality is seen as a sign of interest in Communism (in Capitalist nations) and decedent bourgeoisie behavior (in Communist ones). It vanished rapidly in Germany as early as 1933, as did many of the films and books made. But right now, lesbian salons in Paris, gay men\u2019s clubs in many major cities operating with only the mildest of fig leaves, and one can have magazines for living the life. Queer women in Paris are advised to keep a monocle handy; it is a sure signal, even if worn briefly, that one is open to such things.<br /> <br /> While those German movies are being made, there is a much more ambitious films being made. In fact, a lot of people in Paris are talking about a little film that came out last month in Germany and just arrived in Paris: <i>Nosferatu</i>. Can it possibly be as scary as they say? <i>The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari</i> a couple years back made an impression for sure.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the old world collapses. The Struggles you have seen held onto the past this story? It\u2019s failing. Dying. Charles I of Austria, the last monarch of Austria-Hungary who rose when Franz Josef died, was voted as King of Hungary and arrested by the English before he could take power and whisked away to a forgotten island, where he died under mysterious circumstances this month in a shattering blow to many among the Austrian old guard. The last of the Hapsburgs who reigned are gone. It\u2019s only a matter of a short time now till the untimely death of Lothar von Richthofen, the Red Baron\u2019s younger brother and last scion of the family. In Vienna, the left and right and building personal armies that will next year have open warfare to see if Austria becomes a Fascist or Communist state. In Berlin the economy just collapsed. Again. People carry money in wheelbarrows, and prices sometimes triple based on time of day.<br /> <br /> And yet the young dance.<br /> <br /> The old world burns, the new world rises. That which has risen may fall. That which has fallen may rise again.<br /> <br /> Through Kindred eyes, Paris is a stronghold of the Invictus. Unlike Vienna, their hold is not precarious. Prince Etienne has held control of the city for a long time, and it is unlikely to change. The mysterious lineage of Nosferatu called House Machten serve him from the sewers. It seems unlikely he will be removed. Unlike Vienna, all the major Covenants are present and not at war. Lancea et Sanctum are not as strong as Paris, but with the backing of the twisted Sangiovanni line, they manage to hold power even if the heart of the city grows secular. The Carthians began here in Paris, in the Terror, and have never left. The mysterious Emmanuel Baptiste Carth\u2019s identify was never discovered, and he (or she) may still be in Paris. Ordo Dracul and Circle of the Crone operate here as well, as do the mysterious Architects of the Monolith whose leadership is here, as is the Elders of the Duchagne line. The Kindred of Paris do not look back at Rome and the Camarilla. They have surpassed it.<br /> <br /> Paris is Uratha territory, but not held so securely as the Kindred. The Great War saw a great deal of upheaval, and many Uratha perished. Of course, the records say it was fighting the Pure, just as the Pure claim their losses were to Uratha, but all too often it was the same groups fighting each other along national lines. With so many \u201cfires\u201d popping up the Werewolves are busy, and often don\u2019t have time to consolidate. So they are there, but claiming hunting ground is easy. They are quite busy. Of course, the Pure have almost as many problems, and are no closer to seizing Paris than they have ever been, and their infiltrations so often come to naught. And yet they try. And all to often, the young ones want to go dance.<br /> <br /> Paris, like Vienna is held by the Seasonal Courts. It rotates though the cycles according to the pledges. The Spring Court has always been the strongest Court in Paris, short waxing on the parts of the Autumn and Winter recently aside. The Queen of Flowers and Lights is legendary for her beauty and her unusual, stained glass appearance, while the rumors of Autumn Court rites held in the sewers beneath Paris (which too often lead into strange parts of the Hedge and stranger Goblin Markets) keeps the Autumn Court from being too trusted. They seem to like it. Like many others, the Changelings lost many to the war, but they are bouncing back. After all, there is no shortage of people back from the Hedge. A number, however, gone for more than a decade or so have found the changes so jarring they never get their footing back, numbering among the Mad. They are a growing concern to the Freehold.<br /> <br /> In 1913, a Sin-Eater would probably say they don\u2019t have a culture, per se. They have their \u201cfill in the blanks\u201d sort of culture that has existed longer than any remember. However, Sin-Eater culture has had a huge shake up. Never in any record have as many Sin-Eaters appeared of nearly every Threshold as the time of the Great War. Now they embrace the flames of youth as do few others. The old pseudo-Catholic culture of Sin-Eaters being rapidly replaced with the \u201cEvery night is carnival\u201d approach familiar to readers of the <b>Geist </b>rule book. A glass of rum with the dead and celebration of what was never celebrated before. These numbers grow faster and exist in greater amounts than the old guard can find, and many Sin-Eaters have found their way to Paris, and among other things noticed there seem to be an awful lot of vampires here. Some look to form Krewes. Some don\u2019t. Some party. Some kill. In some ways, they are as bad as the ghosts\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to be working out many of the details of these broad strokes and am looking for feedback. What do you want to do? How is your character adapting to the arrival of the jazz age? The settling of the old world into it\u2019s grave? Paris is a place to be. A whirl of arts, of culture, of sensation, shining with a brightness it will take many years to rebuild after the war. Where do you go while you walk to streets of Paris in late April of 1922?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Next week we return to the heroes of the Golden Eagle. Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s players had to miss, with holidays and vacations and such, but we had the rest. The group learns secrets of the Archaeologists, but not enough, and Greta faces the price of her stubbornness, but the results are nothing like expected. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-26-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T01:16:22-08:00","id":792656,"title":"","content":"If you missed it, post above has a lot of background for my 1920s setting, check it out.<br /> <br /> The day of the initial press meeting about the artifacts has come. The PCs help to protect them, even as sinister figures move on he edge of their vision. Seduction and murder change how the game is being played, as irritants become threats and the group finds itself more deeply entangled with the archeologists than intended\u2026and that one of them has more secrets than she lets on becomes very apparent.<br /> <br /> Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s players had to miss due to vacation, so they are not present. They will be back next time.<br /> <i><br /> Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 24 April 1922<br /> <br /> The day started off in an interesting manner. Dana Barlow called to confirm that Lizette and I had met with her last night and that Dacian had been in the vicinity. I confirmed this and she seemed relieved. She then asked if it would be possible for us to come and meet them at the hotel around 1:00pm. I said that would be fine and that we\u2019d meet her there. I told the others and we made the appropriate plans. Most of us were going to meet up with the archaeologists. Dacian and Dearbhail had some fae business to attend to and were not able to join us. <br /> <br /> The rest of us met Nathan and Dana at the hotel at the arranged time and chatted briefly before leaving for the museum. Nathan wanted to make sure that we did not underestimate Dana, and assured us that a good bit of the information that they had on the artifacts was due to her hard work. We said we did not doubt it and he seemed relieved. Dana also confided in us that she does not completely trust their \u201cbenefactors,\u201d (ie the vampires). I do not blame her for that sentiment. The amount of political intrigue that seems to go on with that lot is intimidating.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at the museum we were greeted by Sean, the curator. He seemed to be a friendly enough fellow and showed us the room where the artifacts were displayed. We arranged ourselves into those guarding the archaeologists, those guarding the artifacts and the rest walking the room periodically. Lizette was assigned to watch Dana, Wolfram went with Nathan, Alla watched the artifacts while Tatiana and I walked the room. It was decided that we could respond the quickest to trouble, so if we had free range of the room it would be easier for us to react. We, the pack, had a discussion before the presentation started and the idea was put out there that the individuals who are after the artifacts are the same sort of creatures that were after the Eagle before. We agreed to let the archaeologists know that those that are seeking the relics may be \u201cspecial,\u201d but we were going to leave off the specifics for now.<br /> <br /> So, the presentation went well. Nathan did most of the talking, though he did give credit where credit was due. Too bad most of the audience didn\u2019t really pay attention to that. So, it seems that the relics were found in Egypt in a part of the desert that even the Bedouin do not travel in. They consider the place to be bad luck and avoid it at all costs. Our intrepid archaeologist though walked right into that place and found a structure. It was guarded with booby-traps, but between the two of them they figured out the puzzles to get in. Not all were so lucky, as was attested by the hundred year old corpse they found near the entrance. Apparently even the entrance had a machine like aspect to it that was similar to the artifacts. Once inside they found a secret room that housed the artifacts. Nathan said that there was evidence of a booby-trap, but it seemed to have failed due to age. They dated the artifacts to pre-two hundred B.C. I\u2019m not sure why Dana was so confident on that date, but she was. Nathan went along with her determination. We also found out before the presentation that while the outsides of the relics are stone, there are mechanical looking insides, and that they are warm to the touch. Makes me wonder what is really inside those things and what they do.<br /> <br /> After the lecture was done several people tried to get in to talk to Nathan and a few vied to get Dana\u2019s attention. I let Wolfram and Lizette help deal with the crowds. Tatiana on the other hand followed Greta out and tried to talk some sense into her. I think she tried to explain why investigating the relics so avidly would be a bad idea, especially at night. We hoped that Greta would take the hint and scale back her investigation. Also while they were out Greta spotted some of her father\u2019s men that had been sent to take her back home. She had no interest in doing so, so she ran. She even ran through traffic to stay ahead of the men. Tatiana decided to help and stood in the way of the men coming after Greta. She asked them to stand down and leave Greta alone. They did not listen, so she hit one of them. They decided to stand down. Wise choice.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Lizette, Dana, Nathan and I headed back to the hotel to rest before the evenings viewing. I did not plan on resting, but the others may do as they please. I can tell you that Dana and Lizette were in no way resting. I almost didn\u2019t need my wolf senses to tell you what they were up to. I\u2019m just glad they managed to hold off so long. There were some looks going between those two this afternoon. <br /> <br /> Wolfram took Christina back to the hotel they were staying at. Christina and Marlene both came to the lecture. I was half expecting Christina to stay in her room since she hadn\u2019t been feeling well earlier. I know she claims that it was some bad dressing or some other such nonsense, but I can tell. Her scent has changed and that paired with suddenly having stomach problems means only one thing. She\u2019s pregnant. Propriety says that I can\u2019t say anything about it because of legitimacy issues if the baby is conceived before they\u2019re married. Some sort of political bullshit like that. So, I will hold my tongue and only say something after the wedding. I am happy to see the pack grow though. And it goes without saying that I will keep the child safe. I, along with Tatiana, am uniquely equipped to protect the mother and baby should anything threaten them. Death will come on swift wings to anyone attempting to harm my pack.<br /> <br /> After the \u201crest\u201d Lizette and I escorted Dana and Nathan back to the museum to meet with their benefactors and discuss the relics. The Prince of the Kindred, Etienne, called the different groups that wanted to learn more about the artifacts Fraternities. There were three of them. I believe those that revere the Crone were there along with the Lancea Sanctum and another called Order Dracul, I believe. Tatiana and I continued to walk the room, keeping an eye out for any trouble. <br /> <br /> And trouble came. Agrippa came over to our group and said that they were missing some of the outer guards. We split up. Alla and I patrolled the inner ring to see if someone had gotten past the guards, while Tatiana and Constancia patrolled the outer ring to see if they could find out what happened to the guards. Apparently Tatiana and Constancia arrived to find Greta standing over a skeleton and a badly decomposed corpse while holding a sword. She was also giving off a great deal of smoke, much like Wolfram does when he is wounded. Her clothes are in shreds and there is a great deal of blood on the ground. It seems that Greta tried to get past two of the vampire guards, who reacted perhaps overreached, and killed the young reporter. Unfortunately for the two vampires she didn\u2019t stay dead. She attracted the attention of a spirit, what Wolfram calls a geist, and she got back up fully healed. She then attacked and killed the surprised vampires with the weapon that was used to kill her.<br /> <br /> Tatiana talked Greta down from attacking Constancia and offered the young woman her coat in order to cover herself. She tried to explain to Greta why she would need to keep quiet about things that she is learning in order to keep herself safe. If anything I think Greta was even more determined that she share everything she learns with the public. From what I was told she was almost fanatical about it. While Tatiana was talking to Greta, Constancia went to go get Wolfram so he could talk to the fledgling sin-eater. He came out and started explaining things to Greta but apparently sounded a bit too much like her father so she got fed up, turned into water and fled. Before she left she repeated that there was information to be shared and that she will not be stopped. Tatiana used some of Greta\u2019s blood from the ground to track the foolish girl.<br /> <br /> The rest of us discussed what to do about Greta. Wolfram warned Constancia that Greta can now tell a vampire just by looking at them and may not react in the most friendly manner if confronted again by the same sort of being that initially killed her. It is possible that she may try to kill any kindred she meets, though her main focus so far has seemed to be to expose any and all secrets she learns, including her own. Constancia warned Agrippa and Marissa, I believe, warned the head of the San Giovani clan. At least I\u2019m assuming what they were telling them. Constancia spoke Greek and Marissa spoke Italian.<br /> <br /> After all that we left the museum and headed back towards the hotel I asked Wolfram some questions about sin-eaters and what we could expect out of the newly changed Greta. We discussed whether or not Greta was going to be a problem and if so what we might do about that. I also asked Wolfram to what extent the spirit within him controls him. He said that the spirit can influence a person, but not take direct control. The question is what kind of spirit is influencing Greta? Is it a spirit of vengeance, perhaps drawn to her because of the manner of her death? Is it a curious spirit that wants to know about the world around it? Or is it a spirit of chaos drawn to the girl because of her unwitting desire to cause just that, chaos. Whether she realizes it or not if Greta for example proves to the world that vampires are real there will be a massacre. Vampires will be killing everyone that they perceive as a threat to their well-being and mortals will be doing the same. Perhaps they will kill actual vampires and perhaps they will kill fellow mortals who just happen to prefer nighttime socializing. <br /> <br /> And that is not the only secret she will eventually learn. She already knows about sin-eaters now and can probably tell who they are by sight as well. If she learns about Uratha she may decide that we are more of a threat to humanity than not and reveal our existence to the world. I have already been hunted once by someone bound and determined to kill me, and he had the weapon that very well could have done it. I do not relish the idea of trying to elude multiple would be killers because they don\u2019t like the idea of my kind existing. Unless she can be taught patience and a good bit of common sense then Greta will continue to be a danger to us all. I do not know how hard it would be to permanently kill a sin-eater, but I will find out. If she reveals herself to be a threat to me or mine I will eliminate that threat. If she cannot be brought to heel then she will die.<br /> <br /> Tatiana met up with the rest of us as we arrived at the hotel. She said that she had talked to and calmed down Greta. While this was good to hear I still do not trust the girl. We realized that we needed answers so we decided to just come out with our questions and revelations about what is going on. We all met in Nathan\u2019s room. Dana was wearing a nightgown and carrying a rifle. Her clothing I think was designed to influence people along certain lines. The rifle however was purely practical. It was a Lee-Enfield .303-inch bolt action rifle. Very nice. Good reliable gun. She sat at the window and held the gun casually, but I could tell that she was proficient enough in its use that if she spotted a threat then she could take care of it.<br /> <br /> During this conversation it was revealed that Nathan was the only human in the room. Everyone else is fae, Uratha, sin-eater, kindred or other. Wolfram explained that he was like Greta, which was also explained to the group at large. Tatiana and I remained silent on what we were, which was just fine by me. Dana was asked what sort of individual she is, but she skillfully evaded the question. We still do not know what she is. We do know that she is more than familiar with kindred and did not seem surprised to learn about Wolfram and Greta. It is possible that she is familiar with Uratha, but the topic was never brought up on either side. Nathan, the poor man, was in for a world of revelations. He learned in one night that yes lesbian sex is a real thing, vampires exist and sometimes people can come back from the dead with a spirit along for the ride.<br /> <br /> Towards the end of our talk Dana mentioned that she saw a man a couple blocks away that had been by several times now and seemed to be watching the hotel. That is more than a coincidence and I asked Dana to give me a few minutes to get down to the street before she turned off the light. We weren\u2019t sure what he was going to do as soon as she went to bed. He would either leave or make his way to her room. So, I took the opportunity to follow the man on the street. As soon as Dana\u2019s light went out the man left and I followed. He led me back to a hostel. He was sharing a room with a young man that looked like a student, and for some reason had a lot of shoes. The man I followed made a phone call and spoke to someone in some language close to Arabic, though he did not look Arabic to me. I\u2019m not exactly sure what language it was. Dana had been sure that she and Nathan had been followed when they were in the Middle East. I guess someone decided to follow her here. I will have to keep an eye on him. After I left the hostel I met up with Tatiana and let her know what I found out.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25 April 1922<br /> <br /> We, including Greta, all met for brunch in the hotel. We needed to have a conversation with her once the adrenaline and emotions of last night ran their course. We let Dana take the lead in this conversation for the most part. Wolfram started off by apologizing to Greta for how he acted last night. He did not mean to come across in a controlling way, but wanted to express his desire for her to remain safe. Then Dana explained to Greta that she doesn\u2019t have to promise not to reveal any information, she just has to reveal it in the right way. Anything she reveals that she can prove will bring attention down on Greta. She will become the center of attention which may make it hard to explore anything new. In my opinion it might also paint a target on her back, but Dana was focusing on the positive side of things.<br /> <br /> After Greta left Wolfram also brought up our ideas about the creatures that we encountered on the train. He explained their capabilities and their goals to those who did not already know about them. They seem to be trying to get their hands on the sort of technology that is found in those relics or to at least control who has them. It is possible that they are connected to the people who have been following Dana and Nathan since the Middle East. They can appear to be completely human. We were only able to tell them apart as something different by reading their desires, which don\u2019t quite \u201cfeel\u201d right, or so Dearbhail says. I tend to trust her on such matters.<br /> <br /> Before she left we also gave Greta ways to get in contact with us should she need help or if she just wanted to talk in general. One can only hope that the young reporter took Dana\u2019s words to heart and will be careful about how and when she reveals any information. I would prefer that she not reveal anything, but she is far too young and idealistic to listen to common sense. If she becomes a threat to me and mine then I may have to take action against her. This will not endear me to some of the others, but I will do what I have to in order to protect our growing pack. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What? We are walking around in this human place because we are bored.<br /> <br /> Oh, is that what you mean? We are here at the museum so that Lizette and Wolfram can look at the statues.<br /> <br /> No, yesterday the others looked over the statues. We guarded them, Dana, and Nathan.<br /> <br /> OK, yes, <u>we</u> did not guard them, at least not the whole night. Greta needed us more.<br /> <br /> You like Greta, do you? How surprising - the foolish volchonok is fond of the foolish human pup.<br /> <br /> Hush you. She is foolish. Brave, strong, passionate, it is true. But foolish also.<br /> <br /> I told her not to come at night, that I would help her learn without her needing to sneak.<br /> <br /> I said she was brave, did I not? And a good fighter, though it was too late. It is probably good that she came back to life and killed them. I would not have been pleased with them. Wolfram either.<br /> <br /> Wolfram did mess it up a little, yes, but not on purpose. He did not want her to get hurt, is all. It is just bad luck that he sounded like her father.<br /> <br /> He made a mistake, volchonok, I still trusted him. If he said she should not be alone with this geist, this thing that brought her back, then she should not. It was a good excuse to climb Notre Dame anyway.<br /> <br /> It was a good enough excuse to show my other form as well, yes. I could scarcely say I would help her learn things, and not even tell her what little I know. Between that and my story of punching her father\u2019s man, I believe she was feeling better.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, Marek probably will not be happy. Perhaps it is good that he has business soon. He was beginning to suspect I think. Perhaps I should not have said that about no one being normal at brunch.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, that is not how it work. You are the foolish volchonok, I am Uratha.<br /> <br /> Because I say so.<br /> <br /> It was a good brunch. Dana said to Greta what I was trying to but she said it better than me. Hopefully Greta will stay safer now.<br /> <br /> Yes, hopefully Dana will be safe as well. She is very crafty, that one. We still do not know what she is or does.<br /> <br /> It is true, she is very good at it, whatever it is. She notices many things, knows many things, has seen many things. Plus, she does not balk from giving everyone hospitality. It was not vodka, but still...<br /> <br /> Indeed volchonok, the man, Nathan, is competent for a human. He is a good partner for her, much better at working with a woman who is smarter than him than most men.<br /> <br /> He was very surprised when she said about the vampires, wasn\u2019t he? Hopefully he now knows enough to run, quickly, when we say.<br /> <br /> From what? From whatever it is we fight, foolish volchonok. The mechanical people, the cultists we followed last night, vampires, I do not know.<br /> <br /> Of course we will fight. The storm is coming, as Dana says. Even if they would not let me fight last night, surely it will come to that eventually.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is true, volchonok, it is glorious to run in a storm. But not this storm. Not right now.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 24th April 1922<br /> <br /> Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God. Oh my God.<br /> <br /> I have considered myself a worldly and capable lover for some time, and the praises from Christina and Marlene, and some of the soldiers I dallied with after the armistice, lead me to believe I was some sort of master of sex. I quite frankly did not know anything, apparently. Dana Barlowe is an amazing lover. Nothing, I don\u2019t think, could have prepared me for this afternoon.<br /> <br /> Okay, so we met at the hotel after lunch, after she called to make arrangements and be sure everyone she spoke to last night was on the up and up. We decided I would guard her, Wolfram would guard Nathan, and Marek would guard the statues (Dana\u2019s \u201cDollies.) We arrived and spoke to Sean McMahan, the curator of the science museum\u2026I confess not expecting to see an Irishman running a museum in Paris but whatever. There is certainly a lack of manpower in Paris these days, and I don\u2019t really have a problem with foreigners. He is quite wrapped around Dana\u2019s finger, and gave us all but unlimited access to our area of the museum. He was not crazy about my brandishing the Thompson, but he got over that.<br /> <br /> Dana took me aside to ensure I knew what I was getting into. She is an intense person, and did not want any chance of miscommunication about her intentions. She found me eloquent, highly intelligent, knowledgeable, independent, and interesting, and told me her interest in me was not romantic but not platonic. I was okay with this.<br /> <br /> The viewing and chat went well. Christina was there and looked radiant. She stayed close to Wolfram, which was, of course, how it was going to be. I stuck close to Dana, and tried to focus on keeping watch not giddy anticipation. I mostly succeeded. Some Academic pestered Nathan a bit, but it was not a big problem. Greta showed, but was supposed to be there so not a problem. Tatiana followed her to talk to her. I hope she had more luck than her predecessors.<br /> <br /> During Nathan\u2019s speech we discovered that Dana acquired her map from traders, and Bedouins apparently tried to warn her away from the area, saying it was some sort of forbidden zone. Several people have previously died trying to enter the tomb, and Nathan and Dana worked together to figure out the traps and puzzles. Nathan was open about his role and hers.<br /> <br /> From the moment I felt my heart pounding as the last of the visitors left to the time we got back to the hotel was a blur. I barely heard the door shut before she lifted me to head height against the wall kissing me. I drew her breath into my mouth and returned it. As she kissed my neck and began to lift my shirt, I steadied my legs over her shoulders. Soon enough I was on the bed, at least my head and shoulders were\u2026.<br /> <br /> It was rough. It was carnal. It was glorious. I screamed until I was hoarse, and I don\u2019t remember stopping, only waking up when I heard the shower turn on. It\u2019s off now, so my turn will be next. I really hope my legs actually start to work by that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> 24th April 1922<br /> <br /> Well, tonight took a darker turn.<br /> <br /> Greta Hess was murdered by Vampires when she tried to enter the museum tonight. Unfortunately for her killers, Greta rose from the dead as an enraged Sin-Eater, caught them by surprise, and cut them down. Unfortunately for everyone, Greta is now hell bent on getting the truth of the statuettes, vampires, and everything else out in the open. Wolfram and Tatiana confronted her (and Tatiana got her to spare Constancia, who was present with her and did not help kill Greta) but Wolfram accidentally pushed too many of her buttons and she left in a rage. Fortunately her blood was all over the walls despite the storm, and Tatiana tracked her by it, and even had given her her jacket (Greta\u2019s clothes were in ribbons, apparently). We later found out she discovered Greta at Notre Dame looking out among the gargoyles, and made sure she was disinclined toward violence.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like Greta. She is a spoiled Prussian deminoble rich girl who does not like being told no. But she did not deserve to be murdered and tossed out in the rain. I will help her, to a point, but not if it risks all of us.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the night was uneventful. The Vampires asked Dana more questions and did not dismiss her as often as the daylight meeting\u2019s guests did. They still afforded Nathan a good deal of respect. That said a few too many of them seemed to take particular note of Dana. I hope they don\u2019t intend to try to add her to their number.<br /> <br /> The particulars of the assignment, what with not wanting to allow Nathan or Dana to be injured, limit my options with flamethowers and explosives. I can handle some corpse candles running around screaming from being on fire, but they might catch too, and explosives would be all wrong even if I came back. As would firebombing for that matter. Unless there is a way to selectively firebomb. That could have potential. Maybe make a Goblin Vow of some sort with fire. Maybe that would work.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Where was I? Right. Afterwards we met at the hotel. Dana allowed for a big meeting in Nathan\u2019s room, and arrived in her nightgown with a rifle and a bottle of scotch. Wolfram then set about filling them in. On the Vampires. On Greta\u2019s Murder and Rise. On the significance of the statuettes and their God-Machine connection. Dana pretty much either knew everything or hid that she didn\u2019t, smiling mysteriously most of the time.<br /> <br /> Dana was an enigma. Tatiana then Wolfram tried to call her on her powers. Tatiana mentioned her not aging, and she alluded to a secret known only to her make up mirror, while Wolfram\u2019s asking her about her powers she may have lead to her alluding to a was she was in possession of which apparently messed with the golems, though she did not herself claim to know all it could do. Never did she truly explain herself, and she dodged questions with a rather cocksure attitude, even alluding to not being a virgin when asked about secrets and flaunting her bisexuality to sideline the conversation on a different occasion.<br /> <br /> I was really prepared not to like Nathan, but he is a good guy. Fairly handsome, well spoken, and respects Dana and her intellect. When speaking her gave her a fair amount of credit, and was open about them being a team not him strictly calling the shots. He seems to have something of a crush on her (I am sure all right thinking people do) but maintains respect at all times (I have seen). He was rather unprepared for her supernatural (and sexual) revelations, though, poor guy. I did find I had to concur with Dana there though; he is adorable.<br /> <br /> Dana spotted someone watching the hotel, and when she went to bed Marek and Tatiana shadowed them. We will have brunch with Greta then look at examining these statuettes.<br /> <br /> I worry. Dana says a storm is coming. Tonight was a major thunderstorm, and a woman rose from the dead hungry for revenge\u2026and I am not sure this is even it. What else is going to happen?<br /> <br /> <br /> 25th April 1922<br /> <br /> Dana is amazing. There is no need to say more, except she is the reason I missed breakfast because my legs were not working yet.<br /> <br /> I made it to Brunch, however. The meeting with Greta went as well as I suspect it was going to, with Wolfram and Dana talking her into a measured approach (in practical terms, not feeding her martyr complex) and Tatiana being encouraging. I confess I have softened my view on her a little. She clearly wants to help people, and will sacrifice herself to do so. But as Dana warned with her comment on 1914 Sarajevo, just because you think you are acting for right in a world affecting way does not mean you are. She left with a lot on her mind, and after returning Tatiana\u2019s jacket.<br /> <br /> As for Dana, at one point Greta said \u201cI am no different from you,\u201d to indicate she was not so different from normal people, and pointed at Dana, then seemed to stumble and changed to pointing to me. Confronted directly with someone saying she was not a normal human, Dana just smiled and shrugged. No one called her on it.<br /> <br /> With Greta hopefully not about to cause too much trouble, we go back to the museum to see what the statuettes tell us. And possibly then check out the hostel Marek and Tatiana tracked the agent to. The storm, however, hasn\u2019t broken.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> Near the beginning, Dana commented a storm is coming. The incoming storm built over the session, until it was a downpour that night.<br /> <br /> The description of the location where the statuettes were found was vague. Dana claimed to have gotten a map from a trader, and when they got there there were a number of bodies, all fairly old. The traps and puzzles both Dana and Nathan solved\u2026they both contributed to that. Dana also seemed to know more about the age of the artifacts than she let on. Playing her and dodging questions of what she is/powers she had was great fun. Also at that viewing, Christina observed Lizette\u2019s interactions with Dana, and her smile slowly disappeared. She remained quiet at the end.<br /> <br /> When Tatiana went to look for the guards with Connie, I described the bloody scene and the voice saying \u201cGood, more. I was hoping for more.\u201d and Greta coming around the corner with turn clothing and fog pouring off of her \u201clike a smokestack.\u201d The follow-up scene where Tatiana found her she was crouching, still in the storm, among the gargoyles on Notre Dame. I was proud of my descriptions of those scenes.<br /> <br /> Also, I would be doing Tatiana a disservice (and I don\u2019t want to do that!) if I did not say my plans regarding Greta did change somewhat. I planned on having her circle on the periphery more, rather than sitting down to brunch, but Tatiana made a real effort to bond with her and help her, so I allowed her to make some rolls (willpower was spent) and she convinced Greta to be more cooperative. So right now it looks like that is going to go easier on them than my original plans.<br /> <br /> Marek is obviously working from limited information. The Sangiovanni are not a Clan, but he is not aware of the distinction.<br /> <br /> I was asked (before the questioner knew she was to rise from the dead this episode, obviously) if Greta was intended as a love interest. The answer is most of the characters are potential romantic connections for the PCs. Nathan, Dana, Greta, Harlow, Agrippa, Constancia, Marissa\u2026just about everyone. Tatiana and Dacian both have some interest in Constancia (amusedly, Alla does not really) and I figured Dana there was a reasonable chance would seduce one of the PCs. They are powerful, knowledgeable, and mysterious, and that intrigues her. All the above characters are herosexual as well, though all had their own bents left to their own devices.<br /> <br /> So! The Vampires have a keen interest in these statuettes (the Mekhet especially) and there is a new Sin-Eater stalking the edges, while mysterious figures watch and it turns out more and more that Miss Barlowe has a secret or two. Having fun? We sure are. Marek\u2019s player will have to miss due to holidays, but otherwise should be full group next time. Comments and Questions welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:42:17-08:00","id":797895,"title":"","content":"And caught up. Whew. Between finals and the holidays I have had trouble keeping up.<br /> <br /> Good stuff Baroness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T12:44:10-08:00","id":797924,"title":"","content":"Thanks! glad you enjoyed, good to have you reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T23:28:23-08:00","id":798128,"title":"","content":"It's all very intriguing. I especially wonder who wanted to kill Marek?<br /> Greta's return as a Sin-Eater was very unexpected and a nice complication.<br /> Lizette's love life is endlessly entertaining. I wonder how Christina will react if her relationship with Dana ends up becoming more than casual?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T23:37:29-08:00","id":798130,"title":"","content":"I figured out what's been rattling in my head about Nathan. Is he being dismissed by Lizette?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T01:26:04-08:00","id":798158,"title":"","content":"First thanks to both for questions. I love questions ^_^<br /> <br /> Anteros: The Marek thing is totally from his player. I am working through some ideas.<br /> <br /> Greta I was hoping would be unexpected. She was a complication with just a touch of comedy relief when she appeared, and her sudden murder, and moving up the danger scale, took everyone by surprise. (her Virtue/Vice is Martyr/Defiant) The fun part is what do they do? Tatiana's getting on her good side saved them a world of frustration, and Dacian did not manage to totally turn her off to them. <a href=\"http://media-cache-ec0.pinimg.com/736x/2b/ee/05/2bee05ce1f079fc5a0b703bc1fea141b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Greta, if you are curious</a>.<br /> <br /> As for Lizette, well, yes she is falling for Dana. Part is hero worship, part is just Dana being awesome. As for Christina well, She is an Esterh\u00e1zy, and is not compelled by such emotions. She tells herself that often. She is focused on her marriage, though, which may keep her rage at bay for awhile. <a href=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/1dc5937ef2d6d49a9b591923b9371ad1/tumblr_nh8y92Wz0k1qgrla1o2_1280.png\" target=\"_blank\">Dana 1</a> <a href=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/0f358975e968d1cd6362d720721415a1/tumblr_nh8y92Wz0k1qgrla1o5_1280.png\" target=\"_blank\">Dana 2</a><br /> <br /> I will leave you with a comment from Agrippa on Dana though: \u201c[The PCs] met a woman of uncertain faith and uncertain motives who by means she is evasive about acquired an ancient well hidden/protected set of artifacts, and brought them to a major population center where she plans to use a special wand on them, and maybe you should be more worried about that than you seem to be&quot; So helping one of the good guys or tools of a master villain. GM's take note. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Omenseer: Dismissed? I don\u2019t really think so. She is not romantically interested in him (as men go her only real interest so far is Wolfram) but as an archaeologist and as a person I don\u2019t think she has dismissed him. She is just more fixated on Dana. Unless I am missing something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-02-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:27:20-08:00","id":798267,"title":"","content":"When I say dismissed I don't mean as a romantic interest. I mean as a person or an adult.<br /> <br /> Good point from Agrippa though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T12:26:37-08:00","id":798348,"title":"","content":"Nah Lizette respects Dr. Hinshaw fine. She is just goo goo eyed about Ms. Barlowe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T01:08:42-08:00","id":804291,"title":"","content":"Parties move following agenda\u2019s throughout the city. Alla\u2019s old friend needs her help, and concerns continue to arise with the statuettes. Marek\u2019s player had to miss due to holidays, so no journal for Marek and Marek is unaccounted for.<br /> <br /> I kept the usual order, but you may want to read Lizette\u2019s first to get some context for Tatiana. Marek tends to have the most complete retelling so Lizette and Tatiana both tried to step up their game a little to cover it.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Well, volchonok, I imagine he asked me if I needed a hospital before he asked if I wanted to be his mate because he didn\u2019t want to mate with someone who was injured.<br /> <br /> What? No, we were not at a hospital already, we were at a den for many humans.<br /> <br /> Ah, I see. They were poisoned by their own choice, and only ill of the mind.<br /> <br /> I - yes, I suppose, like with the scotch and the cigars.<br /> <br /> You are correct, volchonok, the woman with the knife smelled something like scotch. And... other things.<br /> <br /> I would have said anger, not sadness, but I was the one spit on, not you. Her mate left her for another.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is why she called me Claudette.<br /> <br /> I do not believe she could hear or smell anything beyond her own noise and stink, volchonok, much less four men and a vampire.<br /> <br /> Truly? No. Since this Emilie was to be Persephone in the play, once I smelled a somewhat familiar woman vampire smell, I was certain it was Agrippa. I did hope someone there might be helpful still.<br /> <br /> ... Yes, the man who wanted to mate with me tried to be helpful, once I convinced him I was neither missionary nor police, and once Dearbhail sobered him up.<br /> <br /> Why do you ask so many questions about this?<br /> <br /> Oh you are ignoring me now? Wolfram did say it was helpful, that it pointed to the Circle of the Crone, if they were looking for not-Christians. I already knew it was Agrippa though. And it was really the other woman, the friend of the fairy, who said she was not Christian.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was not there because he was looking at the statues, remember, volchonok?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know, I wasn\u2019t paying attention. Something about being pieces of something bigger and missing a power source?<br /> <br /> I know, boring. He did say someone removed and replaced the glass to look at them, so Dana has them in a bag.<br /> <br /> You are correct volchonok, it does not make sense. If you can get to them, and want them, why leave them?<br /> <br /> Perhaps. Dana did say they were cursed by the vampires, so perhaps they could see such things as well. Greta said they left someone to watch, so perhaps they want to know more about us.<br /> <br /> Of course you saw Greta, you are sometimes almost as clever as she.<br /> <br /> To follow the people following us. It was they who moved the glass and also they that Marek and I followed last night. So says Greta at least.<br /> <br /> Well, volchonok, hopefully she will tell us.<br /> <br /> We are not following with her because we are to speak with Agrippa.<br /> <br /> No, silly volchonok, our songbird is not to come with. She speaks to her Queen.<br /> <br /> It is like an alpha, yes, but of a time and place, not a pack.<br /> <br /> Because a German fairy Queen is visiting and her house got burned down.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is why Dacian made such strange faces. He was quite displeased.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the fairy at the den of poisoned humans told us. Told Dearbh\u00e1il at least.<br /> <br /> She is friends of the actress. She was quite upset at how disturbed the room had been, what with everything having been strewn all around.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, she does not live in that den. Why is that important?<br /> <br /> No, I would not want to live there.<br /> <br /> Well, for one, I would prefer to go home without walking past a woman painting dead children, or a pair mating under the stairs, or a neighbor who yells about Armand.<br /> <br /> Even as a human, I would rather have lived outside, even in a storm such as this, than in close quarters such as that.<br /> <br /> You are a clever volchonok. No, I do not wish to run off into the night and away from such foolishness. We have a better den, and a job to do. We will run soon enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 25th April 1922<br /> <br /> Today has not been too eventful so far.<br /> <br /> After brunch, we went to the library. Dana noted someone had been in there, but nothing major had happened. She left the glass very slightly out of place and they had moved and replaced it correctly. Wolfram, Dacian and I looked over the Statuettes and all came to the conclusion they interlocked somehow, but we need Dana\u2019s was in order to make more sense of it. That or travel to Egypt. Perhaps they need a power source. My Contracts showed me the face of the one who entered, but not much with more information. Like with the Necklace, it was not someone I knew. We don\u2019t have much solid to go on with, but I have a much better feel for what they may do. And with Wolfram and Dacian looking them over and backing me up, I feel pretty good about it.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of potential in these devices. Just the technology to construct such a thing would be advanced, with different sorts of metals and wiring like I have never seen. We don\u2019t know what they do, but it is likely advanced and outside our idea of what is possible; we have seen the powers of the Eagle. Imagine what could be done with this! Such advanced technology could probably build us some amazing weaponry, such as planes that have all sorts of advanced weapon system and can withstand tremendous speeds, or aereocars, or tanks the likes we have never seen! Such advanced weaponry could be a huge amount of fun to make!<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Of course, super weapons by such advanced technology could be why that technology is no longer around. Too much mayhem?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Alla, Dearbh\u00e1il and Tatiana got involved in a different investigation. It seems like the Persephone from Harlow\u2019s play, a woman named Emilie Barteau, had vanished. Harlow enlisted the aid of the girls to investigate the apartments in the Bohemian part of town she was staying at, and found she was missing, her apartment tossed, though part of it may have been clutter according to Dearbh\u00e1il. I am given to understand her neighbors were eccentric. Tatiana was fairly sure Agrippa had been there, though the scent was faint, which I can only assume made Dearbh\u00e1il even more paranoid.<br /> <br /> They were stopped by Lucille Nadeau, a girl who prowls the Salons often for ladies, and Th\u00e9r\u00e8se, a local Spring Courtier. They were there to pick Emilie up for Salon. Lucille apparently dropped giant hints that Emilie was pagan, which is unfortunate, and that the people who were looking for her were asking about non-Christians, though I am given to understand that is a bit of a problem in the Bohemian districts right now so Emilie was surely not the only one. Still, Alla and Tatiana plan to speak to Agrippa later, and it will be dealt with.<br /> <br /> Also, Skadi, the Winter Queen from Berlin is in town, and had the rooms she was staying at set aflame. Fire is effective. She escaped, but must have been upset. She has been relocated. I knew the Winter Queen was in town, but I don\u2019t have time or a mind for politics so did not care. I know some good Germans, so I am less biased against her than some of my countrymen understandably are. Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian will be checking with the Spring Queen tonight. They intend to help her, which makes sense. I will back them up as I can.<br /> <br /> But I am getting ahead of myself. We all met after working at the museum and investigating the apartments, and took Nathan and Dana out to eat. Dana has started doting on me, patting my head and scratching my hair behind my ear. She and I often make eye contact and smile, and that is getting more frequent. Dana was up front that ours was not romantic, but would friendly, physical, and need not end after a single encounter. That is certainly true, as Dana has been flirty and promised to continue our liaison in private tonight. But I worry that one, or both, of us may have fallen for the other. Dana is not a woman given to long-term relationships, she has made that very clear twice now. But how will we be walking away from this? As friends? Intimate friends? Am I too close to the\u2026events\u2026with Christina to really let myself honestly do this? Would someone like Clara be better for me? All the time in the workshop does not help me know how to handle this. I must think.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, dinner. So we hashed out a general plan at Dinner. Wolfram and I would stay with Nathan and Dana to guard the statuettes. Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il will be talking to the Queen and Tatiana and Alla Agrippa as I say. Greta was lurking hidden at the restaurant, so Wolfram approached her, but she was actually lying in wait for our pursuers. She had seen the ones breaking into the museum, and ambushed the guard they left. They are operating under orders and not staying in the same place. A \u201cmaster\u201d of some sort is coming, hence their scouting. She does not know what they are up to, but plans to try to get more information. She agreed to share. Her conversation with Wolfram seemed more civil than the one in the rain I understand.<br /> <br /> Back at the hotel, Dana explained to Wolfram, Tatiana and I about her plan with her was. A package from her, in a box the rectangular shape for a was, will be coming from London. This is a decoy. A package for a Ms. Boyles will be coming from Cardiff, which was square shaped and has the actual was. She expects them in 48 hours, give or take a day. Is it any wonder I hero worship her a little? I hope to be as capable as her someday. I digress; tomorrow she does research, and in the meantime is the waiting game, at least for this project. Tatiana left with Alla, so we are left here to talk.<br /> <br /> The rain is continuing; the storm Dana predicted has not passed. It is good to be inside with a lovely lady. And Wolfram. Stay on task, brain\u2026we have a lot ahead of us.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XX</i><br /> <br /> Man I had fun with the apartment complex. I had a wide range of encounters ready, and Tatiana mentioned most of them in her journal. The woman painting dead children droning happily on about how \u201call children die\u201d eventually leading to her miscarriages having people to play with was especially disturbing, and after meeting the woman calling Tatiana Claudette and screaming about Armand I kinda think they just wanted to turn rocks over and see what kind of people they found. There was also high guitar guy, but he was less colorful.<br /> <br /> Tatiana detected a vampire, but vampires have lighter harder to follow scents, so it was hard to say who, and the storm did well for obliterating scents.<br /> <br /> We have hit on most plots now, the Statuettes, the Play, the visiting Queen\u2026only took three sessions, right? I don\u2019t expect this story to take as long as Vienna (that got extended by about 2-3 extra sessions by circumstance) but still should be fun.<br /> <br /> Not covered was the meeting with the Queen of Flowers and Lights. Any idea where I can get a good picture of a woman who appears to be made of stained glass? Basically they got more info about how she had been in the chateau commonly used by the four monarchs for guests, that someone had broken into the room while she was asleep, and left accelerant there, but did not harm her. They were waiting for Court to finish so they could accompany the Queen to speak to her at the Queen\u2019s home. With any luck we will get a Dacian next time to cover that.<br /> <br /> Oddly ominous/tragic lines included the Queen of Flowers and Lights speculating that in a couple decades everyone will associate Berlin with music, theater, and cinema, and that she would not see Germany as a military power again in her lifetime.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Full crew for the next one, where we spend much time on the missing actress and burned room. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-09-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:53:26-08:00","id":804367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=804291#post804291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not covered was the meeting with the Queen of Flowers and Lights. Any idea where I can get a good picture of a woman who appears to be made of stained glass?</div> </div> </div> </div>Google Image Search? Depending on the skill, stained glass can look fairly accurate/lifelike. Maybe have the lines and joints darker and obvious, like the seams connecting the glass together? I'm assuming there needs to be flowers featured too?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:27:49-08:00","id":804616,"title":"","content":"I am working on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just did not know if anyone had one they knew of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:39:30-08:00","id":804624,"title":"","content":"Lizz putting the words too, much, and mayhem together in that order must be hard for her to compute &quot;I know you are saying words, but I do not understand.&quot; Like when someone once told me I had bought too much ice tea for a convention trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:44:37-08:00","id":804628,"title":"","content":"First and foremost they are wrong, there is never too much ice tea.<br /> <br /> Well Liz is kinda speculating there. I mean, hypothetically it is possible, but nah, probably not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:28:50-08:00","id":804890,"title":"","content":"I know right? On both counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:03:20-08:00","id":815060,"title":"","content":"A casual word from a Vampire and distrust begins to spread between the Conspiracy and the Archaeologists they are there to guard. Meanwhile there is an actress to find, and a queen that needs help.<br /> <br /> I recap what is going on after the session journals in simple terms. It has session 21 spoilers, but if things are convoluted for you it may help.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 April 1922<br /> <br /> Yesterday seemed to be the day that just wouldn\u2019t end. I left the pack for a short time to talk to a messenger sent by Jamal. I had to meet him outside of Paris since he could not be seen there for various reasons. I didn\u2019t ask. It doesn\u2019t really matter anyway. Turns out I ran all that way just to find out that Jamal did not have any new information on my would be assassin, but he was still looking into it for me. I thanked the man for his time and we went our separate ways.<br /> <br /> Some of us, Tatiana, Alla and I, went to talk to Agrippa to talk to her about the missing actress. There was some concern that she might have taken offense at something in the play and encouraged the young lady to leave. We did find out some information so the trip was not wasted. Agrippa also expressed her concerns about Dana and activating the artifacts. She pointed out that we know next to nothing about the archaeologist and what hints we do have just paint her in a more ambiguous light. All valid points in my opinion.<br /> <br /> After that we came back to the hotel to talk to Wolfram, Lizette, Nathan and Dana. We mentioned Agrippa\u2019s concern that Dana wants to activate the artifacts in a populated city without first knowing what the artifacts do. They could be destructive. We don\u2019t know. We proposed using the W\u0101s outside of Paris at our Chateau. It is a safe location and deliberately far away from other people. Dana wasn\u2019t keen on that idea. She said that it would put her at a disadvantage. I would have preferred to be able to tell her to live with it, but I had to speak on the behalf of the pack, not just myself. It was then suggested that Nathan rent a cottage outside of Paris. It would be neutral ground and we would provide the security.<br /> <br /> I believe that Dana\u2019s W\u0101s was being shipped to a nearby place and a another more \u201cW\u0101s-shaped\u201d package was being delivered to the hotel. The actual W\u0101s will be in the non-descript package though. Seemed like a decent security measure to take when you are being watched. Here\u2019s hoping that it actually works.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Dacian and Dearbhail went to go meet with the German Winter Queen, Skadi. The purpose of their visit was to offer their assistance in promoting her message of peace and goodwill between Nations and Courts. After the war there are still hard feelings between some nations. I can understand that. Before I became a courier I was not overly fond of Germans, but after working with several over the year I lost the blinders that the war put in place and discovered that they were just people living their lives.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail and Dacian also discussed the security for Skadi since the fire. From what they said the fire was set from inside the room while Skadi was asleep. An accelerant was used to light the fire and she was kept asleep by some sort of Fae magic while they did so. They then allowed her to wake up once the fire was lit. So, it is likely that they were not out to kill her, they just wanted to scare her. If they wanted her dead then they would have done it while in her room as she slept and used the fire to cover up the evidence of murder.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail apparently was rather adamant that Skadi have a guard and offered Dacian\u2019s services as a bodyguard/knight to keep watch over her. I\u2019m sure that conversation was amusing to watch. When Dearbhail gets an idea in her head she usually finds some way to make it happen. And this time it sounded like most of what happened was her idea and Dacian got caught up in it. Not that I think he opposed the idea too strenuously, but I\u2019ll bet it was still amusing to watch.<br /> <br /> Now to look for our missing actress.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> Very early this morning we started our search for the missing actress. Unfortunately for us the weather did not cooperate and it was rainy and somewhat miserable out. That storm that Dana was talking about before seems to have found us, literally. So, Tatiana, Alla, Connie and I started looking the last place she\u2019d been seen \u201cgetting out\u201d of a car. More like jumping out of a moving car. It was near a Cathedral called Sacr\u00e9-Coeur. As soon as we pulled over and stepped out of the car I felt like we were being watched. Tatiana and I exchanged looks and I nodded. I slipped into the shadows and crept toward the Cathedral so I could get a good vantage point and see if I could find our watcher. I climbed to the top most point, even went outside, and the whole time the feeling persisted. It followed me the whole way. Once at the top I looked around but did not see anyone. Discouraged I crept back down to the main part of the church and met up with the others. I told them what I\u2019d discovered, or the lack thereof. While I\u2019d been looking upstairs Tatiana had tracked Emilie sent to a certain pew, where it appears that she slept, but left again.<br /> <br /> As we left the area Tatiana used a gift to see if what we\u2019d sensed was supernatural or not. Turns out that it was. It was some power that affected the whole area and we could actually feel it when we left the area of influence. It was rather disconcerting if you ask me. Tatiana said that the energy felt necrotic and emotional at the same time. Necrotic makes me think of Vampires but I don\u2019t know if something like this is within their purview. I\u2019ll have to ask Alla and see if she knows. The only other supernatural entity that might give off death energy might be Sin-Eaters. Wolfram for example actually died and came back, joined with a spirit. The same happened to Greta. They can see and interact with any ghosts that they see as well. I will have to ask Wolfram if his kind have any powers that can affect a whole area rather than just an individual.<br /> <br /> After the search at the Cathedral turned up nothing of import we decided to go back to the actress\u2019s apartment and see if anything new could be discovered. As it would have it, not much. A drunk woman in the hall had not seen Emilie and her apartment had not been returned to. Her scent there was not fresh. Our next option was to talk to Lucille and Terese, two of Emilie\u2019s friends and see if they have seen the wayward actress.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> After some time to rest, the pack met up with Connie, Dana and Nathan to discuss all that we\u2019d been up to the past day and anything that we\u2019d discovered. Wolfram confirmed that the power we described at the cathedral can be utilized by someone of his kind with the correct gifts. We also agreed that it would be a good idea for us to meet with Skadi and see if there was anything further that we could do. Dearbhail had offered our packs services to the Lady and it seemed only appropriate that we meet with her. When the idea was brought up Dana was very keen on going to the meeting. I\u2019m not sure why. Perhaps she has not had an opportunity to socialize with a large group of Fae, or perhaps it\u2019s the idea of meeting Fae royalty. Though Dana does not seem to be the type to be awed by the idea of meeting someone of noble birth. She seems rather accustomed to dealing with all manner of folks regardless of status. It is probably just curiosity but I will keep an eye on her.<br /> <br /> After some time Alla received a phone call from Harlow, the man that is putting on the play that she is in and that is missing an actress. He said that the theater had been ransacked and that several scripts and such were missing. Alla\u2019s theory was that it was the four men that had followed Emilie. Perhaps they don\u2019t like the revisions that Harlow made to the story. He found the book that he got the story from in Greece, so it might be too close to a truth that someone wants kept quiet. So, Harlow asked Alla what he should do. Her suggestion was that he take the copy of the script and the original book to an occultist to make sure that there weren\u2019t actually any hidden spells in the text. She recommended Wolfram and had Fenric arrange a meeting for later afternoon/early evening. Harlow also asked if Wolfram could look into the break-in at the theater.<br /> <br /> My guess is that Harlow came across something that he shouldn\u2019t have and decided to share what he found in the most public way possible. Someone obviously doesn\u2019t want this to get out and is taking measures to scare off actresses and get rid of the means to perform the play altogether. So far they have elected to not use more lethal means to make sure this play is not performed, which is probably for the best. I guess we\u2019ll see what the future holds on that front.<br /> <br /> Later that afternoon we as a pack went to meet with Queen Skadi and the Queen of Flowers and Light. I believe she is the Spring Court monarch. Somewhat disturbingly one of the other Fae there, someone aptly named Mrs. Skitters, asked my Fae pack mates if she could have their faces after they died. They all said \u201cNo.\u201d Just a little disturbing if you ask me.<br /> <br /> During this meeting the Therese mentioned that something had happened during a recent Salon. Apparently a woman was there that was dead, but walking around and dropping bits of herself as she went. Sounded rather disturbing, and supernatural. I\u2019m not sure if my pack is going to look into it or not. I think it might be a good idea. After that Dacian introduced the rest of us to Queen Skadi, who was appreciative of our willingness to help her and to keep her safe.<br /> <br /> Tatiana went to talk to Terese who mentioned that someone named Lucille might be better able to help us find the missing actress. As we left to find this Lucille Dacian took us aside and mentioned that a note had been slipped into his pocket by Mrs. Skitteres that we must be careful what we tell Terese and that she doesn\u2019t trust her motives. Apparently there is intrigue wherever we go lately.<br /> <br /> As the day went on Wolfram had a talk with Lizette about her relationship with Dana. He did not seem happy that she was falling head over heels in love with the archaeologist at all. I warned Lizette a little while ago that she was getting too close to the woman, but she did not listen. Maybe she will listen to Wolfram if she will not hear me.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Wolfram, he had an enlightening talk with Harlow on the phone. They spoke of meeting to go over the script and any possible occult information. While they were talking Wolfram noticed that Harlow\u2019s German accent was put on. The man is not actually German. Granted he is an actor so one would assume that he could adopt an accent if he wanted to. Alla also confirmed that Harlow initially did not know that Wolfram was a man\u2019s name. So the question remains, why is he pretending to be German? What does he gain from it? Makes me wonder if he\u2019s hiding from someone or something. I will have to ask Alla if she has always known him as a \u201cGerman\u201d and if so how long she\u2019s known him. All that combined with the stolen scripts and the missing actress, it seems like we have more questions than we do answers. Time to get some answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Hello volchonok. Do I tick?<br /> <br /> No, we have not found the actress. And she is not Persephone, she is pretending to be Persephone. And worships her, I think.<br /> <br /> What? No, volchonok, we will not be declaring Siskur-Da. She is not so important. What is important is whether you can hear me ticking.<br /> <br /> I hunt for her because there is nothing better to do. I could read plays, I suppose, to see if there is a magic spell in them. Or stand still guarding statues. Or talk politely with Queens. Or stand around guarding Dana, or Skadi, or whoever we are guarding now.<br /> <br /> Yes, I suppose I could have spent time with Constancia. But Alla had asked for the favor, and was right there. If I\u2019d known she just wanted me to sniff around the house again, I would have just gone with Constancia. It\u2019s not like I could follow Emilie from the place in this damn rain.<br /> <br /> It is a different sort of biting. Alla\u2019s women seem to like it.<br /> <br /> It is not your concern, impertinent volchonok, whether Elena would like it.<br /> <br /> Or whether she would like me to like it! Volchonok, focus. Do you hear Lizette ticking?<br /> <br /> Because Dana heard her ticking. It is how she knows we are tied to the Golden Eagle.<br /> <br /> No, Lizette did not tell her, for all that she is besotted.<br /> <br /> I do not know, volchonok, I do not know what she is or how she knows these things.<br /> <br /> No, I do not care. I mean, I would not have her watch my back, but it is us who are watching hers, yes? This makes her nervous now, Lizette says. I do not distrust her though. After all, it is not as if Agrippa is so trustworthy herself. Bah. It is a question for the others to answer. I will stay alert and not allow harm to come to my pack. And if they say we should protect Dana, I will do so.<br /> <br /> It certainly makes it easier that she has come along with us. But no, Dana has come along in order to meet a fairy queen.<br /> <br /> Yes, the stained glass woman. And a woman made of snow.<br /> <br /> Yes, foolish volchonok, they are both beautiful. But the glass woman is far too fragile for me, and Dearbh\u00e1il has declared that the snow woman is for Dacian.<br /> <br /> She has decided he should be her protector and lover. I do not know how that works, but she is quite firm when she wishes. She said she would cut off Dana\u2019s legs if she hurt Lizette. I do not know how, but I believe she would try very hard.<br /> <br /> We will probably protect this snow woman too, perhaps try to find out who it is that set her house on fire. They were very sneaky, so probably a fairy like Dacian.<br /> <br /> Exactly. Dearbh\u00e1il made a good decision to have him guard. A thief is best to catch a thief. Especially since this Skadi does not want a big fuss, Dacian is very discrete.<br /> <br /> No, silly volchonok, it was not an invisible fairy watching at the cathedral that Emilie slept at. It was probably someone like Wolfram, or perhaps a vampire. It was magic and it smelled like death.<br /> <br /> I do not know. Perhaps we will know when we find Emilie. It is more questions to ask, at least.<br /> <br /> Do you question me, little volchonok? The only question I needed to have for Th\u00e9r\u00e8se was if Emilie had friends. If Lucille is the better one to ask, so be it.<br /> <br /> I do not care about a walking dead woman at one of Lizette\u2019s boring salons. If she wished to speak to Lizette of it, then again, so be it.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I did listen. Perhaps it would have been about Lucille, or Emilie.<br /> <br /> You are sure I do not tick?<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I would feel better if we were to run. To get out of this city and these politics and motivations and games and such things. But there are things to do, and a pack to protect. And perhaps, in the end, there will be some proper hunting, once this storm has lifted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 26th April 1922<br /> <br /> I feel a sense of disquiet. Last night Marek, Tatiana and Alla returned from speaking to Agrippa about the missing actress. While she did have some information, she also challenged us about Dana. She noted she was a woman of uncertain motives, uncertain faith, uncertain origin and powers, who through means she was evasive about acquired some sort of powerful technology and brought it to a population center to use her wand on for an effect she never defined. This is uncomfortably true. Now, she was angry Dana took the relics away, but felt some sort of ritual could be done if they were not observed. None of those were untrue.<br /> <br /> Dana once again neither denied nor confirmed anything. Well, almost. She said she had no plans to cause major destruction to the population center. She was otherwise rather cavalier, noting we had not told her about the Golden Eagle (which had been unmentioned until now) but said she \u201cheard the ticking\u201d from me when we were close. She did not elaborate. Wolfram agreed we did not tell everything. Dana did not push us for more information, she simply noted \u201cGood Secrets make good neighbors\u201d and whispered to me she figured I liked mystique. She also stressed that she does not know precisely what the statuettes do. She did not expect anything catastrophic, though.<br /> <br /> We argued a bit, but agreed perhaps to test the was somewhere away from the city. The Ch\u00e2teau was mentioned, but she rather surprisingly noted she was uncomfortable with being so vulnerable, and that she did not entirely know our motives. We had, after all, collected the Eagle. I think she drove a harder bargain than needed, and made a big show of compromise.<br /> <br /> We retired, and Dana wasted little time seducing me, and outdid even her previous performances. I was rather content, until she quietly asked me to please be on her side as much as possible; she was concerned the others were being turned against her by vampiric manipulation and wanted to feel that she could count on me. She said she trusted me as much as she does anyone if not more, and said she would not betray me if I did not betray her. We had a pledge, after all. I am unsettled; she seemed a bit spooked by Agrippa\u2019s move. I love her. Do I trust her?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think I do.<br /> <br /> We had a late breakfast to discuss things with the other fae. Alla, Tatiana, and Marek had not discovered Emilie (the actress) during the night, though they know she visited Sacr\u00e9-C\u0153ur, the new Cathedral out at the neighborhood she lived in Montmartre. The Spring Courtiers met Queen Skadi, and Dearbh\u00e1il apparently felt Dacian was insufficiently forward. I have trouble imagining that. He is usually happy to leer at women or tell them he was spying on them when they thought they were alone. Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian decided to come back today with the rest of us. It seems a good idea. Apparently she is meeting Ms. Skitters before us. I don\u2019t think we can make a worse impression than that Darkling does.<br /> <br /> I was very surprised Dana wanted to go. Nathan (wisely) had reservations about faerie gatherings, but Dana suggested in life we must seize the opportunities, so long as we are not going in the Hedge\u2026something I had warned her about, but I suspect also many a tale had made her cautious. She went up to get changed, so I confessed my concerns to Wolfram. Wolfram seemed unconcerned about whether she was trustworthy, but was worried I was falling for her. Which is true, I am. I was not sure what to tell him. Eventually I followed Dana up. When she is done getting ready, I will tell her about my feelings, and see how she feels.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26th, April 1922<br /> <br /> Dana told me in no uncertain terms not to fall for her. Again.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26th April 1922<br /> <br /> We met the Queen of Flowers and Lights, Queen Skadi, Th\u00e9r\u00e8se, and Mrs. Skitters. Mrs. Skitters was herself, but passed Dacian a note to be wary of Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. I really don\u2019t know Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. I have seen her at Salon and maybe once at a social event for the Kind.<br /> <br /> We had light conversation. Dacian made clear his desire to deal with the \u201crudeness\u201d shown to her. Skadi was, I think, even handed in her comments; we have ample reason to hate each other. I do not hate her, specifically, perhaps only due to Wolfram, Christina, and Marlene. I understand why some people would, as does she, I am sure she has fed on many Sorrows whose ultimate origins hail from France, just as the Germans have brought Sorrow and Fear here. She was asleep at the time, despite pouring of accelerant, which suggests Darkling work. They did allow her to wake, suggesting more interest in terror than murder. It smacks of the Court of Fear to me. We are about to go investigate.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there was some woman who was rotting and fell apart at the Salon, according to Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. I should contact Clara and make sure she is okay.<br /> <br /> But I can\u2019t stop thinking about Dana. She stayed at my side but was\u2026well for Dana, very muted. She did not talk at all. Rather, she stayed near me, and kept some contact, but did not at any point scratch my ear. Nathan stayed quiet, but I suspect that was his wisdom again. We Faerie are capricious.<br /> <br /> Dana did not say if she loved me or not. Just forbade me from falling for her, and reminded me almost harshly we talked about this before we spent our first time together. Maybe she loves me and is upset because she does not like her feelings. Or maybe I have made a huge mistake. Maybe she has some big nefarious plan I am inadvertently helping her carry out. Maybe I am betraying my city. Maybe for Dana I don\u2019t even care. What does that say about me?<br /> <br /> God, this storm. It reflects my emotions too well. I could really use some Mayhem about now.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> Things may be getting convoluted. To summarize:<br /> <br /> Plot 1) Dr. Nathan Hinshaw and Dana Barlowe brought statuettes from Egypt they found using information Dana got from a mysterious source. The Vampires took an interest, especially the Lancea et Sanctum, Circle of the Crone, and Ordo Dracul. Agrippa, sire of Constancia, Princess of Evil is the Circle of the Crone representative studying it. They discovered Dana has been shadowed by cultists who arrived in town, and the reporter Greta Hess was killed investigating, and rose as a Sin-Eater. Meanwhile, Lizette fell in love with Dana on the rebound from her dealing with Christina Esterh\u00e1zy\u2019s upcoming wedding to Wolfram on the 1st of May. Which complicates things, as Agrippa noted Dana\u2019s background is mysterious and she is evasive, and no one really knows much about her, her powers, or her goals. Agrippa is also linked to\u2026<br /> <br /> Plot 2) Harlow von Hoddenberg is putting on a play based on a book on Greek Mystery Religions. Alla is to be in it as Agrippa, the same figure the Vampiric Agrippa claims to be, a powerful Maenad. Emilie Barteau, who plays Persephone, has gone missing, and it is clear Agrippa as well as a cult of unknown intent is interested. Agrippa claims she rescued Emilie from the Cult, but Emilie fled. It appears after talking to everyone, including a Fairest named Th\u00e9r\u00e8se and a young woman named Lucille Nadeau, that Emilie is part of a mystery cult, but a Dionysian one (like Agrippa) not an Orphean one, and she may have made alterations to the play from a more Orphean approach it originally had. Recently the Theater was broken into and copies of the play stolen, and it looks like either Emilie is a Sin-Eater or one is who is also hunting her. Also, some sort of zombie showed up at the Salon Lucille and Emilie attend. Adding to the chaos, Th\u00e9r\u00e8se is linked to\u2026<br /> <br /> Plot 3) Queen Skadi, Elemental Winter Queen of Berlin, arrived on a quiet mission to encourage Pledges between once enemy Freeholds, being welcomed by Spring Queen and the Autumn King. The Fairest Queen of Flowers and Lights put her up at a guest house controlled by the Freehold, but a fire broke out and she barely escaped. There was Speculation Fae magic kept her asleep for its starting and was removed. Dearbh\u00e1il declared Dacian would protect her, and was the investigator for Spring while Autumn assigned Mrs. Skitters, an odd Darkling, to help. Other than the Monarchs, only Th\u00e9r\u00e8se of Spring and the Beast Jean-Jacques of Autumn knew she was coming. Allegedly. Mrs. Skitters subtly clued in her counterpart that she did not trust Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. But then, she asked for people\u2019s faces. And all this is going on while some people are worried about\u2026<br /> <br /> Plot 4) Wolfram and Christina are getting married in less than a week. Lizette has thrown herself into a relationship to escape her own heartache, while Wolfram works to ensure everything is just so, and that angry reporters, mysterious archaeologists, missing actresses, faerie nobility, and a sinister storm does not bring it all crashing down.<br /> <br /> Simple, right?<br /> <br /> Further Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-23-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T00:44:50-08:00","id":824863,"title":"","content":"Our heroes investigate the attack on the Winter Queen of Berlin, and discover an old flame of Dana Barlowe\u2019s at the hotel. Greta unexpectedly provides a lead on Emelie\u2019s disappearance, Tatiana and Lizette interview Lucille, and Dana confronts Agrippa with Alla and Marek in tow. It all ends at the theater, where a trail stops and a hunt begins.<br /> <br /> This session was moved due to snow, and Wolfram\u2019s player was unable to attend. It was assumed he was seeing to wedding plans.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 April 1922<br /> <br /> We have appointed ourselves the investigative team for a variety of problems it seems. This time we went to the townhouse that Skadi was staying at to examine the crime scene and see if we could pick up any clues that the Fae could not. We arrived and were greeted at the front door by a woman named Madeline. She seemed to be the woman in charge of guests and their needs, and welcomed us warmly. There were some more pleasantries and before they were done Tatiana started off in the direction of the burned room. I was about to follow when Dearbhail and Dacian stopped her and chastised Tatiana. They told her that we needed to observe the pleasantries. I did not think that the inconsequential things that they spoke of were all that important, but I stood my ground and waited along with my pack mate.<br /> <br /> Eventually we were allowed to go to the room that Skadi had been staying in. Madeline escorted us there. Dacian asked Skadi about what happened and she recounted the events of that night for us. She said that she\u2019d been asleep and was woken by the smell of smoke and the heat from the fire. During our investigation we found that an accelerant had been used in front of the door and wall, and in a semi-circle around the bed. It was specifically set so she could not get out through the door, but that the window was an option. Both windows were unlocked, though Skadi herself remembers them being locked that night before she went to sleep. It appears that the arsonist specifically left the German Winter Queen a way out.<br /> <br /> Of the two ways into the room the window would have been the quickest and quietest way, so Tatiana and I focused our senses there and unfortunately came up with nothing. There is, unfortunately for us, a Fae power that covers up ones tracks and scents so they cannot be followed. It seems that whoever set the fire had this ability. It definitely makes things harder for us.<br /> <br /> We were also introduced to someone from the Autumn Court named Jean-Jacques. He seemed curious about our investigation and admitted that he knew about Skadi\u2019s arrival and identity beforehand. He apparently helped to escort Skadi to the house, though he said that he was not the only one. He revealed that Terese also knew who the Winter Queen was and when she was arriving.<br /> <br /> Madeline has been in the process of setting up a new room for Skadi to stay in. Before we entered Dacian checked to see how good the locks were and how the room was set up for ways in and out. He determined that the lock on the door was good and the windows locked as well. Overall it was very much like the old room. Even the floor plan was pretty much identical.<br /> <br /> It is obvious that someone in the city does not want Skadi there, whether it is because of her nationality or because of what she wants to do remains in question. There are plenty of people here that would not appreciate a German woman trying to set up an alliance. There is also apparently a whole Court of folks, the Winter Court, that rely on sadness and despair and if peace is made with the German Courts then that level of sadness goes down. After the war there are a lot of places where people are still upset or angry about the war and its aftereffects. I guess time will tell if the person(s) that want Skadi to leave take offense at her message or her nationality.<br /> <br /> Dacian came up with the idea that we leave someone in the room as a decoy while we hide Skadi away somewhere more secure. That way she will not be in real danger if someone decides to scare her out of the new room. I believe that the idea was to leave Alla there as the decoy since she has practice playing roles and she is tall enough to pass as Skadi. I do not think that this plan was set in stone though. It was merely brought up and discussed in a short time. We may have to revisit this idea later tonight and see if it is feasible.<br /> <br /> After that the lot of us went back to the hotel to check on messages and to get the phone number for Lucille. As it turns out there was a message at the desk for Dana. After she read it she turned her back on the clerk pulled her gun, checked it and put it back. That piqued the interested of all those present. So we walked a ways off so we could talk privately and she told us that an old friend was waiting for her upstairs. Given her reaction I got the impression that she was not on the friendliest of terms with this person. Several people, including Lizette, offered to go up to the room with her but she turned them all down. After some persuasion that she needed to take someone she asked me if I would accompany her upstairs to meet this old \u201cfriend.\u201d I said I would and asked if this old friend should be considered a threat or not. Dana asked what I would do if they were and I answered her. She admitted that she might need to get information from her acquaintance so I said that I would leave them alive should they attempt anything. She told me to play along with whatever she did. I agreed.<br /> <br /> Turns out that her old \u201cfriend\u201d is a woman named Iris DeVeers. Dana knows that this is not the woman\u2019s actual name but didn\u2019t know her real one. I supposed it doesn\u2019t matter unless the woman becomes a threat. They greeted each other cordially enough, but there was a distinct tension in the air. I do not think that Iris was expecting anyone else to come with the archaeologist if the champagne was any indication. Dana said that she was in town with Nathan which kind of implied that I was him. Then they started going back and forth about Iris having stolen the W\u0101s and Dana\u2019s room being ransacked by cultists looking for the same instrument that Iris had already stolen. Iris claimed she took it to protect it from the cultists. It was all smiles and very flirty, but I don\u2019t think Dana believed her in the slightest. Eventually Dana got fed up with Iris being cagey. She sweet-talked Iris into turning around to help her undo her dress, then pulled her gun and put it to the other woman\u2019s head. Iris quieted immediately and put on a hurt look. I don\u2019t think was actually afraid that Dana would shoot her, but she was certainly on guard.<br /> <br /> I told Iris that she should start talking, thus ruining the illusion that I was Nathan. I will admit that I was getting a little tired of the coy back and forth between those two. As amusing as it was to see Dana so ruffled I wanted to make sure that the conversation progressed. Iris admitted that she wanted to take a look at the artifacts that Dana had brought to the city. She said that she could keep them safe from cultist or anyone else that wants to get their hands on them. Dana really did not want the other woman near the statuettes. She doesn\u2019t trust her. Dana was adamant that the statuettes go to a museum, which is more altruistic than I was expecting. I think Iris was more keen on keeping the artifacts away from the \u201cwrong hands\u201d (ie. Cultists). She also wanted to get a look at the statuettes. Dana didn\u2019t really like that idea, but said that it might be possible with supervision.<br /> <br /> After we left the room Tatiana joined us in the hall. She had followed us upstairs and listened in to the conversation. She suggested as we walked that Dana let Iris take the statues once the archaeologist was done with them. Lizette was there too, though she had hidden really well. We met up with the rest of the pack, among others, and went back to Dana\u2019s room to discuss things. Dana explained her past with Iris to everyone, including the theft/protecting of the W\u0101s and cultists breaking into her room. Dana was not sure that she wanted Iris looking at the artifacts even with someone there to keep an eye on her, but she was tempted to do it. Dacian didn\u2019t think that it was a good idea. I didn\u2019t see the harm in letting the other woman look at them, especially if she has unique knowledge about this kind of ancient technology. It was implied during our meeting that she did.<br /> <br /> Tatiana went back to her own room to call Lucille and see if she knows anything about the missing actress. Waiting for her was Greta. Apparently Greta had some news for her about a \u201cFather Blackstaff\u201d who was also looking for Emile. He seems to be part of the Greek cult that was involved in stealing the scripts and hunting down our missing actress. Greta warned us that he comes across as rather off putting and disturbing. She also offered to help us find Emile. After that Tatiana called Lucille, but the other woman was not very forthcoming over the phone. Turns out that she was otherwise engaged, but she said that she\u2019d meet Tatiana after dinner. Greta offered to go with her in case it was a trap. I\u2019m not familiar enough with Lucille to know if she\u2019d set a trap or not, but it seems that our newest sin-eater is rather cautious about certain things. Not a bad thing in my book.<br /> <br /> We all met up for dinner and talked about what our options were going forward. We have answered some riddles, but in doing so have created more questions. We decided that Nathan, Dana, Alla and I would to talk to Agrippa about the artifacts and bring them back to the museum. Apparently she had absconded with them earlier. Agrippa wanted to take a look at the statues herself and was upset to find them missing.<br /> <br /> Another group containing Tatiana, Lizette and Greta planned to meet up with Lucille and ask about the missing actress, and find out if it\u2019s a trap or not. They also planned to ask about the dead woman that was walking around at the Salon. Dacian agreed that he would stay with Skadi to keep a guard on her as well as to show her around town so she could see the sights. Dearbhail, not wanting to be a \u201cthird wheel\u201d went back to her room to read. I guess we\u2019ll see how all of these meetings go.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> So Nathan, Dana, Alla and I went to the museum to meet with Agrippa. I carried the statuettes in a duffel bag since they were fairly heavy. We were greeted by Marissa who led us to Agrippa and Constancia (Connie). There was some definite tension in the room at that meeting. Agrippa was still upset about Dana taking the statues out of the museum in the first place and Dana retorted that the museum wasn\u2019t safe. Dana was also upset about Agrippa sowing dissent between herself and my pack. Then, I think in an effort to cause a scene and get Agrippa to back down, Dana reached over to the duffel bag and touched one of the statuettes. It suddenly glowed and the room shook just a bit. Agrippa backed down at the display of power. I looked to Dana and asked her what she had done. She just smiled at me. After that the tension was still there, but it had broken enough for there to be dialogue between the two. As Agrippa was looking over the artifacts I asked Dana again what she did to cause that effect. She started to prevaricate again but I flat out warned her that her mysterious attitude was only going to go so far and that people were getting annoyed. She seemed to understand that I was serious about not wanting to put up with anymore bullshit. She said that she has learned things over the years about those kinds of artifacts and that she\u2019d explain later at the hotel. That seemed reasonable to me so I nodded.<br /> <br /> Soon after that Tatiana and Greta came back from talking to Lucille. They were told that our missing actress might hide out in the Opera House or in the catacombs beneath it. Given how much it\u2019s rained lately it is entirely possible that her means of getting out has been flooded and that she is stuck down there for the time being. She might have also gone down there to go to a shrine dedicated to Persephone, the goddess she worships. It appears that she was making edits to the play so the text would be more in line with her religious beliefs rather than the original message. The cultists seem to have taken umbrage with this and are trying to sabotage her work, and possibly her as well. We agreed that it would be a good idea to go to the Opera House and see what we could find.<br /> <br /> While Tatiana and Greta talked to Lucille, Lizette went to talk to her friend from the poetry Salon, Clara, to talk about what happened at the last Salon with the walking dead girl coming in. Greta mentioned that this is something that she can do so it is likely that this Father Blackstaff is also a sin-eater. If he is the one that put up the monitoring spell over the cathedral he is also likely the one that sent the dead woman in to spy on the Salon. Not very subtle if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Once we were all gathered together and had talked about what we\u2019d learned we agreed that some of us should go to the Opera House and look for Emilie there, and possibly search the catacombs. It was agreed that Tatiana, Greta, Connie and I would go to the Opera House while Lizette and Alla stayed at the museum with the artifacts. I believe those two ladies are more than capable of watching over the artifacts and dealing with any trouble should it arise.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at the Opera House we saw that there was already someone there watching the front entrance. Tatiana motioned that she would go confront the driver while I snuck around back to keep them from escaping. Greta also decided to go the quiet route and turned into water in order to sneak up on the car. That gift is useful if you ask me. Connie stayed back for the moment to watch and make sure everything went alright with us.<br /> <br /> Tatiana confronted the driver and asked what they were doing there. He did not answer, so she tried all the languages she knows. She started in French, then moved on to German, English and Russian. They did not reply to any of it. You would think that they at least would speak rudimentary French, being in France and all, but they did not seem to understand anything that Tatiana was saying. Getting frustrated she used a gift to intimidate the passengers. It worked. The three others in the car shoved the driver out and proceeded to drive off as fast as they could. They might have gotten away too if Greta hadn\u2019t sent a rather large wave of water to shove the speeding car into a tree. Needless to say we don\u2019t need to worry about those three giving away our location. Tatiana proceeded to try and intimidate the driver, but without a common language it was difficult. Seeing my pack mates difficulty Connie went up to the car and started talking to the driver in Greek. Her eyes went yellow and her appearance was suddenly much more intimidating. She found out that he and his three friends had been watching the Opera House for a couple of days now. This could mean that Emilie is not there, or that she is but has been confined to the catacombs due to the rain. When asked who he worked for the driver said that they were employed by the \u201cBlade of the Orphic Oracle.\u201d It is likely that he means Blackstaff, or whatever his actual name is.<br /> <br /> As irony would have it the Greek cultist was under the impression that Greta was on their side and asked if she would hit Tatiana to get her away from him. I\u2019m assuming this misconception arose when Greta first met Blackstaff and he talked of his goals and what he believes. He seemed rather fervent in his belief that the play should be performed in its original form and that Emilie must be persuaded to do the \u201cright\u201d thing. Needless to say Greta did not hit Tatiana. It might have been amusing if she did. At least Tatiana\u2019s reaction would have been funny. Normally I\u2019d say Tatiana would beat her hands down, but sin-eaters have some pretty amazing gifts. Turning into water is just one of many that I\u2019ve seen from their kind.<br /> <br /> When the man was asked why they were sent he said that they were to follow a magician who had gotten a hold of a holy book. They want the play to happen but there was an intervention by a rival group. We\u2019re assuming this to mean Emilie and her worshipers of Persephone, or the Dionysian branch of that religion. We didn\u2019t really have any more questions for the man so Tatiana, who had him by the front of the shirt, handed him to me and she shifted into dire wolf form to better track Emilie\u2019s scent. She had been here since she went missing and Tatiana tracked Emilie through the building to where everything is set up to perform the play. She backed off when she smelled Harlow. Connie then went forward to talk to Harlow, after she made herself less frightening, and manipulated the man into leaving the room so he wouldn\u2019t see my pack mate in her wolf form.<br /> <br /> The trail led to a wall and stopped. We assume that there is a secret door there, but the mechanism to open the door is not nearby it, or is not obvious. While we looked for the door we discussed what we were going to do with the cultist. It was pretty much unanimously agreed that if he survived to tell his superiors what he knows about where we\u2019re going it would be bad for us. I offered to take care of the problem. I know that my pack mates know of my work as Reznik and understand that I have no problems killing people. The others do not know, nor do I wish them to, but it is likely that they will see me kill a man in cold blood. I find at this point that does not bother me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> We are waiting, volchonok, that is what we are doing.<br /> <br /> Because it is late, we have many things happening, and I do not know about secret doors. Soon, Wolfram will be done with wedding things and Agrippa will be done with the statues so Lizette and Alla and perhaps the archeologists join us. Perhaps even Dearbh\u00e1il will be done with her meeting.<br /> <br /> Dacian is sleeping with the Queen from Berlin and then guards her. He will not be here tonight.<br /> <br /> I already told you, distractible volchonok, we need them because I do not know about secret doors and the trail of the actress goes behind one.<br /> <br /> True, it is possible the writer Harlow knows such things. It is the theatre he works at after all. Constancia has managed to get him to avoid us though for now, it is probably best to not call him back.<br /> <br /> Yes, she called me an animal to do it. I am an animal. It was a good way to get him to leave without being hurt. It made Greta more happy.<br /> <br /> I do not know why Greta thinks it is ok to kill three people by being a giant wave of water and not ok to kill one by being a vampire. Probably because she was killed by a vampire.<br /> <br /> She did say that Constancia killed her. I think she is confused though.<br /> <br /> Greta is not helping the vampires, volchonok, she is helping the actress. The cultists, the Orphean ones - their leader made her nervous, so she is also working against him. Also, she does not like religions.<br /> <br /> This Father Blackstaff, or the Blade, or whatever he calls himself, is dead like her. It was probably him who made the church his territory before.<br /> <br /> Yes, the man we have is in his pack. It was Greek he was speaking, I think. It does not matter. Constancia spoke it, that is what is important.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we have two places to find him, the catacombs and the hotel he met Greta at. That will not be a problem. Perhaps if we cannot open the secret door we will just go kill him. She will be safe then. We make good plans, volchonok.<br /> <br /> No, that is a different cult. They are not from Greece, the ones who want Dana\u2019s statues. Those are the ones we are going to lure onto a boat to kill them.<br /> <br /> Well, Iris says the cultists will not stop coming after them ever, so probably we will need to kill them all.<br /> <br /> Of course I do not trust her, silly volchonok. But her telling the truth about this is the most dangerous, so it is best to assume she is. About this. Probably not about other things.<br /> <br /> I do think we should give them to her. After Dana has studied them, if they are not dangerous enough to destroy or some such. It is safer than giving them to a museum. She, or the cultists, or some other person who is stronger than regular security guards will just take them. It is for other people to decide though, I do not care.<br /> <br /> Dana slept with Iris because she is nice to look at, I imagine. Also, she is smart and clever and good at lying. Like Dana. Not everyone only mates with trusted friends, volchonok. Dana is very good at using sex as a tool.<br /> <br /> I am not going to mate with Greta.<br /> <br /> Yes, she is smart, clever and even nice to look at, I suppose. But I am not going to mate with her. She is just a friend.<br /> <br /> That was not sex things, I was showing her how to best hurt a man who has attacked her.<br /> <br /> Well, we had to wait for Dana and Lizette to make up. At least they didn\u2019t have sex.<br /> <br /> They had to make up because Lizette didn\u2019t yell at Wolfram and Alla for being suspicious, and because Dana was nice to Iris.<br /> <br /> Oh. I do not know why they didn\u2019t mate. Probably because we were to go to Lucille\u2019s and Lizette wanted to ask after the dead woman<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, I do wish it had been a trap at Lucille\u2019s. Some woman delaying things is much less exciting.<br /> <br /> It is true, Lucille was quite helpful and I did get to growl at someone later. But still...<br /> <br /> It was her that told us there were secret places to hide at the theatre. She also said Th\u00e9r\u00e8se had been spending more time than her with Emilie recently, which is not what the fairy had said. Also that she might be hiding in the catacombs, in the places the water has blocked off.<br /> <br /> It is not always blocked off. It is this damned rain. Lizette thinks the statues are perhaps causing it. If so, Iris can have the things with my blessing if she takes them very far away.<br /> <br /> I am distractible, you say, volchonok? That is not how this works. Yes, Lucille did also speak of the dead woman at the salon. Greta says it is something people like her and Wolfram can do. It was probably sent by Blackstaff to find Emilie there. She was supposed to be there.<br /> <br /> You mean Clara? She is the one that is forever picking Lizette up. She was also at the salon, so Lizette worried over her.<br /> <br /> I do not know, volchonok. She came quickly to relieve Marek, at the museum, so Clara is probably ok?<br /> <br /> Why are you so obsessed with mating today, volchonok? Perhaps. I did say she came back to the museum quickly.<br /> <br /> Well, Agrippa and Dana do not like each other and we are supposed to protect Dana, so we could not leave them alone together. And I think Alla is on Agrippa\u2019s side.<br /> <br /> I do not know why Agrippa is so worried over Dana. We probably did not help things, coming in all sneaky with Greta picking the lock. Constancia was happy to see me though.<br /> <br /> It is true. I do not like that Greta and Constancia are so at odds. They were doing better recently, after Constancia did not hurt the writer.<br /> <br /> I told you already, Dacian could not come because he is watching over the Winter Queen.<br /> <br /> Yes, the one whose den got set on fire.<br /> <br /> I do not like sneaky fairies. They have no scent. It is unnatural.<br /> <br /> What did you say, volchonok?<br /> <br /> I do not get scolded! I am not a foolish volchonok to get scolded.<br /> <br /> Bah. Dacian does not understand. We were already invited into the territory. We were supposed to look at the room. That is why we were there, not to make pretty talk with fairies.<br /> <br /> Yes, well...<br /> <br /> Hush, volchonok. Yes, I stopped when Dearbh\u00e1il <u>asked</u> me to. That is because she asked nicely, not because she scolded.<br /> <br /> Wise volchonok. No, there was nothing. There was a big fire at the door and a thin line of it around the bed. She got out by the window - it was unlocked. Mrs. Skitters had been there, but a long time ago.<br /> <br /> Mostly it smelt of fire. Mrs. Skitters was in the ventilation shaft, so her scent lingered a little.<br /> <br /> Yes, I chinned up there to check on the scents. Why? Did Madeline notice?<br /> <br /> Hush. You will give Dearbh\u00e1il ideas.<br /> <br /> That might make guarding worthwhile, but it would not be good for guarding. We have a plan though - tomorrow when the German Queen goes back to the guest houses, it will only be for pretend and we will catch whoever sneaks up on the disguised Alla.<br /> <br /> An ambush is different from guarding, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Because... I do not know. Because I say so.<br /> <br /> No, this is not either one. It is waiting. Waiting is more like guarding. Boring.<br /> <br /> Figure out how to open this door and perhaps we will run along the underground lake. But not right now volchonok. Now, we wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 26th April 1922<br /> <br /> What a day.<br /> <br /> The visit to the guesthouse was smooth. I met Madeline, A Fairest who called herself the Chancellor, though I did not know the Spring Court had such a position. She was helpful, though, letting us examine the room used by Queen Skadi, but the previous one set on fire and the next one for her to sleep in. Dacian determined that the windows were the most likely way in, and that the fire was set such that it was unlikely to burn Skadi right away. I think it was Marek who pointed out the windows had been unlocked, which made her escape easier.<br /> <br /> The talk of Darkling magic, along with the ventilation as possible access and terror inflicted, suggests a Darkling, possibly of the Autumn Court. At the same time, Mrs. Skitters suggested Th\u00e9r\u00e8se might have had something to do with it. But perhaps Th\u00e9r\u00e8se used Separation to enter and either had some Darkling magic or Darkling help. On the other hand, Mrs. Skitters is a Darkling of the Autumn Court.<br /> <br /> Madeline, for her part, suggested the Winter Court might be involved. They are the least positively inclined toward Germany. I think Dearbh\u00e1il was skeptical. Dacian for his part poured on the charm with Queen Skadi. He did, at least, do better than with Dana. Or me. You might think if Dearbh\u00e1il wanted him to get laid so bad she would be a bit more hands on with it. But then, aside from Marek, she has shown little interest in either men or women, ignoring interest both Dacian and I have shown.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we got back to the hotel and Dana had a message. She calmly checked her pistol and said in a level voice that she needed to go alone to talk to the person whom she was careful not to name or gender. I protested strongly, and she adjusted to saying she would take someone with her but not Nathan or I. After a moment she chose Marek. Of course. They went up, and Tatiana and I snuck up to keep an eye on things. She waited at the door; I hid in the ventilation shaft (hey, Dacian had <u>just</u> pointed them out at the house).<br /> <br /> Iris DeVeers, it turns out, was an old flame of Dana\u2019s. Not lost in the past, she had Champaign ready and was put out to see Marek (becoming the first woman on earth this has apparently ever happened to.) While she fawned over and kissed Dana at first, she proved to be evasive of her intentions, at least with Marek (who Dana implied to be Nathan) present. So, Dana caught her by surprise with her gun. Iris was rather hurt. It turned out Iris was a wealthy woman from Alexandria of British origin, and had hired Dana before and knew something of the sorts of tech we were dealing with as she helped turn her on to relics such as these statuettes or the Golden Eagle. She also had stolen Dana\u2019s was in the past, and framed cultists for the crime. Well, that or foiled them, which was her protest. I am skeptical as Dana is.<br /> <br /> Iris wants to see the statuettes. Dana is agreeable but wants us to watch her very, very carefully. She may have knowledge we can use. She also insisted the cultists will just steal them when our guard is down. She says she can hide them. We discussed it, after she came down (leaving Iris in the room) and I know we worked some things out and I gave Marek the bag with the statuettes, but unfortunately I missed a lot of it as I was quietly seething. When the immediate issue was worked out and Tatiana went to her room to telephone Lucille, I told Dana I need to talk to her and we went upstairs.<br /> <br /> I told her maybe it was all my fault, maybe she was totally in the right and all that, but I was falling for her and I was upset about how cavalier she was with my feelings. She snapped back she thought I was a modern woman and she does not want to be anyone\u2019s conquest or wife or anything like that ever. Her freedom is paramount and she won\u2019t give it up for love. I said I did not want her freedom; I wanted her love. I can\u2019t say I don\u2019t care who she sleeps with, but I don\u2019t want to limit her, however much she has a light in her voice when she discusses Iris or however much she looks at Marek. I don\u2019t want our liaison to be purely physical. After yelling awhile we agreed to separate and calm down at her suggestion.<br /> <br /> I know what it is. Christina Esterh\u00e1zy. Soon to be Christina von Klingemann. I am not over her. I am not over her choosing Wolfram over me. Is this influencing my feelings for Dana? Dana Barlowe is everything Christina isn\u2019t. Dana is bold, needs no one, men are wrapped around her finger; she is unafraid to throw charm around. I envy her. It is hard not to fall for her. If I didn\u2019t, I might loathe her for being what I dare not. Not that a misshapen little freak such as myself has any option to go turning the heads of men or women.<br /> <br /> Pleasant thoughts. Ugh. I was quite convinced after my return I would die a virgin. It was not foremost on my mind of course, compared to avenging my family and driving the Germans forever from French soil. Still, after Armistice Day I found some French airmen more than willing to prevent such a fate, each did, after all think it was he. I should not complain. I have had lovely ladies attention as well, even if none sought anything serious from me. Why would they, after all, with someone like myself?<br /> <br /> Of course, both are women of character and backbone. Both have a strong sense of morality. Perhaps I have a better idea of what I like now. Perhaps they are more alike than I give them credit for.<br /> <br /> So I went downstairs where we were sitting for dinner, and while we talked Dacian was going on about how Dana would prefer Marek\u2019s conversation to his. I lost it. Dacian may be creepy around women, but he is witty and urbane, where Marek chooses words carefully and is quiet a good deal of the time. I knew exactly what Dacian meant; he was talking about Marek\u2019s handsomeness, which everyone notices. Marek is the only one who has been good enough for Dearbh\u00e1il after all, despite Dacian and I flirting with her. Which her right but\u2026it makes me twitchy that everyone notices Dearbh\u00e1il she just does not care. Such attentions are meaningless to her.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I exploded and stormed off.<br /> <br /> A short time later Dana came up to my room and said she loved me. She quickly clarified nothing has changed, she will not be tied down, and if I wanted a girlfriend that would not be her, but that our feelings were mutual.<br /> <br /> I was so happy. I think I cried. We spent a little non-intimate time together, and she promised to sleep beside me tonight.<br /> <br /> My distraction was fairly unfortunate; I missed a lot of what happened. However, we split into groups, as Dana went with Alla and Marek (of course) to the museum while Tatiana and I went to speak to Lucille, with Greta in tow. I am not sure when she showed up but she and Tatiana were getting along well. It was sort of frightening. Dacian took Skadi to see the city, and Dearbh\u00e1il retired with her book. The chat with Lucille went well, no thanks to Greta, who indulged her German total lack of respect with gusto.<br /> <br /> We found that this Sin-Eater called Father Blackstaff Greta had encountered had sent (we think) a female undead creature to the Salon where it began to fall apart and frightened several guests. When Emilie did not show and the bizarre creature was around her usual haunt, Lucille left early. She was, however, helpfully able to give some suggestions of where Emilie might be, namely the theater and possibly somewhere under the city. The catacombs are long and winding; though with the storm some are impassible. I am told the Autumn King is fine but cut off due to the sheer amount of rain. Emilie has a shrine down there, Lucille says, to Persephone and she speculated Emilie may be cut off too since she has not returned to she or Harlow or Th\u00e9r\u00e8se.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve wondered before if I were to build something of a battle platform for the catacombs what would be best. Something spider-legged with wall crawling capabilities seems like a good idea, but some sort of water based aereofoil that could function similar to a speed boat might also be good. Something where I can rig it with machine guns but also closer combat weapons for corridor to corridor combat. The aereofoil would be good for water to ground. I keep thinking of something inflatable maybe to help steady it. Must research. If well steadied I could even attach some flamethrowers or something, or ignitable oil slicks if facing a similar vessel.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I asked about Clara, but Lucille was unsure, so when we parted ways I went to see her while the other two went to the Museum to try to recruit Constancia. Clara was okay. She was <u>very</u> happy to see me, and wished I had been there at the Salon. I did have to scold her about picking me up again. It\u2019s less bad when not in front of people but she needs to break the habit. Clara is such a dear sweet girl. We had tea, then I gave her a hug and went back on to the Museum, where I was to relieve Marek.<br /> <br /> Most of the excitement at the museum was over. Dana had clashed earlier with Agrippa, but they were warily keeping their distance now. When Agrippa was done, she told Dana she would need them again in the next night or two, and Dana made no promises but seemed disinclined to argue. We returned to the hotel, and are waiting to hear from Tatiana and Marek.<br /> <br /> Oh! There is a message now\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> Iris DeVeers is a Demon, as in Unchained. This became apparent OOC, when she asked Marek a question, made a roll, and told the player \u201cYou feel like you can tell her.\u201d Also, her jumpiness about her background. I was pretty transparent about it, but IC they don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> Contrary to what Tatiana told foolish volchonok, Dacian didn\u2019t sleep with Skadi. He spent time with her though and certainly worked toward it. We will see what happens. And yes, Madeleine noticed Tatiana doing a chin up in her \u201cinvestigating\u201d<br /> <br /> Werewolves crazy tracking abilities put interesting twists on stuff like missing persons.<br /> <br /> Next session the search for Emilie concludes, and the group has to decide how to proceed with the play given certain revelations. And speaking of which, Dana Barlowe\u2019s nature is revealed. Join us, won\u2019t you? Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T22:24:22-08:00","id":833044,"title":"","content":"Our heroes descend into the Catacombs to find the lost star, but even doing so what is her agenda. While weaker than Agrippa or Blackstaff the serpent is not without fangs. Revelations within show the truth behind Dana\u2019s condition, but only leave questions about her old flame.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 April 1922<br /> <br /> Well, the trip to the catacombs was productive. Not necessarily sure if it was entirely a good thing, but we completed what we set out to do. First of all the rest of the Pack, minus Dacian (He was still guarding Skadi) came to the Opera House and we all started looking for the lever or switch that would open the hidden door we\u2019d found. It didn\u2019t take long for Wolfram to find it and pull it, opening the passage to the Catacombs. He decided to stay behind and study the play with Harlow. Nathan, Dana and Lizette stayed to watch the door, and our \u201cguest\u201d while the rest of us crossed the running water. Tatiana gave Dearbhail a boost so she could glide over the water, while the rest of us swam. We made our way with what little light we had and found yet another lake, or something much like one. This one was further across and the water was running faster. We decided that we could need rope and more light if we were going to continue with our explorations. So we retraced our steps. Harlow found us some rope and Lizette, Dana and Wolfram joined us this time. Wolfram used a gift to make his body glow like firelight. It came in very handy. So we all made our way back across the first lake and used the rope on the second one. Each time we crossed Greta turned into water and appeared on the other side. That is a handy gift.<br /> <br /> Once on the other side we ran across two skeletons carrying swords. The skeletons themselves were very old, probably pulled from the Catacomb walls. The swords were much newer. Wolfram did not believe that they were animated by a Sin-eater. His opinion was that it was some other kind of magic. In short order Greta took care of both of them and ended up throwing them both in the water to be carried away by the current. We continued on for a while before Alla and Connie picked up the sound of one very fast heartbeat ahead. Tatiana and I heard someone moving, and then I heard the telltale sound of a round being chambered in a rifle. I halted the group and Wolfram called out to identify us to the scared individual with the rifle. We figured it was Emilie, and we were right. She walked slowly out of the next chamber, still holding her gun in a ready position. We explained what we were doing here and that we\u2019d been sent to come find and protect her. Her concern was that she would not be safe until after the play was over, and maybe not even then. She was worried about more cultists coming to find her. Some of our number were trying to convince her to come back to the surface, while others were not trying to pressure her either way. At first I don\u2019t think she actually believed us, but we eventually convinced her of our good intentions.<br /> <br /> Emilie for her part decided to come back to the surface with us and allow us to protect her from the cultists and from Father Blackstaff. She still wants the play to go on with her changes but is afraid that Blackstaff will kill her or have is men do it. I can understand her fear, but if she stayed in the Catacombs it would only be a matter of time before he found her and killed her. His men were already waiting outside. If they decided to come in and followed the path we did she would have been trapped. Her skeletons, while threatening to non-combatants, were not much to deal with for anyone with any experience fighting. Greta took out both by herself without breaking a sweat.<br /> <br /> We made it back to the Opera House without issue. The rope and Wolfram\u2019s light both coming in very handy. Once back Emilie said that she would be at the practice for the play but specifically told Harlow that she doesn\u2019t want anyone to know that she\u2019s been found. That should provide some modicum of security, for a while anyway. The less people that know that she\u2019s back the better. What is the phrase? Loose lips sink ships.<br /> <br /> While we were searching for Emilie a couple things came up. First off Dearbhail took Dana aside to talk to her in private. I heard her anyway since my wolf senses were activated, but I don\u2019t think anyone besides Tatiana and myself heard. Dearbhail said something to Dana about treating Lizette right and to not hurt her feelings. She explained that Lizette loves several people and that it didn\u2019t make her feelings for Dana any less. Dearbhail also threatened to come after the archaeologist if she hurt Lizette because she\u2019s afraid of commitment. I can see her doing it too. Dearbhail may seem like the sweet non-combatant, but she\u2019s got paired knives that she is pretty good with. Dana assured Dearbhail that she did not intend to hurt Lizette. Apparently Dana has trust issues because she\u2019s been betrayed by one too many people she considered friends. I can understand that.<br /> <br /> During their conversation Dearbhail also claimed me as her special wolf. Not that I think Dana was interested in me, but it came up during Dearbhail\u2019s speech about how close our Pack is. I had to smile at that. I rather enjoy the Irish firebrand\u2019s company in and out of bed. I have not felt quite so close to anyone else, though I\u2019m not sure if what I feel for Dearbhail is love. I know that I love my brother and my father, but that is different. That is familial. With Dearbhail I wish to keep her safe but that feeling is stronger with her than it is with the rest of the Pack. Don\u2019t get me wrong, if anyone hurts a Pack mate of mine they will regret it, but if someone hurt Dearbhail I would take pleasure in tearing their throat out and watching them choke on their own blood. I rather prefer to see Dearbhail happy and smiling though. I know that something is not quite right with me. I don\u2019t feel emotions the same way others do. Things are muted. I just know that I care for the Irish singer and like to see her happy. I just don\u2019t think I\u2019m very good at showing it though.<br /> <br /> As far as the play goes Wolfram figured out some things about it. The play is designed to put the audience into a trance like state that may make you susceptible to a spirit or other similar being. The goal it seems is to put you in contact with a god. The original version would possibly put the audience in touch with Hades or something like that. It is the Orphean version. The adjusted version of the play would put you in contact with Dionysus or perhaps Persephone. Still not sure that option is much better. A god of chaos would likely cause a good bit of problems for the people involved. I don\u2019t think Hades, or whoever, would be a better choice though. My personal vote is for neither.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing that was mentioned by Emilie was that the storm we are currently experiencing is connected to Dana somehow. Dana believes that it is because of the artifacts. Seems feasible to me. We don\u2019t know what they do and she has been in close proximity to them for a while now. The storm didn\u2019t start until a day or two after she arrived in town with the statues. So did the storm just take it\u2019s time to build or did something else happen after she arrived that would have triggered it?<br /> <br /> After all of that there was a short discussion on where Emilie would stay. Greta was adamant that the actress not stay with Connie since the slight vampire seemed especially interested in turning her into one of her own kind. Greta was very much against this and threatened Connie, and Alla to a much lesser extent that no one was going to turn Emilie. I think being killed by vampires has colored her world view quite a bit in regards to them. Tatiana tried to calm things down, which worked for the most part.<br /> <br /> Once that conversation was done Greta went on her way and the rest of us quickly decided what to do with our cultist \u201cfriend.\u201d I was fine with just taking him a little ways off and killing him. I have a knife. Tatiana thought that would be too much of a waste and suggested that our vampire friends get something out of it. So, Alla fed off of him, then Connie did. Connie ended up killing the man by taking too much blood. I suppose it doesn\u2019t matter how the situation was ended, as long as it is done. We did not need Blackstaff hearing about anything that man had seen or heard.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 27 April 1922<br /> <br /> Well, we finally got some answers out of Dana today. Before breakfast she asked those of us in the Pack to come upstairs and talk to her in her room. As soon as the door closed she asked us to make a Pledge that we would not speak of what we heard with anyone outside the room. We agreed since it was an easy enough thing to do. She also agreed not to speak to anyone about what she had learned about us. She then went on to tell us about how she, like us, was connected to an artifact that granted her, in essence, immortality. It was not the same kind of technology that the Golden Eagle or the statues are. It is something different, but it essentially does the same thing. She can be wounded, but she will heal faster than usual. She can be killed, but it will not be permanent. She also will not age. I think our aging will be slowed due to the Eagle, but don\u2019t think it will be stopped altogether. Dana said that she had an interest in studying the Golden Eagle, but has no desire to take it since she is already immortal. Her main aspiration for living so long is to learn as much as she can about the world around her and its history. She seems to truly just wishes to gain more knowledge so she can understand the world around her.<br /> <br /> She also told us that she believes that Iris would not have any problems trying to kill her if she felt the need. Dana also mentioned that Iris has a way of \u201cinterfacing\u201d with the kind of technology that the statues are. We\u2019re not sure how she can do it, but it is clear that we are far from the only unique creatures around. Dana herself can interact with the technology in some small way, making light and such. She can only do more by using her W\u0101s. She does have other abilities from her association with the device that makes her immortal. She can strengthen objects past the normal tolerance and can sense if an object is magical and other basic information about it. She could not get specific details off of a hedgespun item, she\u2019d just know it was magical. That would be an interesting talent to have if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Apparently Iris also likes to collect these same kind of artifacts and has been a patron to several archaeologists over the years. Perhaps because she has such a unique interaction with the artifacts Iris is also very keen on people not investigating her past too closely. Anyone that Dana has sent to investigate Iris\u2019s past too deeply has ended up dead or missing. So, she is definitely hiding something but it is difficult to find out what. Unless she becomes a threat to my Pack I am content letting Iris keep her secrets. Dana\u2019s opinion is that Iris is dangerous but useful. Sounds fair to me.<br /> <br /> After the initial conversation about abilities we discussed what we needed to accomplish going forward. We talked briefly about the plan to protect Skadi. I think what we\u2019re going to do is have Alla impersonate Skadi and take her place tonight in the new room. Before she goes there however she is going to spend some time in a freezer so she will radiate cold the way that Skadi does. Doesn\u2019t hurt to be as realistic as possible. We will also need people to stay and protect the archaeologists and Emilie. Not sure if we\u2019re going to do that in one location or split up. I would recommend against splitting up.<br /> <br /> We talked about seeing if Greta could help with our various protection jobs, but some were unsure if she\u2019d be more of a help or a hindrance. She is rather impulsive.<br /> <br /> In the end the conversation turned to the play, as seems to be the case a lot lately. We talked about whether or not we should interrupt the play to keep the magic from activating or if Alla should subtly change her lines or something along those lines to derail the magic, but keep the essence of the story intact. Either way we do it will have to be discreet. Agrippa seems to have an interest in the play and may be been tangentially responsible for Emilie hearing about it in the first place. Maybe she knew that the actress would want to put her own religious spin on it? Emilie does worship Persephone which is related to Dionysus. And Agrippa, and Connie for that matter, have been referred to as Maenads. If I remember correctly they are worshippers/followers if Dionysus that can be rather violent if the mood takes them. Considering the power that Agrippa has we should probably do what we can to be as discreet as possible if we are going to sabotague the play. I think Alla\u2019s plan was to confront the elder vampire about the play and its purpose without mentioning Agrippa\u2019s involvement in the whole affair. I guess we\u2019ll see how it all goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Volchonok, would you stop your yapping!<br /> <br /> No, I am not going back over the water.<br /> <br /> I do not know what I shall do today.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, \u201cI don\u2019t know\u201d is not the same thing as \u201cyes, I will go across the water because I wish to get away from annoying whining volchonoks\u201d.<br /> <br /> I am sorry you could not get across using the rope. It is not my fault; I do not know how to make spirit rope.<br /> <br /> If you do not wish me to say so, you should not whine.<br /> <br /> I am not helpless without you, my worriful volchonok. Greta could be wherever she wished, with so much water, and besides, a few skeletons are no real danger.<br /> <br /> I told you about the skeletons! The creatures with no flesh? Remember?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure you would have loved seeing if they still had marrow. Greta handled them with no problems, though. They were Emilie\u2019s anyway.<br /> <br /> Ah, I see volchonok, now it comes out. Come now, you got to see me help our songbird fly many times, almost as many as she did.<br /> <br /> She did look quite beautiful, did she not? And it was nice to have her so close in the dark, to hear her heartbeat in her fingers. Ah, but she says Marek is her special wolf.<br /> <br /> She did, while you were sulking, when we came back to ask the writer man for rope.<br /> <br /> I do not know, I wasn\u2019t paying attention. She was speaking with Dana, something about Lizette being in love with many people, and us killing people she does not like.<br /> <br /> You keep saying such things, volchonok. Dearbh\u00e1il did not scold me. Perhaps she looked at me sternly after I shook dry, but that is all.<br /> <br /> Pshaw, I do not care how that one looks at me. The actress became far less interesting once we found her.<br /> <br /> I do not know. She has magic? She can make skeletons walk and knew what Greta and Wolfram and Alla and Constancia were right away. And her play is magic, Wolfram says.<br /> <br /> She was not properly grateful at all. And now we have someone else to guard. I still say we should just kill all the cultists. Then we will not need to guard her. And she will not be able to make Greta angry at Constancia anymore.<br /> <br /> Because Constancia wants Emilie to become a vampire.<br /> <br /> What? Volchonok, where do you get these ideas? Who has taught you \u2018jealous\u2019? No, I am not jealous. I don\u2019t want to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> No, I just do not like that I had to be growly at Greta so she would not try and kill Constancia.<br /> <br /> I did. If we were to kill the cultist we questioned, there is no reason to have his blood go to waste. It is not against the Litany to let a vampire consume a human.<br /> <br /> No, growly is not like lecturing. Greta can still show up in my bathroom.<br /> <br /> It is true, it is amusing to watch Wolfram\u2019s face when he lectures. He goes all noble, and sputters so when you tell him the truth.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know, volchonok, I stopped paying attention to watch his face.<br /> <br /> Oh, you mean before that? We were talking about putting Alla in a freezer so she could pretend to be an ice giant better. Dana thinks Greta could help and said we should bribe her with telling her things.<br /> <br /> She did say many things, Dana did, that were important. If we must kill her, we will not attack her, but some object that is probably not this was. And if we are to protect her, it is good to know she will not stay dead, and that there is some important object.<br /> <br /> The object is hard to break. It is her magic, she says. I do not think we will need to though. Dearbh\u00e1il likes her and the archaeologist and Lizette are friends again. Even Wolfram and Dacian have liked her more since she told us of her magics. I still do not understand her and her wanting to know everything there is, but that is for the others.<br /> <br /> I already said, I do not know. It will not be across the water though. Perhaps I will see what Greta is doing. It will be more fun, whatever it is, than writing a play over again so that it does not make people dream of God. Or sleeping in a freezer.<br /> <br /> Where would we run, eh volchonok? Perhaps when it comes time to leave the city again. But not this day, volchonok, not this day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 26th April 1922<br /> <br /> We have rescued Emilie. It remains to be seen if this is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Everyone (sans Dacian) descended on the theater, and it took little time for Wolfram to find the lever that opened the hidden way beneath it. It was pitch dark beyond the light from the doorway. Harlow was around but kept some distance. We needed to get across the lake where water had flooded in from the catacombs due to the rain and swollen the lake. Wolfram stayed behind to study the play, while Dearbh\u00e1il, Tatiana, Alla, Marek and Greta went in. Dearbh\u00e1il apparently glided over the water with Tatiana\u2019s help, where the Werewolves swam across. Alla did, but needed help from Tatiana. Greta just did that creepy teleporting across water thing she does. Nathan, Dana and I went back in to keep an eye on the door in case cultists returned.<br /> <br /> A short time later, they returned and declared they needed rope and more light. Harlow went and fetched rope, while Dearbh\u00e1il buttonholed Dana who went and talked to her in a side room. I have a feeling it was about me. When we reconvened, Wolfram explained that both plays, if performed, would cause a magical effect, bringing a dreamlike state to the audience and opening communion with\u2026something. The Orphean version he was unsure with what, but the Dionysian version would be with Dionysus, or some entity claiming to be Dionysus. As Dana noted, creating contact with something at least claiming to be if not being a god of revelry, chaos, madness and wine did not seem like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Speaking as a Catholic, I don\u2019t like the idea of creating a communion with some ancient god a good idea at all. That this sort of paganism exists in Paris is sort of disturbing, and I am unsure what to make of it. It\u2019s hardly my place to lecture; I am a terrible Catholic, but nonetheless\u2026<br /> <br /> We ventured below, with Wolfram glowing rather brightly. Tatiana tossed Dearbh\u00e1il over the lake, and she secured a rope on the far side, which we used to get across. Well, all but Greta who just sort of teleported, and Tatiana who swam to show off. Nathan remained behind with Harlow at Dana\u2019s instance, her noting he was less resilient than the rest of us. Despite the current, I had an easy time getting across, and Alla apparently had an easier time of it then before.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never traveled the catacombs without a light, so I can only imagine how unnerving it was the first time through, especially with the silence replaced with the sound of rushing water. I spotted a glyph from the Autumn Court indicating the area was not part of our direct turf but not super dangerous or tied to anything specific. All sorts of things use the catacombs, I can only guess what some of them are, but the rushing water both meant it was safer from them but the environment was more dangerous. Also, I may need to bring Wolfram again his fiery light was terribly useful.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and fire. Yum.<br /> <br /> Eventually we came to a wide river of water, with two skeletons of the far side, wielding swords. The skeletons looked old, and brittle. Tatiana began to swim across with the rope, while Greta quickly and easily teleported across the river and overcame the skeletons out of hand. She pinned one at first while keeping the other at bay, but eventually tossed them in the river, despite Dana\u2019s comment about \u201cbypassing guardians rather than destroying them.\u201d Tatiana set the rope and we carefully made it across, though the current was much stronger here. Eventually the Werewolves smelled her and Alla heard her heart, and Emilie emerged from the darkness with a rifle.<br /> <br /> Emilie was not happy to see us. Yes, she had been trapped in her shrine, but it was semi-purposeful. Having been tracked first by Blackstaff then Agrippa, she had sought refuge in her shrine beneath the city, and the rising water kept both away from her. She was, needless to say, not pleased about two Sin-Eaters and two Vampires (Greta and Connie were with us as well as the usual Wolfram and Alla.) Discussion had few surprises, beyond Emilie was remarkably forthcoming. Yes, she changed the play. Yes, she did so in service to Persephone for her son, Dionysus. She \u201cfound out\u201d Harlow would be coming with the Orphean holy book and \u201chelped\u201d with a few revisions, revisions that would turn the invocation to \u201cher god\u201d though while we assume (based on context) that it is Dionysus, it could be Persephone. I am not sure Emilie Barteau is completely sane.<br /> <br /> Connie was certainly interested. Interested in turning her into a vampire. Emilie recognized her as a maenad, but was unsure about being turned. She said she would need to \u201cCommune with the Goddess.\u201d Greta expressed a threat to kill Connie if she turned her, or to kill Emilie. This went over like you would expect, especially with Tatiana who seemed upset her friends were fighting.<br /> <br /> In the end, Emilie agreed to come back with us. She followed Dana\u2019s advice to stay in the hotel, as her home is almost certainly being watched. Hopefully we were not noticed on our return. Harlow saw us, but I doubt he is in league with Blackstaff. Emilie swore him to secrecy for now.<br /> <br /> Now I rest in Dana\u2019s room. She wanted a bath and to change, and would be out in a moment.<br /> <br /> Mother of God.<br /> <br /> <br /> 27th April 1922<br /> <br /> I think Dana has appropriately apologized as well as shown her feelings. I suppose I might get used to this, but good God I can\u2019t imagine how.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il was out early (given how late we got back) getting glamour, and we decided to meet for lunch, then return the rooms to discuss our next move. We used Dana\u2019s room, and she even shut the windows so Alla could join us.<br /> We looked at our timeline. The fake was is arriving today, the real was tomorrow, the 28th. Ideally we want to hopefully end the storm by or before the 30th, as the play is that day, and the wedding is on the 1st. Whose idea was it to have a play like that on Walpurgis anyway?<br /> <br /> We also discovered Dana is a sort of semi-immortal being called an Eternal. She has bound her life energy into an object (which is not the was) and cannot be killed without it being destroyed. She can also strengthen objects and have some idea of their function, and presumably age. Nothing flashy, but a good kit for an archeologist. No word on how she discovered how to do this, however. Her status is why she is not seeking the Eagle, however.<br /> <br /> We also discussed how to resolve the issue with the play. Wolfram intends to research a way to have Alla flub her part just so she disrupts the spell without it going haywire, and the rest of us need to determine how to prevent Blackstaff, Emilie, or Agrippa (or possibly Connie) from wrecking havoc and sidelining the play or having Alla controlled. Alla intends to confront Agrippa soon more directly.<br /> <br /> Tonight though she masquerades as Skadi, she will sleep in ice to give off cold and use her acting skills to disguise as that fairest. There will presumably be an ambush prepared. With everything going on, I could use a little ambush.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> Eternals can be found in World of Darkness: Immortals in the back. Dana did not outright lie but implied there was an artifact involved, but it was in fact crafted by her.<br /> <br /> The play is a sort of ritual for Communion, as per the spell in Second Sight, while bringing the Audience into a dreamlike state. What would be contacted they can only speculate. Context suggests a Greek god, but who knows what would actually be contacted.<br /> <br /> Spelunking and conversation took much of the session\u2026despite only two or three major scenes.<br /> <br /> We are going to miss a session due to vacation timings. In two weeks will be stats for any PC I can easily get a hold of stats for\u2026I expect Alla, Lizette, and Wolfram but we will see. See you then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:13:17-08:00","id":833437,"title":"","content":"Eternal and Stigmatic? Or just general faculty with Relic/G-M stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:35:05-08:00","id":841661,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you have already done it and I've just missed seeing them, but could you post character sheets for your 'pack'. Preferably starting sheets and those for the beginning of the 20's for comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:16:32-08:00","id":841724,"title":"","content":"(Wow I missed that somehow sorry Vent)<br /> Vent0: Just Eternal, she has some capacity to use D-M stuff but is not technically a Stigmatic. She has enough minor abilities it seems excessive.<br /> <br /> 2ptTakrill: As it happens, since we are missing a session I have the current stats for 5/7 of the group here. I don't have original to compare to, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> There was no game two weeks ago as I was out of town. In it\u2019s place, I figured I would link a few PCs so you can get some character stats. These were the stats which players provided. Not everyone is represented here, but over half the PCs are.<br /> <br /> <b>Alla Garin, Daeva Invictus Vampire</b><br /> <br /> Alla<br /> Vampire<br /> Concept: Miss Piggy + Mr. Gustav<br /> Mask: Courtesan<br /> Dirge: Spy<br /> Clan: Daeva<br /> Covenant: Invictus<br /> Aspirations: Acquire means to live comfortably (Sponsor) (Long Term), Gain fame in the human world (Short Term)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 2<br /> Resolve 2<br /> <br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Presence 4<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Composure 2<br /> <br /> Academics 1<br /> Crafts 0<br /> Enigmas 0<br /> Investigation 2<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Politics 3<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Athletics 1<br /> Brawl 4 (Punching)<br /> Drive 0<br /> Firearms 0<br /> Larceny 3<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 0<br /> Weaponry 0<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 0<br /> Empathy 3<br /> Expression 3<br /> Intimidation 0<br /> Persuasion 3<br /> Socialize 4 (Russian Culture)<br /> Streetwise 3<br /> Subterfuge 4 (Impersonating Nobility)<br /> <br /> Celerity 2<br /> Majesty 2<br /> Resilience 2<br /> Vigor 1<br /> <br /> Blood Potency 3<br /> Humanity 7<br /> Willpower 4<br /> Health 9<br /> Vitae: 12<br /> Size 5<br /> Defense 5<br /> Initiative 5<br /> Speed: 12<br /> <br /> Covenant Status: Invictus 1<br /> Herd: Bitties 1<br /> Multilingual 2<br /> Striking Looks 1 (2)<br /> True Friend: Fenric 3<br /> <br /> Languages: English, Russian; Multilingual: French, German<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fenric, Alla\u2019s Ghoul</b><br /> <br /> Fenric<br /> Ghoul<br /> Concept: Pepito<br /> Virtue: Optimism<br /> Vice: Lust<br /> Regent\u2019s Clan: Daeva<br /> Regent\u2019s Covenant: Invictus<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 3<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 2<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Presence 4<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Academics 1<br /> Crafts 0<br /> Enigmas 0<br /> Investigation 2<br /> Medicine 2<br /> Occult 0<br /> Politics 2<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Athletics 0<br /> Brawl 0<br /> Drive 0<br /> Firearms 0<br /> Larceny 3 (Magic Tricks)<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 0<br /> Wea