h a motley crew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there.<br /> <br /> Yea I don't think any of the players were familiar enough with Mage to dare it in a mixed group. Mage was not even one of the considered ones that were not gone with (which include a Demon, Colony Werecat, and Changeling Summer Court Beast Seeming)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T01:25:52-07:00","id":849645,"title":"","content":"Stats for several characters just above, check them out.<br /> <br /> The Conspiracy seeks closure for the Changeling situation and finds it, but not in a way they were expecting. All had to ask themselves questions of love and death as they face a greater threat to Skadi than predicted. Meanwhile, deals with vampires made, and Iris returns to the picture. Just another typical night for this group.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 27 April, 1922<br /> <br /> To start off our conversation Tatiana said out loud what we all knew, that Christina is pregnant. Apparently she got tired of people dancing around the subject by asking Christina if she was okay, or suggesting she rest. The thing is, humans have this ridiculous custom among them that they pretend a woman is not pregnant until after she is married. Or they try not to get pregnant before that happens. Well, those things can\u2019t always be planned so here our friends are actively ignoring the elephant in the room. Seems silly to me, but then humans put a lot of weight on whether someone\u2019s parents were married when they were conceived or not. Yes, technically Wolfram is a Claimed but he is close enough to human that it doesn\u2019t make a difference. So, Tatiana was chided for saying what was known or suspected out loud. When she looked at me I just shrugged. I think they\u2019d want to celebrate the child, but they won\u2019t let themselves just yet. Honor dictates that they pretend until after the wedding. Silly nobles.<br /> <br /> Of course this conversation actually led to Dana opening up a little bit about herself. She mentioned that if at all possible you should not cross a desert when you are very pregnant as they are not good places to give birth. This sounded like personal experience to me, and she admitted that she had a young adult daughter. She also said something about a son that is younger than her daughter. It can\u2019t have been easy for her to be a mother on her own, especially after the war. As progressive as some people like to act, raising a child on one\u2019s own would be hard. She might have been able to claim that the father was killed in the war, but that leaves all the time before the war when the children were growing up to deal with nosy people. And people do like to poke their noses into other people\u2019s business more often than not. Wolves stick to their own territory and don\u2019t usually mess with others intentionally. Tatiana and I are something of an exception. We have both human and wolf in us so we so we do cross the territory of others, but I think we\u2019re pretty good about leaving them to their own business. It is not unheard of for a wolf to lose one of its parents and be raised by the rest of the pack. For humans though, a single parent, especially woman, are looked down on for raising their child by themselves. I don\u2019t understand. Humans have families and friends. Why do they not aid in the rearing of loved one\u2019s child?<br /> <br /> After the conversation wrapped up we broke up into separate groups to take care of different business. Alla, who was dress as Skadi, Dacian, Tatiana and Greta went to the Changeling Townhouse to set a trap for whoever has been after Skadi. Alla\u2019s disguise even fooled Madeline, who showed \u201cSkadi\u201d to her new room with Dacian in tow. After Madeline had left they let Tatiana and Greta in through the window so those two could hide in the closet ready to ambush anyone that came to do \u201cSkadi\u201d harm. <br /> <br /> Back at the hotel Dearbhail, Skadi and I stayed in one room while Dana, Nathan and Lizette were in another. I have an idea of what she had planned for the other two and wasn\u2019t going to get involved. Dana did extend the invitation to me, but I politely declined. Dana may be an interesting woman, but she\u2019s not my type. So, instead I got to spend time with Dearbhail, and Skadi, just talking and catching up on what we\u2019d been doing the past couple years. I was just about to ask Dearbhail if she\u2019d run into anyone that had been searching for her or any of the others, but was interrupted by the sound of Iris inviting herself into our friend\u2019s room. I walked down the hall to see what was going on. They talked back and forth, Iris in Arabic and Dana in French about this not being a good environment for experiments. I\u2019m assuming they were talking about the statues again. They eventually switched entirely to French, which was good for me. Iris offered to take a look while Dana and the others did their own thing, which did not seem to be the right thing to say to Dana at the moment. I heard a gun cock and Dana tell Iris that she would shoot the other woman if she tried anything. I decided that was my cue to intervene and so I did.<br /> <br /> I knocked and walked into to see Dana aiming a handgun at Iris\u2019s chest. Lizette sitting in a chair within easy reach of her chainsaw and Nathan standing to the side in striped pajamas. Dana for her part continued in English to tell Iris to come back another time and she can look at the statues then. Iris reiterated that the other could go on with what they were going to do and she could just look now. Suddenly Dana lowered her gun and Iris told her to put it down. Surprisingly Dana did just that and put the gun down on the table next to her. I stepped forward and at the same time Nathan stepped between Iris and Dana to protect his friend. Iris seemed to take in the situation. Looking from Lizette to me and back to Dana and decided that perhaps she ought to come back another time. Lizette was not hiding the fact that she was eyeing her chainsaw. That might have tipped things in our favor just a bit. I was not trying to act overly intimidating, but wasn\u2019t hiding the fact that I wanted Iris to leave.<br /> <br /> I walked Iris to the elevator to make sure that she got on it and left, then made my way back to the room with Dearbhail. Dearbhail as it turns out was waiting in the hall for me. She said that Skadi insisted that she needed to go to the Townhouse. She needed to go where her double was. So, I offered to drive and the three of us headed over there. She was not sure if Alla was in danger, she just said that she needed to be there. So we went. As I was slowing down to park Skadi surprised us both by opening the door and jumping out. Immediately upon landing she masked her presence and her scent and took off. We assumed that she was heading for the room that Alla was in so we parked the car and headed that way.<br /> <br /> When we got there it was to a stand-off. Th\u00e9r\u00e8se was in the room aiming a gun at Alla, who she thought was Skadi. She accused Skadi of killing her lover, Jarbeaux. Then just as suddenly the real Skadi was there and putting a knife made of ice toTh\u00e9r\u00e8se r\u00e8se\u2019s throat. Tatiana and Greta came out of the closet to confront the would-be killer. Tatiana let Dacian in and a moment later and Dearbhail and I joined the group. We all tried to talk Th\u00e9r\u00e8se down. So, it boiled down to Th\u00e9r\u00e8se wanting revenge for her lover, and Skadi arguing that she had killed Jarbeaux because he\u2019d been a commander during the war. She was eliminating a threat before he could act. Th\u00e9r\u00e8se of course did not see it this way. She only saw that her fianc\u00e9 was killed and she finally found out who had done it.<br /> <br /> Everyone tried a different tactic for talking to Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. Dearbhail was trying to appeal to her love of Jarbeaux and keep to that memory instead of the hate for Skadi. Dacian tried to talk her down with reason. It was discussed that killing that killing Jarbeaux was not honorable because it was done by stealth. The response to that was that Th\u00e9r\u00e8se\u2019s own actions regarding Skadi were not honorable then either. Tatiana tried arguing that commanders die in war and that Jarbeaux should have known that he was in danger and that he might die. I tried telling her that the dead do not care about revenge. Vengeance is for the living, not those who have passed on. In the end I don\u2019t know if we convinced Th\u00e9r\u00e8se of anything, but Tatiana did take the pistol away from her and Skadi let her ice dagger melt. Th\u00e9r\u00e8se did at least relent on her plan to attack tonight, but then a moment later she broke down into tears. Dearbhail took Th\u00e9r\u00e8se to another room to calm down. The French woman\u2019s anger had seemed to run out and she became upset and was crying for her lost love. I found that I could not relate to her pain. I know that I should at least feel sympathy, but I did not. It is one of my failings. I just don\u2019t feel empathy for those outside of my pack. I can fake it sometimes, and sometimes if a stranger gets close enough to someone in my pack I may become somewhat protective of them, but not often. Dana has become dear to Lizette and I do not want to see the slight French woman upset, so I protect Dana. I will admit that when I interrupted her conversation with Iris earlier I was ready to protect her should Iris become violent. <br /> <br /> Later Dearbhail asked me if I would go after someone if they murdered someone that I cared about. I answered \u201cYes.\u201d I would hunt that person down and tear out their throat in a heartbeat. I did admit that my response may not be the correct answer though. I am not a good person and will not always take the \u201cgood path.\u201d Dearbhail tried to argue that I am a good person. I conceded that I am good to the pack, but not to strangers. They don\u2019t matter. Not to me anyway. She, it seems, wanted to know what I would do because she wasn\u2019t sure what she would do in that situation. I told her that death leads to death and that it has to stop somewhere. If a person can stop the cycle then it can end, but killing someone in vengeance does not bring them back, it only causes retaliation in kind. Well, sometimes it does. I think that if Dearbhail can just hold onto the love of the person she lost that will make her the better person. I know that is not me, and am fine with that. I am an assassin by trade. I kill strangers for money. I have no problems doing that. If someone were to actually hurt or kill one of the few people that I actually do have feelings for they would die a very slow and painful death. I did not tell Dearbhail exactly what my plans would be for someone that killed someone dear to me. She didn\u2019t want to hear the details and that is fine. I did not want to upset her with them.<br /> <br /> In a way I have two packs. I have my biological family. My father, brother, his wife and their little girl. My sister-in-law\u2019s family is included because they are blood kin to her and she is pack. My other pack is this disparate group of people that I find myself with now. They have all become important to me and anyone that hurts them will answer to me. If I am unable to exact revenge then I know that Tatiana will carry it out for me. She is just as protective as I am of those she regards. The difference is she has empathy for a much larger number of people than I do. There is strength in that I suppose.<br /> <br /> After we talked I took Dearbhail back to the hotel. I think she was a little depressed over the events of the evening. Or perhaps she wanted to focus on being alive rather than contemplating the dead. In either case I was surprised when we got back to the room to have her jump up and straddle my hips. She was obviously interested in one thing and I was not going to turn her down. The conversation earlier did nothing to put me in a bad mood, so I kissed her back and laid her down on the bed gently. Have to be mindful of those beautiful wings.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 28 April, 1922<br /> <br /> I found out this morning that after Dearbhail and I left that Alla went to the theater to talk to Agrippa. That was her plan anyway. Wolfram pointed out that Agrippa had been working hard to make this play happen so it might not be a good idea to confront her about wanting to summon some other worldly being. Instead Alla decided to socialize with Constancia. The actors had left the theater already so Alla went to the Museum, assuming correctly that they would be there. Against Wolfram\u2019s advice Emilie went to talk to Agrippa alone, in her car. Connie it seems persuaded the once reluctant woman to finally go talk to the elder vampire. My pack mates were not sure if some sort of vampire gift was used or not, Wolfram couldn\u2019t tell, but he did his best to make sure that Emilie would walk away from the conversation as she entered it, still breathing. They were assured that Emilie would not be \u201cconverted\u201d that evening. Alla arrived shortly after that and talked to Wolfram and Fenric. Emilie came back okay and it was discovered that she is at least safe from the vampires until after the play is over. Alla then got her chance to catch up with Connie and did so.<br /> <br /> Dacian also mentioned that he tried to talk to Terese after the confrontation last night. Apparently she was very upset and despondent. He was afraid that she would try and kill herself. It was probably a good thing that when Tatiana and Greta left to go for a walk Tatiana took Terese\u2019s gun with her. Madeline took Terese to get some help and to make sure that the suicidal woman was not left alone. I will admit that I did not quite understand her desire to do herself harm. I have admitted that I\u2019m having a hard time empathizing with the woman, and that may be playing a part in not understanding her situation. I do not know what I would do if I lost someone important to me now. I remember losing my mother to illness when I was a child. She had been sick for a while that winter and eventually it got to the point that she couldn\u2019t breathe. It was pneumonia that got her in the end. The local doctor could only do so much for her and we couldn\u2019t afford to go to one of the big cities to go to a hospital. My brother, father and I mourned. They mourned longer. I seemed to accept it quicker than they did, though I did not let that be known to the village in general. Again, nosy people. I was ever the topic of conversation among the villagers. I was \u201cthat odd little Ruzicka boy.\u201d I didn\u2019t make friends as easily as others did and tended to prefer the company of adults. Children are so unpredictable, it was always easier to mimic the adults around me. They at least seemed consistent in their behavior.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t really thought about loved ones dying lately. I worried for my brother during the war, but the war is over now. We are not likely to see such a conflict again in our lifetimes. I forget about the mundane things, such as illness, that can claim a life. So I find myself this morning thinking about mortality and wondering how I\u2019ll react when someone I care for dies. Practically, if Andel dies, then I will provide for his family as best I can. I cannot be present to help raise the child, but I can provide financially for them. Money is not the answer to all problems but it certainly helps solve some of them. Emotionally I do not know how I\u2019d handle it if my little brother passed away. I suppose it would depend on the manner of his passing. If he were killed then the guilty party would die. However long it took, they would die. If illness takes him I would be without a target, so I don\u2019t know how I\u2019d react. I suppose that I\u2019d be angry. Sad seems a given. I just don\u2019t know how I would react to those emotions.<br /> <br /> But back to the issues at hand. This morning we discussed whether or not we were going to let Iris take a look at the statues before we try to use the W\u0101s or not. We might find out something about the statues beforehand if we do let her investigate them. She can interact with them in a way that others cannot, which is interesting in and of itself. If we let her do that then we can try the W\u0101s on them at our chateau. Dana agreed to let us try the W\u0101s on the statues there instead of a rented house, since we know our place is secure. I believe that Lizette was instrumental in getting Dana to agree to that. Nathan just went along with the plan as we discussed it. <br /> <br /> So far the plan is to have Dacian \u201cacquire\u201d the W\u0101s from the Post Office so no one is seen picking it up by any interested parties. Then Lizette and myself will go with Dana when she goes to meet with Iris to make sure everything works out okay. Sounds too easy if you ask me. I can\u2019t help but wonder what obstacles or dangers await us as we attempt to pursue information about these statues. A storm already seems to be following Dana because of them. What else is out there preparing to sabotage our plans? I guess that I\u2019ll just have to prepare for the worst and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Bah, volchonok, I do not wish to speak of that now.<br /> <br /> Because. It is a... well, fairly unpleasant morning for walking, but there are no boring jobs to tend to at the moment, and I do not wish to spoil my mood for visiting Elena by speaking of foolish things.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, foolish human things. Bah. Pampered noble women, believing that because they have money and power and beauty, they are immune to war. At least I know it is not because she is a fairy noble. Skadi is the least pighead stupid about these things of any noble I have met.<br /> <br /> Do you wish me to count the foolish human things, volchonok? You might run out of toes.<br /> <br /> Well, there is the foolishness of Wolfram and Christina\u2019s pup.<br /> <br /> I do not understand, volchonok, do not ask me. But it is important to Wolfram that we do not speak of it. I would have thought that would just be around others, but apparently we are not to even speak the truth among pack and mates.<br /> <br /> Bah. I have given up understanding Christina at all. She is lovely and kind and cares for Wolfram very much, and is so very noble-stupid. The others said it was because Lizette cannot be with Christina because she is to be married and therefore Lizette is with Dana and so Christina is angry at Dana. I am glad none of them are my mate.<br /> <br /> Pfff.<br /> <br /> What? No, volchonok, I did not leave before Madeleine got there because she would be like Christina and be mad at Greta. It is nothing like that at all.<br /> <br /> I left because that place was full of foolishness - like this conversation - and besides, Madeleine probably agrees with Th\u00e9r\u00e8se and she would be much less attractive if I knew that was true for certain.<br /> <br /> Of course I would kill anyone who assassinated Elena! That is not a question, and you would do well to not test me, volchonok.<br /> <br /> I do not blame her for her attempt. I do not think she should be punished. As I said, I would do the same. Well, except I would succeed. But her words, her blathering about honor, as if Skadi did something wrong... she does not understand what war is, just what it does to those who touch it from afar.<br /> <br /> Skadi was a leader of men on the battlefield, who saw the pain and suffering of her soldiers and decided to end it by cutting off the head of the enemy. If one goes to war, one must expect to die. If her fiance believed himself above such thing because he was an officer, because he was one who merely decided who would be sent to die, that does not make it true.<br /> <br /> I did make a promise I would kill Skadi and promises to fairies hold weight. Still, it was an easy promise. If war begins again in my lifetime, I am unlikely to fight for the Germans, for certain. If this happens, and Skadi leads them, I will make use of her own plan and cut off their head. I do not believe it will come to that however.<br /> <br /> Come now volchonok. Leave me be.<br /> <br /> You are wro -<br /> <br /> Fine. If I say this thing, you will leave this conversation be?<br /> <br /> Very well. Yes, Dearbhail did scold me, and rightly. I was unkind to Th\u00e9r\u00e8se, who has felt true loss, no matter how foolish she was being. I apologized, as I was in the wrong. Satisfied, volchonok?<br /> <br /> Thank the spirits.<br /> <br /> We are walking to Elena, as I told you.<br /> <br /> Well, we do not know who set the fires, but thanks to the commotion, an ambush will not work so soon. Agrippa has promised to leave the actress alone. Marek and Lizette are with Dana as she speaks to Iris. Dacian will steal the true was. There is no fighting to be had. So I am free to do as I wish.<br /> <br /> Since the was will be arriving shortly, Dana wishes Iris\u2019 advice about the statues, before we take them to our den to test them.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we cannot run off today. I must convince Elena to take the boys on a holiday. Later perhaps, once this storm has broken and my love is safe. But not right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 28th April 1922, Morning<br /> <br /> Well! Yesterday turned awkward.<br /> <br /> Christina came by while we were preparing. She was, of course, radiant. It was wonderful to see her. But a lot of awkward things happened. For one, She started asking me about men I might settle down and start a family with, and pointed me toward Nathan. I told her Dr. Hinshaw was handsome, but I was not looking to settle down and besides he is not Catholic. Well, I guess not, it is unusual for Scotsman to be Catholic, isn\u2019t it? She noted he could convert, and indicated Wolfram. I admitted this was so, but I was unsure about the whole thing. <br /> <br /> Somewhere in there Dana arrived, and the temperature dropped. Christina was nothing but polite to \u201cMiss Barlowe\u201d but looked like she wanted to hurt her. Christina was not mean or crass per se, of course, such is not in her nature, but her distaste for Dana was quite apparent. Dana seemed somewhat taken off guard by the whole thing, and soon retreated to keep the peace, which returned Christina to her good humor. I know it was about me, and it became clear why she wanted me to have a family; even though we have broken off our relationship (I can\u2019t sleep with my best friend\u2019s wife!) she is intensely jealous of other women with regard to me. I guess men are okay? This does explain why has been reluctant for me to be alone with Marlene. Speaking of which I am hopeful Marlene meets someone at the Wedding. She is an intelligent girl and has made an excellent student. She can fix a car and field strip a Tommy Gun now. Not a bad shot with a pistol either. Oh, and I helped her with Math.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Dana seemed a bit dumfounded. She (and I) thought my relationship with Christina was over. Do I need to talk to her about this? Dana says most women don\u2019t hate her so much unless she has stolen something from them. Perhaps Christina feels like she has.<br /> <br /> So in case this was not bad or embarrassing enough, Marlene dropped a few hints Christina should not exert herself (which is fine) but after she left this prompted discussion were Tatiana noted out loud she was pregnant. I am not one given to Noble foibles; I think Nobles are crazy however I care for Wolfram or Christina. However\u2026this really is beyond the pale. One does not point out a soon to be married woman is pregnant. There is no reason to soil her good name. Are Russians really that boorish, or just Tatiana? Probably just Tatiana. But still, it was awkward.<br /> <br /> I suppose the pregnancy could be making Christina jealous or moody. Oh what would happen if I had children? I hope they would be tall. And\u2026not green. I mean, actually as I think of it maybe green would not be so bad, if it was secret green. But if they were small they could use my custom airplane seat. Or as kids. I mean, children will inherit this new world they should be able to fly a fighter plane. Yes! And Wolfram\u2019s kids can too! They will be the ultimate fighting flyers!<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway then\u2026then Dana\u2019s children came up, and it came up somehow I was apparently not that far in age from Christina\u2019s daughter. I am twenty-one, she is in her later teens I think, so I suppose it is close, but Dana began to feel rather uncomfortable about this and some of the Motley seemed to find this amusing. Dana also mentioned she was going to try to keep us from meeting. If she is anything like her mother, I can imagine why, and suspect this is a very good idea.<br /> <br /> I wonder if she could help me with Marlene\u2019s training. Any young woman in this new century could benefit from the sort of tips and tricks Dana knows. There is more to life than housekeeping. There is also piloting planes into enemy territory and raining bombs and gunfire on the ground.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> So we split up for the night. The plan was I would guard Dana, Nathan, and the statuettes. Wolfram and Fenric would go with Emilie to practice for the play, and Wolfram would puzzle out how to prevent the ritual. Dearbh\u00e1il and Marek would guard Skadi, and Dacian, Tatiana and Alla would lay a trap for the arsonists, with help from Greta, who they brought in because Tatiana is insane.<br /> <br /> For my part things were quiet but, again, awkward. Dana wanted to get Nathan and I in bed at the same time. I am fairly unsure about having sex with two people at the same time and I don\u2019t know Nathan well, and I don\u2019t want to get pregnant. Yet. Also, he seemed\u2026unsure himself. The detente was broken anyway when Iris arrived, wanting to see the statues. Also, her locking faces with Dana may have put the others of us off a bit. Dana was quick to draw a gun on Iris, but Iris was quite smooth, talking to Dana as a lover and talking about how they are on the same side. Dana was highly suspicious; I found out later she suspected Iris had stolen the fake was that arrived today. Then Marek showed up, because of course he did. There were women in their nightclothes. The only good thing was when Iris was faced with Dana, Nathan, Marek and myself she decided discretion was the better part of valor. Marek walked her out and we were returned to our discussion. I had presumed Marek went to be bedded by Iris, but apparently not.<br /> <br /> Iris had broken the spell a bit, though, and Nathan rather quickly retired to his room. Dana was frustrated, and I asked if my being around was helping or hurting. She admitted she wanted time alone to clear her head, so I took the statuettes, told her I loved her, and waited outside a bit. After a little while, Marek and Dearbh\u00e1il came back and went straight to his room to make some headboard music. When Dacian and Skadi returned, they told me that Th\u00e9r\u00e8se had tried to kill Skadi as her fianc\u00e9e Jarbeaux had been assassinated by Skadi during the war. Skadi was an assassin and lead other Winter Court assassins during the war to apparently kill French freedom fighters. The others had sided with Skadi, but not killed Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. I have to say, they were kinder than I. Had my lover been murdered, I would see the assassin put down. My Motley seemed to have a different opinion on how to deal with the murder of their lovers. Or I should say, how to deal with other people\u2019s lovers being murdered. Had it been one of them, I suspect they would have done what Th\u00e9r\u00e8se had done, not stood in her way.<br /> <br /> After a time Wolfram returned with Fenric and Emilie. He reported Alla had gone off hunting with Constancia. Apparently Agrippa had met with Emilie after sending Connie for her, and they established a d\u00e9tente of the their own. However, it seemed likely a Vampire might make a play for her after the, well, play, but then if we sabotage it who knows what might happen?<br /> <br /> I filled him in on the Changeling situation. We also spoke briefly on Dana and Nathan. Wolfram assured me I was not being prudish for not going along with Dana\u2019s \u201cparty.\u201d We discussed it a bit. As a modern woman I want to be up for modern things, but I don\u2019t need to move too fast.<br /> <br /> I returned to the room, where Dana was feeling some better. She is, I think, greatly unaccustomed to rejection. We spent the night cuddling and being warmed by each other, and we both went to sleep happy. It was, in some ways, almost better than the nights of torrid sex.<br /> <br /> Almost.<br /> <br /> <br /> 28th April 1922, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Morning meeting is becoming a tradition.<br /> <br /> Dana had fire in her eyes. She plans to get her was at 3:00 today and wants to get to work experimenting with the statuettes. First subject was where do we do it? The Hedge came up and was rejected based on my advice. I confess I missed some of the discussion as I was getting petted, but Dana has tentatively agreed we should meet at our Chateau. It was made clear this was against her usual way, but she almost implicitly trusted me, so she was willing to go with it. As soon as she gets the was, she wants to start trying to use it with the Statuettes.<br /> <br /> Once the decision on where was complete, Iris came up again. Dana really seemed to want her along, while most of us really did not. Dana admitted Iris knew a lot, but could not be trusted. She got Dacian\u2019s attention noting Iris had a lot of the strange tech, but also said she could not find any of it, you know when she was robbing her. Sigh. So apparently stealing from each other is a thing those women do. What am I getting into? Does Dana actually love me?<br /> <br /> Okay time to roll out. Dacian is going to steal the was for Dana, and Dana is going to talk to Iris with Marek and I. Because of course Marek. We will see how it goes.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> Oh Lizette, you so silly.<br /> <br /> The clash between Th\u00e9r\u00e8se and Skadi had been foreshadowed, somewhat. Skadi said she did things she was not proud of during the war, Lucille said Th\u00e9r\u00e8se lost someone important, and Mrs. Skitters noted Th\u00e9r\u00e8se\u2019s dislike for Germans despite her being a Spring Courtier trying to get Skadi to come. It was nothing I expected to be predicted, but the signs were there.<br /> <br /> So who was right? Does Th\u00e9r\u00e8se deserve vengeance for the death of her Fianc\u00e9e? Would you forgive the person who killed your Fianc\u00e9e? Does the war mitigate it? It makes punishment harder, true, but what if you had the chance. That is the question posted to the PCs, and perhaps the players, this time.<br /> <br /> Past that how about Iris eh? That sets up for tonight\u2019s session, just as Wolfram saw the setup for the next. This story is winding down. Another comes soon. But Dana (and Iris) unlock the secret of the Statuettes next time, and they must decide what to do with such dangerous relics\u2026and who is right in Dana and Iris\u2019s conflict. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T09:49:44-07:00","id":852459,"title":"","content":"I started reading Balance of Shadows at work a while ago, while trying to work out how Geist works to help a player in my own crossover game. Now it is 2 months later, and I have ran out of CoD AP's by you to read. Great stuff! I suppose I'll have to start the VtM or Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:44:03-07:00","id":852515,"title":"","content":"Heh I will pass it along, thanks! But the good news is at least two updates a week ^_^ If you have any other comments or questions let know, and thanks so much for the feedback.<br /> <br /> ETA: I run WoD and CoD in a very similar style, so since you enjoyed CoD so much<i> Conspiracy</i> will be most like them. I mean, 500 year old vampires but otherwise like them. Scion is much more action oriented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-24-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T05:13:38-07:00","id":852903,"title":"","content":"I actually started reading Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora, lol. <br /> <br /> I do have a question for you actually. How do you manage to plan so many games at once? My game is only a couple of hours a week, and I feel like I'm always underprepared for all the crossoverness. We have a Mage, a Sin Eater, a Changeling, a Hunter, and a Custom Template, plus a Stigmatic and second Sin Eater that sometimes show up, plus dealing with Vampire and Mummy for antagonists. You have at least as many gamelines on your mind, plus seperated into three (?) games per week. So are you an Arcanthus or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:55:21-07:00","id":852972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=852903#post852903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually started reading Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora, lol.<br /> <br /> I do have a question for you actually. How do you manage to plan so many games at once? My game is only a couple of hours a week, and I feel like I'm always underprepared for all the crossoverness. We have a Mage, a Sin Eater, a Changeling, a Hunter, and a Custom Template, plus a Stigmatic and second Sin Eater that sometimes show up, plus dealing with Vampire and Mummy for antagonists. You have at least as many gamelines on your mind, plus seperated into three (?) games per week. So are you an Arcanthus or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm betting on a distributed AI masquerading as a human to gather sociological and behavioral data. No way a simple meat and bone human has enough time or processing power to conduct this many games, at this level of quality, in parallel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:58:00-07:00","id":853155,"title":"","content":"Heh, okay, actual answer:<br /> <br /> I run 2 games per week. My weekly prep time is near zero. Because I am a freak. I have Attention Deficit Hyperactive Disorder (ADHD). This was hellish in school. This works to my advantage in game. My mind has &quot;tracks,&quot; which is to say I can be running a scene with one &quot;track&quot; while planning the next scene with a second &quot;track.&quot; I can have outright conversations with myself IC because each &quot;track&quot; is following one speaker, and I essentially have two &quot;subroutines&quot; going each of which is a different personality. Once a PC or NPC has their &quot;subroutine&quot; in my mind, I can talk IC as them endlessly without thinking about it, because their &quot;subroutine&quot; is well fleshed out. You get that with authors talking about voices. Character voices or &quot;subroutines&quot; crystallize quickly for me, and they can go so independently <i>I have to stop and think about/catch up with what an NPC just did, because my focus was elsewhere</i> while I ran that NPC and I<i> did not realize </i><i>what they were doing</i>. That is not normal. It also means that it is harder to plan strictly, because for example often Dana is going to do whatever the hell Dana is going to do, even if it runs afoul my plans (Dana is a pain that way). Last session Dana pulled a gun and kidnapped Iris. I was not planning that; she just did it.<br /> <br /> So while I am crazy, I am so creative my mind can barely cope. This means it does whatever it does, and often this involves scaring the hell out of myself while alone at night, because my mind is a bitch that way. But, it means I can often just let it do it's thing. This has a huge impact on how I run. For most games, not including <i>Golden Eagle</i>, this means the games essentially run themselves. Most games have a ton of prepwork initially and little afterwards<i>. Balance of Shadows</i> had almost 3 months of work before session 1. Since then, while I have worked on future plotlines, I have sat and worked on prep for an imminent session approximately three times in six years, and those were all cases where I had to prep combat. And some of the initial work is still not touched on. We touched on a plot for that game last Sunday I worked on February of 2010. Now, I have prepped for Geist\u2026the Haunted Hotel plot I had later, but I worked on it a month before it happened in game. The skeleton of the Bright Shadow Plot? Before the first session.<br /> <br /> This means I create scenarios more than plots. What\u2019s going on? Who are the personalities? I work that out first. Then, I make sure there is a way for the PCs to deal with it. In the late 90s I ran several \u201cBig Empties\u201d, Vampire games with huge, intricate plots and major movements and bored PCs because they never saw any of it. But these outlines are rarely prepping for the session immediately. Some are worked out way ahead because I got an idea in the car (or had a nightmare, the case with the Hotel BoS one), some are, literally, planned from spark to finish in the scene before they begin, while I am running that scene, because I got an idea and set my second \u201ctrack\u201d on it while my main one does the scene. Next scene I introduce a plot that did not exist when we sat down for the game an hour ago, and by the end of the first scene of the PCs dealing with it, 30 minutes after it\u2019s genesis, it is done and ready.<br /> <br /> <i>Golden Eagle</i> is something of an exception. It\u2019s not a big sandbox, it is little sandboxes, and thus <i>Golden Eagle</i> is more work than every other game combined. I prep scenarios, not sessions, even then. We have ~2-3 sessions of Paris left, and I am prepping Berlin story. By the time we get done, it should be (mostly) ready. Then I won\u2019t need to work on <i>Golden Eagle</i> again till the next scenario after Berlin. I mean, I may do so, but won\u2019t need to. Still, compared to the small prep time for other games, that is a lot.<br /> <br /> The main prep time is pictures. I am always adding NPCs, and everyone needs a picture. So webcrawls for pics do happen. Sometimes a single picture creates an entire scenario in my head; In <i>Night Train</i>, Nikka\u2019s entire storyline came from a single picture. I looked at the picture, I had a plot. Same with Chalcedony; it was a picture I had from Castle Falkenstein; I looked at the picture and said \u201cNow who would you be in Changeling?\u201d and it all came out. My games are very driven by PC and NPC personalities, this is a big part of why. My players are happy to spend a lot of time exploring their PCs and NPCs more than Dungeoneering, which is not to say a damn thing against Dungeoneering, but I know where my talents lie.<br /> <br /> This means, incidentally, I suck at crunch heavy games. I can be a bit airy fairy with WoD or CoD stats, but crunch can be rough. My Deadlands: Lost Colony game slammed to a halt because while I had a sandbox, it was far, far too much bookkeeping to plan the many combat encounters that went with that game. Both because it was a lot of combat, and because I could not eyeball it and say \u201cOkay, she probably has 3 Dexterity, 4 Athletics\u2026say 2 Wits\u2026\u201d if combat came up I did not expect, so I had to prep for anything like that the PCs might do. It was a good game, but it fell apart for that reason (and then <i>Malibu Dream House</i> started with the same group and went well.)<br /> <br /> So I run 4 games a fortnight, two a week. I can do this because they are low prep and I am a freak of nature. But if I can clarify anything lemme know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-25-2016, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:31:57-07:00","id":853242,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks for such a detailed answer! I'm pretty bad on the crunch myself, and play pretty fast and loose with more complicated rules. I'm 100% certain that I'm doing paradox risk for my Mage's Creative Thaumaturgy wrong, but I figure as long as everyone is having fun and the players understand the risk, than no harm, no foul. <br /> <br /> Sadly, my players love going in for dungeon crawly type situations, especially if they can try to dive into something I hadn't expected them to even go near, lol. Most recently, they rescued a PC's daughter from a cult, and fixed her memory alterations. So, rather than sit down and talk to her about where the escaped cult leader might have gone, they decide to go dive into investigating where some hunters (that had helped them against a group of Vampires almost 6 months ago) had gone, leading them into a Vampire nest (I had decided long ago that had been their off screen fate). So... fun times preparing a short dungeon crawl on short notice.<br /> <br /> Speaking of pictures, I love yours. I've noticed you seem to have Amanda Seyfried in just about every game, which is funny to me cause I have her as an NPC myself. Do you do pictures for locations too, or just people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T18:39:31-07:00","id":853271,"title":"","content":"I and one of my players are in love with Amanda Seyfried, so it is a thing. I think it is just Demon and Geist. Ms. Seyfried seemed a good example for Inhuman Beauty.<br /> <br /> And yea I have to play fast and loose with the mages sometimes.<br /> <br /> In the end, you have to work out with your group what everyone wants. I try to be as transparent as possible, and let my players alternate between Actor and Author stance (seeing their game through their character and seeing the experience as the writer of the character) and give them some ability to make narrative changes. it is good you account for your players tastes in planning your sessions.<br /> <br /> ETA: It goes without saying borrowing characters or scenarios or concepts is fine for readers. I would be curious to hear of their use if people did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:36:40-07:00","id":856769,"title":"","content":"Lizz's comment about flyers makes me think she will absolutely love the Night Witches when they form during the next war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:46:14-07:00","id":856874,"title":"","content":"Probably. I will have to make sure to work something with them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:02:00-07:00","id":857569,"title":"","content":"The moment of truth: Do the PCs back Dana, who has refused to explain herself frequently and mislead them but never lied, and helped them with their business, or back Iris, who has used powers on them but has not lied anyone knows of and had Dana pull a gun on her every time? Lizette\u2019s affections muddy the water, but it is time to see what the statuettes are, at least in part, and determine if the Conspiracy sides with Dana or Iris<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 28 April 1922<br /> <br /> We decided that Dana, Lizette and I would be the ones to go and meet up with Iris in her room. When we arrived and walked inside Dana surprised all of us by pulling a gun on Iris and telling her that the only way that she\u2019s going to be taken to the Chateau is bound and blindfolded. Dana really does not trust Iris, not even a little bit. Iris for her part went along with it and allowed herself to be bound and blindfolded. We then proceeded to escort Iris to the Chateau via the \u201cHedge\u201d as my fae friends have called that strange place between worlds. This would provide a faster way to get to the house than driving there. It also gives the illusion that the house is much closer to Paris than it actually is. So we arrived a short time later and untied Iris so she could freshen up and wait in one of the guest rooms in the Guest House. I believe it is called that. We were not in the main Chateau, just one of the smaller buildings behind it. Still rather nice though. I guarded the door to make sure that Iris would not leave.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Dacian went to the post office to retrieve the w\u0101s discreetly. Apparently upon arriving he noticed Ewan Brandon waiting outside the post office smoking a cigarette, and inside there was another Changeling going over the packages with her hands like she was trying to sense something. The postal workers seemed to ignore her so she must have had some gift active that allowed her to blend in like she was supposed to be there. After she left Dacian was able to step up his search, but all told it still took him about an hour to find the right package. He grumbled that he had forgotten how to read French. I think that there was just a lot of packages to go through. His explanation is possible too. When you speak a number of languages sometimes it is easy to switch to different one mid thought. I myself think in different languages sometimes. I don\u2019t know if there is a pattern to it, but it is easy to mix things up. Lizette then spoke up saying that she recognized the Changeling that Dacian described. Apparently she is an Autumn courtier named Shalice who is something of a Librarian for the Autumn Court. We\u2019re still not sure what she was doing there.<br /> <br /> So then Dacian gave Dana the w\u0101s back. An interesting thing happened at that point. Dana\u2019s eyes and the w\u0101s glowed blue for just a moment before going back to normal. She was also very keen on getting that thing back, so I\u2019m not sure exactly what kind of connection Dana has with that device but I have a feeling it\u2019s probably not an especially healthy one. After Dana got her wand back and Lizette had rigged the statues with explosives, just in case something went really wrong, I was given the go ahead to let Iris out of the guest room. So I did. Iris and I walk into the main room and almost immediately Dana pointed the w\u0101s at Iris and suddenly there is a blue light between Dana and Iris and then Iris was no longer there. In her place was a creature like the ones we fought on the train when we first met. She had six arms, reverse articulated legs and metallic skin. Now, apparently this creature was Iris, it talked with her voice anyway, and her human form is a way for her to blend in. I\u2019m not thinking her natural form would be overly accepted by the public. Dearbhail confirmed that iris\u2019s main desire at that moment was to acquire the w\u0101s.<br /> <br /> Iris called herself an unchained and that she is actively working against something she calls the machine god. She said that she was here to determine what the statues are and what they do. She also entreated Dana to let her turn back to her human form because she would be visible by this machine god while she was in her natural state. Dana was controlling when Iris could change with the w\u0101s, which is just interesting, and eventually agreed and shifted her nemesis back to her human shape. Around this tie Lizette comes back to say that everything is all set with the statues, so we all go to the room where they were being kept. We allowed Iris to take a look at the statues and in turn Iris asks some basic questions which seemed applicable to the devices. She asked where they had been found, which Dana was reluctant to answer. I\u2019m not sure why she is keeping the location a secret. Maybe there are more statues like the three that she has and she doesn\u2019t want Iris to find them. Or she could just be spiting her once lover. In any case Iris said that the three statues are part of some larger machine. They are merely a device used to store energy, much like a battery. Only the kind of energy that she describes sounds like what ghosts and spirits use to power their abilities. It is possible that these statues are responsible for the storm in Paris as well, though Dana did not knowingly create the storm in the first place.<br /> <br /> The thing that is troubling to me about these statues is that it is likely that there is a way to release the energy that they contain both with and without the original machine that they are a part of. Without the machine we don\u2019t know what would happen. It might release the energy in a rapid flash and injure those of us around it, or it could release in a slow steady stream. I think we are all leaning towards the former possibility. Now the difference comes when they are plugged into the machine that they came from. Iris\u2019s theory is that they could be used to power a weapon that would cause destruction on a global scale. Or if it\u2019s not designed as a weapon it might be used that way by some inspired individual. I recommended that we destroy the statues. They are too dangerous to keep around. It was argued that if we try to destroy them we might release the energy that is stored in them and cause mass amounts of damage. Iris also revealed that the w\u0101s is a master control device, and that while there are other such devices out there they are rare and hard to find. The w\u0101s it seems can also override and control the statues and Iris for that matter. I guess that explains why Iris wants it so much. <br /> <br /> We talked for a little while longer about the devices, but in the end there wasn\u2019t much more to say. Dearbhail offered to take Iris back to Paris and Tatiana went with her to make sure she was safe. We blindfolded and bound Iris again so she wouldn\u2019t know where our Chateau is and let our winged companion guide her back to the hotel in Paris. As soon as they\u2019d left Dana reiterated that Iris is not a good person and that we cannot trust her. She suspects that if Iris had the w\u0101s she would use it to control similar devices to what we had to destroy her machine god. Dana herself tried to use the was on the statues and got them to light up individually. She believed that she would be able to exert the correct amount of control to end the storm once we got back to Paris. When we met up with Dearbhail and Tatiana later they said that Iris warned them not to trust Dana and that she is not a good person. Same warning from both sides it seems. She reiterated that Dana cannot be trusted to keep her word and that she was afraid that Dana would betray us the way she did her. The warning is fair. Dana did betray her lover, so it stands to reason that she\u2019d have no problems betraying people she just met. For my part I am keeping an eye out for any suspicious behavior from Dana or Nathan, nothing has changed in that regard.<br /> <br /> The topic of what we were going to do with the statues after the storm was dealt with came up, and we all agreed that it would not be safe to leave them in the museum. As much as they should be there and I think Dana really wishes they could be left there, it\u2019s just not safe. There are too many people and groups out to get their hands on the statues. They\u2019d be stolen within the week if we left them at the museum. And we don\u2019t know what these different groups know about the statues and their capabilities. It\u2019s entirely possible that others know about what they can do and want to take advantage of that knowledge and use them. It\u2019s also possible that those different groups don\u2019t have unethical plans for the statues, but we don\u2019t know what they will do and can\u2019t take the chance. These statues are too powerful to let them fall into the wrong hands. Especially if they could cause global damage. The world is just now starting to get over the Great War, it doesn\u2019t need more trouble. In the end I think we agreed that we\u2019d store them in the Hedge house, or Hollow as Dacian called it. It would only be accessible by other fae-kind and even then would still be protected while in the house.<br /> <br /> So, we went back to the museum to use the statues to stop the storm. We ran into the curator while we were there and told him that we would not be leaving the statues in his care. We were perhaps not as polite as we could have been when dealing with him, but he got the message in the end and left us to our own devices. Dana used the w\u0101s to activate the statues and concentrated on stopping the storm. It wasn\u2019t immediate, but eventually the rain started slowing down and the clouds dispersed. After we\u2019d done what we came to do we left the museum and headed back to the hotel. We passed Tatiana and Dearbhail on the way back and we all made our way to the hotel for dinner. Today was long and eventful and didn\u2019t stop there.<br /> <br /> At dinner Dana explained about what happened with the w\u0101s that started this whole distrust between herself and Iris. We knew that Dana had been hired to acquire the w\u0101s for Iris, but then decided to keep the thing for herself. She explained that she did not trust Iris\u2019s intentions once the artifact was turned over. Apparently Iris had hired another up and coming archaeologist, who was also her lover, to retrieve an item for her and soon after he\u2019d delivered it he was murdered. Dana believed that it was Iris cleaning up any loose ends. So she was extra vigilant after she had gotten a hold of the w\u0101s, and discovered that there just happened to be a number of assassins in town during the time that Dana was supposed to be turning it over to Iris. Dana assumed that the assassins were there for her and so she decided to keep the w\u0101s for herself. That incident is also what prompted Dana to begin looking for the Golden Eagle in the first place. She wanted to be able to survive if Iris should send more assassins after her. Dana was sure that Iris has had other people that opposed her murdered, which is why she doesn\u2019t trust her at all. I guess that explains why she\u2019s always pulling a gun on the other woman and why she insisted that Iris be bound and blindfolded when we took her to the Chateau. Now, we have no absolute proof that what Dana said is the truth, but she certainly believes it.<br /> <br /> The last thing that we talked about over dinner was my little run in with someone hunting me in January. I had wanted to mention this earlier but we were always surrounded by strangers, Dana and Nathan usually. Over time those two learned about our unique qualities and we learned of theirs, well at least Dana\u2019s. So, I figured it would not cause harm to mention this bit of pack business in front of them. The others were angry that someone had come after me and they asked several questions. Only some of which I had the answer to. I could tell them where the man found me and that he had silver bullets. I also mentioned the photograph. They were all very interested in finding the person responsible, even Dacian who is normally so affable, was enraged on my behalf. If we didn\u2019t still have business in Paris I\u2019m fairly certain that my pack would be actively trying to hunt down the person that hired the assassin. I assured them that I had people looking into it, including Jamal, and would let them know as soon as I heard anything definite.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I was heartened by the reaction of my pack. I know how I\u2019d react if any of them had been hunted and their reaction mirrors my own. My reactions are not always what would be considered normal, so at least in this issue I can be assured that I would have reacted correctly. I am perhaps not as patient as I\u2019d like to be concerning my would-be killer. I find myself having to wait on others to find information for me. I do not have the resources that Jamal and Hans do, so I have to wait until they find out something that I can work with. Once I have what I need to find the individual(s) responsible I will just have to do some hunting of my own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Listen carefully, volchonok, this is very important. You must be on your guard - there may be assassins.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it has stopped raining. These assassins may be from the Pure in Vienna, so even you must be careful.<br /> <br /> No, I did not stop the rain. It was Dana, as I said before. Now, listen, they came after Marek with silver, so...<br /> <br /> With the was! Did you not pay attention? Dacian retrieved it, with only a little difficulty with the reading apparently. That is not important. What is important is they had a picture of Marek, and knew to use silver.<br /> <br /> What other threats, volchonok? The mechanical Scot that only Dacian saw? The fellow thief who stole nothing we care about? Our vampire \u2018allies\u2019? The mysterious cultists who have done nothing but linger on corners? How do these stack against a man who shot at our alpha with silver bullets?<br /> <br /> Well, yes, the assassin is dead.<br /> <br /> Bah. I do not know about this Iris. She is another of these mechanical men, but Dearbh\u00e1il says her wants are different feeling. More like a real person\u2019s. Iris says Dana broke their deal and she did. Dana could possibly say she didn\u2019t steal the was, since she had not been paid for it, but she did break the deal. But, if what Dana says is correct, she had very good reason. And kidnap her at gunpoint. She might have warned Lizette however...<br /> <br /> It would not have been an option, since they needed Lizette to cheat and bring them through the Hedge.<br /> <br /> It is true, volchonok, the mechanical woman did seem forthcoming. I don\u2019t believe we truly needed her help though, I believe Dana just wanted to use the was on her. With us around to protect her if it did not incapacitate her.<br /> <br /> We have chosen her side because Lizette likes her better.<br /> <br /> No, that does not mean Iris is a threat. She even promised so, as we walked her back, Dearbh\u00e1il and I.<br /> <br /> Ppppbt. Of course not. I am not a foolish volchonok, you are. Of course she may be lying. But soon the was and statues will be out of her reach and she knows very little of us. She is not the same threat as assassins with silver bullets.<br /> <br /> Just because one is dead, it does not mean there are no more, volchonok.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to chase for now. Soon Lizette will speak with the bullets. It is simply that you must be careful that I speak with you of this.<br /> <br /> I would not be so sure. Marek was not in the city when they found him.<br /> <br /> I said no, volchonok. There will be no running this night. Soon, we will run down those who threaten the pack. But first, we must find the scent. Calm yourself, excitable volchonok, and prepare for the hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 29<sup>th</sup> April 1922<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been an emotional rollercoaster, but I am currently riding quite high on it. I have concerns, but I have hopes as well. They say the beginning of a relationship is the most exciting part. Well Dana is exciting. She has successfully kept me off guard, and shows no sign of changing that now.<br /> <br /> It has come to pass that \u201cFollow my lead\u201d are the words I most dread hearing Dana say. In this case they preceded her taking Iris hostage at gunpoint. Of course, we were supposed to just be fetching her to take to the chateau, but apparently Dana had other ideas. We bound Iris\u2019s hands and blindfolded her. I did not feel terribly pleased about that. We cut through the Hedge, and were careful to ensure she did not know where she was. I knew Dana had claimed Iris had tried to kill her, but even so I felt sorry for Iris.<br /> <br /> While we were guiding Iris back, Dacian stole the was as planned, though he saw Ewan outside, and Shalice was looking for something. She left eventually and he went in. It took him some time to find it, but he did. Wolfram, Dearbh\u00e1il, and Fenric came back here with Nathan directly.<br /> <br /> Dana was a little scary when she got the was, to be honest. I mean she did not go mad with power, but close to it. When she acquired it, her eyes glowed momentarily. She had Marek bring in Iris, and used the was on her, which transformed Iris into a machine woman. She had reverse articulated legs, wings, several arms, and glowing amber eyes, along with red metallic skin. Sort of terrifying. But Dearbh\u00e1il confirmed her concerns were more in line with a normal person than the machines we fought, which confirmed her claim she was rogue.<br /> <br /> She said the Statuettes were modular power sources, which could release the power in controlled ways. She could, or Dana could with the was, try and work out specific power, but they are mostly bursts of power as light or weapons. Iris said with the whole greater machine, she could fire a blast at the sun.<br /> <br /> If I were building a super weapon, I am thinking some sort of floating city or citadel in the sky. You know, a sort of flying city, which would rain death down anywhere needed, and fly out over whatever lands it is needed. Would need a lot of anti-aircraft cannons, and of course a ready team of gorgeous French Gremlins. We would let Wolfram come along and be all handsome and stoic of course. I mean, why have a giant flying base without Wolfram? Maybe I should go with something like a big palace shaped like my head with some sort of huge lightning rod device in my ears I can use to smite unbelievers, or failing that people who say I don\u2019t dress femininely enough.<br /> <br /> Mayhem! Okay, where was I?<br /> <br /> And then things got ugly, and we get to the part I was dragging my feet on. Iris flat out accused Dana of taking the was and double-crossing her in Egypt. She did not hold back, telling Dana she had loved her, that she broke her heart, warning everyone, me especially, that Dana would double cross me for power. Dana angrily insisted that was not how it happened, that she had good reason to betray Iris, that she had loved Iris too, but that Iris was betraying her. Iris seized on Dana\u2019s reluctance to explain, saying Dana was not doing so for fear Iris would show the truth, and pointing out Dana had pulled a gun (or was) on her every time they had met to prove Dana\u2019s treachery.<br /> <br /> She looked right at me and called me her replacement; said Dana would betray me too.<br /> <br /> That was when Dana asked what we wanted to do with Iris, implying she was willing to kill her. She pointed out Iris might know too much. She did however, she admitted still have a soft spot for Iris. She would not kill her personally. None of us, myself included, wanted to kill Iris. Tatiana and Dearbh\u00e1il wound up taking her back to the city. She told them she was going back to Egypt.<br /> <br /> By the way, just speaking as a Catholic, I wish people would stop using this \u201cAngel\u201d and \u201cDemon\u201d terminology. These are not terms to throw around lightly. I prefer \u201cUnchained\u201d as Iris called herself, and I really think a renaming of this \u201cMachine God\u201d would be nice. Just, so we don\u2019t get blasphemous without need. I realize not everyone is Catholic here.<br /> <br /> I digress. The rest of us returned to the museum. I think things were a little muted. I was distracted and did not remember the conversation well, but I think there was little. I wore the apron with the Statuettes. Dana held my hand.<br /> <br /> Sean was upset at the museum the Statuettes had been gone. Dana ignored him and Nathan sidetracked him. Thankfully Greta did not show up to bug us. I am going to sit her down, tell her they are connected to a super weapon that can destroy the world, and if she publishes that then she may be responsible for the death of mankind. See if that shuts the little bitch up.<br /> <br /> Dana focused her power and dispelled the storm. It did not go away immediately, but after a few hours Paris was clear again. We met Dearbh\u00e1il and Tatiana at a caf\u00e9 (I took the Statuettes with me in my apron again) and Dana began to explain her side. She said she discovered her own predecessor as Iris\u2019s right hand was a handsome man who, like her, was an Archeologist without formal schooling. He had helped acquire an \u201cOld Testament Artifact,\u201d she discovered from a guide, and then immediately after giving it to Iris was murdered by assassins. Dana said she discovered assassins had come into the city but did not know their target. She did realize if she gave Iris the was she might be next, so fled. She was unsure how much Iris knew she knew. This was clearly not their last meeting, given Iris stole the was thereafter\u2026they clearly have a complicated relationship.<br /> <br /> Marek informed us at lunch that he had been hunted by a man with silver bullets. We have little to go on. Marek killed him of course, but who he was and why he was after Marek was not known. He had a picture of Marek, so probably an assassin. What skeletons in the closet does Marek have from the war? Or maybe a jealous husband hired him.<br /> <br /> All that done, Dana and I retired back to the chateau. She spent the night in my room, my first partner to do so with me. She spent much of the time trying to reassure me about her feelings for me, and trying to be emotionally available. It\u2019s hard for her.<br /> <br /> While we had breakfast this morning, she told me she hated she could not have children by me. I was not sure what to say. I still don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> <br /> 29<sup>th</sup> April 1922, Afternoon.<br /> <br /> Wolfram\u2019s bachelor party is tonight. Tatiana is planning it. I am very afraid. Dana, Dearbh\u00e1il, and Alla are keeping the statues, while Tatiana, the boys as I go. At least, I presume Alla is staying\u2026she is Sapphic as well, so one never knows.<br /> <br /> I wonder what Tatiana is planning\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> Answers that lead to more questions<br /> <br /> Lizette had to make a Clarity check for taking part in the kidnapping, but I gave her an extra die as she did not know it was a kidnapping till it started. She almost got an exceptional, so she was unfazed. The other two did not, having been mostly left out of those shenanigans, and as I say I am doing fewer such checks in this game than my others.<br /> <br /> Dacian was given a fairly simple Investigation roll to see how quickly he could find the package. It was not fast. He did it eventually. I was gonna have him compete with Shalice, but it did not seem like it would add to the story especially when his rolls were total shit, so I changed my mind.<br /> <br /> Next time is a fun all IC session: Wolfram\u2019s bachelor party! Join us then! Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T05:51:44-07:00","id":857646,"title":"","content":"I love the ambiguity with the assassins (Iris and Dana related, not Marek related). Is it an Unchained cleaning up loose ends, or someone/something else targeting the was and related items. I can see it falling out an number of ways, which is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:25:30-07:00","id":857852,"title":"","content":"Thanks Vent0. As I noted wrapping up that session &quot;So yea, Unchained femme fatale, mysterious assassins, superweapon...no way this will come up again! You will totally never fight nazis for the superweapon&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpat