/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T21:12:28-07:00","id":859446,"title":"","content":"It was a promise to my players at the beginning of the game. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:19:53-07:00","id":859868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=859446#post859446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a promise to my players at the beginning of the game. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Pure from Germany <i>was</i> a subtle nod to <a href=\"http://robzombie.com/movies/grindhouse-werewolf-women-of-the-ss/\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf Women of the SS</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:29:54-07:00","id":862410,"title":"","content":"Lots of nods like that, down to the Prussian Ivory Claw named Ilsa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T23:54:22-07:00","id":867399,"title":"","content":"Bachelor party! While technically two nights till the wedding, Walpurgis is the play, so the Conspiracy threw Wolfram a party early. Alla\u2019s player had to miss, so they drug it out a bit into a long IC session with lots of fun. So enjoy five journals this time, including the first from Wolfram! Also, Tatiana will fight you.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 29 April 1922<br /> <br /> Today picked up where yesterday left off. Lizette looked at some of the silver bullets that I had saved from the would-be assassin from January. She used a gift to \u201cread\u201d it and get any impressions she could off of it. The way she described it was like it had eyes and she was looking through them at it\u2019s past. She saw that the bullets were created by a grizzled man. From there it went to a city where it was stored for a while before being collected by my attacker. It wasn\u2019t clear if the bullets had been specifically made for him or if he was just buying them off a known seller of silver weapons. The former could be used to kill me. They got far closer to completing that goal than I would generally like to admit. If it\u2019s the later, then it\u2019s disturbing in and of itself that there is someone out there that makes silver bullets as a part of his livelihood. Either way he is causing problems for me, and by extension, my pack. I do not think that there are any kinds of weapons that my friends are particularly susceptible to, save Tatiana. It might be a good idea to just flat out ask them.<br /> <br /> Well, today was also Wolfram\u2019s bachelor party. Tatiana planned it, so you know that it had plenty of drinking and girls. Wolfram\u2019s brother Heinrich came in addition to the pack. I believe that he knows that his brother is a Claimed, a sin-eater, and probably has a good idea by now that something is odd about the rest of us as well. So, to start the bachelor party off we all went to the sauna. The lot of us wore towels and we enjoyed the hot steam. Tatiana made things more interesting by wearing her towel around her waist like the guys did. So, we all relaxed and talked about what the plans were for the rest of the evening. There was also a good deal of discussion about fire and setting people on fire and landing a plane while it was on fire. The later adventure was Lizette\u2019s. That should come as no surprise. Apparently she jumped into a plane that was on fire, threw the pilot out and proceeded to land the plane herself. All while it was on fire. Tatiana mentioned a time that she was protecting a lady\u2019s honor and doused a man, who was making unwanted advances to said lady, with vodka and lit him on fire.<br /> <br /> Then to lighten things up the conversation moved on to teas. Apparently Lizette has an interest in making her own flavored teas. Of course, things couldn\u2019t stay innocent for long and before long we were talking about pulling a tea heist to emulate the British who, according to Lizette, steal things from everyone else. I will admit that this whole conversation was a little surreal for me. I know that Lizette has interested outside of flamethrowers and heavy ordinance, but the idea of her making flavored teas seems so boring in comparison.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing to come out of the whole sauna experience was everyone\u2019s scars were exposed. I mean, I knew that Wolfram had died when a piece of metal was put through his chest when his plane exploded. It was another thing to see the scar that injury left behind. It was not a pretty scar, and was right where his heart is. Not the most pleasant way to die I would think, but at least it would have been fairly quick. Dacian has a number of sword scars high up on his chest. I\u2019m not sure if he got them sparring or if it was a remnant of his time spent in Faerie. Either way, not a happy memory I\u2019m sure. For my part the others saw my scars. I didn\u2019t point anything out but I clearly had bullet scars on my chest, arm and leg from that would-be assassin. Definitely not a happy memory for me.<br /> <br /> After the sauna we moved to a brothel where there was more drinking, dancing, and yet more drinking. We might have also had some food, but it was mostly liquor. Vodka, if Tatiana had anything to do with it. I do not think that I drank too excessively but I will admit that the events of tonight run together after a point. I do remember that we danced. Tatiana and I did a traditional Slavic dance. Lizette did a modern dance, that was really rather good. Wolfram also seemed to be enjoying himself on the dance floor. After the dancing we played a game called Spin the Bottle. It was interesting playing it as an adult. I remember playing as a boy and trying to get the bottle to point to the girl that I wanted to kiss. Not because I liked her mind you, but because it was expected of me to go for the prettiest girl. I didn\u2019t get flustered the way the other boys did when the bottle pointed to another boy. Mostly the others turned bright red and tried to get out of it or get it over with as quick as possible. I at least knew that I was supposed to be an embarrassed kid, no matter who the bottle pointed to, but it\u2019s hard to blush on command. This time around I didn\u2019t try to emulate those around me, I just kissed who the bottle pointed to. At one point Tatiana got frustrated with the bottle not pointing at her, so she took it upon herself to kiss the nearest pretty girl that was walking by.<br /> <br /> After Spin the Bottle there was darts. I believe by this point my aim was becoming impaired and I did not do as well as I\u2019d hoped. I wasn\u2019t horrible, but Lizette was much better. You\u2019d think with as much alcohol as she\u2019d consumed that she\u2019d be worse off than the rest of us, but she proved that idea wrong. Slight though she may be, she can hold her liquor. At some point during this Dacian had invited another Fae woman over to join us. She had heard about Lizette\u2019s interest in fire and asked that nothing be set alight while she was with us. So, what did we do? We played a game with fire of course. Tatiana talked us into playing a game where you coat your hand in vodka then light it on fire. You pass the fire to the next person who has done the same and so on. Once you pass the fire on you put your hand out in a bucket of water. We made it all the way around the table. Everyone in the pack played. The new fae girl did not. To each his, or in this case her, own.<br /> <br /> Lizette then suggested a demonstration of her skill with a bullwhip. She had someone, me, light a match that was being held between someone else\u2019s, Tatiana\u2019s, lips and then flicked her whip, putting out the fire. It was quite well done. Lizette certainly was having fun. The stunts gave way to more dancing and more drinking. I asked Dearbhail to dance a couple of times and we made our way across the dance floor. I know that I\u2019m not the most skilled dancer, but I think I handled myself well enough. At least Dearbhail had no complaints.<br /> <br /> Dancing gave way to more games and to a challenge of wrestling. Dearbhail, surprisingly, took up Tatiana\u2019s challenge and was after a good start, finally beaten. Lizette then took up the challenge, but to make things interesting wrapped her upper body in extra cloth and lit it on fire. Wrestling while on fire! I supposed I should have expected that, considering our earlier conversations about fire. Both combatants were taking damage from the flames so Dacian and I grabbed the buckets from earlier and extinguished our friends. Wolfram decides to show off and lights himself on fire. He is of course immune to his own flames, but Lizette, who decided to join in the fun, was still not immune and was hurt further. I\u2019m starting to think that my friend has an unhealthy interest in fire.<br /> <br /> After the wrestling and the fire, there was brandy and cigars. And more Spin the Bottle. I ended up kissing Heinrich this time. And Dacian. I still prefer Dearbhail. The cigars and brandy were pretty good. The brandy tasted a bit odd after having so much vodka, but it wasn\u2019t bad. It just left a different kind of burn in its wake.<br /> <br /> The last thing that we all did as a group was to take some items that represent Wolfram\u2019s life as a bachelor and blow them up. I think the idea was to take the items and bury them in a coffin shaped box as a way of putting to rest his single life and move forward as a married man. But, much to our annoyance the ground at the park was much too sodden and muddy to dig in it. So, we had Lizette rig the box with explosives when we got back to the Chateau and we blew it up. Somehow I\u2019m not surprised that our group resorted to explosives. It seems to be our modus operandi. Fire. It might not be the best answer to all of life\u2019s problems but it certainly has made things more interesting. From fights on trains with supernatural monsters to friendly drunken brawls in brothels.<br /> <br /> Once the fire was out we went our separate ways. Dacian went to take up his position as Skadi\u2019s bodyguard once again. Tatiana started off on her own saying that she was going back to the brothel, and the rest of us went back to the house. From there we further split up. Dearbhail and I made our way upstairs, leaving the rest to their own devices. I\u2019ll admit that by that point I was more than ready to spend some time alone with my beautiful songstress. Watching her dance, and even wrestle, just reminded me what a vibrant and alive woman she is. She grasps life and holds on and lives it to the fullest. I can appreciate that. Sometimes when I\u2019m with her I think that I can start to see the world the way she does. Perhaps slightly more jaded, but things seem just a bit brighter than they did before I met her. Even my happiest moments in the past don\u2019t hold a candle to the vibrancy that she brings to the world. And now that I\u2019m starting to wax poetic it might be time for me to go to sleep. I have had perhaps a bit too much to drink. It was all worth it though. I got to dance with Dearbhail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What are you saying volchonok?<br /> <br /> I am not sick, you are sick.<br /> <br /> I will fight you!<br /> <br /> I will! You just stop being two volchonoks for one minute. That is cheating.<br /> <br /> No, I did not fight Dearbhail and Lizette because I am sick. It was for fun, because I am good at fighting. Besides, I am not sick!<br /> <br /> Of course I am good at fighting while I am on fire. I am good at all fighting.<br /> <br /> I will fight you volchonok.<br /> <br /> Why am I sick? I told you before, yes? Plus, I am not sick.<br /> <br /> Before! I said... right? I said it is Wolfram\u2019s stag party.<br /> <br /> No we did not eat bad stag meat. It is... it is metaphor, like Dacian said. It means. It means Wolfram is to be married in two days, and this is a thing to be celebrating.<br /> <br /> I do not know why they call it a stag party volchonok. I am not in charge of naming things, that is not like fighting at all, why would you say so? But it is the word.<br /> <br /> What? Of course you didn\u2019t say I was in charge of naming things, that sounds even too foolish for you.<br /> <br /> Bah.<br /> <br /> All of it was a stag party. The sauna, the marching, the singing, the brothel with the dancing and the kissing and the fighting and the games and the explosions.<br /> <br /> They were the best games! Foolish volchonok, doesn\u2019t understand best games. Well, the bottle game was broken, because it would not land on me for fifty times. But I kiss who I want anyway!<br /> <br /> No, I did not kiss Dacien because I want, he is a boy, why would I want? That was bottle\u2019s fault. I kissed that pretty girl because I want, the one I picked up on the bench.<br /> <br /> Now you are just trying to confuse me volchonok. I did not kiss the red haired fairy. Marie, I think? She was very light, adding her to the bench did not make it harder at all. And she squeaked so!<br /> <br /> It <u>was</u> red like fire, you clever volchonok. There was much fire.<br /> <br /> Fire and vodka go best together. Like me and fighting. Vodka is perfect for lighting your hand on fire and not burning and for chasing off some mudak who will not leave Elena be. And wrestling with fire!<br /> <br /> Wolfram cheated, he did not need vodka to wrestle with fire because he has dead person magic.<br /> <br /> The other? There was many others...<br /> <br /> Oh!<br /> <br /> Oh, yes. That was Wolfram\u2019s brother. He was a good man. I like him.<br /> <br /> Is that...?<br /> <br /> Holy shit!<br /> <br /> I am not scared of plane. I will fight you. And plane. At the same time!<br /> <br /> You saw nothing of the sort, foolish volchonok. I just did not want it to hit me on the head. Wolfram is very drunk after all. He should have eaten more potatoes and pickles and herrings, like good Russian. It is why I am not drunk at all.<br /> <br /> I do not know. I thought they were going to bed, not flying around in a plane.<br /> <br /> I suppose after exploding the metaphor coffin they did not feel much like sleeping.<br /> <br /> It was the best song! You hush.<br /> <br /> I made them up! I am good at making words for songs!<br /> <br /> No. I am much better at fighting. I am best at fighting. And yelling, but that is not so good when you are trying to stack broken ceramic pieces.<br /> <br /> Well, because the yelling makes them fall over, especially if you are good at it, like me.<br /> <br /> Why didn\u2019t you say so?<br /> <br /> Huh?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. There was broken pieces because it is rule, when you make toasts, you break your cup.<br /> <br /> Only for stag parties, it is rule.<br /> <br /> Whips are not a rule. That was a game, silly volchonok. Lizette is very good with it. And with the fire game.<br /> <br /> I am fine at counting! I will fight you.<br /> <br /> There was 8 playing the fire game, like I counted.<br /> <br /> 1...2...3, 4, 5...6..7... Bah!<br /> <br /> They cheated, it is not my fault.<br /> <br /> I do not know who cheated, but someone did, because I am good at counting.<br /> <br /> No I will not fight them. Why would I fight them?<br /> <br /> Pssh.<br /> <br /> No I will not go running instead. We go to see Elena!<br /> <br /> Because she is beautiful and smart and strong and wonderful and mostly I wish to see her.<br /> <br /> Later, my volchonok friend. We will have all the time in the world later for running off into the night. But not this night.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Elena frowned at the sight of Tatiana coming up the path so late. The frown didn\u2019t last long, driven away by the amused upturn at the corner of her mouth as she watched the other woman sway slightly, shooing away what she assumed was one of the neighborhood cats, though she saw no sign of it. She sighed. The boys had just gone back to bed.<br /> <br /> She got to the door and opened it before Tatiana could knock. Stepping outside, she closed the door softly. \u201cTatiana, what are you doing here?\u201d The taller woman swayed closer, putting her hands on Elena\u2019s waist. \u201cYou are drunk.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d Tatiana smiled happily. \u201cI am here to see you! Do you not want to see me?\u201d She nuzzled Elena\u2019s neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is late.\u201d Elena rolled her eyes, but wasn\u2019t able to keep a smile completely off her face. \u201cAnd you are <u>very</u> drunk.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her lover grinned down at her. \u201cIt was l\u2019entre... l\u2019entern...l\u2019entman... a stag party. For Wolfram. He marries in two days. It was a celebration! And now I am with you, so there is more celebrating. Let\u2019s go inside, my love...\u201d Tatiana reached around behind Elena and turned the knob.<br /> <br /> \u201cTanya, be careful!\u201d They stumbled inside, thumping into the wall. Tatiana bit her lip on a giggle and tried to carefully shut the door. Elena raised an eyebrow and caught it, barely making sure it didn\u2019t slam.<br /> <br /> \u201cElena, Elena, Elena, you worry too much. It is late, they are sleeping and I am here...\u201d Tatiana leaned in for a kiss.<br /> <br /> \u201cTanya!\u201d At the boys\u2019 shout, Tatiana stood up, eyes widening as she looked down at Elena\u2019s stern face. The smaller woman moved out of the way. \u201cTanya!\u201d The boys barrelled into the room, tackling their aunt.<br /> <br /> She swayed, attempting a grin. \u201cHello boys. What are you doing up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere was a plane, right by our house!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was upside down and the people\u2019s hair and scarves and things were dangling down and it was screaming...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it wasn\u2019t, it was sideways and the wing drew a line on the ground and that\u2019s what made the noise!\u201d<br /> <br /> The boys started shoving each other, arguing about the plane. Tatiana moved between them while Elena just watched, arms crossed. \u201cA plane is certainly exciting, even if it were right side up.\u201d They left off arguing to tell her more about it.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt went very fast, zoom!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFaster than anything I\u2019ve ever seen, ever.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd there was a dog inside and it waved!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, stupid, it was a cat that waved. I was closer, I saw better.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSurely you mean it wagged its tail, not waved. That does sound more like a dog.\u201d Elena said tiredly, for the hundredth time. \u201cProbably it was not either...\u201d she muttered to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah!\u201d<br /> <br /> Sasha threw a punch at the older Pyotr, but Tatiana moved faster, grabbing the back of their nightshirts and pulling them apart. \u201cBoys, boys, it is not time for fighting. It is a special night, a celebration.\u201d<br /> <br /> The boys looked sheepish for a second, but then Sasha got a calculating look in his eyes, eying Tatiana\u2019s jovial demeanor. \u201cSo... if it is special, does that mean we can have a story?\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena hid a smile as Tatiana looked pleadingly over at her. She managed to give the taller woman a serious look. Tatiana looked between the boys. \u201cIf I tell you a story, will you go to bed?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes!\u201d they said in chorus.<br /> <br /> She began walking towards their bedroom, both boys following along behind. \u201cVery well. I will tell you a German story, one my friend Wolfram has told me. Once upon a time, there were two boys who went exploring in the forest and got lost. Then they ran across an owl. They asked the owl if it knew the way home...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dacian\u2019s Book of Shadows</b><br /> <br /> 29 April 1922 - Night<br /> <br /> I have been dreadfully delinquent in recording my comings and goings. My last entry could mislead and suggest I was once again captured, but nothing could be further from the truth. We actually finished our task with the House of Esterh\u00e1zy, moved the cabal back to a Chateau outside of Paris, and have made great strides in the status of our Hollow.<br /> <br /> This week has been more exceptional in that we have been called on to act in the interest of the Queen of Flowers and Light to protect a visiting monarch, discover a fascinating way to hide magic via playwright, learned more about the metal creatures of fate, as well as prepare for Wolfram\u2019s wedding night!<br /> <br /> I am again standing at my post outside the room of Skadi, Winter Queen of Berlin, seeing to the protection of the Ice Queen. But as I have partaken of many teacups worth of Tatiana\u2019s Russian Vodka, I will keep my descriptions to today. I fear I would confuse most of the details for anything longer ago than that.<br /> <br /> We began our festivities in a sauna. Tatiana planned the events for the day, which may be why Dearbh\u00e1il and Lizette were both in attendance as well. Tatiana has no time for modesty, wearing her towel the same as the men in the sweltering heat. I couldn\u2019t help but pay her more attention than usual when she spoke, but she didn\u2019t see to care. Dearbh\u00e1il covered herself more delicately than our Uratha friend, though her towel was no match for ...I should let that thought float away unfinished. I shall feel no shame in my likely inebriation as I\u2019m mostly sure even Marek exceeded his abilities. The time it took to remember how to spell inebriation in any language tells me there is not likely, only certainty. But I\u2019m losing the story. Many drinks were had as we steamed together. Discussions of fires on planes and using vodka as a weapon versus spraying with hot tea still stand out. And at this point, anything I can remember must have happened.<br /> <br /> Collecting ourselves and our clothing from the sauna, we moved to an upscale CanCan club. There were ladies and gentlemen for hire, but we were mostly there for privacy and our own shenanigans. A few of the ladies and one or two of the men began to orbit us as our party continued into the afternoon. Spin the bottle was a game I was unfamiliar with, I assume because I was taken so young. One more thing to blame on my Keeper. So much kissing, and yet so little of interest. It was interesting when Dearbh\u00e1il kissed one of the dancers or when Lizette kissed Dearbh\u00e1il, ...also when Lizette kissed Wolfram, but I don\u2019t really remember most more than that. Until Tatiana grabbed a dancing girl and pulled her into a kiss before stomping off to play darts.<br /> <br /> I noticed Marie Rouge as we were mustering for this next round of games. I found the red headed Emerald Court Manikin adorably attractive and invited her to join us. I remember somewhere in my mind thinking that if word of our parties got out, it might help Dearbh\u00e1il and I within the Court. Also another beautiful woman in a group which played Spin the bottle was an excellent idea. I was apparently still at least mildly charming as Marie joined us with the understanding she did not wish to be set afire by Lizette. I found this ridiculous and assured her of her safety. This was immediately before Tatiana and Lizette announced that the Fire Games would begin. Still I believe I made an impression on poor Marie. Hopefully she will continue to speak to me after Pass the Flame, Flame Wrestling, and Whip out the Flame were all lined up. I remember dancing with her when I noticed Dearbh\u00e1il wrestling Tatiana. However briefly, the Fairest proved she was no wilting flower.<br /> <br /> After a point, Lizette and Tatiana were trying too hard to show who was best as Flame Wrestling. Marek and I dowsed them both with the buckets from Pass the Flame. Then Wolfram erupted into flames and wrestled Lizette. I dowsed them both as I found this to just be silly. I do wish they would exhaust themselves upon one another to end this silly tension between them. Dearbh\u00e1il healed Lizette before Brandy and cigars made an appearance. I admit that I\u2019m not much for smoking and the Brandy was odd given the vodka I had consumed. Spin the bottle was odd this time. I kissed Tatiana, which was mildly terrifying given her state of sobriety.<br /> <br /> The evening found us returning to the chateau through the Hedge as the Paris rain left digging a hole unwanted. Perhaps we were more drunk than I thought, as thinking back on it, soft mud would be easy to dig. Either way, we moved outside our walls to bury Wolfram\u2019s bachelor life. Lizette constructed a casket, as befits a Sin-Eater, and we carried it out like pallbearers. Dearbh\u00e1il sat atop and sang a dirge. I had lost Marie by then as she found something less terrifying than dealing with us and explosives. Once we were clear of the chateau, we dug a grave, Lizette set the explosives, we moved back and Wolfram\u2019s single life was ended in fire and force.<br /> <br /> With the goal of our day complete, I headed back to guard Skadi. The rest of my cabal scattered though I didn\u2019t see where everyone went. Now I must remember to keep this account with me until I return to our wonderful abode.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 30th April 1922<br /> <br /> I remember I was on fire part of last night.<br /> <br /> And an explosion<br /> <br /> Okay, we went to a Sauna, the Motley apart from Alla (who needed to practice and watch Emilie)<br /> <br /> The Sauna reminded me of being on fire. It was hot, and the heat pressed on. Tatiana said it made her relax, but it didn\u2019t make me relax. It made me think of being on the wing of a plane. The plane was on fire. I was on fire. A chunk of the wing was torn out as the pilot looked at me. I hung on, my weight tipping the plane, and looked back. Burning I crossed on all fours as soon as it went almost level and grabbed him, yanking him out in the conflagration. The plane was burning. We were going so fast I felt the wind. I was burning. We were going so hard I vibrating. I smelled it all burn. I heard screams. It was glorious. I was truly alive.<br /> <br /> I refocused on the Sauna.<br /> <br /> We started talking about tea, and I started talking about flavored tea. At some point I need to start working on some flavored teas. I mean, I would not have Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re if I did not like tea.<br /> <br /> Next was the brothel, because Tatiana, and that\u2019s where it gets hazy. Tatiana was big on playing games in there. I remember there were darts. I remember there was dancing. I know I danced myself a lot, and danced with Wolfram. And Dearbh\u00e1il? Regardless, there was dancing.<br /> <br /> Also Spin the Bottle. I know I was gonna be bad and control the bottle to kiss Wolfram and Dearbh\u00e1il. Since I remember what kissing each of them was like, I am pretty sure that happened.<br /> <br /> I remember something about a whip. As in I had a whip. Did I whip Dearbhail? I am pretty sure I would have remembered that.<br /> <br /> So, I remember there was this Manikin there, and that she was scared of fire. I don\u2019t remember where she came from. And Tatiana immediately wanted us to play a game where we set each other\u2019s hands on fire like right after Dacian talked her into sitting with us and she had said she was afraid of fire. I guess Tatiana did that to scare her. But then my hands were on fire?<br /> <br /> Marie Rouge, that was her name.<br /> <br /> I know I wrestled Tatiana and Wolfram while on fire. Separately. I think I lost both times. Your heart has a way of pounding when you are on fire. The crackling in your ears is matched by the pounding. Adrenaline makes you stronger, faster, the licking flames urging you on. It\u2019s pretty awesome. Anyway.<br /> <br /> We played spin the bottle again. I think. I remember snippets of setting some explosives and an explosion a bit away from the ch\u00e2teau; I think that was the coffin. I hope that was the coffin.<br /> <br /> Also, flying the plane with Wolfram. Did I buzz Tatiana? Maybe? Why was she on the road to the village? I mean, she could have told me I would not remember. Maybe I should ask.<br /> <br /> I\u2026hope I did not do anything too personal with Wolfram. Ah, he is a gentleman. I am safe.<br /> <br /> So Walpurgis Night, my third with this group, and tonight is the play. I guess we see what happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wolfram\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> The roar of the plane's engine rose to a window rattling peak as the fighter skimmed dangerously close to the elegant rise of Chantilly before circling and descending to the small airstrip that now graced the chateau\u2019s grounds. The plane taxied to a stop and a with a flash of yellowed cat's eyes a small figure slipped free and dropped to the ground while the larger form of the pilot climbed out with unhurried and purposeful motions. More laughter drifted on the late night air as the two saw to the craft with a well practiced ease and walked it back into it's hangar. The mismatched shadows did not part ways until they reached the main house, the taller watching as the other swayed away before turning and finding himself less alone than he'd expected.<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook his head as he faced his brother. Half brother technically, but such had never been given import in their house. Wolfram's surprise shifted to warmth and he gave a smile. \u201cI didn't expect you to still be up. I hope there isn't a problem with your rooms.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh no brother. They are as luxurious as the rest of this chateau. Mother and I are most comfortable. Of course, someone seems to have flown a plane close enough to my window to reach out and touch it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram's smile widened even as he looked self consciously away for a moment. \u201cAh, yes. Perhaps it was a bit late for such theatrics...\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook his head again. \u201cI suppose I should be happy to see you doing something so carefree for a change. You have always been so serious. But is it really appropriate to be flirting with her like that so close to your wedding day?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram straightened and drew his lips into a tight line. \u201cI was not flirting. We were simply flying...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd dancing. And kissing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEveryone was dancing. And kissing was the whole point of the bottle game.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one else was kissing like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTatiana swept that dancing girl up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook his head and crossed his arms. \u201cNot the way you swept Lizette up brother. And there was the fire. I think you are overly fond of this woman.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram frowned. \u201cWe are close friends and tonight was a night for celebration and letting loose, nothing more. She's an expert on occult devices and a fellow pilot. We have many common interests. I don't understand why you seem to dislike her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich adjusted his glasses and sighed. \u201cI didn't say I disliked her. But she is very... French.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram lifted an eyebrow. \u201cYou say that like it matters.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe it does brother. You haven't been home recently. You have not seen the occupation's effects.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd so just because she happens to be French?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKeeping the factory running and trying to see that my men and their families can make do means I have to deal with the petty cruelties of French bureaucrats and soldiers every day Wolfram. They don't limit their vindictiveness to those who fought.\u201d Heinrich looked up and lifted a hand to forestall Wolfram. \u201cAnd no, it's not all of them. It's not even most of them to be honest. But there are enough and even the ones that don't go out of their way to abuse the situation are there to squeeze blood from a stone that has been bled much to dry already. There are those that feel that they should be driven out by force.\u201d Wolfram gave an exasperated sigh as Heinrich continued, \u201cDefeat does not sit well well with many. Having that compounded with indignity is a dangerous mixture.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram nodded. \u201cTrust me, I am well aware of this. I see it whenever I go into Paris. I see the looks, the occasional quiet or not so quiet comments and it does stir my ire. But striking out only leads to more of the same. We cannot move forward chained to the grievances of the past. So it falls upon me to be the better man.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich gave a tired smile. \u201cAnd if there were more like you then the world would be a better place. I'm sorry. This is no conversation to be having on the eve of your wedding.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI haven't been there to help. Perhaps I should make more time...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what exactly would you do? This isn't the work of angry ghosts or lost souls. There is no dark magic curse over the land to be lifted. This is just normal business and politics. I'll see it through and I'll do right by my workers one way or the other just like Father always did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should make time to see to yourself as well. The world is changing brother. I was surprised that you didn't bring someone with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... Like I said, I have been so busy dealing with everything. There isn't a lot of time for going out and meeting people. And many of the people I have to work with are still mired in the old world.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram stepped closer and put a hand on his brother's shoulder. \u201cYou deserve to be happy. Life is too short and too precious to waste.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich placed his own hand atop his brother's and nodded. After a few moments of quiet he looked up and frowned. \u201cPlease tell me Christina and her Maid of Honor know...\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram laughed. \u201cActually it was Lizette who started gearing up to play matchmaker. She and Marlene are close. But I explained to her that it wouldn't work out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks for that. I mean, she does seem like a fine woman and all and I am sure she would make an excellent wife.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut that's not what you're looking for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it's not. Now, if that handsome friend of yours happened to be interested...\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram laughed and shook his head. \u201cHe'll be at the wedding, you can ask him to dance and find out. But for now, it's late and we should both get some sleep before the sun rises.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026And the owl ripped the little girl\u2019s face clean off\u201d<br /> <br /> So as I say social heavy session. Lizette won a lot through gratuitous use of Artifice and Animation. She also used Animation to control the bottle, because nothing is more awesome than cheating at Spin the Bottle. We had a lot of fun with all the IC RP. Good bonding and character building.<br /> <br /> Next we deal with a play as we prepare to move to Berlin in Autumn. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br /> Tatiana will fight you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-ca