er","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:42:42-07:00","id":872949,"title":"","content":"That's fair. Part of what rebound does for you. You should see her next Journal in about a week...short recap, looooong rant. Good to get the feedback, take care of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:12:24-07:00","id":878551,"title":"","content":"Time to check in with the Golden Eagle Crew! I need to head this one off with some explanation to follow the journals a bit, as a lot focuses on Ghosts, being this covers the play. So the Uratha did the Siskur da ritual to allow the whole Conspiracy to interact with ghosts physically. The thing that makes this complicated is only a few of them can see or hear ghosts; Wolfram, being a Sin-Eater, can, and can use his Keystone (a flaming sword) under the influence of the Ritual to affect ghosts as well. Dacian can through the Darkling Contract of Shade and Spirit (but is not skilled at barehanded fighting). Marek can because of Bone Shadow Gifts. However, Alla, Tatiana (by far the best barehanded fighter), Dearbh\u00e1il, and Lizette are essentially blind and deaf to them. I believe Wolfram may plan to get some Ceremonies to deal with this problem for next time. Dana, not being part of the Conspiracy, did not participate in the Ritual. So the play on Walpurgis Night 1922. Begin! <i>Session XXVII</i> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b> 30 April 1922 Today was the day of the play. We started things off by calling down a Sacred Hunt on the play and our intentions to make sure that no rituals are completed. We included most everyone in the pack, so they would have the ability to see ghosts. Much like the last ritual I conducted, Lizette represented the ritual within the play and I snuck up on her and ran my claws along her throat. I did not carry my rifle this time since my gift does not allow me to shoot ghosts, only bare handed or melee attacks will work. That was fine by me. I\u2019ve been practicing and have gotten better since the last time we called Siskur da. We arrived at the play early so we could position ourselves. Dacian immediately went up into the rafters above the stage and hid. Dearbhail, Fenric, and Dana all went to the audience area. Tatiana stationed herself in the orchestra pit. I went backstage and hid among the shadows. Wolfram and Lizette arrived shortly after the play started. Wolfram went to the audience while Lizette snuck backstage and made her way up to the catwalk. Shortly after the play started I noticed that Greta was around. I could not see her, but I could smell her. I let Alla , who was waiting for her scene to come up, know that Greta was hiding backstage. Alla tried to get Greta\u2019s attention to no effect. Between the first and second acts I noticed that aura that accompanies Blackstaff\u2019s gift when he wants to spy on an area come up. It had a slightly different feel this time, but it was the same gift. I climbed up to the catwalk to let Lizette know what was going on. I tried to find Dacian, but he was too well hidden. I just hoped that he had heard me talking to Lizette. Around that time I also spotted Greta and pointed her out to our slight mechanic. I figured all of this was important for the others to know, so I made my way to the audience seating discreetly and told Wolfram what was going on. My message passed along, I made my way back to the backstage area. During the second act I noticed two ghosts walking towards the stage from the back. It was a mother/daughter pair. They looked emaciated, like they\u2019d died of starvation or possibly exposure. I thought that they might have been refugees. They spoke Greek. I stepped in their path and tried to make myself understood though we apparently did not share a language. I tried different languages until I hit on one that they had some familiarity with, Russian. I think I managed to get the word \u201cstop\u201d across to them. Then suddenly the aura of the power surrounding us changed and I was suddenly struck blind, deaf and mute. It was rather disconcerting to say the least. The only reason I didn\u2019t become more upset was because of my wolf senses. I could still smell and that gave me an idea of where everything and everyone was. I indicated my eyes, ears and throat and made a slashing motion to tell the others that I was blind, deaf and dumb. I do not know if they saw me or not, but I think they did. That I will admit is an experience that I would rather not repeat. It reminded me a little too much of when a grenade went off too close to my trench. The sound was deafening and for a while all I could hear was ringing in my ears. I could not hear it when I tried to talk, nor when someone tried to talk to me. My squad and I were brought back to the medical tent for a while until our hearing returned. I was never so happy to hear a bird\u2019s call until that day. As soon as I was struck by that power the ghosts made a dash for the stage. I managed to catch the mother ghost and Wolfram, who\u2019d come backstage, grabbed the little girl. He tried to tell them to stop, and that he cannot let them continue. Then just as suddenly I was able to hear and see again. Maybe Blackstaff realized that the power wasn\u2019t restricting me the way he\u2019d hoped it would and decided to try something different. I will admit that it was good to be able to see with my eyes again. My sense of smell gave me a good idea of what was around me, but it doesn\u2019t take the place of my eyes. Then, before we could do anything, we were all pulled through the floor of the stage. The ghosts were pulled with us. We were not alone. The other man there asked us what we were doing, so we told him. He said that he was not a friend and then seemed to disappear. It wasn\u2019t until later that I realized that he was likely one of the vampires charged with keeping any powers from being used on the play or the actors. I guess he assumed that we were all a threat and pulled us beneath the stage. While we were down there Wolfram continued to talk to the mother and they eventually came to an accord. They would stop trying to influence the play and Wolfram would do something for them. After that was settled we found the stairs and climbed back up to the backstage area. We were greeted by the sight of two armed ghosts wearing bone armor and carrying maces. We figured that they were part of Blackstaff\u2019s guards. The mother and daughter ghost went back below the stage to stay out of danger. The fight with the guards didn\u2019t go too badly. It was especially unpleasant for Dacian, but he doesn\u2019t remember what happened. That\u2019s for the best. It started out with me grabbing one of the guards and Wolfrman materializing a sword and going after the other one. He wounded it, if it can be said that ghosts can be injured. After a relatively short time the one that I was holding got away and Greta went after him. She used one of her powers and grappled the ghost that I lost my grip on. The power was a little disturbing to watch. Suddenly she resembled a somewhat bloated corpse. Her skin was blue-ish and distended. I think even the humans saw that. They started to react and Tatiana got them out of the backstage area to safety. We continued the fight in private. One of the ghosts then decided that possessing one of us would be his best bet and went after Dacian. Upon possessing him, Dacian\u2019s body deformed. His ribs came out and made claws for his hands. His spine lengthened and his skull was pushed upward. It looked rather painful to me. Tatiana went ahead and grabbed Dacian to ensure that the ghost could not harm anyone on or off stage. While she was grappling that one I attacked the one that Greta was holding. I shifted to Dalu form and attacked him with my claws. I managed a couple of hits on the ghost before it finally faded. It is not permanently dead, but it will be awhile before it is possible for him to come back to the waking world. Meanwhile I believe that Alla was trying to use one of her Vampire gifts to convince the ghost to leave Dacian\u2019s body. I believe she was successful, as the ghost fled our friend and his body returned to normal leaving wounds as it did so. As it fled I tried to attack it, but did not manage to take it down or restrain it. Dearbhail came backstage at the intermission and we caught her up on all that had happened. She immediately healed a confused Dacian. While she was doing that Wolfram, Tatiana and I discussed going after Blackstaff before he got away. We had felt his area-wide power come down shortly after the last ghost fled. The problem we ran into was the area that he could affect with that gift is awfully large and there were only three of us. And of those three only the two of us could track by scent. In the end we decided that Tatiana, Greta and I would track Blackstaff. We headed out in a South by Southeast pattern. We caught a faint scent of him, but it ended. We assume that he got into a car and fled that way. We were told, while we searched for Blackstaff, that Alla did a very good job with her altered lines in the play. The audience didn\u2019t know that anything had been changed. I believe that Connie and Agrippa did and Agrippa at least was not happy with it. From what he heard from Dearbhail those two plus Fenric disappeared from the audience for a while and reappeared at the end. My guess is that the same guy that pulled us through the floor of the backstage did something similar to Agrippa and her two companions. Perhaps they were trying to influence the play and were removed to keep their powers from working? Fenric was likely just caught up in the wrong place at the wrong time. He was asleep when he was returned to his seat. I would have been angry if he\u2019d been returned in worse shape than when he \u201cleft,\u201d but he was fine. After the play we discussed Wolfram\u2019s wedding. It was decided that Marlena will be the maid of honor, and Heinrich will be the best man. Dacian and I will be the groomsman, and Dearbhail and Lizette will be the bridesmaids. Tatiana will be the ring-bearer. I believe that something was also discussed about Lizette building a \u201cflower cannon\u201d to replace the need for a flower girl. That should be interesting to say the least. I will admit that I was honored to be asked to be a groomsman. I missed my brother\u2019s wedding two years ago when I was dealing with the situation with the orphans. Sometimes I feel like I have let my brother down because I was not there for him, but I\u2019m not sure what else I could have done. Those children needed to be freed from those monsters and I was hired to do so. I was also in a position to help them after the Deuderman\u2019s had been dealt with. Speaking of which, I received a letter from my brother a little while ago letting me know that Denisa and Erik were able to adopt both Kv\u0115ta and Dominik. They are both growing well and seem to be happy with their new home. I am glad that I was able to help them find them a safe and caring place to live. I have been told that both children insist on calling me \u201cUncle Marek.\u201d I guess I made an impression. As for Desnisa and Erik, I only met them the one time, but they seemed like good people. Andel has confirmed this with his letter I am glad to say. That said, I am looking forward to Wolfram and Christine\u2019s wedding. They will finally be allowed to act like the mated pair that they are, though I\u2019m sure they would find my choice of words uncouth. I am happy for them though. They make a good couple and will make good parents. I am looking forward to it all. <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b> Hush volchonok. No, I have not caught the scent of this Blackstaff. Nor has Greta seen any ghosts. It is sad. I too wanted to fight. He hurt one of our pack, this is unacceptable. Yes, volchonok, it was he who did that to Dacian. What is that even? No, volchonok, he did not decide to become a were-skeleton, whatever that is. It is true, ribs do make better weapons than human claws, but we need them in the place they are usually. He was possessed by a spirit of the dead, one of Blackstaff\u2019s ghosts. That is what did it. Not the small girl who called Wolfram names, I don\u2019t believe, a different one. I agree. Roach head is an excellent insult. It was good of Greta to share what the child said. I do not know. I believe they are our friends now, the small girl ghost and her mother ghost. Even if the mother could not help find Blackstaff. Anyone who tells Wolfram that he eats mudpies and kisses roaches while he has them held up off the ground should be a friend. That? That was not ghosts. It was other vampires stole the vampires. And Fenric, but they gave him back. He was probably too small. Alla says Constancia is probably alright. Because we told the Prince that someone might try something foolish. He seems to favor this direct control. I will have words with him if he has harmed Constancia. Yes, volchonok, the words would be fighting. You are learning! I could not see these ghosts, so I could not fight. I had other things to do anyway, like scare the human away and keep Dacian from attacking anyone. Yes, I bit Dacian. It was the best way to keep the ghost from using his rib bones to stab one of us. He does not even remember. I didn\u2019t actually hurt him, and Dearbh\u00e1il kissed and made him better anyway. Uh... perhaps. I do not know if Alla\u2019s very large hat helped her control the ghost. It was for the play not for ghosts. Foolish volchonok. Of course the play was perfect! We Hunted to make it so. Yes, volchonok, that means the Hunt is over. No this does not mean we can go run. Tomorrow I will be bearing the rings for Wolfram\u2019s wedding - it is important. There will be time and time enough for running after we see to the happiness of our pack. <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b> 30th April 1922 We prevented the play from becoming a disaster. It soon proved out of my league. First, I escorted Wolfram to see Prince Etienne and negotiate having Vampires make sure nothing vampiric and supernatural happened at the play. This lead to the Prince sending out his goon squad of Nosferatu Vampires who thoroughly intimidated all the vampires there, well except Alla who decided they were cool. They did overstep their bounds a little with Wolfram and Marek, but that did not prove too dangerous. The real problem was the ghosts. Marek, Dacian, and Wolfram were the only ones on our team who could see ghosts, and while we could all, say, punch them, Wolfram and Dacian are not known for their fisticuffs. I suppose one could say we should have foreseen the problem, but I am not sure what we could have done about it. Greta\u2019s arrival helped, but she is a slip of a girl and not a skilled brawler either. I need to invent some sort of ghost goggles. That would be useful. I don\u2019t even know where I would begin to work on that, though. It will take a lot of thought. Perhaps, some sort of box trap I can store ghosts in. Possibly to release on my enemies\u2026 Mayhem! Er, where was I\u2026 Dacian took position in the catwalks and rafters above stage with me, and quickly vanished from my view. Marek came and checked on us near the end of act one, and pointed out that Greta was there as well. Soon after act two began a pair of ghosts, mother and daughter I am told, tried to get in. Marek and Dacian intercepted, but after a short conversation I could not really understand, they tried to bolt. Marek grabbed the mother, while Wolfram got the little girl, coming from the audience to back stage just in time. That was when they were grabbed by the Nosferatu and pulled beneath the stage somehow, and Dacian, Marek and Tatiana went below with Greta. This was an error, as ghosts got in I could not see. Armored ones, apparently. When they got up there was a fierce brawl, and while initially Marek and grabbed one, they escaped. Greta managed to hold onto one Wolfram tore apart, but the other briefly possessed Dacian, turning him into an awful monster. [I]That[I] I could see. Fortunately Alla, who arrived at that point, turned her Vampiric charms toward influencing that ghost to leave Dacian. He fled, since Tatiana terrified him and Wolfram had destroyed his counterpart. Alla made her change in act three. It was over. We won. But none of that matters to me now. Tomorrow, Wolfram and Christina are getting married. I am feeling morose. Dana was waiting for me when I got home. She offered her companionship, and I do not want to sleep alone tonight. She has gone to get her clothes, a few items, and pick out a bottle of Champaign and perhaps port from the cellar. I\u2019ve got two bottles of Cognac here. Dana hopes to cheer me up. With her wit, intelligence, beauty, attitude and mystery, she is an amazing woman. One I have known for a week. A week of laughter, crying, sex, and tears, but a week. I\u2019ve been in love with Christina for two years. And if I am being honest with myself, probably Wolfram a chunk of that. Now there is something I won\u2019t say out loud. How can she compete with that? I mean, I guess she does not have to. She has to cheer me up for a night. But my relationship with Christina is over, even as my my, hell, I don\u2019t even know what to call it, sort of relationship with Dana has started? I have no idea what my future will be like. It won\u2019t be like Wolfram and Christina\u2019s, though. Changelings wonder if they have a soul. I know I do; mine hurts. Even mayhem feels hollow right now. I should be fair to Dana. She is going to do her best to take care of me the next few days. She promised. She wants to prove herself, prove Iris a liar. That will take a long time. Even a week of taking care of me, while a mewl like a child, won\u2019t do it. But why should she? Here Dana is opening her heart to me and I am whining about another woman and man who have been engaged to each other for nearly two years, most of the time I have known them. Why on earth should Dana even put up with or speak to me? She has shared her body with me, her weaknesses, and her private thoughts, and all I am thinking about is this other woman who never put me first. I am disgusting. I am awful. She would do better to spit on me and walk away, than have her care so roundly ignored. Okay, I washed my face. Dana would be upset if she knew I wept while she was choosing drinks. I must be the strong woman she fell in love with. Is in love with. Does she have a Wolfram like Christina does? A second partner she loves more than I? I do not know. I only know she has others, and she does not care to discuss or compare. Seems like an attitude she would only have with a main partner somewhere else. She is probably in love with Marek. I am insane. Paranoid. I mean, she is probably hot for Marek, because everyone is fucking hot for Marek. God, fucking Marek. Even Wolfram is probably hot for fucking Marek. But Marek is not the one marrying Christina, or Wolfram, tomorrow. And I can\u2019t hate either of them, and the only one to hate is myself, the little misshapen green freak of nature. I\u2019ve become very good at hating myself. It takes little talent or work to be able to hate a freak like me. What do I even offer anyway, but a lifetime of embarrassment at being seen in public with me, anyway? I don\u2019t see why -- Dana dropped off the bottles, and stepped out to change into \u201cSomething a little more comfortable.\u201d That woman is going to do everything in her power to make me feel better. I should appreciate it. I should soak my mind in alcohol and bury my face between her breasts, and maybe, just maybe, forget what is going to happen tomorrow for a while. I hope. <i>End Session XXVII</i> Tatiana will fight you! (wait, wrong session) At the beginning of the session Alla\u2019s player noted Alla was going to wear the biggest, most magnificent hat they had in the theater. I am sure it helped. House Machten made their presence known this session. There was an amusing scene where Alla was lured into a room by herself and given a stern warning no breaches of the Masquerade would be tolerated. Hilariously, she found their intimidating manner amusing, and started complimenting them on how \u201cawesomely scary\u201d they were. They did not reply. Similarly, it was them who pulled people under the stage later, and intimidated off Agrippa and Constancia (due to Wolfram\u2019s meeting the Prince). The child was a source of amusement as she seemed to constantly insult Wolfram, with bug or roach combined with eater, kisser, or head. Only Wolfram (and Greta) could understand her as she was yelling in Greek, but the group was amused overall. Blackstaff started with Stigmata Boneyard to empower his ghosts, but when Wolfram and Marek prevented the two from possessing anyone with muscle and social approach, he shifted to Stillness to try to stop them and back up his more martial members. He got Marek once, but Werewolves are barely inhibited by the limitations of the Stillness Boneyard, and neither he nor Tatiana were slowed down, and he could not land the effect on Wolfram. The ghosts used a version of Transmogrify Victim on Dacian. They made several attempts, but Wolfram, Marek, Tatiana and Greta were outright immune. Dacian had a poor pool to resist it with. That covers the play. Next session we cover the wedding and downtime between May Day and late October 1922. So normal journal in two weeks, then in three weeks some general discussion of the Golden Eagle version of Berlin circa 1922. I hope you can join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:14:27-07:00","id":878554,"title":"","content":"Okay my general site issues seem to have extended to being unable to post coherently. I will put this up when those issues get fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:18:56-07:00","id":878963,"title":"","content":"Holy carp, what happened? It forgot line-breaks exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T00:30:49-07:00","id":879352,"title":"","content":"Let's try this again<br /> <br /> Time to check in with the Golden Eagle Crew!<br /> <br /> I need to head this one off with some explanation to follow the journals a bit, as a lot focuses on Ghosts, being this covers the play. So the Uratha did the Siskur da ritual to allow the whole Conspiracy to interact with ghosts physically. The thing that makes this complicated is only a few of them can see or hear ghosts; Wolfram, being a Sin-Eater, can, and can use his Keystone (a flaming sword) under the influence of the Ritual to affect ghosts as well. Dacian can through the Darkling Contract of Shade and Spirit (but is not skilled at barehanded fighting). Marek can because of Bone Shadow Gifts. However, Alla, Tatiana (by far the best barehanded fighter), Dearbh\u00e1il, and Lizette are essentially blind and deaf to them. I believe Wolfram may plan to get some Ceremonies to deal with this problem for next time. Dana, not being part of the Conspiracy, did not participate in the Ritual.<br /> <br /> So the play on Walpurgis Night 1922. Begin!<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 30 April 1922<br /> <br /> Today was the day of the play. We started things off by calling down a Sacred Hunt on the play and our intentions to make sure that no rituals are completed. We included most everyone in the pack, so they would have the ability to see ghosts. Much like the last ritual I conducted, Lizette represented the ritual within the play and I snuck up on her and ran my claws along her throat. I did not carry my rifle this time since my gift does not allow me to shoot ghosts, only bare handed or melee attacks will work. That was fine by me. I\u2019ve been practicing and have gotten better since the last time we called Siskur da.<br /> <br /> We arrived at the play early so we could position ourselves. Dacian immediately went up into the rafters above the stage and hid. Dearbhail, Fenric, and Dana all went to the audience area. Tatiana stationed herself in the orchestra pit. I went backstage and hid among the shadows. Wolfram and Lizette arrived shortly after the play started. Wolfram went to the audience while Lizette snuck backstage and made her way up to the catwalk. Shortly after the play started I noticed that Greta was around. I could not see her, but I could smell her. I let Alla , who was waiting for her scene to come up, know that Greta was hiding backstage. Alla tried to get Greta\u2019s attention to no effect.<br /> <br /> Between the first and second acts I noticed that aura that accompanies Blackstaff\u2019s gift when he wants to spy on an area come up. It had a slightly different feel this time, but it was the same gift. I climbed up to the catwalk to let Lizette know what was going on. I tried to find Dacian, but he was too well hidden. I just hoped that he had heard me talking to Lizette. Around that time I also spotted Greta and pointed her out to our slight mechanic. I figured all of this was important for the others to know, so I made my way to the audience seating discreetly and told Wolfram what was going on. My message passed along, I made my way back to the backstage area.<br /> <br /> During the second act I noticed two ghosts walking towards the stage from the back. It was a mother/daughter pair. They looked emaciated, like they\u2019d died of starvation or possibly exposure. I thought that they might have been refugees. They spoke Greek. I stepped in their path and tried to make myself understood though we apparently did not share a language. I tried different languages until I hit on one that they had some familiarity with, Russian. I think I managed to get the word \u201cstop\u201d across to them. Then suddenly the aura of the power surrounding us changed and I was suddenly struck blind, deaf and mute. It was rather disconcerting to say the least. The only reason I didn\u2019t become more upset was because of my wolf senses. I could still smell and that gave me an idea of where everything and everyone was. I indicated my eyes, ears and throat and made a slashing motion to tell the others that I was blind, deaf and dumb. I do not know if they saw me or not, but I think they did. That I will admit is an experience that I would rather not repeat. It reminded me a little too much of when a grenade went off too close to my trench. The sound was deafening and for a while all I could hear was ringing in my ears. I could not hear it when I tried to talk, nor when someone tried to talk to me. My squad and I were brought back to the medical tent for a while until our hearing returned. I was never so happy to hear a bird\u2019s call until that day.<br /> <br /> As soon as I was struck by that power the ghosts made a dash for the stage. I managed to catch the mother ghost and Wolfram, who\u2019d come backstage, grabbed the little girl. He tried to tell them to stop, and that he cannot let them continue. Then just as suddenly I was able to hear and see again. Maybe Blackstaff realized that the power wasn\u2019t restricting me the way he\u2019d hoped it would and decided to try something different. I will admit that it was good to be able to see with my eyes again. My sense of smell gave me a good idea of what was around me, but it doesn\u2019t take the place of my eyes.<br /> <br /> Then, before we could do anything, we were all pulled through the floor of the stage. The ghosts were pulled with us. We were not alone. The other man there asked us what we were doing, so we told him. He said that he was not a friend and then seemed to disappear. It wasn\u2019t until later that I realized that he was likely one of the vampires charged with keeping any powers from being used on the play or the actors. I guess he assumed that we were all a threat and pulled us beneath the stage. While we were down there Wolfram continued to talk to the mother and they eventually came to an accord. They would stop trying to influence the play and Wolfram would do something for them. After that was settled we found the stairs and climbed back up to the backstage area. We were greeted by the sight of two armed ghosts wearing bone armor and carrying maces. We figured that they were part of Blackstaff\u2019s guards. The mother and daughter ghost went back below the stage to stay out of danger.<br /> <br /> The fight with the guards didn\u2019t go too badly. It was especially unpleasant for Dacian, but he doesn\u2019t remember what happened. That\u2019s for the best. It started out with me grabbing one of the guards and Wolfrman materializing a sword and going after the other one. He wounded it, if it can be said that ghosts can be injured. After a relatively short time the one that I was holding got away and Greta went after him. She used one of her powers and grappled the ghost that I lost my grip on. The power was a little disturbing to watch. Suddenly she resembled a somewhat bloated corpse. Her skin was blue-ish and distended. I think even the humans saw that. They started to react and Tatiana got them out of the backstage area to safety. We continued the fight in private.<br /> <br /> One of the ghosts then decided that possessing one of us would be his best bet and went after Dacian. Upon possessing him, Dacian\u2019s body deformed. His ribs came out and made claws for his hands. His spine lengthened and his skull was pushed upward. It looked rather painful to me. Tatiana went ahead and grabbed Dacian to ensure that the ghost could not harm anyone on or off stage. While she was grappling that one I attacked the one that Greta was holding. I shifted to Dalu form and attacked him with my claws. I managed a couple of hits on the ghost before it finally faded. It is not permanently dead, but it will be awhile before it is possible for him to come back to the waking world. Meanwhile I believe that Alla was trying to use one of her Vampire gifts to convince the ghost to leave Dacian\u2019s body. I believe she was successful, as the ghost fled our friend and his body returned to normal leaving wounds as it did so. As it fled I tried to attack it, but did not manage to take it down or restrain it.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail came backstage at the intermission and we caught her up on all that had happened. She immediately healed a confused Dacian. While she was doing that Wolfram, Tatiana and I discussed going after Blackstaff before he got away. We had felt his area-wide power come down shortly after the last ghost fled. The problem we ran into was the area that he could affect with that gift is awfully large and there were only three of us. And of those three only the two of us could track by scent. In the end we decided that Tatiana, Greta and I would track Blackstaff. We headed out in a South by Southeast pattern. We caught a faint scent of him, but it ended. We assume that he got into a car and fled that way.<br /> <br /> We were told, while we searched for Blackstaff, that Alla did a very good job with her altered lines in the play. The audience didn\u2019t know that anything had been changed. I believe that Connie and Agrippa did and Agrippa at least was not happy with it. From what he heard from Dearbhail those two plus Fenric disappeared from the audience for a while and reappeared at the end. My guess is that the same guy that pulled us through the floor of the backstage did something similar to Agrippa and her two companions. Perhaps they were trying to influence the play and were removed to keep their powers from working? Fenric was likely just caught up in the wrong place at the wrong time. He was asleep when he was returned to his seat. I would have been angry if he\u2019d been returned in worse shape than when he \u201cleft,\u201d but he was fine.<br /> <br /> After the play we discussed Wolfram\u2019s wedding. It was decided that Marlena will be the maid of honor, and Heinrich will be the best man. Dacian and I will be the groomsman, and Dearbhail and Lizette will be the bridesmaids. Tatiana will be the ring-bearer. I believe that something was also discussed about Lizette building a \u201cflower cannon\u201d to replace the need for a flower girl. That should be interesting to say the least.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I was honored to be asked to be a groomsman. I missed my brother\u2019s wedding two years ago when I was dealing with the situation with the orphans. Sometimes I feel like I have let my brother down because I was not there for him, but I\u2019m not sure what else I could have done. Those children needed to be freed from those monsters and I was hired to do so. I was also in a position to help them after the Deuderman\u2019s had been dealt with. Speaking of which, I received a letter from my brother a little while ago letting me know that Denisa and Erik were able to adopt both Kv\u0115ta and Dominik. They are both growing well and seem to be happy with their new home. I am glad that I was able to help them find them a safe and caring place to live. I have been told that both children insist on calling me \u201cUncle Marek.\u201d I guess I made an impression. As for Desnisa and Erik, I only met them the one time, but they seemed like good people. Andel has confirmed this with his letter I am glad to say.<br /> <br /> That said, I am looking forward to Wolfram and Christine\u2019s wedding. They will finally be allowed to act like the mated pair that they are, though I\u2019m sure they would find my choice of words uncouth. I am happy for them though. They make a good couple and will make good parents. I am looking forward to it all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Hush volchonok.<br /> <br /> No, I have not caught the scent of this Blackstaff. Nor has Greta seen any ghosts.<br /> <br /> It is sad. I too wanted to fight. He hurt one of our pack, this is unacceptable.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it was he who did that to Dacian.<br /> <br /> What is that even?<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, he did not decide to become a were-skeleton, whatever that is.<br /> <br /> It is true, ribs do make better weapons than human claws, but we need them in the place they are usually.<br /> <br /> He was possessed by a spirit of the dead, one of Blackstaff\u2019s ghosts. That is what did it.<br /> <br /> Not the small girl who called Wolfram names, I don\u2019t believe, a different one.<br /> <br /> I agree. Roach head is an excellent insult. It was good of Greta to share what the child said.<br /> <br /> I do not know. I believe they are our friends now, the small girl ghost and her mother ghost. Even if the mother could not help find Blackstaff. Anyone who tells Wolfram that he eats mudpies and kisses roaches while he has them held up off the ground should be a friend.<br /> <br /> That? That was not ghosts.<br /> <br /> It was other vampires stole the vampires. And Fenric, but they gave him back. He was probably too small. Alla says Constancia is probably alright.<br /> <br /> Because we told the Prince that someone might try something foolish. He seems to favor this direct control. I will have words with him if he has harmed Constancia.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, the words would be fighting. You are learning!<br /> <br /> I could not see these ghosts, so I could not fight. I had other things to do anyway, like scare the human away and keep Dacian from attacking anyone.<br /> <br /> Yes, I bit Dacian. It was the best way to keep the ghost from using his rib bones to stab one of us.<br /> <br /> He does not even remember. I didn\u2019t actually hurt him, and Dearbh\u00e1il kissed and made him better anyway.<br /> <br /> Uh... perhaps. I do not know if Alla\u2019s very large hat helped her control the ghost.<br /> <br /> It was for the play not for ghosts. Foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> Of course the play was perfect! We Hunted to make it so.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that means the Hunt is over.<br /> <br /> No this does not mean we can go run. Tomorrow I will be bearing the rings for Wolfram\u2019s wedding - it is important. There will be time and time enough for running after we see to the happiness of our pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 30<sup>th</sup> April 1922<br /> <br /> We prevented the play from becoming a disaster. It soon proved out of my league.<br /> <br /> First, I escorted Wolfram to see Prince Etienne and negotiate having Vampires make sure nothing vampiric and supernatural happened at the play. This lead to the Prince sending out his goon squad of Nosferatu Vampires who thoroughly intimidated all the vampires there, well except Alla who decided they were cool. They did overstep their bounds a little with Wolfram and Marek, but that did not prove too dangerous.<br /> <br /> The real problem was the ghosts. Marek, Dacian, and Wolfram were the only ones on our team who could see ghosts, and while we could all, say, punch them, Wolfram and Dacian are not known for their fisticuffs. I suppose one could say we should have foreseen the problem, but I am not sure what we could have done about it. Greta\u2019s arrival helped, but she is a slip of a girl and not a skilled brawler either.<br /> <br /> I need to invent some sort of ghost goggles. That would be useful. I don\u2019t even know where I would begin to work on that, though. It will take a lot of thought. Perhaps, some sort of box trap I can store ghosts in. Possibly to release on my enemies\u2026<br /> <br /> Mayhem! Er, where was I\u2026<br /> <br /> Dacian took position in the catwalks and rafters above stage with me, and quickly vanished from my view. Marek came and checked on us near the end of act one, and pointed out that Greta was there as well. Soon after act two began a pair of ghosts, mother and daughter I am told, tried to get in. Marek and Dacian intercepted, but after a short conversation I could not really understand, they tried to bolt. Marek grabbed the mother, while Wolfram got the little girl, coming from the audience to back stage just in time. That was when they were grabbed by the Nosferatu and pulled beneath the stage somehow, and Dacian, Marek and Tatiana went below with Greta.<br /> <br /> This was an error, as ghosts got in I could not see. Armored ones, apparently. When they got up there was a fierce brawl, and while initially Marek and grabbed one, they escaped. Greta managed to hold onto one Wolfram tore apart, but the other briefly possessed Dacian, turning him into an awful monster. <i>That</i> I could see. Fortunately Alla, who arrived at that point, turned her Vampiric charms toward influencing that ghost to leave Dacian. He fled, since Tatiana terrified him and Wolfram had destroyed his counterpart.<br /> <br /> Alla made her change in act three. It was over. We won. But none of that matters to me now.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, Wolfram and Christina are getting married. I am feeling morose. Dana was waiting for me when I got home. She offered her companionship, and I do not want to sleep alone tonight. She has gone to get her clothes, a few items, and pick out a bottle of Champaign and perhaps port from the cellar. I\u2019ve got two bottles of Cognac here.<br /> <br /> Dana hopes to cheer me up. With her wit, intelligence, beauty, attitude and mystery, she is an amazing woman. One I have known for a week. A week of laughter, crying, sex, and tears, but a week. I\u2019ve been in love with Christina for two years. And if I am being honest with myself, probably Wolfram a chunk of that. Now there is something I won\u2019t say out loud. How can she compete with that? I mean, I guess she does not have to. She has to cheer me up for a night. But my relationship with Christina is over, even as my my, hell, I don\u2019t even know what to call it, sort of relationship with Dana has started? I have no idea what my future will be like. It won\u2019t be like Wolfram and Christina\u2019s, though.<br /> <br /> Changelings wonder if they have a soul. I know I do; mine hurts. Even mayhem feels hollow right now.<br /> <br /> I should be fair to Dana. She is going to do her best to take care of me the next few days. She promised. She wants to prove herself, prove Iris a liar. That will take a long time. Even a week of taking care of me, while a mewl like a child, won\u2019t do it.<br /> <br /> But why should she? Here Dana is opening her heart to me and I am whining about another woman and man who have been engaged to each other for nearly two years, most of the time I have known them. Why on earth should Dana even put up with or speak to me? She has shared her body with me, her weaknesses, and her private thoughts, and all I am thinking about is this other woman who never put me first. I am disgusting. I am awful. She would do better to spit on me and walk away, than have her care so roundly ignored.<br /> <br /> Okay, I washed my face. Dana would be upset if she knew I wept while she was choosing drinks. I must be the strong woman she fell in love with. Is in love with. Does she have a Wolfram like Christina does? A second partner she loves more than I? I do not know. I only know she has others, and she does not care to discuss or compare. Seems like an attitude she would only have with a main partner somewhere else.<br /> <br /> She is probably in love with Marek.<br /> <br /> I am insane. Paranoid. I mean, she is probably hot for Marek, because everyone is fucking hot for Marek. God, fucking Marek. Even Wolfram is probably hot for fucking Marek. But Marek is not the one marrying Christina, or Wolfram, tomorrow. And I can\u2019t hate either of them, and the only one to hate is myself, the little misshapen green freak of nature.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve become very good at hating myself. It takes little talent or work to be able to hate a freak like me. What do I even offer anyway, but a lifetime of embarrassment at being seen in public with me, anyway? I don\u2019t see why<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Dana dropped off the bottles, and stepped out to change into \u201cSomething a little more comfortable.\u201d That woman is going to do everything in her power to make me feel better. I should appreciate it. I should soak my mind in alcohol and bury my face between her breasts, and maybe, just maybe, forget what is going to happen tomorrow for a while.<br /> <br /> I hope.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> Tatiana will fight you! (wait, wrong session)<br /> <br /> At the beginning of the session Alla\u2019s player noted Alla was going to wear the biggest, most magnificent hat they had in the theater. I am sure it helped.<br /> <br /> House Machten made their presence known this session. There was an amusing scene where Alla was lured into a room by herself and given a stern warning no breaches of the Masquerade would be tolerated. Hilariously, she found their intimidating manner amusing, and started complimenting them on how \u201cawesomely scary\u201d they were. They did not reply. Similarly, it was them who pulled people under the stage later, and intimidated off Agrippa and Constancia (due to Wolfram\u2019s meeting the Prince).<br /> <br /> The child was a source of amusement as she seemed to constantly insult Wolfram, with bug or roach combined with eater, kisser, or head. Only Wolfram (and Greta) could understand her as she was yelling in Greek, but the group was amused overall.<br /> <br /> Blackstaff started with Stigmata Boneyard to empower his ghosts, but when Wolfram and Marek prevented the two from possessing anyone with muscle and social approach, he shifted to Stillness to try to stop them and back up his more martial members. He got Marek once, but Werewolves are barely inhibited by the limitations of the Stillness Boneyard, and neither he nor Tatiana were slowed down, and he could not land the effect on Wolfram. The ghosts used a version of Transmogrify Victim on Dacian. They made several attempts, but Wolfram, Marek, Tatiana and Greta were outright immune. Dacian had a poor pool to resist it with.<br /> <br /> That covers the play. Next session we cover the wedding and downtime between May Day and late October 1922. So normal journal in two weeks, then in three weeks some general discussion of the Golden Eagle version of Berlin circa 1922. I hope you can join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-07-2016, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:27:15-07:00","id":880600,"title":"","content":"Wow, Lizette's rant made me do a sloooow blink. She's got it almost as bad as Calamity when it come to self-loathing, and the paranoia and jealousy are getting much worse. Did she lose Clarity recently? Is the thing with Marek because of Dearbh\u00e1il?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Marek it's interesting to see how he separates his impressions from the facts he relates in his narration. All he says about his feeling is gathered at the end of his recollections once he's done with his report. It's like his feelings are only switched on when he's dealing with personal stuff, family, frends and such. Very well done and very fitting.<br /> <br /> Why did the Nosferatu interfere?<br /> <br /> Tatiana's comment on giving Fenric back because he's too small made me snort in a most undignified fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T21:05:56-07:00","id":880720,"title":"","content":"She hasn't lost Clarity. Lizette's problem is her first &quot;real&quot; relationship has ended with her girlfriend getting married. It was not a surprise, but still hurt. Also she has a thing for the man her girl is marrying, Also, she is a 21 year old in the body of a 19 year old, so there is a lack of perspective and plenty of hormones. Being a Wizened she struggles with spite, which was definitely directed at Marek, and she has issues with her height and issues with her femininity. And Marek just cuz lots of women like Marek, including Dearbhail, Dana and Iris. Everyone is also in love with Dearbhail. <br /> <br /> Yea Marek's detachment means he tends to look at those things separately.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu were with House Matchen, a group of Invictus enforcers loyal to Prince Etienne. They were dispatched to make sure the masquerade was not broken after Wolfram and Lizette talked to the Prince. Which was rough with the ghosts but they strongarmed Agrippa and Connie into not interfering.<br /> <br /> Hen.<br /> <br /> Glad you enjoyed, next time the wedding and downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T23:50:03-07:00","id":891600,"title":"","content":"Oh man you guys, this has been a shitty week. I have barely slept until last night and I am still sore. Hopefully I will sleep tonight. But because my level of comfort rates just higher than sliding naked down a 10\u2019 greased razorblade, I am late with journals, and commentary will be low.<br /> <br /> This session covered the wedding, and downtime after. The session was more downtime than wedding. Tatiana has a convo for wedding and story for downtime Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 1 May 1922<br /> <br /> Today was the wedding. Overall I think the ceremony went well. There were no troubles to interrupt things, which was good. There was an addition to the bridal party when Fenric was added as a groomsman and a friend of Christine\u2019s was added as the other bridesmaid. I do not remember the woman\u2019s name. She was paired with Fenric, I was paired with Dearbhail and Dacian was paired with Lizette. There were many compliments given on Christine\u2019s dress. Lizette made the bride\u2019s dress as well as the bridesmaid\u2019s dresses. They all came out very well. Apparently Christine\u2019s dress was exceptional. I\u2019ll admit that it was pretty and had some intricate designs worked into it. I will admit that I don\u2019t pay all that close attention to clothes.<br /> <br /> After the wedding was the reception. There was music and dancing and a lot of socializing. I danced with Dearbhail a few times and Lizette once. Most of the time I spent watching other people. I am not the most socially adept person so I stayed to the sidelines as much as I could. It was interesting watching people as they danced or just talked to others. I could tell among Wolfram\u2019s friends who had been in the military or who still were just based on their bearing and how they carried themselves. There always seems to be an economy of movement among ex-military personnel. I know that I am no exception. But a lot of people fought in the Great War. It\u2019s not so surprising to see so many ex-soldiers about.<br /> <br /> Dearbhail sang at the reception, which was rather pretty. I find that I enjoy her singing. Even her humming is pretty. She is a talented artist. I know that Wolfram and Christine were complimented on many aspects of the wedding, including the dresses and singing. Dearbhail took the praise with her usual aplomb. I know that she does it for the enjoyment of the performance and to make people happy. Overall she is rather concerned with the moods of others and does her best to improve them if she finds someone feeling down. We are opposites in many ways. I do not think about others much at all unless they are interacting directly with my pack or doing something that affects my pack. She almost always thinks about others. Her compassion is one of her greatest strengths. It would not be a strength in my line of work, but it is good for her.<br /> <br /> <br /> 22 May 1922<br /> <br /> I met up with Adawolf\u2019s pack today. It had been awhile and I was curious to see how they were doing. I also wanted to see if there was any way that I could repay them for their kindness earlier this year when I needed help. They had nothing that needed doing immediately so the visit was just a social one. I talked to Griswold some more about making fetishes. I had an idea in mind for a fetish and wanted to run it by him and see if he had any suggestions. I thought it would be helpful to have something that would give me or Tatiana an advantage to tracking in adverse weather. The storm in Paris made it clear that being able to track during weather like that would be a boon.<br /> <br /> So, I made my first fetish. I found a minor spirit that really wanted to travel the world and made a deal with it. I travel extensively, as does my pack, so I figured regardless of who held the talisman the spirit would be happy. The fetish itself is a carved piece of wood in the shape of a wolf. A rough approximation of a wolf, but still recognizable as one. My wood carving skills are only so good. I made sure to put focus on the eyes, ears and nose of the wolf to show its connection to the senses and tracking. I also inscribed the symbols for the senses and one for wind to represent bad weather. It is kind of crude looking, but it serves its purpose. Griswold said it was a good effort for a first try. I took that as a compliment.<br /> <br /> On a different note, Adawolf has taken a mate. Her name is Greta. She seems like a decent person. She was friendly to me and was a very good hostess while I visited. Her cooking was really good, and I am told that she is rather talented when it comes to electronics. She fixed their radio in no time and tweaked it so it has a farther range than it did before. I think she would get along well with Lizette should the two ever meet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 12 June 1922<br /> <br /> It seems to be that I always visit my brother in June. I decided that it had been long enough since I had seen my family so I came home. Father is doing well though his hearing is not what it used to be. Cousin Josef is also well. He is courting a girl named Alena, who does not seem to like me much. She does not approve of me traveling and being away from home for such long periods of time. I will admit to being a little irritated with her. Today was the first day we had met and she already had opinions about me. She also did not approve of me giving foreign gifts to Kv\u0115ta, Dominik and Darkja. I brought back dolls for the two girls from France and a Polish pocket knife for Dominik. I made sure that he knew how to be safe around a blade and showed him how to whittle with spare wood. I made another wolf and let him keep it. It came out a little bit better than the fetish I made. But practice makes perfect as they say, and I have been practicing.<br /> <br /> The girls love the dolls and I said that I would see about bringing back dolls from other countries in the future. They loved the idea. Alena did not. But that is fine with me. She is not pack despite her closeness to my cousin. I do not have much regard for her and her opinions. I think that she was a little put off by my reaction, or lack of reaction to her. She strikes me as the type of person that demands attention and expects to be listened to. I simply do not care enough to pay that much attention to her and that annoys her. Josef is used to my somewhat detached interactions with strangers and tried to reassure his lady love that this is just my way and that I will warm to her after we\u2019ve known each other awhile. I did not have the heart to tell him that even if she were pack I would still not likely have much regard for her. I will protect pack, but I don\u2019t always get along with everyone. Josef is not usually fond of me, but treats me with some amount of respect since we are family. We\u2019ll see what the future holds for Alena and my interactions with her. It will largely depend on her.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9 August 1922<br /> <br /> I am in trouble. I arrived at the border to Yugoslavia this morning and was detained on the charge that I was trying to enter the country illegally. Apparently they must have changed things around because my papers have been valid every other time I have been to this country. Granted, it has been awhile since I\u2019ve been here. So, I tried to enter and almost as soon as they looked over my papers they pulled out handcuffs and bound my wrists. I do not take well to being manhandled and might have tried to step away from the man with the restraints. They took this as license to grab me and push me with some force into the nearby wall and bind my hands behind me. I asked what I was being arrested for and they told me with some amount of satisfaction. I get the impression that I\u2019m not the first person that has been detained for similar reasons. They took my pack, my package and my pocket knife, but left me with this book and a pencil. Apparently they saw no harm in a journal or pencil. I will have to do my best without my pocket knife to keep the pencil sharp, or at least usable.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 August 1922<br /> <br /> This building appears to be relatively new. It does not have the wear that you would expect from a place that has so many \u201cguests.\u201d I am being kept in a cell by myself. Thank goodness for small favors. There are other men in cells around me and I can see one person diagonally across from me. The man next to me is called Vincenc and is fairly talkative. I do not know what he looks like though. The man diagonally across form me doesn\u2019t talk to anyone it seems. So, I have taken to staying quiet or talking occasionally to Vincenc.<br /> <br /> <br /> The food tastes like military rations and possibly is. It is mainly tasteless and brown. There might actually be some meat in it if you look really hard. I do not know how long I\u2019ll be able to do without food that actually does something for me. Hopefully I will not be in here much longer. I have decided to let this farce play out. I need to maintain my identity as Marek and keep it clean. I don\u2019t need any irregularities following me from trouble that I may or may not cause here.<br /> <br /> <br /> 11 August 1922<br /> <br /> The guard asked tonight if I needed or wanted anything. I said as an aside that I wouldn\u2019t mind the meat being a little more rare. He smiled and said he\u2019d see what he could do. I\u2019m not sure if I trust that smile, but I suppose tomorrow will tell. On another note Vincenc was moved. I do not know if he was freed or just moved to another facility. The man that replaced him is quiet. I managed to get his name though. It is Pietr. He seems to be about as talkative as I am so I do not foresee much conversation happening between the two of us.<br /> <br /> <br /> 12 August 1922<br /> <br /> The guard is an asshole. He brought me my dinner this evening with a smile. The food, all of it, was so over cooked it was almost unrecognizable. I drank the water that he brought but left the rest on the plate. There was no point in trying to force myself to eat the mess that was on the plate. It would only make me sick and not actually do anything for me anyway. I will admit that I am rather hungry, but am trying to put that to the back of my mind for now. I need to focus on what I can do.<br /> The guard allowed me a short phone call today. I called Hans and explained as quickly as I could what had happened. He said that he would do what he could to get me out of the mess that I find myself in. I do not know how long it will take him to work that political magic that he does, but I hope that it is soon. I have gone hungry before, but that was before I had become what I am. I guess time will tell how well I am able to stand up to a lack of food. If I wasn\u2019t trying to keep my reputation clean I would have \u201cconvinced\u201d them to let me out by now.<br /> <br /> <br /> 14 August 1922<br /> <br /> I find that I do not have a lot of energy and do not know how long I will continue to write in this book. Nothing really changes around here. The man diagonally from me still does not talk and Pietr is only slightly more vocal than a corpse. I know that he is married and has two children. He was arrested on charges of smuggling. From what I gather he was trying to bring something into the country that he had bought in Germany. The officials at the border decided to charge him with smuggling and confiscated his goods and locked him up for his trouble. I do not know if the whole system is corrupt or if it just the border crossing that I decided to go to. Whatever it is though they are having a fun time detaining innocent people and stealing their stuff. I overheard the guards talking about what they were going to do with the Russian man\u2019s \u201ccontraband.\u201d Apparently he was just bringing in bratwurst and crackers from Germany. Just his luck that he married a Yugoslavian woman and had to get locked up for his kind gesture.<br /> <br /> <br /> 16 August 1922<br /> <br /> I am more tempted than I care to admit to transform into Gauru form and break out of this cell. I am afraid however that if I shift I will come too close to the wolf and attack someone. Not that I\u2019d feel bad about killing any of the guards here, but I do not want to make things more difficult for myself. I do not want to be hunted again. The guards have been deliberately cruel to me and the others. They continue to bring me overcooked food and unclean water. I am not sure what they do to the other prisoners here to torment them, or if they are saving their special attention for me. I would like to tear out their throats and watch them struggle to breathe as they lay dying on the floor. I am beyond caring if that is an appropriate thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> 17 August 1922<br /> <br /> Pietr died last night. I\u2019m not sure how. I do not know if it was natural causes or if it was something that the guards did to him. Either way it does not matter. The man is dead. I find that my patience wans and I am more and more tempted to shift. The only thing that holds me back is the knowledge that if I do not kill every last person in this facility they will be able to report on a ravening beast that killed many of the guards. I do not want bring unwanted attention to myself or any others of my kind. I will have my revenge, though I do not yet know how. I will\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> 21 August 1922<br /> <br /> Hans came through for me. I was released the evening of the 17th. Hans managed to work his political magic and get my papers updated so that I am legal to travel to and from Yugoslavia should I choose. I am seriously considering never coming back to this country again. I\u2019ll see if time tempers my anger or not.<br /> When Hans came to get me out I will admit ashamedly that I needed his help to walk out of the cell. I had not eaten in essentially nine or ten days. I drank all the water that was brought to me, but ate very little. Most of it was burned anyway. It would have been inedible even if I didn\u2019t have a more refined diet. After Hans helped me walk out of the facility I told him that I was going to leave. It didn\u2019t matter that it was night time. I was going to start walking and just get out of that country. Hans is used to my eccentric behavior and just promised to deliver the package that I was paid to bring to this god forsaken country. I walked across the border and into the nearest forest where I shifted and ran until I found prey, and then I hunted. It was not my best kill, but I did manage to take down a doe and ate for the first time in many days. And despite having eaten my fill I still feel drained. I believe that I ended up sustaining myself on spiritual energy for a good part of my imprisonment. I will need to find some place that is strong with spiritual energy to refill my reserves.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9 September 1922<br /> <br /> I found a spirit that I think will do for a second fetish. I found it by accident. I happened to be passing through a small town and heard rumors about a spirit haunting an old mill on the edge of town. It had been burned out during the war, but some parts of it remained. I thought it likely that a ghost had taken up residence, but figured that it might be something else as well. So, I investigated the mill. It was not a ghost, but a spirit of chaos. It was drawn to this place during the war because of all the turmoil. It seemed to be enjoying the attention that it got from terrorizing the area. I couldn\u2019t very well let it continue, so I fought it for a bit and eventually wore it down until it agreed that powering a fetish was better than being banished. It will get attention and likely be in chaotic situations since Tatiana and I seem to be drawn to chaos. Not that I mind, but we do seem to manage to find trouble on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> I made this fetish so that Tatiana and I can share gifts. It was brought home to me at the play that Tatiana could not see the ghosts that were trying to disrupt the production, and it would have been useful if she could. I made this one out of copper and leather in the shape of a bracelet. The copper and leather intertwine and it kind of looks like one becomes the other. I also inscribed runes for sharing and strength into the copper. This one was harder to make, I think because of the strength of the spirit I bound to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 October 1922<br /> <br /> It\u2019s kind of the opposite of tradition but today I decided to give other people gifts on my birthday. During my travels I have carved several good luck charms out of wood for the children and for my brother to put in his house. I believe that my grandmother would have been proud to see how much of the old stories I remembered. I carved little spiders for everyone for good luck. For the children I made it a line of Papa and Mama spiders with baby spiders following. They are all connected by a string. For the adults I just made a single spider that they can put in the corner of a room or on a window sill. Alena actually seemed to like that one, even if she was somewhat derogatory of superstitions. She was not happy with me bringing back a set of table linens from Poland for Andel and Lenka though. Anything from out of the country and she has a problem with it. I can understand national pride, but I think she takes it a little too far.<br /> <br /> As far as presents for myself, Lenka knit me a scarf for the winter, and Andel got me a set of pens. He has noticed, I think, how much I write in this book. I appreciated both gifts very much. They were thoughtful. My father, ever the pragmatist gave me a knife. It is a sturdy all-purpose blade that can be used for pretty much anything. He said that he was concerned with me traveling so much and wanted to make sure that I could defend myself if I had to. I wanted to laugh at that, but did not. I thanked him for the practical gift and told him that it would come in useful. Father does not need to know the kinds of trouble that I have found myself in, and I\u2019m sure he would not approve of my chosen profession, but I appreciate the thought behind the gift regardless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> No, volchonok, go away, it is time for sleeping.<br /> <br /> The party is done, loud volchonok. It is time for sleeping.<br /> <br /> No, I am not angry because there is no one in my bed. I am angry because you are not letting me sleep.<br /> <br /> Because I wished to sleep, not mate.<br /> <br /> She was fine for dancing. I think she may have fainted if I asked her to bed.<br /> <br /> It was a celebration. Wolfram and Christina are now a mated pair. Nobles require many people to celebrate such a thing.<br /> <br /> Volchonok...<br /> <br /> I was defending the rings, as I said, should someone attempt to disrupt things.<br /> <br /> Yes. Yes volchonok, the cannons that shot flowers were Lizette\u2019s part to keep it safe as well. You are a foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> Blech. Then I would have had to stand in front of everyone and stand still and wear a dress lest I damage the poor souls\u2019 delicate natures. Carrying the rings was much better.<br /> <br /> Would you leave me be?<br /> <br /> I will fight you.<br /> <br /> You are right, I am too tired to fight you right now. Ask your questions and leave me be.<br /> <br /> Yes, it means we can speak of their pup. I presume.<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> No, I don\u2019t... I don\u2019t think Dacien was making a pup.<br /> <br /> With who... no, foolish volchonok, he definitely wasn\u2019t making a pup with Heinrich and Gunter. That does not wor-<br /> <br /> At the same time?<br /> <br /> No, I do not care. Bah.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am sure that does not work that way, even with three at the same time. Are you done?<br /> <br /> Yes. Yes volchonok, we will run. As far as you want. After I sleep.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Elena glanced over at Tatiana. The muscled woman was distracted and making more of a botch job of her mending than usual. The corner of her mouth began to turn up in a fond smile - the boys did prefer Aunt Tanya\u2019s uneven stitching and slightly bunched fabric. These would just be extra \u2018special\u2019.<br /> <br /> The slight smile faded as she caught sight of her lover\u2019s newest scar. It was another of the small collection that Elena could almost convince herself that it looked like a script sometimes. This one inspired strange feelings, much as Tatiana\u2019s temper did. When Elena had first married Tatiana\u2019s brother, her sister-in-law\u2019s temper frightened her. As she grew to know her better, it became more of a thrill, a dance along the knife\u2019s edge. Now she knew that temper was a shield, and a weapon, that Tatiana used to defend herself and those she loved.<br /> <br /> Tatiana looked over at her and caught her staring. \u201cEnjoying yourself?\u201d She set her mending aside and stretched, linking her fingers behind her head and leaning into her hands. \u201cDo I distract you from your work?\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena raised an eyebrow, but allowed the enjoyment of the sight before her to show on her face. \u201cMy work is finished.\u201d She looked down at Tatiana\u2019s last piece then back up at her, a smile playing around her lips.<br /> <br /> Tatiana groaned good naturedly but picked up her last piece and got back to work. She looked over at Elena frequently, an open smirk on her face. It was not too long before she finished, laying her last piece on the stack with a flourish. Elena rolled her eyes and picked up the pile, moving towards the door.<br /> <br /> The floorboards creaked as Tatiana stood up quickly, moving around behind Elena. She laid calloused hands on her lover\u2019s hips, pulling her close so she could bury her face in the curve of Elena\u2019s neck. \u201cWhy do you leave me? My heart is full of love for you.\u201d Elena shivered as Tatiana\u2019s lips brushed her neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that so?\u201d Elena moved away. The muscular woman let her, her fingertips trailing slowly across Elena\u2019s side. After placing the pile on a dresser, the smaller woman turned around to see an odd look on Tatiana\u2019s face. It was a serious look and full of uncertainty.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would prove it to you. Anyway you wish.\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena took a step towards her. \u201cI know it, love. Truly.\u201d There was an intensity in Tatiana\u2019s eyes, one Elena had caught there a couple of times these past few months. These past few months since her friend\u2019s wedding. This was the first time it had been aimed at her openly. She bit her lip nervously, wondering if she had the courage to ask for the proof that those eyes were already offering.<br /> <br /> A moment passed. Before she had the chance to gather her courage, Tatiana smiled broadly, her usual cockiness returned. She closed the distance between them quickly, kissing her tenderly. \u201cGood.\u201d She pulled Elena close, one hand pressing gently on the small of her back and the other caressing her cheek. \u201cSee that you do not forget.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b>Reunion</b><br /> <br /> \u201cDoes France get a lot of Thunderstorms in October?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana Barlowe looked out of Lizette\u2019s window. In the darkness outside, rain hit the glass. The smaller woman was preparing a glass of Cognac.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s still September until tomorrow, dear.\u201d Lizette put the bottle back in her cabinet.<br /> <br /> Dana turned away a moment to look at the pajama\u2019d Gremlin. \u201cOh it must be after midnight by now.\u2019 She casually turned back to the window.<br /> <br /> Lizette \u00c9toile sat her glass of Cognac on the bedside, and began to climb onto the bed. It was a well-practiced motion, as she pulled her lower body up with her upper body strength, her foot supporting her on the frame.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou British\u2026.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWelsh\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWelsh is British just not English.\u201d Lizette sat down. \u201cYou\u2026Welsh\u2026don\u2019t seem to understand how big France is. Much bigger than\u2026Wales.\u201d She grinned at her paramour.<br /> <br /> Dana turned and leaned against the window frame as thunder rumbled behind her. \u201cI\u2019ve taught you well on your answer dodging, love.\u201d Her smile was mildly seductive, not the sort that demanded action, but promised more to come. \u201cIt\u2019s so good to see you again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is.\u201d Lizette smiled. \u201cEverything is going well. Wolfram and Christina are happy\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you?\u2019 No change in expression, but her eyebrow quirked.<br /> <br /> The Inventor made a shrugging gesture. \u201cI am okay. Far better than I was when you saw me last.\u201d<br /> <br /> She did not seem to be lying. Dana felt some relief. Picking up the pieces of Lizette after the wedding was harder than crawling out of some of the traps in old tombs. She really did seem better. Dana was inwardly a little intimidated at how glad she was. There was a pause.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow was the reception, by the way? You were not in the best mindspace, dear, afterwards.,\u2018 The archaeologist sipped her own Cognac leaning against the frame. A flash of light lit the night outside showing her silhouette through her gown.<br /> <br /> \u201cChristina was happy\u2026um\u2026not much else\u2026\u201d Lizette scrunched her face. Then she started to smile. \u201cOh, wait, um, Dacian seduced Christina\u2019s brother, and Wolfram\u2019s brother at the same time. He wasn\u2019t real obvious about it, but it was kinda awesome.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana smiled and shook her head as she walked away from the window. \u201cI\u2019m glad he enjoyed himself, I suppose.\u201d She walked past Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re. She hissed. The archeologist turned to Lizette. \u201cCan we send her out of the room when we make love this time? I don\u2019t think she was very happy last time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette shrugged, \u201cI told her to leave. She chose to stay to keep an eye on you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana smiled and walked over to the night table. \u201cAnything else?\u201d Lizette stared at her several moments. Dana was so beautiful. A girl could lose herself in those twinkling eyes and knowing grin. Wait, she was talking. \u201cWh-what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Party.\u201d Dana leaned forward and smiled. \u201cThat I did not attend, remember?\u201d A crash from outside.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, Dearbh\u00e1il sang\u2026that\u2019s about it. There was\u2026.stuff.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana sat down on the bed. Her hand ran through Lizette\u2019s fine green hair, her left index finger rested on the point of the gremlin\u2019s left ear. \u201cHave you been okay? Emotionally, since then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I mean I have been fine. I said I was fine. I have been busy on work.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, made your plan go faster? New modification to the automobile?\u201d<br /> <br /> &quot;No, I invented a new sort of firebomb to drop from planes that can light huge areas on fire. But I haven\u2019t thought about the wedding or the pregnancy at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> The room momentarily lit with a day\u2019s brightness. Dana bit her lip. \u201cRight. Well I am here now.\u201d Her finger traced the edge of Lizette\u2019s ear. Dana thought the largish pointed ears of the Gremlin were terribly cute, but she dared never say. There was quiet as Lizette\u2019s eyes closed and she enjoyed the sensation. Dana felt the weight of her feelings, and spoke to break the silence.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been working in the field. Went to Morocco after Paris, and lost myself there. Then, the Riviera, to flirt with nobles and chase heiresses.\u201d She smiled. Not that she had had much real luck with women recently; they just were not enough like Lizette. Nor, really, had her heart been into the men she pursued. But she would not say that. \u201cHave you gone back to skirt chasing?\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette looked down. A lighting flash outside caught her eyes, which seemed to illuminate for a few moments. \u201cAfter spending time with you and Christina\u2026honestly I have barely looked at Dearbh\u00e1il anymore, much less gone hunting,\u201d She paused. \u201cI\u2026will confess there have been dalliances with Marlene. These were not planned, but I have been teaching her a good deal of mathematics and sciences, and, well, one is in the room for hours\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana nodded. Her hand slipped down to the waistband of Lizette\u2019s pajamas. Lizette\u2019s hips were warm underneath. \u201cMarlene is a lovely girl. No shame in that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe needs a husband though. She is lonely, and I can\u2019t give her what she truly needs any more than she can with me.\u201d There was a pause. \u201c Have you met anyone? That might be a match for her I mean\u201d The Wizened added the last part quickly and looked up at her paramour.<br /> <br /> Dana bit her lip again. She was close enough to smell Lizette now, and it was sending her mind in desirous directions. Perhaps she could wrap up the conversation. \u201cMorocco is not conducive to meeting eligible men\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou were in the Rivera though\u2026\u201d Even with the storm, Lizette\u2019s mind was apparently not in the gutter enough. Dana shook her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Marlene is not who has been on my mind. You have.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette looked away. \u201cI am sorry, you come all the way here and I ask about other women\u2026\u201d Dana cupped her chin in her hand and turned to face back to her. Large, golden mischievous eyes looked into her soul. Dana had missed them. Deep down, there was a twinge of fear. How far was this going to go? Despite not being truly human looking, Lizette\u2019s eyes were very deep indeed.<br /> <br /> There was silence, and Dana lowered her lips to the Gremlin\u2019s own, their electricity matching the storm outside. The kiss she received was entirely too emotional for Dana once upon a time. Now she returned one like it. A loud clap of thunder came from outside. Her hands slipped into Lizette\u2019s waistband, even as Lizette\u2019s dexterous fingers slipped under her gown.<br /> <br /> \u201cI came all the way here to see you, my love. Right now, I care about nothing else\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Dana\u2019s eyes fluttered open. After looking around for her bearings, she smiled slightly at all the bizarre knick-knacks around the room, the ticking of several clocks and small warm ticking ball at her side. She began to slowly extract herself from the little green ball and slipped out of bed. Her evening gown would not be the same, but she didn\u2019t much mind. She walked over to the window and looked out. The sun was bright, and the trees were beginning to turn the colors of autumn, which matched the firelight that often illuminated her lover. Tatiana was outside on the lawn, gesturing and talking to nothing. Probably a spirit, the Russian was a werewolf after all.<br /> <br /> This wasn\u2019t the first noble bedroom Dana had woken in, but this might be the one it happened most often in. The archeologist frowned. Was she getting soft? Perhaps she needed to disappear again. She glanced back at her stirring lover. Not now.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood Morning Mon Amour,\u201d The Wizened smiled brightly. \u201cIs all well out there?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana nodded. \u201cIt is a gorgeous day to spend went you. All is well, though Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re may never forgive me.<br /> <br /> Lizette laughed and covered her face. \u201cI probably would not either, if someone had asked me for a cup of tea in that position. I would hope fleeing the room in a fit of pique would be my entire reaction.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana smiled too. \u201cThen we should enjoy it. Plenty of time will be spent in this room. Hopefully without your teapot.\u201d<br /> <br /> The lovers dressed. Whatever stresses they had that pulled at their hearts, this October morning was theirs.<br /> <br /> And with it, the future.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Optimistic endpoints. Well, except with Marek, but optimism and Marek are not on speaking terms. Only comment needed is Adawolf\u2019s Greta and Greta Hess, Sin-Eater, are not the same person.<br /> <br /> We say goodbye to Dana, Nathan, and Iris for awhile. Look for Skadi and Greta in the next story, though.<br /> <br /> Okay a few things moving forward. First, in (less than) a week now, there will be a short post giving some information on Berlin in October of 1922. It is a very different world than Paris right now. Second, while I felt like the underside of a gorilla last Friday I did manage to run, but it was short and not my best work. Already got Tatiana for it. Also, a lot of events in late May/Early June has some game schedules shuttered around, but that won\u2019t affect you guys any.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome. I put up this, the Balance of Shadows journals, and get some fucking sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-16-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:54:25-07:00","id":894560,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week! Technically I do have Golden Eagle tomorrow as late May-Early June schedule shifting is in full force, but Journal Schedule is staying regular. <br /> <br /> This post is the handout given to prepare the PCs for Berlin in October 1922. I have a few comments for you here<br /> <br /> One, as always, I did my research, but don\u2019t take anything as absolutely historical. I love the 1920s, I love queer history, and this game hits both subjects fairly directly since five of seven PCs are at least mildly queer (very mildly, in Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s case). And this is a love letter to the era, and I <i>tried</i>. But don\u2019t assume I got everything right. The broad strokes are true, however.<br /> <br /> Second, it is tricky, dealing with Germany in this era. As with any group, there are good Germans, bad Germans, and bad Germans who are Nazis/proto-Nazis. My goal is not to make my villains all eventual members of the group (if they live) and not to play stereotypes despite dealing with the fact the Nazis are objectively awful people. It\u2019s still a decade till they rise, though, and connecting any villainy to them is silly. So yea, there are signs. Some things are obvious in retrospect, but that is just how it goes. My goal was and is to treat the German people fairly, insofar as that matters is some random chick\u2019s spooky game.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s have a look at Berlin in October 1922<br /> <br /> Berlin was an Invictus city until the end of the War, and was every bit as stable as Paris. That is true no longer; the Invictus were driven out. The Circle of the Crone (called locally Gullweig-Gesellschaft) and the Ordo Dracul are the two strongest factions, but as neither will allow the other full power, they both tug the strings of Prince Werner, of the Carthians. Werner has barred the city from Invictus, but there is little that can be done if an Invictus protected by the Ordo Dracul or Gullweig-Gesellschaft entered the city. He dares not anger either faction, and rules at their sufferance.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, Werner and his Carthians arranged for the ouster of the Prussian Invictus, but he ultimately had help. In the Chaos that followed the Armistice, both Belial\u2019s Brood and VII made incursions into the city. Well, it is believed VII did, no true proof came. But Belial\u2019s Brood worked to topple those in power, and topple the Invictus they did. Officially, Belial\u2019s Brood was driven from the city; their losses were massive. Unofficially, Werner fears they may be out there still. <br /> <br /> Both the Ordo Dracul and Gullweig-Gesellschaft are very much pursuing their own interests, leaving Werner stuck with trying to influence the rebuilding of Berlin. He hopes for a socialist paradise, and the Communists within the Carthians seek to woo him to their side\u2026or oust him if they can\u2019t. <br /> <br /> The Uratha of the group know little about Berlin, except that it is the territory of the proud Prussian Pure. Unlike the Invictus, they did not lose power in the war, though the Ivory Claws\u2019 position within the Pure was weakened. The Fire-Touched Tribe\u2019s power waxes, and the Ivory Claws struggle to maintain their own influence. The lack of alliance with Vienna\u2019s Pure was meaningless to the power of the Pure as a whole, but a major setback for the Ivory Claws, as well as a boon for the Fire-Touched.<br /> <br /> Spirits run wild in Berlin. The Pure do nothing to stop them, and the Fire-Touched actively try to bring in more. The bad news for Uratha PCs is unlike Vienna they have no back up here. There are alone in enemy territory. The good news is the Pure are not looking for them. They are certain Berlin is theirs, and so the Ivory Claws and Fire-Touched struggle with each other. Strange Werewolves are more likely to be rivals of the other faction than Forsaken, unless they get a good look at you.<br /> <br /> The War was unkind to the Changeling Courts of Berlin. The Winter Court, under Queen Skadi, is ascendant, and while she may not be High Queen, control of the Changelings is hers. Many love her, many fear her. Kind and Ruthless, Gentle and Cruel, the towering Elemental holds the keys to Berlin. She is, however, not without rivals. The Spring Court, completely rebuilt from the ashes under Prince Sascha, is patroning the rise of the arts within the city and has aligned with Queen Woebegone of Autumn and her influence on the film industry. They look to spread love, hope, dread and terror throughout the world, and their combined power has begun to threaten Skadi\u2019s control. The Summer Court, stripped of their teeth, are little more than more minions for Skadi.<br /> <br /> Still, Skadi does not rule with an iron fist. She is very well liked among the people, and her affections are widely and highly sought after. But many also know her rivalry with Prince Sascha and Queen Woebegone is bound to heat up.<br /> <br /> The situation among the Dead is even more chaotic than these others creatures. While Germany has many war ghosts, much of the fighting was outside, meaning while Sin-Eaters in France run about putting out fires, the many German dead have time to consider other things.<br /> <br /> Black Company, or Schwarze Reichswehr, is a Second Tier Krewe of the most dangerous Sin-Eaters in Germany. All ex-military, the Black Company seeks to protect Germany\u2019s interests and quietly help them rebuild. Rumors of ghost-driven factories abound, and some wonder if Black Company are not looking outward with their plans.<br /> <br /> While the Black Company are the most dangerous, they are not the most feared. Die Wacht, or The Watch, are a Krewe who seek to kill or drive out the foreigners weakening Berlin. A minimum sized second Tier Krewe, Die Wacht may sound like natural allies for the Schwarze Reichswehr, but not all ex-soldiers are racist fuckheads, and the Black Company remains conflicted on how to deal with them. Unofficially, smaller Krewes within Schwarze Reichswehr have both cooperated with and fought Die Wacht.<br /> <br /> Two Sister Krewes growing in influence are Heilige Schar, or The Sacred Band, and Die Freundinnen, or the Girlfriends. The two Krewes welcome any homosexual members, and have stationed themselves as the protectors of the burgeoning queer Mecca that is Berlin. Operating often in and around the cabarets, they seek primarily to defend and educate. They often clash with Die Wacht, and occasionally with Schwarze Reichswehr, though like with Die Wacht Schwarze Reichswehr has no official policy toward them. <br /> <br /> These are not the only Krewes. There is also Die Karnevalklub, or The Carnival Club, a celebratory Krewe dedicated to enjoy their new life and, apparently, wearing creepy-ass masks. But seriously, given the nature of the game, they are probably not who should be on your mind right now (unless you like doin\u2019 it with people in masks, in which case have at, but it will be your fault I have to download a bunch of damn creepy mask people pictures).<br /> <br /> Weimar Berlin is dancing madly on the lip of the volcano. Economically, the city is in utter ruins. People literally push wheelbarrows full of money to afford bread and milk. And sometimes prices can as much as triple over the course of a few hours. It is possible to see a price, go home to get more bags on money, come back and no longer be able to afford it. Many lost their homes, and while the government is long on blaming others, it is short on what to do.<br /> <br /> King Wilhelm II remains in exile. Friedrich Ebert is President, and will remain so until 1925 when Paul von Hindenburg takes over. Lothar von Richthofen, brother of the Red Baron, is dead, and with him flying ace branch of the Richthofen line. We are about a year from the Beer Hall Putsch being staged by Adolph Hitler in Munich. Speaking of Bavaria, despite its place in the coming new order, it was only recently a Soviet Republic. Despite the Bavarian Soviet Republics fall, a deal has been made (no doubt influenced by Black Company) with the Soviet Union to allow for training and weapons. Illegal under the armistice, but the Russia is not in the League of Nations. Extreme Left and Right struggle for supremacy, but neither retains the upper hand here.<br /> <br /> And yet, the people dance. Burlesque houses, cabarets, and jazz clubs and bars pop up all over, and the culture of Weimar Berlin is one of dancing and music. Berlin is the largest trendsetter on new music outside the United States, and among the leaders in fashion. Her movies are among the best in the world. The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari, Nosferatu, The Golem, all are movies known throughout the world. In time, M, Der Blaue Engle, (with Marlene Dietrich) and The Last Laugh will be among the most famous movies in the world. <br /> <br /> Science is also thriving. Mathematics and Psychology are just two of the disciplines with some of the leading minds in the world located in Germany. Leipzig University especially but not exclusively was famous, attracting many Nobel Prize Winners. <br /> <br /> Much like Paris, perhaps even more, homosexuality has reached its high water mark of acceptance in Berlin. The number gay clubs, lesbian clubs, gay periodicals and lesbian periodicals exceeds Paris notably. Some films even deal with queer subjects. <br /> <br /> What I said before when introducing you to Paris still applies, and I have quoted it below here.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The Roaring 20s have fully hit Europe. Bobbed hair is not unusual, especially in the west. The stereotypical flapper dresses, with less adhering to the body and more leg showing, has caused wigs to be initially flipped and are now all over. Similarly, the (what is now called) \u201cGatsby Look\u201d is popular with the menfolk, as men value \u201cmodern\u201d suits over those before the great war. More than any time previously, there is an intense gap between the old and the young. And the young are on fire.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s not just Fashion. Flappers demand the right to vote, to take whatever job they qualify for. They march in and apply for jobs not specifically listed as being for women and ask men what their problem is. And women\u2019s voting is breaking out everywhere. Germany and the United Kingdom in 1918. Austria allowed it in 1919. Czechoslovakia allowed it in 1920. The Italians haven\u2019t yet but it will clearly be any year now. France and Belgim are nowhere close, and women are hopping mad about that and constantly pushing for it. <br /> <br /> By this time Jazz has exploded into Europe. The popular songs sound very different. It\u2019s a year before the Charleston has hit, but dancing, performing, the very done is different. Women move on stage in all sorts of ways. This is less a surprise for the French PCs than former German, Russian or Austrian, but it\u2019s still a major shift. Dearbh\u00e1il likely recalls totally different types of music less than a year ago, but this is what people want to hear. Music has always echoed all over Paris, but never like now.<br /> <br /> Of course, no Prohibition here.<br /> <br /> Women are taking all kinds of advantage of freedom they did not have before the war, and its happening at an astonishing rate. Walking alone on the street won\u2019t likely the questions about where one\u2019s father or husband is\u2026maybe from some old fool, but no one a gal has time for.<br /> <br /> In Europe (unlike America) we are at a high water mark for gay acceptance we would need see the like again of till the 1990s and have not seen over much of the continent since the fall of Rome. Movies, non pornographic ones, are being made in Germany and France discussing stuff like coming out for men or men who become involved with couples, and gay men have their own magazines in the United Kingdom (not Ireland, of course, it\u2019s banned) France, and Germany. Germany and France even have magazines for queer women. Minor queer subplots appear in more mainstream films or stories, which are often not translated to English\u2026.a mysterious siren may have an old female lover she mentions offhandedly, or good friends may be involved with each other. This does not mean there were not vicious attacks on gays and lesbians, but never had it been so publicly acknowledged or discussed, and it would be about 50 years after WWII that it would be again, as Homosexuality is seen as a sign of interest in Communism (in Capitalist nations) and decedent bourgeoisie behavior (in Communist ones). It vanished rapidly in Germany as early as 1933, as did many of the films and books made. But right now, lesbian salons in Paris, gay men\u2019s clubs in many major cities operating with only the mildest of fig leaves, and one can have magazines for living the life. Queer women in Paris are advised to keep a monocle handy; it is a sure signal, even if worn briefly, that one is open to such things.<br /> <br /> While those German movies are being made, there is a much more ambitious films being made. In fact, a lot of people in Paris are talking about a little film that came out last month in Germany and just arrived in Paris: Nosferatu. Can it possibly be as scary as they say? The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari a couple years back made an impression for sure.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the old world collapses. The Struggles you have seen told hold onto the past this story? It\u2019s failing. Dying. Charles I of Austria, the last monarch of Austria-Hungary who rose when Franz Josef died, was voted as King of Hungary and arrested by the English before he could take power and whisked away to a forgotten island, where he died under mysterious circumstances this month in a shattering blow to many among the Austrian old guard. The last of the Hapsburgs who reigned are gone. Lothar von Richthofen, the Red Baron\u2019s younger brother and last scion of the family, is dead. In Vienna, the left and right and building personal armies that will next year have open warfare to see if Austria becomes a Fascist or Communist state. In Berlin the economy just collapsed. Again. People carry money in wheelbarrows, and prices sometimes triple based on time of day. <br /> <br /> And yet the young dance.<br /> <br /> The old world burns, the new world rises. That which has risen may fall. That which has fallen may rise again. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Okay there you go. I have at this writing journals from Marek, Tatiana and Lizette for last session, and I am going to prep them while the memories are fresh. Despite being half out of my mind from being sick the session went reasonably well if not real focused right off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T18:52:43-07:00","id":895215,"title":"","content":"I hope you are better.<br /> <br /> Does Prince Sascha have any thoughts towards Dadaism?<br /> <br /> I can readily imagine the Changelings being interested in German Expressionism. Quite fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 05-21-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T21:18:03-07:00","id":895279,"title":"","content":"Hope you're better now Baroness.<br /> <br /> Looks like Marek can't travel without getting into trouble!<br /> Lizette is seemingly beginning to move on, but I wonder if she's not setting herself up for another heartbreak with Dana who appears kind of scared by the idea of a stable relationship.<br /> I had a strange desire to high five Dacian, which probably means I'm watching too many american sitcoms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And Tatiana had me giggling like an idiot.<br /> <br /> Thanks for sharing!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:44:39-07:00","id":895313,"title":"","content":"Omenseer: Getting there. Turns out I had a virus, then when I began recovering I got two different infections. But I am bathing myself in antibiotics. I shall have to consider Prince Sascha's view of Dadism. Right now I got nothing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anteros: As I told Omen, getting there. Marek's player seems to have a thing for tormenting their characters. Well, rather this character, their character in MDH less so. Lizette is doing better, the sessions we have had of the new story she has been much more her usual self. We will see how the Dana romance goes when we get back to it. The character's main interests atm being Christina, Dana and Wolfram, but then Lizette is pretty poly. Dana has a lot to unpack and any relationship with her is bound to be interesting, which is good I have a few old fashion archaeological stories coming up which will feature her so good to have the extra interest. Dacian seems to be making up for lost time; his last romantic connection was the Solstice party in Vienna with an essentially unnamed character. We will see how things/if things with Heinrich or Gunther progress. And Tatiana never fails for awesome. <br /> <br /> Thanks both for the feedback, it is most appreciated. Journals for last session in just under a week!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T22:46:48-07:00","id":901775,"title":"","content":"Berlin teeters on the edge of disaster, a dark fate looming like the shadow of Vesuvius over Pompeii. But this golden fountain will cover Europe. But it is a decade before those days, and in these times of desperation there is dancing, music, and desperation and starvation. It is into this place the PCs walk, where joy and sorrow are a heartbeat from one another.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXIX</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 21 October 1922<br /> <br /> So it seems that fate is drawing all of us to Germany, Berlin in particular. The fae members of the pack received an invitation from Skadi to come to Berlin. She explained in a brief message that she needs discreet help from people who are not connected to the Berlin Courts. So Dearbhail, Lizette and especially Dacian are keen on going. Also Alla had already made plans to go to Berlin to do something with the horror film industry people. She is going with Marissa, who has connections in the city and can make it safe for Alla to travel there. Alla explained that the Invictus group, of which she is a part, is not allowed in the city. But Alla is connected through Marissa to the Lancea et Sanctum group, so all is made well. At least she won\u2019t be killed for entering the city. It would still be prudent to be on guard for any possible threats to Alla. And lastly Wolfram was contacted by a fellow Sin Eater in Berlin with a request for a meeting. The man, Willie Schmidt, needs help but can\u2019t look for help within the city. Much like the Fae Winter Queen. Schmidt needs some discreet help that cannot be traced back to him. So we are all going to travel to Berlin and find out what\u2019s going on and what we can do to help. <br /> <br /> So, we discussed our options and the idea of buying a house in Berlin to act as a base of operations came up. It seemed easier than renting a house due to the possible danger that we might find ourselves in. I would like to say that there wasn\u2019t much chance for trouble in Germany, but I would be lying. There is the possibility for a great deal of trouble in Berlin. And not the least of our problems is that the city is pretty much all Pure, either Fire Touched or Ivory Claws, but no Forsaken tribes. That will make things interesting for Tatiana and me. At least in human form we can pass as one of them. The moment we shift though, I believe it will be obvious which side of things we\u2019re on.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 24 October 1922<br /> <br /> We bought a house and put it in Wolfram\u2019s name to be on the safe side. The situation in Germany is getting tense where it comes to foreigners so we put the house in the name of the only German citizen in our group. That should keep things good on that front at least. We have also had Lizette go ahead in the plane and create a door to the Hedge in the basement and rig the house with explosives in case of emergencies. It\u2019s not my first plan for what to do in case of trouble, but I do have to admit that it would make a good way to eliminate all potential enemies in a single action. I am still hoping that it will not be necessary to blow up the house. It is a nice house, practical enough for all of us to live in and fancy enough that Alla can entertain film industry guests and look every bit the successful leading lady.<br /> <br /> The other thing we discussed was having each of our fae pack members assigned, so to speak, to one or two of the non-fae members so if we need to escape through the Hedge we will all be able to do so quickly. Dearbhail has been assigned to me and Tatiana. Dacian has been assigned to Alla and Fenric, while Lizette has been assigned to Wolfram. I thought it was a good precaution to have in place. That way no matter what happens we know who to go with to get us out. Tatiana may not like the idea of running from trouble, but I at least have a healthy respect for a good exit strategy.<br /> <br /> Tonight we also met with Schmidt. Wolfram and I went to the meeting openly. Lizette and Dacian followed but stayed to the shadows. We did not want to spook Schmidt, nor did we want to underestimate him. For all we knew he might have been followed or could have brought friends with him. He greeted us cordially enough and offered us dinner. We accepted and we all sat down to eat and talk things over. The meal was good, but simple. I got the impression that the farmstead that we met at is failing. I only saw a couple of animals and the house itself looks mostly unlived in. I think Schmidt is sleeping there, but not really living in the house. <br /> <br /> So, Schmidt told us about the factions of Sin Eaters in the city. Though he never used the term Sin Eater. He called them groups. I think he was assuming that I was not aware of my friend\u2019s condition or powers. That\u2019s fine. I don\u2019t mind being underestimated. He told us about the Black Company and The Watch. The Black Company, who Schmidt is a member of, is a group of fallen soldiers that served in the Great War. They got together to protect the Fatherland during this post-war troubling time. The Watch is also out to protect the Fatherland, but they have a slightly different agenda. Their idea of protecting their country is to run off or kill any foreigners that live in the country. To me that is like cutting off your nose to spite your face. They are pushing away possible allies and help by reacting so violently to foreigners. Countries can\u2019t stand completely alone. Not in this modern era of trade. Everyone relies on trade and good relations with our neighbors to ensure a healthy economy and stable government. Unfortunately for Germany they have fallen on hard times financially. Inflation has skyrocketed and what used to be a fortune is now almost worthless. People carry hug bags of money just to buy bread and milk.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Schmidt was describing the two different factions in Berlin and what they\u2019re up to. Right now some members of the Black Company are smuggling in guns from a communist group called Red October. The weapons are supposed to go to communist revolutionaries within the city, but they are actually going to be misrouted to go to The Watch. So in essence the communists will be supplying weapons to kill communists. Schmidt didn\u2019t want to see more weapons in the hands of The Watch, nor was he happy that members of his own krewe (as Woflram calls Sin Eater groups) are involved in this whole thing.<br /> <br /> The idea that we eventually decided on to combat this threat was to have Lizette fly Tatiana and Dearbhail ahead so Tatiana can board the same train as Ruskov, the commander of the smuggling operation and member of the Red October krewe. Dearbhail will take a picture of the two conversing. Meanwhile some of us will be adding a little something extra to the Russian\u2019s shipment. We plan on adding a quantity of silver ammunition so when we alert Ilsa and her allies, by way of a damning photograph, they will sense the silver in the shipment and get upset at the Russians. This would take care of at least some of our enemies without us having to get more directly involved. Tatiana was a bit upset that the plan does not involve more fighting on our parts, but I think she is on board with the plan as we have it. I am not discounting the possibility of future fights while we are in Berlin. <br /> <br /> To add more problems to everyone\u2019s plates there are several groups of Communist agitators in town as well. They are trying to sow the seeds of their beliefs in Berlin, which is just adding fuel to the fire for groups like The Watch who want nothing to do with them. There are just so many groups popping up in Germany right now in response to the political and financial unrest. We will need to do further research in order to find out who some of these groups are and where they meet. <br /> <br /> Greta, who came by after our planning session, offered to help us find the Communist agitators within the city when she found out our need. She noticed our activity in the area and decided to come by and see what was going on. So, without prompting Tatiana filled her in on everything that we had heard and had planned so far. I wouldn\u2019t have laid it all out on the table like that for Greta, just because she is such a wild card, but I couldn\u2019t stop Tatiana before she started talking. I suppose it all worked out in the end when Greta offered to show us around and help us ferret out the Communist groups within the city. I think she that she\u2019s just aiming to find a fight. I am not sure actually if she would fight in her home city. Her father has plans for her to settle down, get married and be a good dutiful wife. I do not see that in Greta\u2019s future. Even before her change she was far too headstrong to settle down. I do not know how openly she defies her father though. She may do so just to make him mad, or she may hide her activities. I do not know. Time will tell on that count.<br /> <br /> I was given pause to think earlier during our conversation with Schmidt. Wolfram mentioned that in an ideal world there would be no need for soldiers or for fighting. Schmidt said that he wasn\u2019t sure what he would do in such a world. I did not say anything at the time, but had similar thoughts. I do not know what I would do with myself if there were no conflicts. Political strife creates a lot of work for me as Reznik. If there were no fighting or tension then I would be out of work. I suppose that would not be a bad thing. At least that is what I should be feeling I think. I find it hard to think of my work outside of practicalities.<br /> <br /> It might be nice for the majority if there were peace, but I am a realist. Governments are made up of people and people are greedy. They want more land, more money, more power. Always more of something. This makes governments corrupt. The Communists preach equality for all and a government ruled by the masses. It won\u2019t work. It won\u2019t work because people are involved, and any ideal will eventually be ruined by people. It never fails. So, while it might be nice if there were no fighting it\u2019s not realistic. There will always be wars because there are always more greedy people who want more. Or there are more people that want to prove to others that they are right and everyone else is wrong. Ideally there would be no need for people like Schmidt or people like me, but we don\u2019t live in an ideal world. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we will not be going back to the green place again. Well, not now or soon, probably.<br /> <br /> Yes, I will take you with me if I do.<br /> <br /> I know you like being solid and letting all the others see how foolish a volchonok you are, but we have no reason to use the Hedge to go back to Paris.<br /> <br /> The odd smell is probably explosives. You will get used to it, it is not a good enough reason to go back to the green place.<br /> <br /> They are there in case the Pure find our new house. Also to keep Lizette happy.<br /> <br /> I will be very unhappy with you, volchonok, if you blow up our house.<br /> <br /> How wise you are, to change the subject. We are here for many reasons. All human things, nothing to interest you, oh so superior volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, Wolfram's visit was one.<br /> <br /> Because the person he was meeting was nervous, so we did not wish to frighten him. Probably it was good. He likely would have thought me a Bolshevik.<br /> <br /> The Bolshevik Sin-Eaters are giving the nationalist German Sin-Eaters guns by way of Wolfram\u2019s friend\u2019s pack, this is why.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, are you not paying attention? Wolfram\u2019s friend wishes to stop them. This is why he is nervous. And the nationalist Germans altogether. This is why he spoke to Wolfram.<br /> <br /> No, we are not to fight them. Not tonight or tomorrow night at least. Probably sometime before we leave.<br /> <br /> I know! It is horrible. I even had a clever plan, where we were to attack the weapon trade, and kill the Red and his men. Then Wolfram would rescue his body and tell him what was happening. <br /> <br /> When he came back to life, of course, foolish volchonok. He is a Sin-Eater, like Wolfram, remember?<br /> <br /> The Reds do not know that their guns are going to nationalist Germans. They would not like this, since the nationalist Germans do not like foreigners, or the Reds.<br /> <br /> Because... bah. To keep secrets, or be complicated, or, I don\u2019t know. I forget why we are doing the other thing. The others in the pack believe it is best however, so, there it is.<br /> <br /> Well, Alla will take a photograph of me and the Red speaking congenially when Lizette has flown us to his train. We get these photographs to Ilsa, who will recognize me, and think this is dangerous. So she will watch the Red and sense the silver bullets we will put in his things. Then the Pure will fight the Reds.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it is very complicated. And I do not get to fight.<br /> <br /> After? We take photographs of Germans shooting Bolsheviks with Russian weapons. Then they will no longer send weapons.<br /> <br /> Photographs are like memories, but on paper.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that is a very human thing.<br /> <br /> I do not know when I will fight. Perhaps Greta will help me find a fight.<br /> <br /> Yes, you missed her. She found that we had bought the house and came to visit.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I will fight her father.<br /> <br /> He keeps trying to decide a mate for her. She would do well to find a pack, even though all the packs of her kind here seem to be improper fits. But he should not choose for her, either for pack or mate.<br /> <br /> We will not be running, volchonok, with or without Greta, not here in Berlin. Out there it is not our territory, there is much to do and our pack has need of us. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans<br /> </b><br /> 24th October 1922<br /> <br /> We are carrying out an operation in Berlin. We spent the past four days purchasing a house to use as a base of operations and establishing a link to the Hollow. Today we began to take action.<br /> <br /> Alla has vampire business involving the Circle of the Crone, Constancia\u2019s group of vampires. Dacian is eager to once again try to please Skadi in his quest to woo her, though he risks running afoul Prince Sascha of Spring and Queen Woebegone of Autumn in the process. But much of today was spent helping Wolfram with his mission, concerning the Prussian Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Compared to those in France, the German Sin-Eaters have rather organized on a military level, the Schwarze Reichswehr being the most impressive. Willie Schmidt is a member of the Schwarze Reichswehr, and wanted to meet with Wolfram in secret. Wolfram and Marek went to speak to him at a dreary farmhouse outside Berlin. Dacian watched from close range invisibly, while I hid on the edge of the property. Tatiana was at a general store not far away. Willie invited Marek and Wolfram in, so I did not see or hear much, but I smelled that he prepared them a meal. The rest I heard back at base that night. The meeting went fine, though Wolfram was of course grateful for our diligence.<br /> <br /> While I was out there in the tree, I considered how flat the land is in that area. Swampy in places. Some sort of huge Spider-modeled tank seems a good way to traverse the area, and useful for deployment of arms. Would be totally frightening too. Firing rockets or grenades while creeping along, I bet I could make it so it could walk low to move under a waterline, then pop up and use it\u2019s flamethrower, as all tanks need flamethrowers.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> So the Schwarze Reichswehr are an umbrella group of fallen German soldiers. Having fallen in the War is the sole criteria for joining, and they seek to guard Germany. However, they disagree with how to do this. Some side with Die Wacht, a foreigner-hating bunch of thugs, while others worry the Soviets may attack from within or without, a sensible fear. The bear has been hungry of late, and the Reds are pretty active in Vienna these days. Willie has discovered a plot by some in the Schwarze Reichswehr to acquire arms from a Russian Soviet Krewe called Red October, which are supposed to go to Communist Revolutionaries (which according to Greta there are several groups of), but instead would be given to Die Wacht. Willie discovered when a shipment would arrive.<br /> <br /> We discussed a lot of plans. Many many plans. Everything from outright battle to various forms of sabotage. The Sin-Eaters ability to rapidly rise from death is a major problem here; it is pretty much impossible to assume that we will not be seen and described by those there, dead or not. <br /> <br /> So the plan we settled on was to arrange for the Pure to do our dirty work for us. The plan is I will fly ahead to have us meet the train at an earlier station. There have Tatiana speak to the Red October\u2019s Commander Ruskov, and have Dearbh\u00e1il take a picture of the meeting. We also sneak some of my silver ammunition into the weapons being sent. We then get the photo to Ilsa and her Prussian Pure, and they believe it has to do with us since she fought Tatiana personally before. The Pure attack the drop off, and fight hopefully both Red October and those in Schwarze Reichswehr who are helping Die Wacht. Whoever wins, both sides will be weakened and there will be suspicion between Red October and Schwarze Reichswehr. The fact these Fog Men will be displaying powers and effects similar to Wolfram when she was in the battle before can only help. <br /> Phase two is we spy on Die Wacht who already have some Russian weapons, and next time they attack Communist Agents in Berlin we get pictures to send to Russia to prove the Red October are being taken in. I am no fan of Communists, but I will take them over German Nationalists any day. This conflict may also serve to dissuade Schwarze Reichswehr from assisting Die Wacht as much. I hope.<br /> <br /> Some of this information came as a certain familiar yet irritating bundle of Daddy Issues waltzed into our meeting. Greta Hess was eager to pester us again. That girl has learned nothing. She was, however, eager to help us against Die Wacht, and not a fan of Schwarze Reichswehr either. Macho as German Soldiers tend to be I don\u2019t blame her. She did not seem to like most local Krewes. Die Karnevalklub sounded simultaneously intriguing and creepy.<br /> <br /> I guess I can\u2019t completely blame her. Her Dad\u2019s eagerness to marry her off so she can be a productive housewife should be frustrating to most modern women. That Greta walks her road and needs no one else is admirable. I wish she would be nicer to Wolfram though.<br /> <br /> I also feel pangs of sympathy for Willie. His family has gone, leaving him with a farm he barely knows how to use, and which there is not enough of him to keep up. I know what it is to be the only one standing at the empty house you grew up in, knowing every other soul has passed. German or not, he has my sympathy.<br /> <br /> But now is not the time. Now is the time for Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> Technically, they added a Door to the Hollow in the basement, to make traveling back to Paris, and that Haunt and such easier. And Lizette wanted to be prepared to blow up the house because of course she did.<br /> <br /> I played Schmidt for pathos, and I worked it. I noted the small amount of meat in the meal, and that providing it was probably expensive for him. I noted how Wolfram and Marek got more than he did. I talked about the deteriorating house, lean animals, and really conveyed his desperation, even outside the situation. It worked, with the PCs, snug in their large house (which connected to their mansion in a magic realm, connected to their other real world mansion) having a fine dinner discussing it feeling a bit guilty. This was not like Paris. I also threw in a few other comments just for effect, such has his talking about how The Watch wanted to \u201cMake Germany great again.\u201d I am subtle.<br /> <br /> There was also talk of \u201cReds\u201d and \u201cWhites\u201d when the Russians came up, Wolfram noting his Russian friends were \u201cWhites\u201d for example\u2026which is sort of an oversimplification with Tatiana, but good enough in a binary conversation.<br /> <br /> And volchonok, being a spirit, got to play with everyone in the Hedge! Who is a good volchonok?<br /> <br /> Okay, this leads into the next session, where we meet more of the players and this rather interesting plan is put into action. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:19:34-07:00","id":911510,"title":"","content":"Back to Berlin! This time the Conspiracy gets moving on dealing with the immediate problem with the Black Company and Watch even as they start investigating the Changeling and Vampire plotlines. We meet the local Circle of the Crone, Queen Skadi, and Queen Woebegone. <br /> <br /> Also a short fic for Wolfram, covering where he was at the start of the session.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXX<br /> </i><br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> Today was a fairly eventful day. We started out with Lizette flying Alla, Tatiana and myself to Krakow to meet up with the train that the Russians are on. We adjusted the plan so Alla would be the one taking pictures. Tatiana still met up with Ruskov and chatted with him briefly at the station. I\u2019m not sure what they talked about but it appeared to be amicable enough, or so I was told. While the ladies were setting up the shot and getting the photograph I snuck into the baggage carriage and planted the silver bullets that Lizette had made in the appropriate luggage. It took me a little bit to find the right bags. They are cleverly disguised, but I found them in the end. We used the most common type of ammunition that we had for this plan and were lucky to find that the rounds we planted would work with the guns I found. I quickly made my way off the baggage car and left. I met up with the others a short while later. We flew back to Germany a little while after that.<br /> <br /> After we had gotten back to Berlin and we had the photograph developed Dacian used his superb disguise skills to make me look like a completely different man. I wouldn\u2019t have recognized myself if I hadn\u2019t been in on the whole thing from the start. Once that was done I took the photograph and a note and located some wolf-blooded that we were assured were connected to Ilsa and her pack. The meeting was quick and uneventful. They accepted that I had important information for Ilsa and let me go on my way. I was pleased with how well that went. And I will not have to worry about hiding my face around Berlin since they will not be able to recognize me as I normally am. Ilsa and her pack did not see me the last time we engaged them since I was sniping from the Cathedral roof. Tatiana unfortunately does not have the luxury of being unrecognizable. Unfortunate but unchangeable. I would not have changed her role in the fight from several months ago if I could. She was essential to taking out the spirits.<br /> <br /> After night fell is when a majority of our dealings happened. I went with Alla and Tatiana to go meet with the local head of the Circle of the Crone group. Tatiana and I accompanied Alla as her escorts. I think she likes the idea of having two werewolf bodyguards when she meets with important people. I will admit that I wanted to make sure Alla stayed safe. This town is not friendly towards the Invictus group, of which my pack mate is a member. We met a woman while we waited named Durga. She seemed to be a little less than completely sane. She was going on about coming to Germany to investigate and dissect examples of the strong genetic stock that was supposed to be here. I\u2019m not sure exactly who she means, but I was under the impression that killing humans was a no-no when it came to Kindred politics. It might draw too much attention. I suppose that she was there asking permission to do her experiments. Her meeting was short. I wonder if she was approved or denied.<br /> <br /> So, we met with a woman named K\u00e1ra, she is the head of the Circle of the Crone. She offered protection to Alla and Marissa while they are in the city. She warned my pack mate to be careful while in Berlin. There is unrest in the city and different groups of Kindred are \u201cbecoming irksome\u201d according to K\u00e1ra. In particular the group known as the Order Dracul. Related to Dracula perhaps? The main purpose for this meeting came up then. Alla was to give K\u00e1ra a list of requests from Connie. K\u00e1ra read over the letter and said that she would do what she could. <br /> <br /> While Alla, Tatiana and I were dealing with Vampires, Wolfram was in the Rhineland visiting his brother, and Dacian, Dearbhail and Lizette were dealing with Fae matters. They had been summoned to a meeting with Skadi, so they all went. Skadi is currently in charge of the Winter court and essentially in charge of the Summer court, while someone called Woebegone is in charge of the Autumn court and Sascha is in charge of the Spring court. Skadi\u2019s concern is that Woebegone and Sascha are working together and are possibly lovers. She is convinced that if those two have their way then the intentional or unintentional result could be a rise in violence in the city. It seems to boil down to the fact that while the Winter court is in charge right now, or at least holding most of the power, they control the sorrow in the city. I\u2019m not sure how it all works but the Fae can feed off of emotions. The Winter court controls sorrow and they are making sure that the people in the city remember the pain and heartache of the Great War and have no desire to do start fighting again. Woebegone controls the Autumn court which manipulates fear. She seems to want to keep the people afraid. This could cause problems down the line if the people of Berlin start to fear for their lives and retaliate against those that they are afraid of. Sascha controls the Spring court, which is all about desires. He is currently rather interested in a new kind of show called a cabaret. His possible paramour is really very interested in making horror films. Nosferatu did so well that she wants to create more. Skadi kind of glossed over what appears to be their main objectives and insists that if fear and desire were to become too strong in the city then people might decide that they want to fight back against those that beat them down. She has even gone so far as to cull, her words, any new possible Summer courtiers that seem to be exhibiting their standard trait, anger. Or at least particularly Nationalistic anger. Personally the whole thing sounds like a nightmare to me. I do not know if the Spring and Autumn courts rising in power will really have that substantial an impact on the city, but Skadi is convinced of it.<br /> <br /> Skadi also mentioned the Watch as a supernatural group in the city. Dacian suggested that Skadi should meet with the Black Company and have them come to an agreement so they would be allies. That way they might be able to channel the wrath and desire into activities other than revenge or violence. There is also Skadi\u2019s concern that Queen Woebegone is actually a Gentry, which I\u2019ve come to understand is one of the beings that kidnaps people in the first place and rules their own realm in the Fae lands. She is rather powerful and it\u2019s been said that she can warp the world around her when she\u2019s angry.<br /> <br /> After all of that was done we met up and compared notes. We decided to split into different groups and go out to speak with more people, observe transactions or to just let off steam. Wolfram went to the train station to see how the trade went off. He got there in advance of the other Claimed and hid himself. Five men showed up, all of them lightly armed. One man used a gift to be able to see what was happening in the southwest. The train arrived on time. Five Russians including Ruskov get off, all heavily armed. They planned on trading food stuffs and other such supplies for the weapons. Unfortunately for them a large group of individuals were heading toward the train station at a decent speed. Turns out that these eleven individuals were all wolfs running at a good clip. They arrived and a fight ensued. The Germans or Russians, not sure which, started shooting the werewolves after they had shifted to human or mostly human form. The gunfire only succeeded in annoying them and they kept coming. The werewolves fired back and quickly discovered that some of the combatants were Claimed. They quickly changed tactics from taking out the men to taking out the munitions. They did not seem surprised that some of the men were Claimed.<br /> <br /> In the end the Claimed were winning the fight but losing the objective. Once all of the weapons were destroyed the werewolves shifted to wolf form and ran off. The Claimed were all angry at what had transpired and suspected a possible leak. The Russians also suspected that someone had inside knowledge, but were not quite as angry as the Germans were. Wolfram stayed hidden until all parties had left the area before leaving himself.<br /> <br /> Alla and the Fae members of our pack went to go pay a visit to Queen Woebegone. Apparently the building had a playing card theme with doors shaped like the different suits, and much of it was in shadows with scary images projected on the walls. The whole place was designed to induce just a hint of fear in any visitors that come by. There was also a phrase written on the ceiling and walls that spelled out \u201cChildren always stray from the path.\u201d Alla was enjoying herself trying to figure out where the projections came from and how the effects were done. Being a show-woman she takes a great interest in such things. She was also interested in talking to Woebegone about horror films and films in general. They met with the Autumn court queen and talked to her about movies and specifically Kindred in film, and if it might be possible to find a way to allow Kindred to actually be captured on film. Woebegone said something about the masquerade when the idea was brought up, but Alla seemed interested and said that she would talk to those in charge in the city and see if some experimentation might be allowed. Apparently during the entire visit Woebegone\u2019s figure flickered frequently. I\u2019m not sure if that is just how her Fae nature presents itself or if that is an indication that she might be a Gentry. I\u2019m assuming the former, but will not rule out the latter.<br /> <br /> While all of this was going on Marissa, Tatiana and I were going out to pick a fight. Well, Marissa had promised Tatiana a fight earlier so she was living up to her end of the bargain. I went along just in case someone decided to play dirty. Plus, I enjoy fighting. Just not as much as my pack mate. So, we went to a neighborhood that is known to really dislike homosexuals, and Tatiana and Marissa proceeded to hold hands and act like a mated pair. It brought about the desired result and a group of gay-hating individuals came out and harassed the ladies. Three of the men attacked Tatiana, while one of them went after Marissa. I decided to even up the odds just a bit and tapped one of the men accosting Tatiana on the shoulder before punching him in the face. A fight ensued. Tatiana had fun. She knocked out the two men attacking her while Marissa and I each handled our guys. I will admit that the fight was fun. It\u2019s been awhile since I was in a regular street brawl. <br /> <br /> Overall I think that we\u2019re going to be in Berlin for a while. There are numerous things that we have uncovered and from what I can tell we have just scratched the surface of all of them. I have a feeling that things are going to get a lot more complicated before it\u2019s over. Fortunately, my pack seems to thrive on \u201ccomplicated.\u201d <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I got in a fight.<br /> <br /> It is not my fault you got bored and wandered off.<br /> <br /> I do not know what you are talking about. How is it boring to look at someone so beautiful?<br /> <br /> No, not the crazy woman.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we will make sure she doesn\u2019t dissect Wolfram, even though he is German. Just because Alla is afraid to fight her doesn\u2019t mean I am.<br /> <br /> Oh, I don\u2019t remember what they talked about. It was friendly though. I was too busy looking at her eyes.<br /> <br /> Be still, volchonok. Do not push me about Elena. I mean it. <br /> <br /> Of course you want to hear about the fight. And change the subject.<br /> <br /> It was Marissa\u2019s idea - she did promise me a fight.<br /> <br /> We behaved as mates on a street she knew.<br /> <br /> Not like that!<br /> <br /> Nuzzling and such. She smells very nice.<br /> <br /> Because some humans are foolish and do not care for mates that cannot have pups.<br /> <br /> Bah. I do not know, volchonok, why foolish humans are foolish. I just know that when one offers me violence, I return it. They were certainly not expecting it - the look on their face was glorious.<br /> <br /> No, Alla did not fight. She went off with the fairies. <br /> <br /> To meet the movie Queen.<br /> <br /> No, they already met Skadi, while we met with the beautiful vampire.<br /> <br /> Something about anger being dangerous, and the sad Queen being more dangerous.<br /> <br /> I did too, volchonok, but... I think the name was Woebegone? That sounds sad.<br /> <br /> Mostly she wishes to stop another war, by killing the ones who are angry enough to fight.<br /> <br /> If Dacian wishes to fight them, I will fight them. I like Skadi, I will fight for her. But it is the fairies\u2019 decision.<br /> <br /> So what were you doing volchonok, if you were not following Dearbh\u00e1il?<br /> <br /> What?!<br /> <br /> Volchonok, he was spying on the Pure!<br /> <br /> It is dangerous for you, if they were to see you.<br /> <br /> And what would you have done? Nipped his Spirit?<br /> <br /> No, it does not work that way, and do not try it! If it did, his Spirit would hit you with his fire.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am angry at you!<br /> <br /> OK, no, I am not angry, volchonok. Just worried.<br /> <br /> Yes, you are OK. This is good.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, thank you for getting that last bit of blood off.<br /> <br /> So, what happened?<br /> <br /> Eleven Pure? That... well. I am glad you are OK.<br /> <br /> They were afraid of the Sin-Eaters?<br /> <br /> Ah, I can see that. Once they knew they were fighting people that would not truly die, losing any Uratha would be a true loss. Still, it is good to know that they know so much, and this is what they will do.<br /> <br /> So they destroyed all the weapons. Good enough, I suppose/<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, not good enough to run. Good enough for Wolfram\u2019s friend\u2019s purposes.<br /> <br /> No, my brave volchonok. We have done much, we two, this night. We will not run tonight. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 25th October 1922<br /> <br /> The operation in Berlin is proceeding. This morning Marek, Alla, Tatiana and I flew to Krakow to intercept the coming train with the members of Red October. Everything went smooth, Tatiana spoke to Commander Ruskov, Marek planted the silver bullets, (which I made, meaning I need to make more, because of course they had to use ones from the Thompson, good thing I remembered to remove them from the custom drums) and Alla got a clear photo. The trip took a few hours since I could not use the fighter plane, but it was worth it, and we set up everything for the evening. Besides, I like flying.<br /> <br /> I do need to work on the planes more. Talking to Dana the other day made me realize I have not been working on them much like I did when we moved to Paris. I can\u2019t work on weapons all the time, after all. Increasing passengers and comfort seem a good way to go for a direction to expand. Also, how to add more guns!<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> When we retuned, Dacian helped Marek get a disguise, and did quite an excellent job. Marek got the letter and false information to the Pure via one of the locations he knew of from the Paris Forsaken. Dacian seemed justifiably proud of his work, and Marek managed his delivery without issue.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was still visiting family, so we split into two groups to deal with immediate business. Alla (flanked by the Werewolves) went to visit the local Pagans (sigh) with Marissa Sangiovanni, while Dacian, Dearbh\u00e1il and myself went to talk to Queen Skadi. I am given to understand Alla\u2019s trip went well, though Marissa was sassy.<br /> <br /> The visit with Queen Skadi went as well as could be expected, I guess. She had a whole lot of wind about how Prince Sascha and Queen Woebegone were taking Germany in a dangerous direction. She is, of course, the only one that has all the answers. The specifics were she has killed emerging Summer Courtiers who have appeared with a feeling of wrath from the Hedge (she put it as \u201cdeath to France on their lips\u201d) while Queen Woebegone and Prince Sascha are protecting them. She implied Sascha was Woebegone\u2019s boy toy, and that her sorrow was keeping the fires of wrath still in Germany. She even referenced Die Wacht once.<br /> <br /> I challenged her, noting she secured alliances with Paris\u2019s Spring and Autumn Court that would prevent cooperation with Queen Woebegone or Prince Sascha. I noted she feared Queen Woebegone, perhaps so much that traveled to Paris without telling anyone she would be gone, so the Autumn Queen would not move against her. I also found that she feared Queen Woebegone might be of the Gentry. I brought all this out, as if she was bringing us in to work against someone who might be Gentry, she should say so. She, for her part, said it was a very unconfirmed suspicion, and that accusing the High Queen of Berlin of being Gentry would be\u2026a dangerous move. Which was true.<br /> <br /> Queen Skadi no doubt believed I was siding with Queen Woebegone, and to a degree I am. But I do not like being jerked around by Nobility, Faerie or otherwise. This was a battle between two Queens, possibly with Prince Sascha as a full partner of one, perhaps not. But I have better things to do than be the go girl of some two-bit Noble who thinks she is better than me. However nice she looks. Still, I was civil, as there in \u201cIce Heart Castle\u201d I was hardly in a place to be sassing her.<br /> <br /> I spoke to the others as we got out. Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian were both troubled by Queen Skadi killing Summer Courtiers. Both also seemed to heed her fears about Queen Woebegone. Dacian felt introducing some of the fanatical Summer Courtiers to members of the Schwarze Reichswehr was a good idea. I think those full of wrath are the problems, like Willie fears, not the good ones, like Willie himself. Dearbh\u00e1il, being measured and intelligent, wanted to get an idea where Queen Woebegone and Prince Sascha stood first. It seemed fair. Queen Skadi had made a lot of requests but never quite told us exactly what to do, so for now we had some range.<br /> <br /> So we split into three groups this time for the evening. Marek and Tatiana went with Marissa to \u201cget in a fight\u201d and from what I understood succeeded. Wolfram observed the meeting and battle between the Schwarze Reichswehr Krewe, the Red October Krewe, and the Pure. Both sides had around ten people. Once the Pure discovered they were fighting a mass of Fog Men, they changed tactics, rather than going for kills they fought more defensively, and destroyed both the weapons and Red October\u2019s supplies before retreating. Both sides took a beating, but neither had fatalities (mostly because they Pure focused more on destroying supplies than killing, and the lack of silver for the Sin-Eaters). It was a success, but not as much as if there were losses; ultimately, though, the supplies were destroyed and local Pure and Schwarze Reichswehr were angered with each other, and hopefully the Red October is less inclined to deliver munitions.<br /> <br /> Alla, Dacian and I went to meet with Queen Woebegone. Dearbh\u00e1il was tired and went to bed. The meeting went well. Woebegone was heavier on theatrics as it was Alla and Dacian\u2019s first visit to the Haus von Schaudert. Alla seemed impressed by the playing card themed rooms and hidden doors, and illusions throughout the place. Dacian just stayed near me. Alla was particularly happy when she noticed \u201cChildren Always Stray From the Path\u201d written hidden along the walls. Anyway, Rudolph admitted us entrance after a bit, and the meeting with Queen Woebegone began.<br /> <br /> Dacian, wisely, elected not to discuss Queen Skadi\u2019s fears or theories, and simply spoke to Woebegone very politely. Alla seemed absolutely fascinated, and she and Woebegone discussed vampires and film, and Alla asked about Woebegone researching how to film vampires. Woebegone politely noted she felt vampires might have an issue with that (she did use their word, \u201cKindred\u201d for them). Woebegone did offer to work with Alla on it if Alla pledged she would shield Woebegone from any negative effects. Woebegone did discuss using ghost voices with film or even filming them, which sounded very interesting.<br /> <br /> I mean, an effective means of playing ghost voices could add new levels to the horror films she loves so much, and given their creepy powers could have weaponry potential as well. I mean imagine a gun that fires a Banshee scream? An excellent assault deterrent device. I wonder if something that could, say, solidify (Plasmidify?) ghost flames could work as a spectral flamethrower as it sort of translates the ghost flame to the world. I need to write this down and ask Wolfram. <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, Alla seemed very excited about the possibilities of working with Woebegone. Also Rudolph, since he is so tall and lanky. But then, Alla always reacts oddly to scary things, like those House Machten guys in Paris. Dacian was pretty quiet, but did not seem too upset.<br /> <br /> Okay, well, we have had some success. Need to contact Willie so we can see our next move there, and meet Prince Sascha I presume? Never met him. But now, bed for me. For tomorrow, mayhem!<br /> <br /> Hopefully.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Wolfram\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Duisburg <br /> 25th of October<br /> <br /> The office was familiar. The chair Wolfram sat in as he looked out the large window that dominated one wall was as old as he could remember. The furnishings were equally unchanged from his childhood. He looked away from the view of the factory below to the ancient desk of strong dark wood and to his brother sitting behind it scowling down at the papers before him before removing his glasses to pinch the bridge of his nose and sigh. Heinrich had taken over the running of the factory when their father's health had begun to fail but even now with the elder von Klingemann years in his grave his office remained unchanged. Heinrich had not claimed this space so much as it had claimed him. <br /> <br /> \u201cI wasn't expecting it to be so quiet today,\u201d Wolfram said with a glance at the mostly still and darkened floor out the room's sole window.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe farmers can hardly afford seed and stock,\u201d Heinrich replied as he leaned back, \u201cLet alone new tractors. We're getting by making parts for repair and there are orders still, mostly foreign. It's not easy to keep all of the men working and rather than let some go I've had to cut back on the hours.\u201d He shook his head. \u201cSorry, I wish I'd known you were coming, I would have met you at the station. It is not as if I don't have time right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a bit spur of the moment on my part. I found myself at a lull in the business that brought me to Berlin and wanted to see you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou saw how things are there and decided you were worried about me and wanted to drop in unexpectedly to see if it was as bad here without giving me time to hide how grim it is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. Is it not an older brother's prerogative to worry?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough I suppose. But I think there may also be some guilt in there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram leaned back in his chair and shrugged. \u201cWhen we were younger I did sometimes feel jealous of how tightly knit you and father were. Now I wonder if it was I that was fortunate. I was free to chase my books and my scholarly pursuits.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich smiled then, wanly but genuine. \u201cYou would never have been happy sitting here. I think we all knew that. And as heavy as it can weigh on me at times, especially lately, there is no place I would rather be. We both carry on his legacy brother, just different parts of it. And speaking of which, how is your wife?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram's face brightened at the mention of Christina and he sighed wistfully. \u201cVery much with child,\u201d he chuckled, \u201cAnd all the more radiant for it, despite what she might think. You will be an uncle quite soon. Alas, but she's not well suited to travel right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich nodded. \u201cShe makes you happy. I am glad for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I do try to make her happy as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course you do. Love brings out the best in you I'd say. So what has pulled you away from her side and drug you to Berlin? It is the weary centerpiece of a tired and angry land, I cannot fathom you choosing it over such domestic bliss.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram's smile faded and he nodded. \u201cIt pains my heart to see the Fatherland so. Even the lights and the dancing is... desperate. There is much anger building here. Much more than I realized.\u201d<br /> <br /> His brother nodded. \u201cThere is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram looked out at the quiet lines below and then back. \u201cThere are others like myself. Those who fell in the war and rose again. They have banded together to continue to serve the interests of Germany and protect her people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like a noble enough purpose, but I am guessing from the way you speak that there is trouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey agree on their goal, but not on how to seek it. Or even on just what is in the best interests of the Fatherland. And there are others... angry souls who are lashing out at anyone who is not German. Agitating to strike at those who defeated us while they are still weak...\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich snorted. \u201cI have heard that talk well enough. They all speak as if we ourselves are not also struggling to rebuild.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe war is over. Victory was not ours and as bitter as it is we must accept that fact. It does nothing for what we have lost already to throw more lives upon the bonfire of war and hate. It is a fire that warms the blood but sears the soul. Its light only serves to blind us to the devastation we make to feed it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram sighed and then continued, \u201cA fellow Sin-Eater called me because there are some in the Black Company who agree with this madness and have been aiding those who strike out at the foreigners. His hands are tied, he cannot act against his fellows but he cannot allow such hate to go unchecked.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you can.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I can. My companions and I have taken the information he gave us and begun working to unravel the plans as best we are able. To weaken these misguided souls and to turn the various groups that seek to steer Germany into another war against each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYet you do not sound particularly pleased.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI worry my brother. There is so much pain. Such much suffering. So much fear and anger. And so little healing. There are those who would offer us a hand to get back to our feet out there, but these people bite at them like rabid dogs. Can we truly blame those who have been so attacked if they do not offer their help again, or even if they think of us as dangerous and mad? And it is not just here in the Fatherland that this madness festers. These men and their actions feed their counterparts in France and elsewhere to point and claim that there should be more hardships and more burdens and more reparations. That kindness is wasted upon us or worse yet that only by keeping us weak can they be safe from us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich nodded in silent agreement. \u201cYou're right, but what can you do? You are one man Wolfram. An extraordinary one perhaps, and blessed with strange and powerful allies, but you are still one man striving to hold back the tide. Perhaps you should return to your home when this business is done and stay there. You have a family to look after now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what of you? You are my family as well brother.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy place is here. This factory was our father's dream. These men and their families depend upon me. For good or ill I must stay and do what I can. But you should think of your wife and your child.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do. And that is why I cannot ignore this. Even if this is beyond me, I cannot, will not, let this tide of evil sweep us all into another war without fighting to give them the world they deserve.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey deserve a world with you there to care for them and protect them Wolfram.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is the Golden Eagle and as a Sin-Eater I have ways. No matter what happens I shall always return to them. I am risking nothing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomehow, I think you'd be fighting even if that wasn't the case.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf a man turns a blind eye to the evils of another, is he any less evil?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is not always so simple as that Wolfram.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is actually. Now, there is a difference between ignoring evil and knowing your own strength. This is why those of us who can face the greater evils are duty bound to do so but one must never allow the light to be diminished without outrage.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook his head. \u201cIt must either be very nice or very exhausting to be so certain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOften both, but I have no desire for a life without honor.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook is head again and rose from his seat, moving over and clapping a hand to his brother's shoulder. \u201cIt's a pity there are not more who feel as you do. But come, there is yet time to put this gloom aside and share a fine meal and speak of lighter things before your train back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram rose from the seat and nodded. \u201cYou should come to visit Chantilly some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce my niece or nephew has been born perhaps.\u201d He paused and then added softly, \u201cSo how has your handsome friend been?\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXX</i><br /> <br /> Not a lot of sex for a session XXX is it? Oh well. <br /> <br /> I should note there was a deliberate attempt from Marek\u2019s player to use Werewolf terminology. So he called the Sin-Eaters Claimed, referred to gifts, etc. But they were all Sin-Eaters, not Claimed. <br /> <br /> Alla went along heavily covered, her high Humanity and low Blood Potency making it possible, with hats with netting.<br /> <br /> The Woebegone scene involved her flickering in and out, even to reappear in mid new sentence. Also rising as if on a film reel. Doors that were not doors, that sort of thing. I was going for a very surrealist vibe with it. Rudolph, suited and impossibly tall and then, added an air of surreal menace, and predictably Alla loved it.<br /> <br /> Prince Sascha is the player we have not met yet, and I believe the next session we will hit the Cabarets of Berlin even as both the Prussian Pure and Black Company seek to discover how they were tricked. Who knows, we might even meet the Watch. Hopefully not. Ghastly people. Regardless, join us then, won\u2019t you? Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:29:36-07:00","id":913448,"title":"","content":"So, Berlin's Changeling courts are scary. Power games are a thing. &quot;Culling&quot; people is another.<br /> I was pleasantly suprised to see an entry by Wolfram.<br /> Can volchonok manifest or interract with people apart from Tatiana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:27:13-07:00","id":913690,"title":"","content":"I really wanted to get a journal out for him since this arc hits rather close to his heart. Also, he is the best person out of my characters so he deserves to be heard.<br /> <br /> volchonok was manifest in Hedge but is otherwise can't manifest as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:31:24-07:00","id":913716,"title":"","content":"Yea, it was part of my portrayal of Berlin as being in a desperate time. The next session focuses on the Cabarets, so it has a decidedly different tone.<br /> <br /> I am pretty sure volchonok can't manifest, so usually only Tatiana and Marek can interact with him.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the commentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:27:54-07:00","id":920173,"title":"","content":"The Conspiracy finally visits the infamous cabarets of Berlin. Here they meet the Spring King, and Faerie, Sin-Eaters, and beings even they are unsure of.<br /> <br /> Marek\u2019s player was busy and unable to work on that journal this time. Lizette will give you a fairly complete picture of what happened, with comments from Tatiana and Wolfram. Note Wolfram\u2019s story takes place at the end of the session. Enjoy<br /> <br /> Update: Got Marek in just under the wire!<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek's Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 October, 1922<br /> <br /> Well, today proved to be an interesting day. It started with Lizette working on a new weapon. Something akin to a crossbow, but instead of firing bolts it will fire the equivalent of saw blades. It is of course an interesting device. I\u2019m not sure how practical it will be to use, but it will definitely provide the ability to do massive damage to enemy combatants. Especially if she perfects her idea of setting it up so it lights the saw blades on fire upon release. I\u2019m not sure what it is with Lizette and fire, but the two are inexorably linked.<br /> <br /> During this conversation we found out that Fenric does not know how to fire a gun. Well, Lizette offered to teach him how to shoot using her Thompson. I argued that it might be better to start with something smaller, like a pistol, before he works up to a machine gun. Lizette argued that a machine gun was more effective since you didn\u2019t really have to aim it, you just point it in the general direction of the enemy and fire. While that may be true, a machine gun is something that you should have to work your way up to using. Getting used to the recoil on a pistol will help, not to mention he should be taught gun safety before any shooting actually happens. Tatiana was also against the idea of starting out with a machine gun, but didn\u2019t stick around long to argue the point. I don\u2019t think she wanted to get in the middle of all of that.<br /> <br /> Wolfram came outside around that point and after hearing what we were discussing, took my side about showing Fenric how to fire a pistol first. Wolfram brought up the gun safety idea as well, which was a good thing. I think Lizette got a little frustrated with us. She espoused the idea of starting with the gun that doesn\u2019t take fine aim to work effectively. I can see that not needing to aim would be a good thing, but from my perspective it is important to know exactly how guns work and how to fire one responsibly. Guns were created with one purpose in mind, and that is to kill. They kill animals and humans with great efficiency. They should not be thought of as toys or seen like a simple tool. They are far too dangerous for that mindset. Not that I think Lizette sees guns as toys, but she is rather more blas\u00e9 about their use than I am. Granted I am a sniper by trade, so I do specialize in hitting individual targets with accuracy and am very careful about who and what I hit. <br /> Eventually Lizette realized that we weren\u2019t going to have Fenric start his firearms training with a Thompson, and she lent him her pistol. I let Wolfram go through the safety issues first and we\u2019ll start on actual target practice later.<br /> <br /> So, while we were doing all that Dearbhail was researching the different Cabaret\u2019s in town to see which one(s) we should go to. She also spent some time shopping for German style clothing so she doesn\u2019t stand out as being from Paris when we go out later. Thankfully men\u2019s cloths look much the same no matter where you go, so I just wore my usual button up shirt and slacks. They are neutral colors and don\u2019t stand out all that much.<br /> <br /> After Dearbhail came back with her information and the sun has sufficiently set we decided to go out to one or two of these Cabaret\u2019s. The first one that we went to was called \u201cThe Hedge Maze.\u201d Needless to say it was run by people like my fae companions. It was also the place to be if you want to meet the Spring Court leader Prince Sascha. So we went to this club. It was fine as far as clubs go. My fae friends were greeted by a woman named Oneida, who is the bodyguard of Prince Sascha. She would not let the others meet with her Prince until they had taken a vow that they would not do him any harm. Apparently a day or two ago there was an attempt on his life by one of the Bound, as they called him. I would have called the man one of the Claimed. He was like Wolfram, a \u201cSin-Eater.\u201d He came to the club and pulled an oriental style sword out of this chest, like Wolfram can do, and proceeded to attack Sascha. Oneida was not overly forthcoming on the details, but apparently the Claimed man was driven off and the fae Prince saved. He made it out with no visible injuries. Or if he was hurt they used their fae magicks to heal him, like I have seen Dearbhail do in the past. It is a very useful ability.<br /> <br /> Once Dearbhail heard that it was a Claimed that attacked the Prince she left and went back with Wolfram in tow. I think she wanted his perspective on the events of that night, or so he could confirm whether or not it was a Claimed man. They did not know to which group of Claimed the man belonged to, but Oneida is under the impression that Skadi had something to do with it. I am not sure if Skadi would actually try and eliminate a fellow monarch or not. She has been \u201cculling\u201d possible Summer Courtiers that are particularly angry about the political state of affairs in Germany, so she might turn her attentions on Sascha, but I don\u2019t really know her well enough to make an informed guess about that.<br /> <br /> After that we went to the club called \u201cSaints and Sinners.\u201d The owner of the club is a wolf-blooded man named Herr Holbien. In his employ he has a Claimed woman named Sabine. Wolfram talked to her a couple of times over the course of the night. Apparently she is rather protective of the other dancers and will defend them if needs be. She also has an interest in bladed weapons and was carrying a couple on her when they met. Her act also included knife throwing. I do not know if she has a knife throwing act on stage to explain why she carries blades around with her, or if it was a happy coincidence. Either way, it worked out well for her. Sabine also said that members of The Watch frequent the club in order to cause trouble. There are also a few \u201cforeign\u201d neighborhoods that they go to on a regular basis to also cause similar problems. It does not take much to imagine what kinds of trouble they get involved in when they go to the club or those neighborhoods.<br /> <br /> In the course of our visit we saw the headliner for this club. It is a woman named Della. She sang a rather haunting song about killing anyone in the army remotely connected to the death of her lover. This reminded me of the situation with Th\u00e9r\u00e8se. She was rather adamant about killing the one responsible for the death of her lover. I don\u2019t think she went through as many people to find the one that did it, but the similarity was there all the same. <br /> <br /> So, Dacian used a power to evaluate whether or not Della was supernatural or not. Apparently she is. We do not know what kind of supernatural being she is though. She is not a fae, we would have all seen that. She is not Uratha, Tatiana and I would have known that. And she is not dead, so she is not a Claimed or a Vampire. She may be one of those creatures like Iris, or she could be a magic user. We don\u2019t know for sure. I do not know if this will be a mystery that we will be able to unravel or not. I will make sure to keep an eye out for her though, to be on the safe side.<br /> <br /> Overall it was an interesting experience. We learned more about what The Watch is up to, and about another supernatural being in town. We found out that a Claimed tried to kill the Spring Court monarch, and that at least some people believe that Skadi was involved in that incident. We also saw several \u201cinteresting\u201d acts at the clubs. There was knife throwing and cross-dressing and a lot of groping for breasts. I think the others enjoyed that bit more than I did, but I will admit that it was entertaining to watch. Not just the acts but people\u2019s reactions to the acts. Some people openly enjoyed them. Others were more discrete in showing their interest, and still others probably shouldn\u2019t have come at all given their reactions to the acts.<br /> <br /> We left the clubs pretty late and headed back to the house. When we got back we saw Greta leaving just as we were arriving. She seemed rather pale to me and I was about to inquire into her health, but then I remembered that Marissa was at the house as well. Those two together is the likely cause for Greta\u2019s wan appearance. <br /> <br /> Greta did have some information for us though. She said that we could find the Communists at a place called the \u201cGold Sparrow.\u201d She also said that Willie had left us a message, that she may have \u201caccidentally\u201d steamed open when she was making a pot of coffee. The message simply said that the Black Company was descending upon the railyard to look for clues to what happened there. It was good to know, but not something that we could actively do anything about then. It was late and if we showed up it would be obvious that we had something to do with the events that took place. It will be known soon enough that we are in town since we delivered that picture of Tatiana to Ilsa, but it may not be known what exactly we did that day. I can only hope that our involvement will go undiscovered. If it is revealed then Willie will be in trouble, and we will have enemies on two fronts looking for our blood.<br /> <br /> We are after all strangers in a potentially hostile place. Alla\u2019s affiliations make her more of a target from her own kind, as do me and Tatiana\u2019s. We are surrounded by the Pure, and as soon as they know that we are here, life will become difficult for us. Alla is thankfully protected by the Circle of the Crone, but Tatiana and I have no such protection. Not that my fiery companion would ever ask for protection. She is far too interested in fighting her own battles to want someone else to do it for her. I just happen to think that we would be greatly outnumbered if things go badly for us. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I am going to bed.<br /> <br /> No, it is not because I was sent there like a small child.<br /> <br /> Because it is pleasant to be drunk and lie still on a comfortable bed.<br /> <br /> Because that is what you do at a cabaret. That and watch attractive woman throw knives and sing and dance and put on very amusing little plays.<br /> <br /> Yes, that place with the smoke and the many humans and many human noises was a cabaret, foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> I did not drink so much at the first one because our pack was separated and those away had made a promise that tied their hands.<br /> <br /> I did not think the fairy was a threat, no, but they were asked to make such a promise because of an attack by a Sin-Eater who pulled a sword from his chest, like our Wolfram can do.<br /> <br /> Because this Prince Sasha is a Jew and has sex with men and owns a club. He says. The other fairy, the pretty one, thinks it was Skadi.<br /> <br /> I do not know, noisy volchonok, that is for fairies to find out. I do not think Skadi works with Sin-Eaters though.<br /> <br /> Our Sin-Eater is very upset, yes. He does not like this Watch and what they do to his land.<br /> <br /> But it is true. The Pure and wrong and wrong-headed, but it is not the same. I do not think the Pure would kill someone because they slept with the same sex or because they were a Jew. One might because they were not a werewolf, but... just because the Wolf Blooded is likely to be kin to the Pure, it doesn\u2019t mean they will be friends to these Watch.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, the Cabalith of the second club was Wolf Blooded. Probably kin to Firetouched.<br /> <br /> Not that I could tell. There was the Sin-Eater with her knives...<br /> <br /> Yes, she was very pretty, do not interrupt me.<br /> <br /> Because I am stronger than you.<br /> <br /> Yes, foolish volchonok, even when I am drunk.<br /> <br /> You are wise to not make me show you. What were we talking about?<br /> <br /> Oh yes. There was also the singer Della, who Dacian says is magic.<br /> <br /> I suppose. Her song was foolish though.<br /> <br /> Soldiers die in war. It is those who start the war, the ones who make their petty decisions from so far away, not the one who fired the bullet, who are at fault. Such revenge foolishness is not well aimed.<br /> <br /> What? No, I am not afraid of her.<br /> <br /> No, I am not afraid of Lizette either.<br /> <br /> I did not run away! Bah, you make foolish noises volchonok.<br /> <br /> I did leave, yes. She was being foolish and I had no intention of being in our backyard as Lizette had Fenric fire a machine gun the first time he ever used a gun.<br /> <br /> I was already intending to. It is important to know all I can about our territory, how to get in and out and around.<br /> <br /> Like Greta did..? Oh yes. Probably Marissa let her in. I wonder...<br /> <br /> Oh? Oh, yes. I wonder if that\u2019s why Greta was so pale.<br /> <br /> Marissa letting her in.<br /> <br /> Bah, I am not foolish, you are foolish.<br /> <br /> I am talking sense.<br /> <br /> No, I will not stop talking foolishly and run. For one, I am not talking foolishly and for two, I am tired. We will run later, noisy volchonok. But now I sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 27th October, Morning<br /> <br /> Yesterday was wild. We went to two Cabarets and met cute charismatic guys and beautiful, deadly women. Tis almost enough to make me like Germany. Then Greta showed to remind me I don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> I began the morning working on a buzzaw bow, which I saw in a dream. After working on bows for Dacian, I got the idea of a crossbow base that fired round, serrated blades. It took longer to design than I expected, though building went quick. I even built an upgrade to light the saw when fired if it was covered with accelerant. I could saw arms or legs right off with this thing, making it a near perfect non-lethal weapon.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> However, some members of my group are just suspicious of progress, and bound to old-fashioned ideas about how to learn to use weapons. Even otherwise rather dashing members.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the problem began when I was trying out using one buzzaw bow in each hand. It was a bit much, so since the bow was sized for me not, say, Dacian, I offered Fenric the other one. I then discovered Fenric did not know how to shoot! Well, I saw a golden opportunity.<br /> <br /> See, in the 19th Century, people had to rely on target practice from even the start of their shooting career, be it hunting, skeet shooting or dummies. However, we were in the 20th Century now, and machine guns are far more effective. Also, easier to learn to use as a starter weapon. After all, one need only aim in the general direction of foes and spray the area to achieve maximum effectiveness. Advanced skills at targeting and hitting a single target with a single shot are useful, but less immediately important to the new shootist. After all, which is easier, aiming in the vague direction of a target or aiming for a weak point? You could give schoolchildren machineguns and they would be able to mow down a number of foes without training.<br /> <br /> However, many members of the Motley are mired in archaic practices. For example Marek, a sniper himself, seemed to feel that aiming for a target, the entire thing he has advanced skill in, is easier than simply spraying a few dozen bullets in the air. I cannot imagine how he came to this conclusion. It is utterly bizarre. Tatiana also argued and then quickly left, but she had seemed leery ever since I was firing flaming buzzsaws, so she probably feared my wrath. Not that I would shoot a Motley mate with a flaming buzzsaw, whether their limbs would grow back or not.<br /> <br /> The real disappointment was Wolfram, and I imagine this is one of the few times I will find myself writing that phrase. He also strongly felt that introducing Fenric to the modern firearm via a machinegun (particularly one so handy as the Thompson) was a bad idea. Yes, he too felt shooting one bullet at one target was somehow an easier start for Fenric than spraying an entire area with bullets. I cannot imagine what he is thinking.<br /> <br /> I figure in the future we will have weapons which can turn an area dark as nightfall by filling the area so full of bullets. Then people won\u2019t be teaching archaic technology like single shot pistols. No, we will be firing hundreds, possibly thousands in the air from a single weapon, possibly from a flying artillery platform.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, we eventually finished that up. I loaned Fenric my Star. Seemed the kindest thing to do, since his education was going the slowest way possible, and to show my magnanimity.<br /> <br /> That evening, we planned our evening out. Dearbh\u00e1il had looked into the Cabarets and found the most promising, including the residence of the Spring King, Prince Sascha. As the sun went down and Alla became more animated, we set out.<br /> <br /> I neglected to tell her I tried to improve her Ghoul\u2019s education. I am sure she would have appreciated it. Anyway.<br /> <br /> We wound up visiting two Cabarets. The first, <u>The Hedge Maze</u>, was a club run by Prince Sascha, the Spring King. Going in we met Oneida, a Fairest Shadowsoul who was the new Claviger, and she was intent on keeping us away from Prince Sascha until we had made an Oath not to harm him. He had been attacked by a Sin-Eater she presumed was sent by Queen Skadi. Dacian, Dearbh\u00e1il, Alla and I went back. He offered us drinks, and flirted heavily with Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian. Alla and I were apparently less his type. He downplayed the threat to himself, but my Witch\u2019s Intuition told me he was very afraid. Oneida was worried too, but it was more in line with her visible behavior. Dearbh\u00e1il went and got Wolfram when she heard the Fog Man had used a similar power to his, much to Oneida\u2019s irritation. I am not sure if Prince Sascha got anything useful from Wolfram, but he was added to Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian on his flirt list. In the end, the five of us had alcohol brought to us and three of us had the option to \u201cwalk him home\u201d for safety, but few answers.<br /> <br /> Prince Sascha is Jewish, Bisexual and influential in the club scene. It is small wonder Die Wacht dislike him. They may not even know he is faerie. He is also a Romancer and Dancer. I found him a fop, but a harmless one. Oneida was pretty, but so tired and driven to protect her king it was hard to learn much about her.<br /> <br /> Next we visited <u>Saints and Sinners</u>, a much larger club with a religious motif. I was not real crazy about that. It is run by a Herr Holbein, who is apparently not a Werewolf but kin to them. We never really got to talk to him, it was busy, and Tatiana and Marek did not seem to really have a consensus for how to deal with him anyway. <u>Saints and Sinners</u> was possibly twice as big as <u>The Hedge Maze</u>,, and more than twice as busy.<br /> <br /> Soon after arriving we met a Sin-Eater named Sabine who was rather suspicious of Wolfram. Listening to her conversations, it was clear she was a dancer, and took a protective view of the other dancers. Watching her, she wore tells that she was Sapphic, suggesting she was a member of Die Freundinnen though I don\u2019t think she ever confirmed that. She was a pleasure to see, dancing, walking, or catching and hurling knives, as her rather unusual show demonstrated. Her skill with knives was quite impressively displayed in her act, and I am pretty sure everyone, male or female, was impressed, and a little bit in love. Apparently she died of suffocation. I don\u2019t even want to think about the implications of that\u2026<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the acts were entertaining. There was one with a \u201cguy\u201d (clearly a woman, and not even a butch one) and \u201chis\u201d wife, where she got her head stuck and he tried to get her out, accidentally undressing her at one point and taking advantage of the situation a bit. The next act had a \u201cguy\u201d and girl where the \u201cguy\u201d had her look at the sun with binoculars, which had her blinded and feeling all the way around and, shockingly, groping several women\u2019s breasts. It was rather lowbrow and juvenile, and I had seen the latter interpreted in Paris, but reasonably entertaining.<br /> <br /> The act that really caught my attention, though, was a chanteuse named Della with a smokey voice and bedroom eyes, who sauntered onstage and sang a tale of revenge that began as a sad song but was a long, lurid ballad of seduction and murder, with her pulling the hearts out of men responsible for her lover\u2019s death in the war. Despite their bloody ends, one could almost envy them as the bourbon-voiced siren sang of how she seduced them to their ends. I found myself utterly distracted by her performance, not even thinking about my steel hardening process. I felt like I was coming out of a trance when she sashayed off stage, and the others agreed she was supernatural, if not what her deal was. I am sure finding out will be intriguing.<br /> <br /> Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il did not care to \u201cguard\u201d Prince Sascha, and of course Wolfram didn\u2019t, so we went back to the house. We met a slightly disheveled and very pale Greta Hess leaving. I suppose Apparently she and Marissa Sangiovanni had made up. Intensely, from the look of it. Anyway, her obvious sexual exploits were not what she brought up, but that Willie had contacted Wolfram. She had read the letter of course, making a half assed excuse. Willie was warning us that Schwarze Reichswehr was looking heavily into what happened. Wolfram had warned him he might be looked into. Wolfram elected to not chastise Greta for breaking into our house, reading our mail and sleeping with our housemate, but to let her go staggering back to her car.<br /> <br /> By that point, I was tired, with beautiful singers and dancers roaming in my head and not imagining what gross stuff that child had been up to. Then I slept, and dreamed of a tank that could grow airplane wings and fly around shooting rockets.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Now tis my Birthday. We will see if anyone remembers.<br /> <br /> Birthday Mayhem?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wolfram\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Berlin<br /> 26th of October<br /> <br /> Wolfram lifted a glass of wine from the tidy desk before him and sipped it as he held the phone to his ear and waited. The study around him was well ordered but it was all new and lacked the charm and familiarity that only time spent living in a space could give it. A fire crackled, freshly stoked and flickering brightly as it cast dancing shadows about the otherwise dark room. From behind him, Wolfram could feel the heat of the Firebrand Templar standing vigilant and ready for battle. More than ready, eager. Conflict was what kindled and fed his Geist's fiery spirit after all and there was no shortage of conflict brewing in the city around them.<br /> <br /> But before his thoughts could follow that trail further his wife's voice came to his ear and his lips curled up at the corners automatically in response. \u201cSorry to keep you waiting darling, I was resting and it takes so long for me to do anything these days.\u201d<br /> <br /> He closed his eyes and let the smile claim more of his lips. \u201cI wish this business had not called me away from your side, Christina.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is important. You're needed there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are important,\u201d he countered, \u201cBut yes, there is much that needs to be done here. So very much.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs it not going well? Is everyone alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon't fret my love. Everyone is fine. Things are going as well as could be hoped. Our initial efforts proved successful and we're considering how best to proceed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou sound troubled dearheart. What's the matter?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing...\u201d Wolfram stopped and shook his head slightly. \u201cWe are dealing with the Watch very cautiously, I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAll of you?\u201d There was a hint of concern and doubt in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cAll of us love,\u201d Wolfram assured her, \u201cEven Tatiana and Lizette. We spent the evening meeting with one of the fay monarchs at his cabaret and investigating another larger and more prominent one where I met a member of one of the other Krewes here. We are being careful and not rushing into anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI've heard some things about those cabarets...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was all a bit risque to be honest. But the others seemed to enjoy it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe others you say.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe performers were talented but my heart has found it's home with you my love.\u201d There was a pause as Wolfram took a slow breath. \u201cBesides which, there is so much that needs to be done. Too much to be distracted.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, is it really as bad as we've heard?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram's lips drew into a thin line as he considered his answer. \u201cWorse,\u201d he admitted honestly, \u201cOr perhaps it is simply that it has to be seen to truly be understood.\u201d His voice trailed off and there was a long silence before he shook his head and spoke again. \u201cBut please, let us speak of something brighter. Is everything ready for tomorrow night?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt will be. The servants have set up tables in the west green and I have enlisted several men from the village to bring lumber and tomorrow they'll be setting up the bonfire. I do believe they are convinced that I am mad to insist on such a large one but one of the advantages of my condition is that I am allowed such flights of whimsy without question.\u201d As she continued to speak of the other details involving the food and drink and music Wolfram listened to Christina\u2019s voice and felt himself relaxing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you so much.\u201d<br /> <br /> Christina\u2019s ongoing recount halted mid-sentence. \u201cI love you too. Are you sure you're all right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will be,\u201d he answered softly, \u201cI just miss you. It's good to hear your voice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes it is. I worry about you. I know the Eagle won't let you or Lizette come to permanent harm but still...\u201d Her voice trailed off.<br /> <br /> \u201cI will always return to you my love. Always.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t have Lords of Summer, a Claviger is essentially a guardian for the Spring Court. Sabine would be one of the Silent; she is \u201cplayed by\u201d Dita Von Teese while Price Sascha is \u201cplayed by\u201d Alan Cumming. I don\u2019t use many celebrities, but happened to with those two.<br /> <br /> So much tension. But I also tried to play up the sort of desperate frivolity this time. Less of the \u201ctimes are tough\u201d sort of talk, though their was some, more beautiful women, handsome men, and music. I wanted the Cabarets to feel unreal, and they did.<br /> <br /> The shows Lizette described are from particularly lowbrow acts that played in Cabarets, or so the Internet tells me. The players seemed terribly amused, though Tatiana\u2019s player points out Tatiana was far more amused than they were.<br /> <br /> Okay most of the major players have been met. Time to get a little more adventure.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-24-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:09:18-07:00","id":920520,"title":"","content":"We got a Marek after all! Added to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T23:27:19-07:00","id":927980,"title":"","content":"Today we have a birthday, a battle, and a revelation. Not quite in that order. This session covers two days.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXII<br /> </i><br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 27 October 1922<br /> <br /> Today was Lizette\u2019s 22nd birthday. We started the day like any other. Wolfram and I started Fenric with his gun safety and shooting lessons in the back yard. He is doing pretty well for a novice shooter, I will give him that. He just needs to work on the correct positioning of his arms. He needs to make sure that they are in the correct position to be able to absorb the recoil from the gun. He tends to bend his arms a bit too much and the angle of his elbow is too shallow. It must be wider to create the right shape to absorb the shock. He will get it though. I do not doubt his resolve to learn this new skill.<br /> <br /> Tonight we all planned on \u201cluring\u201d Lizette to the chateau. Most of us went back via the gate in the basement earlier and left Wolfram to get Lizette to come through. I think he just said something about needing to come back to the house and Lizette offered to come with him. He accepted and we surprised her as she stepped through the gate. While we were in Germany, Christina was busy having a bonfire set up in the backyard. There were also fireworks. Overall It was a relaxing night. I think Lizette enjoyed herself I know she definitely enjoyed the present that Fenric and Alla got her. It was a lighter shaped like a gun. So appropriate for our fae pyromaniac.<br /> <br /> <br /> 28 October 1922<br /> <br /> Today started off with Oneida sending a message to us saying that she wants to meet with us to discuss the Claimed problem that they had. One of the Claimed specifically went after Prince Sascha and Oneida is still concerned for her monarch\u2019s safety. They did not succeed in taking out their target and she was worried that they may try and finish the job. So, we all met at an outside caf\u00e9 for lunch so we could discuss our issues in public. We did have a couple people watching us. The unsurprising one was a man in Woebegone\u2019s employ. He was hard to miss at seven feet tall and bald. He kept a respectful distance and Oneida said that Woebegone likely sent him to act as security for Oneida herself. Seems likely. The second watcher was not someone that we were expecting. It was William Forsythe from the train. Back then he had wanted help in spying on the demon woman while we were on that trip. It seems that we have made a lasting impression on several people due to our actions on that damned train. Dacian saw the demon man that could turn into bees outside the post office a little while back, and now we have William spying on us in Germany as well.<br /> <br /> Oneida\u2019s main concern was that the men who\u2019d attacked Sascha the first time were in the club last night. She was afraid that they were going to try something else tonight and wanted to ask for our help. We readily agreed and proceeded to make plans on who would be where and when we would arrive. We figured that if Dacian and I arrived early we could take positions up in the rafters where we could both snipe from. Dacian was going to bring his bow and arrow and I my sniper rifle. The idea was also for Tatiana to communicate with the doorman to let him know who was unacceptable to come into the club, and that would be Pure and wolf-blooded. They would be able to sense that we were there and it could blow the whole thing. Greta was even called by Tatiana to see if she wanted to join us to at least take pictures. Alla would be in the crowd and be ready to use on of her gifts to compel all the guests to leave the club once the violence started. The others did not want there to be more collateral damage than there had to be. I was not keen on drawing too much attention to ourselves, since we do not know who the police are allied with in this town. That should be something that we look into in the future. We have a house here now and it would do well to identify any possible allies or enemies.<br /> <br /> We also talked about the problem with killing those that are Claimed in the way that Wolfram is. If he were to die, if he hadn\u2019t been connected to the Golden Eagle, he would eventually come back but someone else nearby would lose their life to provide him with a new one. It is a payment that the Claimed must make to come back from the dead. A stranger dies in their place. We discussed ways that we might incapacitate the Claimed so that there would be no random people dying due to a Claimed man dying. I personally did not have any problem killing the Claimed, but it would be beneficial if we could get them to run away, as was our plan. That way we wouldn\u2019t have to deal with bodies.<br /> <br /> While we were discussing our plans Sabine stopped at the table to talk to Wolfram. She complimented his choice in company, but then proceeded to be exceeding rude to Oneida. Turns out that the two are estranged sisters. Sabine blames Oneida for her death (and resurrection) and the death of her lover. As it turns out Sabine and her lover were planning on getting married. Her lover convincingly passed herself off as a man so Sabine\u2019s father would bless the marriage. The disguise was very good, but unfortunately did not fool Oneida\u2019s fetch, who ratted the couple out to their father. The father got upset and locked Sabine up in a steamer trunk and killed her lover. Sabine unfortunately suffocated while she was in the trunk.<br /> <br /> Apparently when people are taken to the Fae lands, Arcadia, a duplicate is left in their place. This duplicate is called a Fetch. The duplicate does not always act like the original would and unfortunate things can happen. I do not know if my Fae friends have Fetch\u2019s or not. I know that Lizette\u2019s village was bombed off the map. Her fetch died with her family. The others I\u2019m not sure of. I do know that Dearbhail has had to take care that her identity cannot be traced back to her actual family. That makes me think that her duplicate is still there. Not sure about Dacian\u2019s duplicate.<br /> <br /> So, the sisters made it known that they do not get along. I believe that Oneida tried to explain what had happened, that it wasn\u2019t her, but it sounds like Sabine was too upset to really listen and so she is still angry at her \u201cbetrayer.\u201d The sister\u2019s estrangement does not directly affect us, but may cause trouble down the line if we\u2019re not too careful. I do not know how Sabine will take it if we associate overly much with Oneida. I do not think that Oneida will get too upset if we keep company with her sister though. It is an awkward situation all around. I would prefer not to get involved in it at all, but I have a feeling that others in my pack will feel otherwise.<br /> <br /> The rest of this evening was both satisfying and extremely painful. We arrived at the club at 4:30pm and got into position. Two hours after the club opened Rudolph, the very tall gentleman that works for Woebegone, came in and told Lizette that there was a group of armed men waiting outside the club. Their description matched that of the original attackers. So, our plans changed. Dacian and I snuck out onto the roof and took up positions up there. Dearbhail came up on the roof with us, planning to provide healing as needed and any other assistance she could from a distance. Lizette, Wolfram, Alla and Tatiana all went outside to deal with the men on the ground. They managed to surround the group in a pincer move. I thought it was fairly well done. Also as they were heading out, as Lizette passed three parked cars they all started up, but stayed idling where they were. I assumed at the time that she had a plan in mind for them. I was right.<br /> <br /> I started things off by shooting one man in the eye, blinding him. I believe that Dearbhail used one of her Fae gifts to make that first shot easier than is would have been usually. Normally it is fairly hard to hit such a small target, but I had no trouble doing it tonight. Dacian shot one of them in the arm in an effort to keep them from firing upon us. It was a good plan, but those men had gifts that didn\u2019t require use of arms, just intention. While we sniped from above Alla attacked one of the men in front of her. I believe that he will well remember that hit. I have sparred with Alla and know that in a fight the nice and polite woman drops away and she becomes terrifying with her strength and ability. Unfortunately for her one of the Claimed realized the very real danger that he was in and immediately set Alla on fire. He could see that she was dead and knew what she was. From my understanding Kindred that go into a frenzy because of fire either go all out and attack their enemy or they flee. Luckily for her attacker, but bad for us, Alla ran. I did not blame her. Fire does worse damage to those of her kind that it does to me or the others, and it hurts us bad enough as it is.<br /> <br /> Then one of the Claimed used some sort of gift on Tatiana. I did not see a physical attack but suddenly she staggered and acted as if she had taken a substantial blow. I saw red and shot that man in the head for hurting my pack mate. He remained standing after the shot. The Claimed are very hard to kill and he was no exception. Then one of his fellows used a nasty gift on Tatiana to make her start bleeding from her eyes, nose, mouth, everywhere. It was not a pleasant sight. It was even less pleasant to experience. Another of the Claimed used that same gift on me. It felt like I was burning from the inside out. It hurt just about as much as getting shot in the chest with silver did, but I think the damage was more extensive. At least I kept bleeding for a little while after that. My natural healing replenished most of the blood I lost but it was starting to take its toll towards the end of the fight.<br /> <br /> Well, I wasn\u2019t going to let them get away what they had done so I aimed for my original target and fired. The man had no chance. For me the whole plan on leaving them alive left and all I could think about was putting down my target. I don\u2019t have a high regard for those that are not pack anyway, and even less of one for those who are actively hurting my pack mates. Needless to say, that man died.<br /> <br /> After getting hit a second time by the devastating gifts of the Claimed Tatiana shifted to Guaru form and started attacking another man. I believe he was engaged fighting with Lizette. At least she was bleeding everywhere like Tatiana and I were. There was more than one of the Claimed that could do that attack and I was determined to make sure they paid in kind. It seemed that Tatiana was of a like mind.<br /> <br /> Just after that a gift was used that I recognized as the one that you can use to spy on an area. I believe Wolfram called it Boneyard. It obviously wasn\u2019t one of the attackers since they were as surprised as I was that it went up. I am assuming that it was Greta who put it up. In the same instance a large wave of water came moving down the alley towards Alla and put out the flames that engulfed her. She seemed to pause a moment and regain control of herself. She acted like normal, but certainly didn\u2019t look like it.<br /> <br /> The fight was not going well for us. Most of us were significantly hurt. They were hurt as well, but seemed to be able to soak up damage and discharge white smoke like it was nothing. I am given to understand that there is a limit to how much damage that can be negated by the smoke, but it was substantial enough. I was getting ready to line up another shot when all of a sudden those three running cars came barreling forward into the group of Claimed. I think they decided that discretion was the better part of valor and decided to run. One man apologized out loud before raising his dead friend as a zombie so they could all flee. We left them an opening so they could leave and we let them. Mostly. I will admit that I was more than a little angry to see my pack mates in such a state. At least two of them had been hit by that horrendous gift and were bleeding quite freely. Tatiana was healing the smaller wounds but was still bleeding. Lizette was in much the same condition, though she does not have the natural healing of my kind. I should have let them run, but I was angry. It is rare that anger takes over my actions but this time it did. I fired a parting shot at one of the men in the back. It hit him and he stumbled. I paid for it though. I second later I was hit by a different gift and set ablaze. I just about fell to my knees in blinding pain. I had to shift to Guaru form to avoid dying from that last hit. I stayed in that form long enough to soak some of the damage and heal some of the lesser wounds. I do not think I would have survived if I had not shifted forms. <br /> <br /> I do not understand Lizette\u2019s fascination with fire. It hurts. A lot. Thankfully Dacian was there to help me put out the flames, and Dearbhail came over and helped stop my bleeding. I was reminded again how remarkable our Fae friend\u2019s gifts are. I was not in a good way before her ministrations, and wasn\u2019t too much better afterwards, but I was at least no longer bleeding out. I have come this close to death twice before and really do not feel like repeating the experience any time soon.<br /> <br /> I watched from the roof as Wolfram scooped Lizette out of the trunk of her car. Apparently she has a tendency to curl up somewhere safe and nurse her wounds when she is badly hurt. I wish she did not have the experience often enough for this to be a habit. But Wolfram carried her into the club through a back entrance, while Dacian and Dearbhail helped me get back into the club though the roof. We all met up with Sascha and he used the same gift that Dearbhail had to heal our wounds. He completely healed Tatiana, and was able to heal most of Lizette\u2019s and my wounds. I thanked the man for his help and looked around to make sure that my pack mates were alright. Everyone seemed okay. Wolfram was doting on Lizette a little more than usual, but I can\u2019t say that I was surprised. She had been badly hurt, and my German friend has feelings for our Fae inventor. I think he always has. Dearbhail was a little clingy with me, but I assured her that I was fine and that that the rest of my wounds would heal in time.<br /> <br /> Tonight was overall a success. We encouraged the Claimed men to run away and we kept Sascha from getting hurt. We fought a group of individuals who were definitely more prepared and capable of dealing out damage than we were, but we held our own and sent them running. That was satisfying. I\u2019m also assuming that Greta got some decent photographs of the incident. I will have to check with her later to see if she got what she wanted from the evenings events.<br /> <br /> Overall, I was not happy with my actions towards the end of the fight. I know that my pack is my weak point, but I was not expecting to get so angry that I\u2019d go against the plan we had in place. We were only supposed to incapacitate them, but I intentionally killed one because he had hurt my pack mates. Granted I had no qualms about some random person dying later, but my pack did and for them I was going to go along with the plan. But, my anger got the better of me. I do not regret what I did. I would likely do it again. I was just a bit surprised by how easily my emotions ruled my actions. It is not usually something that I have a problem with.<br /> <br /> We have definitely made our mark on this town. We will likely begin to see more of an interest in our presence here. It will not be a friendly interest from The Watch. I\u2019m not sure how the Black Company will take our actions. They may not have any problems with us dealing damage to their rivals. It is possible that they will see our actions as an intrusion in their city though. We have definitely disrupted the status quo. I wonder if the Pure in this city will be attracted to us due to our actions. There was no secret that two werewolves were involved in that fight, and it is likely that The Watch will talk about it. Some of the Pure or wolf-blooded may hear about it. In which case we should be cautious from here on out. Definitely no travelling alone regardless of the errand. <br /> <br /> I will have to offer an apology to the rest of the pack for deviating from the set plan that we had come up with. I will explain that I reacted in anger. It is not something that I usually have a problem with. I should have expected others to get hurt. I guess I just did not expect the amount or type of injuries that they were able to do with what looked like relative ease. I will not underestimate the Claimed again. I am sure that there will be future altercations with them. Unless they took tonight\u2019s meeting to be a warning that we can beat them. I wonder if they realized that there should have been more of them dead than just the one. Tatiana switched targets, as did I for the most part, in order to avoid killing some of them. If we had been aiming to kill them there would have been at least two more in that total. If I had not killed that one it would have been more obvious that we were holding back. My actions may have muddled the overall message. Perhaps they will understand it nonetheless. Hopefully they will at least leave Sascha alone. We are prepared for them, Prince Sascha is not. Time will tell. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Peace, volchonok, I am alright.<br /> <br /> I did not say unharmed, did I? But I stopped the bleeding, and the fairy Prince put my insides back in order. I will be fine in no time. Marek and Lizette are still hurt, you should fuss over them.<br /> <br /> Well it is very tiring to feel like you are carrying the world on your back. And Greta was not fussing over me.<br /> <br /> She hugged me once. You have licked me far more than once. <br /> <br /> No, volchonok, you are not to tell Ocranny. Greta said so.<br /> <br /> Because she was concerned for me, like you, foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> She did - she brought the big wave that stopped Alla from being on fire. But she was taking photographs before that.<br /> <br /> So that we can get these Watch people in trouble.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. But Greta is smart and Wolfram approves as well. So it is a good plan.<br /> <br /> The bald fairy? He guarded Oneida, who guarded the fairy Prince, so they were all inside. Guarding.<br /> <br /> We did not need him. It would have been nice to see Oneida fight though.<br /> <br /> With knives, like her sister Sabine, the Sin-Eater from the big cabaret. They performed together, with knives, before Oneida became a fairy.<br /> <br /> No, the thing that was left behind who looked like Oneida got Sabine and her fianc\u00e9e killed. It is a shame - they had a good plan for getting married.<br /> <br /> The fianc\u00e9e was pretending to be a fianc\u00e9, so that the foolish human customs would allow them to be mates.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t be foolish volchonok. The village knows I am a woman. A Russian man of my size who suddenly appears and begins courting Elena would be obvious.<br /> <br /> I have not decided. Now hush volchonok.<br /> <br /> Wise. Yes, it was a good fight.<br /> <br /> What? Of course we won. I am the best at fighting.<br /> <br /> Yes, we only killed one, but we frightened them and caused them to spend much of their kind of Essence.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, recall, it is bad to kill them. They will kill a human to return to life. <br /> <br /> I believe Marek was angry with that one. He is a very good shot.<br /> <br /> It is true volchonok. We do have a good pack.<br /> <br /> No, I do not think they want to go running. I believe they all want to rest. There will be time for running later. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 28th October, 1922<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve seen better days, but I have seen worse.<br /> <br /> Yesterday was my birthday. I am twenty-two years old. I still look like I did at nineteen. Actually I guess I have not aged much in the six years since my return, but still. Spent the day in the workshop, modifying the Buzzsaw Bow a little, then took Wolfram back to the house to check on Christina, where there was a surprise party waiting. The whole Motley, Christina, Marlene, everyone. Wolfram was cheerful and enthusiastically spent time talking to me. Christina hugged me several times, more affectionate than she has been in awhile. She was huge, of course. Poor dear had trouble hugging me. I got gifts from everyone, even something from Marlene. Heck, I even had something from Dana in the mail. I think the most ironic gift was from Alla and Fenric, an ornate lighter shaped like a gun. <br /> <br /> Marlene showed up at my room that night, said I should not sleep alone on my birthday. It was a good night. The first birthday night since meeting her I did not spend with Christina, but Marlene was\u2026quite well enough of a distraction from that. She was the second other woman besides Dana to sleep in my bed. I went to sleep happy, and certainly so did she.<br /> <br /> I think I heard Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re sigh when Marlene was slipping inside though. I did not think a teapot could sigh. <br /> <br /> Today was less blissful. We were contacted by Oneida at the house, who wanted to meet at a caf\u00e9. It turns out Prince Sascha was being menaced by what Wolfram was sure was members of Die Wacht. It sounded like them, and they wore the colors of the Imperial German flag. Queen Woebegone sent help in the form of Rudolph Gusser, the tall lanky Darkling. He kept an eye on the meeting. We agreed to come by The Hedge Maze and provide security. <br /> <br /> While we were there, Sabine, the knife dancer, came by, speaking sharply to Wolfram. She and Oneida got in each other\u2019s faces. It turns out they are sisters. Twin sisters. But Oneida was Taken, and when Sabine attempted to leave with a woman disguised as a man to be married, the Fetch saw through it. Their father killed Sabine\u2019s fianc\u00e9e and stuffed Sabine in a steamer trunk, where she suffocated. I am given to understand he died horribly when she rose as one of the Bound. When Oneida returned, she found Sabine decidedly disinterested in making up. It did not help that she walked in on her in flagrante delicto with another woman, and responded with shock. As one would, I suppose, seeing their twin with anyone. At any rate, the conversation between the two could be best described as \u201cchilly\u201d and at worst \u201chostile,\u201d though they never came to blows. I would not wish to see Oneida or Sabine hurt, but to see those two lithe, leggy amazing women in a knife fight would be\u2026exhilarating.<br /> <br /> The thought of spinning blades did remind me of the umbrella I had been working on, which would have steel serrated plates which when activated would spin in a deadly fan, carving up ones foe while the umbrella protected you from the gore splatters of whomever you were carving up. And if not carving anyone up, it could provide a nice breeze to passersby, provided they did not fall into it or something. I would have teapot designs on it. <br /> <br /> Given the gore shield, I could have used it tonight. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> We arrived at The Hedge Maze and met up with Greta Hess, whom Tatiana had invited and who managed not to fall into bed with a vampire in the process. Rudolph showed up too. We made a great deal of planning, and had drinks on the house. Marek and Dacian took up positions on the catwalks over the stage, Tatiana near the door, Rudolph, Dearbh\u00e1il, Oneida and Wolfram near Prince Sascha, and Alla, Fenric Greta and I in the crowd. However, after a bit, Rudolph warned us they were awaiting in ambush outside, so we regrouped and headed out, with Dearbh\u00e1il, Dacian, and Marek on the roof. Alla stayed near me, and the other moved to attack from different sides. Rudolph stayed with Oneida inside in case it was a ruse.<br /> <br /> I animated several cars en route, but held them in reserve as I, Wolfram (with my Buzzsaw Bow!) Alla and Tatiana charged them directly. They heavily attacked Tatiana, enough to send her into a rage. I did not catch everything, but I know she started coughing and slowed down, and Alla burst into flame, and Tatiana and I both bled heavily from our mouth, eyes, ears, and places not described in polite company. It was agonizing, like my organs were liquefying and running out of my body. I still manage to carve them with my chainsaw, and wound up as much covered in their blood as my own. <br /> <br /> Not to brag, but my chainsaw never got clogged up even with the viscera flying around. <br /> <br /> It was hard to fight; feeling like your entire abdomen was full of razors. I envied Alla; at least she was on fire. Well, until Greta put her out with a wave of water. As the pain was making my head spin I ran the cars into them, and heard several crunches. I could not see it, but apparently Marek and Dacian were tearing them apart from the air, even as Wolfram was sending blades into their body. There was so much fog from their wounds with five of them it was hard to see. That and the eyeball blood. <br /> <br /> Eventually, they fled, taking their temporary dead with them. As is my way, I crawled in our automobile\u2019s trunk to sleep, which is what I did on the battlefield when injured, find a trunk away from the fight to sleep in. Wolfram came and got me however, and took me inside. I remember him carrying me. Despite the pain, that was nice.<br /> <br /> I will need to get a performance assessment of the Buzzsaw Bow from him. It seemed to be carving nicely, but I really did not get a good view of the fight, with blood and sinew flying in my face and the fog and whatnot. Did I mention it hurt, like sliding down a greased razor blade while inside out? <br /> <br /> I wish I set them on fire.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il had already healed me some, and Prince Sascha also used his healing powers. I am still hurt, but it is a more natural kind of hurt, like falling from a plane or getting shot five or six time. Not this liquefying organs thing. Marek is still hurt too. They did not have guns, they must have used some Sin-Eater power I have never seen Wolfram or Greta use. Speaking of the daddy\u2019s girl, Greta got several pictures she was eager to leverage against them. For my part, I was ready to sleep. As much fun as carving screaming Sin-Eaters with a chainsaw was, I needed to recover a bit. I doubt Die Wacht is going to let this lie.<br /> <br /> Speaking of lying, though, I play to lie down on this very soft bed, and sleep a very long time.<br /> <br /> Dream Mayhem\u2026.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, let\u2019s do this. The 27th was a light RP, just what people were up to at the party. <br /> <br /> Each member of the Watch had Rage 4, a Manifestation at 3, and a Manifestation at 2. 3 keys each, most had Passion, Stigmata, and one other\u2026Pyre-Flame and Grave-Dirt was used. They were Psyche 3. Sin-Eaters are tough, and Manifestations are powerful. They were, however, unarmed beyond knives or pistols, and given the firepower incoming Rage, Curse, and such were more useful. Given the PCs were ambushing, for many Manifestations the Sin-Eaters had to weigh activating them and standing there being pounded. They knew they were fighting a Sin-Eater, Werewolf, and Vampire, but did not know what Lizette, Dearbh\u00e1il or Marek were, and never saw Dacian. The PCs were larguly trying to pile tilts on them, since Sin-Eater killing is temporary at best, so you had blinded, maimened people throwing powers around, hence Wolfram using the Buzzaw Bow. <br /> <br /> Greta used the Tear-Stained Boneyard to put Alla out.<br /> <br /> So, in case you have fallen behind a bit, the reader\u2019s digest.<br /> <br /> The Conspiracy was brought to Berlin by a number of things, Alla to do Constancia (the Maenad Mekhet Princess of Evil) a favor, Wolfram to answer a request by a former soldier named Willie, and Dacian to Skadi, the Winter Queen of Berlin. So far, there was a short meeting with the Circle members for Alla, so far, so good.<br /> <br /> Willie talked of an alliance between the Watch (proto-Nazi racists) and some elements of Black Company (an officially apolitical large Krewe of former soldiers) that he feared would embolden the Watch. It specifically included acquiring weapons from a Krewe called Red October from Russia (weapons are harder to come by due to sanctions) making them think they are destined for Communists in a Fifth Column, but actually going to the Watch. Our Heroes arranged for the meeting to be broken up not by them, but by the Pure, who are overconfidant in their control of the area, and whose members in the Ivory Claws tribe hate Sin-Eaters (and ghosts, and Vampires). They used a photo of Tatiana who had fought the Ivory Claw Ilsa in Vienna to get their attention, and left silver Lizette had made in the packages. The Sin-Eater Greta who they met in Paris, who lives in Berlin, is helping too.<br /> <br /> Skadi fears an alliance between the Spring King Sascha and Autumn Queen Woebegone. She also seeks to keep Germany in mourning so it will not be able to channel it\u2019s anger into another disastrous war with France. She is even murdering some Summer Courtiers in a bid to keep Wrath weakened. She fears the waxing powers of the Courts of Desire and Fear, who combined are her equal, may also strengthen the resolve of Germans too quickly to fight. She gave the Conspiracy no instruction, but implied weakening the courts would please her. Otherwise they are honored guests.<br /> <br /> Alla and Lizette met with Queen Woebegone and it went well. Alla began negotiating for experiments involving film and Vampires. Meeting Prince Sascha revealed that he has been targeted by the Watch due to his being a bisexual Jewish man running a club. They were menacing him so the PCs ambushed a group that came by to beat him, taking damage while utterly taking the Sin-Eaters off guard and routing them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, they also saw evidence the largest cabaret is under the control of an unknown Wolf-Blooded and with a number of supernatural denizens, including a singer of unknown nature and haunting voice and powerful Sin-Eater with the Girlfriend\u2019s Krewe. <br /> <br /> I think that is where we are, but if you have comments or questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T22:50:30-07:00","id":935454,"title":"","content":"After the battle with The Watch, the Conspiracy has interest. This could help them or hurt them. Let\u2019s see how they begin to leverage it.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 29 October 1922<br /> <br /> After the big fight last night Tatiana went back out. She went to neighborhoods that were supportive of the Watch, or where there was at least some Fascists and she started some fights. She said that she wanted it to look like there were multiple attacks on the Watch in general and that it wasn\u2019t just the group at the club that got the attention. She did end up fighting a couple of Claimed but didn\u2019t have too much trouble with them. They were alone and didn\u2019t pose all that much of a threat to Tatiana. She is too good a fighter and hits hard. I do not know if the ruse will work or not, but we have made the attempt. If all else fails, then at least Tatiana got to release some of that pent up energy and beat daylights out of some less than savory people.<br /> <br /> This morning Greta called to say that she had been contacted by Sabine. Apparently Sabine wanted to know if we were involved in the fight against the Claimed last night and if we were, she wanted to talk. We agreed to meet Sabine tonight at the club Saints and Sinners. Before our meeting though Wolfram and I continued our firearms lessons with Fenric and Lizette, per Alla\u2019s request, made our Kindred friend a pair of spiked brass knuckles. She has the set of silver knuckles, but sometimes you need to have non-silver weapons. Plus, she wanted to be able to do more damage than just hitting would normally do, hence the spikes. The finished product looked good. I think whoever is on the receiving end of that blow will well remember it.<br /> <br /> So tonight, the pack plus Marissa and Greta all went to Saints and Sinners to meet up with Sabine. We got there before it got too busy so Sabine was able to meet us right away and we all went to a table to talk. Sabine wanted to know if we were going to continue fighting against the Watch and if we were she was going to offer to lend us the support of her group, though it will not likely be in the form of combatants. That is fine. Any support against the Watch would be appreciated. We admitted that we were likely going to come into conflict with them in the future and she seemed happy with that. I got the impression that Sabine and her group do not like the Watch and have wanted to do something about them for some time, but have not had the resources to do so. We also told her that our goal was to get the Watch and the local Pure fighting one another. She seemed amenable to that idea.<br /> <br /> We discussed taking over some of the resources of the Watch, such as their \u201cHaunts,\u201d what we would call a Loci, so they cannot regain their strength and use those devastating gifts. This conversation moved to stealing caches of their weapons and redistributing them to our allies or to other places. Anywhere that the Watch cannot access them. They are dangerous enough without the guns. Sabine said that she should be able to have some information for us by tomorrow. <br /> <br /> Dacian stayed to talk to Sabine alone and came back a few minutes later with warnings for the rest of us not to wander the club alone. Apparently there have been two men so far that have ventured to the back of the club on their way to the private rooms that never made it to their destination. The ladies that were waiting for them never saw them or where they went. There have been no duplicates left in their place so it is not likely to be the work of the Fae Gentry.<br /> <br /> Tonight we also talked a bit about the Pure and wolf-blooded in the area and Holbien in particular. We know that he is wolf-blooded, but do not know if he is allied with either of the Pure factions in town or not. Tatiana knew what kinds of things someone that was loyal to the Fire Touched might have in their possession, so we sent Greta to go scout out his place of residence to see if she could fine any such items. Tatiana and I waited at the club for Greta to get back, while the others split up and sent to different places. Wolfram, Lizette, Alla and Marissa were going to visit Queen Woebegone. Fenric was going to meet our fae friends at the Hedge Maze after the club closes, while Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian go to that club.<br /> <br /> One thing I did notice tonight at the Saints and Sinners club was a woman walking in with a sack over her shoulder. She walked near the stage and specifically made eye contact with Della the singer. The stranger then went behind the stage and Della followed after. I am curious what that woman had in her sack and in general what kind of creature Della is. Dacian flat out asked Sabine earlier if she knew what kind of supernatural creature the singer was. Sabine did not know. I\u2019m not sure that she was aware that Della is different in that way.<br /> <br /> Greta came back a relatively short while later. She had not found anything like what Tatiana had described so we are still in the dark as to which group Holbien is allied with. It is probable that he is not allied with the Fire Touched. He\u2019s not likely connected to the Ivory Claws either given his ethnicity, but could be connected to a Uratha pack that we haven\u2019t come across yet. It is also possible that the man does not know what he is. We may have to resort to less subtle means to find out who he\u2019s allied with. Either that or we surveil him frequently and see if we can catch him meeting up with any Pure packs etc.\u2026<br /> <br /> So, after that news we decided to see what we could find out in the Communist club. I thought it would be a good idea to reconnoiter the club and listen out for anything interesting. So, we headed for the Gold Sparrow. The was a brief discussion on whether or not it would be just me and Greta going or if Tatiana would accompany us. Tatiana was concerned that she would be too angry to go and would just end up provoking someone into a fight. Greta told her not to underestimate herself and convinced Tatiana to come along. We agreed that Greta would do the talking since she had been to this club in the past and was known among the local patrons. We were not at the club long all told. We had just found out that they have been having some kind of supernatural problems though a lot of people didn\u2019t believe it. We speculated that it could be the Watch. Then too soon there was a disturbance at the front door. An older man came in and loudly asked the assembled patrons if his daughter was there or not. Greta swore under her breath about her father and tried to make herself less noticeable. Tatiana offered to get the man to leave and Greta and I would sneak out the back. Plan in hand, Tatiana proceeded to go to the front of the club and intimidate the man until he finally stepped down and left the club. Apparently this was cause for celebration among the patrons and they bought a couple rounds of drinks for Tatiana. Much to her chagrin she has been labelled a hero to their club. She eventually joined us outside and we all headed home. Greta dropped us off at the house and she headed on her way, presumably home, to deal with her father. Tatiana and I after a short discussion decided against beating up any more fascists tonight. We agreed to give them a break and let them think they were safe before revisiting their neighborhoods. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian went to the Hedge Maze. They were greeted warmly by Sascha and given free drinks. Oneida came over to talk to them and Dacian explained that he had talked to her sister about what fetches are and what likely happened with the whole situation with Sabine\u2019s lover and their father. I\u2019m not sure what her reaction to that was. It is a very delicate situation overall and there is a lot of room for error. I would have cautioned Dacian to tread carefully, but he did not tell anyone that he was going to talk to Sabine about this. I hope for his sake that things go well. Also while they were in the club Dearbh\u00e1il talked to Sascha about performing for the club sometime in the near future. I don\u2019t think they arranged any definite dates yet, but I\u2019m assuming they\u2019ll work all of that out soon. I know that Dearbh\u00e1il likes to sing in different venues, so this should be interesting. I am curious to see her perform. She sings beautifully and you can tell that she really likes to do it which makes her shows that much better. Apparently after they talked about Dearbh\u00e1il singing for the club Sascha started flirting heavily with both of them. Dearbh\u00e1il politely turned the Spring monarch down, but Dacian accepted.<br /> <br /> The group consisting of Wolfram, Lizette, Alla and Marissa went to go visit Queen Woebegone. As they arrived at the lot they saw none other than Harlowe, the director from the play in Paris, walking out. They stopped and caught up for a little bit and discovered that Harlow was looking for someone to direct his new movie called \u201cCurse of the Pharaoh.\u201d Harlow asked Alla if she would like to be in the starring role, but she politely declined, saying that she would rather be involved behind the scenes and intimated that she\u2019d be one of his backers. She also arranged to get a copy of the script so she could get Wolfram to look over and make sure that there are no hidden rites or rituals in it. I thought this was prudent given the man\u2019s history. They parted ways and went on to see Woebegone. They discussed the problem with the Watch, and Wolfram said that they need to be dealt with more subtly than just outright killing them. Woebegone just asked for 24 hours\u2019 notice on when we were planning on moving against the Watch and she would have the Autumn court prepared to hit them with terror attacks. She seemed keen on helping us drive them out of the city. Of course if we do succeed in driving the Watch out of the city it\u2019s going to create a power vacuum and I\u2019m not sure what will fill it. We would need to make sure to back the people that we want to take over that place of power, or arrange it so someone that will be good for the city takes control. We may not have any influence in the group, but we may be able to assist their move. Of course, all of that is presuming that we plan on driving the Watch out of the city in the first place. That is no small feat, nor is it something that we should take lightly. <br /> <br /> After that meeting concluded Wolfram and Lizette headed back to the house so he could read the movie script and Lizette could rest. When we talked later he said that the script did not have any rituals or rites hidden in its pages, but did say that it was heavily edited by Harlowe himself. It was apparently not a very good edit either. That said I can see the man being wary of anyone else editing something he wants performed after the mess with Emilie. <br /> <br /> While Wolfram and Lizette were doing that Alla and Marissa went to go talk to the head of the Circle of the Crone to discuss Durga, the woman that was interested in dissecting people of \u201cpure stock.\u201d Alla asked how to contact Durga and K\u00e1ra asked why she wanted to do that. Alla explained that she found a group that claims to be pure and are calling themselves the Watch. She said that she merely wanted to pass along that information to Durga and she could do with it as she liked. K\u00e1ra informed Alla that she was aware that the Watch is a supernatural group and that it is not good to antagonize them. I do not think she gave any specific reasons why, but she definitely discouraged my pack mate from messing around with them.<br /> <br /> All of this talk and planning concerning the Watch has made me wonder if we\u2019re doing the right thing. I do not like the Watch, nor do I like what they stand for, but they are one of the major players in the city. Are we doing the right thing by working on weakening them or flat out driving them out of the city? Many of the groups we have encountered in this town have expressed a desire to see the Watch gone, which I suppose is incentive to act against them. We are not alone in our desire to see the Watch taken down a peg or two. I suppose we are kind of like the catalyst for change in this instance. Overall, I think it\u2019s the scale of what we\u2019re attempting that has me cautious. Whatever happens with the Watch will affect the entire city, and possibly make a dent in the political future of the country. It may not make much of an imprint, but I do think that our actions will have more than local repercussions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations<br /> </b><br /> No, volchonok, we will not be going after the fascists again tonight.<br /> <br /> Because Greta says it will have them more scared if I don\u2019t attack every night and Marek thinks they will go to ground. Besides, it is late.<br /> <br /> I could have gone earlier, yes, impatient volchonok, but we had a meeting with Sabine. <br /> <br /> She was pleased that we had bloodied the Watch\u2019s nose last night and wished to offer her aid.<br /> <br /> Oh, in knowing things, mostly. <br /> <br /> She knows of the local Sin-Eaters. Their Loci and such. Though they call it Haunts.<br /> <br /> Well, no, we cannot break them, Wolfram says. But perhaps we can still make it difficult for them to use.<br /> <br /> Probably not. She is the only one that fights in her pack.<br /> <br /> We have Dearbh\u00e1il in our pack, forgetful volchonok. She does not fight. Well, she does not care for fighting, mostly.<br /> <br /> You would do well, I think, not to forget our songbird.<br /> <br /> You are getting quite good at changing the subject, volchonok. Yes, we did speak of the Wolf Blooded at Saints and Sinners. Sabine was unaware of what he was.<br /> <br /> Well he is from Turkey, so...<br /> <br /> Oh right. You do not know so much about human places. Turkey is, in many of the larger human places, Uratha territory, though the Firetouched challenge. So it makes him likely to be an ally, but... also likely not.<br /> <br /> Yes, Greta looked through his house, but could find no sure sign, either way.<br /> <br /> Well, of course. If someone is not a friend of Greta\u2019s, they are none of mine. But it seems Sabine was merely teasing Greta. <br /> <br /> I do not know about what. Something about recruitment she said?<br /> <br /> What? No, foolish volchonok, Sabine is not communist. What do you know about that anyway?<br /> <br /> I am not a communist hero! You will take that back, volchonok, now.<br /> <br /> Yes, well, Greta is allowed to say things foolish volchonoks are not. And she took it back as well.<br /> <br /> I yelled at Greta\u2019s father to distract him from her leaving. Not because he was a bourgeois toff.<br /> <br /> Yes, well, if a communist wishes to spend his money on drinks for me, that is less money to do foolish things with.<br /> <br /> We were there to find out if and where the Watch was attacking the communists, so we can get evidence to tell the Russian communists what was happening with their weapons.<br /> <br /> Oh. I was there because Greta said I was smart enough to not start a fight just because they were stupid.<br /> <br /> Well, I was not going to argue with her.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I did argue some. But not much.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t want to go with them. They were going to meet with the scary Queen - she is not the sad Queen, even though her name is, Marek has said.<br /> <br /> I do not care about movies. Though I think Alla was then to go to find Durga, the vampire who wished to dissect Germans because they are supposed to be pure.<br /> <br /> The Watch are German and claim to be very pure. So we make the vampires and the Watch attack each other, like we are doing with the Pure and the Watch.<br /> <br /> It is true that Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il went to the Hedge Maze. But I had enough of cabarets for the night, so I did not go with them. Besides, Dacian has not returned, so he and the Fairy Prince are probably mating.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, our songbird did return and left again to take the vampires to feed.<br /> <br /> I would not have minded spending a night at home myself, but they did not know.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we will not make up for it with a run. Perhaps another night. But not now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 29th October 1922<br /> <br /> Today was spent well, getting an alliance of supernatural beings against Die Wacht. Even if we cannot kill them, we can make their lives a living hell. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> During the day I worked on some knuckledusters for Alla. She does not look like a brawler, but she does have those long arms. Not Rudolph long, but long.<br /> <br /> Greta Hess told us after our conflict with Die Wacht Sabine was now interested in talking to us. We met her at <u>Saints and Sinners</u> that night, along with Marissa Sangiovanni and Greta again. We were there earlier, and got there as an optimistic ditty about April showers was being performed. I liked it.<br /> <br /> As things got a little raunchier on stage we started talking to Sabine. She was quite interested in us since we fought Die Wacht. As it turned out, Die Freundinnen are not fighters. They are factory works and teachers, even prostitutes. They could offer spying and raw materials, even some crafted support, but not fighting. <br /> <br /> Die Freundinnen being factory workers means they do have access to heavy machinery. I wonder if I could design something they could build in secret, like a car with a chainsaw coming out of every side and top. Or a car that launches me out of it with a chainsaw in each hand. Hmmm I could build that myself. Maybe a fleet of chainsaw tanks! Yes a fleet of chainsaw tanks. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Alla had a question about feeding which lead to the idea that we could try to cut off Die Wacht from their haunts. Tatiana wanted to destroy them, I preferred they fall into the hands of Die Freundinnen myself, but Die Freundinnen is unequipped to defend them, and a turf war had the same problems as a war of attrition. I\u2019d still like to find their base and blow it up though. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, we can still cut them off and weaken them. This could be useful if they are already facing the Pure, since they would be weakened, and we could have Die Freundinnen stealing as much energy as possible. There was some talk of getting the Pure fighting them, but that was for another night.<br /> <br /> Herr Holbein came up as there was questions about whether he was Fire-Touched kin or not. Sabine vouched for him, but knew little of his background. He is Turkish, and Tatiana knew frankly an astonishing amount about Werewolf conflicts in Turkey, but it did not give us answers. Greta offered to break into his house.<br /> <br /> I like Greta like I like a toothache, but I have to admit her friendship with Tatiana is sort of adorable, as is her schoolgirl-like crush on Marissa Sangiovanni. Marissa seems to find it amusing, and Sabine implied Greta should join Die Freundinnen, which made Greta even more uncomfortable, which is hilarious.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Della came out and did an interesting, if menacing, song about meeting her after eventide. It was sexy and creepy. Still wondering about her. Sabine, like so many other things, claims not to know. I wonder. Theodora from Vienna, the Gorgon, was there with another woman who apparently was turned by Alla\u2019s Sire. Apparently vampires just know these things. It took Alla (and the vampire) off guard, but that was all that came of it. Well, all but Alla and Marissa doing the vampire equivalent of chest thumping at them and getting it back. Vampires are weird. <br /> <br /> Eventually we parted ways. Dacian spoke to Sabine alone (I am guessing about Oneida) and found out there had been disappearances. Wolfram had a theory but elected not to share. We split into three groups, with Dearbh\u00e1il, Fenric, and Dacian going to <u>The Hedge Maze</u>, Marek and Tatiana waiting for Greta to finish turning over Herr Holbein\u2019s house in <u>Saints and Sinners</u>, and Wolfram, Alla, Marissa and I went to the Haus von Schaudert and the studio to talk to Queen Woebegone.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian spoke to Prince Sascha and Oneida, and Dacian was picked up by Prince Sascha, or vice versa. I am given to understand Oneida was standoffish and Rudolph Gusser was there, which was why he was not at Haus von Schaudert. Marek and Tatiana went with Greta to <u>The Gold Sparrow</u> where Greta\u2019s father showed up and Tatiana drove him off while Marek and Greta snuck out. We got some information, that Die Wacht were causing the communists problems, but that was it.<br /> <br /> When we got to the movie lots, Alla saw Harlow von Hoddenberg, who has gotten his hands on a movie screenplay about a Pharaoh rising up and wrecking Berlin, and the nations rising as one to battle them. He also got this from a play he picked up. This time, seeking to avoid cultists like Emilie, he re-wrote chunks himself. Apparently he is a better director than writer, though, as Wolfram said his additions were obvious. He also said after he got time to read it that it was not a spell this time, though it may have had a riddle or message it was butchered by Harlow\u2019s re-writing. Regardless, Alla agreed to back it, if not star, and got Wolfram the copy of the screenplay he read. Harlow was still looking for backers when we parted way. God give me patience.<br /> <br /> As I say, no Rudolph at Haus von Schaudert but we did meet Queen Woebegone. She knew of Die Wacht, of course. She was concerned of their attack on Prince Sascha and very willing to back an ally against them. Rather than a direct attack, she suggested we wait until there are losing and call in the Autumn Court, at which point she will call \u201cthe creatures of darkness around Berlin\u201d to descend on them and break them. She seemed rather gleeful at that.<br /> <br /> The only part that bugged me is she mentioned Autumn Court \u201cEngineers\u201d but when I asked about it (being an Autumn Court Engineer myself) she became coy, say saying only that it was not the sort of engineering I do. Well, I can do all sorts of engineering and said so. She put me off a bit but agreed to ask her engineers. I wonder if it is because I am French.<br /> <br /> I bet I could build a fleet of chainsaw flamethrowing tanks that would be pretty scary. Especially with Die Freundinnen\u2019s help. <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> After that, Marissa and Alla wanted to go talk to the Pagans (sigh) so we dropped them off at the temple and returned home. Their talk with the leader of the Pagans was apparently not all that productive, and Marissa was apparently mouthy again. Good old Marissa. Alla (with Tatiana\u2019s encouragement) wanted to turn Durga, an insane vampire she met, against Die Wacht, but the Pagans were disinclined to help with this, not wanting to provoke the Bound. That part actually made sense. Alla and Marissa came here a bit before having Dearbh\u00e1il take them to the Chateau to feed. <br /> <br /> I have been relaxing with Wolfram in here before it is time to sleep. He says now that the others are back is a good time, and he is right. Good old Wolfram. Hanging out with him while he read the play and marveled at what Harlow stumbled onto this time was marvelous. His comments and open mouthed staring were amusing. But he insisted I sleep, and admittedly bed will feel nice. Hopefully I will feel a bit less sore tomorrow.<br /> <br /> After all, who knows when Mayhem will strike! <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> In order to not bog things down with the combats with The Watch at the beginning, we used one roll combat and description to work out the combats, rather than roll out each fight. Tatiana did better than her opponents, so things went her way.<br /> <br /> The knuckles were ornate so more valuable, but I did not want their damage going up or their initiative going below zero. Lizette\u2019s insane pool and merits meant they were made in less than an hour with exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Lizette is referring to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5cg99no76Ko\" target=\"_blank\">April Showers</a> of course. Not an anachronism, it came out the previous year. I was coy about it, never saying it outright.<br /> <br /> Tatiana got just the best roll, you guys, for Politics to know the Uratha political situation in Turkey. Not a great die pool but the dice were explosive.<br /> <br /> Theodora was the Ventrue who had Constancia steal the cursed necklace in Vienna. Alla sided with the cunning Connie over the imperious Theodora. I am sure she has forgotten by now\u2026<br /> <br /> Liz offhandedly referred to another vampiress that was there and made Alla act odd. In fact, she detected Blood Sympathy as she had the same sire as Alla. Intriguing! All we know for now is she was with Theodora. What could that mean.<br /> <br /> It was taken as a given OOC and probably IC that Della was the cause of the disappearances in the club. They have no idea how to handle this. For clarification, this was the back areas which are intended to be staff only. <br /> <br /> Prince Sascha got an excellent social roll to charm Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian, but it was an optional case, no supernatural powers, so Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s player decided Dearbh\u00e1il would not sleep with the Spring King of her own accord. <br /> <br /> What will happen next? I am curious myself. Comments in Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:56:19-07:00","id":944199,"title":"","content":"Setbacks and opportunities. Our heroes arrange for the Black Company to be thrown off the scent to ensure there is room to move in the comflict to engineer between The Pure and The Watch. Alla gets a task from her sister with great potential for trouble, and Lizette challenges all comers to table tennis. And Greta spends most of the session in jail.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> Today started out sedate enough with Lizette challenging anyone who dared to play table tennis with her. Only a few people took her up on it, and only under the stipulation that she not use any gifts to enhance her ability to play or to control the ball. She agreed readily enough and started off playing Wolfram, who accorded himself pretty well. Next she played Fenric and Dacian and beat them both. I was distracted after that by a phone call from Greta\u2019s secretary. Apparently she was calling to let us know that her employer would be unavailable today but that she would call us as soon as she was able. As it turns out Greta got arrested for throwing a particularly heavy book at her father and knocking him out. The family\u2019s lawyer is working on getting Greta released and dealing with the whole affair as a family matter. Tatiana was particularly upset at the thought of Greta in jail and was making tentative plans to break the other woman out of the cell. It was pointed out that Greta could escape anytime she liked through a drain or sink if she wanted to, but had elected to stay in her cell. In the end we convinced Tatiana to let the family lawyer handle the situation.<br /> <br /> Not long after that the phone rang again. Wolfram answered it and found out that his contact within the Black Company, Willie, had some time sensitive information that he needed to pass along. We invited him over to our house for lunch which was only fair since he hosted us last time. We also decided that it would be prudent for him to meet all of us this time. If Wolfram is unavailable it would be good for Willie to be able to come to someone else in the pack. <br /> <br /> So, Willie came over and we treated him to lunch. I think he was a little overwhelmed by the experience if you ask me. He was very polite to everyone and spoke deferentially to everyone. He told us that the Black Company wanted to hash things out with the werewolves in town, meaning the Pure, due to the trouble that was had the other day at the train station. They were planning on bringing a letter to a particular part of town and seeing if they could find a werewolf. Willie said that a Lieutenant Hartman and two others would be delivering the letter. The only problem is that if the Black Company made contact with the Fire Touched it would be bad for us. If they made contact with the Ivory Claws, it would be very bad for them. The Ivory claws would kill any Claimed individuals that came into their territory. Tatiana suggested that we intercept the letter and pretend to be the werewolves that they are looking for. They will not know that we are Uratha and not Pure. The idea was that we would tell the Black Company that the werewolves only have a problem with the Watch.<br /> <br /> As for Willie he said that there was a certain amount of scrutiny going around since what happened at the train station. Some of the leaders in the Black Company didn\u2019t even know about the meeting, that we interrupted, so it is suspicious that information about it was leaked to outsiders. There was also some discussion about some people within the Black Company that might not be interested in helping Jews or gays even if they did love Germany. Dearbh\u00e1il then asked the hard question and asked why should we help the Black Company if they were only going to turn around and be racist. This conversation went on for a bit and I believe Willie eased Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concerns somewhat by stating that it was just certain individuals and that their ideals should not influence our decision to help the entire group.<br /> <br /> After Willie left, one idea that we came up with was to intercept the letter with me pretending to be a German werewolf. I can do a German accent pretty well, but was not completely convinced that I could fool a native German. I have pretended to be from other countries besides my own when traveling, but I do not usually try to play a native if I will be interacting with other natives of that country. In the end we came up with the idea of getting someone that is German to pretend to be a werewolf. The catch was that it could not be someone that registered as a Claimed or dead since other Claimed can sense that. The only native German in our group is Wolfram but he would not be able to pull it off since he is Claimed. The idea then was to approach a local friend to play the part while Tatiana and I acted like out of town werewolves that were called in to deal with the situation. Someone suggested that we ask Sascha since he is German and is experienced at playing roles.<br /> <br /> Lizette suggested that we make their car break down before they arrived at the destination, which is a particular club. Willie had the address. If we could make the car break down Tatiana and I could be walking from the direction of the club, without having to enter it, and head towards the car. Tatiana could then \u201cinvite\u201d them to leave our territory, but with the promise that we will pass along the note. We will also let them know not to approach the club on their own due to the danger it represents. Tatiana and I will then show up at whatever meeting is arranged with our German actor.<br /> <br /> There was also some talk of irritating the Pure by sniping them from a distance with silver bullets and make them paranoid about who is shooting them and why. This could be a good or bad idea. I will not deny that it could be fun, but it might hamper any talks that we have with the Black Company. We do not want the Pure to think that the Black Company is shooting at them and retaliate. There would be no proof of course who is shooting them, but we are not sure what groups the Pure are aware of in the city and who they might blame if provoked. This plan might need to be talked about a little bit more before we put it into practice. <br /> <br /> After a little while we got another phone call, this time from Sabine. She wanted to let us know that she had talked to her sisters and they had agreed to help us drain any \u201chaunts\u201d/loci that belong to the Watch if we can wrest control of it away from them for a time. They can also break down any weapons that we find into basic materials to be made into whatever we need. She said that her group has access to a factory if the need should arise and they could break down a large amount of material or make something big if needs be. She even offered to make a vicious (her words) excavator to use in taking down any \u201chaunts\u201d/loci that we find that below to the Watch. I am not sure if destroying the physical location of a loci will diminish or cut off the power, but it is certainly an idea to keep in mind. This of course is one of the least subtle plans, but it is certainly a viable option should the need arise.<br /> <br /> As it turns out the first part of the plan worked really well. Once we got the call that the Lieutenant and his men had left Lizette drove to get to the area of the club before they did. She did so handily. Tatiana and I positioned ourselves close to the club. Dacian went up onto a roof top to let us know when the Lieutenant\u2019s car was coming so Lizette could stop it. The plan worked well. Lizette caused the car to stop and Tatiana and I walked towards the car with as intimidating a posture as possible and asked the Claimed what we could do to help them leave our territory. Tatiana was rather good at being intimidating, as usual, and convinced the men that the club was dangerous to them because of what they were, but that we would take their message to those that are not antagonistic towards the Claimed. After they left we met up with the others and read the letter. It basically said that there had been a misunderstanding between the Black Company and the werewolves and that they wanted to meet to talk things out and resolve any issues that they might have.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the house Dacian penned a response to the letter and we all planned what we were going to do next. Alla and Wolfram went to go talk to a woman named Kara who had called. Well she had a woman named Hilde call and set up the meeting. Our pack mates then left to go meet with Kara. They were going to discuss what task our pack was going to do to repay the Circle of the Crone for acquiring a certain item for Connie. This task was apparently to remove a large group of Kindred from the city called \u201cBelial\u2019s Brood.\u201d They are holed up in a building that is near the seat of government for the city. That particular detail makes dealing with this group problematic. The idea was to kill them all, but setting off explosives might not be feasible. Setting smaller fires would allow for the authorities to arrive before we had dealt with the Brood, so again, problematic. If we can guarantee that the Kindred wouldn\u2019t catch us setting the explosives, we could set them up and detonate them at an appointed time. Then the lot of us could escape through a gate into the Hedge. We will need to discuss this in further detail.<br /> <br /> Dacian and I went to talk to Sascha at the Hedge Maze. He was amenable to talking once he had finished up with a Kindred gentleman. We retired to his office so we would not be overheard by anyone, but the vampire in particular. So, we broached the subject of him playing a werewolf for an evening. He seemed interested but had questions. He asked me what he needed to know to be able to pull off the act of being a werewolf. So, I went over mannerisms, body language and terms that any werewolf would do or know. He seemed to grasp what I was telling him pretty quickly and only asked a few follow up questions. He is a professional, I will give him that. <br /> <br /> We have set up the meeting with the Black Company for the 1st of November. Now we just need to have Dacian complete the response letter and get it delivered to the Black Company. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we are leaving now.<br /> <br /> No, I was not chasing something. I was pacing.<br /> <br /> Because I was concerned! Greta was in jail for throwing a Bible at her father. <br /> <br /> Probably because he is foolish. He thinks she is a prostitute and that spending the day in jail would calm her down.<br /> <br /> That is what I said! Foolishness.<br /> <br /> I would have, volchonok, but Wolfram pointed out she could not be held if she were willing to be obvious about her escape. And I am very obvious.<br /> <br /> It was a good day, but for that, indeed. We got to feed a good man and I got to yell at foolish men. I am very good at yelling.<br /> <br /> Watch it volchonok - I am very good at table tennis! It is just that Lizette cheats. It was very impressive that Wolfram tied her.<br /> <br /> We were talking about yelling.<br /> <br /> That is right, volchonok. We were yelling because the Black Company Sin-Eaters were going to meet with the Ivory Claws. Pulling the Black Company into that fight would be bad.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eaters wanted to make peace, which would have been bad enough for our plan, as it might end the fight between the Watch and the Pure as well. But since the Ivory Claws hate death tainted things, they likely would have slaughtered the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Because, volchonok, not all of them are bad. And they are too numerous - it is a delicate line to hold.<br /> <br /> Bah, no. We still are not to attack the Pure. Well, Marek and Dacian will - they will shoot them with silver from far away to keep them angered. I will get to fight more of the Watch though, tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> Oh, right. Yes, I got a letter when I yelled at the Sin-Eaters. So now we will be pretending to be the Pure and lying to keep the Black Company out of it.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not the best at lying. Dacian will ask the Fairy Prince to lie for us. It will be better to have a German anyway.<br /> <br /> Now? Now we are going to Saints and Sinner, where Liz and Dearbh\u00e1il are. Wolfram and Alla will go there as well once Alla\u2019s meeting is done. She is meeting with someone who has a task for her, for the Crone vampire who will help Connie.<br /> <br /> I can hope, volchonok. Perhaps it will involve fighting.<br /> <br /> Indeed, volchonok, perhaps it will involve running. But not right now. Right now, there is a Sin-Eater who wanted to know if I was single at Saints and Sinners. So we will run later. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 30th October, 1922<br /> <br /> I am having a bit of a break while I relax at <u>Saints and Sinners</u>. It has been a rather busy day.<br /> <br /> The start of the day was Table Tennis. I was waiting for the radio to play \u201cApril Showers\u201d after hearing it last night, as it is being played a lot I am told. Messing around the house, I found a table for table it upstairs, so I challenged people to a game. While most chickened out, even when I promised not to use Contracts, not all did. I walked on the table playing, most others stood on the far side except Fenric. Wolfram played first and it was essentially a draw, though I had to work hard at it to get there. He is perhaps better at table tennis than I suspected. Fenric and Dacian soon fell before me, however, none of the rest had the guts to face me. Well, to be fair Alla was asleep. Still sad none of the girls would do it.<br /> <br /> While these duels were going on we kept getting calls. Greta Hess\u2019s aggressive petulance landed her in jail for at least the day. Chucked a book at her father, apparently. I presume over the stuff at the club. The second call was important, though, Willie Schmidt had more information, which he wished to discuss in person. We invited him for lunch, as I had completed my domination at that point. Willie Schmidt is humble and rather handsome, probably the second most handsome German I know. He said he was a not so good farmer, but a good soldier, and seems very loyal to his Krewe.<br /> <br /> I should note there was some back and forth of the virtue of the Schwarze Reichswehr. Dearbh\u00e1il said that if they did not wish to protect the Jews or homosexuals, they do not deserve respect. I agree and am glad she felt that way. It is a reason to examine how I feel on Jews, honestly, since I had not considered it much. There seemed a consensus that they are what they are, and are too divided to be said they really have a goal beyond protecting Germany. Anyway.<br /> <br /> The Schwarze Reichswehr are, wisely, looking to head off problems with the local werewolves. They know of a gentleman\u2019s club, <u>The Young Wolves</u>, where they know there are werewolves. Subtle, guys. The thing is if they meet the Fire-Touched they may be able to piece together that they were tricked. If they meet the Ivory Claws they may be attacked almost on sight, provoking a major conflict. After some discussion we decided to head them off. The plan was brilliant.<br /> <br /> I was to cause their car to have a malfunction on the way to the club. Then while fixing it Marek and Tatiana come out to play the heavy, suggesting they are local Pure. They will receive the letter, and the Schwarze Reichswehr will instead meet with our confederate, possibly Prince Sascha (who is an accomplished thespian and practitioner of the Contract of Mirrors) who will disguise as a werewolf. We agreed to come out and set things up when Willie contacted us to say they were en route. He left, and I went and prepped the automobile.<br /> <br /> When I came back I heard the tail end of \u201cApril Showers\u201d playing from the radio so was sad. I switched the channel in case it comes on again, and sat on the radio while we talked. Sabine had called while I was prepping the automotive, and let us know some of Die Freundinnen were willing to fight, though unlike Sabine they were not skilled fighters. They also could seize control of a factory, via themselves, their girlfriends, and people intimidated by them. She suggested they could build a \u201cparticularly vicious excavator\u201d to destroy some of the weaker haunts, but Wolfram was against that. Still, the factory had previous been used to build tanks for the Kaiser, and so there was\u2026potential. I decided I would design a flamethrowing tank excavator and maybe or maybe not wind up using it.<br /> <br /> I mean, big shovel to crush buildings, cars, hills or hapless enemies. But also heavy armor, since it would have treads, and, of course, a rotating flamethrower as an antipersonnel device. Maybe some sort of Molotov cocktail launcher too. Maybe two in the back, so to rain burning doom on those too far for the flamethrower to reach. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> After a while Willie called, and we set out for the operation. Everything went smooth. Dacian climbed a building and signaled us with a mirror when the car was coming, I used my contracts to shut it down, and the Werewolves did their strong-arming. So far, everything going off without a hitch.<br /> <br /> That car was not as fast or suped up as the car at home, but it functioned well enough. Several of my passengers had to hang on to their hats. I enjoy having it go at a considerable speed, personally. <br /> <br /> Then it was dinner and prepping for the evening. There was even more discussing what to do. Just as we were about to split up Alla (who was awake now) got a call from a mysterious Hilde, a vampire who is a member of the pagans (sigh) and wanted to meet with her, about something involving the priestess. Alla agreed. She decided to take Wolfram and Fenric. Meanwhile Marek and Dacian went to<u> The Hedge Maze</u> (Prince Sascha is apparently being bribed to help us against the Schwarze Reichswehr with man candy) and I have the pleasure of Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s company at<u> Saints and Sinners</u>. For her part Tatiana was going to remain behind hoping the delinquent would call, then they would decide where to go. Probably wherever Marissa Sangiovanni went. <br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il and I have been relaxing. Della came on with another song, and Dearbh\u00e1il and I watched. She is rather cute. Now, just time to wait for the others. Then Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Whenever April Showers come along\u2026</i></span><br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> The Krewe split up at the end, so not everyone reported in. Hilde revealed she was indeed Alla\u2019s vampiric sister, but seemed to play coy to Alla\u2019s curiosity. Alla\u2019s group was chosen as they could operate during the day, and were more reliable than ghouls and better able to handle a sudden problem. I left how to dispose of a dozen or so angry vampires to the PCs. I am sure they will impress me. <br /> <br /> Willie continued to go over well. The others certainly sympathized. The plan mostly involved Lizette using Contracts of Artifice to sabotage the car. Tatiana got to make an intimidation roll and she is, as she says, best at intimidation.<br /> <br /> Okay, couple wrinkles coming up but hopefully will be moving ahead. And it will be Halloween! Won\u2019t that be exciting. Thanks for Reading, Comments and Questions welcome. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T14:53:23-07:00","id":947244,"title":"","content":"OK, caught up. I somehow got three postings behind. I don't know how that happened. Maybe I was too focused on BoS and MDH?<br /> <br /> Its is amusing in one way. Just as I am realizing that I am behind in this and start vigorously catching up I get to the Father Figure episode of Forever Knight (I have been rewatching my DVDswhen I go out to eat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T01:54:01-07:00","id":953720,"title":"","content":"Cool, glad you are caught up Omenseer. This one is a doozy.<br /> <br /> In this installment, the heroes set our current record for most Kindred killed at once, Dacian gets lost in the hedge, Greta gets an unwelcome engagement, and the PCs accidentally loose a flesh eating mermaid on the city.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXV</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 30 October, 1922<br /> <br /> This evening did not end the way I expected it to. We all met up at Saints and Sinners to discuss what we\u2019d been up to and what we\u2019d found out. It started out with Herr Holbien coming over to talk to Dearbhail about singing at his club. They worked out a date for this coming Friday, the 3rd of November. Dearbhail looked over the contract and said that it looked okay. He also invited Dearbhail back to talk to Della, who is the headliner for the club right now. He figured that it would be a good idea for them to be on good terms. Tatiana went with her for this conversation. Dearbhail didn\u2019t seem like she thought that she needed a bodyguard, but Tatiana was insistent so she came along. After the conversation with Herr Holbien Della invited the two ladies to have a drink in her dressing room. Dearbhail and Tatiana agreed and they all went back. Apparently during the earlier conversation between them Dearbhail used her Fae gifts to see that Della, Herr Holbien and something in the desk drawer were all magical. We knew that something was going on with Herr Holbien so that was not a surprise. We also knew that Della was a magical creature of some kind. So no surprise there. We did not know about something magical in the desk drawer. In private Della implied to my pack mates that she was not there entirely under her own volition and that she\u2019d like help leaving, but needed whatever was in the desk drawer to be free. <br /> <br /> So, while the ladies were talking Dacian let himself into Herr Holbien\u2019s office to have a look around. Dearbhail let us know that they\u2019d be talking to Della, so we knew to expect the delay. While they were talking Dacian did his investigating. He managed to get past the trap that was in the drawer and found a seashell comb in the drawer. He then took the comb and reset the trap. He then hid as someone else came into the room. That someone else did not open the door, they just walked through it. It was Sabine. Dacian hid until she left the room swearing. He slipped into the Hedge after that to get out undetected. I will get back to that though.<br /> <br /> The ladies had their own troubles. What had been Della transformed into a mermaid type creature with several rows of sharp teeth, and was acting rather intimidating towards Sabine. Her demeanor was aggressive which belayed her reasonable speech. She kept saying that she would not harm Dearbhail or Tatiana if they would just let her go. They said that they would come back to that, but in the meantime were going to leave the club. Dearbhail pretty much fled the room with Tatiana in tow and came to the table where the rest of us sat and told us that we needed to go home right then. She said it with some stress so we all agreed to leave. We went back to the house where she explained what had been going on. She told us about Sabine rushing into the room to fend off whatever kind of creature that Della had turned into with a knife. I have to give her credit for that. That took some guts to fend off the type of creature that Dearbhail described with a single blade. Sabine also said that what had been in the drawer was what was being used to keep her under control. So much for spur of the moment actions on our part.<br /> <br /> On the way back to the house we discussed what was going on and Greta had to go and bring up her idea of exposing this kind of thing to the world at large. She seems to be under the impression that if she had enough information on the good and bad things about supernatural creatures then people could make their own informed decisions about what was right and what was wrong. She thought that they would choose what is right. The question is, what would they consider right? I do not think that people are going to stop and think about the good and bad things about Vampires. I think that if informed, they will just go around and hunt down all the Vampires and kill the lot of them. If they have the knowledge of strengths and weaknesses about them they will use that to their advantage. If they know that they outnumber the predators and know how to subdue them, then they will rise up and do just that. There will be murder in the streets. Not to say that the predators, us, will not fight back. We will, and we will take a good number of the humans with us, but they, will eventually outnumber us and bring us down. I do not think that spreading this information is a good thing. I do not think that it will end the way that Greta thinks it will. I for one do not want my friends and family hunted down because they are connected to me. I will protect them to my dying breath. No matter how many times that comes. <br /> <br /> So, we went back to the house and entered the Hedge in an effort to find Dacian and bring him home. Given how long he\u2019d been gone we figured that he had become lost in the Hedge and needed our help to find his way home. Dearbhail was rather insistent in finding him. So, we all left through the gate in the basement to find Dacian. We found him pretty quickly and he told us what had happened to him. Apparently in order to get away from what he called Briar wolves he had to flee from the established path. He had met what appeared to be a young girl looking for her lunch basket. They both stepped off the path and promptly got lost. It wasn\u2019t too long before the little girl revealed her true colors and tried to eat or at least attack Dacian. Dacian overpowered her and forced her to stop. He then continued on his own. He came across a house and a graveyard. The graveyard contained the graves of the people from his village, the ones that died in the Great war. There was also a stone for him. It seems that the Hedge is a reflection in some ways of the real world and he found himself moving away from the cityscape so he turned around and managed to find his way back to the path. For our part Dearbhail used her gifts to find her way through the Hedge to find Dacian and I was able to give general directions based on my pack awareness gift. We found him shortly after that, but not before he had to make a pledge with a Troll to bring back sweetcakes as payment for crossing the Troll\u2019s bridge. And yes, I just wrote that in my journal. It seems like something out of an old children\u2019s story, but those old tales must have had some basis in reality. <br /> <br /> When we finally got back to the house we found that a message had been left for us, or at least for Wolfram. A note from Herr Wolfgang Von Ingersleben wants to meet with Wolfram tomorrow at lunch time to have a talk. The meeting place is a Gentlemen\u2019s club in town. Wolfram sent word that he would attend. We\u2019ll have to wait and see what Ingersleben wants.<br /> <br /> After the arrangements were made we sat down to discuss what we were going to do with Belial\u2019s Brood. We went over different ideas until I think we all agreed on one plan. Lizette will sneak in and plant the explosives in such a way that they will create a fireball big enough to eliminate the vampires but with enough force to take down the building. Wolfram will use his gifts to get an idea of the layout of the place so Lizette will be armed with the knowledge she needs to plant the explosives and avoid any day time guards. Dacian will sneak in and retrieve any documentation that seems interesting. We will sort out what we are looking for later, we just need to get the papers and get out. Tatiana will be disguised, as will Wolfram as they wait outside near the building so the former pilot can use his gifts to get the layout of the building. Tatiana will be there to guard him. Fenric and I will be some distance away. Far enough to not be associated with anything that happens yet close enough to render aid if needs be.<br /> <br /> <br /> 31 October 1922<br /> <br /> Greta arrived this morning rather upset and swearing quite proficiently. Apparently her father has become tired of trying to reign in his rebellious daughter and has arranged for her to be engaged to some man that she has never met. I believe he hopes this younger man can curb Greta\u2019s contrary nature. She was rather upset by this. I have no doubt that she will be successful against this intruder into her life. She may need to run and remain hidden to truly escape the fate her father has laid out for her. Time will tell what she does.<br /> <br /> In addition to having news about her upcoming betrothal, Greta also had news about a young woman, named Suzie Zhang, who may be in danger. Apparently this young woman may be the daughter of the Ambassador from China. They are keeping it quiet if they are related. But it is known that she goes to the market to pick up spices and other food stuffs on a fairly regular basis. It seems that the plan is for the Watch to come after her the next time she goes to the market, which will be tomorrow. For her part Greta got this information from breaking into the homes of the Watch members that we fought with the other night. The ones that she took pictures of. My pack is nothing if not altruistic and we agreed that we would meet with her later tonight, after dark, to discuss the dangers with her. We will likely offer our services tomorrow when she goes to the market so she might be a bit safer from an attack. It seems likely.<br /> <br /> We also discussed the situation with Della. Even I agreed that something needs to be done to contain her. We asked if Greta had a way to contact Sabine so we might be able to work out a way to keep Della from becoming a problem. The idea of making a Fae Contract with Della was brought up, perhaps with the stipulation that she cannot harm anyone within the city limits, or something along those lines. I do not know if the others plan on giving her the comb back or not. It would be a way to free Della, which some of the others seem keen on, but it would also negate any sort of control we might have over the situation. Perhaps the Contract will work to keep her under control.<br /> <br /> At noon Wolfram walked into the gentlemen\u2019s club to meet with Herr Wolfgang Von Ingersleben. The Black Company man once again invited Wolfram to join their cause. Wolfram declined politely. Apparently the Black Company wants to hire Wolfram in his capacity as an Occultist. They would like him to help them deal with the problem they find themselves faced with, namely the Werewolves. The Pure. The Black Company does not know what they did to gain the ire of the Pure, but they want to try and make it right. They want Wolfram to accompany their representatives when they go and meet the members of the Pure, which will actually be us. This whole situation is almost funny. The way things are working out we will be having a conversation amongst ourselves about the Werewolf/Claimed situation. Wolfram said that he tried to advise Wolfgang out of forming too deep a connection with the werewolves so they will not get embroiled in werewolf politics. The other man seemed receptive to the idea. <br /> <br /> After that we set about making our plans to deal with Belial\u2019s Brood a reality. Dacian disguised Tatiana and Wolfram, who were outside of the building, to look like member of the Watch. Wolfram leaned up against the building with the idea that he was sick and needed the support. Tatiana went along to keep an eye on him as he was helpless as he used his powers to get the layout of the building and find likely places for documents and where the daytime guards were. As planned, the information was passed along to Dacian and Lizette, who did what they do best. Dacian came back with a handful of interesting looking papers and Lizette rigged the building to explode in such way that it would not burn down surrounding buildings. Lizette, also disguised as a Watch member walked slowly away from the building shortly before the whole place exploded. It was an impressive explosion, I will give it that. Lizette certainly knows what she\u2019s doing when it comes to pyrotechnics. And of course the idea behind the disguises was to blame the whole thing on members of the Watch. I guess we\u2019ll see over the next day or two how well that plan works out. <br /> <br /> Overall we\u2019ve had a rather eventful couple of days and this one isn\u2019t even over yet. I can\u2019t help but wonder if things will be more interesting since today is Halloween. I guess we\u2019ll see. Anyway, we still need to meet with Greta\u2019s friend Suzie. My guess is that if there is an attack then Tatiana will be able to participate in her favorite activity, fighting. As will the rest of us. I am not averse to getting into a fight, but my pack mate certainly goes out of her way to engage in fisticuffs with pretty much anyone. Though to be fair in this city she has picked her targets carefully. My hope is that our luck holds out and any conflict with the Watch tomorrow will end well for us. Time will tell. <br /> <b><br /> <br /> Taitana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that was very loud.<br /> <br /> I am not upset!<br /> <br /> OK, maybe a little.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, because it would have been fun to fight the vampires instead of merely exploding their house.<br /> <br /> There is their Masquerade to consider. And there were twenty of them. Even though I am the best at fighting, having twenty is like cheating.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was not sleeping. He was doing Sin-Eater things and seeing inside the building walls from the outside, while Dacien stole the papers and Lizette put the explosions in place.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, Greta was there. She distracted guards from the house.<br /> <br /> What? No, foolish volchonok, I said she was not my mate because she is my best friend.<br /> <br /> Because Greta does not think she is pretty. And because Lizette was being unkind.<br /> <br /> She does not like it when there is talk of her mating with women. Greta is strange sometimes.<br /> <br /> Oh, no, she was yelling this morning because her father promised another man she would be his mate without asking her.<br /> <br /> Believe me, volchonok, she will not. Not unless she decides she wishes to. <br /> <br /> She probably will not decide so. I think she likes Marissa more. Or possibly this Susie.<br /> <br /> Susie is the rich non-German that the Watch will try to kill next, but that we will save first.<br /> <br /> Foolish human reasons. Because she is not German. And maybe also because she is the daughter of China\u2019s ambassador to England and is important therefore. It is foolishness, whatever it is, and besides Greta is fond of her, and it is the Watch, so we are protecting her.<br /> <br /> Our hunt goes well enough, though you know we have not called Siskur-Dah yet. Perhaps when we do I will get to fight someone properly. We did have a stroke of good fortune - Wolfram will be helping the Black Company during their meeting with Prince Sasha where he pretends to be a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Because he is a German soldier and is known to be knowledgeable about many things. It is reasonable. But I will be on guard for a trap, do not worry, wise volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was the Black Company\u2019s card that was left last night. That is the way nobles howl to each other.<br /> <br /> We were gone when the card came because we went into the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Well then, distractible volchonok, you shouldn\u2019t wander off so far just because I am talking and having drinks with beautiful women, yes?<br /> <br /> I know, I know. But truthfully, it was that Dacien was possibly in trouble, so there was no time to look for wayward volchonoks. Next time it is not an emergency I will howl for you.<br /> <br /> The pretty singer is a werefish, with many teeth. And Dacien stole the comb that let Holbein control her.<br /> <br /> Because I told him where it was and that it was forcing Della to work for the Wolf-blooded man. That was clear by how she looked at the drawer while Holbein and Dearbhail talked about our songbird performing.<br /> <br /> Yes, after he stole it is when he went to the Hedge. He had fun, I think.<br /> <br /> Yes, my insightful volchonok, I am making a joke. He was quite unhappy. But unharmed.<br /> <br /> Not everything was bad. I had drinks with a pretty werefish who will be fun to fight. <br /> <br /> Also, I did find out that Holbein is probably Pure - his family was powerful and had a turn of bad fortune recently, which matches the Ivory Claws the most in Turkey. Plus, it is possibly good that we have freed Della.<br /> <br /> I do not know. I kept getting confused. I think mostly we simply do not know enough. Possibly she killed many people and it is only fair that she is held captive and made to do the thing she enjoys for a living. Perhaps people are merely frightened of her many teeth.<br /> <br /> No, I am still best at biting. But she is probably very good at it. It will be a fun fight.<br /> <br /> That is true, volchonok, it is sad if she has never run free. But we will not be either, for now. There is much to do before the night falls. Running free shall have to wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 31st October, 1922<br /> <br /> I think I need a cigarette.<br /> <br /> Just blew up a building with twenty vampires and two ghouls in it, with some internal firebombs just to be sure the job was done. But I am getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> So\u2026last night Herr Holbein asked Dearbh\u00e1il about playing in his club. As it turned out, this was a mistake on his part. She and Tatiana went back, and he brought Della in (she being the headliner), and managed to work out a plan for Dearbh\u00e1il to sing on the third. However, Tatiana noticed Della staring at a drawer. <br /> <br /> After the meeting, Della invited Dearbh\u00e1il and Tatiana back to her room, after she warned us about Della\u2019s odd behavior. They spoke of a \u201ccontract\u201d which was not literal, as it turned out. Meanwhile, Dacian snuck into Herr Holbein\u2019s office, and stole the \u201ccontract.\u201d That was when all hell broke loose.<br /> <br /> Sabine went back and checked Holbein\u2019s office. How she knew something happened I have no idea. Then she went straight to see Della, who was acting very odd. She drew a knife and menaced Della with it, who became a toothy-mawed mermaid, sensuous and snakelike. Despite entireties to Dearbh\u00e1il to \u201cfree\u201d her, Dearbh\u00e1il fled. She quietly told us to leave, and soon was out with Tatiana, who seemed to find the mermaid fascinating. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, despite lacking the survival skills to navigate a cornfield in January, Dacian went into the Hedge. When he did not turn up after a bit, we went in to rescue him. To his credit, while hopelessly lost the entire time he only almost got eaten two or three times and only owed a favor to one hob. <br /> <br /> It turns out the \u201ccontract\u201d was a seashell comb. I had heard the stories of marrying mermaids after finding their combs. Mermaids are, however, different than I had heard. But then, such things are often more sinister than it appears.<br /> <br /> I needed my beauty sleep, so curled into a little ball with the radio on. The next morning we got word that a \u201cCaptain Wolfgang von Ingersleben,\u201d which may be the most excessively German name I have heard since I got here, wanted to talk to Wolfram. He is a captain in Schwarze Reichswehr. <br /> <br /> As it turned out, he wanted Wolfram\u2019s help negotiating with the Pure. As Wolfram was a military man, as well as a Sin-Eater and respected occultist, Wolfgang wanted his help. And of course Wolfram was willing to provide it. This honestly has me hopeful we can tie up that end and get the rest of this taken care of. Once that giant is back to sleep we can focus on Die Wacht.<br /> <br /> Perhaps with rotating blade hats and flamethrowers. Mayhem! <br /> <br /> Also, Greta arrived, in her usual ladylike and considered fashion. Shouting obscenities and slamming doors. Apparently her father has given up and intends to marry her off, feeling a younger man was needed to keep her in line. Now in this, she has my sympathy; arranged marriages are so last century. And frankly, if he thinks he should control her, he can get over it. It is the Twentieth Century now! Women don\u2019t need men, or other women, to tell us what we should do or who we should be! That is so last century!<br /> <br /> Now, I am fairly sure Greta is not exclusively Sapphic, but her coyness about it got under my skin. People are not going to learn to accept it if we hide it. I hid it with Christina, sure; she was engaged, and while Wolfram was okay with it, I did not want to seem to be mocking him. But Dana and I were pretty obvious. Unfortunately Greta won\u2019t acknowledge it, despite mooning over Marissa and despite how she was talking about Susie.<br /> <br /> Ah yes, Susie. Susie Zhang, apparently not her real name, is the supposed daughter of the ambassador to England of China, except that female children are rarely brought to Europe. And Greta seems suspicious that she is actually the ambassador\u2019s daughter. So what she is doing and the specifics of her business in Berlin is unknown and possibly nefarious. Not that it slows down her obvious affections. Anyway, she is going to be targeted by Die Wacht, and we know ahead of time and can make a plan: to ambush them when she goes to \u201cthe market\u201d for food and spices. We will be meeting her in a few minutes. I don\u2019t trust her myself, but we will see how things go after the meeting.<br /> <br /> But more importantly, we wiped out the Belial\u2019s Brood Vampires. This felt like an unequivocal blow against the forces of evil. Wolfram, guarded by Tatiana, used his power to haunt the building they were sleeping in, Dacian snuck in and stole ownership papers and finantial records, and then I snuck in and rigged the building to blow. I worked to ensure that it would implode, not explode, and set firebombs to deal with the vampires. The implosion, and internal explosions, were glorious. It felt good to level a building after such a long dry spell. I had missed the earthshaking and seeing walls meters high crumble. That shows them who the small one is.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> But it is Halloween. Time for mischief! Time for mayhem! Well, talk to Susie, then Mayhem.<br /> <br /> Though it will be hard to out-mayhem blowing up a building\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> Okay\u2026<br /> <br /> First scene: Dacian made some excellent, and difficult, Larceny rolls. Then made the somewhat questionable flee into the Hedge, for which he was badly unequipped. He surived, though luck and because I was (perhaps excessively) kind. <br /> <br /> So, Della. Della is a Mermaid. I stated her similar to a sort of Werecreature. She has a battleform, she has a few sort of gifts, but not really renown. Much like the Banshee (in Balance of Shadows) there is no specific CoD creatures, and that is all for the good. The unknown is a theme of Chronicles of Darkness, and I was very deliberate in having her be something not covered. Della is not a Beast, she is not a Changeling, and she is very definitely not human, nor was she ever. Where does she come from? The PCs may learn that, but what is she? A Mermaid. And not the little Mermaid kind. There are other Mermaid stories that are true the PCs may discover if she survives (a probably, Mermaids are very hard to kill). <br /> <br /> Not covered was the dragging sound Tatiana heard from her room when Holbein (whom she called Farouk) went to fetch her (where he called her Ms. DuMer). It stopped and she opened the door. It quickly became apparent in the fight it was her tail, as she moved very much like Medusa in the old Clash of the Titans. <br /> <br /> I had not planned on them going for her \u201ccontract\u201d immediately\u2026I had a scene planned where she waits outside Saints and Sinners watching the rain fall where she might discuss more of her background, which would have more clues to her motivations and background. Wound up not happening. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve let slip Suzie is supernatural. She is a Supernatural which has not appeared in any of my CoD games yet but which I have written about in my published writing. Don\u2019t give it away, but I suspect my Players will have strong guesses after tonight\u2019s session. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to note while Greta is a queer woman, she is bisexual; she is not objecting to marrying <i>a man</i>, she is objecting to marrying <i>against her will</i>. There was some confusion about that at the table. She has shown interest in more women than men, but that is because I have a majority female cast both of players and NPCs. Man or woman, anyone who seeks Greta\u2019s hand had best be ready to prove themselves. Sadly, no PCs seem interested in her. <br /> <br /> There was a lot of rolling out the bombing, but Dacian did excellently on stealth and worked well with Wolfram on investigation, and Lizette did well enough on stealth and her science and craft rolls. There was no follow-up combat because it was done right first. The vampires took eight aggravated levels and eight dice (four successes, total 12) before building damage even came into the picture. Not that they were all the Belial\u2019s Brood in town, but Halloween is going to be a lot easier than it could have been. Which is good, that would have been a difficult mark on German history to ignore.<br /> <br /> Wow, that is a lot of talking. I hope you have enjoyed. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T02:15:33-07:00","id":962165,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Halloween, the night when the dead walk, when devils play, where the doors between worlds slip open. It is Berlin, 1922. There is dancing, there is death. Tonight the dead make war.<br /> <br /> Two combats this time, one 2 Werewolves vs. 2 Sin-Eaters vs. 2 Vampires, the other 1 Changeling and 1 Sin-Eater vs. Two Wolf-Blooded vs. 2 Vampires. Enjoy.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXVI</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 31 October 1922<br /> <br /> Before we did anything else we sat down to plan out our next few moves. Tatiana came up with the idea of forging copies of the documents that we found in the Vampires building and including names of known Pure members to implicate a connection between the two groups. Dacian and Wolfram will go to the Gentleman\u2019s club later tonight after they close and see about acquiring a name or two to put in the new document. We did not after all promise to bring back documentation, that was an added extra bonus. So, we will not be expected. We can bring the documents by at our leisure. <br /> <br /> Overall I think the meeting with Suzie Zhang went well. We arrived at the hotel that she lived in and either took the stairs or elevator to the fourth floor. We were greeted by a man in traditional Chinese armor. Suzie soon arrived and showed us to a sitting room. Everywhere we looked was decorated in the Chinese style. The colors are a bit bright for my tastes, but it was nicely done. Wolfram later explained that it was strange for a Chinese woman to have bought the fourth floor. Apparently the number four in Chinese culture is bad luck and has a connection to death. There are other open floors in the hotel that are not owned by anyone, which means that she specifically chose the fourth floor. I could be that she doesn\u2019t believe it is bad luck, or she chose it for a reason that is not readily apparent.<br /> <br /> Greta introduced everyone to Suzie and the other way around in English. We explained to Suzie that she was being targeted by a group called The Watch and what they were. We figured that being up front about some of the strange stuff that she might see would be a good thing. Dacian explained some of the groups more mundane talents and Wolfram hinted that the rest of us were uniquely talented in some way. I generally do not like what I am being revealed to mortals, but there was nothing specific mentioned and Dacian hinted that she was supernatural herself.<br /> <br /> Suzie obviously has a good deal of wealth and has been using it to collect legal and illegal, occult and mundane Chinese objects and returning them to her homeland. Her apartments were full of various examples of items that she had acquired during her time in this country. This may be how she got on the Watch\u2019s list. She is obviously foreign and has been spending a good deal of money in and around the country. She has drawn attention to herself, unfortunately in a bad way.<br /> <br /> After Wolfram hinted that the lot of us were special in some way Suzie revealed her own nature to us. Her eyes glowed red and she held out her hand and produced flames. She said that she can throw them should the need arise. At that point I think we all realized that Suzie is likely more than capable of taking care of herself with smaller groups, but we had already offered our aid, we were not going to rescind the offer. She was appreciative of our plan to help.<br /> <br /> So, we planned with Suzie that we would go to the market with her tomorrow and that some of us would be following her so she would not appear to have a large group of people looking out for her. After all we want our targets to come out and make their presence known. We want them to attack. That gives us nominal justification for attacking them back. If any witnesses are asked, then they can verify that we were provoked. Ideally there will be no mortal witnesses to the fight we are planning, but there is always the possibility. <br /> <br /> As we were heading back to the house Wolfram revealed to the rest of us what he had deduced about Suzie and her nature. He said that she was a type of Demon blooded individual that had the powers of someone from the group called the Lucifuge, or Seventh Generation. They are Hunters whose prey is other demon blooded who will not join the organization, full demons, or dark supernatural creatures. Wolfram said that given her open display of power it is likely that she is not actually a part of the Lucifuge and possibly does not know about them. That might make things more interesting in the future for my pack if we remain allied with this woman. If the Lucifuge find out about her they may come recruiting or hunting as the case may be.<br /> <br /> After we all talked be planned on splitting up and taking care of multiple things at once. Greta excused herself to take care of her own projects. So, Tatiana and I decided to go hunting members of the Watch. I know that Tatiana was keen on getting into a fight and I wanted to be out and about and see if what was left of Belial\u2019s Brood did anything. The group that we blew up were just some of them. Granted it was a good number of them, but not by any means all of them. I was curious to see if they tried to get up to any mischief. And I can honestly say that my curiosity is sated. I don\u2019t feel the need to find out any more about Belial\u2019s Brood. <br /> <br /> It was easy enough to find members of the Watch out and about and to ambush a pair of them. We got a hit or two in before we were joined by two other men. These men were not wearing shirts and were both carrying what looked like Molotov cocktails. Things did not improve with their involvement. They threw the firebombs before any of us, Uratha and Claimed alike, could react. The Claimed started to run away, while Tatiana and I stood our ground. This unfortunately led to us being set on fire. I was not amused. Then one of the Vampires, I\u2019m assuming they were Belial\u2019s Brood, attacked Tatiana. He did a grievous wound to my pack mate and in the process set himself on fire. He did not react to fire like I would have expected him to. He was amused and began laughing. It was disconcerting. His friend sprayed the area with a machine gun and all I could think about at that moment was Lizette trying to teach Fenric how to shoot a gun. Her arguments came to mind that spraying an area lets you hit your target more often. I almost laughed. <br /> <br /> Tatiana managed to take down the Vampire that had been attacking her. He fell unconscious, or what passes for unconsciousness among the Kindred. I believe Alla called it torpor. I then managed to put myself out just before one of the Vampires threw a grenade into the mix. That hurt everyone and Tatiana shifted into Guaru form. She was about to attack the remaining Vampire, but he started running away inhumanly fast. She could not have caught up with him, so she shifted back. We let the other Vampire burn to ash. <br /> <br /> We were both looking rather rough after the fight. Tatiana had suggested that we go talk to the Faeries and wanted to head straight for the club that they\u2019d gone to. I said that we should change our clothes first at least. We were both wounded, me more than I\u2019d like, and our clothes were shredded and burnt. We would draw undue attention if we headed into more public areas. She did not agree but eventually acquiesced to my idea. <br /> <br /> I will admit that my healthy respect for fire remains well and truly intact, and that I am once more amazed and a little concerned with my pack mate\u2019s obsession with it. Lizette incorporates fire into just about every weapon design that she comes up with, including that contraption that shoots saw blades. I\u2019m not sure why the saw blades need to be on fire, but she had added that functionality to the weapon\u2019s design.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Dacian went to Saints and Sinners to talk to Della only to find that she was missing. Sabine was also not performing tonight. Herr Holbien was there, so they talked to him to find out what was going on. They discovered some of his history. He was in the Ottoman military, and said that during the war his unit was wiped out in the Mediterranean and he was found by Della. He realized quickly what she was and took her comb when he found it. They came to an agreement. They would travel together and Della would perform and sing. They made a good living at it, though they were hunted a couple times before they became more careful. Setting up the club here made for a nice stable environment and a good cover for the both of them. Herr Holbien honestly seemed to not know where Della had gone, but was keen on finding her. He was also keen on finding the person who stole the comb and punishing them for the theft. Dacian and Wolfram said that they would do what they could to find the comb and to find Della. Also, while they were at Saints and Sinners they received the same advice from Police that the others did. If you have to travel, do so in groups.<br /> <br /> After they left the club, Wolfram and Dacian went to the Gentlemen\u2019s club after they\u2019d closed to do their bit of burglary. Wolfram used his gifts to take a \u201clook\u201d inside the building and determine where any guards were, there were two, and get the general layout of the place. He communicated this to Dacian who quickly scaled the walls and crept in through a window, that Wolfram had unlocked for him. While Dacian was searching for documents Wolfram had problems of his own. He heard a pair of men sneaking up on him, badly. He said that they were talking quietly in Czech and seemed to think that he was asleep. He surprised them by using one of his gifts to glow rather brightly. The Vampires, as they soon revealed themselves to be, threw a firebomb at Wolfram. The two guards tried shooting ineffectually at the Belial\u2019s Brood Vampires. Wolfram managed to set one of the Kindred on fire, who then pulled the pin on a grenade but did not throw it. The explosion was centered on himself, killing him and shredding Wolfram\u2019s clothes. Wolfram himself was not wounded due to his gifts, but his clothes were not exempt from the effects of fire and explosive. The remaining Vampire threw a grenade in the window where the wolf-blooded guards had been firing from. They were both killed. Wolfram then set the building on fire. Dacian quickly stole a list of names that will not be missed, particularly since it will be believed to be destroyed in the fire, and left the premises. They also came back to the house and we met up with them there. <br /> <br /> So far it has been fairly exciting and the evening isn\u2019t even over yet. We still need to meet with Sascha and let him know that Wolfram will be negotiating on the behalf of the Claimed so he will not be surprised by our group being represented on both sides of this little discussion. I need to bind my wounds long enough to make it to the club without bleeding all over the place. Tatiana should do the same, so she doesn\u2019t bleed on her fresh clothes. Which is another thing that we will need to do in the not too distant future. We, including myself, Tatiana and Wolfram, will need to acquire some clothes to replace the articles that were destroyed by fire or grenades. I never want to have to write that sentence again. I had more than enough dealings with grenades during the war. I was really looking forward to not having to deal with them in my civilian life. Gunfire I can understand. We put ourselves in enough situations where those on the other side have guns, so that makes sense. My alternate profession deals heavily with guns. Claws and teeth are also understandable given my nature, and Tatiana\u2019s predilection for fighting. But grenades did not figure heavily into what I expected from my civilian life. I do not want to think what would have happened to others in my pack if faced with such a thing. Wolfram is uniquely suited to dealing with fire. He also has certain gifts from being Claimed that allow him to shrug off wounds that others cannot. Dacian, quiet and stealthy though he may be, is not up to the task of dealing easily with explosives. Neither are Lizette or Dearbhail. I hope that they had the good sense to stay in the club instead of venturing out this evening. I do not know if they received the same warning that we did about the roving bands of trouble makers. I will be rather put out if anything has happened to them. No one harms my pack. If anyone has been hurt then I will be going on a hunt and seeing about picking a fight. It may not be the wisest course of action considering the shape I\u2019m in, but it won\u2019t kill me, and I sure bet it would be a surprise to my prey when I come back to finish the job. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, you did very well.<br /> <br /> He did run from you very quickly. <br /> <br /> It is not your fault you did not catch him. He cheated, like Alla can.<br /> <br /> I am sure he also ran faster because he was afraid of you, yes. He was oddly unafraid of the fire however...<br /> <br /> I mean nothing by it volchonok, you are much more frightening than fire.<br /> <br /> That is true, it was his fire, but still. Alla is very frightened of fire, even when it is her trusted friend\u2019s.<br /> <br /> No, Suzie does not count as a trusted friend. I meant Lizette. Suzie is very interesting however.<br /> <br /> No I will not try to mate with her...<br /> <br /> Mostly because Greta is smitten. It is not that she is unattractive - she is very pretty and dangerous. And quite in charge of herself.<br /> <br /> It is no shame to accept help when many will be attacking you. You can only light so many people on fire, only so quickly, even if you are part demon.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it would be a good fight. The big man in the armor who is probably a demon would be good to fight as well, I am certain. Or he is just there to intimidate. That is less fun.<br /> <br /> We will probably not fight, it is true. My packmates are too intrigued. I believe Lizette will mate with her if Greta does not.<br /> <br /> Yes, we may still get to fight Della. I believe they intend to merely return the comb however.<br /> <br /> No, they will say they found it. The Wolfblooded wishes to punish the thief, so it would not be good to say it was Dacian.<br /> <br /> They went to speak to the Wolfblooded. before they fought the vampires. They fought them at the Pure den.<br /> <br /> It is a clever plan, volchonok. You see, the papers Dacian got from the vampire house we exploded did not have anyone we knew on them. But my thinking was, what if they did?<br /> <br /> Bah. You are no fun. <br /> <br /> It is ok. No one in the pack was fun either. What I mean is we will put names on them. The names of the Pure that Dacian found at their den. Then we will have the Pure and the vampires that dislike Alla fighting each other.<br /> <br /> Because they will think the Pure are helping the vampires that everyone dislikes.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is those vampires you chased away after they interrupted is fighting the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> They did help! The Sin-Eaters never made me feel buried or set me on fire, just the vampires. <br /> <br /> Well, yes, the Sin-Eaters got away, but they would have anyway - we were not to kill them, remember, volchonok?<br /> <br /> The claws were very painful, yes, but I got better.<br /> <br /> I was on fire!<br /> <br /> The humans were all long gone before I took Father Wolf\u2019s form, it was fine. You worry too much, volchonok.<br /> <br /> We came by the house because our clothes did not take well to grenades and firebombs. Neither did Wolfram\u2019s, even though he was not hurt.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, now is not the time to run. Even if we might find more of the Watch. But Marek is hurt and needs a fairy. Later, perhaps. Once our alpha is healed.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 31st October, 1922<br /> <br /> I am sitting in <u>The Hedge Maze</u>, watching a dark haired vixen dancing, waiting on the others to arrive. Alla and Dearbh\u00e1il are here\u2026Alla is especially reveling in \u201cThe night life;\u201d I suppose as a vampire used to everything shutting down at sunset this is heaven.<br /> <br /> Halloween night has been fairly calm, though Oneida says that there have been attacks out there tonight. I suspect this is part of Belial\u2019s Brood\u2019s movement, though without their vanguard I cannot imagine they will be too successful. Marissa actually recommended not hunting them, to help Alla\u2019s faction, but I suspect we will deal with any vampires we meet. I wonder if the other\u2019s have.<br /> <br /> No vampires (beyond Lady Garin) in here, though as I find myself surrounded by beautiful women, I think about Dana and Christina. I would like to spend the night with one of them again. I mean I won\u2019t be spending any more nights with Christina ever, but I miss her none the less. The lack of affection does lead to some rather unladylike thoughts, especially as I take risks fighting Sin-Eaters and similar.<br /> <br /> I also had some unladylike thoughts earlier. After destroying Belial\u2019s Brood\u2019s base near the Reichstag, we went to visit Suzie Zhang to warn her of danger. She controlled the fourth floor of the failed hotel several wealthy people lived in. it was decorated in a very oriental fashion, though Suzie herself was dressed as a western woman. Greta introduced us in English (which we stayed in) and we were lead to a small room that was sumptuously decorated. Outside was a huge man in traditional Chinese armor who never spoke. Suzie believed Greta that she was in danger, and quickly caught on that we were supernatural. She did not seem to be concerned, however, by that. She clearly was herself, and sprouted fire rather ominously from her hand. <br /> <br /> It seems she is recovering treasures from China to return to her homeland, which explains the focus on England. She was fairly polite to occidentals like us, but nonetheless I wager she watched us very closely. I only hope Dacian did not try to steal anything, or won\u2019t go back and try.<br /> <br /> That brings me around to my Sapphic thoughts. Suzie is very attractive, with porcelain skin and angular features. She is only the second Chinese person I have seen in the flesh, and the first woman. She is quite beautiful, even alluring, and despite her western attire, was unafraid to flaunt that, moving sensually with fluid motions and without lowering herself to appear to be trying to be seductive. Greta was well woven into her spell\u2026her eyes never left her. That silly little lesbian.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t really call Greta a rival though. For one, I am not looking to start a serious romantic relationship, second I can\u2019t imagine given the work she has to do she would enter a relationship, sexual or romantic, with a European, and despite my luck I cannot assume a woman from a foreign culture is Sapphic. Still it is pleasant to dream, and she tempted a dozen impure thoughts just by smiling.<br /> <br /> I admit the fire was appealing too. I mean what is not to like about a woman who can spray flames from her hand. Imagine driving a car around with her standing and throwing fireballs at other cars! I could have a flamethrower on the front and back to not feel left out. We would rule the highways with an iron fist.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> But for now, I watch this lovely lady dance and I wait for the others. Then maybe more Halloween Mayhem? Though things are exciting already\u2026<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> \u201cBut what if they did?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana\u2019s player made a roll for Tatiana to think to do some creative forgeries on the recovered papers to benefit the group. There was a hilarious IC conversation where she kept repeating \u201cBut what if they did?\u201d and several of the group took a moment to grok what she meant by that. It was funny.<br /> <br /> Not so much happened due to the combats, they took a fair chunk of the session. But I did promise more combat this story, and there is more to be had. The Belial\u2019s Brood mainly had physical disciplines, and low Blood Potency. Shock troops.<br /> <br /> The main non-combat part is Susie. She is of the Seventh Generation, but has never encountered the Lucifuge. Wolfram knew of it due to a monstrous occult roll. The Lucifuge as a group won\u2019t be a plot, yet\u2026though it could happen in the future, depending on what happens with Susie. Her knowledge is non-Christian, pertaining to the Chinese Hells. She referred to Sin-Eaters as people who escaped the line into Hell. <br /> <br /> Next session we finish Halloween night, and the Vampire arm of the story. Then we fire the shots for war between the Pure and Watch, and have the Changelings decide what, if anything, to do with the detente between Skadi and Sascha and Woebegone. <br /> <br /> See you then, Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:18:57-07:00","id":971201,"title":"","content":"Halloween Night. The battle of the Reistag. Belial\u2019s Brood, deprived of their Vanguard, still makes their play to crush Berlin\u2019s vampires. But a motley group of Supernatural Creatures creeps from the shadows toward their flank.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 31 October, 1922<br /> <br /> Well, the evening did not start out interesting for Dearbhail, Lizette, Alla or Fenric. They went to the club and listened to music and enjoyed themselves. At one point Oneida took the group to the back to warn them that Della is a dangerous creature and that they should stay away from her. She also warned the group about the roving bands of Belial\u2019s Brood that were out and about attacking people. She advised them to stay indoors or travel in a good sized group for protection. I am happy that they did not meet up with any Vampires on their way to the club. Granted, Alla is a fierce combatant and would have been able to protect the group, but the other Vampires were using fire and Alla does not laugh when fire is involved like the Belial\u2019s Brood does.<br /> <br /> So, we all met up at the Hedge Maze and discussed our options for the evening, and asked Sascha if he would be able to heal Tatiana and I from some of the injuries that we took from the earlier fight. He was accommodating as usual and worked his magic. What he was not able to heal with his gifts was soon healed by our natural ability. After that was taken care of Alla told us that she had received word that Belial\u2019s Brood would be making a large scale attack against the Reichstag. All told there was supposed to be close to 30 Vampires attacking the building. We discussed our options. We agreed that we would help the city, and the city\u2019s Kindred, and protect the Reichstag. The options that were presented to us were join the Kindred in an all-out attack on the front line, or stay to the rear and attack those that fled from the fight. We came up with a third option. We decided that we would flank the enemy and attack them from a place that they were not expecting. The Belial\u2019s Brood had also summoned a demon to fight for them. Tatiana and I planned to aid one another fighting Kindred until we reached the demon. At which point that would become our main target. The first thing we did after that was ask Ochran\u0144y to lend us her strength and she helped by giving us the ability to shrug off wounds, at least a little bit. Then because Lizette was still hurt from our encounter with the Claimed the other night, Ochran\u0144y possessed the diminutive woman. Lizette\u2019s eyes glowed yellow and stayed that way through the end of the fight.<br /> <br /> The rest of us also prepared for battle. Wolfram grabbed the arcane sword that inflicts greater wounds on Kindred and then set himself and the sword on fire. The flames were not visible to human eyes, but they were there. Lizette gathered her chainsaws. One of them she held in her hands and set the blade on fire. She also had her second chainsaw with her. This one she animated so it would act of its own accord during the fight. Everyone else prepared for the fight as well. Nobody else was on fire though, which seemed to be a theme with some of my pack mates. Tatiana and I dressed in clothes that were good for fighting, as did the others. We planned for Dacian and Dearbhail to stay to the rear of the fight and act as support. Dacian is good at blinding the enemy and Dearbhail can heal from a distance should the need arise. They are not front line combatants.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was the key to our fight. He wielded the sword that hurts Vampires, and they knew it. They hate that blade and usually attack the person holding it. That was the point. Wolfram is uniquely able to shrug off injuries that would leave anyone else reeling. Just as the other Claimed shrugged off injury in a plume of white smoke, so did Wolfram. He also used the sword to good effect, dealing out injury left and right. He managed to attract the attention of most of the Kindred, some of which were far more powerful than the run of the mill shock troops. One of those more powerful Kindred hit Wolfram hard, and he started to actually bleed. I saw this out of the corner of my eye, but could do nothing to interfere. I was too wrapped up in enemies of my own to go and help him. Dearbhail did her job well though, and healed Wolfram when his injuries started to become too bad. One enemy with a pentagram carved into his chest attacked Wolfram and used some special gift because the hit actually made my friend stagger and grip his chest. Wolfram later said that it felt like the Kindred was trying to pull out his very soul. This enemy did not remain standing much longer after that between the combined efforts of my pack mates.<br /> <br /> Lizette was a force to behold. She swung her flaming chainsaw with deadly accuracy, sometimes killing enemies with a single hit. Her secondary chainsaw, that she had animated, also did its share of injuries but not to the extent that Lizette did herself. Because she was so effective at taking down shock troops she did not really have to worry about them attacking her. They either fell to her blade or decided that she was not a good target. In the end it worked out well for my friend. She was not injured any more than she had been previously.<br /> <br /> Dacian and Dearbhail acted as support for the rest of us, blinding the enemy, making them temporarily less effective in the fight or healing people. They stayed to the rear and were thankfully not attacked. I got the impression that Dacian felt like he should have been more effective in the fight, but I did not see him as being a liability in the least. Everyone has their own strengths and weaknesses. Compared to Tatiana I am not very good in a hand to hand fight. She inflicts injuries in ways that I just can\u2019t. My skill is in my stealth. I can attack an enemy without them seeing me, or I can snipe them from a distance. I am skilled with a rifle and have used that to my advantage on several occasions. Dacian for his part is better at sneaking into places and acquiring things than hurting people. That is not a failing on his part. So, for this fight we had Dacian and Dearbhail stick together. Tonight it was not advisable for any of us to be alone since the Belial\u2019s Brood were very good at covering great distances in a very short time and would be able to take out any of us that were by ourselves. This is also why I did not snipe the enemy during this fight.<br /> <br /> Suzie even showed up to the fight. I\u2019m not sure how she knew something was happening, but she showed up dressed in black Chinese clothes and stood on a rooftop throwing flames down on the demon that had been summoned by Belial\u2019s Brood. The flames that she threw seemed to scream in an ear splitting way. I could even hear it over the sound of Lizette\u2019s chainsaws. Anyway, the demon was an impressive sight and Tatiana decided that was going to be her ultimate target. Suzie did her part in wounding it before my fellow Uratha could get to the demon. Our new Chinese friend left the fight as soon as the demon fell. From what Wolfram said of the Suzie\u2019s particular kind of supernatural individual, they fight demons, and that is exactly what Suzie did tonight. I had not expected her to show up at all, so she was a nice surprise.<br /> <br /> Marissa was also there fighting alongside my pack mates. She did not like the sword that Wolfram was wielding, but she managed to put her dislike aside and concentrate her attacks on the leaders of the enemy Kindred troops. She had what I\u2019m assuming was some sort of magic book and she used her gifts to good effect injuring the enemy. Though the wounds she inflicted were not physical they were effective nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Tatiana and I made a path to the demon. We fought through several storm troops first though. It was mainly Tatiana and her impressive strength that took down the enemies that we fought. Once we got to the demon we changed our tactics somewhat. I did not go straight in to hurt the demon, but instead used a flanking maneuver to confuse and slow the creature, making it more susceptible to Tatiana\u2019s furious blows. In the end Suzie and Tatiana managed to injure the demon enough that I was able to take it down with one well-placed strike. I will admit to being a little surprised that it was my attack that finished the creature off. Tatiana had been hitting it with such strength I thought for sure that she would land the killing blow. I am not complaining though. It was rather satisfying to take down such an impressive foe with my claws.<br /> <br /> After we took down the demon the fight was not over. There were still enemies to engage and Tatiana and I did just that. We split up our attacks so we were not doubling up on enemies any more. I went after the shock troops as did Tatiana. I will admit that I was riding on a bit of an adrenaline high after taking down the demon. Tatiana was attacking the enemy to good effect. At one point she switched forms to Gauru and went into Basu-Em. I managed to resist the rage. Though It was only a matter of time before she lost control so I kept a careful eye on her. She took out her targets with a practiced ease, including one of the leaders. The man had impressive claws of his own, and used them to good effect, but they failed him against Tatiana. Once the fight was over I shouted to everyone in a guttural voice to run and proceeded to make a target of myself and lead the raging Tatiana away from the rest of the pack. Having a raging werewolf chase you is disconcerting even if you are Uratha. I was able to keep a level head however and kept us away from areas that were too heavily populated by humans or Pure. It was something of a zigzagged path, but it was effective. Once the rage wore off Tatiana and I switched forms and ran back to the Hedge Maze to meet up with the others.<br /> <br /> At the club the others sought out Sascha in order to be healed of their injuries. It was mainly Wolfram that was taking advantage of his skills as a healer. Some of my pack-mate\u2019s wounds sounded pretty bad, but Sascha was able to heal them up a good bit before he had to stop. Later in the evening Wolfram did his trick where he set himself on fire in order to heal the rest of the way. I will admit that the Claimed ability to shrug off injury in a fight and heal afterward is impressive. Wolfram is not one to seek out a fight, but if he so desired he and Tatiana would be a force to be reckoned with.<br /> <br /> Also after the fight Alla left to meet up with the allied Kindred and compare notes and share news. I guess we will find out more of what happened at her meeting when she gets back. Meanwhile, Wolfram told Sascha about having been invited by the Black Company to sit in on the talks with the \u201cPure\u201d tomorrow. It was only sensible to warn him, since he will be involved so heavily in the talks, that one of our own would be on the other side of it. After the explanation of why Wolfram would be aiding the Black Company Sascha just nodded his understanding. Throughout our time at the Hedge Maze Lizette was staying close to Wolfram. It is no secret that she has feelings for our Claimed pack member, and she decided to keep close to him in case he should need anything. I think towards the end of the evening Tatiana decided that things had gone far enough and she picked up Wolfram, then Lizette and headed back towards our house. I just shrugged and picked up Lizette\u2019s extra chainsaw and followed them to the house. The others came along in short order and we were all able to rest for the evening. Once back at the house Wolfram did that fire trick to heal the rest of the way.<br /> <br /> Overall that was a good fight. There were some injuries, but that is the price we pay for getting involved in such a large scale battle. Thankfully none of the injuries were lasting. We all walked away and no one had to find out just how the Golden Eagle works. I believe that even Tatiana was satisfied with that fight. The only problem with the whole thing is if it will be mentioned by the press at all, or if it will just be chalked up to being a riot in the streets on Halloween. I guess time will tell on that count. I do not remember seeing any mortal bystanders, but I do have to admit that my attention was rather centered on the fight and those involved in it. I will need to talk to the others and see if they noticed any witnesses that might have seen what happened. It would be good if people abided by the Police\u2019s warnings and stayed indoors while the trouble was going on. But, as I said, time will tell on that count. We\u2019ll know more when the papers come out.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 1 November 1922<br /> <br /> Greta came by this morning to pay us a visit, so we filled her in on what had happened last night. I\u2019m not entirely sure if she was sorry that she\u2019d missed the fight, or that she\u2019d missed the opportunity to take pictures of all the supernatural people involved in the battle. She might not have been interested in fighting, at least in the last fight that we had with the Claimed she stayed to the background and only provided support when the need was dire. She is effective in a fight, but I don\u2019t think that she is as keen as Tatiana to get into them. There was also some light teasing on Lizette\u2019s part. She continued to rib Greta for allowing Marissa to feed from her. This has happened in the past. Greta denies having any interest in women, but is obviously keen to spend time with our Kindred friend. I do not understand why she denies this. I suppose it is just that part of human nature that I do not understand.<br /> <br /> We also discussed our plans for today. Greta was going to go to the market and scope out defensible positions that the Watch may use later in the day. But before our Claimed friend could go to the market we had Dacian use his skills to disguise her so she will not be recognized. I thought he did a very good job making her look Ottoman. Her skin is a shade darker and her hair is hidden under a scarf. He is very good when it comes to disguise. The one time that I had him disguise me when I was going to meet with Wolf blooded in the city I almost didn\u2019t recognize myself when I looked in the mirror. Dacian also left to go to the market with Greta. He is going to stay to the shadows and not be seen at all. That is another of his specialties. If the timing had worked out better, I would have gone to the market in place of Dacian. I am good at finding defensible positions in pretty much any environment. But, things did not work out that way. I need to be ready to go to the meeting with Tatiana and Sascha, which is coming up shortly. The only other thing that we really discussed was Dearbhail getting ready for her show tonight. It is interesting how easily she can switch from support in a fight to performer in a show. She has versatility that I do not. I will report later on how the rest of the day\u2019s activities go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Peace, volchonok, I am well.<br /> <br /> I promise you, none of the vampires nor their pet demon harmed me enough to overcome my ability to heal on my own.<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, you do smell burning.<br /> <br /> Well, Wolfram was injured. He had the sword that angers vampire after all, the one Dacien stole from Gunnar, the Pure in Vienna. So he set himself on fire.<br /> <br /> He will feel better after, he says.<br /> <br /> Foolish volchonok, why would Lizette light herself on fire? I mean, unless she was wrestling someone. Or one of her machines broke. Or she was doing experiments. OK, perhaps you are not foolish for that question. But she is not injured, and she is not a Sin-Eater, so she is not on fire now.<br /> <br /> She has been fussing over Wolfram since I saw them at the Hedge Maze.<br /> <br /> I believe she enjoyed the fighting, but for Wolfram\u2019s injuries. She did make good use of Ochranny\u2019s blessing, with her flaming chainsaw. The hopping chainsaw did well also.<br /> <br /> They also used fairy magic, Dacian and Dearbhail. Dearbhail cursed the enemies and healed Wolfram, and it was much easier to hit the clawed one after Dacien blinded it.<br /> <br /> I did not enter Kuruth because he was blind, what sense does that make volchonok? I lost myself in the kill is all. One death flowed from another and there was just the rage.<br /> <br /> You were lucky, volchonok, that Marek got my attention. You should be careful, following so close when I rage.<br /> <br /> Our alpha is well able to lead me away from innocents without the aid of foolish volchonoks.<br /> <br /> Oh, yes, there was much fighting before the rage. I fought a demon, did you see?<br /> <br /> Yes, Marek and Suzie did help and Marek hit him last. But I tore an arm off. And I finished off the clawed officer and many of the soldiers.<br /> <br /> You are impertinent, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, the good vampires did win. I think. The others said Alla went off to speak with them.<br /> <br /> No, that does not mean it is time to fun. There is much to do tomorrow. Now is the time to rest and the time for running is later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 1 November 1922<br /> <br /> Halloween Night ended with a bang. I have slain more vampires, this time with my chainsaw. I used the tricks of my Seeming to animate one chainsaw to fight independently, and the other I enhanced with my magics to fight for me better. Despite being good at evading, the chainsaw almost guided itself and I managed to hit several with my flaming chainsaw of doom. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> It helped that Wolfram was there to use his magic sword to draw almost all of the vampires wrath upon him. He was an absolute bulwark, and difficult to hit, so the Vampires rarely hurt him much, only those particularly powerful stood a chance. One did attack his soul, though, and that was not okay. He is Catholic, it belongs to God.<br /> <br /> Marissa Sangiovanni was there, and even she was giving Wolfram dirty looks while he used the sword, as was Alla. Still, she used her Necromancy to attack the animating forces of the vampires, while Dacian used his Darkling magic to blind them (and occasionally his bow, to little effect). Dearbh\u00e1il cursed enemies and healed us when needed. Marek and Tatiana fought in their wolfish battle forms. Tatiana was especially deadly.<br /> <br /> They had summoned a large demonic creature, because vampires are largely evil. Tatiana went right for it as Tatiana is largely fearless. Susie showed up and hurled white fire at it from a building, which injured it; Tatiana soon distracted it, and when it died Suzie withdrew from the fight. Apparently she does not care one way or the other about Vampires. She wore Chinese clothes this time, as opposed to the western clothes she had on earlier. I wonder what she will be dressed as tomorrow.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Vampires were victorious, and while Alla dealt with them the rest of us went to The Hedge Maze, where Prince Sascha did more healing. Tatiana has her blood madness, so she and Marek were late while he lead her away. The rest of us mostly sat quietly, and in the case of we Changelings restored Glamour. Marissa tried to pick up Oneida for biting without success. In the end, we retired.<br /> <br /> Tatiana carried Wolfram and I hope. Largely to show off. Which is fine\u2026its not like she picked me up thinking I looked like a child. She picked up Wolfram first. It was fun, I suppose. I won\u2019t admit that though.<br /> <br /> Coating weapons in fire seems effective against vampires. I had been thinking about my blade hat anyway, I wonder how a hat made of spinning blades on fire would work. It might sling accelerant though. I can find something. Or maybe scythe blades from a car. Hmmmmm\u2026.<br /> <br /> This morning we worked out the schedule for all souls day. Tatiana, Marek, and Wolfram will be taking part in the negotiations between the \u201cPure\u201d and the Schwarze Reichswehr, with help from Prince Sascha. Then we meet Susie and deal with the ambush in the market. Greta showed up (having been Marissa\u2019s chew toy) unaware of the night\u2019s events, and will (with Dacian) be scouting the market. Tonight Dearbh\u00e1il performs at The Hedge Maze, so she will be going to work on that.<br /> <br /> I will be working on cleaning and repairing my chainsaw from being on fire and carving the undead, but also thinking. I had worried about hating Wolfram when he and Christina got married, but seeing him hurt I became deeply worried about him. I had trouble leaving his side. Much like, not long ago, he carried me into <u>The Hedge Maze</u> himself. It is hard to imagine having feelings for a German, especially a German man. They did, after all, invade my homeland, slaughter my countrymen, and kill my family. And Wolfram was an invader; he was not toiling on his farms, but attacking my countrymen from the air. It is hard to forget he was once my enemy. But now? His treatment of me injured, and mine of him have given me a lot to think about\u2026or avoid thinking about at all costs.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I need to be prepared for the combat this afternoon. I am still hurt from my first battle with Die Wacht. I need to not be so careless next time. But I do look forward to my chainsawing! Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Just be careful Lizette. Physically and Emotionally.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXVII</i><br /> <br /> I am really late and sleep depping, so summery, but questions are fine.<br /> <br /> The vampires each had a small amount of Choronzon, Vigor, Resilience and Celerity. They came in sort of waves, with a more powerful Kindred with them. The Demon was a largish one based on Inferno. The battle was long, and sort of spectacular. Wolfram\u2019s use of the sword meant he could \u201ctank\u201d a large number of Kindred, with his Manifestations he was rarely hit and damage was often dealt with. Lizette was able to obscene damage, having buffed her chainsaw attack pool to around 21 dice, and with the firey chainsaw inflicting aggravated damage to the Kindred. She was (fortunately) kept safe by Wolfram\u2019s taking the heat.<br /> <br /> Marissa was using Cattiveria, Ultimo Respiro specifically, to attack, some of the leftover Plasm going to Wolfram. She managed to avoid attacking him, Marissa is stubborn with high Resistance stats and was okay. Her power was slightly enhanced by the<i> Voce Della Morte</i>, a book she had with her that allowed her to use Ultimo Respiro on a given target a number of times per night equal to her Blood Potency. They managed to funnel a lot of damage with their plans to have Wolfram use the weapon.<br /> <br /> Next time an ambush in the market as they try to make sure the Watch know their enemies are the Werewolves. One more (probably) huge battle for this story as it begins to wind down. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-17-2016, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:29:15-07:00","id":978889,"title":"","content":"All Souls Day<br /> <br /> The ambush at the bazaar is itself ambushed, as Suzy has allies and is more dangerous than she appears. However, as the group works on completing their business, they find no consensus on how to act regard the Courts of the Fey, and a burgeoning relationship is cast into doubt. <br /> <i><br /> Session XXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 1 November 1922<br /> <br /> The rest of today went pretty much as planned. Tatiana, Sascha and I met up with the Black Company representatives and Wolfram. They sent one of their leaders, Wolfgang Von Ingersleben and another man whose name escapes me at the moment. Sascha made an impressive entrance by making himself appear larger and hairier as he walked in the door and then slimming down to his natural body shape. I think the ruse worked rather well. And occasionally during the talks his eyes would flash almost golden as if the wolf were peeking through. His performance was more than enough to fool the Claimed as they negotiated with Sascha. Wolfram also did an admirable job playing the interested Occultist. I tried to give him opportunities to react off something that I did or said and he did so with great skill. All told I think the talks went well. We worked out an agreement with the Black Company that they will not interfere with the business of the Pure and that the violence between those two groups would cease. We did not say anything about the Watch, but we did stress the Black Company, so hopefully they will not see any agreements broken if something occurs with the Watch. <br /> <br /> After that we all went to the Market. Tatiana, Alla and I each manned one of the three entrances to the market and rigged the entrance with a rope of caltrops that Lizette designed. We learned from Greta and Dacian that an attack by car would be the most likely strategy. There were no good sniping positions in the area. There was too much in the way of line of sight to get a reliable shot off at anywhere in the market from one stationary location. The market was accessible by three different entrances though, all of which were wide enough to accommodate an automobile. So, we took up position at our three locations, Tatiana to the North, Alla to the West and me in the South. The three of us being the fastest runners, we could make it to any of the other two entrances without taking too much time. Dacian, Wolfram and Lizette planned to be in the middle of the market posing as shoppers. They would be able to make it to the entrance that the Watch came by fairly quickly. Dearbhail and Greta agreed to accompany Suzie as she shopped and generally made a target out of herself. <br /> <br /> As it turned out cars came from two sides, the North and the South. I heard that there were two people in the car that came in Tatiana\u2019s entrance. There were three in the car that came through mine. Tatiana apparently jumped the car before it could even make it to the caltrops and proceeded to impose physical violence upon their persons. I let my car hit the caltrops, waited until the car had stopped and just reached in and pulled one of the gunners out through the window. I got shot for my trouble, but shrugged off the injuries a moment later when I shifted to Guaru form. The others that had been in the center of the market split up to help both Tatiana and myself. Alla and Dacian headed North. The rest headed south, including Suzie. I was not expecting her to want to jump into another fight, but she came. At some point the second shooter got out of the car and tried to fire at me to no avail. His gun would not function. I believe Lizette was behind that. She has a talent for making mechanical things not work properly. Wolfram did his part as well by hitting the car that the driver was in the process of literally merging with. I did not know that some Claimed individuals could do that.<br /> <br /> While I was dealing with the man I\u2019d pulled out of the car several things were going on around me. Apparently Dearbhail cursed one of the gunners that Wolfram shot at. Lizette was disabling firearms left and right, which was greatly appreciated. Several of us would have been shot, including Suzie if she hadn\u2019t done that. Suzie for her part threw fire at the car which certainly gave the driver something new to worry about. At some point during all of this the driver even tried to run me down with the car. I managed to stop it before it could hit me or anyone else for that matter. I think the driver was a little surprised at that turn of events. I just smiled and continued what I was doing. The driver later tried to hit Suzie but missed. She then threw more fire at the car and hit it pretty squarely. The driver was thrown from the car. I changed targets and went for the driver. The guy I\u2019d been fighting was clearly looking to run and was going to let him. The plan, like last time we dealt with the Claimed, was to leave them alive so random innocents do not die later so they can come back. Last time I reacted out of anger and killed one of the fleeing Claimed. I was determined this time to reign myself in.<br /> <br /> Around this time those that had been in the North arrived and lent their aid. Most of the guys were running. Dacian, who\u2019d been carried on Tatiana\u2019s back, jumped off and fired his bow at one of the fleeing me. He used a gift to make the arrow do more damage than usual and ended up killing the man. I do not know if it was his intent to do that or if it was an accident. Alla picked up the driver and threw him after his friend who was still running. He quickly got up and followed the other guy out of the market. Since we suddenly had a body to deal with we decided to bring it to the Watch\u2019s meeting place and leave the man propped up by the door with an intimidating note attached to his clothes. I\u2019d say that sends a pretty clear message if you ask me.<br /> <br /> As we were going out separate ways Suzie offered to lend us her aid if we had need of it in the future while we\u2019re in town. I believe this was her way of paying us back for saving her at the market. We nodded our assent and went our separate ways. Wolfram went to the airport to pick up his brother Heinrich who was coming to town to visit. We then all met up at the Hedge Maze to hear Dearbhail perform. <br /> <br /> While Dearbhail was singing Queen Woebegone came in and sat down next to Sascha and they started talking. I admit that my curiosity was piqued so I decided to listen in. Turns out that Woebegone was informing Sascha that the Autumn Court had made a move against Queen Skadi last night. The Winter Queen was not happy. She apparently called for a meeting of the monarchs, but Woebegone was advising Sascha that they should not go and that it was likely to be a trap. They were planning on waiting to see what happens. To see if anyone tries to usurp Skadi\u2019s position or not. Woebegone, and Sascha for his part, were worried about possible reprisals from Skadi against the club. The Autumn Queen also said that their allies (us) have already done enough heavy lifting lately. I suppose it is a mark in her favor that she was not going to try and lever us against Skadi and take sides in their personal war.<br /> <br /> Sascha then talked to Oneida about what Woebegone had said and what had happened. They discussed Skadi and how they can continue to disrupt her plans to take over Berlin. They were talking about whether or not they should just kill the Winter Queen. I\u2019ll admit that I was a little surprised that Sascha would be having such a conversation. He seems like a fairly non-violent type, but then looks can be deceiving. I know better than to assume that someone is not a danger just because they are slight in build or young. Lizette is incredibly dangerous and yet someone just looking at her would assume she couldn\u2019t possibly do anyone harm. You never can tell what lurks just beneath the surface. <br /> <br /> Also during the show Alla\u2019s \u201csister\u201d vampire Hilde showed up to talk to my packmate. The other woman wanted to know who she shouldn\u2019t feed off of and what favor Alla might ask of the Prince in return for her/our help in dealing with the Belial\u2019s Brood vampires. Alla advised Hilde from feeding on anyone that was pack and gave our names, as well as some of our closer allies like Greta. As for the boon, I believe Alla asked for safe passage to and from the city in the future. Since we have a house here it seemed prudent to get the Prince\u2019s word on such a thing considering her group is not favored in Berlin. <br /> <br /> Later after the performance we all went back to the house and I told the pack what I had overheard from Sascha and Woebegone. To say that Dacian was upset is an understatement. He was seriously unhappy about it, though he wasn\u2019t overly vocal about his irritation. He did express his anger that we might have been used as a distraction so they could attack Skadi though. Lizette thought that we, or at least she, should support Woebegone since she is the Autumn Queen, and my packmate is in the Autumn Court. I think she assumed that Dearbhail and Dacian would automatically support Sascha for the same reason. I am not sure that us getting in involved will end well for us. If everyone supported their own court monarch things would be cut and dry, but they don\u2019t. Dacian clearly has feelings for Skadi so he does not want to side against her. In that case the pack would be divided and things could get ugly. <br /> <br /> I could be persuaded to go with a diplomatic plan and try and get Sascha and Skadi together to hash something out. We would make sure that we were present as an interested but non-involved party to make sure things stay peaceful. Woebegone has already proven that she has active plans to move against Skadi and has rejected offers of a peace talk between the monarchs. She would be counterproductive to the whole situation. I do not know if Skadi and Sascha would want to talk, but it might be possible. The point to bargaining a peace would be to help do what was right for Berlin. Not necessarily what was right for each of the courts, but what was right for the people. Skadi had expressed an interest in doing what was right for the people, though her methods may be seen as harsh. I do not know if Woebegone or Sascha has done much of anything other than support themselves. I think that Sascha believes that his clubs will generate hope and inspire the people to be happy again. Woebegone thinks that she can do something through her films. Their actions however so far have just been to go after Skadi. I don\u2019t know who is right, and which side would actually be better for Berlin. I just see tensions mounting and my friends taking sides.<br /> <br /> Marissa\u2019s whole take on this was that we should just pick a side and then influence that side into being the right one. Greta got seriously upset by this attitude. She said that attitude would just make us as bad as them, and then she stormed out of the room. I actually kind of agree with Greta on that point. Just picking a side and declaring ourselves the right side would put us on a slippery slope. That kind of attitude has been used too many times in the past to justify wars or conflicts that ended into too many people getting killed. I may not have much in the way of empathy for people outside of my pack, but even I know that war, while sometimes inevitable, leads to entirely too many innocent deaths. I saw too many people I actually cared about killed in the Great War. I don\u2019t feel like watching my friends go through the same thing as the Seasonal courts battle between themselves and possibly kill each other. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What? Volchonok, I missed nothing!<br /> <br /> Oh. No, Greta was not crying because she got injured in the fighting. She was just heart-hurt and angered.<br /> <br /> By Marissa. She is very much a vampire. And sometimes Greta forgets this.<br /> <br /> I mean that Greta is an idealist and Marissa is... not.<br /> <br /> Marissa thinks we should simply pick a side in the fairy fight and because we are the good ones, it will be the right side and we will gain power so it is good. Greta thinks that a side is not right just because we say it is, that power is not good just because we have it. And is hurt and angry because she thought Marissa better than that.<br /> <br /> I agree with Greta. Marissa sounds like the generals who say we fight for what is right and send others to be killed for the betterment of generals and their friends.<br /> <br /> Bah, I do not know volchonok. Skadi seems reasonable, I like Sascha and the sad scary queen makes my hackles rise. I do not like the way Marek said Sascha spoke of the sad scary one, as if she had hold over him. I think they should speak, Sascha and Skadi at least.<br /> <br /> Because I do not want another war where soldiers will die, even if it is just Germany being pinned by the other countries. If something has the slightest chance to cause such a thing, it should be stopped. But apparently it is too difficult and we know nothing and should just give up.<br /> <br /> No, I am not a fairy replacement. I merely mock Wolfram.<br /> <br /> He was rolling over and showing his belly. Lizette thinks it is easy and we should support her sad scary queen.<br /> <br /> I do not know what we will do. We are sleeping on it.<br /> <br /> It was a long day after all. We spoke to the Black Company of staying out of the fight between the Pure and the Watch.<br /> <br /> Sascha was very good, yes. If one knew very little of werewolves, he would be very convincing.<br /> <br /> Alright, volchonok, yes, even if one knew more than very little, he was convincing.<br /> <br /> I believe they will stay out, yes.<br /> <br /> No, impertinent volchonok, that was not a long day by itself. We also fought Sin-Eaters who were trying to kill Suzi.<br /> <br /> I thought I saw you there! You should not bait me so.<br /> <br /> It was an excellent fight, was it not?<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, you should not try the car thing, you are not big enough. It takes bulk to roll across the muzzle of a car and rip a door off. Especially when it is a car possessed by a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> No, I said especially. You should leave all cars alone. They are dangerous for foolish volchonoks.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, you can play with the door. It is mine now. It is only moving cars that are dangerous.<br /> <br /> I did think about leaving it with the dead Sin-Eaters and the note pretending to be from the Pure, but it was my trophy, so I did not.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we were supposed to not kill them, but Dacien\u2019s thorn arrow flew very true at the one who ran.<br /> <br /> We caused them much damage and cost them many resources. It was an effective sortie even so, yes.<br /> <br /> I am sure the sight of Dacian clinging to the car door around my neck as we ran through the market was very amusing. It was the fastest way to get to the other ambush too.<br /> <br /> I do not think amusing or tasty was what Alla was going for. I think she was intending to be frightening.<br /> <br /> She was not dressed as a bird. That is what doctors used to wear when you were dying.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, she was dressed up as a human thing. It is a mask, so the sun stayed away, yes?<br /> <br /> Well, it was dark for Dearbhail\u2019s singing, so Alla did not need a mask.<br /> <br /> I meant outside, foolish volchonok. Inside lights are not the same as the sun, especially for vampires.<br /> <br /> It was very good singing, of course. And good company - Wolfram\u2019s brother joined us, and Sascha made much of him. Greta and Marissa were there of course. <br /> <br /> They were not our company, Alla\u2019s sister and the sad scary queen.<br /> <br /> Alla speaks with many people, that does not make them company. And Oneida seemed to like Alla\u2019s sister, so she is perhaps not bad company.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was there that Marek heard Sascha and the sad scary queen speaking of attacking Skadi last night.<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, it is certainly confusing.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, going running would be much better than dealing with fairy politics. But for now we sleep, so we can make decisions in the morning. And perhaps cement the hatred for the Pure. That will be fun at least, no? <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 2nd November, 1922<br /> <br /> Another day, another battle.<br /> <br /> This time in the bazaar. Tatiana, Marek, Wolfram and Sascha apparently had a good old time pulling Wolfgang\u2019s leg. But the results were to our liking, The Schwarze Reichswehr will have no idea they haven\u2019t averted a war, and we can focus on Die Wacht. Dacian and Greta did an excellent job scouting the bazaar, and together came up with some excellent plans, credit where it is due.<br /> <br /> The bazaar is a big area of stalls, with a lot of people from areas of Asia especially selling various stuff from home. It was crowded, smoky and fragile, low visibility, crowded\u2026great place for a battle. Except terrible for a battle. Collateral damage would be huge. So our goal was to ambush them before they got in, and they would almost certainly be using cars and guns.<br /> <br /> There were three ways into the bazaar. Marek took the South way, Alla West, and Tatiana North. Those three are the fastest on foot. The rest of us clustered into the middle. We had tire shredders we could pull up when their cars arrived, as they could wreck all sorts of destruction with their cars in the thin stalls of the bazaar. They could light them on fire and cause untold destruction, which could have an amazing lightshow and amount of destruction. If an enemy bazaar were there, I could wreck all sorts of havoc with a car with a flamethrower. <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, we expected them to come from one direction, but they came from two. Three came up from the South while two came from the North. Susie had arrived with Greta and Dearbh\u00e1il in tow, but she was not about to stay out of trouble. When Marek engaged in the South, Wolfram and I charged down with her, as did Susie and Dearbh\u00e1il. Tatiana and Alla fought in the North, with Dacian. They used Thompsons, and some merged with their cars. It was funny how Marek just pulled one of the shooters out the window, though.<br /> <br /> In the end, the ambushed Bound had little chance. Tatiana defeated her two opponents, then yanked Dacian down and helped Marek with clean up. I sabotaged their guns, which helped. Dacian did kill one though\u2026he tends to overexert himself. He used a Contract on the wounded Bound, so I know it was deliberate. Can\u2019t resist assassination I suppose.<br /> <br /> But the people were protected, even if terrified. Die Wacht weakened, we just need to move on to cementing this and we need a plan. Preferably involving Mayhem.<br /> <br /> We celebrated that night while Dearbh\u00e1il sang. It was wonderful, as always. Sascha was cheerful after his deception. He seemed to enjoy talking to Heinrich, who Wolfram had brought down for the show. The Queen Woebegone arrived for him, however, and his mood dampened, and did Marek\u2019s. Apparently Woebegone launched some sort of strike on Skadi, though I don\u2019t know the details. Fine with me. <br /> <br /> Still, cheer was high until we returned; we discussed what to do about the Fae. My feeling was if we intervened, we should on Woebegone and Sascha\u2019s side, though I was fine with not intervening. Dacian felt sure we should intervene, but seemed disinclined to settle on who. I know he was soft on Skadi, but Sascha is his Court and had allied with us. Marek disliked Woebegone, because of course he did. The most interesting thing, though, was Greta and Marissa. Marissa felt we should side with whomever seemed best to us and put them in our debt, as if we were such heroes than we could manipulate that side for good. Greta was horrified at the suggestion; she felt we should only choose whoever was best for Berlin. They argued fiercely, as if none of us were there; like a couple, passionately. Eventually Greta stormed off, and Tatiana followed. I decided no more was likely to be done, so retired. <br /> <br /> Wolfram followed. He knew I wanted to back Woebegone, though I don\u2019t see a strong reason to intervene. Dacian and Wolfram were especially insistent and Marek, in his way, dug in his heels. Meanwhile the spat with Greta and Marissa, which I think went beyond the subject, kept tensions high. I know Wolfram wanted to protect me, emotionally\u2026we will see what today brings.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Sascha used contracts of Mirror to alter his shape and give himself various features that seemed Wolfin. That and his acting skills and a little bit of costuming. <br /> <br /> Alla had gone to the studio and found a plague doctor costume from the theaters there. She the bird costume Tatiana was talking about was a plague doctor mask and cloak. GIS it if you don\u2019t know what they look like, terrifying. But kept the sunlight off.<br /> <br /> Lizette did spend time using Artifice to shut down guns. As the Sin-Eaters had not had time to power up (it was another ambush, after all) they were at a severe disadvantage. Even with their guns shut down and powers not yet active they still put up a strong fight, but after the ambush outside the cabaret, the Conspiracy was ready for them. Less with the car merging, but it really proved too little too late. Only wrinkle was the two directions thing; the Conspiracy had not prepared for that. But Tatiana was on the side getting less back up, and she is best at fighting, so it worked out. <br /> <br /> Just about done, then on to 1924. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:20:01-07:00","id":981155,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying this write up (with one mentioned deficiency) in no small part because it is so different from anything me or mine have done or I believe are capable of doing. I am starting to wonder if the Golden Eagle will play a real role or if it is simply a McGuffin to, as you have said, encourage the players to approach the real plot more aggressively.<br /> \u200bI have mentioned before that I would like to run a chronicle with the build up to and WWII as a backdrop and am really looking forward to how you play that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:51:47-07:00","id":981670,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply! Why is it different from what your group is capable of, out of curiosity?<br /> <br /> The plan (not set in stone) is for the Eagle to play more of a role later on, and have a role in the climax. For now it is a MacGuffin and yeah, less fear of character death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T23:16:24-07:00","id":981984,"title":"","content":"With my group I am lucky if I can get them to name their character, any personal details beyond that are either amusing accidents or my doing which never takes them much beyond being a hook. My group, myself included, may role play but we really aren't very good at 'role play', we're more puzzle solvers and tacticians (with a dose of power gaming thrown in so one half of the group can annoy the other half). So much of what your players write is pure character development be it relationships, playing out personal fears or prejudices. They even wrote histories that didn't amount to &quot;that's why I have a black belt and sniper skills&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:44:09-07:00","id":987384,"title":"","content":"Well both approaches are good, whichever people have fun with. I am much better at running this than a more action oriented game. It is nice to have both as options, I suppose. And yes, my players are 100% awesome.<br /> <br /> We begin the Denouement. Meetings with the Seasonal rulers and the hunt for Della<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 2 November 1922<br /> <br /> So, as Lizette suggested we \u201cslept on it.\u201d We then picked up our discussion of what to do with the Changeling Courts this morning. It took a little while, but we eventually came to the idea that we should get all three monarchs together to meet and to come to an agreement. Lizette suggested that we craft a Pledge that will be beneficial to all involved. And to a faerie their word is actually binding, especially if they use magic to back it up. So, we\u2019ll see how that goes. Greta also came by the house this morning. I believe that she is trying to stay away from her house so her father cannot corner her about the arranged marriage. I know that Greta does not want to be tied down in that way, especially to someone that she does not know or love. She also seemed to still be upset by what Marissa said last night about making our side \u201cright,\u201d but she didn\u2019t want to talk about it. <br /> <br /> Lizette also suggested to Tatiana and myself that we go to the burned out Pure club and see if we can find out where their new meeting place is. I thought this was a good idea and we went to the former Gentleman\u2019s club and started our search from there. We managed to follow a faint trail and followed it out of the main part of the city into the suburbs. It led to an old house. We looked around until we could figure out the address and then left. We did not want to be spotted checking the place out since that would give our eventual plans away. We eventually all met back up at our house and shared what we had learned.<br /> <br /> While we were tracking the Pure the others were busy dealing with Faerie business. Dearbhail and Wolfram went to go speak to Skadi. She expressed some concern about our well-being since it had been so long since we\u2019d been in contact with her. They assured her that we were fine, and that we\u2019d merely been busy. After some discussion my pack-mates managed to talk Skadi into agreeing to meet with Woebegone and Sascha. Her only stipulation was that we provide her with proof that Woebegone is not a Gentry. Apparently Woebegone just showed up one day in the Freehold and quickly rose to power. Skadi does not trust her fellow monarch or her intentions as far as she can throw her.<br /> <br /> Lizette, Alla and Fenric went to go meet with Woebegone. From what I gathered Lizette was rather blunt when talking to the Autumn Queen and just laid out plain what our intentions were and what we wanted to do. Woebegone said that she will meet but wants and oath of security to ensure her safety and possibly an oath for Sascha to keep him safe as well. She seems rather distrustful of Skadi as well. Lizette said that she would make an oath with Woebegone right before the meeting. Woebegone also insisted that any meeting of all three monarchs should take place at a neutral location. Lizette and Alla agreed that would be for the best and would let the monarch know where the meeting would be held.<br /> <br /> Dacian and Greta went to go talk to Sascha about setting up a meeting. Before any conversation got started Greta took Oneida aside to talk to her about some updated security issues dealing with the Watch. This left Dacian free to speak to Sascha in private. Sascha said that if his Queen (Woebegone) agreed to a meeting then he would too. He seemed rather adamant on that point. He would only attend if the Autumn Queen did as well. He also told Dacian why he was wary about meeting with Skadi. Apparently some time back, before he was the Spring King, Skadi was involved in a meeting with all the other monarchs. They were discussing the direction that Germany was going and who they supported. She did not support the Kaiser, they did. Things did not end well. Apparently Skadi killed all of the monarchs and their bodyguards all by herself. She is one of the oldest Changelings in the freehold, close to 200 years old by some accounts. This translates into power from what I understand of Faerie magic and gifts. So, Skadi is rather powerful and the other monarchs are afraid of her, or at least wary. Makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> So after all that we met up to discuss our options. Dacian suggested that at the start of the meeting with the Monarchs we all touch a piece of cold iron to prove that no one is a Gentry. It seems that the old stories are true and that the True Fae, as I\u2019ve heard the Gentry described as, are susceptible to cold iron. It hurts them. So just touching a piece of it would prove whether or not Woebegone is one of the Gentry. It would also serve to prove if any of the other Monarchs are True Fae as well. We also talked about where the meeting would take place. Someone suggested that we use our own house since we can control the environment and have a way out if needs be. If things go really badly Lizette can always just blow the house up and we\u2019ll come back. The monarchs would not. I suppose that means that we should not have anyone else involved in these talks, at least no one that can\u2019t survive should the worst case scenario be necessary.<br /> <br /> After our talk Dacian called Skadi and let her know that everyone will make a pledge, again something binding, to promise not to hurt anyone else and that makes sure everyone\u2019s concerns are being addressed. She seemed okay with that. Contingent of course on us proving that Woebegone is not a Gentry. Lizette called Woebegone and just flat out told her what our plans were, specifically about the cold iron. The Autumn Queen was not happy with it but agreed to touch the cold iron, but only as long as it was done in private with only us present. She did not want to do it in front of the other Monarchs. There was some discussion about why she would not want to do that, and the idea came up that she might have a glamour of some sort up altering her appearance and she did not want the others to know what she really looked like. She did agree to touch it, so it is likely that she is not one of the True Fae. Or if she is, she thinks she can take the pack on by herself. Given the stories it\u2019s likely. But given the stories she\u2019d be able to take the lot of us no matter who was present. So, we set up the meeting for tomorrow afternoon. The Monarchs were all informed of the plans and we moved on to other business for this afternoon, namely finding Della. While phone calls were being made Greta went on to leak the information about the Pure\u2019s address to the Watch. Apparently she has an alter ego, Nina, set up that she uses when she needs to find or distribute information around town. Makes sense to me. She is keen on learning things so she can expose the truth about those things to the masses. I may not agree with the kinds of things she wants to expose, but will admit that her alter ego is a handy thing to have around. I know mine is.<br /> <br /> Our next order of business was to deal with Della. We all talked out a vow that Della can take to ensure that she will not hunt human\u2019s, but she still gets something out of it. I\u2019ll admit that some of it went over my head. There apparently is a process that you need to go through to create a vow, or at least certain rules that you have to follow. Both sides should get something out of it and there needs to be a consequence if it is broken. There is probably more to it than that but like I said, some of it went over my head.<br /> <br /> After our talk we went to Saints and Sinners to talk to Sabine and see if anyone has seen Della. She had not seen the other woman and suggested that Della had fled to the river or a swamp. She suggested that if we were going to go looking for the mermaid that we bring wax or ear plugs to use to drown out her siren song. Apparently she can make it sound like a good idea to be eaten by her. Not how I want my day to end. She also advised us that if we should fight and kill her that we should not eat her flesh. The thought had not crossed my mind, but apparently there are myths concerning mermaid flesh and immortality. It usually leads to a horrible death though, so it\u2019s a bad idea all around. We thanked her for the advice and were about to go on our way. Sabine wished us luck and kind of suggested that she thought that we may have had something to do with the disappearance of the comb in the first place. We did not acknowledge her veiled accusation and nodded our thanks before leaving.<br /> <br /> Once we left the club Tatiana and I set about trying to track Della\u2019s scent. It\u2019s been a little while since the trail was left so it took us awhile to find her. We tracked her to a boat on the river. There were two humans on the boat. Once armed with a shotgun and one with a pistol. Just in case we ended up having to fight Della we split up so Tatiana could go back to the house and gather the others. I stayed to make sure that Della didn\u2019t go anywhere. I am used to waiting, hidden for my prey to come by. It was similar to just wait and watch the boat from the shadows.<br /> <br /> After some time, everyone arrived and we set out to learn what Della was up to. Since we were technically in public we decided that a fight might not be the best idea, especially since there were firearms in involved and they are loud. So, I snuck up on the two men guarding the boat and stepped out of the shadows behind them. To say they were startled is an understatement. While they were still reacting in panic, Tatiana jumped onto the deck of the boat and further scared the crap out of the two guards. They decided that fleeing was their best option and we let them go. There was no need to harm them anyway.<br /> <br /> Once on the boat we investigated and found that there were two doors below decks. One led to the Captains quarters and one led to the hold. Dacian picked the lock on the Captains door and found the room empty. There were just a few maps strewn across a table. Tatiana meanwhile kicked open the door that led to the hold and discovered a large tank of water with Della chained inside. As soon as Wolfram walked in she looked right at him and said \u201cHello Husband.\u201d Without missing a beat Dacian launched into his spiel about taking a pledge to not harm humans in exchange for her comb. She did not seem keen on taking the deal. She implied that she\u2019d rather go back to Holbien, that she trusts him. We agreed and she immediately broke the chains that held her and climbed out of the tank. Wolfram, being the gentlemen that he is, offered her his coat. I\u2019m not sure what Della\u2019s plans were for the two men that had been guarding the boat, but it was obvious that she was not there against her will. My guess is that she was waiting for a good time to make them disappear.<br /> <br /> As we were leaving we were confronted by a big guy and eight more thugs. Apparently the men that fled went to go find some allies and they all came back to the boat. I smiled at the poor fools and Tatiana intimidated them into leaving. It was over before anything could really start, and that was just fine. I\u2019ll admit that I was tempted to chase them, but there wasn\u2019t really a point to doing so, so I let them get away. I\u2019m not sure but Tatiana was probably thinking the same thing. At that point Lizette expressed an interest in blowing up the boat. I argued that blowing up the boat would cause the authorities to become involved and might make things more complicated for us. I suggested just letting Tatiana break the boat. We did not actually break it. We just left it with a couple of doors hanging on their hinges. <br /> <br /> When we arrived back at Saints and Sinners Dacian went in ahead of us to get Sabine to let us in through the side door. She did so and we all met up inside. Della went to her dressing room to change while we talked to Holbien, well Wolfram did the talking. We returned the comb to him and Wolfram explained that we managed to apprehend the one that stole the comb and get it back for him. Wolfram did not elaborate further on the supposed thief and Holbien didn\u2019t ask so we let it go. Della offered to give her former \u201chusband\u201d a kiss, which Wolram deferred. Wolfram suggested that Lizette might like the kiss instead, and so Della kissed our inventor. Lizette seemed to enjoy it. Also, in repayment of having returned the comb Wolfram asked Holbien if he had any Pure allies. Holbien said that he did not and that such a thing would be problematic for more than one reason. This could be a positive note for us. If he is not allied with the Pure then we might be able to count him as an ally for ourselves. That would be a boon for us. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we did go running without you.<br /> <br /> Well, you were watching over Dearbh\u00e1il...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m teasing you volchonok. It was only running in the city, and tracking a clumsy mermaid, anyway.<br /> <br /> We did not have a fight. I broke door and yelled at people, that is all. The humans were frightened away and the mermaid obeyed Wolfram.<br /> <br /> The singer of foolish songs, recall? Dacian let her escape when he stole the comb and this is bad because she eats people.<br /> <br /> Oh, well, yes, she is graceful on stage. She is clumsy out in the the city though.<br /> <br /> No, we did not kill her. Dacian tried to make a deal with her, but she preferred the Wolf Blooded. So we returned her and the comb.<br /> <br /> I believe he is an ally, yes, volchonok. We do not know for certain, but Wolfram was clever and asked if he could help us speak with those we knew were Pure. Holbein said those ones do not care for him and would look down on him for many reasons.<br /> <br /> It seems likely he is of our blood. Marek says we should let the fairies check a few things out first, tomorrow when we go to get our reward and hear Dearbh\u00e1il sing.<br /> <br /> The meeting with the fairy nobles is tomorrow as well, yes.<br /> <br /> Of course they listened to me. I am very wise.<br /> <br /> I will fight you, volchonok. <br /> <br /> Very well.<br /> <br /> They did blather on quite a bit. I almost thought they wouldn\u2019t listen to me after all, but they saw clearly eventually.<br /> <br /> We will try and convince them to agree to not work against each other and all work to stop another war.<br /> <br /> Bah, I do not know how they will do it, volchonok. But that is not my job.<br /> <br /> Yes, finding the Pure house was my job earlier and I did it well. With Marek, of course. But that had nothing to do with the fairies.<br /> <br /> I do have the better jobs.<br /> <br /> What? No, volchonok, that is not my job either. That is no one\u2019s job.<br /> <br /> The sad scary queen did refuse to touch the iron in public, but we will not be forcing her to. She agreed to in private.<br /> <br /> My job will be to stop anyone who tries to fight.<br /> <br /> By fighting them, of course. And fighting better.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it will be fun if someone tries to fight, but I do not think they will. If Skadi truly killed at the other monarchs, it would be a glorious fight, she and I. Anyways, it would be an unfortunate thing.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that means it will most likely be quite boring.<br /> <br /> No, I cannot run away instead. It is important. Soon though, volchonok. Soon we will be back to our home and then we will run.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 2nd November 1922<br /> <br /> Getting things wrapped up. Today we focused on finding Della and getting Changeling politics sorted out. Not so much Mayhem.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I just was ready to call it. Let the Bosch fight their own political battles. I don\u2019t see any affecting Paris. We had a long discussion that went in circles, until we settled on arranging a meeting with the Monarchs where a nonaggression pact would be hashed out. Even deciding ourselves took awhile. Meanwhile others set about finding a target for Die Wacht.<br /> <br /> Tatiana and Marek went to follow the trail from the burned out club. Dacian and Greta went to talk to Prince Sascha. Dearbh\u00e1il and Wolfram went to talk to Queen Skadi, Alla and I to Queen Woebegone. The Werewolves were successful; the pair found their way to a house that was likely of the Pure. Dearbh\u00e1il never lost her charms; Queen Skadi agreed if we prove Queen Woebegone is not Gentry. Dacian had an easier task; he convinced his on again off again that he should at least come if Woebegone does. <br /> <br /> The Queen of Illusion was our target. She met us with Rudolph. It was fairly clear she did not quite trust us, so I broke it down, one Wizened to another. I told her we needed the meeting, and asked her to give me one good Wizened reason not to have it. She was afraid it would be a trap, and asked me to make a Pledge to guard her. I agreed to that. We will make the Pledge before she gets there, though.<br /> <br /> We met together. It was decided Woebegone would need to touch cold iron to prove she was not Gentry. I called her, but she was very much against this. Eventually we talked it out, Wizened-to-Wizened and she agreed to it in private.<br /> <br /> Fairest my strut and Darklings may hide, but at the end of the day Wizened are the ones that keep things moving. And it is a little frustrating sometimes when the other Seemings bring their games into things. <br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> We went to <u>Saints and Sinners</u>. Greta met us, having set events with Die Wacht into motion with her alter ego \u201cNina,\u201d a well bred girl wanting to get the rot out of the Fatherland. Cunning girl. I have to admit some grudging respect for the minx. We decided to send out the werewolves to track Della, after Sabine had no ideas to check other than a river or swamp. <br /> <br /> After a little while they returned, having found a boat with her on it. Seemed strange. There were two human guards, but Tatiana drove them off with her loud personality. She and Dacian set about searching the boat in their idioms\u2026Tatiana breaking down doors, Dacian lock picking. It felt like Tatiana was trying to beat the Darkling to doors so she could break it rather than him unlocking it. Maybe she was frustrated. She has had plenty of scraps here in Berlin, but she also has been away from whomever she is seeing in the village. Not a reason to lash out at Dacian, though aggravating he is sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there was Della, chained in an aquarium in the cargo hold. Of course, at a quick glance, I doubted she was trapped. Still, she played up the damsel in distress almost frighteningly well. When she saw Wolfram with the comb, though, he immediately was called \u201chusband,\u201d though she was not terribly romantic about it. Dacian of course launched into his proposed Pledge, which would offer her freedom in exchange for never hunting humans and renewing it in a year. She balked at that. She preferred going back to Holbein to freedom without being able to hunt humans. Holbein seems to try to keep her under control, but I can only assume she is able to slip the leash time to time. I mean, why else would she take going back to him and him getting the comb over freedom. She claimed she fled because she was unsure who had the comb, but that did not sound right to me.<br /> <br /> At this point I wonder if hunting humans is part of how she feeds. She rejected the Pledge quickly, and it was not a bad one. Regardless, we returned her, and Holbein was pleased, Sabine relieved. We enjoyed the show awhile and returned to the house.<br /> <br /> Oh, the owner of the boat did try to stop us, with a crowd of thugs. Tatiana did her thing again and scared off almost ten people. It was funny to see her send them fleeing. Bastards had no idea we were probably saving them.<br /> <br /> When we got back, Della offered her \u201cformer husband\u201d a kiss. He demurred citing being otherwise married, but recommended me. She knelt down and gave me a kiss. That is a kiss I will not forget anytime soon. <br /> <br /> Looking forward to returning to Paris. Berlin politics have been crazy. I am glad for our relatively stable, relatively not trying to kill each other Courts. And watching Christina glide around the house. That is nice too. <br /> <br /> Hopefully this will be solved tomorrow, we can have Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s concert, and go home.<br /> <br /> And enjoy a little Mayhem! <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, Della was not trapped in the aquarium she was in. That boat would have been empty when it reached it\u2019s destination. And Della has to feed on humans a little, so Dacian\u2019s pledge was not really a option for her. <br /> <br /> Mostly RP as usual. This storyline is almost up. One more session unless things go very wrong. Then onto the summer of 1924. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:03:29-07:00","id":987425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=987384#post987384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Della was not trapped in the aquarium she was in. That boat would have been empty when it reached it\u2019s destination. And Della has to feed on humans a little, so Dacian\u2019s pledge was not really a option for her.<br /> <br /> Mostly RP as usual. This storyline is almost up. One more session unless things go very wrong. Then onto the summer of 1924. Comments and Questions welcome</div> </div> </div> </div>So, any previews regarding the next phase's plot? Key characters? General Themes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:53:35-07:00","id":987676,"title":"","content":"The beginning, say, 3-6 sessions, will be in Paris near Bastille Day 1924. Once some immediate problems are dealt with, the heroes will have a couple temporary (?) cast changes, and the story will shift to an on the road story, to break up the past couple sandboxes. In addition to some of the old Paris cast reprised for that part, look for a few recurring characters as the PCs travel across Europe by rail and boat in search of answers. Greta won't be along this time, nor Marissa (probably) but look for Constancia to a problem, er, I mean ally again. Other familiar faces will appear too, some more welcome than others. While some may appear, neither the Bound nor the Fae will be a major focus this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\