, or the old players with new story based characters?<br /> At the risk of sounding like I keep harping off, will any of your future antagonists be Mage based? How about Hunters, influenced perhaps by Marek's creative addition to his character's history between sessions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:37:35-07:00","id":988244,"title":"","content":"At least temporarily, hopefully not permanently, two players will drop as their family expands (again). We have a player who had an interest but there was no space, so they are going to join us for awhile. Their PC will be from a game not represented in the party atm, and not one of my other three active chronicles. If they would like to pop in thread and tease more or say outright that is up to them. Long term one or both may come back; we will work out then what the arrangements will be. Eight players is a lot, 7 is usually max.<br /> <br /> I suppose I am overdue for some Mage aren't I? I have gotten a better grasp of the game having some friendly and unfriendly in Night Train Detective Agency, so it could happen. I shall see what inspires me. Hunters have appeared, but only Susie the Seventh Generation has been a major character. That's the first since the train story. There was a half written other Hunter story for Berlin, but it cluttered things a bit. But i enjoy Hunter, it is a great game. I already have at least one plot for it this story, though it involves Susie again and the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback and getting the wheels turning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:28:46-07:00","id":988276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=988244#post988244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least temporarily, hopefully not permanently, two players will drop as their family expands (again). We have a player who had an interest but there was no space, so they are going to join us for awhile. Their PC will be from a game not represented in the party atm, and not one of my other three active chronicles. If they would like to pop in thread and tease more or say outright that is up to them. Long term one or both may come back; we will work out then what the arrangements will be. Eight players is a lot, 7 is usually max.<br /> <br /> I suppose I am overdue for some Mage aren't I? I have gotten a better grasp of the game having some friendly and unfriendly in Night Train Detective Agency, so it could happen. I shall see what inspires me. Hunters have appeared, but only Susie the Seventh Generation has been a major character. That's the first since the train story. There was a half written other Hunter story for Berlin, but it cluttered things a bit. But i enjoy Hunter, it is a great game. I already have at least one plot for it this story, though it involves Susie again and the Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback and getting the wheels turning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you say which characters are dropping out (hopefully temporarily) yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:00:48-07:00","id":988378,"title":"","content":"Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il.<br /> <br /> This dyke's gonna steal a dump truck and dump rubbers outside their door. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-16-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:33:04-07:00","id":994433,"title":"","content":"One story ends, another begins. The close of the Berlin story, and downtime.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XL</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> November 1922<br /> <br /> Well, the meeting between the monarchs went well. There was the usual griping to begin with but I think things worked out in the end. We started with Lizette, who was rather well-armed, going and picking up Woebegone first. Apparently she was taking her role as protector very seriously. The Autumn Queen arrived at our house and we quickly dispensed with the cold iron test. Woebegone was in fact wearing a glamour and it fell away as soon as she touched the iron. Her actual appearance is that of a short woman with big ears and nose. She looked like something out of the old tales of gremlins or boggarts. I can see why she uses a glamour. While there is nothing wrong with her actual appearance it is rather diminutive and she wanted to strike an impressive figure as queen of the Autumn court. People might not take her actual appearance all that seriously, which is unfortunate but true. So, I can see why she uses a glamour. Wolfram also commented on the interesting wrappings that she had around her wrists. Apparently they gave off an aura of death and Woebegone explained that the wrappings, which looked like film, were made from Fetch skin. Disturbing though it may sound at first, fetches are just fake people make up of detritus that the Gentry find lying around. So, it\u2019s probable that Woebegone destroyed her doppelganger and used some of the pieces for her own ends.<br /> <br /> Soon after that Skadi arrived with a bodyguard. We had her and her companion touch the cold iron to no effect. After that Sascha arrived with Oneida and they both touched the iron. Nothing happened. Not that we were expecting anything to. Woebegone\u2019s associate Rudolph touched the cold iron and released a smoke pellet at the same time to make it look like it was burning him. He was the only one that pulled any kind of joke.<br /> <br /> Once the pleasantries were dispensed with the negotiating began. Wolfram assisted Alla in acting as moderators for the discussion. The arguments boiled down to Skadi wanting at least a generation to grow up remembering the war and the loss and feeling bad about it so they would make sure it didn\u2019t happen again. Woebegone and Sascha wanted to bring the country up out of the mire and revitalize the economy and give hope to the people. I can see why they want to do that. The economy is in shambles. German currency is worth next to nothing. Inflation has risen so fast that the people are going broke just trying to buy bread. So, I can see why they want to bring in outside money and business. Skadi is convinced that if the people forget too quickly the horrors of war then they will be doomed to repeat it. This went back and forth for a while. Mainly between Skadi and Woebegone. Sascha for the most part just fidgeted and complained that he was bored.<br /> <br /> The discussion was going back and forth until Dearbhail finally got fed up and interjected. She explained the troubles of her own country, Ireland, and how keeping the people repressed just leads to people who have nothing left to lose. Her people could only stand to take so much oppression before they fought back and as far as I know the fighting is still going on. Skadi asked to take a break to consider this and we adjourned for a few minutes to let the Winter Queen think things over.<br /> <br /> Skadi came back from her deliberation and apparently what Dearbhail said changed the Winter Queen\u2019s mind. Skadi agreed to allow the Spring and Autumn courts to do their best to influence the economy as long as the growth wasn\u2019t too fast or dramatic. They agreed and Alla came up with the wording for the compromise. Now, because there are four courts in the city they will not be able to come to an agreement should they need to in the future. Sascha will do whatever Woebegone does and the Summer King will do whatever Skadi wants so they needed a tiebreaker. Someone that is impartial and would be willing to act as the deciding vote in future conflicts. We talked for a while about who would make a good tiebreaker and eventually decided on Willie Schmidt. Wolfram went to go talk to Willie and see if he\u2019d be interested in serving in this capacity. The both returned, so it seems that Wolfram was able to talk the other man into it. Willie agreed before the fae monarchs to be the deciding vote should they need him, but wanted to make sure that he was exempt from the fall out of any decisions that he made. They agreed to that and included in the bargain some monetary gain for Willie. He did not ask for money, but they offered it as payment for being the tiebreaker should they need it and he agreed.<br /> <br /> Later we all went to Saints and Sinners. As soon as we arrived Dearbhail read Holbien\u2019s desires as far as werewolves go and found out that he just wants to be left alone. Lizette read his fears with the same focus and found out that he is afraid of being used as breeding stock. A valid fear. Uratha and Pure do not mate amongst themselves, we look to those who are not Uratha. Holbien just wants to be left out of werewolf matters which is fair as far as I\u2019m concerned.<br /> <br /> Before Dearbhail\u2019s act started Greta joined us for the show. She shared that the Watch have attacked the Pure. Our plan to get them going after one another seems to have worked. With any luck they will weaken one another so neither of them will pose a threat to Berlin.<br /> <br /> After Greta updated us Dearbhail went up on stage to sing. She was wonderful as always. She sang a number of songs and people got up to dance. The woman that I would ask to dance was the one singing so I stayed at the table and just enjoyed the show. Dearbhail really is quite lovely.<br /> <br /> Once the show was over Holbien came over to talk to us. Tatiana suggested that if he ever needed help or protection from a threat to call us and we could protect him. He said that he appreciated the offer. What Tatiana did next was not as binding as a Fae oath, but it is binding for us. We had agreed on this course of action before we came to the club tonight. In the course of her promising to protect him she revealed us to be Uratha and herself to be an Iron Master. She did not say it in so many words, but the phrasing that she used is known to be Uratha and Iron Master. Holbien accepted this without comment but nodded his understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> 6 November 1922<br /> <br /> Hans sent a messenger to find me before I left Berlin. I was actually heading out of the city when the courier found me. I will admit that I was a little surprised by the request. It was the first time that Hans has ever asked for a personal favor, but I can see why he asked for Reznik. Apparently his sister Elsbeth married a man named Dale and they had a lovely daughter named Gerda. They had a decent life. Dale was an accountant and Elsbeth stayed home with their little girl. Apparently there was a man in the neighborhood that became jealous of Dale\u2019s family and their success. A few days ago this man took his anger and resentment to new heights and set Dale and Elsbeth\u2019s house on fire. I think he was intending to get the whole family, but Dale was working late and came home to find his house in flames. He also found a sign posted on the front yard that said all Jews should die. There was nothing he could do. The fire was too big. His family died. The other man, Ernst, got away with it too. He hid behind his family name and the police ignored any evidence that pointed to the man having done anything. It was no secret that Ernst hated Dale and his family, and had even threatened them in the past. There were no witnesses to say he was there. He was not even questioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> 7 November 1922<br /> <br /> I have tracked Ernst today to see what his habits are and which places he frequents. He went to his own place of business for most of the day. He then went to a Gentleman\u2019s club when he did some socializing and drinking. At least he left the building on more unsteady legs than when he entered it. He did not do much else today. I will keep an eye on him and await my chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 November 1922<br /> <br /> <br /> Ernst seems to have a routine which I will exploit. Most nights he goes out drinking and socializing with his friends. He usually stays out later than they do and walks home alone. I will follow him tomorrow night and take care of my business.<br /> <br /> <br /> 11 November 1922<br /> <br /> Tonight was definitely an interesting and eye-opening night. I had started to stalk my prey as he was making his way back to his house when I noticed that I was not the only one following him. I caught the scent of someone else, who smelled faintly of bread, also tracking Ernst. When I finally spotted the other hunter I was surprised to see a somewhat short man with a slight build following Ernst through the alleys. His outward appearance was that of a small unassuming man, but as soon as I got close he seemed to be much greater than his stature would indicate. Then I saw him start to throw things at Ernst as he got closer. Big things. Things no man should be able to lift. I decided then that I wanted to find out who this man was and what his interest in Ernst was. So, I approached. I made sure to make noise so he would hear me coming. I was in Dalu form, so if he looked close enough at me he would know that I was not human, just as I could tell that there was something more to him. I greeted him and asked what his interest in the quivering man was. He said that he was \u201cteaching\u201d Ernst the error of his ways. That he should not target those that he sees as less than himself. I admitted to this new man, he said his name was Laszlo, that I had been hunting Ernst myself and was planning on bringing him to justice for killing the woman and little girl. Laszlo said that was fair and just asked that I let him finish what he\u2019d started, and then he\u2019d let me finish my own hunt. I was amused to see Ernst trying to hide, so I agreed and stood back as Laszlo took up the chase once more. I will give him credit\u2026 Ernst tried to run, but didn\u2019t get far. He obviously was not overly familiar with the alleyways and ended up well and truly lost. I followed at a leisurely pace and eventually caught up to the pair. Ernst was once again quivering in a ball on the ground. The air was sour with the smell of urine and fear, and strangely enough a burnt smell. There was also scorch marks on the ground where Ernst cowered. When Laszlo saw me approach he stepped back with a smile. I walked up to Ernst and smiled down at the frightened man. I asked him if he\u2019d learned his lesson yet? Ernst swore that he had. That he would never hurt anyone again. That\u2019s all well and good I suppose. If it was just Laszlo there I believe that he would have let the trembling man live and return to his life. Perhaps a changed man. Perhaps not. But Laszlo wasn\u2019t alone. I was there, and the note that Hans had given me was clear as to what he wanted to see happen to the scum that killed his sister and niece. It was very clear. And so I obliged. Nothing elaborate. I just used a gift to grow longer claws and ripped out the man\u2019s throat.<br /> <br /> Laszlo stood back and watched unconcerned as I killed Ernst. The other man just smiled at me when I was done, and I will admit that my curiosity took over and I asked him if he did that kind of thing often. Laszlo nodded and said that sometimes it was necessary to \u201cteach\u201d those that lose their way and remind them how they should act. I asked him what he was. I was being blunt, but social niceties have never been my strong point. He said that he was one of many and that they call themselves The Children. He told me that he was the mortal manifestation of The Golem and that he protects the Jews of Berlin from those that would prey upon them. I smiled at that. I told them that it was good to hear that the people had a protector. He then said that it was also good that Berlin could count a noble werewolf amongst its guardians. I wasn\u2019t overly trying to hide what I was, but it was still a bit of a surprise to just have him say it like that. I did smile though. I then complimented him on the hunt and told him that I would look for him again the next time I was in Berlin. Laszlo nodded and smiled back. Something made me tell him that if he ever needed help then he should ask for Reznik. I told him how to contact Hans, and he would find me. Just watching Laszlo this evening I know the man can take care of himself, outward appearances aside, but I felt like I should make the offer anyway. In turn he shared with me the name and address of his family\u2019s bakery. They live over the shop. Should I ever need to contact him I have a way.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26 December 1922<br /> <br /> I decided to come home for the holidays this year. I have missed it in the past due to work. Usually I\u2019ve been too far away. This year though I decided to make sure that I\u2019d be home for Christmas. I know that my family appreciates having me home. I don\u2019t visit as often as I suppose I should. The children are growing up so fast. Kv\u00e9ta is now seven and Dominik is fourteen. Darkja is just over one and is walking now. She seems to get into everything.<br /> <br /> I have annoyed Alena again, but I am fine with that. For Christmas I got each of the girls another doll, these were from Russia. For Dominik I got a compass. And for the older children I got a couple notepads of paper and colored crayons with which to draw. Kv\u00e9ta\u2019s eyes lit up at the doll and the drawing supplies. I hope that she puts them to good use. Dominik was happy with his present as well. He wanted to immediately go for a walk in the woods and see if he could find his way home. Erik said that it was far too cold out to do too much exploring, so I suggested that Domink take it with him when he does his chores or when he goes to town with his parents so he can see which direction they are headed.<br /> <br /> For the ladies I got a bolt of cloth that I saw in Berlin. Dearbhail had commented on someone wearing a dress made from cloth similar and said that it was very fashionable. So, before I left Berlin I stopped at a shop and bought some cloth. I thought that the ladies might be able to make themselves something pretty out of it. Lenka and Desnisa seemed to really like it and Alena didn\u2019t complain when I told them I found it in Berlin. For my brother I got a set of warm winter clothes. I know that he would not buy something like that for himself. I got my father a warm winter coat. The last time I saw his coat it had holes in it and I figured that he would need a new one soon. I was right.<br /> <br /> As for myself, my brother and his wife got me a pair of good boots which I immediately put on. They are very comfortable. Alena and Josef made me a warm sweater in dark blue. It was very well made. I thanked Alena for her hard work and she looked at me with a hint of surprise. I can be polite when I try. The children had also made me some presents. Dominik had carved a spider using the knife that I had given him. It was pretty well done and I told him that it would have a place of honor in my house. Kveta had helped her mother make me a hat. It matched my sweater and I told her I would wear it whenever it got cold. Overall it was a good visit. The ladies cooked a wonderful meal and I got to spend time with my other pack, or my first pack I should say. We even got some good news. Lenka revealed that she was with child and believes that the baby will be born in August of next year. There was much congratulations and well-wishes. I am happy to see my pack grow.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 February 1923<br /> <br /> I took a job in France. It has been a while since I\u2019ve been back here for work purposes but I thought the job warranted my attention. The target was a man named Michel Dubois, and he was a factory owner in Toulon. Apparently there were safety issues at his factory and employees that complained or tried to bring to light the problems promptly disappeared. There was some evidence that pointed at Michel being the guilty party, but again, money and family won out and he went free. If he goes missing himself the factory will transfer to the keeping of his business partner Gerard Babineaux. So, I followed Mousier Dubois for a couple of days to get his routine down. He did not have much of a social life. He was married to a stout, patient woman named Julie who greeted his return at night with something like resignation. I did not feel bad making her a widow.<br /> <br /> I waited until Michel was alone at the factory one night. It appeared that he was working late, so I paid him a visit. I \u201cborrowed\u201d a pistol that I found in his night stand the other day when I was checking out his house. I waited until Julie was gone and acquired the gun. I used it yesterday to shoot Michel in the head and then put the gun in his own hand. It will appear that he took his own life. It won\u2019t even be that hard to believe. From the time I\u2019ve observed him he has worked late several times and complained to his wife about the financial stability of the factory. He kept saying that he would figure something out, but I saw no evidence that he had found a solution to his money problems. I do not know if Gerard will have better luck with the factory, but that is not my problem. I was hired to get rid of Michel and make it look like a suicide, so I did.<br /> <br /> <br /> 23 May 1923<br /> <br /> I got a message from Adawolf the other day asking me to lend them my aid. Apparently they needed help with getting papers for the newest member of their pack, Friedrich. He had to leave his old life behind when he changed and did not have a way to procure a new identity. I have friends that can help with that, so Adawolf contacted me. I owe them a favor anyway so I told them I would be in contact with my people.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25 May 1923<br /> <br /> I got in touch with Hans who put me in contact with his man in Berlin. I then arranged with the pack to have Friedrich come with me to get his photograph taken so identification could be created for him. Friedrich is not much younger than I am but seems to be so young. He had never been to Berlin before and was impressed by the buildings and shops. If he had his way we would have explored all over the city. I tried to explain to him that there were certain groups in the city that we needed to avoid, but he didn\u2019t seem to want to listen. Like most young men I think he believed himself to be invincible; especially considering what he is. I briefly considered just letting him wander the city and see if he found any groups of Pure, but I did not. I eventually got him to follow me to meet our contact and we concluded our business in short order. Friedrich had his new identification. I paid the man for his work and thanked him before we headed back out. We made it back to the pack by nightfall. Friedrich was still excited about his trip to Berlin, which led to me giving the pack a warning about what was going on in the city. Adawolf already knew about the Pure, but was not aware of The Watch. So, I informed them of what was going on and how best to avoid trouble should they need to go to the city. I did not go into detail on my involvement on what is happening within the city, I just gave an overview of the places and people to be avoided.<br /> <br /> <br /> 8 July 1923<br /> <br /> I received a letter from my brother saying that Lenka was having problems with the pregnancy. She had been to see the local midwives and they told her that she needed to rest. He asked that I come home just in case something went wrong. I agreed and headed home as quickly as I could. I decided against running this time since having a car might come in handy. I was right. Early this morning Lenka went into labor a full month before the baby is supposed to come. Andel was very upset, but Lenka was her usual calm self. We had one of the midwives come to the house but she said that there was nothing that she could do. The baby was turned around the wrong way, a breach baby, and she did not know how to turn it. So, we put Lenka and Andel in the car and I drove them to the nearest big town that had a hospital. I\u2019ll admit that I did not pay close attention to the town names as I passed them. I just followed Andel\u2019s directions. It has been too long since I spent any real time at home. Anyway, we made it to the town in short order and Lenka was rushed in to see a doctor. Andel and I were told to wait in the lounge area while they saw to his wife. So, we waited. Andel paced the room frequently and all attempts on my part to get him to sit down were in vain. About an hour later the doctor came back out and said that they had managed to turn the baby around and she was born just a few minutes ago. She is a little small due to her being born early, but she appears to be healthy. Andel finally sat down, in relief. We were allowed to see Lenka about half an hour later. She was holding the newborn girl and singing softly to her. Andel and Lenka decided to name the little girl Aneta, after our grandmother.<br /> <br /> <br /> 11 July 1923<br /> <br /> The four of us heading back home much to the delight of everyone else. We had called and informed them of the good news the day little Aneta was born, but they were still anxious to see her and Lenka home safe. Desnisa and Alena offered to come over and help with the baby while Lenka rested up. The house was rather full but no one was upset about that. I offered to leave to make room, but they insisted that I stay so I did. Since they are putting me up I have decided that I should do something for them. I will make a fetish to keep the little girl safe. She is only a couple of days old, but sometimes she seems to see the heart of you with her stormy grey eyes. She is a special little girl.<br /> <br /> <br /> 12 July 1923<br /> <br /> I spent most of today in the woods trying to find a spirit that I could bind to a fetish to protect little Aneta. I found a playful one this afternoon that reminded me of volchonok. So I made a mobile out of wood and leather. I carved pieces of wood into different animal shapes and shaped a circle out of a flexible sapling. The animals hung around the circle and I hung a dark circle in the center to represent the new moon. To the others the dark circle will just be decoration, but to me of course it represents so much more. Alena was not impressed with the mobile that I made, but then I was not trying to gain her approval. Andel and Lenka liked it and Aneta seemed fascinated with it when they hung it over her crib. That is what mattered to me.<br /> I have decided that I will leave in a couple of days. The house is rather full of people and despite their insistence that I stay I know they have enough to deal with without having to worry about a guest. This evening though I was able to lend at least a little aid. Aneta woke up crying. After Lenka fed the little girl she still seemed fully awake, but Lenka was obviously worn out. Aneta had woken me too, so I offered to rock the baby to sleep. I held little Aneta and did my best to imitate the kind of swaying motion that I\u2019ve seen Lenka and Andel use with the baby. Aneta calmed down and proceeded to grab a hold of my shirt and made little noises at me. She seemed to watch me closely so I made sure to keep a pleasant expression on my face. Lenka has told me that Aneta\u2019s eyes will change color within a few months. I found myself hoping that they do not change. I like the stormy grey color. I think it suits her well.<br /> <br /> <br /> 15 January 1924<br /> <br /> I was not able to make it home for the holidays this time but sent gifts to everyone. Andel sent a letter back saying that they were all appreciated. All the presents I sent this time were from Poland. I am happy that they were well received.<br /> <br /> Not long after that letter I got another one from Andel telling me that father, Lenka and little Aneta had all fallen ill with some sort of lung infection. They were all coughing and had fevers. I wrote back to tell Andel that I was on my way home and would be there within a few days. I had a job that I was supposed to do in Poland. A man was preying on young women in Wroclaw. I had initially planned on terrorizing him before finally hunting and killing him. Having met Laszlo gave me the idea and I thought it would be fitting to \u201cteach\u201d him before killing him. That was the plan anyway. My family, my pack becoming sick changed my plans though. I did not have the luxury of \u201cteaching\u201d Nelek so I just followed him to his home where he lived alone and put a sniper round in his head. The authorities will find him eventually.<br /> <br /> <br /> 17 January 1924<br /> <br /> I made it home in time to care for my family as they lay sick in bed. Everyone took special care to wash the linens and keep everything clean. Of the three affected little Aneta was the worst off. Her coughs sounded horrible and I will admit that I was afraid that she would not make it. She is so little and the midwives told Lenka that babies born early often have a harder time fighting off lung infections. I do not believe that it was their intention to worry my sister-in-law, just prepare her in case the worst should happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> 21 January 1924<br /> <br /> Everyone seems to have pulled through the sickness. Lenka was the first to get over it, then father, then Aneta. I will admit that it was good to see little Aneta finally smile after she\u2019d been frowning so much lately. Her breathing is much improved and she instead making noises that sound happy rather than distressed. Andel told me that Aneta really liked the mobile that I made for her and often reached for the little wooden animals. I am happy that she likes it so much. I was also glad to have made it to keep her safe. I do not know if the spirit helped little Aneta get over the illness or not, but I choose to believe that it did. The local doctor and midwives did not seem to think that she would make it. I am glad that she proved them wrong. Despite what people have said, Aneta\u2019s eyes remain grey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 23 March 1924<br /> <br /> I was traveling through Austria and came across stories of a haunted mill. The place had been abandoned shortly after the war due to the troublesome spirit. So, I decided to investigate. As it turns out it was not a ghost but a spirit of sadness. At least the spirit seemed rather upset and I could only assume that the war left its toll on the spirit world here as well as the physical one. It was not hard to deal with it and it almost seemed happy to be sent back to the spirit world.<br /> <br /> <br /> 8 July 1924<br /> <br /> As luck would have it I made it home in time for Aneta\u2019s first birthday. She is still a bit small for her age, but she has become quite the inquisitive little girl and loves to explore outside. She seems fascinated by the trees, the birds, squirrels, you name it. They do not let her wander too far, but I was happy to see that she has taken such an interest in the natural world. I made Aneta her own little train of spiders, for luck, and she seems to really like them. She has already played with them on the floor and had them marching in a little line towards the doll that Alena made for her. Darkja brought out her spiders and played together with her little sister for a while. Together they had a veritable army of spiders marching across the floor.<br /> <br /> I think I well and truly annoyed Alena today. I had taken the children outside to play and after they had tired themselves out running around I told them stories about the spirit world and how we should always respect not just the people around us but the things as well. The trees, the rocks, the animals, even the earth. There are spirits everywhere and too often people do things without considering what they might be harming in the process of building a house, or cutting trees down for firewood. The children listened with rapt attention and seemed to be enjoying my tales until Alena came outside and listened in. She accused me of filling their heads with nonsense and told me to stop telling them such tales. I told the children that I would tell them more stories later, and suggested that we go in and see if their mother needed any help. Even little Aneta stopped chasing a butterfly and came over when I called to her. Alena might not like my stories but they are true and it would be good for the children to grow up and be aware of such things. Alena may try and stop me from telling the tales, but I will not. She may be pack but she will not tell me what to do and what not to do. Father has never seemed to mind the tales so I will continue to tell them until he tells me to stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, the sad scary queen did look very different once she touched the iron. Like a gnome from a picture book.<br /> <br /> What is a picture book? It is a thing for children or those who cannot read.<br /> <br /> That is true, you cannot.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are picture books in France as well. I suppose I could get you one. It is a human thing though...<br /> <br /> How quickly your attention fades.<br /> <br /> Nothing, volchonok, nothing.<br /> <br /> I know you love the thorny paths. I like it as well, this time especially.<br /> <br /> Because we are going home. The fairies have agreed to work together - Dearbh\u00e1il was very forceful and had a strong impact on Skadi.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, Willie is not a fairy now, no more than we two are. He is to break ties, when the nobles do not agree. He is a good man for it.<br /> <br /> He cares for the people of Germany and knows what war truly is. And he has no stake in the fairy business and is unlikely too.<br /> <br /> I am sure, volchonok, that Sascha would like to mate with him. But I do not believe Willie would care for this.<br /> <br /> True, we did finish that yesterday. But there was the concert, recall. No one wished to leave that late.<br /> <br /> It was a good concert, volchonok. But of course it was, Dearbh\u00e1il was singing.<br /> <br /> I believe the Wolf-Blooded is a friend, yes. He does not wish to be used as a breeding stock, Lizette said, and I offered to protect him, should the Pure try.<br /> <br /> Of course I will. It would mean I get to fight the Pure. With good reasons!<br /> <br /> Yes, the Watch are fighting them now, our plan worked. But they are not me. I would fight them better.<br /> <br /> It is true, volchonok. That is Berlin\u2019s problem now. Now we shall run and make sure every corner of our territory knows we have returned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Interlude 4</u><br /> <br /> Tatiana and Elena enjoyed their rare moment of quiet. The boys were occupied with the Meccano toy set Tatiana had brought back from her latest trip, having scampered off as soon as dinner was over. Their mother didn\u2019t call them back to help with the usual clean, as she might have, preferring to have a quiet moment with her love. She smiled slightly over at her, handing the plate she just finished washing over to the muscular woman for drying.<br /> <br /> After a few minutes of companionable silence, Elena spoke up, a matter of fact tone in her voice. \u201cSo, Theodora and Abel are engaged to be married.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs this so?\u201d Tatiana matched her tone, mouth dry. Her right arm twinged as she moved it too carelessly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is and it is good. She has mourned the husband she lost for years now.\u201d Dishes finished, Elena turned to face Tatiana, arms crossed. \u201cHe is good with her son and daughters.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana stretched carefully, feigning casual interest. \u201cHe is the tall one who teaches at the school, yes? Sasha likes him.\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena nodded. \u201cHe has been courting her for some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is lucky then, to get what he wants.\u201d Tatiana gave her an uncomfortable grin. \u201cTeaching is a good profession - he will be able to give her a stable home.\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena laughed, laying a hand on Tatiana\u2019s cheek. \u201cLucky indeed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana growled playfully, kissing the palm of her lover\u2019s hand. \u201cNot as lucky as me.\u201d She snaked out her left arm and pulled Elena close for a proper kiss.<br /> <br /> The smaller woman didn\u2019t resist but responded chastely. \u201cYou think so?\u201d Her stern facade didn\u2019t last long in the face of Tatiana\u2019s rising panic. She shook her head, smiling fondly at the other woman.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I have you, I am the most lucky person in the world.\u201d Tatiana aimed for a cocky smile and managed a hopeful one.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is a bold claim.\u201d Elena stood on her toes and put her arms around the muscled woman\u2019s neck. They locked eyes for a long intense moment before Elena stretched to kiss the tip of her lover\u2019s nose. \u201cShall we test it?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> It's been two years since visiting Berlin. I believe we achieved what we set out to do. The Pure were pitted against the Watch, the Black Company were set on a less offensive path (in that they were not actively supporting the Watch and their crusade against all that didn't fit their narrow idea of who is allowed in Germany). Skadi's request for our help when we arrived showed that we'd gained a modicum of respect. I don't know that our solution honestly satisfied her, but at least we attempted to unite the changelings. <br /> <br /> She seems convinced that war will return to German, but it is so hard to imagine. If that happens, Dear Friend, you know you are always welcome at the chataeu. The village is lovely and would welcome someone with your talents. The whole freehold would be welcome. You were all so kind to me when I returned, I would be happy to offer you safe haven if you ever find yourself in need.<br /> <br /> Since my last visit I've spent a great deal of time in America. Hollywood, can you imagine? It isn't as big a city as Paris or Berlin, but there's a newness &amp; a frantic abandon to the town - just what someone like me needs. I've been working with the movie industry here - you won't see me on the screen I assure you! The stage shall always be home. But even with these silent films there's a need for a score to help the pianist or orchestra provide an emotional tone to the pictures. The cinema is a fascinating place but I do miss the stage. Perhaps I will have the chance to tour again soon.<br /> <br /> For now, I will close. I have to go record a song. It is a new experience for me, and certainly doesn't allow me to connect with an audience. But I have enjoyed listening to many albums so why not try it? Wish me luck!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 3rd November 1922<br /> <br /> We are successful. The meeting was a success and the Pure and Die Wacht were tricked into fighting. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Queen Woebegone arrived first, and went through the humiliating process of touching the cold iron. It dispelled the illusion, leaving her in her small, droopy, pitiable form. I was interested in what appeared to be filmstrip as gloves she was wearing. Fetch-skin she said, given Fetches could make a Mask that even fools The Kind. Noted. I took my place guarding Woebegone for the duration.<br /> <br /> Queen Skadi was fashionably late, and Prince Sascha a bit late for that. The early discussion went nowhere; there was no love lost between Queen Woebegone and Skadi, and Sascha was just bored. A lot of back and forth about Germany\u2019s future, with Woebegone and Sascha keen to repair Germany faster, Skadi wanting to drag it out a couple generations. Eventually Dearbh\u00e1il broke in asking Skadi about Ireland, and her strife. Skadi\u2019s moralizing about how sorrow needed to dominate before later generations would forgive them seemed to fall away as the Elemental considered Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s words.<br /> <br /> Queen Skadi asked for a recess, and when she returned she was more willing to compromise. A general agreement was hashed out wherein they would each work to try to shape Germany in their idiom, Summer included. If they had a two against two impasse, they would call in a tiebreaker. The Dusk Court was discussed, as they had, briefly, had some numbers in Germany, but they faded as quickly as they appeared. Vampires came up, but Skadi wanted a temporary arrangement that would end with the arbiter\u2019s death, though I suggested a set duration would work too. Wolfram eventually suggested Willie Schmidt, the Bound, noting his honesty and integrity. He went to fetch him, and after meeting him they agreed. And Willie may even get some money out of the pledge. So the Courts will cease sniping at each other for now.<br /> <br /> Probably.<br /> <br /> Prince Sascha could not wait to go home and seemed to annoy Dacian. Sascha is a caring man, but not an ambitious one, who has his position due to his caring for his people. I have to say given how much Queen Skadi talked about Humans and how detached she seemed, it seemed odd the Elemental would fear Queen Woebegone a Gentry. We are a paranoid lot it seems.<br /> <br /> We met in the evening at Saints and Sinners and Marissa Sangiovanni joined us. We spoke to Herr Holbein, and told him we were not calling anything in yet, but expressed we wanted him to stay safe. Based on what Dearbh\u00e1il and I sensed, he is likely a Pure Wolf-Blooded on the run. Hopefully he avoids them.<br /> <br /> Greta joined us, and reported The Pure and Die Wacht were fighting now. Mayhem! Out jobs done, we relaxed and enjoyed Dearbh\u00e1il singing (including <i>April Showers</i>!) Wolfram and I danced a little too. Sabine flirted with her a little, but poor Greta was a bit too flustered by it all. Things are winding down now but it has been a good evening, and I look forward to being home.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The Gremlin opened the door to her room, greeted by the sound of ticking from the many clocks and clockwork devices throughout the room. She smiled and the familiar sounds and smells of her room and collapsed onto her bed, as Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re shut the door behind her. Looking to the side she saw a square flat brown package with a bow on it, and a note.<br /> <br /> \u201cLate Birthday Present. Love, Christina\u201d<br /> <br /> The Wizened smiled and pulled off the wrapper, to see a record of Al Jolson singing <i>April Showers</i>, and squealed with glee. Running across the room she set it on her record player (and home defense device) and soon the song could be heard above the steady ticking in the room. Falling on her bed, she smiled broadly and closed her golden eyes as she listened.<br /> <br /> <i>So keep on looking for the bluebird<br /> And listening for his song,<br /> Whenever April showers come along\u2026</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wolfram\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Wolfram Johann Ritter von Klingemann smiled tiredly as he pulled the car to a stop and looked over at the younger man seated beside him. \u201cI am glad you were able to get away and enjoy Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s performances. It is always nice to see you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich chuckled as he exited the car and moved to take his traveling case from the trunk. \u201cIf I were a more suspicious man I\u2019d suggest that wasn\u2019t all you invited me to see.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram cleared his throat and shut the trunk. \u201cYes, well perhaps it did cross my mind that Sasha was someone you should meet while you were here in town.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich shook his head. \u201cI do appreciate that you worry about my happiness brother, but really. As charming as the man may be, we have nothing in common.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram stood and straightened his jacket. \u201cSometimes that is the whole point, is it not?\u201d he replied, \u201cAnd besides, you do share at least one trait with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich scowled but Wolfram continued before he could speak. \u201cYou\u2019ve said more than once that you are concerned with how your business associates in Duisburg would view it if you sought out like-minded company there. I merely thought that perhaps Berlin would be a better location and that meeting someone who could steer you toward the right socials and away from the wrong ones would be useful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich\u2019s dour expression softened and he shrugged as they began to walk toward the train platform. \u201cI am capable of seeing to my own social needs you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you telling me you\u2019d prefer to remain alone?\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich sighed. \u201cNo. But being prodded and nudged, no matter how well intentioned, isn\u2019t what I want either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough I suppose. I am sorry if I overstepped. I just want you to be happy. You deserve that and I worry that you devote all of your efforts to your workers and the factory and don\u2019t take any time for yourself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich pursed his lips as they stopped at the platform and he set his case down. \u201cI did enjoy the shows and I did enjoy Sasha\u2019s company,\u201d he admitted, \u201cAnd I\u2019m not upset with you. But you could have simply suggested this directly you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram nodded. \u201cHonestly, it wasn\u2019t the main reason I invited you. I wished to see you and to have you enjoy the shows. That it would also allow you to meet someone who might help you explore the Berlin nightlife and find some enjoyable company was an added bonus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich studied his brother a moment and shook his head. \u201cEven if I do decide to begin taking in more of Berlin\u2019s nightlife I do not need another soul trying to meddle in my personal affairs or matchmake. Mother is bad enough. Your marriage and the impending birth of your child has had her redoubling her efforts lately.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram reach to clasp his brother\u2019s shoulder. \u201cI did not think of that. Perhaps I should invite her to come to Chantilly for a while to be there when her grandchild arrives?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think she\u2019d like that but are you sure it wouldn\u2019t be an issue with the odd company your group keeps? I mean, you can\u2019t very well tell her you need her to avoid the parlor while you host a diplomatic summit of warring fairy factions or plan a campaign against hostile werewolves.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram chuckled. \u201cChantilly is much larger than the townhouse. I am sure that I can keep such matters safely away from her gaze. Besides which, I am quite done with mad vampires, nationalistic sin-eaters, hidebound noble werewolves, and fay politics for a while.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about rogue sirens?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram\u2019s cheeks tinted. \u201cVery much done with those as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich patted his brother\u2019s hand and laughed. \u201cAh, you are a good man brother, but still a man...\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram straightened and lifted an eyebrow. \u201cI thought you weren\u2019t interested in such things.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am gay Wolfram, not blind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would never be unfaithful to Christina.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know brother. I know. And I am sure she does as well.\u201d Heinrich chuckled again as the train began to roll into the station and more people began to fill the platform. \u201cHave a safe journey back to Paris. As convenient as this hedge gate you\u2019ve told me of sounds, I think I prefer the train.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram moved to hug his brother. \u201cBe well Heinrich. Once I\u2019m back I\u2019ll speak to Christina about inviting Mother for a visit. Have a safe journey yourself.\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Wolfram circled the small round table, looking over each detail of the trio of settings critically.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, I really don\u2019t think a misplaced salad fork or wrinkled tablecloth is going to effect this evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> He paused and looked over to Marlene as she stood in the doorway. \u201cThe smallest things can move the world sometimes,\u201d he answered. She gave him a skeptical look and he shrugged and added, \u201cAnd fretting over details gives me something to do while waiting.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head and moved into the room, looking everything over herself. \u201cThe menu is set. The kitchen has it all well in hand. The wine is ready. The music is ready. Everything is ready save you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram paused and glanced down. \u201cIs something amiss? Is there something?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marlene frowned slightly. \u201cNo. but surely you planned to dress up for the evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis isn\u2019t about me. I am merely facilitating bringing the two of them back together in a setting to spark their former intimacy. Now that Christina has recovered from Regina\u2019s birth she\u2019s been a bit down and could use the attention and company.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marlene started to speak but stopped herself. Then after a moment she wet her lips and smiled. \u201cAnd do you not think that after going to such trouble it will not strike both of them as odd if you are anything less than equally formal? They are not foolish you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram straightened. \u201cWell of course they aren\u2019t. Though I suppose you are right. It would make me more obtrusive if I wasn\u2019t a match to the other arrangements.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course. Though I still don\u2019t see how they\u2019re not going to catch onto your intentions.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh I fully expect they will. That is rather the point actually. I want them to see that I truly see no reason why things cannot continue as they were before the wedding. They make each other very happy and I care for them both.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut Christina is now your wife. That makes it different.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram waved his hand. \u201cIf anything, it makes it less of a concern. I need have no fears that Lizette would sweep her away from me now. Not that that was really an option before. The world\u2019s not that enlighted yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt matters because Christina is a woman of honor who takes her vow to you seriously.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, and I take my own quite seriously as well. But I am truly not threatened by the notion that she can love another or find enjoyment in their company. I do not think so little of her that I think her affection is too finite to include both myself and Lizette. And as to it being improper, there exist rules of how one conducts such affairs and they quite predate the more modern outlooks on the rise of late. And besides, I know Lizette misses her as well. I cannot abide being the cause of sadness for two women who mean so much to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marlene shook her head and smiled. \u201cHave you been practicing that in the mirror for tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Wolfram answered, \u201cIt is simply the truth.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marlene nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s really not hard to understand what she sees in you. Now go please and make ready. Trust me, I\u2019ll make sure to fret over everything for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram chuckled and nodded. \u201cThank you Marlene. We\u2019re fortunate to have such a good friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> She watched him leave and sighed. \u201cNot hard to see what either of them see in you.\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> The late morning sun drifted in through curtains that fluttered in the gentle breeze. Wolfram\u2019s eyes fluttered open and he found himself blinking at the light through a curtain of dark hair as the soft fragrance teased his nose. Shifting slightly he glanced up from the delicate pointed green ear that rose from that tousled hair and saw the face of his still sleeping wife, lips curled blissfully as she held the smaller woman tight and close even now. Gingerly, he eased his arm from beneath the two sleeping women and eased himself free of the bed to creep to the washroom.<br /> <br /> The pair stirred slightly but remained settled into each others arms when he returned to the room. Wolfram paused to gaze adoringly down at them and sighed softly. This was not what he had set out to do last night. He eased to sit on the dressing bench and continue watching as he thought back to the night before. There had been wine and perhaps it had encouraged everyone involved to things they might otherwise have demurred from, but none of them had indulged overly. And here now by the morning light he could not bring himself to regret the course the night had eventually taken.<br /> <br /> He wasn\u2019t sure exactly how long he remained there but before too long the complaint of his stomach grew audible. Wolfram rose, casting about for a robe or his clothing so that he might venture out and find a servant, or better yet to fetch them something to break their fast himself and avoid any waggling tongues. He located his trousers and picked them up and as he glanced back over at the bed, his eyes met Lizette\u2019s bright yellow gaze. A reflex to turn his nakedness away or avert his eyes from her own came and went, a lingering sense of propriety that no longer seemed to apply but in its wake followed an awkward realization of the lack of surety over where things did stand now between himself and his dearest friend. He wet his lips and straightened from where he\u2019d bent to pick up his trousers but let them dangle in his hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning,\u201d he offered with a slightly nervous smile as he tried to judge her reaction to the night\u2019s developments.<br /> <br /> Lizette smiled brightly, if a bit cautiously, perhaps doing the same. &quot;Good morning, how are you?&quot;<br /> <br /> At her smile he released a breath he did not realize he\u2019d been holding. \u201cI am well,\u201d he answered as his own smile grew warmer and slightly playful, \u201cQuite well actually.\u201d He moved closer to the bed, sitting on the edge and reached for her hand. \u201cI enjoyed last night a great deal. I hope you did as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course dear. How could I not? Well, if there was more fire I suppose, but Christina does not need to be around that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wolfram could not hold back a laugh and he squeezed her hand affectionately. \u201cNo,\u201d he agreed between chuckles, \u201cShe most certainly does not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat don\u2019t I need to be around?\u201d came a sleepy voice as Christina sat up and began to stretch.<br /> <br /> \u201cFire,\u201d the pair answered in unison. As they did, she suddenly stopped as she came from half to fully awake, arms hovering above her head before lowering slowly as the previous evening\u2019s events caught up to her waking mind.<br /> <br /> As Wolfram and Lizette turned their attention to her and started to shift closer, she nodded and her eyes lit up along with her own smile as she reached to take their hands in her own. \u201cYes,\u201d she agreed with a nod to them, \u201cMuch as I may love you both, the only fire in this bedroom shall be passion.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Epilogue</b><br /> <br /> To: 196 5791128768- Central Command<br /> <br /> From: 3345678898768769 Ajax<br /> <br /> NOTE: The agents connected to the Static Evolution Device were in Berlin and acted, so far as we can tell, largely within expectations. However, subtle guidance could not be administered, due to the fact that the beacon of Static Evolution Device has been damaged or disabled. In fact, they were more difficult to track, and almost finished while I was waiting for them to arrive. How they accomplished this is unknown.<br /> <br /> None of them are known to have had the expertise to do this. The smallest of the Hedge Tainted could have, but it is unclear how would she know about it and why. It was still functioning when the Unchained fled their compound in the summer\u2026perhaps she told them.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it will be increasingly difficult to guide them to fulfilling the Matrices unless we can track them.<br /> <br /> Recommend study the locations they have been at to determine what has gone wrong. This needs to be understood and fixed, or they might disrupt the next Matrix<br /> <br /> OVER<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XL</i><br /> <br /> Who could have done something like that? It wasn\u2019t Lizette.<br /> <br /> Not much to add really. The session only ran \u00be time then it was discussing downtime. Oh, and a glimpse of the next member of the group in among the downtimes. Not Christina or Marlene, obviously.<br /> <br /> Seems enough for now. See you in 1924. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-28-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:15:23-07:00","id":994504,"title":"","content":"So, a Beast up next?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:30:09-07:00","id":994601,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcemen