:"","content":"Oh, did the characters ever encounter &quot;Ajax&quot; in Berlin? Obviously without realizing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:44:35-07:00","id":994759,"title":"","content":"He was a vaguely described bar patron during the last session I drew no special attention to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:51:43-07:00","id":998101,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week, but here is a little something for Golden Eagle. This discusses the world changes overall between November 1922 and July 1924. Also, some tighter glimpses of Paris, Berlin, and Vienna. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> As an aside, if you read the journals last time the first night, Dearbh\u00e1il had a journal added. <br /> <br /> --<br /> The Charleston has hit. It started in America in 1923 and now, in 1924, it is all over Europe and North America, making it's way into North Africa and South America. In 1926, it will be inescapable, even in places like Beijing and Cape town, but for now, it is all over the west. Charleston parties are already breaking out, and people put record players on the windows of homes and shops, to see passersby stop what they are doing and dance in the street. It is difficult to bring across how different this is to someone living at the time. No song, no music, no such thing has ever been this ubiquitous. Many operas have taken the worlds of the wealthy and noble by storm, and tavern songs often popular with the less well off, but the Charleston shatters boundaries. If anything, the only boundary is the old and the young.<br /> <br /> At this point, Europe is fully into what is known as the Golden Twenties, or Happy Twenties. Paris is booming, and the Moulin Rouge has reopened. As we begin the Olympic Games are finishing up...they began in May and will end in a fortnight. As the economy booms, the quality of life is high, and the arts and music thrive. In Berlin, Radical changes to the economy have lead to an economic boom, and German artistic culture is known all over the world. Berlin would not see this height again until after the turn of the 21st century. Vienna has been successful as well, though the far left and right continue to clash and some worry about civil war. And Ireland is now it's own independent nation after being partitioned. Everything is better, and to many of the young the war is like a terrible, terrible dream. To their elders, it still haunts them. But people move on. And So Europe settles into a period of economic boom and joy it has never, as a continent, seen again.<br /> <br /> Cabaret, Jazz, Flappers, Moving Pictures. An upswelling of countries allowing women to vote, and as women's influence grows, so to does tolerance of queer lifestyles, especially in Berlin and to a slightly lesser degree Paris.<br /> <br /> Not everything is peachy, the Balkans struggle. But compared to the end of the century, it is like a paradise for them.<br /> <br /> Prince Werner holds power in Berlin, trying to implement socialist policies among the kine. But he watches the shadows, as the war between the Watch and the Pure rages on, but it is a war the Watch are slowly losing. Powerful as they are, the Pure have better numbers, better organization, and can go toe to toe with them, unimpressed by feats of ghostly power. Many of the Watch are bullies, and unprepared for the tide the Forsaken know only too well. They are not broken yet, but many have begun to flee, as the Pure become more aware of how to fight their foe. The sudden prosperity has not helped their cause either. Meanwhile Prince Sascha, Queen Woebegone and Queen Skadi continue to cooperate, and Sascha and Woebegone's fortunes grow with the rise in German prosperity, though how much is their doing can be debated. Meanwhile Skadi watches and waits for what she sees as the inevitable. She is, after all, a patient creature.<br /> <br /> In Paris, all has been well. Th\u00e9r\u00e8se has been reinstated into her position, the local Fae unwilling to Banish or kill her. She has been cultivating her power base since. The Changelings are very strong in Paris now with her rises in fortunes. Even so the Queen of Flowers and Lights has continued to have dealing with other Courts, including Berlin. The Kindred have similarly recovered from any losses due to the unpleasantness with the statuettes. The supernatural population grows.<br /> <br /> Europe rises from the ashes, a joyous, desperate dance, and rich and poor, without respect to national boundaries, they dance the Charleston. And as they dance, the darkness surrounds this last light of hope.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Next time we begin in 1924. One of the Spring Court of Paris\u2019s more underground operations suffers an attack. Unable to go to the police and suspecting supernatural involvement, the Chancellor turns to Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian, and their supernatural connections. Meanwhile a mysterious girl with a suitcase and a story arrives at the house, and people must decide who they will be going with to the Bastille Day Dance.<br /> <br /> See you then! Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T22:52:29-08:00","id":1001633,"title":"","content":"It is an age where the light of hope seems surrounded by darkness, we enjoy these final moments where women\u2019s rights and queer acceptance finally seemed to be on the rise, before they faded into a century of war and oppression.<br /> <br /> But let\u2019s step away from the real world a moment to Golden Eagle, where it is 1924, and the Olympics are winding down in Paris. A dirty secret of the Spring Court is about to come to light, and a mysterious woman approaches the Chateau suitcase in hand.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLI </i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 12 July 1924<br /> <br /> I just had to come back to France while the Olympics were going on. I will say that it did make for a thought-provoking walk through Paris though. Hearing so many different languages spoken all around me was interesting. It\u2019s not something that happens very often in my experience. The Olympics are nearing the end though, so the experience will be short lived.<br /> <br /> I met up with the others at the house and we caught up a bit and discussed what was happening now. Apparently Alla has been invited to go to the Moulin Rouge tonight to meet up with Marissa and Connie. There is also a party being held at the Palais in a couple of days. I am not really into going to such social gatherings but Dearbh\u00e1il might want to go and I would be happy to escort her. If that is the case I will do my best to copy the mannerisms of the people around me. My normal social skills are usually considered to be cold at best, or non-existent. I will fake it for her if needs be.<br /> <br /> After breakfast we has someone come calling on the group of us. Her name is Nicolette Dubois. She is a writer that really wants to work for us. She\u2019s not picky about the work either. She said that she\u2019d be happy to do anything we needed if she could only follow us and record our actions. She is writing a fictional story and plans on changing the names of places and people but wants to record the actual events that surround us. And that\u2019s where things get suspicious. She was very informed as to the extra normal abilities of most of our group and has claimed to have seen us involved in a gun fight at least once. She says that she has come across us and our exploits several times in the past but it was never feasible for her to introduce herself until now. We sent her back to her hotel so we could discuss things.<br /> <br /> I do not trust her. Neither does Dearbh\u00e1il. Wolfram is of the opinion that if we allow her to follow us we will at least know where she is and can keep her safe if needs be. Tatiana thinks that the girl has spirit, and is funny. Fenric just likes her. She may be spirited and earnest, but that doesn\u2019t mean that trouble won\u2019t come of the whole affair. Dearbhail read her desires and found that she really wants to write her book. Really wants to write it. The desire actually overshadows pretty much all else. When Dearbh\u00e1il looked at her to see if she was magical it came back that while she is not in fact magical she does have a magical effect on her. Probably having to do with the afore mentioned novel.<br /> <br /> The thing that concerns me is the trail of bodies she seems to leave behind. She has followed several people, presumably to write her novel about them, but things seem to conspire against them and they have all been killed or otherwise died. One of these individuals was Iris\u2019s first lover, before Dana was hired. In another case Nicholette\u2019s companion was attacked while she was there. She could not save him but managed to kill the attacker by hitting him with her typewriter. She said that she wanted to follow us around because she thought that at least some of us should manage to survive long enough for her to write her book. She also kept going on about how she was lucky. I was not sure if she considered herself lucky because she kept finding us or if it was because she managed to survive her prior companion\u2019s demise.<br /> <br /> Not long after all of that happened we got a call from Madeline in the Spring court. She was looking for Dearbh\u00e1il and asked if she could meet with her as soon as it was feasible. She said that it would be fine for other women to come as well as Dacian as long as they were discreet. Tatiana opted out of going since she is not the most discreet person and she knows this. Dearbh\u00e1il, Lizette and Dacian all went to Paris via the door we have in our Chateau and came back a fairly short time later. Dearbh\u00e1il gathered up the rest of us and we all went to Paris. As it turns out there are special hospitals in Paris that cater to woman that find themselves in trouble and need to have an unwanted pregnancy ended. Something happened at one of these hospitals and they needed our help to figure out exactly what happened. So, we all went. It turns out that the doctor, doctor\u2019s assistant and orderly were all killed. They were the only ones in the building at the time. It was a brutal killing. There was blood everywhere, and the bodies looked like they had been savaged by an animal. Tatiana and I used our wolf senses and came to the same conclusion. A female werewolf experienced her first change here in the hospital and the staff were the unfortunate casualties.<br /> <br /> We tracked the werewolf to where she was hiding using her blood to do so, and found that she was hiding in a house in the suburbs. After much explaining and Dearbh\u00e1il going around to the back door we entered the house and Tatiana made her way to the basement where the new werewolf was hiding. There were introductions and explanations about who and what we were, but the new girl, Marie, seemed convinced that she was a monster or witch of some kind. We explained several times that the old stories are not true and that we are not monsters or witches or anything like that. We are supernatural in some ways I suppose in that we are outside the \u201cnorm,\u201d but we are not monsters. Tatiana took the new girl through changing forms a few times to show her how to do it and assure her that she could maintain control in any form she took save Gauru. We also explained what happened at the hospital and that it was not her fault.<br /> <br /> We also met Marie\u2019s friend Clara, who also happens to be Lizette\u2019s friend, as well as Clara\u2019s little sister, Liselle. Liselle seemed rather keen on challenging anyone and anything. She was rather interested in the library and getting into sections that were marked off as being inappropriate for women. It was mainly more esoteric topics, but some occult things were mentioned. I think that is where Marie got the idea of witchcraft. Wolfram was more than interested in sharing real knowledge about occult matters with Liselle if she was really interested in learning it. <br /> <br /> Tatiana called Marcel le Reynard, another werewolf here in Paris, and asked if he would be able to ally himself with Marie so she would not be alone. There used to be many packs in Paris before the war, but since then the numbers have been decimated. There is pretty much just the one group of them now. Marcel said that he would keep an eye out for her and help her where necessary.<br /> <br /> Since she was supposed to have been out getting things for breakfast when everything happened Fenric went out and acquired the necessary items while we were going through the different forms and explaining things. After we were done explaining things we promised to keep in contact. Tatiana walked Marie back home prepared with the explanation that she got caught up in Olympic revels and Tatiana helped her out and decided to walk her home. Dacian followed and turned invisible before the door opened. Marie\u2019s father was less than pleased with his daughter and accused her of spending time with someone named Gerard. Presumably the man that got her into trouble in the first place. Dacian stayed long enough to make sure Marie would be okay before heading out.<br /> <br /> While they walked Marie back home the rest of us went back to the house. We got a message from Madeline saying that the Queen of Flowers and Lights is upset by the deaths of her people and she wanted a wergild paid on their behalf for the loss. If a wergild is not paid then she said that she would tell the other courts that her court was attacked. This would not be good for the hospitals in question since the location of at least one would become public knowledge and there are some that might object to what they do there. I personally do not see the problem with what the hospitals are doing. If a woman decides that she cannot take care of a child, or is assaulted and becomes pregnant then she should be able to do what needs to be done. I can see that some people would become upset by this though, and can understand why Madeline was stressing that only those that can be discreet be brought to help with the situation.<br /> <br /> So, we all met up in the Hollow and exchanged information. Dacian, Wolfram, Lizette, Dearbh\u00e1il and myself decided to go talk to the Queen of Flowers and Lights and see what she is willing to accept for the wergild. Tatiana decided to explore the area of Paris around the Moulin Rouge. Alla was asleep at the house.<br /> <br /> On our way to meet the Spring Queen we came across Therese who escorted us the rest of the way. She was rather challenging in her demeanor and dismissed Madeline out of hand. I do not know if she is this way with everyone, or just us due to our past history. The Queen of Flowers and Light was rather upset and demanded restitution. She asked us if we could provide her with new doctors to replace those that had been killed. We could not. We do not know any that would be able to work in the Spring court\u2019s clinics. We asked if there was anything else that she would accept as wergild and she inquired if we could pay cash to go to the families of those that were lost. This was an acceptable solution for all and Dacian, Wolfram and the Queen hashed out the details.<br /> <br /> After we left the Queen we went to go investigate Nicholette and see what she was doing. We made our way to her hotel and I tracked her sent to her room. We listened outside the room and only heard typing. Dacian let us into the room right next to hers in case we could hear anything else. We did not. She was just steadily typing away. Presumably on that book she says that she has in her heart.<br /> <br /> As soon as we arrived back at the house Christina asked me and Dacian if we or one of our male friends would be willing to escort Marlene to the dance in a few days. I told her that if I was going it was likely to be with Dearbh\u00e1il. When we enquired why Marlene needed an escort Christina explained that if Marlene was escorted to the dance by a friend it would be more socially acceptable than if she did not have an escort at all. It helps somehow with her social standing. Also, being escorted by a friend allows her to still appear to be single so she can look for a potential husband while she\u2019s there. Apparently these social events are used frequently to find mates. I do not understand that, but then I am generally not a part of the same social strata that Christina and Wolfram are. Not that you will find me complaining about that. I am not good at social things so it is just as well that I limit my exposure to such things. It would be good if I do not offend any of my pack mate\u2019s friends. I would not likely feel bad about insulting their friends, but I do not want to cause problems for Wolfram or Christina. <br /> <br /> Anyway, Dacian, not wanting to make decisions concerning Marlene without her knowledge, went to go talk to the woman in question. They apparently came up with the plan that he will escort her to the party in a couple of days.<br /> <br /> After all that Dacian and I got dressed up a bit nicer and went back to Paris. Dacian wanted to go to a couple of tailor shops and get some fabric to have Lizette make a very nice dress for Marlene. The wedding dress she made for Christina was very pretty, so the idea is that she can make something attractive for Marlene to wear to the dance. Sounds like a plan to me. After the shopping was done and fabric was returned to the house we were all ready to go to the Moulin Rouge. Overall it has been a rather busy day and it\u2019s not even over yet. We\u2019ll see what happens later tonight with Alla\u2019s meeting. Hopefully it won\u2019t be anything bad. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not running away.<br /> <br /> We are making sure the area is safe before our meeting.<br /> <br /> The meeting with Connie and the other one, Marissa.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, the meeting that Alla will be coming to later in her car.<br /> <br /> I am not afraid of the car! It is just very loud. It is not my fault no one warned me of the fireworks Lizette put in it before I sat in it.<br /> <br /> I know you do not care for the flashing lights. It is wise of you. The ones in that car are especially bad.<br /> <br /> Alright, volchonok, alright. Yes, we are in Paris so that we do not need to ride in that loud, flashing human thing. <br /> <br /> Of course I want to go to the meeting. Constancia will be there and asked for Alla to bring violent maniacs, so I will probably get to fight.<br /> <br /> It has not been a boring day! There was the writer, Nicholette. She was quite amusing. Almost like one of Alla\u2019s movies.<br /> <br /> Well, no, there\u2019s no sound in them, but it was how I imagine the people on the screen saying the words on the cards.<br /> <br /> The others do not trust her. It is true, everyone she has worked has wound up dead. Only after she mated with them though, so perhaps only Fenric will die.<br /> <br /> She says she wants to write a book of keys and the fairies say this is true. Dearbh\u00e1il also says she has magic on her. Maybe that is why she has seen us in our other forms and remembers.<br /> <br /> Marek and Dacian are spying on her now, if they are done with the Spring Court business. Then we will decide. I hope she stays. She is funny.<br /> <br /> The Spring Court business? The Spring Queen wants wergild from the new Uratha for killing the doctors.<br /> <br /> Wergild does not care about things like First Change. Those under her protection died, she is owed reparations.<br /> <br /> Peace, volchonok. I am sure Marek, Wolfram and Dacian will work out a way to shield Marie. Certainly if she will be satisfied with money, it could be arranged easily, and we will look after the new one.<br /> <br /> It is true, it is a sadness she did not have a volchonok to help her learn who she is. Not all Uratha are as lucky as me.<br /> <br /> Yes, we will have to make up for it. Marcel has promised to help as well, if she does not wish to leave the city for help. She has her friends as well, Clara and Liselle. They are almost as fierce as a volchonok, though less knowledgeable.<br /> <br /> You do not think a human can be fierce as a volchonok, eh? You should meet this Liselle. She might threaten you with a baseball bat too.<br /> <br /> It is... nevermind. She will threaten you with a tree branch, we shall say.<br /> <br /> ...yes volchonok. A baseball bat is a human version of a tree branch.<br /> <br /> Well, hopefully Wolfram gets her to read better books that the one that said I pee on my clothes.<br /> <br /> Of course I do not pee on my clothes!<br /> <br /> No, I do not want to go for a run. Besides, the light is failing, and soon the vampires will arrive. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 12th July 1924<br /> <br /> Today was supposed to be a fairly quiet day. Deciding on my dance date, perhaps listening to some Olympic news on the wireless, try and build a machine gun that shoots chainsaws (ultimate invention). However, stuff kept coming up.<br /> <br /> I am not actually sure whom I will invite. Christina is going with Wolfram, and would not go with a woman to something so fancy. Marlene, well, even if we were still seeing each other, Christina wants her escorted by a man to increase her desirability and have her meet a good husband at the dance. I have no idea where Dana is. Clara crossed my mind. She is sweet, and adores me, but perhaps she is too sweet. I don\u2019t know that it would be right to corrupt her. She also only just figured out some of the women are more than good friends at the salon after going for over three years, and I think she is still unsure of the specifics.<br /> <br /> So, Marlene and I are not physically involved anymore. Christina insisted that end when she, Wolfram and I got involved. Which is fun, but the only thing I don\u2019t like about Christina is her jealous side. She does not need to worry so much about other women. As for Marlene, well, she is not really bothered. We both had fun, but it was never serious.<br /> <br /> So the day started when a girl named Nicholette DuBois came to apply for a nonexistent job. She wanted to work with us cook, clean, travel act as an au pair, whatever we needed. She has a \u201cnovel in her soul\u201d she needs to \u201cget out.\u201d She actually arrived with a typewriter and suitcase. To \u201cget her novel out\u201d, she needs inspiration from traveling with great people. Only, the last three people she traveled with, including Iris\u2019s then boyfriend, died. She also was sharing their beds. She felt with several of us we would not all die off, and she apparently kept running into us. She noted she is \u201cvery lucky\u201d and had some sort of magical effect on her. At the very least, she knew our names; her foremost fear is not being unable to finish her novel, and the Catch did not apply.<br /> <br /> Several of us were suspicious; especially Marek and Dearbh\u00e1il, and we did not take the girl in yet. We suggested the hotel in Chantilly, so she could wait while we decided. She cheerfully agreed. Dearbh\u00e1il noted as soon as she left how good she was at putting on the sort of cheerful persona that she herself uses to get her way sometimes. It remains to be seen what we decide, though Wolfram, without trusting her per se, suggested we have her with us to keep an eye on her. We will see.<br /> <br /> You know, I wonder if you could just combine a car with a chainsaw and ride around on it, you know, park in the top and just speed up and saw enemy cars in half. Maybe with a rocket in the back. What would I call that, though? Chaincars? Sawmobiles? Autosaws? YES Autosaws.<br /> <br /> Autosaws will\u2026wait, this is my diary not my notebook.<br /> <br /> So while we waited I went to work on NOT a Autosaw for some reason, but I was called over by Dearbh\u00e1il in short order; Madeline, the Bright One Fairest Chancellor of the Spring Court, had asked her to investigate something requiring discretion\u2026and women, Dacian aside. She, I and Dacian went to meet Madeline at a caf\u00e9, where she explained the killings took place at a \u201chospital for women in trouble\u201d the Spring Court maintained. The scene and found a bloody mess; a doctor, nurse, and orderly were torn apart. <br /> <br /> Oh yes, a machine gun that shoots chainsaws, that was the reason. Anyway. <br /> <br /> It was sleazy. I mean the facility was clean, just I always knew of such hospitals but I had never seen one. And having to go to a back ally down steps to a basement door had me thinking more of violence than healing. I guess the subject is unpleasant for everyone. They always have been illegal and probably always will be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we got permission from Madeline to involve the others, vouching for Wolfram and Marek. I actually think Madeline was pleased to see Tatiana again. When she and Marek arrived, they needed little examination to determine what happened (which was good, my and Wolfram\u2019s psychometry was not forthcoming). A woman had her \u201cfirst change\u201d into a werewolf while being \u201ctreated.\u201d No one in the path of her rampage survived. Fortunately, as some of her blood was present (Tatiana was able to tell it from the other somehow) tracking her was simple. And awkward. <br /> <br /> You see they traced her to Clara Bellerose\u2019s house. Clara lived there with her younger sister Liselle Bellerose, and I was worried one of them had had an accident. Liselle answered the door, and inadvertently gave away the werewolf was at her house and was neither she nor Clara. She was aggressively protective, if less so against me, and quickly, with Clara\u2019s instance, gave up the game that her friend Marie (not sure her family name) was the one there, and hiding in the cellar. I give Tatiana a lot of guff, but to her credit when the young girl challenged her directly to keep her out of the cellar, she did not hurt her or even actively make her feel pathetic. She did, however, single-mindedly seek out Marie.<br /> <br /> I remember Clara mentioning Marie, but had not met her, unlike Liselle. She said she was quiet, and the Marie I met was. Tatiana came up to tell us the situation was under control, and that she and the local werewolves would help her. I tried to shield Liselle and Clara from as much of this as possible, but could not for all of it. Especially with Tatiana around.<br /> <br /> We left them to meet with the Spring Court. Th\u00e9r\u00e8se had dismissed Madeline and met us there herself. I had seen the Muse at salons a few times since our encounter with Skadi, but this was the first time in a Changeling situation. She seemed to want to ensure we knew she was there. The Queen of Flowers and Lights was, understandably, hell-bent on getting Wergild from the werewolves for their lost doctor, nurse, and orderly. Members of our group made some financial donations, and she seemed mollified. Overall the meeting fortunately ended amicably, Th\u00e9r\u00e8se\u2019s making very sure we knew she was there or no. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t understand Th\u00e9r\u00e8se\u2019s presence, at least in the sense of being alternative to Madeline. I wonder if relations between the two have soured? Outside Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian I deal with the Antlered Court so little I would not know. I do know the situation with the hospital was under Madeline\u2019s stewardship.<br /> <br /> But for now getting ready for the Moulin Rouge. I have not been there in almost a year, and it is always\u2026interesting\u2026to see what Marissa and Constancia have gotten up to. I suspect true to her name the \u201cPrincess of Evil\u201d is up to no good. Which is more fun for me. <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> Oh let\u2019s see. Dearbh\u00e1il used Kenning as well as Fleeting Spring on Nicholette, while Lizette used Fleeting Autumn. <br /> <br /> The Werewolf plot was very much the sort of thing where you toss it out and see how the players responded. There was certainly a point earlier and later in the story where I just let things sink in and watched people\u2019s reactions. That was fun.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, if you have more Comments or Questions let me know.<br /> <br /> As a note, changes in the USA have me deeply concerned. I am not just up and fleeing my home, but quite honestly I have to be prepared to leave if things become dangerous. What this means for you is I might abruptly and without warning, and these campaigns end. I don\u2019t want that to happen, but I also want to live. So there you go. Sorry. Be good to yourselves, and nice to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:54:43-08:00","id":1008258,"title":"","content":"Returning to Paris, 1924. After the revelations of last session, what can the group do but move on. A pair of Vampires at the Moulin Rogue promise intrigue, and the big dance is coming up. But a simple appraisal proves to be a far more complicated situation.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 12 July 1924<br /> <br /> We ended the evening by going to the Moulin Rouge and meeting up with Connie and Marissa. Our fae pack members went to go talk to the other fae that were at the club, Madeline and the manikin lady that was at Wolfram\u2019s bachelor party for a short while. I think her name is Marie Rouge. Fitting given the setting. The rest of us went to go talk to the Vampires. They had some information that they wanted to pass along to Alla and by extension, us. It turns out that they have a smuggler friend named Bernard LeRoi who has an item that he needs appraised. Not for its financial value, but its mystical abilities and worth. Wolfram perked right up and we agreed to meet with Bernard tomorrow at a warehouse. Meanwhile, Dearbhail, and Dacian were talking to Madeline, who was drinking rather heavily if I remember right. She was put in charge of finding replacement doctors for those that were killed during Marie\u2019s first change. I do not envy her the task.<br /> <br /> <br /> 13 July 1924<br /> <br /> We had time to kill during the day so I took it upon myself to make Wolfram\u2019s little girl Regina at toy spider. I figured that it wouldn\u2019t hurt to have a little extra luck around and since I had been planning on making it out of wood she would be able to chew on it as much as she wanted and not damage the toy. From what I\u2019ve observed little kids, especially when their teeth are coming in, will chew on anything they can get their hands on. When she gets older and stops chewing on thing I will make her a fetish that will grant her protection or luck. Either one would be good for a growing girl. Wolfram did not seem to mind the spider, but I may want to talk to him before I make his daughter a fetish. We are all pack, but I do not want to overstep the bounds of parenthood. <br /> <br /> While I was carving wood Alla was recruiting Connie and Marissa to talk to and take a look at Nicolette to make sure the young writer is legitimate. Later in the evening the other vampires were escorted through the Hedge to get to our chateau so they could do their thing. We invited Nicolette back to the chateau and the two vampires took turns questioning the young girl and using their gifts on her to determine if she was being honest with us. Apparently she is. They found out that she is obsessive, which we have observed. She is trusting. She is not being controlled by anyone and she is not a supernatural creature. She is not aware of the magical effect that has been placed on her, nor is she being magically compelled to write that book of hers. They also asked Nicolette about some of her prior employers and what happened to them. She said that some of them got sick and died, and one was assassinated. She also admitted that she was tired of getting stranded in different places when the person she worked for died. We also found out that she did not go into those relationships intending to become intimate with her boss. It just sort of happened. After Connie and Marissa had vetted Nicolette Wolfram offered her a job working for us. We haven\u2019t worked out exactly what her duties will be, but we will come up with that soon enough.<br /> <br /> After we vetted Nicolette some of us went to go talk to Bernard. It was Lizette, Wolfram, Alla and myself that went to the meeting. We met up with Bernard, who is a vampire, and two hired hands of his and then we all went to the warehouse. When we got there it was obvious that something was wrong. The guards that he had stationed outside of the warehouse were gone and we heard sounds coming from around the side of the building. The air was thick with the smell of blood. I\u2019m not sure if the others picked up on that but I sure did. I went around to the side of the building with the two hired men and found a manifested murder spirit eating the remains of the missing guards. Needless to say a fight ensued. The spirit hit me pretty hard, so I hit her right back. One of the hired men managed to hit her as well. The other man only managed to hit his friend. The sound of fighting brought in the others who all lent their aid in attacking the murder spirit. Alla was the last person to hit the spirit before she fled by jumping into the Seine. I them jumped after her and followed her down river. She hit me again, but I managed to get the final blow on her before we got too far down the river. I then swam back to meet up with the rest of the pack. I will admit though that it was good to be able to do something about such a dangerous spirit. Usually my prey is human. I only hunt spirits on occasion and when I must to satisfy Siskur dah. I suppose that I should make more of an effort to deal with problem spirits. Perhaps Tatiana would join me on a hunt sometime. I\u2019m sure that she would enjoy it. <br /> <br /> When I got back I found out that I had missed a second murder spirit who had been inside of the warehouse. The others walked in to the building and were attacked. The spirit managed to hit Lizette really hard bringing her down almost from the start. The others attacked the murder spirit and wounded her enough that she decided to go incorporeal to avoid getting hit anymore. Unfortunately for the spirit Wolfram possessed his Geist, the spirit that uses him as a host, and went incorporeal as well. The spirit then tried to attack Wolfram, who had used a gift earlier to make magical flames surround him. The spirit did not see these flames and she was mortally wounded by them when she attacked Wolfram. Our resident occultist came back to himself afterwards. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s about when I got back. I briefly shifted to Gauru form to heal the wounds I had taken and then we investigated the building further and found no more murder spirits. At first we thought that the statuette that Bernard had gotten a hold of had intentionally summoned the murder spirits, but after using gifts we learned that the statue just bided its time and waited for the murder spirits to come to it and take care of the guards, which they did. All I found was footprints heavy in the dirt on the floor that looked like they belonged to the statue. It was as if the statue jumped down off of the plinth that it was standing on. Lizette used a gift to see exactly what happened and found out that is exactly what happened. The statuette jumped down once the coast was clear and walked off. <br /> <br /> Bernard described the statuette to Wolfram and we discovered that it was a statue of the Indian Goddess Kali. Apparently she is associated with killing and blood, which is likely what attracted the murder spirits to the statuette. I supposed that it should not surprise me that there are religions out there that have gods and goddesses directly tied with murder and death. I know that the Romans had gods for everything, even different parts of the doorway to a house had a god associated with it. Death is a part of life, so it makes sense that there is a goddess of death in the Indian culture. Usually the statues of gods and goddesses don\u2019t get up and move though, so this one is unique. Perhaps it is inhabited by a spirit? Or it could have some other kind of magical effect on it that give it sentience and semblance of life. We will not know for certain until Wolfram can get a look at the actual statue, and to do that we need to find the statuette and bring it back. I would rather be done with the whole affair, but it is possible that the wandering statue could intentionally or inadvertently do harm to other people and Wolfram will want to try and stop that from happening. <br /> <br /> Tatiana will be upset that she missed the fight. She had decided not to come along because she thought that meeting with Bernard was just going to be a boring exchange of information that she is not much interested in. We of course were not expecting the murder spirits to be there, but they definitely made things more exciting. Lizette would probably disagree with me about the exciting part though. She was badly hurt by the spirit in the warehouse. Both spirits hit rather hard, as I and others can attest. We will need to get Dearbhail and anyone else that knows the healing gifts to take a look at Lizette\u2019s wounds and see what they can do to heal her. I do not like seeing my pack mates in pain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Would you stop rubbing it in, volchonok?<br /> <br /> Yes, I know I missed fighting a pair of violent woman spirits.<br /> <br /> How was I to know there would be fighting!? They were supposed to go look at some old statue, not fight spirits.<br /> <br /> I do not know what kind of magic the statue was. Apparently the kind of magic that makes it walk away.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we will probably go looking for it. Perhaps there will be more spirits to fight later. A fight would be good.<br /> <br /> I told you to stop rubbing it in, volchonok! Constancia was just speaking of us teasingly or some such. Perhaps there will be violence later though, with the other business she is working on for us.<br /> <br /> No, it will probably not be burning a church. That would make Wolfram and Lizette sad. And it would make the other one right, and we cannot have that.<br /> <br /> The other one, Marissa. <br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not angered. Not really.<br /> <br /> She is just being unkind to Greta. Or perhaps kindest, in the long run. They have not spoken, or written since we left Berlin.<br /> <br /> Of course it is possible that Greta does not wish it. She was very upset. <br /> <br /> I have already said I am not angry at her! You are testing my patience, volchonok.<br /> <br /> What? Oh, when we spoke to Nicolette?<br /> <br /> Well, we did not want violence then, foolish volchonok. We were speaking with the writer to see if the others would stop being foolish and let her join us. <br /> <br /> Yes, they did decide to. Connie did not find anything damning in her mind, just that she is very good at seducing people and not bothered by anything that she has seen, including my transformation and the deaths of many, many of her mates. But she probably hasn\u2019t betrayed any of them.<br /> <br /> Well, Connie could not be certain someone had not meddled with her memories. This is a thing that could be done, apparently. <br /> <br /> I do not like it either.<br /> <br /> No, it is not a reason to run away into the night! There is business, and there will be for a time. We will run later, volchonok. Be patient.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 13th July 1924<br /> <br /> So I am resting at home after being badly hurt. May as well catch the journal up.<br /> <br /> The trip to the Moulin Rouge was uneventful. Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian saw Madeline and Marie Rouge, so they went to sit with them, while the rest joined Constancia and Marissa. It was mostly Vampire business. Connie had a lead she was following up on, and more immediately a member of the group called the Carthians wanted to meet with us. All the rest of the Carthians we had come across were hostile to Alla, but this Bernard LeRoi was not. Though Connie helpfully pointed out he was a criminal more than once.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Constancia and Marissa kept going back to burning churches, which Wolfram and I found rather upsetting. Apparently Connie burned one but does not make it a habit, which of course Marissa was trying to encourage her to do. Tatiana seemed amused more than anything else. She would. She is not Catholic. You know, I wonder why Dearbh\u00e1il has not worked on Marek to convert yet. I think it would be good if more of us were Catholic. Also, there was teasing Marissa about not having contacted Greta. Their loud falling out in Berlin was the last time the two women had spoken to one another. Tatiana seemed put out that she hadn\u2019t, but I don\u2019t blame her. Greta is a pain. <br /> <br /> At the end of the night we agreed to see Bernard the next day, and Connie and Marissa agreed to come with us for interviewing Nicholette before hand. I went on to sleep after that. It was a rough day, and the visions in the hospital were nightmarish. No wonder Madeline was drinking so much.<br /> <br /> Today I kept busy working on Marlene\u2019s dress and touching up my own. As a noble, Marlene needs to wear pastels and light colors to show she is unmarried. Dull, but I can work with it. Also touched up my, Christina\u2019s, and Wolfram\u2019s outfits. Aside from a brief run to a caf\u00e9 that was my day.<br /> <br /> I did not have time to work on a machinegun that shoots chainsaws (ultimate invention) or an autosaw. Though I realize shorter term I have not modified my car much recently. I should really get on that. I wonder if I can rig it to fly somewhere if needed. You know throw a switch or something. It could be a bomber, and I could put more guns on it.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Of course, it might draw unwanted attention. Ah well, my Cadillac Sedan does now anyway some. I suspect it is the Vickers. Or because it is bright green. Or the oil slick or caltrop dispenser. I wonder if I can design something so that it drops unpinned grenades behind it too. Mayhem! Anyway.<br /> <br /> The evening was a second interview with Nicholette with the Vampires present. Yellow-eyed Constancia would use some of her Mekhet powers on her, including reading her mind while Alla lead the discussion. To her credit, Nicholette was a sport about it. All in all, from our driving a tractor through her brain, the most suspicious thing we got was that she saw a werewolf change without losing her mind. I was starting to feel sorry for her.<br /> <br /> Still, she has had an eventful life. She has been to Anatolia, to Egypt, all over the Mediterranean, traveling with this handsome adventurer or that. She had lost boyfriends to assassins, the desert, and traps in pyramids. She had had all sorts of torrid affairs. Though unlike Dana, she was the sidekick, always tagging along. Still, like Dana, she had seen much of the world.<br /> <br /> They actually had Nicholette go upstairs and back in while Connie reported what she had read and they asked new questions (and conducted more mind reading) based on that. But in the end, she was hired, and moved into the Chateau tonight.<br /> <br /> While Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il made sure that went smoothly, Wolfram, Alla, Marek and I went to investigate the whole statue thing. Tatiana wandered off. Bernard LeRoi was a sleazebag, but a friendly sleazebag. He gave us a general breakdown, and we walked to his warehouse along the quays. We immediately saw a problem when his guards were missing. Marek heard some sounds of eating from around the corner, and he and a pair of ghouls LeRoi had went to investigate. The guards were being eaten by some sort of murder Spirit. It looked like a multi-eyed flapper the bottom half of whose face was a giant mouth. The ghouls opened up, and it was hit but not hurt badly. Marek attacked and Alla raced over there in a blur. Sadly by the time I readied my Tommy Gun the Spirit had jumped into the Seine. Marek jumped after it. When he eventually returned, he had killed it.<br /> <br /> The rest of us went into the warehouse to investigate. There we were ambushed by a second Spirit, which bit the absolute hell out of me. I had to spend the rest of the fight trying to evade it. LeRoi managed to hurt this one, and between he, Wolfram and Alla it was down by the time Marek returned.<br /> <br /> The statue was indeed missing. The four of us looked around, and found it likely jumped down from the pedestal and walked out. I used my Contracts of Animation to look closer. It waited to leave until it attracted the murder Spirits. I realized after a moment why\u2026it was a statue of the Indian Goddess Kali. I don\u2019t know much about her, but I heard about her devotees in the last century. Who knows what havoc it could wreck in Paris?<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Wait, bad Mayhem.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we returned rather than immediately searching. I am rather missing a chunk of my mass, and am hoping for some healing from Dearbh\u00e1il. I\u2019d like to not be wounded for days again. I shall sleep till she arrives.<br /> <br /> If I can ever get comfortable. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> Lizette and Marek\u2019s journal disagree as to whether Lizette went to talk to the other Fae. Only the Spring Courtiers went, Lizette did not. At the other table, there was talk of Th\u00e9r\u00e8se\u2019s ambition, and the difficulty of replacing lost staff at the clinic. Oh, and Marie Rouge was afraid of being set on fire, since she last saw most of the PCs at the bachelor party. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, Constancia used Auspex to extract information from Nicolette, and the PCs fought basically murder spirits of a sort at the statue site. As for what the statue was, well\u2026<br /> <br /> We should have the next chapter in two weeks. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:39:56-08:00","id":1008361,"title":"","content":"My eyes took a left and my brain took a right and I misread the part with the dress and the car. It came out as:<br /> <br /> &quot;Today I kept busy working on Marlene\u2019s dress and touching up my own. As a noble, Marlene needs to wear pastels and light colors to show she is unmarried. Dull, but I can work with it. I wonder if I can rig it to fly somewhere if needed. You know throw a switch or something. It could be a bomber, and I could put more guns on it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:00:53-08:00","id":1010838,"title":"","content":"While such a dress would certainly qualify for mayhem, you should be careful about giving Lizette such ideas Omenseer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T17:48:59-08:00","id":1010877,"title":"","content":"What can I say? I'm a generous person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T17:50:26-08:00","id":1010881,"title":"","content":"Are you suggesting Marlene would be allowed to go around...gundressed?<br /> <br /> I'll get my coat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T02:20:23-08:00","id":1014657,"title":"","content":"Hee hee hee gundressed. Ahem.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the day before the big dance! When a rogue statue is bringing Spirits into Paris, it seems a good time to bring our fledgling Werewolf along to hunt the Spirits and their source. But then Dearbh\u00e1il finds herself reminded of struggles from a home left far away.<br /> <br /> Marek and Alla\u2019s players unexpected had to miss at the last moment due to circumstances outside their control. However, the group remained together most of the session, and Lizette covered the events more thoroughly than usual, maintaining her focus despite distraction. Mostly. Some might find things clearer if the read Tatiana and Lizette in reverse order.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLIIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What? No, volchonok, Marie is not a very tall human pup.<br /> <br /> Most human women are not taught to fight. She did very well, considering. She even hurt that spirit drowning Wolfram.<br /> <br /> Liselle was not there to learn to be a proper Uratha, so it does not matter how well she did. <br /> <br /> Marek was involved, speaking with the local spirits. This was supposed to be a long shot but good practice hunting, we did not expect fighting. So it seemed safe enough.<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, we thought it was a long shot because we thought of asking Ocranny far later than we ought have. I\u2019ve already apologized to him, leave it be.<br /> <br /> Yes, he is why we were able to succeed before Marek, once we brought him to the right place.<br /> <br /> Well, the statue was very short, so it could not move far. Wolfram thought of this.<br /> <br /> Murder spirits would likely be disinclined to carry. I do not know how the large head walking on its hair would carry it anyway. The drowned woman of the murderous flappers would be more capable, but still... carrying is not murder.<br /> <br /> Lizette has appeased it and I am certain they will talk the vampire into selling it, so all is well there.<br /> <br /> The red haired woman? She will probably not try to buy it. She had nothing to do with the statue, she just resonated with murder.<br /> <br /> I do not know precisely what she intended, but her backpack smelled like Lizette before she blows things up.<br /> <br /> Something about Ireland. That\u2019s what she and Dearbh\u00e1il spoke of earlier. The red haired woman was trying to get Dearbh\u00e1il to help incite rebellion. Whoever she intended to kill, it made our songbird very angry.<br /> <br /> She was yelling in Irish. There is no human tongue like there is First Tongue. And at the cafe it just seemed complicated. I do remember she said the woman was acting like Therese, therefore foolish.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, also I was distracted by Liselle\u2019s patting my head. When I am in Urhan, sometimes I am as foolish as a volchonok. The treat Wolfram got for me was also distracting. I should remember, it is much easier to get raw meat when you are a wolf.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is also much easier to get raw meat when you catch it yourself. But I cannot run now - It is Bastille Day and Elena is expecting me. We will run later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 14th July 1924<br /> <br /> I am getting ready for the dance, and resting while Marlene gets ready to assist me. It\u2019s been a long day, but today has gone better than yesterday. That is, I confess, a low bar. The dance will be the final determining factor, of course.<br /> <br /> So last night while I was laid out on the couch waiting for Dearbh\u00e1il, Nicolette came in with some aspirin and prepared me a strong alcoholic drink to help me with the pain until Dearbh\u00e1il arrived. I was I admit mildly annoyed when Dearbh\u00e1il dismissed her in a brusque manner, but this was eclipsed by how angry Dacian made me. Nicolette left, as requested, and left the drink she was preparing me, so Dacian grabbed it and drank it himself. He is quite an impudent ass. I realize I have a ways to go before I can see myself as a proper lady in any environment, but at least I can console myself I am nowhere near as boorish as Dacian. This may even trump the leering thing.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il, unlike Dacian, set things right. She healed me and made sure I was all right. Wolfram fussed over me the rest of the evening. He is such a dear. I felt better as I fell asleep. Dearbh\u00e1il finished healing me at breakfast. I can\u2019t be wounded for the dance, now can I?<br /> <br /> Breakfast went well, as Dacian did not try to steal my drink while I was not badly wounded. Probably wise. Tatiana had the idea of getting Marie to go with us to track the statue to help her learn, and bring Ocranny to help us find it. Much better than my idea of looking off the top of the Eiffel Tower through binoculars, but at the same time less fun. I suggested as I was going to the Bellerose residence they could come with me. Marie is a friend of Liselle so I supposed Liselle might know where she was. Also, I had settled on asking Clara to the dance, and it is Bastille Day and the Olympics are going on. So Marie could be anywhere.<br /> <br /> Maybe we could have used a plane? We could have had bombs in case we saw it! Ah but it would not have worked anyway. <br /> <br /> We got there, and Clara greeted us. I spoke to her about the dance. She agreed, though I don\u2019t think she quite gets the implications of my interest or invitation. It will be fun regardless. Presuming she does not pick me up. Or steal my drink.<br /> <br /> Liselle was happy to go with us to meet Marie, who was meeting her near the Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es. We set out on foot, as Paris in the midst of gay celebration was rather difficult to navigate by motorcar (but probably not autosaw. Mayhem!) We walked while she tried to suss out our plans and we gave her a basic explanation. We stopped for cotton candy (which Liselle, Tatiana and I enjoyed, the others avoided), and Dearbh\u00e1il had a fateful conversation with a woman named Caoimhe. <br /> <br /> Christina still likes to call cotton candy fairy floss, like they did when I was a kid. Probably a reason for that. But I am getting off track again.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe was an attractive Irish redhead. A Spring Court Fairest. She seemed to try to motivate Dearbh\u00e1il with talk of revolution, then moved on. Dearbh\u00e1il seemed to make a point to ask The Queen of Flowers and Lights about her, but she did not seem important at the time.<br /> <br /> We met Marie, and discussed the situation. Once we set off though the celebratory Bastille Day crowd, with Tatiana and Marie in wolf form, following Ocranny (with Wolfram, who had merged with his Geist so he could see Ocranny too.) Ocranny was using a power to seek murderous energy, and it led us across the Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es down toward the stadium. On the way we saw Caoimhe again; Tatiana, Marie, and apparently Ocranny made a direct line for her, and Dearbh\u00e1il whispered something to Dacian about her backpack. He declined to try to take it, but then it seemed a very difficult lift, as Caoimhe and Tatiana had a lot of attention. Tatiana was keeping Caoimhe away from the stadium (not that we were too close) and about to make a move for the pack herself when Dearbh\u00e1il stepped in. <br /> <br /> The two argued, but they argued in Irish, so I could not really follow the conversation. I caught an \u201cErin go Braugh\u201d in the chatter from Caoimhe. Tatiana grabbed the bag with her mouth as they talked and brought it to me, and I found a quite frankly impressive rigging of explosives. I neutralized them. Caoimhe stormed off, and Dearbh\u00e1il wanted to go to a nearby caf\u00e9. She wanted Irish whiskey, and this being the first time Ireland as a nation was in the Olympics, got it. Caoimhe was with a group called the Irish Republican Army, and was going to kill the British Olympic Team while there. I saw the bomb, a well-done piece, and she would have taken them out while not destroying the stadium. Not the usual anarchist garbage as likely to blow up the user as anyone else. Dearbh\u00e1il intends to make sure she speaks to The Queen of Flowers and Lights. That seems fair. <br /> <br /> Caoimhe had lost her family to the British, and sought to get blood revenge. I understood. I lost my family too. Like her, even my Fetch died. But no amount of dead Germans brought them back. Maybe I can talk to her. I can\u2019t exactly say I didn\u2019t kill a ton of Germans before that happened though.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, Tatiana kept getting head scratches from Liselle. They got some meat treats from a vendor. It was kind of adorable. Marie for her part was disinterested in head scratches. This kept up through the hunting. I mean, it is fair, I like it when Christina scratches me behind the ear. But that is not quite the same thing. I don\u2019t think, I mean I would not want Liselle to scratch me behind the ear. It was not weird when Liselle scratched Tatiana\u2019s head despite me making it weird here.<br /> <br /> I wonder if a mechanical head scritcher would work. Four arms, scratch four heads at once. Keep four cats, or dogs, or werewolves happy. Now that could be a home defense device, scratching faces off or grabbing people. You know, if it could grab people and ignite, maybe it could set them on fire. Or throw them, on fire, at other people. Put it on wheels and send it in.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> We decided to try closer to the Seine, since we might have better luck there. It turned out that was right. Ocranny lead us to a flophouse, which looked pretty run down. Wolfram used his powers to haunt it while we waited and Tatiana got more scratches, and found a room had been turned into an abattoir, with several bloody bodies and two foreign men, I think Italian, with knives. They were clearly influenced by the statue.<br /> <br /> We decided on frontal assault. Dearbh\u00e1il blessed us and stayed to watch Liselle. The crowds were much thinner on the docks, and much less friendly. Which is good, for all Liselle\u2019s bravado she is no adventuress. <br /> <br /> I used her magic to help bless my Thompson, and charged in it in hand and chainsaw on my back. Tatiana was in the lead. We made it to the room, where I gunned down one of the men and she mauled the other. Then two Spirits, a Murder Spirit and some head Spirit, materialized, and a drowned woman Spirit joined in quickly. The latter two went after Wolfram. Wolfram and Tatiana put down the Murder Spirit as the drowned spirit tried to suffocate Wolfram. Because of the melee, I switched to chainsaw (despite it not being awakened) and made short work of it, and we whittled down the head. A second Murder Sprit appeared and was cut down.<br /> <br /> Dacian found the statue, and he and Wolfram figured out it was summoning the Sprits as blood had spilled on it and started a ritual. It took a human sacrifice to end. Tatiana and I had just killed, and could use that as the specifications were vague how it was done, as Dacian understood it. It was still summoning Spirits, so we had to close the ritual. Tatiana is best at fighting, but hopeless at Occult ritual. I only knew the basics, but with some Autumn Court training and Wolfram\u2019s assistance I set to it. One Murder Spirit arrived, which was dispatched by the others, and then we finished the ritual. <br /> <br /> We left along with the fleeing tenants, and met up with Dearbh\u00e1il and Liselle. Liselle reminded me that I was taking her sister out, and chided me to get ready, just as she had to go get ready herself. <br /> <br /> So here I am. Getting some help getting ready from Christina and Marlene. Then off to pick up Clara Bellerose in my motorcar.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, it will be a fun night. I plan to dance until I can\u2019t walk, and just maybe expand Miss Clara Bellerose\u2019s horizons a little.<br /> <br /> Sexy Mayhem! <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> Ocranny the Totem spirit could look for a certain resonance, one of its powers. We actually realized this going over options at the start of the session. That plus the fact we decided with two missing to put off the dance for next session and cover other events, lead me to have the PCs meet Caoimhe. Originally, she was supposed to be met at the dance, and the follow up scene (and Dearbh\u00e1il having to decide whether to support or turn on her) was to take place the next day. I think the change of plans went well, and Ocranny\u2019s power revelation made the progression with Caoimhe even more natural than it otherwise would have been.<br /> <br /> Dearbh\u00e1il had long had a dislike for Englishmen and a strong feeling for her homeland, so I thought it would be interesting to see whether she was willing to go toward the dark side with that or not by setting her up with a very dangerous potential friend.<br /> <br /> Wolfram used Boneyard at the flophouse.<br /> <br /> The statue required a Presence + Occult roll to placate. As Tatiana and Lizette had gone first and killed the two humans, it had to be one or both. Lizette can\u2019t reroll 10s, but has a healthy pool, and I let her apply her benifet to magic occult rolls from her Autumn Mantle to the ritual. So it worked out fairly quick. <br /> <br /> Just about to the end of the first part of this story. Next session is the ball, and after one session after that we will begin the next leg start of the New Year with a slightly changed cast. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T01:55:52-08:00","id":1021195,"title":"","content":"The night of the big dance. Everyone dressed to the nines, either enjoying some traditional dancing in one room or Charleston in the other. Here are a couple accounts of the dance.<br /> <br /> Note Tatiana went to a village dance, not the one everyone else was at. So her journal does not touch on what everyone else was doing.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 15 July 1924<br /> <br /> Tonight was the big dance. I asked Dearbh\u00e1il if she would like to go with me and she accepted. Marlene was escorted by Dacian, Christina was escorted by Wolfram, Lizette escorted Clara and Alla was escorted by Fenric. The ladies all looked lovely. Most of them had dresses made by Lizette, so they were quite good. It seems that my friend is just as good at making mundane things like clothes, as she is at making implements of destruction, usually on fire. <br /> <br /> As soon as we arrived at the dance Dearbh\u00e1il headed straight for the Queen of Flowers and Light to talk to her about someone that she\u2019d come across earlier. Her name is Kiva (not spelled like that). Kiva is an Irish compatriot that apparently had made a bomb and was planning on making it into the Olympic games and setting it off near the British team. Her intention had been to kill the British athletes. The others caught her and divested her of the bomb before she could actually do anything, so that was good. Dearbh\u00e1il had made it her aim to talk to the Spring Queen when we arrived at the dance because the would be bomber is a threat to the Fae folk in Paris. <br /> <br /> While Dearbh\u00e1il was taking care of her business I took care of some of my own. I noticed that Marie was at the dance, as was Marcel, so I decided to introduce the two to one another. I figured that Marcel could lend Marie aid and training should the need arise, and Marie would have someone local to talk to about Uratha related matters. So, I introduced them and we talked for a little bit. When I noticed that Dearbh\u00e1il was done with her talk with the Queen of Flowers and Light I excused myself. Dearbh\u00e1il made her way over to me and we danced. She dances as nicely as she sings. I by comparison was not all that good, but we made a good couple on the dance floor. I am not normally fond of such events, but this one was interesting and engaging. I certainly enjoyed dancing with my Fae lady.<br /> <br /> After a while someone announced that there would be a Tango. I am somewhat familiar with the dance so I asked Dearbh\u00e1il if she would like to dance it with me. She agreed and we did our best. I think we did pretty well all things considered. Fenric danced with Lizette, Wolfram danced with Christina and Dacian danced with the Queen of Flowers and Light. They were particularly good and made a very good pair on the dance floor. Most of the attention was on them so I didn\u2019t feel quite so self-conscious.<br /> <br /> Once the Tango was over Dearbh\u00e1il decided that she wanted to socialize with some different people, so I took the initiative and asked Alla if she would like to dance. I think she was a little surprised, but agreed. It wasn\u2019t the same as dancing with Dearbh\u00e1il, but it was still nice. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Wolfram had met someone while at the dance. She is a singer and her stage name is Amethyst. They talked for a while before walking over to talk to Dearbh\u00e1il. I did not meet this new singer, but Dearbh\u00e1il seemed to get along with her well. They talked about their profession for a while as far as I could tell. Alla also talked to her sister for a while. They seem to get along, but some of the smiles seemed a bit forced, so I\u2019m not so certain that they are that close to one another.<br /> <br /> Later I decided to talk to Jamal, who I was surprised to see at the dance. We caught up for a while, talking business for the most part. He mentioned that he had talked to Alla. He said that she had invited him to the Chateau so we could all discuss the Golden Eagle with him. It seemed like a good idea to me. We have not had much contact with Jamal lately and we had agreed to give him our thoughts and findings on the device. We have also discovered other artifacts that seem to be of similar make, so it seemed prudent to mention those statues to him as well. Granted those statues caused a good deal of trouble for us, but they were of a similar design to the Eagle.<br /> <br /> All told I had a good time at the dance. I am not usually a social person except with those that I know. I am usually wary about meeting strangers, just because I\u2019m a cautious individual, I always assume that there is more to them that they say or show. Some might call me paranoid, but I prefer to call myself a realist. There are a lot of dangerous people in the world, and I make it my business to protect my pack and my family from them if needs be. This dance however seemed to have a much lighter air to it. Everyone seemed to get along well. Marlene met several potential suitors. Wolfram made a new friend. Given that he just went up and introduced himself to her I will guess that she is Claimed like he is. The only real serious business that I saw was Dearbh\u00e1il\u2019s conversation with the Queen of Flowers and Light. Overall it was an enjoyable evening. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Titania\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> \u201cIvan arrived as the wedding feast was already in progress. Princess Elena saw Ivan and jumped up from her seat at the table. \u2018There is my dear fiance, not this coward sitting next to me!\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> Elena cleared her throat. Tatiana looked over at her and saw that a couple of the other parents were standing with her beloved, hiding their amusement with varying levels of success. She looked at the many children surrounding her, a couple asleep in each other\u2019s arms, but most hanging on her every word and getting restless at her pause. Tatiana winked at Elena and continued, \u201cThe tsar, confused at this turn of events, asked for an explanation and the princess gladly told him everything. The tsar, obviously, was furious with the brothers Dmitriy and Vasiliy and threw them in prison. Ivan and Elena got married themselves and were so happy with each other that they never parted.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTell the story of the frog princess!\u201d \u201cNo, tell the story of Marya!\u201d \u201cI want to hear about the princess who never smiled!\u201d The children clamored as soon as she gave them the small flourish she traditionally ended her stories with. <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m afraid not, children. It is late, and time for the young ones to go home.\u201d Elena raised an eyebrow at Tatiana. <br /> <br /> Tatiana stood and clapped her hands. \u201cElena is right. Come now, there will be another time for stories.\u201d She ushered them along.<br /> <br /> As they returned to the square, Tatiana stole many glances, imagining her in the red bell-shaped dress Lizette had made for herself, or with the Irish green shawl Dearbh\u00e1il had worn and herself in Marek\u2019s warm brown suit. As she imagined it, her mental image twisted a little so that she was wearing Dacien\u2019s bright green pocket square and bowtie and Elena was in Alla\u2019s fabulous sparkling dress. Elena glanced over as Tatiana snorted aloud. \u201cWhat are you thinking of? Imagining all of the more beautiful women you could be dancing with in Paris?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, my love, I am but a poor soldier, from a long line of humble Russian country folk. When even the best artists of Paris could imagine nothing more beautiful than you, how could I hope to?\u201d Tatiana pulled her close, and kissed her forehead. Elena rolled her eyes but leaned into her embrace.<br /> <br /> The children put to bed, the adults continued with their celebration for a time, with more dancing, singing and drinking. Tatiana had had perhaps a bit more than she ought have when Elena found her sharing war stories with some of the Greek refugees. \u201cTatiana? Will you walk me home?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana jumped to her feet, having to steady herself on the shoulder of one of the men nearby. \u201cOf course! Is it that late?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is, quite.\u201d Elena gave her a small smile.<br /> <br /> Tatiana offered her an arm and she took it. They walked together in quiet companionship, content in each other\u2019s presence. When they reached Elena\u2019s small house, Tatiana opened the door for her love with an excessive flourish and followed her in. When the door shut, she wrapped her arms around Elena from behind, pulling her close and burying her face in the shorter woman\u2019s neck. \u201cI can stay here tonight, yes?\u201d <br /> <br /> Elena\u2019s kiss, after she turned around, was answer enough.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 15th July 1924<br /> <br /> Well, last night went incredibly well.<br /> <br /> I finally let everyone see my red dress I had been working on for some time. I considered something more butch, but I would get a lot less leeway to dance with other ladies if it looked more than playful. Marlene and Christina\u2019s dresses were also gorgeous and Wolfram\u2019s suit was top notch. When all was ready, I jumped in my car and drove out to get Clara Bellerose. <br /> <br /> Clara was my date. Wolfram was taking Christina, Dacian taking Marlene, Marek taking Dearbh\u00e1il, Fenric taking Alla, and Tatiana was going herself to something smaller in Chantilly. There must be someone pretty interesting there to distract her from Madeline.<br /> <br /> Clara was wearing blue and looked enchanting. She could not stop giggling. I complemented her and she giggled more. We made our way to the hotel, and there were a lot of people there. My dazzling red and gold jewelry was self-defense in part; I needed to be visible with all those tall people on the floor.<br /> <br /> Stilts are of course right out; I mean I have to hold them. Also, I am likely to start stepping on feet. But if I could make a special exoskeleton, that might work. With optional flamethrowers in case you and your dance partner are attacked. Or maybe a buzzsaw launcher, to prevent accidentally setting people on fire on the dance floor. I mean unless you want to set everyone on fire on the dance floor; I am not judging.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Wait, actually I should be judging. Maybe at least a tray that can pop out to offer tea? <br /> <br /> Focus.<br /> <br /> I went to the modern dance area with Clara, and we starting cutting the rug. She loves to dance and was adorable. She kept giggling, though. I will be honest, I was a bit worried that she was laughing at me, but no, it was because she found the situation hilarious. That\u2026was not quite what I wanted to hear either.<br /> <br /> I had a dance with Christina (perfect grace) and Wolfram (impeccable style) on the modern and classic dance floors respectively. Wolfram even danced with Miss Skitters once. I did also dance with a shy and blushing Nicolette. I would have danced with Marlene, but she was attending to the important job of meeting potential suitors. I don\u2019t blame her. <br /> <br /> I just finished dancing with Lucille Nadeau, from the Salon, when the Tango call went out. She was sporting a more butch chic. Always a hanger on, not really an artist, but her whispered reputation with the ladies was excellent. Anyway, they called for Tango, in the main room, and when the music started, we moved in. I love the Tango but am too short. Fenric however offered, and in a moment of weakness I agreed. Honestly, to be fair to him, he did a good job. He is built a bit different, with shorter limbs while I am a miniature woman, but we made it work well. Dacian and the Queen of Flowers and Lights, however, did a monstrously good job. Even I have to admit it. Impressive as Fenric and I were, they did excellently.<br /> <br /> I went to do the Charleston after that with Clara, and made a point of dancing with Wolfram, Christina and Lucille again. Even snuck in a dance with Dr. Hinshaw, who was fun to see again. He has done well. Not following Dana around the world well, but well. <br /> <br /> Eventually the evening wound down. I danced one last time with Clara, the only one I danced with three times. I took her home, it was sweet, she was giggly again. I thanked her for the good time, and gave her a kiss. That stopped the giggling, but not the smiling. She invited me inside, but we just shared some coca. She decided she had some thinking to do, and I was not about to put any sort of pressure on her. I think she felt flattered, when she realized my interest. I don\u2019t know how things might shake out, but I will at least let her consider it. She is a friend, and we can see where things go.<br /> <br /> I planned to go to bed, being rather exhausted. That plan was foiled when Christina, in her nightgown, found me soon after I had walked in. I spent the rest of the night in the Klingemann room. Wolfram Christina and I had rather a good time.<br /> <br /> Now after all that walking and dancing and other stuff, if I can manage to actually make everything move properly I will get back to work again.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> So, the dance was a large scale affair. Women could dance with each other for some of the dances, but not anything slow or intimate. There was a room for traditional dancing, one for modern, and a big sort of meeting and talking room. <br /> <br /> There were a number of socialize rolls to dance. A big one was when we had the Tango. If you are not familiar, Tango was scandalously daring, even at the time. The Queen of Flowers and Lights made a huge number of successes, as she is really rather good at the sorts of rolls called for. She was assisting Dacian, so he got a ton of extra dice, and they outperformed every other couple by a notable measure.<br /> <br /> That mostly covers things. It was a fairly long social scene. Next session will wind up this leg of the chapter, then we shift gears to the train trip. It should be shorter, then back to normal.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T17:22:12-08:00","id":1027935,"title":"","content":"It was the closing session of this leg of <i>The Golden Eagle</i>. Mostly a social session, we had a few IC conversations after a group dinner. Marek\u2019s player was out of town (this was day before Christmas Eve) and the last Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il session (in the short term, at least). We have a Tatiana and Lizette journal\u2026Lizette\u2019s is a story but it pretty well covers what happened in the session. You may want to read in reverse order.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLV</i><br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Of course we are going to help Constancia, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Because she is a friend. And the Olympics are getting boring.<br /> <br /> I have told you not to talk of Elena that way, volchonok. No, I am not getting bored of Elena. And no, I am fleeing nothing! <br /> <br /> Are you going to be civil now?<br /> <br /> Not impertinent, I mean.<br /> <br /> Do not sulk. I have told you... oh I see.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we will be going by train. It will not be so bad, only 4, 5 days. Of course, then we will be on a boat.<br /> <br /> It is far away, this Cyprus. Would you prefer we flew on one of Lizette\u2019s planes?<br /> <br /> No, the songbird cannot fly on her own. And she will not be coming. <br /> <br /> I know, volchonok, this trip is the worst of all things for foolish volchonoks. But she and Dacian are having problems with the Eagle, Ruhadze says so. He wishes to make certain they are not in danger.<br /> <br /> He will take good care of them or he will answer to us.<br /> <br /> He thinks it is because Changelings are slippery. Lizette does much with machines, so maybe it holds faster to her? It made sense to the others.<br /> <br /> I do not know when they will rejoin us.<br /> <br /> I do not suppose they will want to go for a goodbye run. There are preparations to make, for all of us. There will be plenty of time to run along the train tracks. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Help</b><br /> <br /> Lizette \u00c9toile entered spare room where her Motley\u2019s Girl Friday, Nicholette, was finishing a hot drink before retiring for bed. She looked up when the Gremlin entered.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy Lady?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have passed a good evening while we were at the Moulin Rouge, Nicholette?\u201d She took off her gloves as she walked in.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes My Lady. I went to the pictures. Saw <i>The Thief of Baghdad</i>. Douglas Fairbanks was quite dashing. Did you get anything worked out with your friends?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, we are going to be departing for Cyprus day after tomorrow, the 17th. Wolfram, Christina, Alla, Fenric, Marek, Tatiana, yourself and myself.\u201d She put her gloves in the pocket of her toolbelt.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot Dacian or Dearbh\u00e1il, My Lady?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, they will be traveling with Mr. Ruhadze for awhile. I am unsure when they are to return.\u201d Lizette sat down in the chair adjacent to hers.<br /> <br /> Nicholette nodded, then looked up. \u201cDon\u2019t like me much, do they? I was not sure what to think. And Dacian treated you shabbily. I didn\u2019t like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes he did. And I suspect they do not. They are suspicious. Albeit with good reason.\u201d The smaller woman walked over. \u201cWe will be taking the Orient Express to Karlovac, though France, then Switzerland through the tunnel, then Italy, then Yugoslavia. Once in Karlovac, we take a smaller train to Zara. The first trip will be a matter of days, second a matter of hours. Then in Zara, we take the cruise ship to Cyprus.\u201d Yellow eyes looked over at Nicholette.<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well My Lady.\u201d Nicholette nodded. Did you complete the business of the statue satisfactorily then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. Mr. LeRoi was paid for the statue. After we withheld a finder\u2019s fee.\u201d The smaller woman smiled. \u201cA satisfactory conclusion to the business.\u201d She slid out of the chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. Any special tasks for preparation? And is it a safe trip for Lady Christina?\u201d She watched the Inventor pace. Lizette still seemed a bit unreal looking to Nicholette, especially when she moved. Even compared to the few other Fae she had seen. She wondered what she would look like in a film like <i>Thief of Baghdad</i>. <br /> <br /> \u201cOh I think the Orient Express, it is safe enough for Christina. It could, I suppose, use some Vickers on the front, maybe mountable turrets on the side, but you cannot have everything. Perhaps I will write to them with some suggestions.\u201d The Wizened looked thoughtful. \u201cMaybe it could shoot fire out of the back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA good idea, My Lady. You have simply the keenest mind. Perhaps a bit\u2026unusual\u2026but it is part of your charm.\u201d Her smile seemed earnest. Lizette smiled back.<br /> <br /> \u201cConstancia\u2026Connie\u2026is coming along. She is a vampire. We are going to pick up some unusual artifacts found in Tyre in Lebanon by, uh, the woman who made her a vampire. Connie is our friend, but be careful.\u201d Nicholette could tell the Gremlin chose her words carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course. Do she and Lady Alla have any feeding arrangements? The usual servants won\u2019t be present.\u201d Did she look hopeful?<br /> <br /> Lizette gave her a side eye. \u201cThat\u2019s between you and her, dear. How are you getting along with everyone by the way?\u201d<br /> <br /> Nicholette smiled brightly. \u201cYou have been very kind to me. Alla has tried to make me feel at home, and Wolfram have been very kind to me.\u201d She paused to think. \u201cTatiana has been doting as well. Marek has kept to himself. He, Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il apparently don\u2019t mingle with servants. Fenric is very friendly.\u201d The young girl shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s been welcoming overall.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is good, Cheri.\u201d The Gremlin had gotten out a bottle of Cognac and poured a glass. \u201cWe want you to feel welcome. I am glad people are warming up to you. Just try and stay out of danger, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Nicholette nodded enthusiastically. \u201cI am very lucky.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, but luck can run out. Promise to stay out of the line of fire.\u201d Lizette looked seriously at her as she climbed back into the next seat. <br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Nicholette beamed. \u201cI am no hero. But you guys\u2026you guys are serious heroes. Amazing from what I have seen. And some very good looking ones. Makes a girl feel a bit weak kneed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah I know.\u201d Lizette grinned back. Then stopped. \u201cYou don\u2019t mean me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Nicholette smiled and shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026think you are thinking more of Wolfram and Dearbh\u00e1il. Marek possibly.\u201d Lizette rose.<br /> <br /> Nicholette looked apologetic \u201cI am very sorry to put you on the spot, My Lady. Plenty of pretty people in your group though. But more importantly, heroes. I am glad to be coming along.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette dismissed it with a wave. \u201cIt\u2019s not a big deal. I need some sleep. Goodnight Nicholette.\u201d She headed out of the room.<br /> <br /> Nicholette shook her head, laughing. \u201cPoor girl. Does not take the compliments well.\u201d Then she looked over at the doorway, and saw Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re watching. Her large arm pointed at her painted eyes, then pointed at Nicholette, before she disappeared back around the corner.<br /> <br /> Nicholette stared several moments at the empty doorway. \u201cStrange group.\u201d <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> Oh Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re\u2026<br /> <br /> The Golden Eagle issue for the Changelings was mostly just a justification for not having them there. <br /> <br /> Constancia was deliberately vague on what they would be picking up in Cyprus. So not much info there is deliberate.<br /> <br /> We got through the holidays unscathed, but the game tonight was snowed out. We live in the Southern USA so that is not hard to accomplish, really. So no session breakdown next time. Instead we will go ahead and introduce you to Laszlo, the new character in the group with his background story. I\u2019ll see you then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:19:40-08:00","id":1035404,"title":"","content":"There was snow last time, so no game. However, should be game on tonight, and to give you your fortnightly entertainment, let me introduce W\u0142adys\u0142aw Piekarski, Laszlo.<br /> <br /> <b>Feet of Clay</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWhen the Gaon [Rabbi Eliyahu Ba\u2019al Shem] saw that the golem was growing larger and larger, he feared that the golem would destroy the universe.\u201d </i> <br /> - Rabbi Jacob Emden, 1748<br /> <i><br /> \u201cAnd who destroyed my house? That boy asked for shelter, and then he stole our gold, our hen, and our harp. Then he killed my husband. I must avenge the wrongdoings.\u201d </i><br /> - The Giant, \u201cInto the Woods,\u201d Act 2<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cOnce upon a time,\u201d Mama\u2019s voice began, and the children sat on the floor at her skirts with eyes wide and mouths open, \u201cin a far-off kingdom, there lived a childless baker and his wife.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, Mama, no,\u201d W\u0142adys\u0142aw Piekarski moaned, his voice petulant and wheedling, \u201cplease not again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Shhhhh</i>,\u201d his sister \u0141ucja hissed in annoyance. Barely four years old and already as strong-willed as the hoariest old yenta. \u201cI<i> like </i>this one, Laszlo!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe always hear this one,\u201d the boy sulked. \u201cIt\u2019s boring.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo not fight, children,\u201d Mama soothed. \u201cLaszlo, you chose yesterday\u2019s story. Be kind to your sister and let her have her turn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo hung his head. \u201cYes, Mama,\u201d he replied meekly.<br /> <br /> Mama smiled, and the world around her dimmed for her beauty. \u201cThere\u2019s my good boy,\u201d she said, stroking his cheek. \u201cNow, the baker and his wife had prayed to Yahweh for a child\u2026 but to no avail,\u201d she continued sadly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWas the baker a bad man?\u201d \u0141ucja asked with the innocence of youth.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo indeed,\u201d Mama said quickly, \u201cbut sometimes Yahweh\u2019s reasons are not for men to know. Perhaps a child would have been more of a burden than the baker and his wife could bear. Perhaps such a child would have grown up poor and unhappy. Whatever the reason might have been, the baker and his wife found it difficult to accept.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow this was in the Old Days, in the Old Country, further to the East than even the place from which our family came. And in those days, there still lived in the deepest part of the woods a wise old woman. Wise, but cruel and capricious. It was said that she could blind a man by poking a sharpened stick of ash into the eyes of his portrait, or cause a woman to miscarry by stamping hard upon her shadow. She knew much that has since become lost to the world. If <i>anyone</i> can help us, the baker thought,<i> it is this woman</i>.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe sought the old woman for six days, and on the morning of the seventh she found him. He told her of his plight, of how he and his wife had worked hard for all their days to be virtuous people, and of how all they wanted was a child of their own to love and to care for. And it seemed to him that the old woman took pity upon hearing his plight, and pulled from her pack an oilskin sack. \u2018Walk seven hours to the south and you will come to the banks of the great Volga River. Follow it west until you find a place where the banks shine like silver. Fill this sack with clay from the shallows, and carry it back to your wife. Together, the two of you must knead this clay into the shape of the child you desire. Let it bake for one night on the stones of your hearth, and in the morning you shall have your wish.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd did it work, Mama?\u201d \u0141ucja asked breathlessly. \u201cDid the Clay Boy\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPatience, my little aniolku! The baker did as the old woman bid, and found the silver clay just as she had said, and filled the sack, and carried it back to his home. He and his wife worked together until the clay was shaped as like a real baby as they could manage, and that night they placed the Clay Boy on the hearth and went to sleep, praying that their family would soon be made whole.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>But the Clay Boy was not the baker\u2019s son</i>, Laszlo thought to himself for no reason he could identify, <i>he was the child of the Witch!<br /> </i><br /> \u201cWhen the baker and his wife awoke the next morning, they heard the cries of the Clay Boy as he rolled around on the stones before the hearth. They rushed out to see their child and stood staring in wonder at the miracle they beheld. All made of silver clay he was, his body soft and yielding but able to hold its own shape. And though they had never had a child of their own, it was clear to them at once that he was hungry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did he eat, Mama?\u201d \u0141ucja inquired.<br /> <br /> \u201cHad he been an ordinary baby, the baker\u2019s wife would have let him suckle at her breast, but they found that the Clay Boy already had silver teeth in his tiny mouth, so the baker instead gave him bread to eat, and milk from their goats. The Clay Boy gobbled this up quickly, and then to their great surprise he said his first word\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what was the word?\u201d \u0141ucja asked, her eyes wide.<br /> <br /> More, Laszlo thought, suppressing a shudder.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was \u2018more,\u2019 aniolku,\u201d Mama continued. \u201cThe Clay Boy had a hunger that could not be sated, for he had been created out of the desires of his parents and the old woman\u2019s evil. Soon, the baker and his wife had no more bread to feed the Clay Boy, and still he called for more. They gave him milk and cheese, they gave him mutton and venison, they gave him ale and cider, and he gobbled them all up without so much as stopping to breathe. And after every course, he called \u2018more\u2019 in his grating, bubbly voice.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Let it stop here</i>, Laszlo thought but did not quite dare to voice, having been chastened once already. <i> Let her leave the story here and go to check on the loaves in the oven, or remember a favor she needs to do for a friend. I do not want to hear any more.<br /> </i><br /> But Mama did not stop there. \u201cWhen the baker told the Clay Boy that he had no more food, the Clay Boy flew into a rage. He had eaten so many good things already that his body had grown, and now he was as tall as the baker himself. He lashed out at the baker with his fist, sending him flying into the wall, where he lay senseless. The Clay Boy strode through the little cottage\u2019s door and began chasing the goats in their pen. One by one he caught them, and one by one he <i>gobbled them up</i>!\u201d<br /> <br /> At this Mama leaned forward quickly and tickled \u0141ucja\u2019s ribs, sending the little girl into gales of laughter. Laszlo turned away and stopped listening. He knew the story well, and had no desire to hear all of the grotesque details once more. The Clay Boy would grow larger with every goat he ate, until he towered above the men of the town. When none of the goats remained, he would feast upon his mother and father, growing to gigantic size, and then chasing down and devouring their neighbors. And just when it seemed that nothing could stop the titanic menace, a wild yet heroic billy goat from the slopes of the nearby mountains would trick the Clay Boy, offering to jump into his open mouth and then ramming him with its horns, shattering him into dried clay fragments.<br /> <br /> <i>That\u2019s foolish, though</i>, Laszlo always thought as the story ended. <i>How could one small goat fell a giant monster?</i> <i>Why did none of the baker\u2019s goats try it first? Why would the Clay Boy believe such an obvious trick?</i> He had asked these questions to Uncle Mateusz \u2013 whom he believed to be the wisest man he had ever known \u2013 and his uncle had simply laughed. <i>People want to believe that monsters can be defeated, Laszlo,</i> he had said, <i>it helps them not to be afraid of the world.</i><br /> <br /> By the time Mama reached the end of her story, Papa and Uncle Mateusz had closed the bakery and returned to the apartment upstairs. Papa groaned when he heard what Mama was saying. \u201cAgain you tell them that horrible story, Ksenia? It will give them nightmares. We will be up all night with their cries.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot me, Papa,\u201d \u0141ucja said defiantly. \u201cI think the Clay Boy is funny, the way he gobbles everything up.\u201d She opened her mouth wide and mimed taking huge gulping bites out of the air.<br /> <br /> Uncle Mateusz laughed. \u201cIt is a good story, Mi\u0142osz,\u201d he opined. \u201cA little fear is not such a bad thing in a tale like that. It teaches caution.\u201d<br /> <br /> Papa snorted derisively. \u201cIf you are so interested in teaching, Mateusz, then perhaps you should have finished rabbinical school. It would have made your parents proud to have a rabbi in the family instead of a baker\u2019s delivery boy.\u201d <br /> <br /> Laszlo held his breath; his uncle\u2019s choices regarding the path of his life had long been a point of contention between the two men. But Uncle Mateusz simply chuckled and patted his brother-in-law gently upon the shoulder. \u201cYou speak the truth, Mi\u0142osz; I cannot deny it. But surely you can see that I would have been a <i>terrible</i> rabbi. I feel that Yahweh has called me to teach in a different way.\u201d<br /> <br /> Papa looked inclined to argue, but then suddenly turned away and began unlacing his boots. After a moment, Uncle Mateusz followed suit\u2026 but for a split-second, Laszlo could have sworn that a strange gloom had fallen over his uncle, like a deep shadow cast by enormous wings.<br /> <br /> Mama cleared her throat softly. \u201cAll right, kochania, it is time for bed. Go and wash up, and don\u2019t forget to kiss your parents and Uncle Mateusz, and pray before you go to sleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja ran laughing to the washbasin, but Laszlo trudged as though he carried an immense weight upon his shoulders. So intent was he on his misery that he did not notice how Uncle Mateusz\u2019s eyes followed him as he slouched off.<br /> <br /> He knew what waited in his dreams, and he was afraid.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <i>The Clay Boy stalked him through the streets of Berlin, always a bend or two behind him. But this was not the Berlin of the sunlit hours; the streets of this Berlin were narrow and twisted upon themselves so that he was never sure of where he was. The streets of this Berlin were shin-deep in viscous, sucking mud which tripped him up and threatened to take his shoes with every step.<br /> <br /> And all the while the Clay Boy\u2019s colossal footfalls boomed and echoed, drawing ever nearer. He knew that at any moment he might feel the beast\u2019s fingers close around him, cracking ribs and\u2026<br /> </i><br /> Laszlo woke gasping, drenched in sweat. He had managed to stifle his screams this time, and \u0141ucja snored peacefully in the bed across the room, her blankets twisted around her slight form and her hair splayed across her pillow.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid it catch you this time?\u201d a voice asked softly from the darkness.<br /> <br /> Once again Laszlo choked back a scream. The voice was deep, and cold\u2026 and yet familiar. \u201cUncle Mateusz?\u201d he asked in a whisper.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat was it?\u201d the voice asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Clay Boy,\u201d Laszlo admitted. \u201cHe was a giant made of silver mud. He was eating everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd did it catch you?\u201d the voice asked again.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Laszlo breathed a sigh of release.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomeday it will,\u201d the voice responded. And then there was a soft rustling sound, and Laszlo could feel the room empty. The shadows seemed less deep, and the only sound was the quiet rhythm of \u0141ucja\u2019s snores.<br /> <br /> It was a long time before sleep found him again.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The room was silent save for the droning voice of Rabbi Glazewski as the old man implored Laszlo to adhere to the 613 laws of the Torah, and his own higher-pitched replies. Laszlo had been afraid that the unfamiliar words would desert him at the last moment, and he would embarrass his family, but much to his delight he found the Hebrew litany easy to recall, and a short time later the ceremony was complete.<br /> <br /> Members of the community came to congratulate him then, from Mrs. Szima\u0144ski (who still pinched his cheek even as she told him how proud she was to see the man he had become) to his friend Andrezj, who had just gone through his own bar mitzvah a few weeks before. \u201cNow we are both men,\u201d the latter said with a smile, and Laszlo felt heat rising in his cheeks.<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja approached him next. At eleven years old everyone could see the beauty she would become, with cornflower blue eyes and shiny golden hair. She threw her arms around him and kissed his cheek, and he was startled to see that her own cheeks were shining with tears. \u201cYou did well, Laszlo,\u201d she whispered into his ear. \u201cI am proud of you. But I am sad, too. Now that you are a grown man, we can no longer share a bedroom.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded soberly. \u201cIt wouldn\u2019t be proper, \u0141ucja,\u201d he replied, \u201cthe neighbors would talk. I must move into Uncle Mateusz\u2019s room tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja\u2019s brows knit with concern. \u201cBut what about\u2026\u201d she began hesitantly. She glanced around the crowded room, noting that those assembled were paying more attention to the cha\u0142ka and racuchy than to the two of them. \u201cWhat about your night terrors?\u201d she asked in a voice barely above a whisper. \u201cWill you be all right without me to calm you?\u201d <br /> <br /> The genuine concern he heard in his younger sister\u2019s voice caused his love for her to blossom like a rose. \u201cPerhaps now,\u201d Laszlo began uncertainly, \u201cperhaps now that I am a man, I will no longer be afraid. Surely grown men never wake up screaming in the middle of the night, sure that fairy tale monsters are trying to eat them\u2026 and besides, Uncle Mateusz is both wise and kind. If the dreams return, he will know what to do.\u201d<br /> The two of them were forced apart after that by members of the community who wished to honor the newly-minted adult with praise and gifts. The neighborhood was poor, so for the most part the gifts were modest but appreciated. Among the kosher sweets and coins were a few stand-out presents. His first tallit, plain yet finely woven from soft materials. A new copy of the Torah from his parents. A fountain pen from Rabbi Glazewski (accompanied by an admonishment not to be distracted from his studies).<br /> <br /> Uncle Mateusz approached him last, a small package wrapped in brown paper in his hands. \u201cCongratulations, W\u0142adys\u0142aw Piekarski,\u201d he said solemnly. He reached out his hand and gently touched Laszlo\u2019s new copy of the Torah with the tip of his index finger. \u201cThere is much wisdom to be found here,\u201d he said, sounding almost grudging in the admission, \u201cbut it does not contain <i>all </i>worthwhile knowledge. Let your mind be open to other possibilities as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo took the proffered package from his uncle and tore aside the wrappings, curious. As expected, he held another book in his hands. This one was also written in Hebrew. It was called Kabbalah, and it seemed to thrum gently in his hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, Uncle,\u201d Laszlo said.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is difficult to read,\u201d Uncle Mateusz said, \u201cbut I think you will learn much if you persevere. But\u2026 perhaps it would be best if you did not show it to your father,\u201d he added with a wry grin.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> That night Laszlo climbed uncomfortably into his new bed as Uncle Mateusz blew out the candle. \u201cDo you still have bad dreams, Laszlo?\u201d Uncle Mateusz asked as the darkness settled around them.<br /> <br /> \u201cSometimes,\u201d Laszlo admitted, his cheeks red with shame had Uncle Mateusz been able to see them. \u201cI thought that maybe\u2026 now that I am a grown man, the dreams might stop. I thought that perhaps grown men are not afraid of the dark.\u201d<br /> <br /> Uncle Mateusz laughed at that. \u201cOh, Laszlo,\u201d he said softly. \u201cHow much you have still to learn! Children fear the dark because they do not know what lies within it. Grown men \u2013 some grown men, anyway; the wisest of them \u2013 fear the dark because they do know what lies within it. But go to sleep, bratanek. No nightmare can last forever.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo breathed a sigh of relief at the words of comfort. \u201cThen you think I will conquer these dreams, Uncle Mateusz?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence for more than a minute, and when Mateusz answered his voice was so soft that Laszlo couldn\u2019t be certain he\u2019d heard anything at all.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t say that.\u201d<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <i>He turned a corner, ducking into an alley as quickly as he could despite the knee-deep mud. Surely the Clay Boy would not be able to follow him this way. Surely the gargantuan creature couldn\u2019t squeeze into a corridor this narrow.<br /> <br /> Its footsteps came ever closer, making horrible sucking sounds as it trudged through the muck, adding to its mass and growing larger and more misshapen with every resounding step. Buildings seemed to move aside in fear, so that paths through which the boy had to squeeze could accommodate the titan with ease.<br /> <br /> He ran again, heedless of direction, knowing only that he had to escape the wrath of the giant which stalked him\u2026 knowing only that his death approached with that stride, never wavering, causing the earth itself to shake with its even passage.<br /> <br /> He lunged for an open doorway, narrowly avoiding the swipe of one huge clublike fist, not daring to look back. But his body betrayed him, and he sprawled face-first in the sludge of the street. It oozed into his nose and mouth, choking him, blinding him, making him deaf to the noise of the street. All he could do was feel\u2026 feel the monolithic pounding of the Clay Boy\u2019s stride and the pressure of the muck pressing in on him from all sides as the enormous fist closed around him.<br /> <br /> He felt himself lifted into the air, and some of the mud dribbled out of his face, allowing him to see his pursuer at long last. Composed of silvery-brown river clay, it resembled nothing so much as the clumsy artistic endeavors of a child. Its limbs were thick and brutish, its eyes mere holes poked into its head (but as deep and dark as two wells for all that). Within its gaping maw, however, an inferno raged, and teeth the size and color of old bricks jutted from its jaws in crazy directions.</i><br /> <br /> This is it, <i>the boy thought to himself.</i> There is no escape this time. I am caught. <i>In a way, it was a relief.</i><br /> <br /> <i>And then the Clay Boy squeezed. The boy felt his bones snap and his organs jelly within his torso. The breath was forced from his lungs, and a liquid pop resounded between his ears. As he died, the Clay Boy pulled his body into its mouth and roared a single word: \u2018MORE!\u2019<br /> </i><br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Laszlo sat up in the darkness, but felt no urge to scream. The fear his recurring nightmare always left behind simply was not present; instead he felt right, like something he had been missing his entire life had suddenly fallen into place. His blood pounded in his veins, his senses seemed sharpened, and his muscles tensed and released like springs. He let out a long sighing breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt finally caught you, didn\u2019t it?\u201d came a soft voice from a shadowy corner of the shared bedroom.<br /> <br /> \u201cUncle Mateusz?\u201d he asked. He found that his uncle was often already awake when the nightmares chased sleep from his exhausted mind. This time, however, there was something different about his uncle. His form, not seated but crouched in a wooden chair in the corner seemed blurred and indistinct. The shadows in which he sat loomed like some stooping carrion bird behind him.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t waste time with idle talk, Laszlo,\u201d Mateusz snapped, and there was a raw hunger in his voice. \u201cThe Clay Boy. Did it catch you this time?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d Laszlo admitted calmly.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what did it do when it caught you?\u201d Mateusz asked eagerly. Laszlo thought he caught the glimmer of two red-orange points of light in the darkness, but no candles burned in the room; nothing could have been reflected so brightly in his uncle\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt ate me,\u201d Laszlo said at once, and he found that the concept did not terrify him as it would have a few hours before. \u201cIt swallowed me whole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAt last,\u201d Mateusz said with something like triumph. \u201cAnd how do you feel?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo considered the question, but found that the answer \u2013 while surprising \u2013 was not difficult to articulate. \u201cI feel\u2026 good,\u201d he answered after a moment. \u201cBetter than I have in years, actually. I don\u2019t feel afraid anymore. I feel\u2026 excited. Eager.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHungry?\u201d Mateusz asked, and he placed so much meaning into those two syllables that Laszlo recoiled. Slavering jaws, knotted muscles, the bitter metallic tang of adrenaline\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026yes,\u201d Laszlo admitted, \u201cbut not for food. The bigos Mama made for supper is still sitting heavy in my stomach. I want\u2026 I <i>need</i> something else.\u201d<br /> <br /> Across the room, Mateusz rose, and something rose behind him. It was impossibly tall and stick-thin, and its eyes burned like brands in the darkness. A sword rested in its right hand, the metal blackened and pitted iron surrounded by a corona of flame. Wings of black feathers, <br /> patterned with elaborate eyes like the tail of a peacock, spread from its back as it approached. For a moment, Laszlo knew what it was to be an insect scuttling madly across the ground, trying desperately to reach the safety of its burrow as the terrible birds shrieked above. But no, he thought, <i>that is not what I am. Not anymore. </i> <br /> <br /> And with that thought, the shadows receded and Mateusz\u2019 predatory grin settled back into its more familiar friendly smile, and Laszlo knew that here was a man who could understand him in a way his parents and sister simply could not. Mateusz reached out and placed a warm hand on Laszlo\u2019s shoulder and then pulled him into a fierce embrace. \u201cWelcome to the Family, Laszlo,\u201d Mateusz whispered with feeling, and Laszlo was stunned to note the tears in his uncle\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> * * * * *","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:20:14-08:00","id":1035405,"title":"","content":"\u201cYou are not concentrating, Laszlo,\u201d Mateusz said with irritation as Laszlo returned to the table they shared at a street-side caf\u00e9. \u201cFear is the chief weapon of the Children; Nightmares are how we feed and how we teach. If you cannot master them, then you are little better than a bully.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA bully, eh?\u201d the small youth said with a wry grin as he sat down. \u201cI don\u2019t particularly look the part, do I?\u201d Half a head shorter than most of his peers, Laszlo was also thin and pale, though not unhealthy.<br /> <br /> Mateusz threw him a shrewd look, and his eyes gleamed in the glow of the street lamps. \u201cHave you been eating properly?\u201d he asked after a moment.<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded. \u201cYou know I have,\u201d he said, \u201cwe eat at the same table. Mama\u2019s stews and Papa\u2019s bread are famous in the neighborhood\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz clucked his tongue impatiently. \u201cYou know what I meant,\u201d he snapped.<br /> <br /> Laszlo hung his head. \u201cI\u2026 it is difficult sometimes,\u201d he admitted. \u201cI don\u2019t want to hurt people\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz sighed and scooted his chair nearer, the metal feet scraping loudly against the cobbles below them. \u201cListen to me, Laszlo,\u201d he said earnestly. \u201cI understand, I truly do. But your Horror must be fed if you are to survive. When it is hungry, it comes <i>forward</i>. You become more like it. This might grant you great strength and resilience, but it will make you rash and reckless as well. When your Horror is well-fed, it is easier to control. Your human discipline will allow you to make more precise use of its abilities. And wielding Nightmares properly requires such precision.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo did not meet his uncle\u2019s eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s easy for you,\u201d he sulked, \u201cyour Horror is almost friendly by comparison. You strike down heretics and other sinners. The Clay Boy doesn\u2019t care what it devours\u2026 it just wants to <i>destroy.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz took Laszlo by the arm until the young man faced him. \u201cThis is not the place for such a conversation,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cLet us retire to the alleys and enter your Lair.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded. Mateusz entered the caf\u00e9 to settle their small bill, and the two of them walked off into the complicated system of back-alleys and side streets which choked certain neighborhoods of urban Berlin. Narrow passages twisted and turned without warning, and high buildings loomed above to either side, occasionally even meeting and joining together some distance overhead. When all sounds of street traffic had faded into the unknown distance, Laszlo concentrated and brought his Lair <i>forward</i>.<br /> <br /> The uneven cobbles beneath their feet became soft viscous mud into which their feet nevertheless refused to sink, and the buildings to either side of them loomed higher and darker than before. Torches burned in sconces at semi-regular intervals along the walls\u2026 the flames had begun seeping in from Mateusz\u2019 own Lair ever since the two of them had joined their sanctums. The darkened windows were skirled with flowers of ice, and were cold to the touch despite the ever-present flames. Laszlo had asked his uncle about this the first time he had accessed the private den known as the Lair, and Mateusz had told him that the ice appeared in all local manifestations of the Primordial Dream, in deference to the most powerful mystical creature in Berlin\u2026 a stately lady of the Fair Folk who styled herself the Queen of Winter. Laszlo had never met her, and wasn\u2019t sure he wanted to\u2026 though others among the loose society of changelings in Berlin had proven to be quite friendly when they had been introduced.<br /> <br /> Laszlo turned to look at his uncle, clothed in the splendid and terrifying form of Azrael, the Angel of Death. Though Laszlo towered over him here in his own Lair, Mateusz still gave the impression of greater size. \u201cI am sorry, uncle,\u201d he said; his voice a glutinous rumble. \u201cI will try to do better in the future. I will practice wielding Nightmares\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd it will do you no good, if your Horror is not well-fed,\u201d Azrael spoke, his words sounding as though they had been engraved upon the stone lid of a sarcophagus. \u201cThe Clay Boy is a part of you, but it is not governed by reason or inhibitions. It hungers, and when that hunger becomes too great, it <i>will </i>feed, whether you wish it or no.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe goes off on his own sometimes, when I sleep,\u201d Laszlo admitted. \u201cI have tried to stop him, but I can\u2019t. He enters the dreams of those around me and devours their dream-selves. They always wake up terrified. If I look at customers in the bakery the next day, sometimes I can tell who he has visited.\u201d<br /> <br /> Azrael\u2019s demeanor became stern. \u201cYou must not allow this to happen again,\u201d he said sharply, and the dark feathers of his wings gave a dangerous rustle. \u201cOnce or twice is harmless enough, but if the Clay Boy visits the same dreams every night, it will take a toll upon the sleepers\u2019 minds. And once he finds an easy hunting ground, he <i>will</i> revisit it again and again\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou think I don\u2019t know that?\u201d Laszlo shouted indignantly. \u201cYou think I <i>want</i> to be responsible for their nightmares? I didn\u2019t ask for this\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo more than you asked to be a Polnischen Juden,\u201d Azrael responded angrily. \u201cNo more than you asked to be small, or thin. No more than you asked to have dark hair. Would you complain about these things? Complaining about the Clay Boy is just as useful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey don\u2019t <i>deserve</i> to be hunted like that,\u201d Laszlo roared, shaking the foundation of his Lair.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen find those who <i>do</i>!\u201d Azrael responded, and all around the two of them the torches flared to brilliance, lighting the darkened passageways and bathing them both in an intense heat (though frost still bloomed on the windows). \u201cTake control of your life once more, my nephew. If you worry about how good people will suffer at the hands of your Horror, then make it feast upon <i>bad</i> people instead! Hunt them deliberately, <i>before</i> the Clay Boy takes matters into its own hands!\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo reared back as though slapped. \u201cI\u2026 I could do that?\u201d he asked meekly. \u201cBut\u2026 the Clay Boy does not care who he devours\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you do,\u201d Azrael responded more gently. \u201cLaszlo, the Clay Boy is powerful\u2026 it has the potential to be more powerful than any of the other Children I have met. But power without determination is useless. Left to its own devices it will feast wherever it can, and that sort of behavior has the tendency to attract\u2026 unwanted attention. But if you can give it a purpose, a <i>reason</i> to hunt, then you can help to curb its less savory appetites. My own Horror was not always as you know it. When it first awakened, it was simply death incarnate, mowing down the good and the evil alike, indiscriminately.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026 Azrael <i>is</i> the angel of death,\u201d Laszlo supplied.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed, in recent years, Azrael has become identified with malakh ha-mavet, the Angel of Death,\u201d Mateusz agreed, \u201cbut in the past this was not always so. The oldest Talmudic scholars argued that no being had command over life and death except Yahweh Himself. To their minds, Azrael was simply His instrument. In fact, the name Azrael means \u2018help from God,\u2019 or \u2018godsend.\u2019 This is how I choose to manifest my Horror\u2026 as one who helps his community.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo thought about this for a moment. \u201cThey say that war is coming,\u201d he said uncertainly. \u201cI could try to enlist, and turn my Horror against the enemy\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Azrael shook his head. \u201cA small pale Jew who has yet to see his fifteenth birthday? The army will never be so desperate for recruits,\u201d he said with disdain.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen what?\u201d Laszlo asked, frustrated once more. \u201cHow else can I direct the actions of a ravenous monster?\u201d<br /> <br /> Azrael thought for a moment. \u201cThe Clay Boy is a Russian fairy story,\u201d he mused, \u201cbut it is far from unique in lore. What other examples of clay men come to mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo pondered the question. \u201cEver the rabbi,\u201d he muttered to himself. \u201cThey say that Yahweh molded Adam from clay in the Garden,\u201d he said eventually.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed,\u201d Azrael agreed. \u201cBut I was thinking of something a bit more recent. Say\u2026 three centuries ago, in Prague\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo\u2019s eyes widened as he remembered the accounts he had read in his uncle\u2019s books. \u201cThe Golem?\u201d he asked in awed tones. \u201cThe great Golem of Rabbi Loew?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed,\u201d Azrael nodded. \u201cBy all accounts, a great friend to the Jews of Prague, and a terror to those who would victimize them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the Golem turned upon its creators eventually,\u201d Laszlo replied.<br /> <br /> Azrael chuckled. \u201cOnly when the rituals controlling it were abandoned,\u201d he countered. \u201cOnly when the holy rites animating it were ignored. Only when those who made use of it grew prideful, and neglected to show the proper respect to Yahweh.\u201d He paused for a moment to let that sink in. \u201cIn a way, the Clay Boy\u2019s story is similar\u2026 one might say that Yahweh sent him to punish the baker and his wife, who had asked a witch for help rather than accepting Yahweh\u2019s judgment that they should be childless.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I could\u2026 hunt those who sin against Yahweh?\u201d Laszlo asked timidly.<br /> <br /> Azrael laughed. \u201cThat would be casting a wide net indeed, my nephew,\u201d he said with good humor. \u201cBut there are many in this city who would take advantage of the Chosen People. We are not well-liked. Surely you would not object to teaching those who would prey upon us a lesson or two, eh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded. \u201cYou really think I could turn the Clay Boy into the Golem?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> Azrael thought seriously about the question for a moment. \u201cAll that is lacking is fire,\u201d he muttered to himself. \u201cIf he was fired, the Clay Boy would be the very image of the Golem. He would harden into the shape you desire\u2026 and it would make him stronger and tougher as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut how are we to fire him? There is no kiln in my Lair,\u201d Laszlo said.<br /> <br /> \u201cLeave the fire to me,\u201d Azrael breathed tonelessly. A moment later, he opened Laszlo\u2019s lair to his own, and there was fire in abundance.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> \u201cCome on, Laszlo, I\u2019m just asking you to look after the counter for a few hours tonight. Is that too much of a favor to grant your precious sister?\u201d \u0141ucja asked sweetly.<br /> <br /> Laszlo rolled his eyes at the seventeen-year-old\u2019s wheedling. \u201cTonight is my night off, \u0141ucja. I only get one of those each week, aside from the Sabbath. I already have plans.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs this because Andrezj and I have started seeing each other, Laszlo?\u201d she said, growing more serious. \u201cI know he\u2019s your best friend, and\u2026\u201d She broke off and glanced around the empty bakery, making certain that Mrs. Szima\u0144ski had indeed vacated the premises before continuing. \u201cI know that you wanted him to be <i>more</i> than a friend,\u201d she finished in a whisper. \u201cI don\u2019t want to do anything to hurt you, brother\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo shook his head. \u201cI realized years ago that Andrezj is\u2026 not like me. He is my best friend, \u0141ucja, and I would not throw that away for a hopeless fantasy. You make him happy, and any fool can see that he does the same for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pouted adorably. \u201cThen why don\u2019t you want me to go out and have a good time tonight?\u201d she asked with a hint of petulance.<br /> <br /> He chuckled in response. \u201cI have no objection to you enjoying your evening, sister. But I have plans tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> She wrinkled her nose. \u201cThe Hedge Maze again?\u201d she asked with distaste. \u201cLaszlo, I know that club caters to people with your\u2026 tastes, and I\u2019m glad you\u2019re getting out and meeting people. But there\u2019s something <i>off</i> about that place. It makes me uncomfortable.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo sighed, thinking about the evenings he had spent in Prince Sascha\u2019s club among the changelings of Berlin. They had opened his mind to so many things. He sometimes wished he could let \u0141ucja see the club\u2019s denizens as <i>he</i> saw them. While it was true that many of them had alarming or frightening appearances beneath the concealing magic they called the Mask, there were others of such beauty\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cNot that it\u2019s any of your business, little sister,\u201d he said sharply to dissuade further questions, \u201cbut I\u2019m not going to the Hedge Maze tonight. I. Have. Other. Plans.\u201d<br /> <br /> Color rose in her cheeks, whether from embarrassment or anger he couldn\u2019t immediately say. \u0141ucja\u2019s skin was pale, like his own, but while he merely appeared pallid and unhealthy, her face had a porcelain glow that set off the blue of her eyes and the dark gold of her hair perfectly. Attractive at the best of times, the flush in her cheeks made her beautiful.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see,\u201d she said softly, almost sadly. \u201cThis is about whatever you and Uncle Mateusz talk about behind closed doors, isn\u2019t it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo started, taken aback. He had no idea that \u0141ucja knew anything about his condition. \u201cYes,\u201d he said after a moment. He hated lying to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe used to be so close, Laszlo,\u201d she went on as she sliced a loaf into thin segments. \u201cYou are welcome to your secrets, of course\u2026<br /> everyone has them. But it makes me sad that you refuse to share something so important with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> He walked toward her and put his arms around her shoulders. Leaning in, he kissed her softly on the forehead. \u201cI am sorry, \u0141ucja,\u201d he said as they embraced. \u201cI truly think that it is best you know as little about Uncle Mateusz and I as possible. I think we would lose something if you knew. Do you trust me?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI trust you with my life, Laszlo. And I will always love you, no matter what you think you must hide from me. You are my brother.\u201d When he released her from his embrace, she returned to slicing the bread morosely as she continued speaking.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I might know a little of what you won\u2019t tell me already,\u201d she said, her voice regaining a hint of its typical mischief. \u201cI\u2019m neither blind nor stupid, no matter what people might say about me in the neighborhood. I know that you did something to Lukas Fischer two years ago, after he tried to\u2026 hurt me,\u201d she ended with a grimace.<br /> <br /> Laszlo said nothing, inwardly seething as he did every time he thought of that schweinhund Fischer. That anyone calling himself a man would try to force himself upon a young girl \u2013 his <i>sister</i>, no less \u2013 brought the rage as nothing else did. He had called upon the Golem\u2019s strength and frightened the life out of Fischer, chasing him through the alleys, punching through brick and concrete walls, and tossing heavy garbage bins around like skittles. In the end, cornered, Fischer had cowered against a wall, certain that he was going to die, but Laszlo had spared his miserable life. It had been a near thing, and Fischer\u2019s dreams had been troubled by nightmares for weeks to come without any help from Laszlo.<br /> <br /> \u201cLukas was <i>afraid</i> of you,\u201d \u0141ucja said with wonder, \u201cand he\u2019s not the only one.\u201d She looked at him critically, barely an inch taller than she was herself, slight of build, pale, jug-eared, and altogether forgettable. \u201cI mean no disrespect, brother, but why would <i>anyone</i> be afraid of you?\u201d<br /> <br /> He leaned in once more and kissed her, this time standing on his toes to reach the top of her head. \u201cAll you need to know, \u0141ucja, is that you need never fear me,\u201d he said softly. \u201cAnd you need never fear anyone else while I am around to protect you.\u201d<br /> <br /> And in the back of his head, the Golem stirred restlessly. Down the block, the owner of an apartment building had been forcing his Jewish tenants out to increase the value of the property so that he could sell it. Many of those tenants had nowhere else to go. Tonight, he would see the error of his ways. Tonight, the Golem would <i>hunt</i>.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The blood pounded in Laszlo\u2019s ears as he followed the burly man through the streets, always half a block behind, never too close, but never out of sight, either. Ernst Gerhardt was drunk; this much was clear to anyone who came within two yards of him\u2026 but even taking that into consideration, it had taken him much longer than anticipated to spot Laszlo.<br /> <br /> Laszlo had rarely been so angry. Dale M\u00fcller could be a bit full of himself from time to time; a bit proud of his own success, but he was a <i>good man</i> for all of that. His wife Elsbeth had been a kind and soft-spoken woman; she had always taken the time to pass a few words with Laszlo\u2019s mother when she had visited the bakery, and had often left coins in the tip jar on her way out. Their daughter, Gerda, had been a joy to know. She could brighten a room with her smile and had never spoken a harsh word within Laszlo\u2019s hearing.<br /> <br /> And this khnyok Gerhardt had killed them. And why? Because Herr M\u00fcller had succeeded in a business where Gerhardt himself had failed? Because he had made a happy life for himself, with a beautiful wife and a loving daughter? No. It was because he was a Jew, and Jews stole the birthrights of proper German Christians. So Gerhardt had burned the M\u00fcllers\u2019 house to cinders.<br /> <br /> In a way, Herr M\u00fcller had been lucky\u2026 he had been down at the local pub, celebrating the closing of an important business deal with a few friends. But Elsbeth and little Gerda had been at home.<br /> <br /> It had been nearly a week since the fire, and Herr M\u00fcller had collapsed into a shadow of the man he had once been. The people of the neighborhood pulled together to help take care of him, but it was whispered that if he didn\u2019t rise from his deep depression soon, his business partners would start to desert him. Laszlo knew that the poor man could not care less about such things at the moment; the loss of his family was all he could contemplate. But Elsbeth and Gerda would not have wanted him to throw his life away for their sakes.<br /> <br /> Tonight, Laszlo hoped to give Herr M\u00fcller peace of mind. Tonight, Laszlo intended to see that justice was done. Tonight, Laszlo would make sure that Gerhardt never victimized his people again.<br /> <br /> He knew that Gerhardt was guilty. Everyone knew that Gerhardt was guilty, but Laszlo had gone the extra mile to make <i>sure</i>. After five days of stalking the man, he had baked a tray of the fruit-filled pastries locally known as berliners and had carried them to the gentlemen\u2019s club Gerhardt patronized. Ordinarily, he would not have been allowed past the doors, but when he explained to the doorman that the pastries were a gift from a prospective member, he had been ushered quickly through the common room to the kitchens. Along the way, he had heard Ernst Gerhardt bragging to his cronies about how he had chased the uppity Juden out of their district\u2026 and about how at least two of them would never come back.<br /> <br /> When Gerhardt staggered out of the club that evening, he was both alone and drunk. It was well past midnight, and even cosmopolitan Berlin had mostly shut down for the evening. The streets were sparsely populated, and those few pedestrians who did roam late chose to avoid the stumbling man with his boisterous singing. Laszlo remained at least a hundred feet behind Gerhardt at all times, waiting for his opportunity to strike.<br /> <br /> The Golem was hungry. Laszlo had not allowed it to feed for quite some time, and its senses were sharp as knives. He could feel its clay muscles knotting beneath his skin; its strength pulsing in his veins. He would not be able to restrain the Golem for another night. There was a clear transgressor before it, and it wanted to mete out punishment.<br /> <br /> When they approached the system of alleys which so resembled Laszlo\u2019s Lair, Laszlo struck. Checking to see that there were no witnesses present, he tossed a large garbage can at Gerhardt\u2019s back. It struck the drunk between the shoulders, sending him sprawling into the street. When Gerhardt turned angrily to confront his attacker, Laszlo casually pushed a streetlamp over, never pausing in his advance.<br /> <br /> Gerhardt screamed shrilly and turned to flee into the alleys, no doubt hoping that he could lose himself in their labyrinthine twists and turns. Laszlo smiled to himself at the man\u2019s mistake; he had spent half of his life navigating such mazes\u2026 first in his dreams and then in his Lair, and they had lost the power to confuse him. He ducked into the alleys in time to see Gerhardt streaking around a corner in front of him. He stomped his foot, creating deep cracks in the cobbled street, and lashed out with his arm at the railing of a dirty stoop, pulling several cast-iron bars free and tossing them aside.<br /> <br /> Gerhardt\u2019s fear was thick and acrid in the air now, and Laszlo inhaled it with relish. He was so intent upon his goal that it was perhaps unsurprising he did not notice the other\u2019s approach until he was nearly upon them. It was obvious that he newcomer was not attempting to be stealthy; he cleared his throat while still more than ten yards away.<br /> <br /> Laszlo turned quickly to regard his new companion, upset that he might have to postpone the hunt. The man was tall and thin, with finely chiseled features, bright eyes, and dark hair. The tell-tale points of his ears and teeth marked him as a werewolf in near-human form, but Laszlo would have recognized him as Kin even in his fully-human form. All Children of the Dark Mother called to him.<br /> <br /> Laszlo paused in his pursuit, confident that he could catch Gerhardt at his leisure later. The werewolf complicated matters. The fact that he was a supernatural being meant that Laszlo did not need to hide his own gifts, but\u2026 according to Uncle Mateusz, the local packs were not friendly to their kind. This man, however, wore a slight smile and held his hands out in a pacifying way.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am sorry to interrupt,\u201d the newcomer said in conversational tones. \u201cMight I ask what your interest is in that man?\u201d He indicated the alley down which Gerhardt had disappeared with a shake of his head, leaving his hands visible the whole time.<br /> <br /> Laszlo considered deception, but he had never been much good at such things. He shrugged instead. \u201cThat shmuts killed a woman and a little girl last week. They were good people. I wish to teach him the error of his ways, so that he will not do so again.\u201d<br /> <br /> The werewolf nodded as though he had been expecting this answer. \u201cElsbeth M\u00fcller\u2019s cousin Hans is a friend of mine. He asked me to take care of the man who has attacked his family.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo considered this. \u201cYou wish to kill Herr Gerhardt?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> The werewolf shrugged. \u201cI want him dead. I suppose it is a matter of professional pride.\u201d His German was faintly accented, marking him as a foreigner. Not Polish\u2026 Czech, perhaps?<br /> <br /> Laszlo\u2019s instincts surged forward, and the Golem bellowed in his mind. It had to be fed. \u201cI must finish my hunt,\u201d he told the newcomer helplessly.<br /> <br /> The werewolf nodded, understanding perfectly. \u201cI would not interrupt another\u2019s hunt,\u201d he said mildly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do not need to kill Herr Gerhardt,\u201d Laszlo explained, grasping at straws. \u201cI must <i>teach</i> him. But I would not weep if he was to die shortly after learning his lesson.\u201d<br /> <br /> The werewolf grinned, and his teeth gleamed in the moonlight. He shook his head toward the alley once more, his pointed ear twitching a bit. \u201cHe\u2019s getting away,\u201d he said softly.<br /> <br /> Laszlo returned his grin in kind. \u201cNo,\u201d he said simply, \u201che\u2019s not.\u201d<br /> <br /> A few moments later the chase was over. Ernst Gerhardt cowered in a corner, having attempted to cover himself in the garbage strewn across the alley. Laszlo loomed over him, the Golem giving him stature greater than his five and a half feet. The werewolf was nowhere to be found, though Laszlo assumed he hadn\u2019t wandered far.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy are you doing this?\u201d Gerhardt shrieked, his voice several octaves above its normal range.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have to ask?\u201d Laszlo said with no small amount of disgust.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey were only a couple of Jews,\u201d the man said, as though that explained everything.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Laszlo said quietly. \u201cThey were a <i>woman</i> and a <i>six-year-old girl</i>.\u201d His fist shot out and created a crater in the dark bricks by the man\u2019s head. \u201cAnd you killed them for what? Because you were <i>angry</i>?\u201d Punch. <i>\u201cJealous?\u201d</i> Punch. <i> \u201cLustful?\u201d</i> Punch. <i>\u201cSpiteful?\u201d</i> Punch. Fragments of brick rained down on Gerhardt\u2019s head, and he whimpered like a child. The warm, wet smell of urine filled the air.<br /> <br /> Laszlo forced down the rage and made himself look the spineless coward in the eyes. \u201cDo you know what it is like to<i> burn</i>, Herr Gerhardt?\u201d he asked in silky tones.<br /> <br /> Gerhardt shook his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not,\u201d Laszlo conceded. \u201cIt is a terrible way to die, Herr Gerhardt. There is the pain, of course. But there are so many other facets to death by fire that people never consider. There is the fact that after a while you cannot breathe for the heat. Not the smoke, mind you, but the<i> heat</i>. It presses in on you from all sides and squeezes the air out of your lungs. If you are lucky, your nerves will die before you feel the skin flaking and sloughing off your bones. Before your eyes burst. Before your blood begins to boil.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gerhardt whimpered and covered his face with his hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one should have to experience that, Herr Gerhardt,\u201d Laszlo said softly, \u201cbut I think I will give you a taste of it anyway.\u201d And with that he opened a pathway to his Lair. Ever since Uncle Mateusz had helped him to fire the Clay Boy into the Golem, a bit of Mateusz\u2019 divine fire had taken root in Laszlo\u2019s sanctum. Where before there had been only twisting streets and sucking mud, now colossal ovens loomed at every corner, resembling both baking ovens and potters\u2019 kilns.<br /> <br /> The wall to the right of Gerhardt seemed to burst outward and gouts of flame leapt out to cover him head to toe. He screamed and clawed at his face, rolling about in the muck and garbage, trying to regain some semblance of control. After a few seconds had passed, Laszlo allowed the oven door to close, and it became a brick wall once more.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was a small taste of what you did to a woman and a little girl,\u201d Laszlo said, backing away slightly. \u201cKeep in mind that it probably took Elsbeth and Gerda <i>minutes</i> to die. Think about that the next time you get <i>angry</i>, Herr Gerhardt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will,\u201d the cowering man said, his charred hands quivering. \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I will never do such a thing again, I promise you\u2026 not even to a Jew!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh,\u201d the soft voice of the werewolf came from the entrance to the alleyway, \u201cso Ernst has learned his lesson, then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes!\u201d Herr Gerhardt almost shouted. \u201cI am sorry\u2026 so sorry! I will never do anything of the sort ever again. I will never hurt anyone as long as I live. Please, you must believe me!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do believe you,\u201d the werewolf said as he stalked closer, \u201cbut I don\u2019t care.\u201d With that, he extended his lethal claws and swiped once at the murderer\u2019s throat. Herr Gerhardt goggled at him, blood running down his chest and bursting from his mouth in thick bubbles. He gave one last despairing moan at the unfairness of it all and then pitched forward face-first into the garbage.<br /> <br /> The werewolf turned to face Laszlo, a look of mild curiosity in his eyes. \u201cYou do not approve, my new friend?\u201d he asked simply.<br /> <br /> Laszlo shook his head. \u201cIt is difficult to argue that he did not deserve it,\u201d he allowed. \u201cI might have killed him myself had I come upon him alone\u2026 but I did not want to deprive a noble werewolf of his kill.\u201d<br /> <br /> The werewolf nodded, taking the appellation in stride, and then sniffed the air delicately. \u201cMostly garbage,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201c<i>Burned</i> garbage, and piss, and sweat, and\u2026 baking bread. What are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo laughed at that. \u201cI am a baker,\u201d he said after a moment, \u201cand a Jew, and one who does not like bullies and racists. But to answer your <i>real</i> question\u2026 we call ourselves the Children. We are the monsters out of nightmares, the things under the bed, the all-consuming krakens in the darkest trenches of the ocean. But we are also people, like everyone else.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUratha are strong,\u201d the werewolf said, \u201cbut I have never seen anyone do what you can do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am the physical manifestation of the Golem of Prague,\u201d Laszlo explained, \u201cand I can call upon great strength when I hunt. It is very difficult to hurt me, too\u2026 though I am not the warrior your own people are said to be. Not by half.\u201d<br /> <br /> The werewolf nodded and extended his hand. \u201cIt is good that your people have such a guardian to look after them,\u201d he said as Laszlo shook it. \u201cIf you ever have need of me, contact a man named Hans Ausfeld. He is a local. Tell him that you have need of Reznik.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cW\u0142adys\u0142aw Piekarski,\u201d Laszlo said, and then, \u201cLaszlo. My family runs a bakery on Marianstra\u00dfe. We live in the apartment above. Please stop by when you can. Even if you do not have need of the Golem, the krem\u00f3wka are divine. And I will give you a discount,\u201d he added with a wink.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The scent of freshly-baked pastries filled the air as steam rose from the tray. Laszlo pulled it from the oven bare-handed, since Mama was in the front of the shop seeing to the evening\u2019s few customers. \u0141ucja winced at this, though she had seen him do it numerous times before.<br /> \u201cI wish you wouldn\u2019t do that in front of me, Laszlo,\u201d she said with a shudder. \u201cI don\u2019t like being reminded of\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf what I am, dear sister?\u201d he asked teasingly. \u201cI tried to protect you from the truth for many years, but you seemed incapable of letting it go. <i>You</i> were the one who wanted to know everything about me, remember?\u201d He began placing the pastries on a serving plate one by one, and set the pan on a metal rack to cool.<br /> <br /> She leaned in and kissed his cheek when he had finished. \u201cOf course,\u201d she said softly, \u201cand you know that I still love you, dear brother. I just\u2026 I\u2019m not used to thinking of you as someone who might be powerful and dangerous yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo snorted in mock effrontery. \u201cWell, thank you for the vote of confidence,\u201d he said wryly.<br /> <br /> Her laugh was musical, and everything was all right between them once more. \u201cI\u2019m going to go up front and let Mama know that the P\u0105czek are nearly ready to serve. If it\u2019s not too busy, she might let us go out tonight. Andrezj has a new phonograph record he wanted me to hear; I\u2019m sure he wouldn\u2019t mind if you came along as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded his assent, though privately he was not sure of this at all. Though he and Andrezj still maintained their friendship, he often thought that the other man would prefer to spend more time alone with his pretty young sister. P<i>erhaps I\u2019ll drop by the Hedge Maze</i>, he thought to himself. <i>It has been too long since I looked in on the local changelings</i>.<br /> <br /> He was wiping the sweat from his brow with a towel when he heard excited murmurs from the front of the store. A moment later, \u0141ucja\u2019s head appeared in the kitchen door. \u201cLaszlo, you must come up front for a moment,\u201d she said breathlessly.<br /> <br /> He gestured at himself: sweaty, grimy, dusted in flour. \u201cPapa doesn\u2019t want me at the counter when I haven\u2019t washed,\u201d he reminded her.<br /> She winked. \u201cJust this once, it will be okay. Now hurry up!\u201d<br /> <br /> Mama\u2019s voice called from the front of the store. \u201cYes, Laszlo, come on out. It will be all right,\u201d she said.<br /> <br /> Despite their entreaties, Laszlo took a moment to clean his hands, and then reluctantly walked toward the front of the shop, conscious of his appearance. The sun had set while he worked, and for the most part the neighborhood had finished its shopping. The shop was empty save for Mama, \u0141ucja, and two men\u2026 one of whom he recognized.<br /> <br /> \u201cHeinrich, my friend!\u201d he said warmly as he strode into the shop. Heinrich von Klingemann was a frequent visitor to the bakery when his business brought him to Berlin, and Laszlo was always glad to see him. The two had met at the Hedge Maze almost a year earlier. They had begun a fumbling, awkward courtship at first, but each of them had quickly realized that there was no true romantic spark between them, and instead they had become fast friends.<br /> <br /> Heinrich was nobly born, and while his elder brother \u2013 a war hero \u2013 had inherited the family\u2019s land and title, Heinrich had contented himself with managing the family\u2019s business interests, and had settled into a quiet life in the country running his factory. Realizing that rural Germany had little to offer a man of his proclivities, he often took advantage of Berlin\u2019s nightlife when business brought him to the city. He made a point of visiting the Piekarski bakery at least once during each such trip, and on such occasions he and Laszlo often stayed up for hours talking together.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow that both of my children are here to tend to the shop,\u201d Mama said graciously, \u201cI should go upstairs and see to supper.\u201d Her eyes twinkled merrily as she glanced at Laszlo, and he sighed inwardly. Ksenia Piekarski had long suspected that her son preferred the company of other men, but beyond that her insight failed her. \u201c\u0141ucja, perhaps you could help me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja rolled her eyes. \u201cI\u2019ll be up soon, Mama,\u201d she promised. \u201cI\u2019ll watch the store so that Laszlo can speak with his friends.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mama clasped her daughter\u2019s hand and smiled beatifically. \u201cYou are a good girl, \u0141ucja, both kind and pretty,\u201d she said, with a pointed glance at Heinrich\u2019s companion.<br /> <br /> Once Mama had vacated the area, Laszlo turned his own attention to their other visitor. His resemblance to Heinrich was plain, though he was taller and broader in the shoulders. A few years older than Heinrich, the figure he cut was \u2013 there was no other word for it \u2013 <i>dashing</i>. His hair was fashioned with military precision, and his beard and mustache were immaculate.<br /> <br /> But behind the mundane, this man carried an almost visible aura of death.<br /> <br /> Laszlo broke into a guileless grin. \u201cYou must be Wolfram,\u201d he said, extending<br /> his hand.<br /> <br /> The other man sketched a courteous bow before extending his own. His handshake was firm and strong. \u201cWolfram Johann Ritter von Klingemann, at your service, sir,\u201d he said in a deep voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cWelcome to our bakery, Herr von Klingemann,\u201d \u0141ucja said with a bright smile. \u201cYour brother is both a good customer and a delightful conversationalist, and it will be our pleasure to serve you as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, miss,\u201d Wolfram said, leaning forward to kiss her extended hand. Behind him, Heinrich smirked ever so slightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWolfram, I\u2019d like to introduce you to W\u0142adys\u0142aw Piekarski, the best baker in all of Berlin, and my dear friend,\u201d Heinrich said, indicating Laszlo.<br /> <br /> Laszlo grinned. \u201cYou almost pronounced it correctly this time, Heinrich,\u201d he laughed. \u201cPlease, Herr von Klingemann, call me Laszlo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if I can be Wolfram to you, my friend,\u201d the other man said with a friendly smile. \u201cMy brother speaks most highly of you, Laszlo\u2026 both of your skill as a baker, and in\u2026 other areas,\u201d he ended delicately.<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded. \u201cYour brother is too kind,\u201d he said. \u0141ucja cleared her throat significantly behind him. \u201cOh, and you may speak freely in front of my sister \u0141ucja. She is aware of both my romantic preferences and my status as a Beast.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heinrich smiled broadly and moved forward to take \u0141ucja\u2019s hand. \u201cLaszlo told you, then? Good, I always said he shouldn\u2019t keep such things from his family.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja snorted a most unladylike laugh. \u201cNo, he did not \u2018tell\u2019 me, Heinrich\u2026 I had to ferret it out of him over months!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStill, this is excellent news. Now Laszlo has someone close in whom he can confide.\u201d He broke off and his look soured. \u201cSomeone <i>other</i> than Mateusz, I mean. That one is too dire.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo turned back toward their other guest. \u201cIt is nice to see one of your kind here in Berlin. I have always been fascinated by Sin-Eaters, but I have not had many opportunities to speak with one. Most of the Sin-Eaters in Berlin belong to die Wacht, and they are\u2026 not forthcoming to people like me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram\u2019s face darkened as though the sun had gone behind a cloud. \u201cNo,\u201d he said tersely, \u201cI imagine they are not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja came to their rescue. \u201cI am sorry, but\u2026 Sin-Eater?\u201d she asked plaintively.<br /> <br /> Laszlo nodded. \u201cWolfram died during the Great War,\u201d he explained, \u201cbut he was brought back to life.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja\u2019s eyes widened at this remarkable pronouncement.<br /> <br /> \u201cI did not come back from the Shadowlands alone, though,\u201d Wolfram elaborated. \u201cI brought a powerful spirit with me. Together, we find ghosts and help them to resolve their circumstances and move on to the next world. Of course, I have had precious little time for that lately\u2026 my current friends do seem to find themselves in a lot of precarious situations.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u0141ucja\u2019s interest was piqued. \u201cYou have other friends like you?\u201d she asked. \u201cOr are they more like my brother?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wolfram shook his head. \u201cI know a few other Sin-Eaters, yes,\u201d he said, \u201cbut I have never met anyone like Laszlo before. No, I was speaking of a vampire, two werewolves, and three changelings\u2026 people who have been transformed by faerie magic,\u201d he explained when he noted her confusion.<br /> <br /> She glared at Laszlo reproachfully. \u201cYou never told me,\u201d she began angrily.<br /> <br /> Laszlo shrugged. \u201cYou never asked,\u201d he noted, which he knew would infuriate her. \u201cNow, won\u2019t Andrezj be waiting for you, dear sister?\u201d he asked sweetly.<br /> <br /> She blew out her breath in a huff. \u201cLet him wait,\u201d she said sharply. \u201cI want to hear more about the vampires and werewolves!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll get us some fresh P\u0105czeks,\u201d Laszlo offered as he escorted their guests to a table.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, yes,\u201d Wolfram said eagerly. \u201cHeinrich has told me that I must try the pastries here. How much are they?\u201d he asked, reaching into his pocket for a coin-purse.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease,\u201d Laszlo scoffed. \u201cYou are family. Let us speak no more of payment.\u201d<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Laszlo clambered the last few steps into the rotunda at the top of the Berliner Dom, sparing a reproachful glance at Uncle Mateusz, who sat perched on the outer railing like a brooding vulture. \u201cYou couldn\u2019t have chosen another place to meet, uncle?\u201d he said, gasping for breath. \u201cYou had to call me to the top of the largest <i>Christian</i> church in all of Berlin\u2026 at midnight?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz said nothing for a moment. When he finally spoke, it was almost a sigh. \u201cThis is a good place. You can see almost all of Berlin from up here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBe that as it may,\u201d Laszlo grumbled, \u201cwe cannot all of us fly. I had to break a lock and sneak past the caretaker to get up here. Can you imagine what they would do if they caught me, a Jew, breaking into the Berlin Cathedral in the middle of the night?\u201d<br /> <br /> It almost seemed as though Mateusz hadn\u2019t heard him; he continued gazing wordlessly out over the brightly lit streets. After a moment he exhaled sharply. \u201cIt is important, Laszlo,\u201d he said softly. Turning to regard his nephew, he stepped down from his perch and leaned against one of the pillars. \u201cLook out over our city, nephew. <i>Really</i> look, and tell me what you see.\u201d<br /> <br /> His tone made Laszlo nervous. He knew that his uncle was not asking him to recite the names of streets and landmarks. \u201cI see Berlin,\u201d he said after thinking on the question for a minute. He truly couldn\u2019t think of another way to succinctly describe the view. \u201cI see the city where I was born, the city to which my parents moved after leaving Rzeczpospolita Polska. I see theaters and cinemas, concert halls and clubs, museums and temples and restaurants. I see a people who are beginning to emerge from the shadow of defeat and find that they are strong once more.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz nodded, but seemed troubled. \u201cYes,\u201d he agreed slowly, \u201cI see all of these things as well. But I also see something more. Can you not see it, nephew? Can you not feel it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo turned back to the city, perplexed. And then, suddenly, he did feel something\u2026 a sort of darkness; a pulse beneath the ordinary sounds and rhythms of the city. \u201cGotenyu!\u201d Laszlo exclaimed. \u201cWhat is that?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz shook his head. \u201cI\u2026 don\u2019t know. I think that it is nothing much, just yet. But given time\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you suspect, Uncle?\u201d Laszlo asked, unnerved.<br /> <br /> \u201cHeroes,\u201d Mateusz replied.<br /> <br /> Laszlo did not understand. \u201cHeroes?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe ancient enemies of the Children,\u201d Mateusz elaborated. \u201cThey are terrible foes; they seek only the glory of the kill. They fear all things they do not understand\u2026 and they make no effort to understand <i>anything</i> which is different. They are drawn to the Children through the Primordial Dream, and they have terrible powers to weaken and distract us. I have never encountered one personally, but I have heard tales\u2026 read of their exploits in ancient texts\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo shuddered. \u201cAnd you feel that one of these Heroes has come to Berlin?\u201d he asked. \u201cWhat should we do?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz shrugged. \u201cI do not think we need fear them <i>yet</i>,\u201d he said after a moment. \u201cI do not believe any of them have yet arisen. But I fear that a great many of them slumber among the population, waiting to be born. Self-aggrandizement, pride, arrogance\u2026 anything which proclaims \u2018I am good and everything else is evil,\u2019 these are the hallmarks of the Hero. I see these things more and more on the streets of Berlin these days. National pride might seem like simple patriotism, but it can be taken too far. We must be careful. We must not draw attention to ourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo thought about that. \u201cBut\u2026 our Horrors must still feed,\u201d he said helplessly. \u201cWe must still protect our people.<br /> <br /> Mateusz nodded. \u201cOf course,\u201d he agreed, \u201cbut we must do so subtly from now on. And we must be prepared to leave quickly if it becomes necessary. A Hero would not hesitate to strike at us through Ksenia, or Mi\u0142osz, or \u0141ucja.\u201d<br /> <br /> Laszlo contemplated what his uncle was saying. \u201cLeave Berlin?\u201d he asked in a small voice. \u201cI\u2026 have always lived here. I would not know what to do outside of the city. It is my home, and I love it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mateusz placed a hand gently on his nephew\u2019s shoulder. \u201cNevertheless, it may become necessary. If so, this will no longer be the city you love.\u201d<br /> <br /> They leaned against the railing for some time after that, saying nothing, and staring out together over once familiar streets which now seemed threatening.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <i>Golden Eagle </i>journals resume next week. I will see you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 01-20-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:10:22-08:00","id":1038750,"title":"","content":"Called on account of snow? Right now the accursed white stuff is about three feet deep outside my door and the snow banks are taller than I am.<br /> Just curious if you will be connecting Laszlo to the Golden Eagle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T00:49:12-08:00","id":1038796,"title":"","content":"I believe it.<br /> <br /> Hopefully. We will see how things shake out. Laszlo is compatible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:32:55-08:00","id":1043089,"title":"","content":"The Conspiracy boards the Orient Express for Yugoslavia, then Cyprus. This session was meeting people on the train and getting to know them. Different journals cover interactions with different people. Lizette is a story, taking place the night of the initial meetings not covering the next day. It is still a recap, though. Enjoy.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLVI</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 17 July 1924<br /> <br /> Of course a train trip to Italy cannot be without incident, or at least without intrigue. We boarded the Orient Express today to begin our travels and found a few familiar faces. Amethyst was there as well as Hilde and Kiva, which I\u2019ve been told is spelled Caoimhe. I do not understand the way the Irish spell things. It makes no sense when written out in the roman alphabet. Unfortunately, Dearbhail and Dacian could not join us on our trip. Jamal was concerned to some extent about their connection to the Golden Eagle. He could not get it resolved before we had to leave. I do not know how long they will be unable to travel with us due to the possible danger. I will miss Dearbhail especially. I have found her company to be enjoyable and special. I will miss her but would rather she not be harmed. If that means that she must stay behind, then so be it.<br /> <br /> And on an interesting note there was one more familiar face on the train today. Not one that I\u2019d expected to see in my travels. I saw Lazslo. He was sharing a car with Harlow of all people. Lazslo apparently also knows Wolfram so he came over to say hello and Wolfram introduced him to the pack. Lazslo greeted me as Reznik and I remembered that I had been hunting at the time that we met. I probably should have given him the name Marek, but I was of a different mind at the time. I did tell him that he could call me Marek. We traded small talk before Harlow decided that there needed to be a Bridge game. I am not a fan of Bridge so I stood to the sidelines and watched the others play. I was also watching the other people that were not playing the game. They for the most part were paying attention to others in the car. It was interesting to see who was watching who.<br /> <br /> There was also someone on the train that seemed similar to a werewolf but is not one. Her name is Peidad. She must have a different shape when she changes. I did not ask her, but did strike up a conversation with her. She was watching the Spring Courtiers we met on the train, Lizette and a woman in a white hat. I tried a couple of different languages before stumbling on one that she spoke, French. I believe that she is Spanish. Anyway, we talked briefly. Of note, she did ask if I was a hunter. I told her \u201cof sorts.\u201d I just didn\u2019t elaborate what my prey was. I got the impression that she is also a hunter.<br /> <br /> After the Bridge game was done Peidad stayed behind and I watched briefly to see who left with who. One of the Spring Courtiers in a black hat, followed right after Amethyst and Wolfram. Hilde left after that and Peidad paid attention to her as she left. Soon after that I took my leave and went back to my room in our train car. Tatiana and I arranged it so we had rooms on opposite ends of the car to keep everyone else protected. Wolfram was next and Christina and the little one were in the middle. It was a very defensibly oriented arrangement which I thought was practical. I do not know if the others thought the same way but they agreed to stay in the rooms we suggested.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 18 July 1924<br /> <br /> This morning Wolfram called us all into the room that we had designated for meetings. He had some interesting news to share with us. Apparently he had talked to Amethyst last night and she confided in him that she was carrying diplomatic papers to the King of Yugoslavia. I can only assume that she has a side job as a courier. Being a performer would cover her travels fairly well. I personally did not like the idea of going to Yugoslavia again, but as it turns out she didn\u2019t ask us to. She simply asked Wolfram to hold onto the papers until we disembark from the train. I believe that she was afraid that she was being watched and Wolfram did say that he saw the woman in the black hat down the hall from his room last night after they were done talking. It\u2019s possible that she was eavesdropping and managed to move down to the end of the hall before Wolfram opened the door to the cabin.<br /> <br /> We also talked about Lazlo. The others were curious about him. I told them what I knew about him. That he is a hunter of sorts and embodies the spirit of the Golem. I mentioned that I met him in Berlin when we were both hunting the same man. Apparently Wolfram knows him because Lazslo is friends with his brother Heinrich. I do not know Heinrich well, but he seems like a decent man. I am unsure how Lazslo met him. Perhaps Heinrich went to his bakery? I do not know. It doesn\u2019t really matter. All in all Lazslo seems to be a decent man as well. I know that he \u201cteaches\u201d those that need to learn a lesson and is protective of his people. He is much stronger than his visible stature would indicate and at least on the one occasion I saw him hunt, he was good at keeping up with his quarry. I would not mind hunting with him again.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we are not almost there.<br /> <br /> There are three more days.<br /> <br /> Hush, volchonok.<br /> <br /> I know only I can hear you howl, but it is foolish anyway.<br /> <br /> Why don\u2019t you go poking around the train? I am sure there are many interesting smells.<br /> <br /> Well, yes... what have I done? Just be careful around the shifter and the mage.<br /> <br /> The old woman that Alla has taken up with. I do not know what she can do, but there is some magic that deals with spirits, I believe.<br /> <br /> She is a strange one, that is true. Connie is correct, we should have her and Greta converse, somewhere we could watch.<br /> <br /> The other one? Oh, the shifter.<br /> <br /> Just because the shifter is not Uratha does not mean she will be Marek\u2019s new mate.<br /> <br /> I do not know if she can see spirits. Perhaps you should not ask, foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I will. She is an attractive woman.<br /> <br /> It is true, volchonok, there are many strange ones here. More fairies for you to chase. The Sin-Eater friend of Wolfram\u2019s, Alla\u2019s vampire sister, and even a few humans we know - Harlow and the writer friend on Lizette\u2019s from her salons.<br /> <br /> And Constancia, yes, but we brought her with us, volchonok.<br /> <br /> No, she did not bite me. Not that it\u2019s any of your concern. Or are you saying you would not have smelled the blood, volchonok? Do spirits sicken?<br /> <br /> You are the one who said you could not smell.<br /> <br /> Are you challenging me, volchonok?<br /> <br /> There. Do you feel better?<br /> <br /> Oh, we are ignoring all that then? Yes, there was another friend here. The hunter that Marek met in Berlin, the one who is a Golem in his nightmares, or something like that. I did not realize this Lazslo was also a friend of Wolfram\u2019s.<br /> <br /> You think the pack could use another hunter, do you volchonok? He has his own life, not everyone is looking for a pack. Not everyone can drop everything to live forever in a French manor house. Plus, we know little of him.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, volchonok, perhaps. If there is some excitement with the woman Sin-Eater\u2019s documents, perhaps we will see his measure.<br /> <br /> Something about the king of Yugoslavia. She feared she was being followed or watched so not Wolfram carries them in himself.<br /> <br /> Probably not, not if they are sneaking about. But perhaps we will have a fight.<br /> <br /> Hrm? I do not know if Laszlo likes to run. There is no time now anyway. Perhaps when we stop.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Spy vs. Spy</u></b><br /> <br /> Nicolette DuBois had just walked away with Regina von Klingemann as Christina von Klingemann and Lizette \u00c9toile sat in the Klingemann compartment. The Gremlin\u2019s legs slowly kicked over the side of the bed in the compartment while Christina arranged the beds. They spoke to each other in French as she worked, Christina\u2019s accented, Lizette\u2019s smooth.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did you think of our fellow riders, Fairy Princess? I don\u2019t ride the train too often but they seemed\u2026interesting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026when away from the group I mainly spoke to Paula Van Dijk, she\u2019s a playwright from England who hangs out in the salons in Paris. Her plays are\u2026\u201d The Wizened seemed to try to search for the right words, looking at her lover, \u201cperhaps more salacious than you would like. One calls for nude scenes, another has some rather explicit queer characters, so\u2026\u201d A shrug.<br /> <br /> \u201cWas she trying to pick you up?\u201d The noblewoman made the question sound as neutral as possible, but her lips were pursed such as to make rather a sour face. <br /> <br /> \u201cNon\u2026we are friends from Paris. And I am very small.\u201d She watched her feet kick. \u201cWe talked about the other people we saw, it was nice. Hell of a Bridge player though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood at it, was she?\u201d Christina\u2019s expressive eyes looked over.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, Zvezdana is a really good card player, but Paula seemed to call really well. I thought she was overcalling but\u2026no.\u201d She pauses. \u201cActually, I had more luck than usual too. Should have Kenned her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou will have more opportunities to, and to help her cheat at bridge.\u201d A smile played on Christina\u2019s lips. \u201cWho was Zvezdana?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was going to ask if you had seen her. The other blonde woman in glasses. She was \u2018recently of Vienna.\u2019\u201d The Inventor looked up.<br /> <br /> Christina was thoughtful. \u201cThat\u2019s not a German name. Some flavor of Yugoslavian. Serbian? She looks like she could be German\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am not sure but she was up to something. Keeping an eye of several people, particularly Calpurnia, the woman wearing white and also Amethyst.\u201d Lizette was just watching her now.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you know about Calpurnia?\u201d Christina glanced at the door at heavier footsteps to see if Wolfram was returning, but it was just Marek going by the compartment.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing, except she had an English accent. We did not talk really. Just introductions when she spoke briefly to Zvezdana. Paula was watching her, but maybe that was because she was pretty.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am sure there is a lot going on that does not really concern us. And Amethyst?\u201d Christina sat down next to the smaller woman.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, of course Amethyst has the whole thing going on with needing help.\u201d Lizette leaned on the taller woman.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d The Noblewoman glanced out of the compartment to see if her husband was coming. \u201cWe will see what that is about.\u201d An arm around Lizette.<br /> <br /> The Gremlin raised an eyebrow. \u201cYou don\u2019t distrust Wolfram?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, not in the least! But I know you all fought several\u2026unfriendly Sin-Eaters. And I did not want to give the wrong impression by asking someone to go with him. Of course I trust him.\u201d Christina was firm.<br /> <br /> The Wizened nodded. \u201cAnyway. The fourth girl we played Bridge with was Caoimhe, who Wolfram may have mentioned. A member of the Irish Republican Army I helped to foil in Paris. She overcalls her hand. Zvezdana had a lot of work to do to make up for her shortcomings. They only seemed to do well when Paula was Dummy, which reflects badly on me, I suppose.\u201d A crooked grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am sure you were fine, Fairy Princess.\u201d Christina had an easy smile. \u201cWhat did you make of the other German, Laszlo?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh.\u201d The Gremlin thought about it a moment. \u201cDid not speak much, we were introduced and he was not rude but\u2026.\u201d She shrugged, \u201cMarek knew him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough,\u201d Christina\u2019s finger traced the back of Lizette\u2019s ear. The Gremlin visibly relaxed. \u201cI did not talk to too many people personally as I was tired from the day and Regina being fussy. I noticed Izzy, the Brit Alla was talking to. She seemed\u2026.odd. \u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette started to smile. \u201cYes I spent half the time not sure if they were getting along well or fighting. Or both. She kept telling Alla to leave then talking to her like an old friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes well English people are weird, Darling. Not just because they seem inclined to give we Austrians a run for our money of being hidebound. Only other person I noticed was the Spanish girl on the edge of the room seeming to be keeping an eye on things. \u201c<br /> <br /> Golden eyes opened, closed, and opened again. \u201cThe one besides Marek and the guy in the white suit being all sullen at the edge. Almost forgot her. Not sure what either of those were up to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think Marek talked to her there are at the end.\u201d Christina leaned her head out to listen.<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably fell in love with him too then. Hey!\u201d She wriggled as her lover tickled her slightly. <br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t be that way, love.\u201d Christina rose as Wolfram arrived, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cI kept her safe for you! How was your visit?\u201d The Gremlin beamed.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, it went well. We now have some sensitive diplomatic documents. I will discuss it all in the morning.\u201d The Forgotten kissed his wife and then his lover, gently. <br /> <br /> \u201cI should get back to my compartment. A bit tight for three, and I think Nicolette will bring Regina to see you too before bed.\u201d She glanced and saw the Au Pair peer out of her compartment. \u201cBesides, Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re will be mad if I am out any later in your compartment.<br /> <br /> The couple wished her goodnight with one more brief round of kisses and she returned to her compartment, passing Nicolette carrying Regina over on the way. But it was too late; there would be no tea for her.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XLVI</i><br /> <br /> Cast List as given to the players after the session:<br /> <br /> Constancia \u201cConnie\u201d Lampros: The Princess of Evil. Lovely and dangerous Maenad Mekhet. Greek.<br /> Christina von Klingemann: Wife to Wolfram, Lover to Lizette, Mother to Regina. Austrian<br /> Regina von Klingemann: Baby. Wins at screaming. German.<br /> Nicolette DuBois: Au Pair and innocent flower. French?<br /> <br /> <br /> Amethyst Trevelyan: singer with the papers from the King. Bulgarian. Not using her real name.<br /> Isobel \u201cIzzy\u201d Brown: English Mage. People keep talking to her. Bother.<br /> Caoimhe: Redheaded Irish Terrorist. The sexiest kind. Spring Fairest Flamesiren.<br /> Zvezdana Nova\u010d: International Woman of Mystery. Spring Fairest Romancer/Larcenist. Austrian?<br /> Peidad L\u00f3pez: Totally not a Colony, you guys. Spanish.<br /> Hilde Engle: Daeva, Blood-Sister to Alla. Not up to anything. German?<br /> Abigail Jerard: Amethyst's compartment companion. Black Hat. Belgian.<br /> Calpurnia Rhodes: The Woman in White. Not a Spy, definitely. Greek? British?<br /> Paula Van Dijk: Scandalous out lesbian playwright. English, recently of Paris<br /> Harlow Von Hoddenberg: Laszlo's Compartment companion. The poor fuck. Director. German?<br /> Jessica Walthstone: One of the friends traveling around. Nothing to see here. American <br /> Theresa James: The other friend. Also not up to anything. American<br /> Man in the White Hat: Unknown. <br /> <br /> So regular caveat: Do not take this as a historically accurate depiction of the train. There is damn little about how long a train in the 20s would take to get from Paris to Yugoslavia. And my descriptions of the cars may not have been correct for the Orient Express. And also, of course, technically the Simpleton-Orient Express. <br /> <br /> Laszlo did not catch all the supernaturals that time around. Perhaps he will next time. He got most though. Everyone is OOC pretty sure Peidad is a Colony. The Spring Courtier in the black hat Marek mentioned is Zvezdana in Lizette\u2019s journal (Scarlett Johansson from The Spirit). The Spanish Woman in Lizette\u2019s journal is Peidad in Marek\u2019s. <br /> <br /> I had a blast playing Izzy, and she was a crowd favorite.<br /> <br /> Things heat up next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T02:03:39-08:00","id":1050375,"title":"","content":"Hey you guys! Hey you guys!<br /> <br /> There was a murder on the Orient Express, you guys.<br /> <br /> Bet no one saw that one coming.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 18 July 1924<br /> <br /> After our talk with Wolfram we all went to the dining car for breakfast. Lazslo it seems obtained access to the kitchen car and baked pastries. He handed them out to everyone in the pack, and others in the dining car. I thought that was rather generous of the man. He must have gotten up early to do all that and have it ready by breakfast time. Though I suppose as a baker he is used to getting up early.<br /> <br /> Then things got interesting. Abigail, Amethyst\u2019s roommate came up to Wolfram and said that the singer needed to talk to him this morning. Wolfram and Abigail made their way back to Amethyst\u2019s compartment after breakfast and opened the door. Only to find the singer dead, her head caved in and blood everywhere. Abigail of course became rather upset and screamed. Wolfram on the other hand did his best to calm her down and get her back into the hallway where she could not see the scene. He assured her that Amethyst would be fine. Of note, Wolfram saw Caoimhe peek out from her own compartment, and Piedad was in the hallway, staring at Wolfram. Zvezdana had also left the dining car shortly before Wolfram did. She seemed rather curious in what was going on. While all of this was happening Tatiana, Fenric and I were making our way back to the train car where everyone else was. I heard the scream and decided that it would be good to investigate. The others followed after I told them that there was trouble. When we arrived Wolfram had gotten things under control for the most part. Abigail was still upset and Fenric took her aside to talk to her and use his gifts to calm her down.<br /> <br /> Wolfram had said that Amethyst was a little under the weather and Tatiana volunteered to go in and help her since she has medical training. I nodded and said that I\u2019d stay in the hall for now and keep watch. As Tatiana investigated the compartment Wolfram and I ushered people out of the hall, or at least away from Amethyst\u2019s compartment. I went and got water and a flannel to help clean up the singer before she woke up. Waking up in a pool of your own blood is never pleasant so I thought it would be prudent to clean her up, as well as the surrounding area. It is also easier to get blood out of cloth while it\u2019s still fresh, and her blood was just that, fresh. It wasn\u2019t long ago that someone caved in her head with something heavy. My estimate is that it took a professional about 20-30 seconds to lean into the compartment, bash the singer\u2019s head in and quickly go through her bag. The blackout curtain was also on the floor, which made me think that the killer had used the open window as a method of getting rid of the murder weapon. I told Wolfram of my observations.<br /> <br /> Tatiana also did a further search of the compartment for scents and found that there were a lot of different scents in the compartment. We then remembered that Amethyst had been signing autographs in her compartment when we first got on the train. So, we could not narrow it down to who the killer was, but we could only weed out the few that we knew it wasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> After Amethyst was cleaned up I arranged her and the compartment to make it look like, at a glance, she was just sleeping. Meanwhile Lazslo, who was sent by Lizette, came down to see if everything was okay. Tatiana assured him that all was well and he went back to pass the message along. After this Tatiana volunteered to stand guard in the singer\u2019s compartment while Wolfram took the pack, as well as Lazslo, back to the meeting compartment in our car for a talk about what was going on. We explained that Amethyst was one of the Claimed so despite her wounds she would come back to life at sundown. We just had to keep people away from her compartment until then. We also discussed my theories about who killed her and Wolfram\u2019s theories on why. Her bag had been searched and something taken. It obviously wasn\u2019t the diplomatic papers that the killer was likely looking for, but they took something. They may have just grabbed what was in there and planned on looking in detail at what they had stolen later. Our tentative plan was to have Amethyst show up for dinner and the rest of us could watch for reactions and see who was surprised to see her up and about.<br /> <br /> Around this time Harlow asked Lizette to check on the other playwright, Paula. They had a meeting scheduled and she was at least half an hour late for it and he had become worried. Lizette arrived at the other woman\u2019s compartment and knocked. Paula, who has a compartment to herself, insisted that she was fine and was just getting ready. She proceeded to make Lizette wait a while longer before she finally emerged from her compartment. With everything transpiring on the train I couldn\u2019t help but find that suspect. Did she honestly just sleep late, or is there another reason that she couldn\u2019t make her meeting on time? The killer likely would have gotten some blood on them and would need to clean up before they could mingle with everyone else on the train. With the force used and the spray of blood as it was, I\u2019m certain the killer got hit with it I just don\u2019t know if that\u2019s why Paula was late. I guess time will tell.<br /> <br /> After our talk it wasn\u2019t long before the train was due to go through a long tunnel. During that time the train would be completely dark, so we wanted to make sure we were placed appropriately just in case. The dark would be a good time to attempt something, whether it be theft or further violence. So, Tatiana stayed guarding Amethyst. Wolfram stayed with Christina and Regina in their car, I believe that Lizette and some of the others went to the dining car. Meanwhile, I stayed in the hall to keep watch. I figured anyone that tried to do anything to Christina, Regina or Amethyst would have to get past me to do it, and I\u2019m not limited by the lack of light.<br /> <br /> While I was standing guard in the hallway, before the tunnel, another of the passengers walked through on his way to the baggage car. It was the gentleman that wore the white hat. I don\u2019t think that I ever got a name for him, so that\u2019s how I\u2019ll describe him. After we started going through the tunnel he came back out of the baggage car and started on his way back through our car. The moment he entered the car I noticed his eyes flash, kind of like a cat\u2019s, and then it faded. After he noticed me watching him he put is arms out to touch either wall to guide his way back down the hallway. I could be wrong but it very much looked like to me that he could see perfectly well in the dark and tried to make it look like he couldn\u2019t. To conceal what he is perhaps? He acknowledged me on his way back through and continued on to the dining car.<br /> <br /> Soon after that little incident Tatiana used one of her gifts to speak into my head and said that she smelled Piedad in the hallway outside the door to Amethyst\u2019s compartment and that she was curious about what was going on inside. Apparently she had been by a few times, trying the door and finding it locked or just standing in the hallway. I said that I\u2019d go check it out. Tatiana also said that she had heard Calpurnia and Zvezdana talking in the hall but she couldn\u2019t understand what they were saying. She just knew that it did not sound friendly. I made my way to that car. I listened for a moment, only catching a little bit. They seemed to be accusing each other of something, I missed the beginning of their conversation, and were vaguely threatening one another. I opened the door and asked if everything was okay. In that instant both women hid weapons that they had in hand. Calpurnia had a high powered pistol, not sure of the caliber, and Zvezdana had a smaller pistol. Calpurnia excused herself and went into her compartment and Zvezdana made her way to the dining car. I do not know what was going on between those two but there is some obvious tension between those two women. I do not know if either of them was actually prepared to use the guns they were holding, and hopefully will not have to find out. One death is enough on this train trip. After that I went back to my hall and waited until we exited the tunnel. Nothing further happened.<br /> <br /> A couple of hours later the train stopped to pick up more passengers at Turin, one of which was our acquaintance Suzie. She certainly does get around. A strange man got on the same time she did. Interestingly a short while later I was talking to Lazslo and he mentioned what he had noticed about Paula, and our friend Suzie. To him they both smell of brimstone. He also noticed that Paula\u2019s eyes shone amber for a moment before returning to normal. This did not look good to me, so I explained to Lazslo what we knew about Suzie, her demon blood and her powers. Apparently there are others like her out there and there appears to be tension.<br /> <br /> After sunset Wolfram made his way to Amethyst\u2019s compartment and managed to heal her wounds somewhat after she woke up. She at least looks like nothing happened even if there is still some remaining damage from the attack under the surface. Wolfram explained to her what happened and confirmed that the blackout curtain had been up and she had been sleeping. She did remember someone opening the door, but the light from the hall temporarily blinded her and all she remembers is that she thinks the person that killed her was wearing a hat. This would mean that the hat was big enough to be noticed, so not likely a man\u2019s hat. So, unless a man was wearing a wide brimmed hat it was likely a woman that killed the singer. Amethyst also said that Abigail was really protective of her own bag and didn\u2019t want anyone near it. So, of course this prompted Tatiana to search the bag, and she found several pieces of what appears to be stolen art. Statues to be exact, some of which looked Chinese.<br /> <br /> Wolfram then left Amethyst to rest before dinner and made his way to the dining car. He explained to those of us there what was going on and what had been found. We also explained what we had discovered about Paula and Suzie. He said that he recognized the description. After we met Suzie the first time he did some research and found out that there was a group of demon-blooded individuals called the Lucifuge. Not sure if that\u2019s spelled correctly, but I wasn\u2019t about to ask Wolfram mid explanation to tell me how to spell the name of the group. Anyway, he said that they tended to seek out others like themselves and recruit them to their organization. If the person in question doesn\u2019t want to join the Lucifuge then they are killed. So, it looks like I was right about the possibility of tension between Paula and Suzie. I do not think Suzie is aware of the Lucifuge, so the instigator is likely to be Paula. I guess we\u2019ll see what happens on that front.<br /> <br /> Overall, there is a lot of different things transpiring on this train. The man with the white hat is up to something. Calpurnia and Zvezdana obviously have something going on between them that could turn violent. Paula and Suzie may come to confrontation, and someone succeeded in killing Amethyst, presumably trying to get a hold of the diplomatic papers that she carried. I know the killer did not anticipate us getting involved with their little plan at least. It is likely that we will get involved to some degree in the other \u201cgoings on\u201d that are transpiring around us. We always seem to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> It was a joke, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that Liz is often not careful. That is why it was funny to say.<br /> <br /> Yes, the loud noise startled you, I remember, but she did not singe your fur. You are a spirit.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I will not talk to her about whether her bombs can singe spirits.<br /> <br /> Because they cannot and if I ask, it will give her the idea and it would not be a good idea.<br /> <br /> I do not know if the mage\u2019s cannibal worries were the same kind of joke. It is difficult to tell with her.<br /> <br /> Ah, no, it is true that Amethyst was not eaten by cannibal, that it for certain. She had her head bashed in, no bites. And it was not Peidad either. I simply do not know if the mage was joking.<br /> <br /> Peidad did linger, but it seemed like curiosity. Perhaps she is a fox shifter.<br /> <br /> Because, volchonok, she does not wear a hat. Amethyst said the person who killed her had a hat. Or perhaps wild hair.<br /> <br /> It means it is likely not Paula, with her man\u2019s hat. And not Peidad, as I said. But yes, it does mean it could be most any of the other women. Well, not Hilde, Constancia or Christina.<br /> <br /> Because their scent was not in the room, foolish volchonok.<br /> <br /> I think it is the other Fairest, the one who is not the redhead, or the human all in white.<br /> <br /> The Fairest was at breakfast when the murder happened, yes, but she left early. The two I mentioned were fighting in the corridor while I waited in ambush. One of them tried the door.<br /> <br /> I do not know what they were arguing about, as they weren\u2019t speaking in an important language. Marek said they were threatening each other with guns.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it would be better for overhearing if all humans spoke the same tongue. But it would be worse if you wanted to not be overhead.<br /> <br /> I know you did not think of that. It is because I am the more clever one.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have to be clever to know why she was killed. The documents, of course, the ones Wolfram has. Or the statues. Probably not the statues though.<br /> <br /> The other one in her room has stolen statues, from museums and the like. This is probably why Suzi is here, for the dragon ones.<br /> <br /> Yes, the others were talking about her and Paula, something about brimstone and lucifugus.<br /> <br /> What? I don\u2019t care, she is here for the statue. If she asks, I suppose we can stop Paula from monster hunting her. But Paula is Lizette\u2019s friend... It would be a good fight, either way.<br /> <br /> A run would also be good after spending so much time in a small room with death. But someone has been killed because of something a packmate holds. Now is not the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 18th July 1924<br /> <br /> Okay, I am going to organize my thoughts here, to see if it stimulates my genius. I am really better at building train busting bombs than solving murders on them, but eh, a Gremlin\u2019s gotta do what a Gremlin\u2019s gotta do.<br /> <br /> What Happened:<br /> <br /> Amethyst Trevelyan, a singer, was killed on the express this morning. She told her roommate, Abigail Gerard, she wanted to talk to Wolfram after breakfast, but before Abigail brought him back, someone killed her by hitting her on the head with a blunt instrument. They then grabbed the contents of her bag. Wolfram secured the scene and calmed Abigail while Fenric used his Ghoul powers to make her think all was well. Which is scary. Tatiana kept watch, and when Amethyst came back, Wolfram healed her, somewhat. She could not see her attacker clearly but thought she saw a hat on someone when the door opened and light flooded in, which suggests a woman but not definitely. Amethyst remained in her room for the night.<br /> <br /> Why Did This Happen:<br /> <br /> Amethyst is transporting sealed documents to the King of Yugoslavia. We think the killer planned to steal them. Small chance they wanted objects d\u2019art Abigail was transporting; she is either a thief or a fence. Probably, though, Amethyst was the target.<br /> <br /> Who Are The Suspects:<br /> <br /> There are six people that leap to mind. I will hit them in order.<br /> <br /> Zvezdana Nova\u010d is almost certainly a spy; she all but said as much. She left breakfast just a bit ahead of Wolfram, and stayed gone awhile. She is a Fairest, so possibly a psycho. She drew a gun on Calpurnia in the hallway. She could have been trying to get in, but we are not sure which one was. She is also drop dead gorgeous, though, so I hope it was not she.<br /> <br /> Calpurnia Rhodes clashed with Zvezdana in the hallway. She could have been trying to get in, but we are not sure which one was. She never even came to breakfast. She drew a gun on Zvezdana, and has a villain name.<br /> <br /> Caoimhe is on the train, and was stepping into her compartment when Wolfram entered the hallway. She is a woman and owns a hat. She has stayed in her compartment most of the day, though. Maybe keeping a low profile? Tried to commit mass murder a couple days ago. She is a Fairest, so possibly a psycho.<br /> <br /> The Man in the White Hat is not a social type, but he wears a hat and was moving through our car when the train went through the tunnel, in a way suggesting he could see in the dark. He is a man, though, and I did not notice him leave breakfast, but he could have stepped out and returned.<br /> <br /> Peidad has been acting just crazy, and was in the hall when we found Amethyst. Repeatedly tried to get in the compartment, and was foiled by Tatiana. On the other hand, she does not wear a hat, and she really seems more curious than anything else.<br /> <br /> Paula Van Dijk missed breakfast and was up to something in her compartment. Also has her own compartment so does not risk a roommate coming in and finding blood. Paula was definitely acting suspicious this morning. Also she is apparently part demon. However, while she is a woman, she wears a man\u2019s hat.<br /> <br /> Why Have We Not Used Magic:<br /> <br /> It was dark inside, and I don\u2019t think Animation would be of much use without a weapon. The sack was in the dark, and I know from past experience things in the dark are near useless. Several people had been in the room as Amethyst used it so sign autographs, confounding the Uratha. We think the weapon was thrown out the window as the Uratha did not smell blood at anyone\u2019s door.<br /> <br /> What do I Need:<br /> <br /> Something I can use to set with the Amethyst\u2019s blood, have Amethyst hide out of the range, and activate it causing any of Amethyst\u2019s blood to burst into flames, so a murder weapon or coat with blood would turn into an inferno. Mayhem! However, I don\u2019t have time to build or design anything like that.<br /> <br /> What Is Probably Unrelated:<br /> <br /> Well. Abigail seems an art thief or fence. She has high value items in her bag, at least some of which are stolen. Suzy Zhang got on, a prime person to sell some bejeweled dragons to. Paula is also apparently half demon like Suzy and from some monster hunting organization. She could have been preparing for a confrontation with Suzy in her room. I am not sure what the White Hat Man is up to, but he has seemed to take no interest in the door, though he was in our car when the lights went out. Finally, there is a Mage on board, who seems to be trying to appear harmless as possible, when not ranting about cannibals. She may just be trying to get under Alla\u2019s skirts, but I doubt it.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, now we just wait. We have what the killer wants, after all, and Amethyst is still alive (again.) Searching seems unlikely to get us anywhere if we are dealing with a professional, and Marek says we are, and being a professional he would know.<br /> <br /> I will consider all this as I go to bed and see if anything comes to me in the morning. Also best prime and ready the trainbuster just in case.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVII</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, I know.<br /> <br /> Anyway despite my suggestion for \u201cwacky Weekend At Bernie\u2019s style action\u201d, they hid the body until she came back. I thought it would be a good twist on the murder thing; easier to openly search for a murderer when you can admit there was a murder.<br /> <br /> Susie was in Berlin, the Lucifuge they met before the battle with Belial\u2019s Brood.<br /> <br /> The accounts left out (mostly, Tatiana touched on it) the whole thing where Izzy decided there were cannibals who tried to eat Amethyst, and wound up with Alla having a conversation with Amethyst thought the door asking if she had teeth marks anywhere. She also threatened to turn Alla into a lawn chair at one point. I thought that was funny anyway. Also the weird almost game of curious Peidad trying to get into the compartment and Tatiana keeping her out.<br /> <br /> When Wolfram found the body, I described the scene as frozen; Abigail looking in, horrified. Caoimhe peeking out her door. Peidad walking away almost fully across the car and stopping to look back. I then asked Wolfram\u2019s player what he was going to have Wolfram do, nothing things were about to start moving rapidly and his next action would set the tone for what the PCs were going to do.<br /> <br /> Anyway, good times. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:09:22-08:00","id":1057732,"title":"","content":"Our heroes solve the murder of Amethyst Trevelyan. So why aren\u2019t they happy?<br /> <i><br /> Session XLVIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> The train made a stop this morning in Milan that was going to last several hours, so the pack and Laszlo took advantage of the lay over and went out to get breakfast. It was a very nice restaurant. I do not know if I will ever be in that city again, but will have to remember the place we stopped for the future. When we got back Izzy, the mage woman that Alla has been chatting up the past day or so, came up to Laszlo and decided that he needed to wear a hat to make him look less scary. Not that Laszlo looks scary, but his presence has become more intimidating since he boarded the train. I will have to ask him about that. I am assuming that it is a product of him being one of the Children. Nevertheless the hat did not work and Izzy eventually gave up trying to make the man look less intimidating.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the train we went to our car to talk in private. Nicolette then informed us that the man in the white hat had been through our car again while we were out. I do not know if he was looking for something in our car or if he was on his way to the baggage car again. We will need to keep an eye on him. Also, Amethyst came back to talk to Wolfram and let him know of her observations at breakfast. We wanted to know who was surprised to see her up and about for the morning meal. It turns out that Piedad was surprised to see her, as was Zvezdana and Calpurnia and to some extent Caoimhe. I believe that Piedad was surprised to see her because she probably smelled the blood yesterday and believed that Amethyst was dead or badly hurt. She was right about that as it turns out, but she didn\u2019t know that the singer was going to heal so quickly from her injuries. Zvezdana and Calpurnia being mildly surprised is interesting. They were not present in the hallway when Abigail screamed and we had to calm her down. They would have no reason to be surprised to see her and yet they were. Caoimhe heard the commotion and looked out from her own compartment to see what was going on. She likely thought that something had happened to Amethyst as well and would have reason to be surprised to see her up and about. Amidst all this Tatiana asked me if I trusted Laszlo to watch our car. I thought for a moment and said yes. I do not know the man well, but from what I have seen he seems to be an honorable sort. If he betrays my trust though there will be a reckoning, but I do not think that he will do anything to harm my pack.<br /> <br /> After breakfast there was yet another Bridge game. I do not know why this game is so popular, but it certainly is. Tatiana and I elected to not play and instead sat on the sidelines and talked and kept an eye on things. Lizette played at a table with the man with the white hat. He introduced himself as Miles Anderson. Laszlo also played. He was in a game with Calpurnia, Abigail and an Italian gentleman named Luciano Torrez. It turns out that Luciano is an investigator for the Italian government. He talked to Calpurnia in Italian for a little while. I could not understand most of what he said but did pick up on the name Gaspar. He was the man that had originally stolen the Golden Eagle and gave it to his man Brandon. Also on a train I might add. Anyway, I remembered that Gaspar uses middle men to transport artifacts. Brandon as it turned out was some sort of creature that turned out to be rather dangerous. It is possible that Abigail, with her bag full of artifacts, is a courier for Gaspar. That might also explain why Luciano sat at the table with her.<br /> <br /> Later in the day, around dinner time, Izzy recruited Laszlo and Alla to go to the kitchens and look for her elusive cannibals. I\u2019m not sure how that woman got it in her head that there were cannibals on the train, but she did and has been in search of them for a while now. It is likely that she doesn\u2019t actually believe such a thing and is just playing the investigator in order to pass the time. She seems to like to cause a stir. Tatiana followed to watch the three search the kitchens. I think she thought that the whole thing was amusing. She eventually did get Izzy to use her powers to help us find out who attacked Amethyst. They investigated Amethysts room, then moved on to Caoimhe and Zvezdana\u2019s room since they were surprised to see the singer up and about at breakfast. They didn\u2019t find any sign of blood, but did find weapons and ammunition for those weapons. There was a shotgun and shells and pistol ammunition. Presumably Zvezdana was carrying the pistol. It was likely the one that I saw last night.<br /> <br /> Next was Piedad and Calpurnia\u2019s room. There had been blood in that room though there were no bloody clothes. Granted Tatiana did not smell a lot of blood, but the scent was definitely there. Calpurnia also had a lot of poisons in her possession. Specifically, arsenic and hemlock. I do not know what her intentions are but they are likely not good for the rest of us on the train. There were also drawings of all of the passengers on the train in Piedad\u2019s belongings. Including one of Suzie. Next was Paula\u2019s compartment. Tatiana smelled smaller amounts of blood in this compartment, but it was present. Piedad started to take an interest in what my pack mates were doing and went down the hall. I followed her and tried to distract her. I don\u2019t think it worked very well. Piedad tried to open Paula\u2019s door a couple of times and each time it was held shut from the inside by Tatiana. While all that was going on Christina and Lizette talked to Paula and tried to convince her that having someone, namely us, investigate her room was okay. I think Christina eventually convinced her and Paula came down the hall. She slipped into her own compartment and shortly came back out with everyone that had been in there. She acknowledged that she was having us investigate her compartment. It seemed rather flimsy to me, but Paula not being mad at the group lent credence to their presence. Through all of that I kept getting the scent of ozone and after talking with my pack mates came to the conclusion that it was from Izzy using her magic to open the doors of everyone\u2019s compartments. Apparently her magic smells like ozone. <br /> <br /> Piedad for her part was still curious about what was going on and Alla decided to let the young Shifter in on what was happening. We had pretty much agreed that we didn\u2019t think Piedad had been the one to kill Amethyst so she didn\u2019t see the harm in bringing her in on the investigation. It also helped to have an additional ally rather than have to constantly work around her and hide what we were doing. Initially I didn\u2019t think it was a good idea to let Piedad in on our activities, but then that tends to be my first reaction to most things. Keep the group small. Don\u2019t let others get involved in pack business. In this case though I think it worked out okay. Well, it mostly worked out okay. Alla then confronted Piedad about the drawings in her room and ended up really making the other woman mad. Alla ended up having to use some of her Kindred gifts to calm Piedad down and get her to help us out instead.<br /> <br /> After Piedad was calm we searched Luciano and Miles\u2019s compartment. Miles had nothing out of the ordinary in his belongings. Luciano on the other hand had several pieces of spy gear, weapons and burglar\u2019s tools to name a few things. He was definitely prepared to keep a watch on people and get into places that he might not be invited into. I would have been more concerned about the contents of his bag if I didn\u2019t know that he worked for the Italian government. After that they went to the Americans\u2019 room and found nothing but things that a tourist might have. <br /> <br /> Once we had searched everyone\u2019s compartments we made plans to go back and search the baggage car after everyone had gone to sleep. We figured that it would give us more freedom to move and investigate without being seen. To pass the time we went back to the dining car and ended up getting involved in a game of charades. I did not do well. I thought I was being pretty obvious in my portrayal of a baker, but not even Laszlo got it, so I assume that my rendition was not very well done. The others did better than I did, but some by not so much. I suppose that I still need to work on getting social cues right. How people act and such. I know that I am not the best with people, as is evidenced by my attempted distraction of Piedad and my performance at charades. I suppose that being able to empathize with people better will help me blend in that much better. It is not an easy task though. It is not in my nature to understand humans all that well. I am much better with animals.<br /> <br /> Later that evening we searched the baggage car and went through everyone\u2019s bags. Most came up clean or not very interesting. The ones that we paid attention to were Calpurnia\u2019s, who had documents in Greek in them, and Zvezdana who had documents in Serbian. Wolfram was able to read the documents in Greek and discovered that some of them were for plans for a military tank, as well as a discussion about plans to rearm certain groups in Germany. The later plan was in direct opposition to the treaty that was drawn up at the end of the Great War. The papers spoke of an alliance as well between Yugoslavia and Germany, as well as the aforementioned arming of certain groups within Germany. The documents that Calpurnia had basically explained that the alliance was the topic of Amethyst\u2019s missives, and why they should not be delivered. I think that we all thought then that Calpurnia was the one responsible for killing the singer in an effort to keep the papers from making it to Belgrade. After finding out all of this we decided to include Amethyst in the next discussion, what to do with the papers she was hired to deliver to Belgrade. Wolfram got her up and brought her back to the baggage car and we all talked. Initially we asked her if she could read Serbian and found out that she could. She read Zvezdana\u2019s documents seemed a bit alarmed, but did not say what the papers said. She just said that it was nothing important. Then we brought up the papers that we found in Calpurnia\u2019s belongings and what her own documents were about. A few options were brought up. Amethyst could deliver them as she was paid to do. She could go to Belgrade and say that the papers were stolen, or she could just drop off the map and not deliver the documents to Yugoslavia. She didn\u2019t seem to know what she wanted to do and asked that she be given the opportunity to sleep on it and she\u2019d let us know in the morning. We all agreed that would be okay and she headed back to her compartment.<br /> <br /> On the way back to our own compartments I happened to look out the window and saw a figure running alongside the train headed back the way we came. I didn\u2019t recognize her at first, but then Tatiana pointed out that it was Zvezdana. For her part Tatiana wanted to immediately jump off the train and run after her. She seemed rather eager to do so, and I was tempted to let her, but ended up telling her to stay. The train was moving far too fast for her to catch back up with us after she had dealt with Zvezdana. I will admit to being rather curious about what the other woman was up to, but did not want to separate our pack. Our final destination is coming up soon and once we arrive we will be boarding a boat. The boat cannot wait for Tatiana to catch up. Tatiana seemed disappointed but agreed to stay on the train. We will have to get Amethyst to translate the papers for us in the morning. Maybe they will give us a clue as to why Zvezdana jumped off of a moving train and was running away. Hopefully one of my more socially oriented pack mates will be able to talk Amethyst into translating the papers. I could convince her, but that would likely dissolve any good will she had with us. I am not subtle or overly friendly when it comes to convincing people to talk. We will see what the future brings. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations<br /> </b><br /> No, we are not running right now!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not yelling, YOU\u2019RE yelling!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not upset, foolish volchonok. And if I were, of course I have a good reason.<br /> <br /> They let her leave without telling us what is in the papers!<br /> <br /> The one that is dead like Wolfram.<br /> <br /> No, not those papers! The Serbian woman\u2019s papers, the one who is running away and we are not chasing.<br /> <br /> Well, we brought the dead one in to read them, because she reads Serbian. But then they started going on about honor and loyalty. As if it were honorable to help someone start a war. As if loyalty to kings and czars and countries and parties were not what was going to destroy this world. <br /> <br /> You mark my words, volchonok. I know many things more than you about humans. <br /> <br /> Yes, even dead ones. <br /> <br /> Bah, volchonok, it was just yesterday the woman was killed again. Remember, we took a nap in front of the door to stop the other hunter, the woman, from finding her dead?<br /> <br /> No, today I blocked the door to the woman writer\u2019s room so that the other hunter could not find us, not until the writer gave us permission.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, the old woman is insane, but it was more fun that bridge, or sitting around watching people eat. And she is very good at ear scratching.<br /> <br /> I do not think the cooks were prepared to defend themselves from charges of cannibalism, no.<br /> <br /> But, you are distracting me, volchonok. The dead woman was killed yesterday, and today we used Izzy\u2019s magic to open all the rooms to investigate. Once we convinced her it was not Harlowe who was killed and it was not the lesbian who did it.<br /> <br /> No, we found nothing. Well, except that the Greek woman\u2019s room smelled the most of blood. And the other hunter had drawn pictures of us all. Oh, and the Italian man had a drawing of the Golden Eagle and the one we stole it from.<br /> <br /> He is a detective, and looking for the one who stole it, it seems. The one before us.<br /> <br /> It is not important! Next we decided to check the baggage car - <br /> <br /> Oh yes, first they played Charades. We wanted to wait until the others were asleep.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, Marek is very bad at Charades. <br /> <br /> Bah, Constancia is very good at it. Very, very good. They were just too embarrassed to guess properly.<br /> <br /> Of course I was not embarrassed.<br /> <br /> Do not hurry me, volchonok!<br /> <br /> Maybe I will not tell you the rest. You were the one who decided to go running off in the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Very well, I will tell you. Stop looking at me like that. In the baggage car, it was like I said. The Greek woman had papers saying the king of Yugoslavia promised to let Germany move weapons through them, even though human rules say the Germans can\u2019t have weapons, not like that.<br /> <br /> She was supposed to stop the papers Wolfram now has from getting to this king. So she probably killed the dead woman.<br /> <br /> No, the running away woman is the Serb. We don\u2019t know what her papers said, because the others let the dead woman go without telling us, even though there was obviously something interesting there.<br /> <br /> It was very bad of them.<br /> <br /> What good things? We are stuck in a train and don\u2019t know what the papers say.<br /> <br /> Laszlo is not pack, he is just helping guard. He was alone after Harlowe left, Marek trusts him and we had a spare room.<br /> <br /> It is true, volchonok, he seemed much more wolfish today. And large. That is why Izzy tried to make him wear a large flowery hat. It is because he hungers.<br /> <br /> I do not know for what. Whatever he eats, I suppose. Not pastries, he made those this morning.<br /> <br /> No, Suzi is not pack either. Why...?<br /> <br /> I was just warning her to be careful. It would be annoying to save her from the Watch just so the writer could kill her.<br /> <br /> That is right, everything is horrible and there are not good things. I hate trains. And languages I can\u2019t read.<br /> <br /> Marek said we can\u2019t run. So no. When this horrible trip is done, we will run. For days maybe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 19th July 1924<br /> <br /> May as well do a second document on the case, it is all but solved.<br /> <br /> Who did it?<br /> <br /> Calpurnia Rhodes, probably. She was not at breakfast, was a woman with a feminine hat, was a spy, and had documentation (in Greek, which Wolfram could read) charging her with stopping Amethyst\u2019s delivery of certain documents.<br /> <br /> What about the others?<br /> <br /> Caoimhe and Zvezdana Nova\u010d couldn\u2019t have, unless they were in cahoots. Also, it seems Zvezdana and Amethyst are allied in some way we don\u2019t understand yet. That is the last piece. Regardless, it seems unlikely.<br /> <br /> Miles Andersson, the man in the white hat, is acting suspicious, but he has nothing implying he was involved in that. I am sure he is involved in something.<br /> <br /> Similarly Paula Van Dijk has a different agenda, and does not wear a woman\u2019s hat. It seems unlikely. Peidad does not appear to own a hat, and clearly does not know what is going on.<br /> <br /> We solved it. So why aren\u2019t we happy?<br /> <br /> Because it turns out it was agreements between elements in Yugoslavia with elements in Germany backing people like Die Wacht. If Amethyst succeeds it will ultimately harm our cause. Not that she had any idea. When she read the documents we found in Calpurnia\u2019s things she was shocked and dismayed. But she feels torn between honor and duty and doing what\u2019s right. We also found documents that apparently gave Zvezdana instructions but none of us could read. Amethyst could, but managed to avoid doing so.<br /> <br /> Zvezdana then fled the train. In motion. In the middle of the night.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s next?<br /> <br /> We decide what to do about Amethyst and Calpurnia. We confront each after deciding what to do about the murder and finding out what Zvezdana is up to. Probably something needlessly complicated.<br /> <br /> What is the Cannibalism Thing?<br /> <br /> Hell if I know. Izzy dragged Alla and Laszlo into the kitchen then, during dinner, broke into several rooms to search them. Found out Lucciano Torrez is carrying a great deal of weaponry. I think at some point they changed it to investigate Amethyst\u2019s murder, but I will be honest I am not entirely sure anymore.<br /> <br /> What are the other time bombs?<br /> <br /> Abigail and Lucciano, as Abigail is either working for or is Gaspar, and Lucciano is investigating Gaspar. This is of some interest as Gaspar stole the Golden Eagle to start with. And we stole it from Ewan, his mechanical minion. Related, Abigail is selling objets d\u2019art and artifacts to Iris DeVeers (who is a mechanical creature also) and Suzie Zheng, who is part demon. Susie is due to be confronted by Paula over some secret Catholic demon society, which seems strange. <br /> <br /> Can I make a better time bomb?<br /> <br /> Oh yes! I have enough explosive with me to blow up about two thirds of the train. I just need to put together with an alarm clock or something. If I were hunting Werewolves there would be chunks of silver in it. Vampires would take chunks of sunlight, I guess. Not sure how you would do that.<br /> <br /> Actually, sunlight is absorbed as heat, if it is special sun heat I could maybe have the stored (as heat) sunlight in chunks of something consumed by the explosion to release the sunlight. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Wait, I got off track.<br /> <br /> Who is bad at charades? <br /> <br /> Marek. Marek is very bad at charades.<br /> <br /> No more focus. That\u2019s okay, that\u2019s everything, I think. One more day\u2026<br /> <i><br /> End Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> Lazlo is Hungry, so his perceived size increased. Isobel reacted as she always does: with aplomb. <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see, arranged and rolled out more bridge games, but nothing came of that in journals. It got a name for Miles Andersson, and ultimately lead to Christina and Lizette talking Paula into letting people in her compartment. <br /> <br /> Marek\u2026really is bad at charades. <br /> <br /> And no, there were no cannibals. <br /> <br /> Okay, one more train session. Time for things to get exciting. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:31:24-07:00","id":1064424,"title":"","content":"And then all hell broke loose\u2026<br /> <br /> Sorry about the delay, I got the last (well, first) journal in right at the last minute before the session and it is by far the one that requires the most formatting, so no way to even start on journals before going to the game last night. But here they are now.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLIX</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 20 July 1924<br /> <br /> Today picked up where yesterday left off. Izzy continued her \u201csearch\u201d for cannibals on the train by trying to order human flesh for breakfast. I think she just ended up disturbing the wait staff more than anything else. After breakfast was over Wolfram invited Amethyst back to our car to talk in private. She arrived a few minutes later and we all discussed the documents that Wolfram was holding for her. She eventually agreed not to deliver the documents or the message that they contained to the Yugoslavian King. In return she wanted to keep the papers that we found in Zvezdana\u2019s belongings that were written in Serbian. She also said that she was not going to translate the documents for us. I was a little annoyed at that, but she had leverage and knew it. I know that Tatiana was not happy with that turn of events as well. We didn\u2019t really have any leverage to use on her either. She knows the content of the original papers and could still pass along the message to the King. She could also mention our names and our interest in making sure the documents never made it to their destination. I do not know if she was planning this the whole time or if it just worked out for her in the end. I think it\u2019s somewhere in the middle. So, we had to agree to let things lay with the Serbian papers and we would destroy the other documents at our leisure. <br /> <br /> After we talked to Amethyst we confronted Calpurnia as a group about her involvement in Amethyst\u2019s death. Wolfram told her straight out that we knew what she had done and why. We assured her that the documents that she was sent to retrieve will not see the light of day. I believe that she was content with that outcome. She would not be destroying the documents herself, but they would be dealt with regardless. Also during this conversation, we found out that Calpurnia is a British Intelligence agent who had been sent on this mission a while ago. I believe that she said the plan was conceived at the Olympics and she had been following Amethyst since then.<br /> <br /> Before we left Calpurnia, Laszlo had a little \u201cconversation\u201d with her about Amethyst\u2019s death. He used his aura of menace to scare the woman into admitting that she had murdered the Claimed woman. She seemed honestly contrite, and more than a little scared, after that. Laszlo for his part seemed satisfied that she had learned her lesson and was content to leave things there. After that he was also a little less physically imposing. I think he appeased the spirit of the golem that lives within him by making a guilty woman confess her crimes.<br /> <br /> Later in the day we were all in the dining car when the excitement started. Abigail, Suzie and Iris were at one table making what appeared to be a business deal, when they were interrupted by Luciano. The Italian man confronted them and told them that they were under arrest. He named the charges as acquiring and selling of stolen artifacts. I think he was expecting the ladies to come quietly. That is not what happened. Paula moved up behind Luciano and said something to Suzie in Chinese. Then Abigail said \u201cFuck it\u201d and flipped over the table she was sitting at and pulled a gun. At that point Christina and Regina fled the dining car and made their way back to our own car. Caoimhe and Calpurnia both pulled pistols as well. Then the shooting started. I was expecting a blood bath considering the number of people shooting at each other in such a confined space, but it appeared that no one could hit their targets. Not even Suzie and her fire ball could hit who she intended. Statistically speaking someone should have at least been hit, and at least one person should have died, but that wasn\u2019t the case. I suspect that some sort of magic was in effect, though I do not know who used it.<br /> <br /> Of all the people involved in the fighting Suzie was the closest to a friend that we had, so Fenric went to her side to assist her while Tatiana grappled Paula so the other woman could not shoot Suzie. While all of that was going on Miles and Iris had their own showdown. Miles turned out to be a creature like Iris in that his arm turned into a red molten looking sword, which he immediately swung at Iris. It cut through the wall of the train like it was tissue paper. After that swing he turned into a big metal shelled creature. Iris matched him with her own metal form and they fought. She attacked him with her scorpion tail and appeared to hit him. I did not know at the time if this had any effect on him or not, but in retrospect I think it was a poisonous sting.<br /> <br /> Amethyst decided that discretion was the better part of valor and fled the room. I didn\u2019t blame her. There was more shooting and missing from several people, which was getting dangerous. Caoimhe was shooting at Calpurnia because she was British and Calpurnia didn\u2019t get a chance to shoot back at Caoimhe before Lizette make her gun jump out of her hands and stay near the mechanic. Piedad shifted forms and attacked Abigail which just made Luciano upset and he told her to back off and interposed himself between the two. I have to give him credit for telling a were-creature in Gauru form to back down from anything they were doing, or for standing up to one for that matter. It takes guts to do that. After that I decided that Caoimhe was just going to make things worse so I grappled her and pulled her weapon from her hands before she could shoot at anyone else. Unfortunately for me I forgot what type of fae she was and she burst into flames, setting me on fire. I have had enough experience with bad burns in my life and I really had not wanted to reacquaint myself with the feeling. Unfortunately for me that was not among my choices at that moment. Luckily, after Caoimhe started to run off, I was able to put myself out. So I still sustained some bad burns, but not as bad as it could have been.<br /> <br /> Lizette, after finding out how ineffective guns were in the dining car, animated a chair to attack Miles, which it did with some amount of power behind it. The chair was destroyed, but it hurt Miles, which was the whole point. Miles for his part continued his attack on Iris. She managed to dodge and he cut through the wall again leaving a large gaping hole in the side of the train car. Caoimhe and Suzie made for the exit, Suzie grabbing the bag full of artifacts on the way. Then Laszlo attacked Miles, hurting the metal man pretty badly from what it looked like. Then Tatiana joined in the attack on Miles. He seemed to stagger for a moment after her strike but then he collapsed into a pile of scrap metal. After that Wolfram and I blocked the exit so Suzie and Abigail would not leave the dining car. Alla, who had just recently come into the car, joined us. Abigail decided that she really didn\u2019t want to get caught actually jumped off of the train through the big hole that Miles left. Fortunately for her the train was slowing down. Laszlo jumped after her to retrieve the would be criminal. Iris climbed out the hole and made her way onto the roof of the train and headed back toward the sleeping cars. Suzie for her part held out her hand like she was going to shoot another fire ball. The three of us, having had enough of fire for the day, stepped out of her way and let her escape. Luciano followed. In the end, he never found Suzie or Iris for that matter. He did find a young stowaway girl though. <br /> <br /> When the train had come to a stop Laszlo managed to catch back up to the train carrying an injured Abigail. She did not look happy to have been brought back, but she was hurt pretty badly and needed medical assistance. I believe that Luciano took custody of her after that. I\u2019m not positive on that since I headed back to our sleeping car. I needed to shift forms long enough to heal the burns that I\u2019d sustained from my interaction with Caoimhe. I am thankful for my ability to heal since I became what I am. Back in the war I was badly burned when an explosive went off right near me and my brother. I managed to shield Andel from the worst of it, but was burned on my back because of it. It was worth it though. My brother was hurt enough in the war he didn\u2019t need to deal with any more pain than he already had. I remember the burns taking a long time to completely heal. At that point in my life though I was not fully Uratha yet and had to heal normally. After I became Uratha however I discovered that I could heal rather quickly in my Guaru form. This has come in handy on more than one occasion.<br /> <br /> I believe that Luciano tried to take over the train but was told that since they were in Yugoslavia he had no authority. So, the train eventually made it to its destination and we switched trains so we could get to Zara. Izzy decided that Alla was interesting and decided to come along for the ride. I\u2019ll give the mage credit. She stays calm in the face of trouble. Almost the whole time the fight was going on in the dining car she was sitting there knitting. She paused in her craft a couple of times, but was knitting away when the fight finally ended. Makes me wonder what kinds of things she\u2019s seen.<br /> <br /> During the comparatively short trip to Zara I talked to Laszlo and found out that he is kind of exiled from Berlin. He said that he angered the wrong person and had to leave for his own safety. He did not elaborate on that, and that was fine. So, I asked if he would like to travel with us. He seemed interested when I described where we were going and accepted the offer. When we arrived at Zara we all got rooms at a decent hotel. Then we decided to do some sightseeing since we had the time. In our travels about town we found out that Iris is staying at a different hotel, and Piedad was lurking about as we walked. Tatiana noticed Piedad and asked if she wanted to go look for criminals together. The other Shifter seemed keen on doing that and the pair of them headed off.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I noticed that Laszlo was back to seeming scarier than he actually looks and figured that he needed to hunt to sate the Golem, so I suggested we look for quarry to teach. He seemed interested in that idea and the pair of us headed out into the city. We decided to look for the criminal element in the city and see if we could find someone that needed to learn a lesson. We ended up running into Tatiana and Piedad. They were also looking for criminals and found them in the same place we did. We had ended up at a warehouse on the docks, and it was inhabited at the time by pirates. We decided to show them the error of their ways. Piedad shifted into a big panther and attacked a pirate while Tatiana started her own fight. She really does love to fight. And she\u2019s good at it too. Tatiana harried people back towards Piedad and I worked on taking out those that were trying to escape. Laszlo intimidated the hell out of a couple of guys that he had cornered. That man can put the fear of God into people. It\u2019s impressive. <br /> <br /> After the fight Laszlo admitted that he had nowhere to go to the others and Tatiana offered him a place in the pack. Before this volchonok kept bouncing around pestering Tatiana until she finally asked Laszlo. Laszlo for his part seemed a bit surprised to be asked, but accepted the offer. I later took Tatiana aside and asked that she remember it\u2019s my responsibility to offer someone a place in the pack. I admitted that I was going to ask Laszlo myself so it all worked out, but to remember that for the future. She nodded her understanding and volchonok seemed to calm down somewhat. Tatiana then offered to teach Laszlo how to fight properly and he accepted. The man knows the basics of fighting, but should really learn to refine his talent if he is going to continue to hunt successfully. Tatiana is a good teacher to have. I will assist as needed, but will leave much of the training to my packmate. <br /> <br /> I do not know if it is fate or not, but strange and/or interesting things tend to happen around us. Not that I\u2019m complaining mind you. I prefer an active lifestyle to a sedentary one. On this trip alone we successfully investigated a murder on the Orient Express, discovered a plot to rearm dangerous groups in Germany in violation of treaties already in place, and fought a large metal monster in the dining car. I\u2019m not sure what it is about trains and those metal creatures we keep running into. Brandon was one and he was on the last train we traveled on. This time it was another unassuming man on yet another train. On the plus side, we also met new possible allies and added to our pack. Izzy is a mage who seems interested in following us where we\u2019re going, and Laszlo is a good addition to the pack. I look forward to future hunts with him. So far I\u2019d say that we\u2019ve had a pretty positive journey, and it\u2019s not even over yet. I suppose time will tell what else is to come on this trip. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it is very exciting that our pack has grown.<br /> <br /> He did fight very well, though his instincts could use honing.<br /> <br /> That is true, we will have plenty of time to train him.<br /> <br /> He may possibly wish to join us in hunts, though he hunts people who have done wrong, not spirits.<br /> <br /> Much like the cat, yes volchonok, it is why she and I ran into him and Marek.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok. Peidad will not join our pack. I do not think cats have packs.<br /> <br /> She also fought well against the pirates, yes. And against Abigail, though that hardly counts. She was scarcely fighting back.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it was a strange situation.<br /> <br /> Well, Abigail is a thief, so when the policeman came to arrest her, she kicked the table down.<br /> <br /> I do not know if Dacien has ever kicked a table at a policeman. I do not think he has been caught by one.<br /> <br /> After that, everyone pulled out guns and shot very poorly. Iris and the not-police man turned into robots and started fighting.<br /> <br /> I had already gone after Paula, foolish volchonok. She was threatening Suzi.<br /> <br /> No, she will not be pack. She disappeared after the fight, and is not following us like Peidad and Iris are. And she does not fight like pack.<br /> <br /> I thought if I held Paula, she would knock her out.<br /> <br /> You are right, volchonok, none of my pack did either. Next time, someone else will be the one holding, and I will be biting. This is clearly better.<br /> <br /> I am the best at biting. I took the robot down after all, the man robot.<br /> <br /> Bah, yes, he stayed standing a little. But if I had not hit him, he would not have fallen down so soon, eh?<br /> <br /> Is that not so, volchonok?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s right.<br /> <br /> I resume Laszlo jumped off the train to retrieve the thief. That is what he did, after all.<br /> <br /> She jumped off because Wolfram and Alla and Marek were guarding the door.<br /> <br /> Oh. I presume he brought her back because the policeman wanted her.<br /> <br /> The fire fairy? Oh, no, she is not a thief, just an exploder of buildings. She was just shooting at the Greek spy because the spy was British. Marek took her gun, but then had to let her go because she was on fire.<br /> <br /> It was not so important why she did it anyway, just more of the fire fairy\u2019s foolishness.<br /> <br /> Of course that is why I left it out when I told Connie. She didn\u2019t need to hear the unimportant parts.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I was very impressive in the important parts. Why?<br /> <br /> I spent the night in her den because I am amazing and she is beautiful, not because I left things out in the story.<br /> <br /> Do not push me, volchonok.<br /> <br /> That counts as pushing! I do not want to talk about the documents in that other language.<br /> <br /> Because Wolfram gave them to her, to protect the reputation of stupid, foolish Germans who want war. Now we will never know what they said and we have to trust the spy, who had to be bargained with to not help start some foolish war, that whatever it said will not hurt us.<br /> <br /> Bah! Nothing can hurt us. Even still... Bah. It is not important.<br /> <br /> That is true, it is much less important than running. But we have had our freedom for now. Soon, we will board the boat and finish Connie\u2019s business.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, then we will run.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 22nd July 1924<br /> <br /> Past couple days have been interesting. Yesterday we started off confronting Amethyst Trevelyan about the papers we had and the document she read. She was willing to let us have the papers, so long as it did not come to light (which was fine with us) so long as we told Calpurnia and we pressed her no further on the document we found in Zvezdana\u2019s bag. This went over poorly, but she was willing to otherwise sacrifice herself and leave our names out of it, so it served our purpose not to be associated with the paper\u2019s theft, and to ensure they never arrived. Tatiana especially was notably displeased, but I think several of us got the idea Amethyst had gotten the better of us.<br /> <br /> Calpurnia was easy to talk down. Laszlo, aping my court, used his fear powers on her anyway, but he has issues. Long as he does not go around doing it too much he should not be hard to deal with.<br /> <br /> That evening before dinner things went absolutely batty. Abigail Gerard was completing her deal with Suzie Zhang and Iris De Veers, when Lucciano Torrez attempted to arrest them. Paula Van Dijk sort of stood behind him to stare Suzie down. Abigail flipped the table and drew a gun, Lucciano took cover and drew a gun, and things got crazy. Caoimhe drew a gun on Calpurnia, Calpurnia drew a gun to defend herself, and I found myself really wishing my Thompson and my Chainsaw were not back in our car. I should have had the Starr with me. Though Wolfram pointed out no one who fired a gun actually seemed to hit. Suzie even missed with her flamethrower. Interesting.<br /> <br /> Tatiana grabbed Paula from behind, so Suzie changed targets to Lucciano. I was not sure what to do exactly; Paula is my friend and Tatiana is my friend and I was unsure Tatiana needed to be enacting violence on her. I did not want to turn on a member of my own team though. Then Miles Andersson turned into some sort of machine man with a molten sword, an Angel, and attacked Iris, who took her mechanical battle form. I caused Abigail\u2019s gun to malfunction. Marek also shifted into a hairier form and grabbed Caoimhe, who made herself into an inferno, lighting him on fire. Which was funny. He did disarm her though. Speaking of funny, I animated Calpurnia\u2019s gun to jump out of her hand and come to my side and fire at Miles, though it failed to hit anything.<br /> <br /> Izzy, for her part, paused her knitting and watched.<br /> <br /> Iris had struck Miles with her tail, and Miles attacks had carved a hole into the side of the train trying to hit her, which was beginning to slow. Paula passed out and Tatiana turned into a huge wolf, turning her attention to Miles. I animated a chair to sneak up on him and hit him. Meanwhile Peidad apparently gave up on deciding whom to fight and turned into a huge cat woman and attacked Abigail, slashing her across her abdomen. Caoimhe fled when Marek let go to put himself out, as did Calpurnia. Caoimhe nearly ran down Alla who had arrived in the process, which given Caoimhe was still on fire would have been unfortunate. <br /> <br /> Lucciano fired into the air and rather impressively demanded we stop in the name of the law. We didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Peidad\u2019s attacking Abigail caused Lucciano to change tactics, moving between the cat and the thief, demanding she stop attacking. Abigail and Suzy took this as time to escape. Wolfram (who had been firing at Miles this whole time, along with the pistol I animated) moved along with Alla and Marek to block Abigail\u2019s escape. Seeing this, she jumped through the hole Miles had made. Laszlo, who spent much of the fight wracked with indecision, went out after her. Making them numbers two and three to jump from a moving train this trip. Suzie charged at them with the bag of stolen goods Abigail was trying to sell, palm out where her Hellfire came from, but all three got out of her way. Lucciano pursued, and they got out of his way as well, reluctantly in Alla\u2019s case.<br /> <br /> With so many people eager to jump from the train, it seems like it would be better to just make a sort of catapult for launching people who want to get off, well, off. Also bombs at other trains! You could have train battles, lobbing huge explosives at each other. I mean it is not like I never made an explosive to blow up a train in my time. Blowing up trains is fun, especially if you are on it. But it could be even more fun, maybe, to blow up a train while on a train but not on the exploding train. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> During all this Miles succumbed to the attacks from Iris, myself, Laszlo and Tatiana and fell into pieces. Just before the table I animated could hit him. Iris also fled out the hole but climbed back onto the top of the train. Wolfram went to check on Christina and Regina who had fled when the fight started, but they were fine. Izzy resumed her knitting. Suzie escaped somewhere in there; Lucciano tried to commandeer the train, but he was an Italian lawman in Yugoslavia, so they did not acknowledge him. Suzie and Iris never turned up; apparently an urchin girl who had stowed away stole Iris\u2019s bags. Laszlo brought a defeated Abigail back to the train.<br /> <br /> I apologized to Paula. She understood why someone of my build might not want to challenge Tatiana. At least she used non lethal force. I appreciate that. No need to blow up the whole train. The train is Paula in this example. Anyway.<br /> <br /> The rest of the trip was\u2026subdued. In Karlovac, we changed trained to head to Zara. We sort of picked up Laszlo and Izzy. Izzy was coming along anyway, and Alla kept flirting with her. Tatiana was also flirting with Constancia a good deal on the trip there too. I cuddled with Wolfram, as Christina and Regina had been stayed to take the train to Budapest and hopefully a quieter train ride back to Chantilly. We could hear the tapping of Nicholette\u2019s typewriter all the way to Zara. <br /> <br /> In Zara we had two additional people. I was already rooming with Wolfram, but Tatiana roomed with Constancia (eagerly) to make room for Izzy. My night was wonderful. It was good to sleep so intimately close to Wolfram. Anyway, I think Marek let Laszlo crash with him. The next day a number of us wanted to explore Zara. We went as a group, except Tatiana who wanted to walk around alone and Izzy who was not into walking. And the vampires, of course. We saw that Iris had somehow made it to Zara staying in a different hotel. <br /> <br /> Laszlo still had a yen for punishing the guilty, so he and Marek went to do that after awhile, while Wolfram and I sat on the docks and chatted a bit. It was nice. Very relaxed compared to yesterday. When we got back together, it turned out Tatiana had also stumbled across Peidad, who followed us as we were interesting. She is going to Cyprus to now.<br /> <br /> Well the train was interesting enough. I wonder what will happen with the ship?<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <i><br /> End Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> I am going to be brief with comments, as Marek came in literally minutes before I had to get ready and head to the game so behind schedule. I write this as I prepare to head off again tonight.<br /> <br /> The reason everyone was missing with shooting was Iris got the highest Initiative and used the Embed Check Backdrop to cause everyone not taking turns to aim to miss. In the chaos, pretty much no one did.<br /> <br /> Miles attacked because Iris dropped a couple Exploits, and he picked up on the source. OOC-ly, Miles Andersson\u2019s job was to find the Golden Eagle and determine why the beacon no longer worked. Of course he got brat packed before that happened.<br /> <br /> The stowaway girl was Iris in another Cover, which she used to get her things off of the train. She was going to the same place as the PCs anyway, while Peidad just decided to follow as they were interesting and Izzy\u2026well Izzy said she was just tagging along but you know, Mages.<br /> <br /> Okay, out of time before I need to roll out again. I am happy to explain anything if folks have Comments or Questions though. Thanks for reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:49:29-07:00","id":1064503,"title":"","content":"Izzy is proving to be a hilarious addition. And props to the policeman for standing up to that mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T10:34:36-07:00","id":1064813,"title":"","content":"Luciano got an exceptional success to resist flipping out from the werewolves. He is kinda badass. And yeah, Izzy is fun<br /> Shame Alla's player does not journal...Her thoughts on the British empire and on Cyprus last session were hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:51:14-07:00","id":1064972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=1064813#post1064813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luciano got an exceptional success to resist flipping out from the werewolves. He is kinda badass. And yeah, Izzy is fun<br /> Shame Alla's player does not journal...Her thoughts on the British empire and on Cyprus last session were hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just love the reaction to personalities like hers and Terry's - even for supernatural creatures of the night, there is a certain kind/degree of crazy that even they aren't ready to take in stride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:58:53-07:00","id":1064977,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's fair.<br /> <br /> I have actually stopped the game from everyone laughing at one of Izzy's rants. I guess supernatural powers don't make you immune to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T12:31:34-07:00","id":1071369,"title":"","content":"There was a mystery to solve on the train. Espianage and spy vs. spy. But now we are on the open sea.<br /> <br /> Pirate Battle? Pirate Battle!<br /> <i><br /> Session L</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 21 July 1924<br /> <br /> We parted company with Christina, who continued on the train to Vienna. The rest of us got on a boat headed for Cyprus. Specifically, Nicosia. Piedad and Iris continued to follow us, though Iris pointed out that she was just headed for Cyprus and wasn\u2019t necessarily following. Piedad was. And as it turns out the boat ride was just as \u201cinteresting\u201d if not more so than the train ride to Zara. It started out with an Italian military vessel following us for a short while. Iris, who can \u201chear\u201d radio waves, said that the Italian vessel was offering us protection from Ottoman pirates, for a fee of course. The captain of our ship declined the offer and the military vessel moved off. Some people thought that the offer of protection for a fee was suspect, so the idea that we would then run into pirates backed by the Italians was brought up.<br /> <br /> Later in the evening an unnatural fog rolled in. Fearing trouble Tatiana asked Alla to speak to Izzy about getting rid of the fog if she could. Turns out that she could, and a strong breeze came up and moved a good bit of the fog away. The fog moving revealed an Ottoman pirate ship off our starboard side. They were closing with us and transmitting to our captain over the radio. Iris did not specifically tell us what was being said. She simply asked if we were ready for trouble. When we assured her that we were, she said okay and apparently transmitted her own message to the pirates. They did not like what she had to say and continued heading our way.<br /> <br /> Tatiana and I could see the deck of the other ship from where we were and realized that among the number of pirates on deck were two Pure werewolves. It appeared that the pirates on deck had rifles and the ship was armed with several cannons. Their intentions were clear so Lizette took the initiative and had one of the cannons flip around and fire at the deck of their own ship. I think it left them appropriately scared. After that Tatiana and Alla jumped from our vessel to theirs. Tatiana was carrying Wolfram and Alla took Laszlo. I probably could have jumped across and met them in hand to hand combat, but decided that I just wanted to shoot them. So, I collected my rifle and took out one of the pirates that looked like he was giving orders. Always take out the command structure first. <br /> <br /> I was able to see the deck of the pirate ship clearly thanks to Wolfram\u2019s powers. He had enabled a gift that made his body glow really bright. Lizette then made a second cannon shoot at the pirate ship\u2019s deck. There was a lot of shouting in Italian on the Ottoman ship, which confirmed ideas that the pirates were connected to the Italian military ship we had already passed. <br /> <br /> After taking out an officer I decided to change targets and start shooting at the Pure. I wounded one. Laszlo then hit that same man with one of the cannons from the deck. That man is strong! The Pure then turned around and hit Laszlo in turn. Around that time Wolfram got hit by some gift that looked an awful lot like something I\u2019ve seen Autumn Courtiers doing. So, we figured out that there was an invisible Autumn Courtier hiding out on the ship dishing out injury. I think one of the rifleman shot Laszlo, but it didn\u2019t seem to do him much in the way of harm. It looks like our newest packmate can shrug off some injuries as well as wield cannon as weapons. I think he is a good man to have on our side.<br /> <br /> Alla kept up the attack on one of the Pure while Lizette threw a grenade in the midst of the riflemen. That in and of itself is a good reason to not bunch up together during a fight. Especially if you are fighting Lizette. Wolfram then set one of the Pure on fire with his pyre flame gift. He didn\u2019t seem to pay much attention to the fire though because he then went on to attack Tatiana. The proof of how badly hurt he was came up the next moment when I put a bullet into that Pure werewolf and brought him down. Laszlo, still wielding the cannon, then renewed his efforts against the remaining Pure and managed to kill him with his last swing. <br /> <br /> Lizette switched tactics after the riflemen spread out and started shooting at them with her Tommy gun. I managed to spot a Claimed on the other boat, briefly, before he turned into a wave of water. Same trick that Greta can do. But briefly is all I needed and I shot him. He had to use his gifts to shrug off the injury and smoke started pouring out of him. After that several riflemen started firing at me and I had to pay attention to getting out of the path of their bullets before I could renew my attacks on the Claimed. Unfortunately, that brief respite is all the Claimed needed to turn into a wave and knock Wolfram, Laszlo and Tatiana into the water, as well as himself. Laszlo could not swim, but Wolfram was good enough to swim over to our new packmate and help him stay afloat. <br /> <br /> While that was going on Alla managed to find, in a general way, where the invisible Changeling was. I think she tracked the other person by the scent of blood or their heartbeat. Whichever method she used worked. I believe that she managed to hit the Changeling at least once before she turned her sights on the rifleman that was firing at Lizette. I think she also noticed the grenade that Lizette was about to throw near the Changeling\u2019s position. So, Lizette threw her explosive and definitively hit the invisible person, as the blood and viscera will attest to. As my packmates were doing their best to thin the ranks of pirates I was doing my best to help them in the endeavor. I took out another rifleman before I turned my attention to our friends in the water. I lowered a lifeboat to my packmates and raised it back up so they could continue the fight on our vessel. Several of the riflemen again tried to shoot me but missed or their guns jammed. I assumed that the guns jamming was Lizette\u2019s handiwork. As it turns out, while all the fighting was going on the Claimed man had summoned skeletons to crawl up onto the deck of our ship. Tatiana then managed to grab the Claimed in a hold and tried to intimidate the man into calling off his skeletons. She succeeded in scaring him. He turned into water again and fled without doing what was requested of him.<br /> <br /> The skeletons managed to climb onto the deck about the time that I got the lifeboat back on board. Wolfram and Laszlo climbed on board while Tatiana simply jumped into the fray. Lizette for her part changed tactics and grabbed her chainsaw, attacked a skeleton and easily brought it down. At this point Lizette was pretty badly hurt. The riflemen that had been plaguing me had also been taking shots at my slight packmate, but they managed to hit her. I think part of it was due to the fact that I am able to move sooner than she is and have a better chance at avoiding the shots.<br /> <br /> The men with the jammed rifles switched to pistols and continued to try and kill us. Wolfram used his gifts to take one out in short order. While he was focusing on the men, Piedad and Tatiana were focusing on the skeletons and doing a good job of it. I killed the remaining pistolman on the pirate ship with a well-placed shot just as Laszlo was taking out the last skeleton on our ship. Tatiana then grabbed a rope, tied it off and jumped back over to the pirate vessel. It had drifted closer during all the fighting. The rest of us used the rope to get over to the pirate ship and we started searching for anything interesting. And interesting is what we found. We managed to come across some documents, written in Italian, that Iris said were rather incriminating to some parts of the Italian military. It turns out that the four supernatural individuals hired some ex-Italian Navy men and decided to go pirating in the waters off Cyprus. After some discussion, we agreed to turn the documents over to the British consulate on Cyprus and let them deal with the fall out. If we turned them over to the Italian government, it is likely that some well-meaning individual would try and address the issue but then get shut down by someone higher up in the command structure. Turning the documents over to a neutral party may work better to get the corruption in the Italian military dealt with. After we finished searching the pirate ship we secured it to our own and started to tow it to shore.<br /> <br /> Following the altercation with the pirate ship several things happened. Wolfram used what gifts he could to heal Lizette, who was badly hurt from the gunfire. Laszlo, who was also hurt pretty bad, managed to heal on his own it seems. At least he was no longer as badly wounded in the few minutes that passed after the fight. Once we were sure that he was okay Tatiana and I gave Laszlo the first of his lessons in hand to hand fighting. Laszlo already had a pretty good grasp of the basics, but I think he made some definite improvement in the course of our lessons on the deck. I will admit that fighting him in hand to hand can be a little disconcerting at first. Laszlo is not a very big man physically, but he seems to be much more of a threat than his physical form would indicate. The feeling of threat doesn\u2019t match with what your eyes see, so it can be a bit off putting until you get used to it. Once you get used to it though it is easier to focus on the fight itself. Laszlo used that sense of threat to his advantage in the beginning of the lesson. He is well aware of how he is perceived, which is a good thing. He can use that to good effect in an actual fight, and he\u2019ll be better able to defend himself physically after we\u2019re done with him. <br /> <br /> Our next stop is the city of Nicosia on Cyprus. I suppose we\u2019ll see if the island has any more adventures for us to tackle. Either way it will be interesting, I have not been to Cyprus before. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Be quiet volchonok, I am trying to sleep.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that the sun is out.<br /> <br /> Because I have been awake all night for three nights! Besides, the sun is warm and comfortable with the sea spray, and there is not much to do on a boat.<br /> <br /> I am sure the old pirate ship is much less comfortable.<br /> <br /> That is true, I could curl up in a more comfortable way in Urshul form and safely, on the other boat. But it is covered in blood and stinks of the Pure.<br /> <br /> \u201cReminding me of a good fight\u201d does not help me sleep, volchonok.<br /> <br /> It was a good fight though, was it not?<br /> <br /> I am sorry I left you behind on our boat, but jumping over to theirs was the only way to fight properly.<br /> <br /> I know Marek and Lizette did not, but I am not Marek or Lizette, to be also to shoot across boats, or make the pirates own cannons fire on them.<br /> <br /> Alla and I could only care so many, and it is good we took Laszlo and Wolfram. I do not think Alla could have taken the second werewolf on her own, and I fight better one on one.<br /> <br /> That was her fighting the invisible one, foolish volchonok. I imagine she could smell the blood as well, once Lizette\u2019s grenade injured them.<br /> <br /> Yes, well, Sin-Eaters cheat. He was like Greta, this enemy Sin-Eater, with the wave crashing and the disappearing into water. And yet, in the water, I still grabbed him and frightened him into fleeing.<br /> <br /> Do you do this just to anger me, volchonok? Is it because you think I am too sleepy to fight you? It is true, he did not do as I told him and get rid of the zombies. It is not as if they were hard to tear apart, anyway.<br /> <br /> The riflemen hurt Lizette, not the zombies. Wolfram made them bleed from everywhere for that.<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> I did not hit the Pure with a cannon, foolish volchonok, because my teeth are better. And because I am not a giant like Laszlo.<br /> <br /> He was already drowning, it is good he dropped the cannon, or Wolfram could not have dragged him to the boat.<br /> <br /> He did fight well, our newest pack member. And he will fight better - he will be here soon for a lesson in fighting, now that you have ruined my nap.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, that means we cannot go for a run. Also, we are on a boat. We will land soon, and finish this business of Connie\u2019s. Then we will run. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b>Pirates of the Mediterranean</b><br /> <br /> Nicholette DuBois entered the cabin where Lizette \u00c9toile was working. Wolfram had gone on deck since the Gremlin was, well, a Gremlin and as much as he loved her he knew sometimes it was a little safer to have a wall or two between them. Nicholette, however, was curious to see the Wizened work. <br /> <br /> Lizette was adjusting her chainsaw and cleaning it. She wore functional pants and her bra as she sat at her small desk disassembling the chainsaw with small quick hands. She still had bandages from the two rifle shots she had taken, and visible on her chest. The writer let her eyes wander to the solid biceps just visible under her firm green skin. She was a distracted by the taut muscle till Lizette spoke.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is good you remained below decks with Connie and Izzie, hein? It was dangerous up there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd who all\u2026what all\u2026did you fight up there?\u201d Nicholette tilted her head a bit.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell as you know, as we all know because Iris knows Italian, some elements of the navy wanted protection money. She had a radio\u2026somewhere she used to eavesdrop. The Navel ship tried a protection trick, so when we blew them off a pirate ship showed. It was an old Ottoman ship like the British and Italians captured at the end of the war. Fortunately the weapons were mid-last century. Rather nasty cadre of people on there though\u2026Two Werewolves, a Changeling and a Sin-Eater. And a bunch of men with rifles and zombies.\u201d Lizette spoke as she worked. <br /> <br /> \u201cOf what sort? Like Tatiana or Marek? Like you or Dearbh\u00e1il?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe werewolves\u2026,\u201d she untwisted a tight screw, \u201cwere Predator Kings, a tribe of Pure, the unfriendly werewolves, we had not run into. As opposed to the comparatively friendly werewolves who are called Forsaken, like Tatiana or Marek. I don\u2019t really know anything about the Predator Kings otherwise. As for the Changeling\u2026,\u201d she paused to squint into the chainsaw, \u201cNo clue, he or she was invisible, and by the time the second grenade landed there was not enough to really identify. Autumn Court like me, though, based on the Contracts they were using.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what did you do?\u201d She watched the bicep flex as Liz lifted the chainsaw.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell I turned the cannons of the ship on the ship itself. That was fun. Unfortunately they unloaded two. Tossed a couple grenades over there that really created some mayhem\u2026took out the Lost over there. And used the Thompson a bit when the ship finally got close enough. It\u2019s better than their nineteenth century rifles, but they had a lot of rifleman.\u201d Lizette winced slightly and carefully put it down.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026what about the undead?\u201d Nicholette pointed to a stain on the saw.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, them. They came up as they were summoned by a Sin-Eater and scaled the side of the craft. The chainsaw took care of them.\u201d The Gremlin paused. \u201cIt is almost as if the chainsaw it was made to kill the undead.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh. Well what about the werewolves, Tatiana and Marek? They were fighting too?\u201d Nicholette paused as she watched the Inventor. Tatiana and Marek were both attractive people too. Maybe she should hang around their rooms too\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, Tatiana jumped across carrying Wolfram. She made a charge for the Werewolves, and did very well. She helped Wolfram with one, Laszlo with the other. Then she fought the Sin-Eater. Marek was on my boat, I had a harder time following what he was doing, but he was clearly sniping enemies on the other side. I am sure he was shooting werewolves then their rifleman. Then probably the Sin-Eater. Hard to say, it was a man pointing a gun, hein?\u201d The Gremlin shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo less heroic I am sure.\u201d Nicholette dark eyes sparkled. She could not see Lizette roll her brilliant yellow ones. She turned slightly back to the writer. \u201cNot charging into two werewolves head on heroic, but I would not imply Marek is not heroic, I suppose. \u201c She picked up her rag and wiped her hands. \u201cNow Wolfram was, he was also fighting a Werewolf despite not being one, as well as hexing the rifleman shooting and me and pulling Laszlo out of the water when he needed help. He got knocked in by the Sin-Eater too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow was he doing that?\u201d She leaned on the doorframe.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, turned into a wave? We have seen Greta Hess do it. Sin-Eaters they have strange powers.\u201d Lizette rose and carried the chainsaw to her bag. \u201cTatiana grappled him, but then he vanished to a different part of the water, which Greta has also done. Anyway\u2026Alla mostly fought the other fae and humans, and Laszlo charged into the werewolves with Tatiana and Wolfram. Anything else you want to know?\u201d The Gremlin pulled a shirt on.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, Lazlo. He hadn\u2019t seem to notice me. Didn\u2019t seem to be the \u2018ignore the help\u2019 sort of person.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette shrugged and sat on the bed. \u201cYou are not really his type. And he gets kinda fixated. I would not take it too personally. I doubt he is putting on airs. At least I presume. Went to his head fast if so.\u201d She grins.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe not. Just some ignore me, others don\u2019t. You, Christina, and Wolfram don\u2019t, for instance. Fenric is enthusiastic and Tatiana is nice. On the other hand, Dacian and Dearbh\u00e1il tried to avoid having me near them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Wizened shrugged again. \u201cI don\u2019t know what they are thinking. But I do know I am taking a nap for a bit. Be sure you are ready, we will arrive in Kyrenia before sunrise, and it\u2019s not even nightfall yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nicholette smiled, \u201cSweet dreams Liz. Dream of mayhem.\u201d And she stepped out into the hallway. Watching the Gremlin, she nearly bumped into Isobel as she stepped out. The Mage harrumphed. <br /> <br /> \u201cYou two were not eating anyone in there were you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo\u2026No?\u201d The writer looked surprised.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh probably a piece of cheese. Nonetheless, I have my eye on you.\u201d The Obrimos gave her a sharp look. She then suddenly changed to a smile and chuckled merrily as she continued on her way.<br /> <br /> Nicholette shook her head. \u201cThat woman has been in a confined space too long.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session L</i><br /> <br /> Lizette did not affect any of the rifleman\u2019s weapons. Marek could dodge bullets, and had a good enough Defense several had chance dies to hit him, and that lead to some Dramatic Failures. For her part the rifle seems Lizette\u2019s natural enemy, she once again took heavy damage from them. Her defense is very very high, and I am using the Hack where Fae can boost defense against a single attack by their Wyrd for one glamour per attack, but she cannot dodge bullets, and while the Wyrd thing helped she was still hit a couple times. Wolfram spent most of the rest of his Plasm healing her with Mending the Mortal Coil.<br /> <br /> We had to determine rules for picking up a Cannon and beating people with it. That was fun.<br /> <br /> The Pure were Predator Kings, the Sin-Eater was a Bonepicker Prey and the Changeling was an Autumn Court Wizened.<br /> <br /> There were, apparently, some who used sized ships from the Ottoman Empire near the end of the war for piracy. There were accusations against the Italians for doing so opportunistically, but more individuals than all the way to the top. It seemed a good place for a side combat to blow off some steam. <br /> <br /> Winding up next couple session, probably. See you then! Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:08:02-07:00","id":1071470,"title":"","content":"Considering all the different supernaturals you were listing on the pirate ship, I was starting to think you were setting up a rival team/nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T02:22:02-07:00","id":1078809,"title":"","content":"Vent0: Heh, Not a bad idea, but nah. This time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It\u2019s the end of the line. The group is in Cyprus, now it\u2019s time for an auction, and an old familiar face.<br /> <i><br /> Session LI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 22 July 1924<br /> <br /> We arrived in Nicosia without incident. There was interesting conversation on the bus ride to the hotel, but nothing bad or out of the ordinary happened. Izzy and Alla were discussing my Kindred pack mate\u2019s feeding preferences. Then somehow the conversation turned to whether or not it would work, as an emergency measure, to turn Alla into a bottle or some other object. I think the idea was to protect Alla from the sun should the need arise. None of us were sure if that would work and Alla did not seem keen on trying it out. I don\u2019t blame her.<br /> <br /> The hotel was very nicely appointed. I suppose I should not be surprised by now. After we arrived we met up with Connie and Agrippa to discuss the auction tomorrow. They wanted to know if we had any interest in bidding with her on some of the artifacts. It seemed like just about everyone was okay with that plan of action. Interestingly it seems that Iris also came to this auction to bid on the same artifacts that Agrippa and Connie are interested in. <br /> <br /> Later this evening Tatiana and Alla went out looking for a gambling establishment. I think Alla was looking to feed. Tatiana was going along for the fun, and possibly to start a fight. This is Tatiana after all. Anyway, the two went out looking for a gambling place and ended up running into Piedad. The werecat joined my pack mates and they all went in search of their desired destination. They ended up finding one and went in to enjoy themselves. As could be predicted a fight broke out. I think someone tried to pick Tatiana\u2019s pocket and Alla spotted it. A fight ensued. Tatiana enjoyed herself, as did Alla and Piedad. The latter apparently ducked under a table and came out the other side as a large cat. Not subtle at all, but it worked at sowing chaos. Alla also took the opportunity to feed from the pickpocket. Again, not the most subtle activities those three could have come up with, but they seemed to have fun and they did not get caught. That was the important thing.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 23 July 1924<br /> <br /> We went for a preview look at the artifacts that Agrippa wanted to bid on. And as it turns out they are very similar to the ones that we saw before in Paris. The cultural influences were different, but they seemed to have the same kind of mechanical workings that the other ones did. So, they are related somehow, we just don\u2019t know the details. I could tell that the others interests were peaked, as was mine. Those artifacts were made by the same people that built the Eagle. Their devices can do amazing things. We just happened, or Jamal just happened, to know how to make the Eagle work. We don\u2019t know what the purpose of the other artifacts is or was. The only thing we know for sure is that they can harness a great deal of power and release it if prodded in the right way. We met with Dana, who happened to be at the auction for the same reason we were, after the viewing and she shared our opinions that the artifacts were of a similar make to the others, but had different regional influences.<br /> <br /> After we talked to Dana we got a message from Nicolette that Iris wanted to talk to us. So the group of us went over to speak to her. She, as noted before, was also interested in the artifacts. She flat out told us that she wanted to work with us to acquire the objects. She wants to use the artifacts to see how they were made and possibly find a way to fight the \u201cCustodians\u201d, as she calls them. The metallic/mechanical creatures that we fought on both trains call themselves the Custodians of the world. Apparently they try and influence events in the way that they think they should go. They wanted us to find the Eagle before, or at least make sure we were strong enough to take it for ourselves. I\u2019m not sure what their purpose on the Orient Express was. The custodian, in human guise, tried to get into our cars on the train, that much is known. We just don\u2019t know what his purpose was. He wasn\u2019t the most talkative guy. Iris said that she is on the side of free will, of allowing mortals to do as we will. Nice sentiment. Not sure if she doesn\u2019t actually have a hidden agenda, but nice sentiment nonetheless. <br /> <br /> Like I said, Iris told us that she wanted to get her hands on the artifacts so that she can figure out how they work and what they do in an effort to fight the Custodians. She also said that working with the artifacts would be dangerous because it would attract the attention of said Custodians. She said that she would need to do a little work, move to another safe location and continue the work, and so on. She implied that it would not be safe for us to keep them at our residence because the Custodians could find our place and attack us there. She wanted to take the artifacts with her. We said that we would talk to the others about her plan and get back to her.<br /> <br /> After Alla woke up, shortly before the auction, the whole pack discussed Iris\u2019s idea. To say that not everyone liked the idea was an understatement. We came up with a few ideas on what to do with the artifacts. One idea was to get the artifacts for ourselves and betray Agrippa and Connie in the process because we would keep them. Another idea was that we could get Connie\u2019s approval of our plan to get the artifacts for ourselves. This would only alienate Agrippa, and leave Connie on our side. It was brought up that Alla could talk to Connie about things and see if she\u2019d be willing to go against her sire. The last option was that we acquire the artifacts like planned, with Agrippa, and just plan to keep them at our residence. Agrippa could look at them as she pleased, but we would keep them safe at our house. Then later down the line, if and when Agrippa\u2019s interest in the artifacts waned, we could give them to Iris to look at herself. <br /> <br /> We decided on the later idea in the end and went to talk to Iris about it before the auction started. She seemed disappointed but understood. We had already made arrangements to bid with Agrippa and if we betray her now we are making an enemy out of an elder vampire. That would not be wise on our parts in any wise. While some of us were talking to Iris, Alla went to go talk to Izzy. The British mage was also here to bid on the items in question. I think Alla got her to agree not to bid against us on the specific artifacts that we were looking at. It doesn\u2019t seem that Izzy was all that invested in them anyway. Which worked out well for us.<br /> <br /> At the auction this evening Iris started out bidding aggressively against Agrippa, but eventually gave way to the elder Kindred\u2019s final bid. There were not any other really serious contenders for the artifacts. So, in the end we won. We managed to talk Agrippa into letting us house the artifacts and she can come and look at them at her leisure. All around I think things turned out pretty well. We managed to get the artifacts. We can talk to the people that are studying them to see if they discover anything interesting, and no strange weather phenomenon happened while we were in Cyprus. All in all a good day. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> We are going a boat again, yes.<br /> <br /> Oh hush volchonok. It is taking us home this time. <br /> <br /> Yes, we have finished our business, despite the foolishness.<br /> <br /> For some reason we did not think the artifacts Agrippa got all of us to come help her get would be powerful enough to be dangerous for her to have. We had to wait until we saw them, and Iris told us so to think this.<br /> <br /> It is true, volchonok, and good that at least they did not want to betray Constancia.<br /> <br /> Because Iris said pretty words. I do not know.<br /> <br /> Oh no, we decided not to, because if we just do what we said we were going to, Agrippa will get bored of them, so then maybe we can let Iris look at them, to help her fight the robots.<br /> <br /> The ones like she fought on the train and like the one we fought on the train, back when we got the Golden Eagle. They like trains, it seems.<br /> <br /> Well, volchonok, she says so, that she will use them to fight robots.<br /> <br /> I would rather Izzy had the statues, because that would be the most interesting. But it was Connie who asked for our help to retrieve them for Agrippa, so...<br /> <br /> We did have fun that first night on the island, it is true.<br /> <br /> It was not my fault! He picked my pocket. I am sure that means he deserved getting thrown into a table by Piedad and drunk from by Alla.<br /> <br /> Well, I couldn\u2019t just let the others try to hit Piedad because she helped me get my wallet back.<br /> <br /> That is true, volchonok, not many were able to hit her even when they tried, not after she turned into a big cat.<br /> <br /> Which one? The tall one, or the one with the companions?<br /> <br /> Oh. He looked at me funny.<br /> <br /> We were there because Alla wanted to hunt at an illegal gambling den.<br /> <br /> I do not ask questions such as why to most of our packmates, except when they wish to put Connie in danger. It just sounded like more fun than waiting until I was tired and falling asleep. Or helping Lizette and Wolfram put bombs in their room.<br /> <br /> That we will, volchonok, that we will. Once we get off this boat we will have much fun. Perhaps we will even get our new packmate to run with us. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Morning After</b><br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not really fair, is it? We only get another day together?\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette \u00c9toile looked out the window to the streets of Cyprus. Their hotel room was extravagant, but that just made it more fragile and dreamlike that she was even here with her love. The sun had dawned, and people were going to work. The Gremlin had barely slept.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe use the time we have.\u201d Dana Barlowe had not gotten up yet. Looking at her small green lover as she wistfully looked out the window. \u201cIt\u2019s our day to make of what we wish. If you want to spend most of it in here, fine, but I insist on going out for meals.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette\u2019s face broke out into a genuine smile. \u201cI suppose you have talked me into it. Been here long enough to have an idea of where the best food is?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana let out a chuckle. \u201cNot really. Only arrived from Lebanon. Your French authorities are very interested in the site outside Tyre by the way. \u201c A smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, were you followed?\u201d Lizette looked out the window a bit more searchingly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot far, and I am accustomed to losing pursuers.\u201d Dana lay on her stomach and turned to look away from the smaller woman. \u201cI notice you have been with a man since we last met.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette turned to her sharply. \u201cMa foi! You are not getting jealous too, are you? I thought our rules precluded concerns about such.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana\u2019s gaze turned back. \u201cNo no, it\u2019s fair. Maybe a little, but I shouldn\u2019t be. Wolfram, I am guessing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, Oui. He and Christina are, as a couple, my lovers. \u201c Yellow eyes fall back on Dana. \u201cThey and you, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d She smiled at the Wizened. \u201cThey and you and the bairn, must have their hands full.\u201d Dana watched the girl closely. Lizette nodded, then raised her chin.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you know Iris was coming? It\u2019s interesting we run into both of you at once again.\u201d The green woman hopped down from the window.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, and had I known I would have either not come or not arrived openly. Well, unless I knew you were coming, in which case I would have anyway.\u201d The Immortal gave a charming smile to the Gremlin. \u201cMore convenient to examine the artifacts here, but I could have in Tyre. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cShe made a plea to have us work with her over Agrippa, citing the \u2018custodian\u2019 we fought on the train.\u201d The Gremlin walked over and sat on the bed. \u201cTalked about their grand plans and manipulations, and how she fights them. All a plea to get her the artifacts, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana smiled wickedly. \u201cOf course.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWere the things she was saying true though? I mean, about the custodians thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, probably. We discussed some before. I just wonder what ancient culture built it all, set it into motion. Because it is all spiraling out of control.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLaszlo said he did not detect anything from her, and he apparently usually does.\u201d She reached over and took the Eternal\u2019s hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd how does Laszlo do that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is a Begotten, some kind of fear creature.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana laughed. \u201cOh one of those. Your life is about to get more interesting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette gave a fairly worried look. \u201cI am not sure how I should feel about that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAt risk of ruining my mystique by giving a straight answer, Begotten are defined by two things. One, they think they understand how the world works, becoming confused and angry when their mythology falls flat, and two they are hungry all the time and have to punish which gets\u2026exciting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh I see. I have noted the hunger at least, though he is fairly easygoing.\u201d The Wizened paused to think. \u201cDo you think we did the right thing, sticking with Agrippa unless or until we let Iris have the artifacts?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana looked thoughtfully at her lover. \u201cI am not sure there was a right thing there. I mean Agrippa is an elder vampire. You don\u2019t anger them unless you have a good reason, and keeping Iris\u2019s control at arm\u2019s reach is good. On the other hand, Agrippa is an elder vampire, so you are handing a weapon to an ancient parasite. And Iris does not double-cross without some reason in her mind. Unfortunately, she is the most paranoid person I have ever met, and I know a lot of vampires.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lizette nodded. \u201cSo are we going to try the Greek place?\u201d Dana nodded, and she moved to pick up her shirt.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh that girl traveling with you, the au pair. Nicolette. Where did you find her?\u201d Dana cocked her head.<br /> <br /> The Gremlin turned around.\u201d Oh, she showed up at the house a few weeks ago. Oddest thing. She knew all about us, knew about our work. She wants to travel around with us, get ideas for her book. Hauls her typewriter everywhere and won\u2019t let anyone touch it. Seems to be doing no harm. Good au pair, though Dearbh\u00e1il and Dacian were kind of rude to her. You have seen her, haven\u2019t you?\u201d Yellow eyes locked on Dana.<br /> <br /> She shrugged it off. \u201cYes, in traveling around the Levant, I have noticed her in the shadow of greatness several times. Such a pretty girl is hard to miss, and such a pretty girl traveling with luminaries and carrying a typewriter is even more visible. Just be careful, I think she has some history with Iris.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, Iris seduced her on the Orient Express.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana nodded. \u201cWell, watch her just in case then. But I am sure having an au pair has been and will continue to be useful. And she at least knows how to survive in less than hospitable climbs. I have seen her in the Valley of the Kings even.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe trip on the Express it was interesting. There was even a murder on the Orient Express. Sort of. I shall explain.\u201d Lizette smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cA murder on the Orient Express? How novel. I look forward to it. Your trips always seem interesting.\u201d Dana\u2019s smile back was charming.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are! We even fought pirates on the boat on the way here!\u201d Lizette winked. <br /> <br /> Dana kept smiling, shaking her head. \u201cI definitely need to hear all about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you sure you can\u2019t come with us, love? Back to the chateau?\u201d Lizette let slip a pleading look.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry love. I ducked out of business in Baghdad in order to look into the Tyre find. I need to get back and continue my work, after this and a meeting Damascus with some artifact hunters. I promise I will come visit you within the next year, when I am done in Mesopotamia, so don\u2019t worry.\u201d Her smile was encouraging.<br /> <br /> The Gremlin did pause, turning to glance at Dana a moment before pulling her trousers on. \u201cOh, how did you know I have been with a man?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana bit her lip, gazing at her lover several moments debating before a shrug and rolling onto her back and murmuring. <br /> <br /> \u201cOh, nothing\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><br /> End Session LI</i><br /> <br /> Not much else to share. The raid on the gambling hall was totally the players doing. It was funny. I will miss Peidad, and Izzy. They will show up again, I am sure.<br /> <br /> One year later, it is August of 1925, and the group finds themselves once again (or for the first time, in Laszlo\u2019s case, traveling to Vienna. Join us then, in just two weeks for us. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:42:44-07:00","id":1079053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-chronicles-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play?p=1078809#post1078809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cOh, how did you know I have been with a man?\u201d<br /> <br /> Dana bit her lip, gazing at her lover several moments debating before a shrug and rolling onto her back and murmuring. <br /> <br /> \u201cOh, nothing\u2026\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Duh duh dunnnn!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:29:27-07:00","id":1079080,"title":"","content":"Someone may have read that closer than most of the group, I see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T12:55:34-07:00","id":1085111,"title":"","content":"August 1925. The Jazz age rolls on, as does the lives of our cast. The Charleston is the rage, The Roaring 20s roar. Let\u2019s check in.<br /> <br /> Only Lizette covers any downtime. Bit of a doozy for her.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 13 August 1925<br /> <br /> The pack was invited to dinner at the Bellarose residence today, so we all met up there. It was interesting to see Liselle and Clara after so much time. They have not changed much. Liselle is still as curious as ever. The dinner itself went well. Our hosts were kind enough to have raw meat for the Uratha guests, which was appreciated. They are friends with Marie after all, so they probably take into account dietary restrictions for her frequently. During dinner Tatiana regaled the group with tales of her exploits working as a mercenary the past year or so. Liselle was obviously interested in my pack mates\u2019 adventures, while her sister\u2019s eyes just seemed to get bigger and bigger as the story went on. I\u2019m not sure if she disapproved or was just shocked. She did not say anything afterwards. <br /> <br /> There was also talk about movies, silent verses \u201ctalkies,\u201d and stage theater. Alla was more than happy to discuss her work on an upcoming film that involves dinosaurs. I think. Liselle got very interested in that and happily debated the whole sound issue with anyone that would talk to her about it. Some people like silent films with the words on cards and music played over the action. Others liked the idea of movies where you could hear the actors and actresses speak. Someone argued that \u201ctalkies\u201d would expand the audience of movies since those that are illiterate can still enjoy the medium. I didn\u2019t have much of an opinion either way. I don\u2019t make it out to the theater very much at all. I haven\u2019t been to the movies with my pack mates or my family. My family lives in a small down, so there are no theaters near them. Nor would they be able to afford to go. I send them money regularly, but can\u2019t send too much without it looking suspect. To them I am just a courier after all.<br /> <br /> After the frivolous talk of movies and theater was over a more serious matter was brought up. Apparently a friend of Liselle\u2019s, Martinique Duchumps, has disappeared. She is a ballet dancer that moved to Vienna. Liselle lost contact with her friend and has become worried about her. She called the police and pretended to be Martinique\u2019s mother in order to get them to at least knock on her door. They did so and no one answered. So, Liselle asked us if we could look into this matter for her. Liselle wasn\u2019t sure if Martinique got caught up in something political or not. Her boyfriend is a Communist, who is apparently rather vocal in his beliefs. Liselle kept calling him a \u201cred ragger.\u201d <br /> <br /> Marie, who had also been invited to this dinner, was interested in looking for Martinique as well. The only problem for her was that she would need to request time off work to go traveling. I believe that Wolfram took care of that matter though. He talked to Marie\u2019s boss at the hat shop and explained that a friend of hers has gone missing, and it would be inappropriate for us to look for the missing girl without having someone who knows her along for the ride. Marie is that person. He eventually agreed and gave Marie some time off.<br /> <br /> Things will only get more interesting after we get to Vienna. From what I\u2019ve heard things have gotten rather tense in the city due to Fascist and Communist disagreements. There is also a World Zionist Congress coming to the city in the near future, to discuss the homeland of the Jewish people. It was explained to me that some Jews believe that they should create a Jewish homeland in which to live, while others do not want to give up their national identity over their religion. Then there are some people in Vienna that don\u2019t want Jews there at all. I do not understand the sentiment. Why does it matter how or why people worship God? There is no right or wrong way to do it, they\u2019re just different. I suppose it boils down to people being afraid of what is different and then doing stupid things in their fear. Fear never fails to make people do foolish things. In some cases fear can be good. During war fear can make you more cautious and keep you alive, but there is such thing as too much fear. Too much fear can make you act in foolish ways or make it so you don\u2019t act at all. Neither are good. So, I\u2019m assuming that it is fear that making some people in Vienna want the Jews to leave.<br /> <br /> Before we leave for Vienna I thought it would be prudent to check with some of my contacts and see if there was anything going on in Vienna that I needed to be aware of. I didn\u2019t learn of anything directly related to the issues we\u2019d discussed, but did find out that the infamous thief Gerard sent the police in the city a letter saying that we would steal a priceless work of art on the night of the 18th of August. I suppose this would lead to a larger police presence in the city. That may or may not work to our advantage.<br /> <br /> The last thing that we need to do before we go to Vienna is call Gunter, Christina\u2019s brother, and see if he minds if we stay at his estate just outside the city. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 17 August 1925<br /> <br /> Getting into Vienna was an adventure by itself. The roads were packed with people coming in to go to the Convention or the protest, so Lizette had to get creative in driving into the city. She ended up cutting people off, driving on the sidewalk and generally ignoring any and all driving laws or practices. But we ended up relatively safely at Martinique\u2019s apartment in the Bohemian district. We found the door to the apartment locked, so Fenric let us in with his lockpick and a little skill. Once inside we found the place rather messy. It looked like someone had searched the apartment without any thought of covering up their actions. There might have been signs of a struggle, but to be honest it was hard to see anything definite, at least in the main room. In the bedroom I found a small blood stain on the floor near the bed, and the bed looked like someone had been pulled out of it. The linens just didn\u2019t look like they do when a person gets out of bed themselves. Our theory is that Martinique was pulled out of her own bed and possibly injured in the struggle. It was not a bad injury, if the blood was in fact from that incident. <br /> <br /> We found the scents of several people in the apartment. One man had been in the living room and the bedroom, presumably the boyfriend. Two other men have been through the entire place. Our assumption is those trails belong to the kidnappers. Other women have been in the apartment but not the bedroom, and one of them was a werewolf. Wolfram also used his gifts to determine that there was what he called a \u201cdeath stain\u201d in the apartment but that it predated when Martinique lived there. We\u2019re guessing that a previous occupant died there.<br /> <br /> Things of note that we found:<br /> <br /> Jewelry and cash were not taken. This was not a robbery. Whoever broke in was looking for something specific, but unfortunately this is no way to find out exactly what they found, if anything.<br /> <br /> Martinique had a habit of going to the same theater every Saturday night. There are ticket stubs in a drawer. There is also a ticket stub for an orchestral performance that was fairly recent.<br /> <br /> There are two different brands of cigarettes in the drawer. Presumably one for her and one for Christopher.<br /> <br /> There is an address on a slip of paper in the drawer. <br /> <br /> There is food still in her refrigerator, so she was not planning on going anywhere for any extended time frame.<br /> <br /> After the mundane investigation of the apartment was done we moved on to more mystical means to find answers. Lizette \u201cread\u201d the front door to see what the last thing that it \u201csaw\u201d was. Turns out that the last person that left here was Christopher. He apparently came looking for Martinique, didn\u2019t find her, and left, locking the door behind him. She read something else and came up with the information that two men had entered the apartment. At least one of them was wearing black and red, Royalist colors, and an armband with the Royal insignia on it. After that Wolfram used his own gifts to \u201cread\u201d the door and was able to get several pieces of information:<br /> <br /> Martinique was carried out of the apartment by the same man that tossed her apartment.<br /> <br /> She was abducted about one and a half weeks ago at night.<br /> <br /> Christopher was the last person at the apartment, and that was about a week ago.<br /> <br /> We got physical descriptions of the two women that have visited the apartment in the past.<br /> <br /> We decided to split up at that point. Tatiana was going to talk to the Communists. Laszlo and I were going to talk to the werewolves, while Wolfram and Lizette checked out the theaters and any ballet companies.<br /> <br /> So the two of us went to the caf\u00e9 that serves as a meeting place for the Uratha in town. On our way there though we noticed a few interesting things. First, there were people, all wearing black shirts sitting at the caf\u00e9 across the street. It is possible that they are Royalists. Another interesting thing was that we saw Zvezdana watching the caf\u00e9 that we were heading towards. She spotted us at the same time that I spotted her and she started moving away. I was tempted to follow her but decided against it at that moment. Given how our lives work I figured that we\u2019d run into her again at some point while we were in town. When we got to our destination we found the Krieger was not there so we left a message for him that we needed to talk. We also discovered while we were there that the werewolf that had been at Martinique\u2019s apartment had also been at the caf\u00e9 recently, within three to four days. This was a good sign as it said that the woman is likely not Pure. If she is, she has a lot of guts.<br /> <br /> While we were out I checked with an acquaintance of mine to see if anything interesting was going on in town besides the obvious. He said that there was a group of saboteurs in town called the Black Swan. They are apparently a group of women that operate sometimes in Austria and Yugoslavia. I\u2019m not sure what it means yet but the information was interesting. It will be interesting to see what they have planned, if anything, in town. I thanked Stutter for the information and we went on our way. Stutter is obviously not his name. I don\u2019t know it. He is a friend of Hans\u2019. Hans introduced him to me sometime back as a good informant in town. The man feigns a stutter when he talks to the police or in the presence of anyone that he doesn\u2019t know personally. I\u2019ve heard that the police have pretty much given up trying to get information out of him because it takes so long for Stutter to finish one sentence, not to mention a detailed account of something. With me though he speaks normally, for which I am grateful. His feigned stutter is a rather good, if somewhat annoying, tactic.<br /> <br /> Tatiana went out in search of Christopher. She looked at a bar that is known to host Communists as the majority of the clientele. The man was not there but does frequent the establishment. Tatiana left a message for him, asking him to give her a call. She gave the name of one of the hotels in town for him to contact her at. She also managed to find out that Martinique was in a ballet troupe called the White Swans. Interesting considering the presence of the Black Swans in town. Then after she left the bar, she went to the hotel that she named and reserved a room. She did not want Christopher, who is a Communist and supporter of the people, to call the number of Gunter\u2019s estate and talk to a servant. It would not look very good for us and may lower his opinion of us considerably. A good idea all around.<br /> <br /> While the rest of us were trying to get information on Christopher or mystery werewolves, Wolfram, Fenric and Lizette went to the theater that Martinique had frequented so much in the past. They found the place locked, so they let themselves in. In their search of the place they found papers written in Cyrillic but not Russian. The last time we found papers in non-Russian Cyrillic we had problems finding someone to translate it. Perhaps we will have better luck here.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we will be making our den here.<br /> <br /> The others will be well able to defend our territory here in Vienna, especially with Lizette\u2019s large guns. But I don\u2019t think Christina\u2019s brother would appreciate you calling his home our territory.<br /> <br /> It is true, he did agree we could have our Hedge connected to it. I did not say it wasn\u2019t part of our territory.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it will be harder for you to mark our territory if we spend the visit here. You are welcome to ride back with the others.<br /> <br /> I know, Lizette drives like a madwoman in this traffic. I am just saying, you don\u2019t have to stay here.<br /> <br /> Bah. The others will probably fuss and fret and say someone must stay with me. And even if I am alone, I will still be fine. The Pure do not come here without cause.<br /> <br /> I must be here because Christopher would probably not talk to us if he thought we were aristo.<br /> <br /> Christopher is... were you paying attention at all, volchonok? Marie\u2019s friend is missing. Christopher is her mate.<br /> <br /> Yes, the communist.<br /> <br /> Eh. Marie likes him. Being a communist makes him foolish, not useless. It is not as if he is one of the ones in charge, with their broken promises and self-serving lies.<br /> <br /> I do not know why he left town, volchonok. We will ask when he returns. Possibly he went for allies. Possibly he was blackmailed into leaving by the fascists.<br /> <br /> The ones who have his mate, of course.<br /> <br /> Wolfram was showed the one who did it by the door, and he was dressed as the bartender said these fascists are.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there will be a fight. I will talk to the others first, probably, and see if they found anything.<br /> <br /> Marek and Laszlo went to speak to Krieger, to see if he knows of the missing girl\u2019s werewolf friend. Wolfram, Lizette and Fenric went to visit the theatre she went to often. I believe they will be looking for the White Swan ballet company when they are back with Alla.<br /> <br /> Because that is the company the other communist said she danced for.<br /> <br /> It will be some time before they are back, with all the traffic. The riots were getting worse and tomorrow is the day that thief has said he will steal something, so it is unlikely that the traffic is better.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, it is not time to run. It is time to look for information. We will find her soon, then we will run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 17th August 1925<br /> <br /> So a lot has gone on since I last wrote. I think it was the Murder Mystery on the train when I last did. Life gets in the way. And life finds a way. I got PWP. <br /> <br /> Since my last entry I have become a Mother. <br /> <br /> Am\u00e9lie \u00c9toile was born April 30th, 1925. She\u2019s two and a half months. She is a healthy and inquisitive girl, like her mom. I hope she will be taller. I will admit it was a surprise\u2026the Kind are not known for anything approaching a high birthrate\u2026it\u2019s unusual. And we were not even sure The Eagle would allow a pregnancy to proceed. That data point is covered. I need to get around to telling Jamal Ruhadze, though any experimenting is right out. She can see my ears though, she wants to touch them all the time. Anything else remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> I of course do not know for certain who is the father. There are, of course, theories. Wolfram is my lover, but I could have been with another man, or a Faerie woman with Contract of Mirrors. It\u2019s a big mystery. This did not stop Christina from going downright arctic at the news. Maybe because I told her I did not think I could get pregnant. She slowly warmed though, and when I had a girl and there was no chance I bore Wolfram\u2019s Eldest Son, she is almost back to how she was. Wolfram will always be the greatest tension between us, I think. <br /> <br /> Nicolette has been invaluable. And strange, but mostly invaluable. She takes good care of Am\u00e9lie, and Regina is eager to too, though we are careful to never claim they are sisters. Strangely Nicolette privately claims (after I put the question off with contempt) Wolfram cannot be Am\u00e9lie\u2019s father, as she and I were sleeping together at the time Am\u00e9lie was conceived so it must have been something that happened while I was out. This is entirely untrue. I have never shared a bed with Nicolette (yet, she is a charming girl who puts herself in a position to be easily seduced, and not just by me. I know Wolfram hasn\u2019t been with her, but I wonder about Marek or Tatiana.) , I was sleeping with Wolfram at the time, though he was not the only person I slept with, it\u2019s just Nicolette was not one, and I had no unfortunate encounters. <br /> <br /> Still, people come to conclusions. I suspect Wolfram will never again be on Mademoiselle Th\u00e9i\u00e8re\u2019s Christmas list.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been\u2026an adjustment, and I was in a wheelchair for awhile. (note to self: If you have more kids be sure to build the ultimate wheelchair before you\u2026WAIT NO ROCKET CHAIR before you get immobile. With machine guns. Mayhem!) But I am Lizette and SCIENCE FINDS A WAY! <br /> <br /> Dana did visit, as promised, in June, stayed about a month. She promised to see me again before Christmas. She has a couple children herself, and noted she should \u201cat least visit them.\u201d While in private I got the longest lecture of family planning I have ever heard, and she left\u2026gifts\u2026of that nature. I was troubled by her note that if I settled down to an easy career of child rearing she would end our relationship. Not because she disapproves exactly, but because she says we would have nothing in common. I noted we both had daughters, but she said if there was one thing she was massively unqualified to speak as, it was a good mother. And she said she respects a woman\u2019s decision to focus on raising her family, and she can be friends with women like that and would be with me, but that is not the sort of woman she is interested in being intimate with. So there is that, I guess. Does not matter, I am a modern woman. I will find balance. And good staff. Good staff helps a lot.<br /> <br /> So the other night the Bellerose sisters Clara and Liselle invited us to dinner. Clara looked very pretty. We had a lovely evening, and Alla spurred some animated talk about movies. Clara wanted Talkies, because she liked songs in movies. Liselle was fascinated by the idea of dinosaurs in movies, hearing Alla discussing The Lost World. So it became songs vs. dinosaurs somehow, with the possible song while being eaten by dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> But then we discussed Martinique DuChamps. Martinique is a ballet dancer, friend of Liselle\u2019s, though nearer Clara\u2019s age. She had a boyfriend, Christopher Harg, a \u201cRed Ragger\u201d as Liselle kept saying. But the Bellerose\u2019s are well to do, so she would. Says the little green lady who has servants taking care of her baby in a big house. Anyway, He had gone to Vienna, and she had gone to be with him, but stopped writing. Liselle impersonated her mother on the phone to get the police to check, but they apparently just knocked on the door. Could we go and look in on her? Of course.<br /> <br /> There was some question if she and Christopher lived together. Clara was certain not, and Liselle believed so. You would hardly believe Clara was the one going to Sapphic salons, but I am uncertain she fully grasps everything going on. Then again, she pointedly never brings Liselle, even as she is coming of age. It was suggested (I forget by which Bellerose, or maybe it was Tatiana) that this could be a good and (possibly) safe hunt for Marie to try out. Tatiana talked to her while Wolfram spoke to her boss, and he agreed she could come. Not that we should have to get his permission.<br /> <br /> We went home and I gave the passenger plane the once-over and we headed out the day after the next, after I spent the last full day with Am\u00e9lie after checking the plane. We arrived in Vienna on the 17th. The same day the World Zionist Congress opened, as it turned out. <br /> <br /> We settled in at Gunter Esterh\u00e1zy\u2019s Estate, though he was not there. I set everyone up with mounted machine guns for their room. Safety first! Laszlo was not enthusiastic. We were not there long before we set out for town to look in on Martinique. Alla stayed behind since the sun was out and we needed the lay of the land.<br /> <br /> I wonder how Am\u00e9lie is doing? I should call.<br /> <br /> Okay she is fine, where was I?<br /> <br /> Ah, driving was really fun. Vienna is full of people with the Zionist Congress and every Fascist and Monarchist for miles around coming to protest. I went up sidewalks, over ramps, and zig zagged into and out of traffic. I wish I had my little green car from Paris, it is much more heavily modified and has the Vickers. It was still easy to lose the police in the city. I should ask Gunter if I can modify one of his cars. Sidewalk driving is easier than they say, people always get out of the way.<br /> <br /> Though really, let\u2019s not kid ourselves here. A flying car would be ideal. The question is rockets on the back or bottom. Or why not both. Rocket up, then out. And Vickers on the top, because of course Vickers on the top why wouldn\u2019t you? And something to drop bombs on the bottom. Like a plane. That is a car. Or something. You know, I am starting to feel like I am reinventing the wheel here. Maybe I should be improving planes instead. Combining cars and planes. Yes. Perhaps by the 21st century, they will consider differentiating cars and planes to be silly and foolish. <br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, we arrived at her apartment. Fenric picked the lock. The apartment had been ransacked, searched. Wolfram found a death stain, but it preceded Martinique. The Werewolves found several scents, including a female werewolf, but only Martinique and two men, one of whom was almost certainly Christopher the other was almost certainly a kidnapper, went into the back rooms. They both got some familiarity with the scents. I spoke to the door and figured out Christopher (almost certainly) had arrived and gotten in the door, but it was after Martinique was taken. I also got a description of the kidnapper (almost certainly) who was from a monarchist organization of some kind from a drawer. We found tickets to a theater, and one to an orchestral performance. But the theater had been a regular visit. Also, napkin from a caf\u00e9 nearby.<br /> <br /> We split up. Wolfram, Fenric and I went to check the theater. Tatiana and Marie went to check the caf\u00e9 we found the napkin from. Laszlo and Marek went to check with Krieger and the werewolves. Wolfram and I found the theater, but it was closed and empty, but not abandoned. Wolfram used his powers to search it some but needed light, but he managed to turn the lights on and unlock the door. Once it was unlocked Fenric and I carried him inside. He found some papers in Cyrillic, but it turned out not in Russian. Fenric looked at them but could not read them. There was a side office the papers were in, not the main. <br /> <br /> Marek checked in with the bar the Werewolves would be at, but they were not there. He left a message for Krieger to call us. The female Werewolf who had been in Martinique\u2019s house had been there, which was a good sign. Tatiana went to the caf\u00e9, and found some communists there. Christopher was less radical in the sort of Leninist murdery sense, but was all about redistribution of wealth. She also found Martinique worked at a ballet company called The White Swan. Christopher had been in Belgrade and would be returning any day now. Tatiana was cunning enough to know not to leave a number for Christopher at a bourgeoisie house servants might answer at, so got a room at a nearby hotel. <br /> <br /> We met back, and Marek noted he knew of a group who conducted sabotage and occasional Mayhem in the area called the Black Swan, rumored to be mostly or all women. And that seems to be finally giving us a piece to connect other pieces with. But the sun will soon set, so we (Tatiana aside) went to get Alla before we going further. It\u2019s time to set back out for Vienna, and I am ready to drive.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Wait, let me call and check in on Am\u00e9lie one more time first\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LII</i><br /> <br /> First, reminders:<br /> <br /> Clara Bellerose first appeared in the first Paris story, where she tried to (literally) pick Lizette up at the theater, and Lizette speaks of her a lot. In the last story, she and her sister Liselle were sheltering the Werewolf Marie who had fled the clinic where she had had an abortion, killing the doctors. The group, (mostly) bonded with the Sisters Bellerose. Neither is supernatural, though at this point Liselle is not a Ceremonial Magician probably because of Dacian\u2019s interference. Zvezdana is the Dancer/Romancer Fairest Spring Courtier from the train last story, who fled. Krieger was the (hot) Forsaken resistance leader in Vienna from the Vienna story. Think that is everyone.<br /> <br /> Wolfram used Industrial Oracle and Lizette Contracts of Animation to gather clues. And the Werewolves of course used their noses. Werewolves have a huge effect on any mystery scenario, let me tell you. They have stood out as much or more for their senses as anything else.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t\u2026think\u2026anything else is opaque, but if it is Comments and Questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:50:31-07:00","id":1085229,"title":"","content":"Ha! I knew it (it being that Lizette was pregnant as of the last post).<br /> <br /> I'm just wondering what complications will arise here - I doubt a simple abduction will last long against the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T13:16:42-07:00","id":1085863,"title":"","content":"Good on ya. ^_^<br /> <br /> As for Complications, they certainly came up last session. Suddenly there is more going on, and more they know they don't know. More old faces show up, from Maximilian and Lizbet to Amethyst and Krieger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:06:10-07:00","id":1091676,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s check back with the group in Vienna. They are looking for their swan even still.<br /> <br /> No Lizette this time, but she should be back next. Enjoy the Werewolves perspective.<br /> <i><br /> Session LIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 17 August 1925<br /> <br /> As it turns out the documents that Wolfram and the others found are written in Serbian. I could make out what language it was, but was unable to read it myself. We will need to find someone in town, that we trust, to read them for us. I am curious to see what they say. <br /> <br /> After we had all met up we decided to go talk to the White Swan dance troupe and see if they know where Martinique is. Getting there was a hassle though. The crowds were rather thick due to the convention and protests in town, so we ended up having to shoulder our way through the people to get to the theater. Once there we met up with the White Swan dancers. They said that Martinique had called them about a week ago to let them know that someone had tried to take her and that she was going to hide. She did not tell them specifically where she was going to go though. The dancers were convinced that the Fascists had something to do with Martinique\u2019s attempted kidnapping. They suggested that we talk to Christopher and said that he might know more. They gave us the name of a caf\u00e9 that he frequents. I believe this was the same caf\u00e9 that Tatiana went to earlier and left a message for the wayward Communist.<br /> <br /> It was obvious that while they were answering our questions they were holding something back, so Alla used one of her gifts to persuade one of the dancers to be more forthcoming. I think she made it so the dancer would see her as a close friend or confidant, so she would speak more freely. And it worked. The dancer that had been doing most of the talking, Lea, said that Martinique may be in Sarajevo. She wasn\u2019t positive, but thought that was a possibility. She also said that our wayward dancer had stayed with Amethyst while she was in town. I suppose that I should not be surprised that Amethyst was in town. She is well traveled. It was interesting that our missing dancer would have stayed with the spy though. It made me think that there was more to Martinique than meets the eye. We found out later that I was right.<br /> <br /> While we were questioning dancers, Tatiana was waiting at the hotel just in case Christopher or Krieger got in contact with her. As it turns out Krieger sent one of his people, a woman named Emma, to talk to Tatiana. Emma, from her scent, is the werewolf that had been in Martinique\u2019s apartment. She revealed that Martinique was definitely associated with the White Swan, and may be linked to the Black Swan as well. She also said that the White Swan dance troupe was associated with a Communist group called the Comintern. It was suggested that the Fascists had something to do with Martinique\u2019s disappearance since the young dancer is so heavily involved in Communist matters. So, my pack mate decided that she wanted to see if she could find out any information from the local Fascists. To that end Tatiana and Emma went to a bar where they found members of that group. They started a fight with the Fascists but made sure to leave one of them conscious so he could be questioned later. They brought the remaining man to Martinique\u2019s apartment and interrogated him about the dancer\u2019s disappearance. He told them that it sounded like an Italian Fascist named Ludovico may have taken Martinique. He tends to go after prominent Communists, and if she was associated with someone that stood out she may have been targeted by him. The ladies were warned that Ludovico\u2019s men are all heavily armed with guns. After they got what information they could out of the man they let him go. Then Emma and Tatiana talked things over. Emma also believed that Ludovico may be connected to a local Invictus vampire. She thought that he may have blood bound humans that work for him.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the rest of us found the club that Amethyst was singing at. She was up on stage when we walked in. She acknowledged us with a nod and eventually made her way over to us after her song was done. When we told her that we wanted to ask her about Martinique she ushered us backstage near the dressing rooms so we could talk in private. When asked, she confirmed that some of the White Swan dancers are a part of the Black Swan group. Apparently, they have been busy. They have helped to take down governments, and had run afoul of an Italian Count. The Black Swan were involved in the assassination of a local politician in Italy, which drew the Count\u2019s ire. This Count was the same Italian Fascist that Tatiana and Emma found out some information on. It seems that the Black Swan had gone to the Count\u2019s property and rescued several girls who\u2019d been given to the Count. They sabotaged several vehicles on their way out and fled with the girls. So, it seems that Martinique was kidnapped by the Count\u2019s men, but she managed to get away from him and went into hiding. According to Amethyst the dancer laid down several false trails before disappearing. <br /> <br /> Tatiana showed up at the club while we were talking to Amethyst and she was shown to the backstage area where we were. We all caught up on what was going on. Due to the possible involvement of the Kindred in Martinique\u2019s disappearance we weren\u2019t sure what had actually happened. We weren\u2019t sure if the dancer had actually escaped and went into hiding, or if she had been \u201cinfluenced\u201d by a Kindred\u2019s gifts and set out to do what she was told to do. After discussing things for a while longer we then decided to split up again to find out more information. Tatiana and Emma were going to talk to Krieger while the rest of us went to talk to Maximillian, Alla\u2019s Kindred friend. He is something of an information broker and we figured if anyone knew who in the Vampire community Ludovico was connected to it would be him.<br /> <br /> We met Maximillian above a very fancy restaurant in a VIP room. He verified that Ludovico has ties to the Invictus, but suggested that we not talk to the man\u2019s Kindred allies/keepers. His reasoning was that if we made it known that we were looking for Ludovico and then at a later date he showed up dead, they would come to us first with questions and accusations. So, we agreed to not tell anyone that we were looking for the Count. Maximillian also suggested that if we did anything to the Count that we should make it look like he got caught up in the violence surrounding the Fascists and Communists. He is involved in all of that after all. It\u2019s not a stretch to think that he may get in over his head and become a casualty of the fighting.<br /> <br /> Maximillian said that he would look into Ludovico\u2019s whereabouts but wanted a favor in return. Of course. He asked that Alla talk to Lisbette, the Eupraxius, and lend her a hand. He did want us to tell her that he had sent us. I\u2019m assuming that is so she knows that she owes him a favor as well as us. So, we went to go talk to the young Kindred. It turns out that she had a rather mundane problem that she needed help with. She was trying to set up a salon in five days, but things kept falling through. She was partially convinced that someone in town was sabotaging her efforts to put together her first salon. To say that Alla was interested in helping the younger vampire was an understatement. She got very excited about the idea of helping with a salon and started brainstorming on the spot. She came up with the idea of bringing in entertainers from outside of Vienna and using a space that Lisbette already owns to host it. I think they decided on doing a haunted house kind of theme and inviting ghosts that we know to \u201chaunt\u201d the salon for the evening. It was all very elaborate, but Alla seemed to be enjoying herself immensely.<br /> <br /> While we were planning a party Tatiana and Emma went to go find Krieger. Emma led them to the basement of a boarded-up library. Krieger was down there working on something. They filled him in on what we were looking into and what we\u2019d found out. He agreed that Ludovico would be a problem, but talked the ladies out of doing any sort of recon at his warehouse. If they were spotted by anyone then it would alert Ludovico that we were looking into his affairs. If they killed the guards that spotted them, then Ludovico would just know that someone was looking into his business but not necessarily who it was. In either case he may choose to pack up his operation and leave Vienna for now. We need him to stay put. It is likely that he has kidnapped other women that will need to be freed. <br /> <br /> Krieger also said that there was an Uratha in the Black Swan. She is a Hungarian woman that does not live in Vienna. He was not sure if this woman was in town or not.<br /> <br /> Also of interest to Krieger was Gerard, the thief that announced that he would be stealing something tomorrow night. Krieger said that Gerard specifically contacted the Pure and told them that he would be stealing something of theirs. Krieger was interested in contacting this thief and planning with him on what he was going to steal from the Pure. He asked Tatiana if any of us knew Gerard. She said that she did not know who he was but that I had mentioned him to the group when we got to town.<br /> <br /> When we all met back up again at the hotel we traded news. I said that I could take a look at Ludovico\u2019s property. I am good at getting in and out of places unseen, so figured I would be the best person to do some recon. We also discussed that when we do go after Ludovico that we cannot leave any evidence that it was us that was there. We could either get in and get out with any possible captives and leave the place standing, or we could get anyone out that needed freeing and burn the place to the ground before we left. Fire would cover up any physical evidence that might get left behind. And we could leave some clues to make it look like the Communists made their displeasure with him known.<br /> <br /> Once we had finished discussing things we, minus Tatiana who stayed at the hotel, went back to the estate and found a surprise waiting for us in the form of a book. Apparently, a veiled woman, who from the description was actually Amethyst, came by while we were out and dropped it off for us. The book she gave us was a copy of T.S Elliot\u2019s \u201cThe Wasteland.\u201d She left a note that said it might come in handy in the future. The thought that occurred to me, and I believe the others, was that she had an identical copy of the book and could therefore leave us coded messages with the book being the key. I\u2019m not certain that is what she left the book for, but she is a spy so it makes sense. I guess we\u2019ll see what the future brings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> What now volchonok? It is nearly dawn and we have been gathering information all night.<br /> <br /> Of course I knew that Emma intended on fighting through the sentries. Why do you think I volunteered to go with her?<br /> <br /> I knew because she is a reasonable werewolf, when you get around all the flirting. To be fair, if she wasn\u2019t Uratha...<br /> <br /> Bah. Yes, volchonok, she is Uratha, so yes, volchonok, I will not be thinking these things. She can still be a friend. And it will be good to have a local ally working with us.<br /> <br /> Pshaw. There is no need to be the best at sneaking when you just kill anyone who finds you. <br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not going now. For one, I already told you I am tired. For two, I am not foolish enough to go alone into the fortress of the enemy. For three, I do not wish to make Krieger\u2019s life more difficult. <br /> <br /> It will make it difficult to go after this count. Yet again, Lizette\u2019s wish to explode everything may provide the answer however. It is difficult to tell that a werewolf killed your minion if your minion has exploded into little pieces.<br /> <br /> No, we are not worried about the Italians coming after us. But this Italian count is allied with the vampires, and Krieger does not want to have to worry about the vampires as well as the Pure.<br /> <br /> Thieves? Oh no, he is not worried about thieves. He is thinking this thief might be an ally, since he specifically told the Pure he would be stealing from them.<br /> <br /> It is confusing, volchonok, because it is stupid human politics. But the thief has nothing to do with the kidnapping. The count had Martinique kidnapped because she and her Black Swan comrades killed a different Italian. <br /> <br /> She is also in White Swan as well, but that is not a politics thing, it is a dancing thing.<br /> <br /> It was Amethyst who told the others of Black Swan and the killing thing. The fascist only told us that the man who kidnapped her probably worked for this count.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it was fun encouraging the fascist to talk. It is amazing how much people are willing to tell you when their feet do not reach the ground.<br /> <br /> I doubt the others got the fat vampire\u2019s help by lifting him up off the ground. Not even Marek is that strong. Perhaps Laszlo...<br /> <br /> No, he did it because of favors trading, probably. That is the vampire way.<br /> <br /> Helping the young foolish vampire with a party, it seems. Alla was very excited.<br /> <br /> Oh, volchonok, I don\u2019t try to understand our packmates, especially about vampire things. I do not know why we care whose he is, if we are not going to ask them to care him to heel. They probably have a reason. I prefer fighting him anyway.<br /> <br /> Yes, she has escaped.<br /> <br /> We will fight him because he may have kidnapped others. Also, she might not have truly escaped, but rather was let out with because she was mind controlled.<br /> <br /> Yes, Emma said they do those things. Alla can do things much like that.<br /> <br /> Probably Alla can fix it, if Martinique was mind controlled. Or perhaps killing the one mind controlling her would fix it.<br /> <br /> Next? Sleep. Tomorrow we will try to find Gerard, decide how to attack the count and see if Martinique or her mate respond to the messages we left. Oh, and probably do party things.<br /> <br /> No, we will not be running. There is far too much to do already. Perhaps later. For now, I sleep.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, familiar faces\u2026Lizbet is the Daeva Invictus of the Eupraxus Bloodline who originally had Constancia and other Circle of the Crone members working for her. Maximillian Nostras is an Invictus Ventrue of the Macellarius they dealt with previously as well, killing is errant childe. Amethyst Trevelyan is of course the Silent Sin-Eater who died on the Orient Express last story. I think that covers everything.<br /> <br /> Emma is a Storm Lord. Came up in session but not journals.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, but if anything is unclear comments and questions are welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T02:00:29-07:00","id":1097463,"title":"","content":"The group meets a new contact, and learns more of the players in the area, including possibly making contact with Martinique. But can they trust this mystery woman? Can they trust Martinique? When one is neither Fascist nor Communist, they may find themselves walking a fine line.<br /> <br /> Alla\u2019s Player had to miss as she was under the weather.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts<br /> </b><br /> 18 August 1925<br /> <br /> So today had an interesting start. A messenger dropped off a coded letter from Amethyst. At least it had references to page numbers in the book that she gave us, so we\u2019re assuming it\u2019s from her. Wolfram figured out the code and we read the message. According to the spy there is a German singer named Magdalena Von Ackerman that knows where Odile is. Since Odile is a reference to Swan Lake, we\u2019re assuming that is referring to Martinique. It was also mentioned in the note that Magdalena has been tied to a number of powerful people over the years and is aging<i> really</i> well. Possibly supernaturally so. Not that it makes any difference. If she has information that can help us, and she doesn\u2019t betray us, that\u2019s all that really matters. The rest is just academic curiosity. <br /> <br /> After we translated the message we decided our course of action for the day. Tatiana, Marie and I were going to do some recon around Ludovico\u2019s warehouse while Laszlo, Lizette and Wolfram went to talk to Magdalena. Tatiana thought that Emma might be interested in the warehouse so she called Krieger\u2019s associate and arranged for her to meet us at the hotel. When Tatiana called, Emma was in the process of watching tensions rise between the Communists and Fascists. Apparently both groups are now armed and violence may break out soon. Though apparently scouting out Ludovico\u2019s warehouse seemed to pique her interest and she headed over to meet us. When we were all together we transformed into wolves and ran along the rooftops to get to our destination. It was quicker and more discreet than running through the streets.<br /> <br /> On our way to Ludovico\u2019s warehouse we came across an interesting scene. There were some Hungarian Fascists guarding a warehouse near the docks and they were watching a group of Russian Communists unload crates and move them into their own facility. To me it looked like the Russians were moving framed artwork. The Hungarians for their part were trying to talk themselves into messing with the Russians, so Tatiana took action. She started helping the Russians unload their truck and generally showed off how strong she was to deter the Hungarians from doing anything. I stood back and watched just in case the Fascists tried anything. Plus, it was amusing to watch Tatiana intimidate the Hungarians from across the way.<br /> <br /> Tatiana talked to the Russians about Ludovico and they warned her that he was a dangerous man and apparently treats women badly. Though they were not so much concerned for Tatiana since she can obviously take care of herself. They also told her about something that may be going down at a bar called Dockside later this evening. It seems that there is going to be a fight later, and the Russians thought that Tatiana might be interested in getting involved. As it turns out we may be trying to work that into our plans for later, so it is fortuitous that we got that information. <br /> <br /> When we finally got to Ludovico\u2019s warehouse we discovered several interesting things. It appeared that there was an old man sitting out by the front door with a rifle across his knees. It looked like something from the war. There were also two children playing with a dog and the old man was watching them. In reality the old man wasn\u2019t really old. He just appeared that way. His scent was way off for an older man. He could be wearing make-up or using some sort of gift to appear older than he is. The children and dog were all spirits donning guises to fool any who wandered past. To the casual observer the warehouse is guarded by an old grandfather who is distracted by watching the kids. In truth, the warehouse is pretty well guarded from the outside.<br /> <br /> We kept walking past Ludovico\u2019s warehouse and made our way behind our target location so we could scout the place out. We discussed our plans. Emma was all for attacking the warehouse and made it look like she was planning just that with Tatiana in Russian. Marie doesn\u2019t speak Russian so she was under the impression that Emma was going to have her lead the assault on the building. Marie for her part was getting more and more nervous, so I took pity on her and told her that Emma was just messing with her, and that we were not actually going to be attacking in that moment. It did come up that the warehouse was very likely a trap. Marie questioned the wisdom of attacking the building if we knew they were expecting us. We countered that it was best to spring the trap if we know it\u2019s there. The question did come up what would we do if the guards had silver weapons. I offhandedly mentioned that if that was the case I would just take them out from a distance with my rifle. Emma thought that this was funny. She asked why I would use a gun and I explained that it was a hobby. I was not going to get into my alternate identity and profession with her. I don\u2019t know her that well, and Reznick is not someone that just anyone gets to know about or meet. From that point on Emma referred to Marie and I as the soft ones. I was not especially happy with this appellation, but I am well aware of my capabilities when it comes to violence. Those that meet me in combat would not call me soft.<br /> <br /> Given the supernatural nature of protection the warehouse has, as well as someone on the roof, we decided to get the rest of the pack involved with the raid. They at least have spirits on their side. There\u2019s no way of knowing what else they have at their disposal, at least the group we had at the time couldn\u2019t find anything more out. So, we went back to the hotel and played snooker for a while. Emma continued to tease Marie, this time with the cue, making innuendos and implying that she was a virgin. This continued until Lizette called to let us know what they\u2019d been up to. Eventually Marie claimed a headache and retreated upstairs. <br /> <br /> So, the other group got as close to the hotel that Magdalena was staying at as they could with the car and then made the rest of the trip on foot. En route they came across a minor inconvenience. A group of men stepped in Laszlo\u2019s way and proceeded to try and intimidate him into leaving the city. Apparently, they have something against Jews. Laszlo for his part simply took hold of a pin that one man was wearing on his jacket and crushed it between his fingers like it was made out of soft clay. He handed the mangled piece of metal back to the man and the group graciously let Laszlo and the others past. The look on the faces of the antagonists was probably priceless. I\u2019m sorry that I missed it.<br /> <br /> Once they got to the hotel they met up with Magdalena in the lobby. The woman herself was apparently very beautiful and both Lizette and Wolfram seemed to be rather smitten with her. Before they even got to the room, Magdalena asked if any of them were armed. Lizette admitted that she was and readily handed her weapons over to the woman we don\u2019t know. Lizette doesn\u2019t hand her weapons over to just anyone. Magdalena seemed to just be interested ensuring her own safety, but it seemed strange that my packmates would seemingly trust this woman so readily. Anyway, after the weapons were turned over they went up to her room. The place was an absolute mess but her things were undamaged so it is likely that she is just messy and that her room had not been tossed. They discussed the fact that they were looking for Martinique, who possibly goes by Odile. Magdalena seemed to know who they were talking about. Ludovico also came up in conversation, related to Martinique\u2019s attempted kidnapping, and Magdalena was interested when it was mentioned that we had plans to go against the Italian Count. Magdalena is particularly opposed to the man and was keen on seeing him dealt with. After being assured that we only had Martinique\u2019s best interests at heart she said that she would do her best to put our group in contact with the dancer. She said that she would let us know when and where we might meet Martinique once she had things set up.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t that much later when she called the house and said that she had set up a meeting between Martinique and us tomorrow at 1 pm at the Sacred Heart Cathedral in Sarajevo. When Lizette called, she let us know what Magdalena had said and what she was planning on doing before she came over to the hotel. Her plan was to make some shaped charges so we could get through one of the walls with minimal damage to the surrounding buildings. When they arrived at the hotel Lizette said that she\u2019d heard on the radio that riots had started in town between the Fascists and Communists. We had heard the same thing on the hotel radio while we were waiting for our packmates to arrive. This was causing many of the city\u2019s police force to leave their posts at museums around town and go deal with the rioting. This left an environment suitable for Gerard to get in and out with whatever he planned to steal. <br /> <br /> After we all met up at the hotel we went upstairs to plan our next moves. Wolfram mentioned that he could use a gift called Boneyard to \u201clook\u201d inside the warehouse and see what kind of defenses they had and if there were any captives present that we needed to be concerned about. We planned that Marie would guard Wolfram while he did this. Laszlo and I would sneak up to the back and make a hole in the wall and go in that way. Meanwhile Lizette, Tatiana and Emma would be coming down the main street laughing and acting drunk, like they\u2019d just left a bar. If luck was with us Tatiana might get some of the folks from the Dockside bar to follow us to a create a distraction at the front door. So, we decided to go with that for now to get a better idea of what we were up against, though we modified the plan slightly. I would guard Wolfram while he did his thing. We would then report back what he saw to the rest of the group. So, we went back to the warehouse district and Wolfram and I snuck up on Ludovico\u2019s building. My packmate used his Boneyard gift to see inside. He said that there were several armed guards by the front door as well as what looked like a weaponized forklift. Then suddenly Wolfram felt the presence of another Claimed\u2019s Boneyard go up over the building and his own power go down. As soon as Wolfram came back to himself we both got away from the warehouse as quickly and quietly as we could.<br /> <br /> When we met back up with the others we changed our plans slightly to take into account the new information. We decided that if they had Boneyard up then sneaking up from the back would be moot since they would know that we were coming. So, we decided to all approach from the front in the guise of a rowdy bar hopping crowd looking for some fun. Right now we\u2019re just waiting for it to get dark enough so that Alla can join us for the raid. It should be a good fight. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> No, volchonok, you should not come.<br /> <br /> It was luck you were not seen the first time! Anywhere that has spirit guards has someone to summon and control such things.<br /> <br /> I do not know what manner of being this Italian count has. Perhaps a Pure. Perhaps a magician. Perhaps something else.<br /> <br /> Well, we know they have a Sineater, since Wolfram was kicked out of his Boneyard by someone reclaiming the territory.<br /> <br /> Bah. He will mostly be a problem as a witness, as he will likely get away. He might be able to control that forklift.<br /> <br /> You are learning, volchonok. Yes, a forklift is a machine like a car, but this one has been improved in the ways Lizette improves things, Wolfram said. Lizette will try to control it instead, in which case things will be much different. If she cannot, Laszlo is very good at breaking things.<br /> <br /> Other problems? Well, there might be vampires, since we will be attacking at night. There were a large number of men with guns. Who knows? Perhaps they are our mirrors and there will even be another Beast.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, we will not let Lizette merely explode it, not without checking for any captives. We are trying to rescue them, after all.<br /> <br /> No, Marie\u2019s friend is not there. We will go talk to her tomorrow, the others arranged it with the singer. But there may be others. This count is a cruel man, by all accounts, and pursues women to force them to be with suitable men, apparently. <br /> <br /> The Leninists at the dock were fairly helpful. That is where I came up with the plan to use the brawl at Dockside as a cover for the attack on the count.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not Red now. But I will help Red against Black any day. I did not like the way those Hungarians were eyeing the art the Russians were carrying. Or the Russians themselves.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is why I helped carry large boxes. I thought also they might know of Gerard, if they were moving art around the city.<br /> <br /> They were from elsewhere, so no. But, as I said, they were helpful regarding the count.<br /> <br /> What singer?<br /> <br /> I mentioned a singer?<br /> <br /> Oh, yes, that the others arranged to talk with Marie\u2019s friend through. Of course I remember. No, it was not the purple Sineater. She did tell them of this German singer who knew where Marie\u2019s friend was. Apparently this singer very much hates the count, so was willing to help.<br /> <br /> Lizette and Wolfram did seem smitten with her. She is probably very pretty.<br /> <br /> I have had enough of singer spies. They are welcome to her.<br /> <br /> Bah. Hush you.<br /> <br /> No, volchonok, I am not too distracted by Emma. She is Uratha. <br /> <br /> Yes, she was flirting outrageously. That does not mean she is intending to do anything. It is safe flirting.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I have found a twin I knew naught about. I will miss her company. She has the best ideas.<br /> <br /> I am sure she has ideas about running. We did our running earlier though. For now, you will stay in away from the fight, and take care not to get the attention of their spirit controller. We will run later, once this is dealt with. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> Allo Allo! Christina!<br /> <br /> Yes How is Am\u00e9lie?<br /> <br /> Wonderful! Can you put her on the phone?<br /> <br /> Ah, well if she is asleep\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, no, I am fine. Et toi?<br /> <br /> Bon\u2026Oh, um, Communists and Fascists, Ballerinas and Anarchists. It has been exciting.<br /> <br /> Oui\u2026Martinique, the girl we are seeking is alive. Well, we are fairly certain.<br /> <br /> Yes. Are you familiar with Count Ludovico? <br /> <br /> Mmm hmm. Mmmm hmm<br /> <br /> Well to less powerful women he is apparently dangerous. Glad has he never given you trouble. We are looking into his interests. Know of any?<br /> <br /> Carvelli? Noted, will pass it along.<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> What can you tell me about the White Swan? Ballet Company.<br /> <br /> Good to hear. Yes it was a nice facility. I am sure they are well respected. What about the Black Swan?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s okay; you are a respectable woman. They are saboteurs. Possibly connected. Or it could be a red herring. What?<br /> <br /> I have some familiarity with Swan Lake, but only what I have absorbed being around people far more cultured than myself.<br /> <br /> Oh you are too kind.<br /> <br /> Well either way we are raiding a warehouse tonight, got a few hours till then, so I wanted to ask about Am\u00e9lie. You know how it is. And how is Regina?<br /> <br /> Ah I see. Excellent. As long as she is actually helping.<br /> She thinks so, does she? Well we will keep correcting her, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Oh no I couldn\u2019t possibly, I mean we have a raid on the warehouse in the next several hours like I said. I\u2026<br /> <br /> It would be nice to hold Am\u00e9lie.<br /> <br /> Misses Mommy, does she?<br /> <br /> Awwwwwwwwwwwwww. I\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026I can get back here in time. Hold on let me drive to the house where the Trod is. See you soon. Goodbye.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> Magdalena Von Ackermann is indeed an Immortal, though her precise nature is unknown. If she is a spy, her masters are similarly blurry. <br /> <br /> The backdrop of the struggle in Vienna at the time got a lot of play. Laszlo managed to use his rote action Strength + Intimidation pool well. Fed the Gremlin anyway.<br /> <br /> Okay think all is well explained. Next session is a big battle. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:36:17-07:00","id":1107107,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the off week. Missed a session due to vacation, and that was around coming home time so everything was crazy. Got the recap tonight though. <br /> <br /> Mostly one big fight. Note Wolfram\u2019s player had to miss due to work issues.<br /> <i><br /> Session LV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 18 August 1925<br /> <br /> After the sun went down the fun began. We as a group went to the bar that the Communists from the port suggested would be fun later on, and found out that they were right. There was a big fight between Communists and Fascists. We lent our aid to the Communists, because of the two groups I would rather support them than the fascists any day. The fight was fun. The Russians, with our aid, had a distinct advantage which they used. We eventually moved our part of the fight down the street to the warehouse district. We \u201cfought\u201d one another, trading realistic looking blows here and there, as we moved closer to Ludovico\u2019s warehouse. When we arrived at the warehouse we just went for the frontal assault. Outside this time was a rather large man and three dogs. Again, the dogs were actually spirits. Lizette used her machine gun and made short work of the man. The rest of us took care of the spirits. One \u201cdog\u201d landed a hit or two on me, but didn\u2019t really hurt me. After they were taken care of Laszlo worked on taking the door down. While he did that I assembled my rifle just in case it was needed inside.<br /> <br /> Once inside things got more interesting. There were several people inside, both upstairs and down, including a vampire on the second floor catwalk. Tatiana ran inside and leapt up to meet the vampire in combat. She hurt him pretty badly and he fled, presumably out a window. I then moved inside taking position behind some boxes so that I would have cover. Then the enemy Claimed controlled the forklift and made it shoot fire at the front door. Those in front, including Alla, Marie, Laszlo and Lizette, took the brunt. Laszlo and Lizette were immune to the fire so it did nothing to them. I can\u2019t say the same for the others. Alla was hurt, but managed not to panic when she was set on fire. Marie was also hurt, but not too badly. I thought that she handled herself well. This was her first real fight after all. <br /> <br /> Up on the catwalk Tatiana went after a man with a rifle, killing him in moments. I took out a second rifleman a moment later. Meanwhile Laszlo focused his attention on the forklift. He managed to block the flamethrower so it could not hurt anyone else. He then proceeded to attack and damage the machine. The other riflemen, deciding that Laszlo was a big threat, all fired at our newest packmate. He bore it pretty well, but I could tell that he was starting to feel the pain. Lizette found four riflemen grouped together near the stairs and decided that what was most needed in that location was a grenade. It exploded and hurt the riflemen. Laszlo, probably tired of being shot at, lifted what was left of the forklift and threw it at the same four riflemen. They did not survive the combination of Lizette and Laszlo\u2019s attacks. Unfortunately the enemy Claimed decided that Laszlo was a threat and used a gift to throw the forklift back at him. Tatiana decided then that the forklift just had to go and jumped down and proceeded to finish tearing it apart. The Claimed wasn\u2019t done and used his gifts again to throw a large crate at Tatiana. She shrugged off the injury and jumped back up to the second floor. I borrowed Tatiana\u2019s gift and jumped up there after her. Alla followed. <br /> <br /> Upstairs there were two rooms that had people in them. Each room had two individuals. The first room that we assaulted had two vampires in it. Tatiana and I attacked them. I went after the man with claws and Tatiana went after the man with the gun. Between the two of us we killed both Kindred in pretty short order. They got a couple hits in on us, with claws and the gun, but in the end they couldn\u2019t stand up to us. In the other room the remaining vampire jumped out a window before we could set our sights on him. I assume that he did not fancy his odds against two werewolves. The remaining person was a ghoul. Alla kept him from escaping since he had seen her face. He had to go. The vampires were Invictus, and we couldn\u2019t have them reporting back that Alla had been involved in a fight that killed several of their number. Tatiana killed the ghoul in short order.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, downstairs Lizette, Laszlo and Emma went down the first floor hallway. They ran into several men, probably ghouls. Lizette used her last grenade on a group of three. The enemy Claimed was also downstairs as our packmates discovered when he used a gift to instill fear. Emma finished off some of the ghouls that Lizette had hurt with the grenade. One man with a machine gun tried to shoot Laszlo and Emma, but missed them both. There was also a spirit of hatred downstairs. My packmates eventually took it out despite the fear effect. Lizette was focusing on the enemy Claimed. She shot him repeatedly with her gun eventually killing him. At least temporarily. It should take him a while to come back from that. About a day if Amethyst was any indication. Or maybe it was with the next sunrise. I should ask Wolfram. It was a good fight overall. Lizette and Laszlo bonded over \u201cmayhem\u201d and we were all satisfied with a job well done.<br /> <br /> After both groups had dealt with Ludovico\u2019s men we found a locked room and freed three Russian girls. Tatiana assured them that we were there to help them and found out that they were in town to support their comrades with the Communists. Russia also had a bad winter, which is part of the impetus for them leaving. They also wanted to support their friends here in Vienna. Unfortunately for them Ludovico saw them and decided that he wanted them for himself, so he kidnapped them. I\u2019m assuming that he targets Communist girls since he is himself a Fascist. I personally do not believe that the innocent should be held against their will. So, I was happy to help free those girls and weaken Ludovico\u2019s hold in Vienna. The man needs to be taken down a peg or two.<br /> <br /> After the fight was over Lizette rigged the warehouse to explode. My packmate is rather skilled with explosives, so she had the whole building wired and ready to go in just a few minutes. The lot of us stepped a safe distance away and Lizette pushed the plunger. I will admit, the explosion was impressive. The charges were set in such a way that Ludovico\u2019s building coming down wouldn\u2019t affect any of the surrounding warehouses. Our goal was not to set the whole warehouse district on fire, just the one building. <br /> <br /> Marie and the three Russian girls went back to the hotel with Tatiana, while Emma went back to Krieger to report on what happened tonight. All in all I think things went pretty well. All of us that had been injured were able to heal our wounds in pretty short order. It looked like clay filled in Laszlo\u2019s injuries, while the werewolves among us just used our natural healing to take care of any cuts or bullet wounds. Luckily Lizette was not wounded during the fight. Without Dearbhail we have no dedicated healer, so if Lizette, or anyone else without a healing ability, is injured they must endure the wounds until they heal naturally over time. Wolfram has some healing abilities but it is very difficult for him to use that gift, especially on other people. <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 19 August 1925<br /> <br /> We are on our way to Sarajevo. Had a few things to take care of before we could leave though. First thing that happened before we left was Amethyst called to make sure that we were alright. She assumed, correctly, that we were involved in the explosion at the warehouse. She was vague in her speech, so I was vague as well. I assured her that everyone was fine. The only thing that I asked of her was to keep an eye out on the fallout from the warehouse explosion. If anyone interesting takes a notice, or anything in particular happens as a result of the fire I want to know about it. The police will be involved, but that is to be expected. The fallout that I\u2019m most concerned about is the Kindred\u2019s interest in the whole thing. They lost several of their people. I just want to make sure that they don\u2019t know that Alla was involved in any way. Things could become politically untenable for her in this city if they suspected her involvement. Amethyst said that she\u2019d keep her eyes and ears open and I thanked her for it. <br /> <br /> After that we left to go to the airport. We had a bit of an interesting time with local police officers. The officers wanted to search the plane before we left to make sure that nothing stolen was on board. Apparently, Gerard stole something pretty valuable last night and the police are on the lookout for the item and the thief. They were also interested in why our airplane had weapons mounted on it. In the end, we let Fenric do the talking. As Alla\u2019s ghoul he has certain gifts, like hers, that allow him to make people amenable to doing things for him, or generally be nice to him. So, he used that gift and explained to the officers that we had no stolen items and the mounted guns were perfectly legal. They seemed to buy it and left us alone to board the plane. Now, we are headed for Sarajevo. Should be an interesting trip.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I know you do not like the flying machine. <br /> Bah. There was no chance the man could make us not fly. <br /> <br /> Yes, Fenric did have to use vampire magics to get him to let us go. Really, it saved him from being knocked about more than anything.<br /> <br /> It would have been bad if he had made us not fly, foolish volchonok. We need to speak with the dancer, the swan woman.<br /> <br /> Because... I don\u2019t know. To make sure she is not mind controlled perhaps? She is not kidnapped, and we dealt with the count.<br /> <br /> It was a good fight, yes.<br /> <br /> I tried to tell you about it earlier.<br /> <br /> I know you were distracted. You are a very distractible volchonok.<br /> <br /> Bah, as if it were the fairy land\u2019s fault that you get distracted at every good smell.<br /> <br /> I do like talking about good fights. I almost thought it was not going to be.<br /> <br /> Well, the fascists at the Dockside were only human, after all, and were cowed very easily. I would have left soon even if we did not have a warehouse to assault.<br /> <br /> Oh, you meant the fight at the warehouse?<br /> <br /> Ah! Alright, alright, volchonok. That was a good pin, I have taught you well.<br /> <br /> It went like this: first, we fought a trio of spirits, and one human guard. They were nothing we couldn\u2019t handle quickly, so we did.<br /> <br /> Tough ones. I do not know what kind, I did not stop to ask. They took on the forms of dogs though.<br /> <br /> After that, Laszlo broke the door down. It gave them time to set up and all, but it also gave Marek time to build his gun.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, it is inconvenient for our alpha to have to build his weapon each time, but he can scarcely carry it around town.<br /> <br /> Yes, a human thing. Anyways, I got the jump on their vampire, and he ran like a small child for his mother. The ghouls were cleaned up by the other - Lizette threw a grenade and Laszlo threw a forklift.<br /> <br /> It worked well until the Sineater threw it back.<br /> <br /> Bah, no, the Sineater was not that strong. He used Sineater magic to do it from far away. He also used Sineater magic to make it spray fire.<br /> <br /> Well, Lizette and Laszlo are immune to fire, so that was alright. Alla had some troubles, but she was alright eventually. It was better after Laszlo stood in the way of the fire, and then after he threw it away.<br /> <br /> I broke it. I did not want it to keep being thrown around. It could do nothing to stand against me, of course. <br /> <br /> Then we split up. Alla and Marek jumped up after me - the others couldn\u2019t reach. Marek couldn\u2019t either, but he borrowed my Gift for jumping. <br /> <br /> It was more fun, up there. We could smell and hear three vampires and one ghoul, but one of the vampires ran away after we started the fight. He ran away before he saw Alla though, so it was alright.<br /> <br /> The ghoul also tried to run, but he had seen Alla, so we stopped him. <br /> <br /> Of course the vampires could not stand against us! Marek took down the one playing at soldier, I took the businessman down.<br /> <br /> He was very fast, for a businessman! Impertinent volchonok.<br /> <br /> They found some to fight. The Sineater, for one. A few ghouls, and what Emma said was a hate spirit. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. There was many bullets though.<br /> <br /> The girls were downstairs with Lizette, Laszlo and Emma. They did not open the door til I got there though, so I was able to reassure them with proper Russian.<br /> <br /> Human things, volchonok, human things. They were Communists, in town to support their comrades. Also because it has been a bad winter, back home in Russia. That you can understand, yes? Even the beasts know of hard winters, though what is hard sometimes differs between our species.<br /> <br /> It is true, we are not having a hard winter.<br /> <br /> No, that does not mean we can go for a run. We still have business to attend to. Just because we have exploded a warehouse doesn\u2019t mean it is time to run. Later, volchonok. Later. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 19th August 1925<br /> <br /> Post Battle Summary for conflict at the Warehouse 18th August 1925:<br /> <br /> The Siege of Count Ludovico\u2019s Warehouse was successful, no fatalities on our side, short term or long term.<br /> <br /> The initial assault on the doors went well. There were three Spirits disguised as dogs and an armed mortal. The Werewolves made short work along with Laszlo. I shot down the mortal. Laszlo smashed the door.<br /> <br /> The first room had a total of six armed mortals. Five behind cover and one on the catwalks above, along with a kindred with long claws and one hell of a beautiful feat of engineering. A forklift with a flamethrower, scythe blades, spikes, and armor. The Sin-Eater on the guardian\u2019s side turned it on and attacked us with flames, which upset Alla but she managed not to panic. My Elemental Contract with Fire helped. Laszlo rather heroically charged in and blocked the tube of the flamethrower while Tatiana leapt for the rafters, where she drove off the vampire with a single blow, and cut down the human. Marek was shooting at the gunners, and I threw a grenade at them, as their rifles were tearing Laszlo up. Having been shot by rifles myself, I wanted to make them stop shooting Laszlo. He deserves better. He eventually lost his patience and hurled the great device into the shooters, whose cover was positioned around the stairs. Having already been wounded by my hand grenade, they could not cope with the machine.<br /> <br /> Laszlo gave me a thumbs up and declaration of \u201cMayhem!\u201d which was berries! Mayhem buddies!<br /> <br /> Of course, then the Sin-Eater threw the forklift at him because he is an asshole. If it wasn\u2019t bad enough that they tried to kill us with a forklift he used it as a projectile. Then started throwing remaining crates. Laszlo was pinned under it at the time, a brief problem for one of his lifting ability, so they threw them at Tatiana. <br /> <br /> He was probably running low on ectoplasm as the throwing stopped. We split into two groups, one being Tatiana, Marek and Alla the other being Laszlo, Emma, and myself. Maria watched the door. <br /> <br /> Tatiana\u2019s group ran into three vampires and a ghoul. One vampire fled before they were even seen. Two were in a room they made short work of, with Alla blocking the way out. We ran into some sort of black spirit with flowing red eyes and knife hands, a couple ghouls, and the Sin Eater. Emma pointed out the room most of those were in and I threw in a grenade rather then let them ambush us, which took a lot of the fight out; the Spirit was still aggressive but I dealt with it, albeit as the last one standing. Laszlo wounds were filling with clay, like Sin-Eaters do with ectoplasm. I charged around and opened up with my Tommy Gun on the Sin-Eater, who was very badly hurt from the outset, even with Ectoplasm. We made short work of him from there. He was terrifying looking, and he we were all shaky, but I filled the air with bullets, first the Sin-Eater, then the Spirit.<br /> <br /> I think all our ears were ringing from my machine gun fire. In addition to drum set in front of the gun, I had a large one on my back, so I could spray the area, and I was walking fire a great deal. Between that and grenades I felt like I was pretty effective. Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Though I need to make myself resistant to fear before fighting a Sin-Eater again.<br /> <br /> We rescued three women, all Russian, all communists, from the warehouse before I set it to blow. We will get them somewhere safe and see what they know about Ludovico. It feels good to help people. Especially when it involves explosions! Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Today we head for Sarajevo. The whole thing with Gerard had the police jumpy, but Fenric smoothed it out. Time to meet our mysterious swan.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LV</i><br /> <br /> I specifically did research to find that yes, they had forklifts. And yes, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vx7ldTl7txQ\" target=\"_blank\">they tried to kill them with a forklift</a>. I\u2019m terrible.<br /> <br /> Time is short and I am behind, but if you have Comments or Questions they are welcome. I may not answer until after the weekend though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:30:01-07:00","id":1112889,"title":"","content":"The team meets their connection in a Cathedral in Sarajevo. Then all hell breaks loose.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> Well, today was possibly more eventful than yesterday. When we arrived in Yugoslavia we paid the customary bribe to the airport personnel so they would look after the plane and make sure we got it back when we needed to leave. Why am I not surprised that they required a bribe to keep planes in their care safe from robbers or saboteurs? In any case we continued on to the Sacred Heart cathedral. We spotted Martinique pretty quickly and started to make our way towards her. As we were walking a body fell from the rafters and landed on the chairs near us. Tatiana and I rushed to the man to see if we could tell what had happened. The man was clutching a silvery crown. I could tell that it was a powerful Pure fetish. Before anyone noticed I slipped the crown from the man\u2019s fingers and surreptitiously put it in Tatiana\u2019s pack. It was not silver. <br /> <br /> We discovered that the man had been dead before he was dropped from the rafters, though we\u2019re not exactly sure how he died. He did not have any obvious wounds on his body. As we saw to the body the others chased after Martinique who had made a run for it out the back door. She was honestly surprised by the body falling and scared enough to make a run for it. My pack mates eventually caught up with her and they made their way back to the cathedral, but stayed outside to talk. <br /> <br /> While the chase was going on Tatiana talked to the priest and asked how she could get to the rafters. After a moment he showed her the stairs to take her up there. She got the scent of the killer, or at least of the person that dropped the body, but did not see them. Their scent seemed to go up the wall, where there were no handholds, and out a skylight to the roof. She then came down and asked how to get the roof. The priest was less inclined to tell her that, but she eventually persuaded him. She went up to the roof and found the scent, but it disappeared into the air. So whoever left that trail either glided or jumped off of the roof. We\u2019re not sure which. All that we could really tell from the scent itself was that the person was not a werewolf. It is possible that the person was a Claimed. They have a wide variety of gifts. Perhaps Wolfram will know.<br /> <br /> So, the others caught up to Martinique and managed to convince her that they were friends. She was still spooked and refused to talk to them in such a public place. Around this time Marie and I made our way out the back door and Tatiana climbed down the outside of the building to join us. We immediately sensed that Martinique is wolf-blooded. Martinique then said that she would talk to us, but only if we moved to a secure location that she knew about. We agreed that this was acceptable and we all went to Martinique\u2019s studio. The front door was manned by a Slav man that looked like he could take care of himself. He let us in at Martinique\u2019s insistence. The building had stairs leading up to the studio, which was set up to be well defended in the case of a siege. The stairs had places to take cover and the studio itself was arranged so you could quickly take cover or escape the building. All in all a good set up.<br /> <br /> Once we were alone Martinique confirmed that she was wolf-blooded and had gifts that allowed her to dampen her scent or use pheromones to make a werewolf find her very attractive. As it was I could tell that those of us in the group who were uratha were feeling rather protective of her. After a moment Tatiana revealed the crown to the group. The idea that the dead man was Gerard was brought up. It was also speculated that Gerard was the one that dropped the body in the first place. We do not know for sure and cannot verify our theories. No one knows what Gerard looks like so we can\u2019t identify him from eye witness accounts.<br /> <br /> As we were talking Martinique told us that Ludovico has an island off the coast of Italy. He has scientists building weapons for him, mostly Russian, and some expatriates from other Central powers. Apparently, he wants to set up something of a shadow government in Italy. She managed to escape from him in Vienna and fled to Belgrade. Ludovico\u2019s men found her there so she fled again to Sarajevo. And as we knew from earlier Magdelina has been helping her escape Ludovico\u2019s men and finding her safe places to stay. It is unknown how Ludovico\u2019s men keep finding Martinique. Someone put forth the idea that Magdelina was double-crossing Martinique, but it was also brought up that Magdelina seems to really hate Ludovico. She has even killed several men that were sent after Martinique or herself. It seems that she charms the men into giving up their guns and then she slits their throats. Then she keeps their bodies. I don\u2019t want to know what for. It doesn\u2019t make sense that she would aid him. Perhaps the man has some other means of locating Martinique. Whether it is mundane or supernatural is unknown.<br /> <br /> Martinique also revealed that she has not heard from the Lake of Tears, which is the headquarters of the Black Swan. She wanted to investigate the situation but said that if she brought us with her she would be shot as a traitor. Apparently they are very strict about their security. Seems sensible to me.<br /> <br /> Martinique revealed that she and several other Black Swans had managed to make off with documents and maps from Ludovico\u2019s estate a while back. Unfortunately the women that had gotten away with the papers were later captured or killed and the documents taken back. Martinique lost the maps that she had in her possession when she was captured. I asked her if she could reproduce any part of the maps that she had seen. I figured that something was better than nothing when it came to intelligence. She said that she remembered some things, but not everything. I told her that was fine. Any advantage that we can use is good. She also said that she knows where the island itself is, so we just need maps of the island and a way to get there and we\u2019ll be set.<br /> <br /> While all of this was going on Lizette went back to the airport to get the plane ready for takeoff. Our plan was to leave with Martinique as soon as she was done with the maps. A little while later we heard a pretty loud boom from outside and a moment after that Lizette came upstairs. She said that she had spotted a car full of heavily armed men sitting outside the building that we were in. She decided to take care of the problem once and for all and rolled a grenade underneath the vehicle. The resulting explosion surely killed all the occupants. But in case it didn\u2019t, we decided to flee. It was obvious that Ludovico had found Martinique again and we had to leave immediately if we were going to keep her safe. Martinique grabbed her still packed bags and weapons and we headed for the plane. As we were heading out Tatiana and Laszlo spotted two suspicious men down the street near the bus station. They decided to approach the Italian Fascists and start a fight. The pair of them made short work of the armed men and they left them lying on the ground. We all met up at the plane.<br /> <br /> Since we had the plane and it was fueled up we decided to go to Italy and see what we could find at Ludovico\u2019s estate. I called the house and left a message for Alla letting her know what we were doing and that we\u2019d be delayed getting back. Then we left for Italy. Since I was familiar with reading maps I acted as navigator while Lizette flew the plane. She flies rather a lot like she drives so it was an exciting ride.<br /> <br /> Once in Venice we made our way to Ludovico\u2019s house. Lizette and I broke in and began searching the house from top to bottom. I took the third floor while Lizette took the second. We both searched the first floor. I had a nagging feeling that I\u2019d missed something so I asked her to re-search the top floor and I\u2019d take one more look at the second. In my second search I found a couple of books handwritten in Italian. They looked like they could be ledgers so I grabbed them. There were several people in the house, two were human women the last was a skeleton of a woman with glowing red eyes reading a book. The sight was a bit disturbing. On the way out Lizette asked if she could burn the place down. I thought about it for a moment and then agreed with her plan. They would know that we had taken the books, so the fire was a way to cover up what was stolen. It was also a way to strike a blow at Ludovico. He is not a good person, and in fact would likely be a prime target for Reznick if there were such a job offered. I\u2019m not getting paid to kill this man, but if I get the chance I will do it anyway. In all reality Tatiana will likely get him before I do. She is fast and deadly with her teeth and claws. <br /> <br /> Once we were done with the house we met up with the others and beat a hasty retreat to the plane and started heading towards Austria. I again acted as navigator until Lizette got into familiar airspace. We arrived safely in Vienna and got back to the house around 1:00 am. Once there we split up to do different things. Lizette took Alla through the gate to France so she could feed on her \u201cherd.\u201d They are a group of older women that stay at the house for the sole purpose of allowing Alla to feed off of them. Anyway, Tatiana called Greta and asked her to investigate the Italian company that Martinique read about in the book I took. It might give us information on supply runs that Ludovico has made to his island. If we could sneak on board a supply ship we would have an easy way there. We do not yet have a definite plan. We will discuss this further after we all have gotten some sleep.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 20 August 1925<br /> <br /> It seems like this is the week for breaking and entering. But before that, Tatiana, Marie, Laszlo and I went to go talk to Krieger. We wanted to show him the crown and see if he knew anything about it. The man saw us and we immediately told him what had happened regarding the crown. He said that the crown was a powerful Pure fetish, which I knew, that could basically make other werewolves really like you and want to do what you say. I guess it increases a person\u2019s charisma. Apparently the Pure are really upset by its loss and have brought in help from outside Vienna to help them look for it. They have even employed some spirits to search for the missing crown. We suggested that we hide the crown outside of the country. We have our estate in France. No one would think to look that far away for it I\u2019m sure. Krieger thought that this was a good idea and gave us leave to do just that. We shared our suspicions that Gerard was involved in getting the crown to us. Whether or not he was the person who dropped the body, or the body itself is unknown. While we were there he also mentioned that the Pure have been somewhat distracted by the Zionist convention in town. They don\u2019t like Jews it seems and some of the Pure have been harassing people instead of looking for the crown. <br /> <br /> Laszlo made sure that there wasn\u2019t an immediate threat that we needed to look into right away. There was not. The Jews are in danger, but not any more than they were already. Tatiana asked Krieger if he thought that Ludovico might be connected to the Pure. He did not believe they are linked.<br /> <br /> After talking to Krieger Tatiana, Lizette and I went to go visit Ludovico\u2019s estate here in Vienna. Tatiana and I led the guard dogs away from the house so they would not detect us sneaking in and alert their masters. I picked the lock and let Lizette and myself into the house. Ludovico had already gotten word about his house in Venice and stepped up the security. There were guards with dogs on both floors of the building, which meant that I could not search it. The dogs would catch my scent and alert the guards. So, Lizette, who can mask her own scent, investigated the house while I kept a look out on the first floor. The only thing of real interest that she found was a map of Ludovico\u2019s island. This was more than we had before, so we both slipped out of the house. This one we left standing.<br /> <br /> Once back at the house we\u2019re staying at we examined the map. It looks like there is only one good approach to the island. There is a good place to land a boat, but it is in full view of the house. There is also a tower at the back of the house on top of the hill. Any paths leading up the hill to the house can be watched from that tower. We don\u2019t have a lot of good options when it comes to infiltrating that island.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 21 August 1925<br /> <br /> Just a quick update. Greta got back to us with the shipping schedules for the supply ship to Ludovico\u2019s island. We then started working on our plan to get onto the island. The idea of taking over the ship and pretending to be the crew was brought up. This might have some merit. If the shipping company doesn\u2019t use the same crew each time then we could easily slip into those roles. If they do use the same crew then that might be more difficult. Well, I guess I should get back to the planning of our attack. I think there is an old saying, \u201cLet luck favor the bold.\u201d Here\u2019s hoping that we have luck on our side. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> How many times do I have to say it, volchonok?<br /> <br /> Once more, eh? Yes, the man flew.<br /> <br /> I do not know if there are werebirds or what they would smell like. But the man\u2019s scent lifted into the air from the belltower. I know what I smelled.<br /> <br /> It was probably Gerard, or one of his agents like we stole from on the train. Presumably he does not bear a grudge.<br /> <br /> He basically delivered the fetish to us, is all. Or I suppose the crown might be cursed and giving it to us is revenge.<br /> <br /> I do not believe, volchonok, that you know what cursed objects smell like. Besides, I can\u2019t. It is in Paris.<br /> <br /> Well, the Pure in Vienna are looking for it, with many spirits. It was stolen from them after all.<br /> <br /> Yes volchonok, it could be that Gerard was not the flying man, but the dead one, but it seems unlikely that the master thief was taken out by strychnine, with no struggling, especially by someone who would just give us the crown rather than return it. <br /> <br /> It is true, possibly the killer could not tell Pure from Uratha. Humans and many other supernaturals are very bad at smelling. I still think that Gerard was the flying man.<br /> <br /> With Martinique? He better have nothing to do with her.<br /> <br /> Nor you!<br /> <br /> That is better, volchonok. She does smell nice. And she is mine.<br /> <br /> Ours. I will not fight Marek. Perhaps he will let her join the pack.<br /> <br /> True. It is how it should be.<br /> <br /> She is who we came here to find. But she has found that the Italian count has an island where he makes weapons and holds women.<br /> <br /> Of course we go to rescue them, volchonok.<br /> <br /> Oh. We have not gone already because we had to learn more things.<br /> <br /> Like what the island looks like...<br /> <br /> Of course we can use our eyes to see what it looks like when we get there, foolish volchonok, but sometimes it is easier to see secret things on a piece of paper. And stop interrupting me.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s right. We also needed to know what boat to steal to sneak onto the island. <br /> <br /> Yes, Lizette and Marek found that out partially when they burned down the house in the water city. Greta found out the rest.<br /> <br /> There was a skeleton reading a book, remember? Also, Lizette likes burning things.<br /> <br /> The count\u2019s house here in Vienna, with the dogs, that is where we got the island map. They did not burn that one down. No skeletons.<br /> <br /> I think we finally have enough. We will see what Marek says.<br /> <br /> No, we do not have time to run. Perhaps once we deal with this island.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LV</i><br /> <br /> We actually started with a chase scene, Laszlo, Lizette and Fenric trying to catch up with Martinique when she bolted. Lizette was close but likely would have lost her; Laszlo actually burned Satiety to catch her.<br /> <br /> Greta Hess was the Bound reporter they bumped into a couple times, remember?<br /> <br /> So yeah, Marek and Lizette broke into and searched the Venice house, Lizette asked Marek if they can burn it down (Liz has kinda a one track mind) and Marek\u2019s player was like \u201cMarek has to the conscience right now? This is bad.\u201d Aaaaaaaand they burned the house. With a number of people in it, and Liz had to make a Clarity check. I am pretty lax about those in this game, but torching a house of non-combatants qualifies. She passed.<br /> <br /> Reflected more in Tatiana's journal than Marek's all three Werewolves feel very protective and possessive of Martinique, as well as some attraction. Kind of a low background level of her pheromones. We will see where that goes.<br /> <br /> Finally I noted OOC-ly that they had, in fact, met Gerard. I did not specify if Laszlo had or not, but I did say either he had or he had read about Gerard in a journal (or both). SO now they get to figure that out.<br /> <br /> Marek\u2019s player is on vacation, but Wolfram\u2019s is back, as they make their next move. Comments and Questions welcome. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:37:39-07:00","id":1119646,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for Golden Eagle! Due to circumstances beyond my control, we only have a Tatiana journal this time. Jacob\u2019s player was out of town and there was no Lizette due to a minor crisis. I will have a brief summery at the end.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVII<br /> </i><br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations<br /> </b><br /> I was not running from the lizard, impertinent volchonok!<br /> <br /> There was an invisible... something with it. Probably a vampire, as they did not bleed.<br /> <br /> Do not speak to me in those tones! Perhaps I will add volchonok teeth to my lizard\u2019s.<br /> <br /> A large number of Wolfram\u2019s bullets did not hit the trees and something strong broke through that wall. That is how I know something was there.<br /> <br /> Ah, yes, volchonok, you are right - that is another reason it was probably a vampire. They had no heartbeat in my forest.<br /> <br /> I was not thinking of vampires when I summoned it, foolish volchonok. I thought it would help me find the monster.<br /> <br /> The fire was not a monster. That was Greta, with the grenades, remember?<br /> <br /> We sent her to explode the labs, to distract the guards. That worked very well, unfortunately. We fought very few, only the invisible vampire and their two guards. And their lizard.<br /> <br /> It was enough to injure Fenric seriously, it is true. But that was also largely due to the fight before the distraction and the fire from the lab explosion. <br /> <br /> I could hardly let the little man burn. I am much better at healing than him. So of course I shielded him.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, we climbed down from the window and then avoided the wall guards because of him. And also the women. There was for too much danger they would be injured. I should tell Lizette that her grenades make good distractions.<br /> <br /> It was not foolish of the guards to check on the explosive before the knocking. Unfortunate for them, but not foolish. Most people could not knock a hole in a wall after all. Laszlo is very good at it.<br /> <br /> Indeed, Lizette is very good at dealing with boats. And explosives. It is good to have packmates who are very good at a variety of things. This is why we should convince Marek to invite Martinique to our pack.<br /> <br /> She and Alla killed a man, with her knives and Alla\u2019s fists. And she can read Italian. And pick locks. And... she smells very nice.<br /> <br /> I do not think she was too unhappy that we did not kill the bad alpha. It was far more important that we shield our pups.<br /> <br /> No, saving our pups does not mean it is time to run. First we must save Martinique\u2019s friends. Then, perhaps.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> This session was the raid on Ludovico\u2019s Island. They hijacked a ship sending supplies and left disguised as suppliers, with Lizette going into the mines under the house to set charges (so journal would have been brief anyway). They got in, killed a guard, and sent Greta Hess with four of Lizette\u2019s grenades down to destroy the lab, while they looked for the prisoners. Greta seemed to be taking awhile, so they doubled back and ran into the castle shaking fireball from the explosions, and fought guards, with Fenric being badly hurt. They then went though the kitchen, interrogated the staff (using Wolfram\u2019s knowlage of Greek) and found where they were held. They killed more guards (with Fenric nearly dying this time) and found they were guarded by two Nosferatu with Nightmare and Obfuscate. This proved a problem, as the Nos kept terrifying them and making them flee, notably Tatiana and Laszlo, though Wolfram kept shrugging them off. Eventually Wolfram, who had merged with a mounted machine gun Lizette provided got a clear shot and sprayed the hallway, injuring the Nosferatu badly due to, well, those mounted machine guns being crazy (the sort of thing usually mounted on a stand or vehicle.) the Nosferatu unleashed a large lizard (Cryptid, technically) and fled. Tatiana brought the Cryptid down more or less by herself. They escaped with the girls though a rope of sheets, rendez-vousing with Greta, then outside with Lizette who detonated the explosives she set, causing the castle to collapse into the mines. They used the last grenade as a distraction while Laszlo broke though the wall to escape to their ship, which was pursued but Lizette seized control of the pursuers guns, turning them on each other while the heroes, and the girls, escaped.<br /> <br /> If you have any Comments or Questions on that, feel free. Marek is back next time, for the showdown at the Lake of Tears. It gets ugly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T15:59:26-07:00","id":1119654,"title":"","content":"Was the Cryptid a Mage, Demon, or other Cryptid? The term gets used a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:39:21-07:00","id":1119672,"title":"","content":"Demon. Like warped animal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:12:45-07:00","id":1125322,"title":"","content":"As we reach the penaultimate session in the storyline, it is the raid on the Lake of Tears. The name is appropriate; Not all victories feel good, or even like victories.<br /> <i><br /> Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 22 August 1925<br /> <br /> I want to find Ludovico and kill him slowly with my claws, then have Greta raise him as a zombie and I\u2019ll do it again. When I find him he will know pain. I will give Tatiana the chance to kill him though. She deserves that after all that she\u2019s been through. I will hurt him nonetheless for what his men did to my pack mates. I suppose Wolfram deserves a shot at him as well, considering. We will see how it goes when we eventually find him. I will endeavor to let my pack mates have the kill, despite how much I would like to take it for myself.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should start at the beginning, though it is unlikely that today will fade from my memory. Martinique took us to the headquarters of the Black Swan. To start we were all blindfolded for the drive there. Once we arrived at our destination we found ourselves at the edge of a lake. Martinique said that we\u2019d have to take boats across, but to follow her closely since there were mines in the water. They take their safety seriously. Unfortunately for them their precautions didn\u2019t amount to much in the end.<br /> <br /> We split up and took two boats. I rowed one boat as quickly and quietly as I could. We had seen boats patrolling inside the line of mines and they didn\u2019t appear to be Black Swan. So, Martinique guided my boat, which had Tatiana, Laszlo and Marie as passengers. Lizette rowed the second boat with the others, including Greta. As we were moving closer to the shore we noticed that there were six people on the bank. Three of which were vampires, one was a Claimed and one of the last two was a creature with many mouths on its body. I believe someone later said that it was a Promethean, or possibly something that used to be a Promethean. <br /> <br /> So, Tatiana and I shared a look and then she did what she does best. She charged straight at the Claimed and attacked. While he was still reeling from her blow I followed it up with a shot from my rifle. Between the two of us we hurt him badly and he fled towards the house. After that a vampire attacked Tatiana, hurting her pretty badly. Not enough to make her stop, but enough to make her bleed freely. After that is where it got bad. The monster with all the mouths, the promethean touched Tatiana\u2019s arm. A moment later mouths appeared all over her arm and hand and it began to move of its own accord. The promethean made the arm hit Tatiana and it went right for her throat, killing her within seconds. Wolfram indicated that he was going to spray the area a moment before he opened fire with his, usually vehicle mounted, machine gun. He hit several enemy combatants. A moment later Lizette threw a grenade into the same group. The promethean was bleeding freely and where its blood hit the ground the rocks it hit suddenly sprouted legs and started walking towards us. Wolfram opened up again and the promethean exploded. Two of the vampires were also killed in that attack.<br /> <br /> I could not attack the monster that killed my pack mate so I attacked one of the only people left, the remaining vampire. Then there was more machine gun fire, but it did not come from Wolfram\u2019s weapon. The mounted gun on the beach had been sprayed with promethean blood and began firing at my pack. Wolfram was hit hard and he stumbled. Smoke and blood was pouring off of his body. The vampire hit me after that, but I will admit that I didn\u2019t pay much attention to the wounds in that instant. I was rather mad that Tatiana had been killed and Wolfram wounded so badly. Laszlo retaliated against the vampire and killed him in one hit. I then started to move forward when Lizette threw another grenade into the group of promethean spawn. I think Wolfram called them pandorans. Whatever they were, Tatiana had become one of their number when the monster\u2019s blood hit her body. A moment later Greta sent a huge wave of water towards them and killed them all. In Tatiana\u2019s case she was killed again. I will hurt Ludovico in ways that he\u2019s never thought of for doing that to my packmate. He will know fear before he dies.<br /> <br /> We took a moment to catch our breath and Greta admitted that she could raise Tatiana as a zombie. She would not be cognizant, but she would be animate and be able to attack. I had mixed feelings about my friend being raised from the dead like that, but conceded that we could use all the help we could get. We headed for the house after everything on the beach was dead. At the front doors we paused and let Lizette throw another grenade. Well, she actually just rolled it through an opening in the front doors. After it went off we all rushed in, Tatiana in the fore. What we found inside was wholly unexpected and rather disturbing. We encountered monstrous women, or what used to be women. They were creatures that were the bodies of two or three women all merged together. The sight took many of us by surprise, and really disturbed Martinique. I wasn\u2019t surprised that she was so disturbed by the sight. They were her friends after all. Anyway, the monsters attacked and we reciprocated. I killed one creature that was two women merged with a head where her stomach should be. As I hit her I thought I saw gratitude in her eyes. I realized in that instant that the women were not dead. They were still alive and aware of what had happened to them. I could even hear them trying to speak. It sounded like garbled German. I endeavored after that to kill them as quickly as I could. They did not deserve what happened to them.<br /> <br /> Tatiana followed the Claimed\u2019s blood trail while the rest of us dealt with more of those monsters that came swarming out of the rooms in the hallway. Several attacked us in the foyer. Lizette was badly hit and Wolfram, Laszlo and I made short work of the few that were immediately in front of us. Lizette threw a grenade down the hall to deal with the ones there. A moment later a wave followed and killed the remaining monsters.<br /> <br /> I found out after we got down the hall that Tatiana had killed the Claimed and began attacking the next biggest target in the room. We all joined her soon enough and began attacking a rather large monster that was in the room. It touched Tatiana and made her attack herself, much like the Promethean did outside, but it missed. The rest of us attacked and eventually I got in the killing blow with my claws. There was also an old man with an equally old gun in his hands. He was a vampire. He shot at Tatiana. Laszlo retaliated. The vampire seeing that he was outnumbered turned into a ferret and ran into the walls. Wolfram was insistent that we follow the vampire so I tracked it outside and around to the front of the house. When he realized we had followed him he turned into mist and tried to get away. Wolfram used a gift that he has called Pyre flame and burned the vampire though he was in mist form. The vampire fled under the water to get away from us. I\u2019m pretty sure that we hurt him badly.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately when we followed the vampire out to the front of the house we forgot about the three boats that had been patrolling the waters near the island. They started making their way towards the house when they heard gunfire and explosions. Right after Wolfram used his gift to attack the vampire the boats opened fire on him. He was already pretty badly hurt and could not stand up to too much more injury. He was killed almost instantly. Lizette was also badly hurt by the gunfire. Alla and I pulled Lizette behind cover and did our best to bandage her wounds so she would not bleed out on the beach. We didn\u2019t have much choice after that. We were outnumbered. We made ready to run and Greta pointed Tatiana in the direction of the boats. She could jump easily to the deck of one and distract those that were after us. She was already dead, so logistically it made sense to leave her to attack the boats. Personally, I hated to do it. We were forced to leave Wolfram\u2019s body and Tatiana\u2019s soon to be body behind. We couldn\u2019t all escape and take them with us. So, we gathered up Wolfram and Tatiana\u2019s personal effects and I put them in my pack with my rifle. Our packmates would regenerate at the site of the Eagle, but their personal items would not, so we took those with us. The rest of us ran for the opposite side of the house and took to the water to escape. I helped Laszlo swim to shore, since he does not know how to swim yet. Alla helped Lizette since she was still so badly hurt. I\u2019m not sure if anyone else was hurt outside of my pack. I think Alla was hit at least once, but she shrugged it off. I didn\u2019t notice her acting pained in any way. My own injuries were making themselves known quite emphatically as I helped Laszlo swim to shore, but I gritted my teeth and kept going. We did not have the luxury of resting while we were fleeing the gunboats. We eventually made it to shore, found our cars and drove back to the house.<br /> <br /> At this point all we can do is wait for our friends to come back to us. I will admit that I am very glad that we took Jamal up on his offer of using the Golden Eagle. I have become rather attached to my pack mates and was greatly pained to see them lying on the ground dead or badly hurt. I have seen my friends bleed far more than I\u2019d like, but I know that we live a dangerous life. We get ourselves involved in problems foreign and domestic, whenever a friend calls out to us. I do not begrudge our lifestyle. We chose it. I chose to be an assassin. I know that there is someone out there that wants me dead, and he or she knows how to do it. Their last \u201cenvoy\u201d used silver bullets, which I\u2019ll admit is an experience I don\u2019t look forward to any time soon. But this is a life that I chose. My friends chose it too. I am only glad that Dearbhail was not with us on the island. If she had been hurt or killed I don\u2019t know what I\u2019d do. As it is, I want to rip Ludovico and his men limb from limb. And that\u2019s just for killing my pack mates. If he had hurt my special lady I am honestly not sure what I\u2019d do. I do know that it would be violent, bloody and possibly involve a grenade. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Volchonok? Volchonok! Where is the pack? Are they alright?<br /> <br /> Oh. Good. Wait - Wolfram woke up yesterday? The others? Martinique? Greta? Marie?<br /> <br /> Just us two died? Good.<br /> <br /> Ah! Volchonok, take care. Uh - bah - stop that. Yes, yes, it is good we are all well.<br /> <br /> I did not bite myself!<br /> <br /> Yes, I scratched at my neck.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, there were teeth in the mouths on my paws where my claws should have been.<br /> <br /> Well, they were not my teeth, so I did not bite myself.<br /> <br /> Just because I died once, volchonok, that does not mean you can contradict me like that.<br /> <br /> Three times? What do you mean 3 times? Explain.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Lizette\u2019s advice to \u2018spray the area\u2019 is not so bad. So, the Sin-Eater ran and Wolfram shot down the mouth creature and some dead men. What then?<br /> <br /> Spider rocks? Volchonok, you...<br /> <br /> OK, OK! It is you who is telling the story.<br /> <br /> Let me get this straight. Everything the mouth creature\u2019s blood touched grew mouths and began walking towards the pack, including a tree, a mounted machine, and me? I did not hurt anyone?<br /> <br /> I must thank Greta then. I would not have been easy with the idea that my teeth finished Wolfram off, after the walking machine gun filled him with holes.<br /> <br /> I must really thank her! A zombie? Did I kill the rest?<br /> <br /> Oh right, Lizette\u2019s grenades and Greta\u2019s wave. Surely there was more to fight? The Sin-Eater?<br /> <br /> Excellent! Of course I tracked him down. I am the best at hunting, even after dying twice. Were there others to fight?<br /> <br /> Another monster? Like with the mouths?<br /> <br /> Only one for each head? How many heads...?<br /> <br /> Four. Of course, volchonok, I should have guessed. What the hell were they doing at that place?<br /> <br /> Grrr...<br /> <br /> You cannot blame Martinique. She is not Uratha, but they were her pack, those women you say were melted together, or molded into new shapes. We killed them all, yes?<br /> <br /> I meant the ones who did such things, though I imagine the women-monsters were well put out of their misery.<br /> <br /> All but one? How did we let it get away?<br /> <br /> A vampire you mean?<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, Alla is much better than him. But Pure are still called werewolves, even though I\u2019m better than them, so he is still called a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course I could track a ferret, even a vampire one!<br /> <br /> Oh. Well, of course Marek could track a ferret, even a vampire one.<br /> <br /> Mist? That is cheating.<br /> <br /> Traps are also cheating. At least Wolfram lit the cheating vampire on fire before he was killed. How did the pack escape, with three boats of riflemen?<br /> <br /> Of course I did, volchonok! Those boats didn\u2019t stand a chance.<br /> <br /> Close enough. The pack escaped, didn\u2019t they?<br /> <br /> So that counts as killing all 12 of them.<br /> <br /> Because I say so, volchonok. Now. Where are they? Not here, but for Fenric, or I would know.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> Thank goodness for the Eagle, eh?<br /> <br /> So, I have to talk about how Tatiana died. Tatiana had taken some aggravated damage from a Vampire with Protean, but what killed her was hitting herself when her arm was, for a single action, infused with Flux from a Centimenti, and attacked her. She rolled twenty dice to attack herself (due to no defense from all out attacking). If she had rolled nineteen successes she would have survived (it was doing bashing because Werewolf). But she rolled twenty-two successes on twenty dice, and died. Poor player is never going to have an attack roll like that again is she?<br /> <br /> So after being a Pandoran for a very brief time before being put down by Lizette and Greta, Greta animated her with the Stillness Marionette. She pumped a fair amount of Plasm into the zombie, and I gave it to Tatiana\u2019s player to run. The resulting Zombie was much tougher, but did notably less severe damage. Still it\u2019s mindless charge after the fleeing Sin-Eater pulled everything in the House, leading to people talking about \u201cScholomance all over again.\u201d Though the hall full of once-women was wiped out by Lizette\u2019s grenades among other things.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Lizette, she ended the fight with 6/7 of her Health Levels full of aggravated damage, and the last with lethal. She only survived because a medicine roll was made.<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned rifles suck? Even a handful of humans with them is dangerous. What happened at the end was the players forget they rushed inside after the outdoor fight was over because the three boats were moving back toward the island, with riflemen aboard. So when they rushed out after the Vampire, the boats were waiting.<br /> <br /> The members of the Black Swan inside were damaged by Flux experimentation.<br /> <br /> So yeah, two members killed one completely incapacitated and only saved via medicine. Everyone on the island dead or wished they were. Not the best end, but they will deal with Ludovico again.<br /> <br /> Last night was a very short session, Alla\u2019s player being there long as she could before leaving with a migraine. Mostly some hunting for Laszlo and the Vampire social. Then ahead is some hero style archeology in Egypt! I\u2019ll see you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T02:18:22-07:00","id":1131166,"title":"","content":"It was a very short session, about an hour of play as we had a scene with Laszlo, had the Salon, and some downtime discussion. Journal from Marek, though. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 24 August 1925<br /> <br /> We are still waiting on Tatiana and Wolfram to come back to us. We cannot do anything until that happens. So in the meantime Laszlo and I decided to go on a hunt. He needed to strengthen his resolve and to do that he hunts and \u201cteaches.\u201d So, we went out looking for Fascists. It wasn\u2019t hard, they are all over the place in this town. So, we found a group and I stayed back while Laszlo taunted them. I think his goal was to make them feel vulnerable when they were away from home, like they do to others. We ended up chasing them through a maze of streets. Sometimes I was in human form, other times I chased them as a wolf. All they knew was that two or possibly three beings were chasing them, and they were damn scary. I am not the most physically imposing man but I like to think that I make up for it with determination. I have been told before that my gaze can be scary sometimes, especially if I was in a fight or hunting. So, I offered these men my best smile and gave chase through the back streets. They eventually got themselves lost and trapped in a dead end. Laszlo did his thing where his presence feels much more imposing than his physical form would imply. He\u2019s good at that. After he made sure the Fascists had learned their lesson he deferred to me and I smiled at the cowering men and said that it was my turn. I then did my best to emulate my pack mate and started a fight. I had wanted to take out my anger on someone and decided that these guys were the perfect target, and so I did just that. I beat them to a pulp, only sustaining glancing wounds myself, and left them senseless on the ground in the alley.<br /> <br /> After that Laszlo and I made our way back to the house for a celebratory drink. I wanted to share our exploits with the others, but did not feel that they were up for it. Lizette was resting, as were the others. Wolfram and Tatiana were not back yet, and their deaths had caused a good deal of uproar at the house in Paris. Christine was very upset when we first got back and had to be reassured that her husband would be back within a few days. I don\u2019t know how much that actually reassured her. She was still upset. She has spent a good deal of time also tending to Lizette\u2019s wounds. Her other lover\u2019s injuries bothered her just as much. So, I left them too it and resolved myself to share the story with Tatiana as soon as she came back. I figured that she would appreciate it. She loves to fight.<br /> <br /> Volchonok has been restless these past few days. He keeps prowling around the property in a circle, like he is guarding Tatiana. I figured he was doing just that. He knew that I was nearby and keeping an eye out myself, but he could be with her twenty-four hours a day, whereas I could not. I know that my own spirit companion has been trying to reassure the young pup that Tatiana would be back soon. Volchonok seemed to listen, but then went back to circling the house. I will leave him to it. I will not stand in his way of protecting his friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> 25 August 1925<br /> <br /> Wolfram came back to us today. Christine was overjoyed, as was Lizette. I felt as if a weight had been lifted from my chest when he drew breath once more. I guess the hunt yesterday did not fully alleviate the stress of losing a friend. Today though, everyone\u2019s mood was much improved. Wolfram came back to us, but he was still very worn out and tired. He replenished what he could of his energy from the locus in our house, but he was still not to full strength. He then within a short time expended a good deal of that recovered energy in healing some of Lizette\u2019s wounds. I know that he was upset to see her injured as she was and set out to do what he could to make it better. I believe that he plans on healing more of her wounds after he replenishes his energy once again. We are lucky to have such mystical loci within our property.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26 August 1925<br /> <br /> Today was the day of the Salon. Alla had been looking forward to this for a while now. Ever since she got involved in the planning for the party she has thought of little else. She has even gotten others of our pack involved in the planning for this event. Lizette, who is much improved since Wolfram started healing her, planned on animating some random objects at the salon. The house that it is was held at is a bombed-out ruin, and the theme was that of ruined finery. Everyone wore clothing to match the theme and the party appeared to be haunted. Wolfram asked some local ghosts to make an appearance and both he and Lizette added to the effects. Lizette animated things such as chairs and candelabras to move and walk around, while Wolfram used his Boneyard gift to make doors open as people approached them, made windows open and close and lights turn on and off at random intervals. I had no really purpose at the salon other than to act as security at the door. That was fine by me. I am not one for social gatherings anyway. I never seem to get it right. It is a failing on my part, but practice doesn\u2019t really seem to help. I am fine with family and with my pack, but strangers are another thing entirely. I\u2019m told that I come across as cold and somewhat uncaring when dealing with strangers. I suppose that is apt. I don\u2019t actually care much what happens with strangers, except where it affects my family and friends. It\u2019s just the way I am and I can live with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 September 1925<br /> <br /> I have resumed my hunt of Ludovico. He is a wily bastard I\u2019ll give him that. I have found a few places where he was, but not where he is now. I believe that he has friends that help him. Supernatural friends, or those familiar with the supernatural. Given some of his past acquaintances I would believe either one. I have hunted many men and have not had as much trouble finding them as I have with Ludovico. I will find him eventually though. He will pay for what he did to my pack mates. I suppose it would be good to bring him to justice for the others that he\u2019s hurt as well, but I\u2019m mainly after him for killing my pack mates. Maybe I should see if Tatiana or Laszlo wants to help me hunt the bastard.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 September 1925<br /> <br /> He definitely has someone working for him, and whoever they are they have gifts of their own. It started out with little things going wrong, but lately as I get closer, I have noticed an increase in the number of unusual occurrences that have happened to me. Today was the worst by far. I was on a boat following a lead when we suddenly struck something under the surface. We were getting close to shore in an area that is normally fairly deep, so I\u2019m assuming we struck something that had sunk just off shore. I have been told that after the war the waters around several countries are more treacherous due to sunken ships or downed planes. Regardless of what we hit, the boat started going down. The small crew and few passengers started making their way to the life boats. I started to join them when I noticed that our plight had not gone unseen. An Italian navy boat was making its way to us in an effort to help. When they arrived they were perhaps more curt than they really needed to be considering most of the passengers were innocent civilians. There were a few ex-military men on board. I could tell from their bearing. So, given the navy\u2019s less than hospitable introduction I opted to allow my backpack to slide off my shoulder and sink with the ship. I did not want to have to explain to any group of military men what I was doing with a sniper rifle in my possession. I was sad to see my bag sink. I liked that rifle. I will have to talk to Hans and see if he can set me up with a replacement.<br /> <br /> <br /> 15 September 1925<br /> <br /> I was arrested. Again. As soon as the Navy helped the life boats get to shore they started pulling people aside as soon as they\u2019d stepped on land. The Captain and a couple of his crew were grabbed immediately. I was also taken into custody. I think they assumed that I worked with the Captain or something. I tried to explain then and there that I had nothing to do with the Captain\u2019s business, that I was just a passenger, but they didn\u2019t believe me. It didn\u2019t help that I don\u2019t really know much Italian. So, they brought me and the other men to a military police station and locked us up. Thankfully this jail was considerably better than the one I found myself in when I was in Yugoslavia. This place was clean, almost to a fault, and the prisoners well treated. When I requested that any meat be rare they looked at me like I was a bit off, but agreed nonetheless. I mentioned a couple of simple dishes that employ rare meat as an example, but it really doesn\u2019t matter to me. As long as it\u2019s rare, it\u2019s good for me. <br /> <br /> They interrogated me through an interpreter for a while before finally coming to the conclusion that I was not working with the Captain at whatever illegal activities that he was up to. It helped that the Captain and I barely had a language in common. It was a nuisance to be detained, but I\u2019ve been in worse jails so I couldn\u2019t complain too much. When they released me the commanding officer apologized for the mix up and offered me a ride to a train station or another port. I said that I\u2019d had enough of boats for a while and accepted the offer of a ride to the train station. I believe that I may need to postpone my hunt of Ludovico until I can find a way to circumvent his mystical protections. I will likely need the help of my pack mates in this endeavor. Wolfram is an experienced occultist and Tatiana is unparalleled in a fight. Alla has her way with social situations in a way I could never hope to emulate, and Laszlo is good at being underestimated. It\u2019s funny. Laszlo comes across as very imposing, but most people push that feeling aside when they look at his stature. They assume that they are mistaken in their senses and that this slight man is not a threat. They are so wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> 16 October 1925<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been two days since Franko. I was hired to kill the Italian businessman a while back, but had not been able to get to him for a while. It was not a high priority. The client just specified that he needed to die before the new year. I researched Franko and found out that he is involved in human trafficking and is an overall asshole to even his legitimate business partners. I thought it would be an easy job. I followed him one night to a dock where he was unloading cargo from a large container. He and his men were just pulling boxes out so I assumed that the only people down there were criminals. I was wrong. I guess I got cocky and was not as careful as I should have been. He must have seen light reflect off my scope or something. I don\u2019t know what gave me away, but something did. Just as I took my shot Franko reached into the container and pulled out a young girl, no more than ten or twelve years old. He pulled the child in front of him and the bullet struck her before going through and grazing Franko. <br /> I was in shock for a moment before the rage set in. I could not get the image of blood spreading on the young girl\u2019s blue shirt out of my mind. I still can\u2019t. I don\u2019t hurt children. That has been a hard and fast rule for me since day one. I do not harm children. And Franko made me do just that. He made me kill that child. I saw red and dropped my rifle. I shifted forms on my way down to the loading dock. I hadn\u2019t even realized I\u2019d take gauru form until I reached Franko and his men. They tried shooting me. It was pathetic. They were too scared to shoot straight. Franko pissed himself when I got close. Though he did manage to grab a gun from one of his men and shoot me square in the chest. I will admit that hurt, but given my state of mind I just shrugged it off and growled. There was no point in telling him what he was dying for. He knew. He wouldn\u2019t have understood me anyway.<br /> <br /> After I killed Franko I shifted to dalu form and told Franko\u2019s men to run. They did. I then turned to the storage container and saw that there were five more people hiding in the back. I told them that their captor was dead and that they should run to the authorities. They had not seen the person who shot the little girl, they only saw me kill Franko. Most of them were afraid of me, but one woman said \u201cThank you,\u201d before running off. I don\u2019t blame them. I was covered in blood and not quite human looking.<br /> I didn\u2019t wait to see if the others left, I just took off and recovered my rifle from where I\u2019d dropped it. I didn\u2019t want to leave this one behind like I did the last one. I managed to stick to the shadows until I could get to the place I was renting to clean up. I got so far as taking off my ruined shirt before I was violently ill. The realization hit me again. I had killed a child. An innocent child. Somehow, I managed to take a shower and wash away the rest of the blood. I packed up my belongings and left town that night. The room was paid up through the following day, but I did not want to spend any more time in that town than I absolutely had to. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2 November 1925<br /> <br /> I still have bad dreams about that night. Franko. I don\u2019t usually have bad dreams about killing people, but then I\u2019ve never killed a child before. They were all grown men or women, and they had all done despicable things. I had no qualms about killing them. But Franko changed that. He pulled that child in front of him to use as a shield. How low do you have to sink to use a child as a shield? My only regret is that I could only kill him once. I went into a rage and killed him so quick. True, he had time to understand what was about to happen to him. He got to see the monster that killed him full in the face. My other targets never saw me coming. Franko did. I suppose that gives me some satisfaction. It doesn\u2019t help with the dreams though. I wonder if this is how normal people react to having done violence to another person? Do they see the faces of those that they killed? Do they have dreams that relive the event over and over? Dammit. <br /> <br /> 6 November 1925<br /> <br /> I feel like I\u2019ve redeemed myself just a little today. I was passing through a fairly big town in Germany, I don\u2019t recall the name, and saw something that bothered me. A young man, more of a boy by his actions, was holding the leash of a snarling dog. The dog itself was barking at another young man, who was trying his best to avoid the animal. The dog was straining against his leash. It was obvious that he wanted to go after the other man. Then suddenly the owner of the dog let go of the leash and said \u201cOops.\u201d He then told his dog, who was running at the other man, to stop, to heel, but there was no conviction in his voice. There was even a small smile on his face. I interposed myself between the target and the dog, and before the animal got to me I growled low in my throat, unconsciously shifting to dalu form as I did so. The man behind me gasped a bit, but I don\u2019t think the other people around us heard or saw anything out of the ordinary. In fact, a good number of people were actively not watching. The dog stopped dead in its tracks with a small whine at my growl. He then started to back off with his tail between his legs. The owner arrived shortly after and demanded to know what I had done to his dog. I answered with my best smiled that I had done nothing. I had simply prevented it from attacking anyone. While the owner looked down at his dog I shifted back to human form and turned to ask the young man behind me if he was okay. He said that he was just startled. He was wearing a blue shirt. Why did it have to be a blue shirt? Anyway, after making sure the guy was okay I walked away. The dog was cowed and would not be attacking anyone else for the moment, so I felt confident that I could leave well enough alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10 November 1925<br /> <br /> I decided to leave my rifle at our house in Paris. I took another job a day or so ago and had the target in my sights when I suddenly saw the young girls surprised face in the scope. She was obviously not there, not even a ghost, but I saw her face in my mind nonetheless. I couldn\u2019t take the shot. I ended up chasing the guy down in a dark alley last night and killing him with my claws. The client was not specific on how the target should die, just that he did. So, I simply shifted my hands to claws and opened his throat. I decided then that I would leave my gun behind for a while. At least until I could stop seeing her face so regularly. My gun brings back the memory of her death, so I decided to distance myself from that for a little while. I need to get my head back on straight before I use my rifle again.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26 December 1925<br /> <br /> I managed to make it home for the holidays after all. I wasn\u2019t sure for a little bit there if I would be able to make it. I was traveling through the woods a couple of days ago when I heard crashing about in the underbrush ahead of me. I shifted from wolf to human and walked ahead to see what was causing the noise. It was a couple of men, each carrying a rifle, a pack and some traps. They had apparently decided to go hunting and got lost in the woods. I made some noise before stepping out in front of them. I did not want to get shot for my trouble. I then asked them if there was anything that I could do for them. They said that they were looking for the town of Bauer. I admitted that I wasn\u2019t sure where that was, but could lead them back to a nearby town. They could then get directions from there to get home. They agreed and I started off. It was not hard to pick up the scent of humanity. It has a distinctly acrid odor. They were overjoyed to see civilization and thanked me profusely. I waved off any reward and headed back into the woods. I then shifted back to wolf form and ran the rest of the way home.<br /> I managed to make to the house on the 24<sup>th</sup>. Since then I have been busy helping around the house. The family has grown so much in recent years that it\u2019s almost too big for my father\u2019s modest house. The children were all very excited and wanted to open the presents I brought as soon as I walked through the door. I convinced them to wait, and managed to keep them away until Christmas morning. For little stormy-eyed Aneta I brought a stuffed bear from Germany. It has a little pink bow around its neck. For Darkja I brought back some doll dresses from Austria. Having gotten her most of her dolls I knew what I was looking for. For Kveta I got a wooden hair comb carved into the shape of a bird. This too I acquired in Austria. And for Dominik I got a nice shaving kit. He has turned into quite the young man since I last saw him and thought that he could use a more adult gift. They all expressed their thanks and handed out their own presents for me. From my family, I got a new pair of boots, a winter coat, a nice set of pens and a picture of the family altogether. They had apparently gone to a photographer and gotten the picture made. Dominik even carved me a wooden wolf. He said that he was working on making a whole pack for me. Curious, I asked him why he chose a wolf. He said that he didn\u2019t know, that it had just come to him. He knows how much I enjoy the forest and to him wolves are representative of the woods. <br /> <br /> I apologized to the adults in my family for the lack of creativity in their presents. I got each household a set of kitchen knives. I had seen how worn their old sets had gotten and thought to remedy that. I believe the ladies liked the present more than the men, but they all expressed their thanks. Later that day the ladies outdid themselves with the Christmas dinner as usual. They put their new knives to good use cutting up the ham and vegetables. The meal was modest but good, and I enjoyed spending time with my family.<br /> <br /> <br /> 29 December 1925<br /> <br /> I told the children more stories about the forest and the spirits that live there. I believe that they enjoyed themselves. Alena as usual was not happy with me \u201cfilling their heads with nonsense,\u201d but she did not stop me. She just clucked her tongue and told me that I was setting a bad example for the children. I honestly asked her why that was and she didn\u2019t have a good answer for me. I explained briefly that the stories did no harm, and would help ground them in their culture. She couldn\u2019t refute the last sentiment, but walked off in a huff anyway. That\u2019s fine. I am not out to win her over. I want to see my family healthy and happy and if that means annoying Josef\u2019s wife every once and a while then that\u2019s fine by me.<br /> <br /> I will stay with my family for a while this time I think. I have missed them, and it does me good to be with them right now. I have been too close to my wolf self for too long now and needed the reminder that humanity can be good too. I think little Aneta has sensed that I needed to be with family. She has delighted in following me around, holding onto her stuff bear, and smiling up at me. I made the mistake of giving her a ride on my shoulders the other day and she has asked in her limited vocabulary to do it again and again. She just looks up at me with a smile and says \u201cUp, up!\u201d I have not been able to deny her yet.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Lizette and Wolfram used the Contracts of Animation and Industrial Boneyard respectively to pull off their tricks. But what happened to Marek over the downtime, eh?<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for a new story, and a little Archeology as the group heads to Egypt. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T02:34:15-07:00","id":1136122,"title":"","content":"New Story. Time for a little archeology.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 25 January 1926<br /> <br /> The pack got back together again. Lizette had gotten an interesting phone call from Dana and she thought that the rest of us would be interested in being involved. I had been enjoying my stay with my family, but felt it was time to move on. I checked my own mailbox and found the letter from Lizette, so I headed for France. Dana came by for dinner and explained to us while we were eating what her plans were. Apparently, Dana is interested in going on an archaeological expedition to Egypt in the search for the Black Pharaoh\u2019s ruins. He was a Pharaoh a long time ago but was not too popular after he died. His sites were considered to be cursed, so many of them were demolished or forgotten about. Akhenaten, another ancient Pharaoh, believed that his god would protect him and he worked on sealing off the Black Pharaoh\u2019s temples and started building over them with his own works. There was something about him following one god named Aten instead of the polytheistic religion of his ancestors. I wasn\u2019t exactly sure how that was relevant but I guess it gave him the guts to build over the supposedly cursed sites.<br /> <br /> Dana received this information through a friend. Her contact, also friends with confidant Emma Brackenstall, told her about the Black Pharaoh\u2019s temples and such, and there was mention of artifacts that were awfully similar to the ones that we saw at that auction a while back. Our theory is that it is more of the technology that the caretakers of reality are interested in. Our goal is to get to that technology first. This is complicated by the fact that Dana is not the only one going to investigate this site. Iris DeVeers is also investigating. There is also something about the aforementioned friend of Dana\u2019s, Emma, having gotten involved with Iris and who has not been returning any calls or messages that Dana has left her. Dana is concerned for her friend as well as being interested in making it to the Black Pharaoh\u2019s site before Iris does. My concern with Iris is her interest in those artifacts. We know that she is a living machine, and very capable in a fight. We will need to be careful when dealing with her.<br /> <br /> As a matter of note it was also mentioned that the Mekhet Kindred in Egypt and the surrounding area have been particularly active. I\u2019m not sure what this means, but it could foretell potential trouble for us during our travels. I do not know if this has anything to do with the Black Pharaoh\u2019s sites or if it\u2019s related to something else entirely. There is someone local that we might be able to get some help from in dealing with the Mekhet. His name is Martin Krueger. We will have to meet with him and find out what is going on.<br /> <br /> We discussed ways to get to Egypt and settled on the fastest way to get there, which was to have Lizette fly us there. We would need to make a few stops before we reached Crete. From Crete, we would have to fly all the way to Alexandria in Egypt. The first few stops would be easy, it\u2019s the leg from Crete to Alexandria that could be problematic. It is an awfully long flight and we would need to worry about fuel in getting there. Tatiana offered her assistance. Apparently, she has learned a new gift that allows her to influence the wind. If she could create a tailwind we could get to Egypt and use less fuel. Lizette also mentioned something about tinkering with the plane to make it more fuel efficient as well.<br /> <br /> From Alexandria, we would take a boat to Luxor and head out into the desert from there. I think we were also going to meet Dr. Nathan Hinshaw when we arrived in Alexandria. I believe he will help us hire locals to help carry our equipment as we travel in the desert. We will also be renting a rugged vehicle capable of driving on the sand and some camels. The main concern we will have while in the desert is water and food, so we have made some plans regarding that. Wolfram can place objects within himself, so we were going to have him store three small kegs of water and one package of food within himself in case of emergency. Tatiana and I will be able to hunt for meat in the desert so the emergency food will mainly be for the rest of the pack. Hopefully these extra supplies will not be needed, but I am one to plan for any eventuality. It is better to be prepared for the worst and not need it then to be caught flat footed.<br /> <br /> <br /> 26 January 1926<br /> <br /> I had not been planning on bringing my rifle but someone asked if I had packed it and I thought it would look strange if I didn\u2019t bring it. I did not want to explain what happened with the little girl just now, so I thanked them for the reminder and got my rifle and case. Everyone else was similarly packed. We brought only what was absolutely necessary since weight was going to be a serious concern for us getting from Crete to Alexandria. This meant that Wolfram was unable to bring his big gun and Lizette had to leave behind her chainsaws. She is not unarmed though. There is never I time where that woman is not armed with something. Even Nicolette came with us this time. It was pointed out that she speaks Aramaic which may come in handy during our trip. She has also been on other trips to the desert while on digs so that experience may also be useful. I have never been to Egypt before, so this will be all new to me. I am looking forward to seeing a new part of the world.<br /> <br /> The flight to Alexandria went without any problems. I will write more later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Volchonok, you must calm yourself.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is very exciting.<br /> <br /> No, I did not call the wind spirits. We do not need them, Lizette would tell me.<br /> <br /> This is what happens, volchonok, when you fly very fast, very high up.<br /> <br /> I thought you did not like trains?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like trains. I do not dislike them, but...<br /> <br /> Oh. We are flying in Lizette\u2019s machine because it is faster, and we are racing Iris.<br /> <br /> The other woman who hunts for old things. The one who slept with Dana, and knew about the cultists, and the statues, remember?<br /> <br /> No, not \u2018some other human\u2019, volchonok. She was one of the robots, the machine people.<br /> <br /> She is not an enemy. I don\u2019t think. But we want to get there first. If we don\u2019t, we will be friends and work together.<br /> <br /> To get the pharoah things. Dana told us. The black pharaoh, the one who had the other statues Dana had, he had another place, and we are going there.<br /> <br /> Maybe there are more statues. It will be fun anyway. I have not been to the desert, and I have never hunted statues before.<br /> <br /> There will probably be fighting. Dana said there were vampires. And storms, but there\u2019s no fighting storms. Oh! And there will be other sorts of hunting as well, since we cannot carry meat into the desert.<br /> <br /> It is too hot, volchonok. The meat would go bad.<br /> <br /> Too hot for fighting? I do not understand.<br /> <br /> Bah, they are not fighting. Dana is just jealous. Or suspicious. One of those.<br /> <br /> Nicolette has also slept with Iris.<br /> <br /> That is the deal, volchonok. She comes with us to things like this. Besides, she speaks Arabic and reads Aramaic. Or the other way around.<br /> <br /> No, the deal is not that she has to run. Do not worry volchonok - there will be plenty of running once we are on the ground again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 27<sup>th</sup> January 1926<br /> <br /> So, here I am in Alexandria, Egypt. It\u2019s been a touch crazy.<br /> <br /> So Dana Barlowe arrived a couple days ago. Unfortunately Christina made only the barest attempt to be civil to her, and in response Dana all but taunted her. It was very uncomfortable. Dana was given a room, but of course slept in mine. Christina refused to not give her a separate room, and Dana refused to sleep in it. We had a good night, but it was annoying. I felt a bit bad about it.<br /> <br /> Dinner was more peaceful. Christina and Dana apparently backed down a little, perhaps Wolfram had a similar conversation to Christina that I had to Dana. All went well there. I really wish those two got along. I am the sole lover for neither. Christina is married to Wolfram, and Dana has several lovers of both sexes. But then, Christina has always gotten a bit jealous of women with me. I assume she would with Wolfram if he were flirtier.<br /> <br /> So a site associated with The Black Pharaoh came up on Dana\u2019s radar. It\u2019s under some<br /> ruins associated with Akhenaton, an old Pharaoh. The site had been ignored as cursed, but Akhenaton was unafraid to build on it, but it was lost in time. It came up on Dana\u2019s radar because Lady Emma Brackenstall, a girlfriend of Dana, discussed going to mutual friends. Lady Brackenstall had had a similar relationship with Dana to me, but was now working closely with Iris DeVeers, the living machine. Dana saw this as a betrayal, and with good reason. But as Iris and Dana are rivals at best, I see the mindset, though I would love to repair the friendship, even if Lady Brackenstall is by default a rival of mine.<br /> <br /> Apparently there is strange weather and a lot of vampire activity, especially with the Mekhet Clan. She does not know the particulars, but a Dr. Martian Kruger is a friend of Dana working at a dig in the area. Dr. Kruger knows a lot about Vampires, so Dana is planning to have us stop by and meet him.<br /> <br /> We planned a route, flying out of Chantilly via Italy, stopping on Crete and then continuing on to Alexandria. It\u2019s all a risky trip, as <i>Moth</i> is made for speed and maneuverability. Wolfram and I modified it yesterday, some, and I used magic to improve the fuel efficiency, to cross with as few a stops as possible. Everyone was loaded inside, Nicholette included, and we took off after I spent a little more time with Am\u00e9lie before heading out in the afternoon. The trip was long and difficult, and Wolfram and I took turns flying. But, ultimately uneventful.<br /> <br /> I hate being away from Am\u00e9lie though. And unlike last time this time I can\u2019t just appear back there if needed. Thank God for Christina. I would be crazy with worry without her. As opposed to, stressed with worry, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Now we are in Alexandria, and are to meet Dr. Nathan Hinshaw. I wonder where Iris and Lady Brackenstall are?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LX</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. Lizette had to make some piloting rolls but beyond that, just a tweak to the airplane, and used Contracts of Artifice to improve it. It was mostly a role playing session and like most new story starts a bit unfocused. Still, looks like a fun story ahead.<br /> <br /> Reminder the \u201cBlack Pharaoh\u201d stuff has been related to the God-Machine in the past, so expect some of that.<br /> <br /> See you next time when the inevitable Mummy business starts. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-01-2017, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T01:02:44-07:00","id":1140443,"title":"","content":"Last session was mostly RP. This time we jump straight into action.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 26 January 1926<br /> <br /> Well, things definitely did not start off on a good note when we arrived in Egypt. When we arrived at the airport we were accosted by a man and eight armed thugs. The man asked for a keystone from Dana, after confirming that she was in fact the woman he sought. She tried to tell him that she didn\u2019t have this keystone on her, but he didn\u2019t believe her. Dana and Alla kept the men talking while Lizette used her gifts to disable at least half of the weapons wielded by the thugs. The members of the pack better able to handle getting hit stood in front of those that would fall more easily against guns. Alla stood in front of Fenric, Wolfram stood in front of Lizette and Laszlo was in front of Dana. Then the fighting began. Tatiana shifted forms and jumped up to the walkway that the still armed men were on and I shifted and copied her gift and followed her up. We made short work of the four men on that side. The other four where dealt with by Lizette and her machine gun and Dana with her pistol. Laszlo had the spokesman for the group well in hand on the ground level after Wolfram used a gift to inflict what looked like painful wounds. The man was bleeding from every place it\u2019s possible to on his face. I\u2019ve had that gift used against me before. It really hurts.<br /> <br /> Once things were over, which only took a matter of seconds, Dana started questioning the spokesman in Arabic after making sure we were okay with that. We said fine and she started asking questions. Nicolette translated for the rest of us. Dana was asking questions like how he found her and how he knew about the keystone. He answered that he had talked to Hinshaw and the other archaeologist gave Dana\u2019s arrival details to the spokesman. He apparently told them that she didn\u2019t have the keystone but they didn\u2019t believe him. The spokesman also said that he worked for a man named Lucius. This may or may not be the man\u2019s real name. Apparently, it is common in this part of the world for people to take on a European name when dealing in shady business. Dana questioned the man further about Iris and found out that he does not know who she is. He appeared to be telling the truth.<br /> <br /> We left quickly after interrogating the spokesman. We did not want to be present when the authorities arrived. We reached Hinshaw without incident and talked to the man about what happened at the airport. He admitted to talking to the men, but he was vague in answering them. He also mentioned that Emma was in town but had traveled North by boat the other day. She seems to be headed for the Sea. He also said that he\u2019s been watching Iris\u2019s house and there has been no activity so far. When we brought up heading out to the dig site he said that it was not safe to travel by boat just yet on the Nile, we needed to wait a day or two for conditions to change. He is the expert in this place so we accepted his answer and went ahead to get rooms for the night. I ended up rooming with Wolfram. Lizette roomed with Dana, Alla with Fenric and Laszlo with Hinshaw. Lizette and Dana at least won\u2019t get much sleep, and given the way Laszlo and Hinshaw were trading glanes, they might not either.<br /> <br /> 27 January 1926 <br /> <br /> This morning Dana said that she needed some people to go with her while she recovered the keystone. Most of us agreed to come along. Alla, Hinshaw and Nicolette stayed behind. The rest of us went with her. While we were walking it was brought to my attention just how much the lot of us stood out in the crowd. Lighter features and hair, foreign clothes. We stood out like a sore thumb. The only one of us that blended in was Dana. She wore the equivalent of men\u2019s clothes, but she still blended in more than we did. As we were walking Laszlo overheard a group of nuns talking in Polish. He heard them say something about monsters, so he approached them and asked if everything was okay and what was going on with these monsters. They described human/animal hybrid creatures that attacked them and some slavers a little while ago. They also mentioned that they had called in some Hunters to take care of the monsters. Laszlo reported back to the rest of us and we continued on our way for now. We made plans to speak more in-depth with the nuns after we had concluded our own business. <br /> <br /> When we arrived at our destination Dana asked that Lizette and I join her inside that the rest of us wait for her outside. She had a plan and she said to just go along with it for now. Before she walked in she loosened Lizette\u2019s shirt so it was more baggy on her frame. I found out why as soon as we walked in. Dana was trying to give the impression that I was with her and Lizette was her or our child. The man argued in Arabic; something about expecting something more in return for holding onto the keystone, but Dana played innocent. I\u2019m assuming he was expecting sexual favors. That didn\u2019t work out to his liking and he stood up and started to try and intimidate us, me in particular, to back down. I glared right back at the man letting a bit of the wolf come through my gaze, and he backed down. Dana then pulled a gun out and handed it to me, indicating that I should keep our host where he was. She then walked over to his safe and expertly opened it and retrieved the keystone. She did stop and look at an artifact that was sitting out on the counter, but left it where it was only taking what we had come for. When she was done, I handed her gun back and we left the shop. <br /> <br /> We had not gotten more than a few feet down the street when we heard a crash from the shop behind us. We turned around and rushed back to the shop to find it being attacked by the very same hybrid monsters that the nuns had talked about. The shopkeeper was already dead, so we could do nothing for him. We stayed to deal with the creatures to keep them from hurting anyone else in the city. Dana pulled out her w\u0101s but it did nothing. I\u2019m not sure what she was expecting it to do, but it apparently didn\u2019t do what she wanted it to. <br /> <br /> There were two creatures, one with a lion\u2019s body and the head of a snake and the other with a snakes\u2019 body and the head of a bull. That one had wings. Lizette had her gun drawn and fired at the snake creature. The bullet appeared to do next to nothing to it. I attacked the chimera with the lion\u2019s body and obviously wounded it, but instead of spilling blood it spilled bees. It then attacked me. It hit pretty hard, but I shrugged off the injury in order to deal with the creature. Wolfram attacked the snake chimera with fire and scorpions started pouring out of the wounds of that one. Apparently each creature bleeds different swarming insects. Tatiana attacked and killed the lion chimera while Laszlo went after the snake creature. Lizette was starting to get swarmed by the insects so she used a gift and engulfed her body in flames to keep the bugs away. A moment later I finished off the snake creature and Wolfram and Lizette began using the fire to kill and smoke out the insects. <br /> <br /> During the fight Tatiana had bitten one of the creatures and bit one of the insects. She immediately spit it out. It didn\u2019t take long to realize that the insects were incredibly spiritually unclean. Tatiana went in search of a food vendor to get the taste out of her mouth while Dana told the rest of us where she had seen those chimera before. She said that they were Tomb creatures, and that they tended to stay around tombs and guard the artifacts that lay within. Our theory is that they were after some artifact that made its way to the city somehow. If we\u2019re right then the shop keeper, the slavers and the nuns all had something to do with it, or came into contact with the artifact. It is probable that the artifact was taken by one person and changed hands and the chimera were following the path. My pack mates made sure the insects were dead, which destroyed much of the shop, and we left to go talk to the nuns. We made it to the church and Laszlo found one of the nuns he\u2019d talked to before and asked her what was going on. The nuns were all gathered outside the church. She said that there were several of the monsters inside. My pack and I shared a look and agreed to go in and deal with them. <br /> <br /> I snuck into the church and attacked the chimera that was nearest to the door. It had the body of a lion and the head of a snake. I did grievous wounds to it in one attack with my claws. There were four other chimera in there as well. Tatiana attacked one that had the body of a bull and head of a lion. Then another one attacked me. Things were rather hectic but I think this one had the head of a jackal. Wolfram killed the one that Tatiana had attacked. They make a good pair. Then the one I\u2019d been fighting initially attacked me followed quickly by another attack by one that had the body of a snake and the head of a bull. Between the two attacks I was reeling. I knew that another hit like that would knock me out or kill me so I shifted to Guaru and went on the offensive. The shift healed a good number of my wounds, leaving only the really bad ones behind. My innate healing ability can only do so much to heal me of my wounds when in that form. I attacked the last one that hit me and killed it quickly.<br /> <br /> There was a flurry of blows going back and forth between my pack mates and other chimera creatures. I know Wolfram took one out after Tatiana wounded it. And at one point centipedes started crawling on me and biting me, but they didn\u2019t have any real effect. After we had dealt with the last of the chimera Tatiana and Lizette used their fire and wind gifts to burn and/or smoke out the remaining insects. After that Tatiana asked the nuns, in English, where the slavers were. One of the nuns gave her an address just outside of town. Dana thought to ask the nuns if they had taken anything from the slavers. The ones that we had run into on the street were not there and the others were not sure. They didn\u2019t think so, but we couldn\u2019t confirm that. All we know is that the chimera were searching for something and if people just happened to get in the way they attacked them. Once we were done questioning the nuns Dana found a phone and called Nathan to make sure that he was okay. He was. The creatures did not come after the rest of our group. That was good to know.<br /> <br /> After we left the church we decided to go back by the moneylender\u2019s place and see if that snake-headed artifact was still there. It seemed to draw Dana\u2019s attention earlier. When we got there though the place was surrounded by police. Dana put on a pleasant face and explained to the officers that something of hers was in that shop and she needed to get it back. She showed them the receipt she had for the keystone, but it either wasn\u2019t specific or she was counting on the police to not read it too closely. She was convincing enough that they let her in and she retrieved the artifact. That took very little time, so we headed to the wally to take that trip to the slaver\u2019s place and see what we could find out from them. When we got back to the vehicle though Dana asked if I was okay. I had been pushing the pain to the background because we had other things to concern ourselves with, but when she asked I had to admit that I had felt better. Wolfram insisted on using his gift to heal my wounds. I will admit that I like Dearbhail\u2019s methods better. She is more gentle. Wolfram\u2019s abilities are effective but much less mild. He had to pour alcohol into the open wounds in order to heal them. I will admit that hurt a lot. But I gritted my teeth as he worked and tried not to make too much noise. The last thing we needed was the police to get interested in what we\u2019d been up to today.<br /> <br /> Once Wolfram had seen to my injuries we headed to the address the nuns gave us for the slavers. We arrived in short order and parked a little way off so as to not arouse suspicion. There were two guards on the front door. When we got a good look, we realized that the guards were skeletons in robes. Wolfram said that he could use his Boneyard gift to \u201clook\u201d into the building so we could tell where any innocent people were and where the slavers were before we actually entered the premises. The pair of us snuck closer to the building and went around back. I guarded Wolfram as he used his gift. He was able to \u201csee\u201d that the building had a couple of levels to it. All the humans in the place were dead. Slaver and slave alike. Instead there were just supernatural creatures inside. The top level had five skeletons. Three surrounded a being dressed in blue robes that Wolfram said had died many times over the past thousand years or so. He guessed that it was some sort of mummy creature or one that serves a mummy. Together they were ransacking the place looking for something. The mummy creature seemed to be getting frustrated so I\u2019m assuming that they were not finding what they were looking for.<br /> <br /> In the rest of the house there were more skeletons downstairs that were keeping another chimera creature at bay. The chimera was spitting scorpions at the skeletons but it was predictably having no effect. After we got all the information that we could we headed back to the group and told them what Wolfram had seen in the building. We decided that the frontal approach was best and Tatiana and I attacked the skeletons guarding the door. Between the two of us and Wolfram we took them down in short order. We made our way inside and confronted the man in blue. Lizette opened up on it with her machine gun. The servitor then transformed into a swarm of bees, centipedes and scorpions and fled from the building. We were disappointed in that. I at least wanted to see what answers we could get from the mummy creature, but it was not to be.<br /> <br /> After the servitor fled we had to deal with the skeletons that were inside. The lot of us made short work of them. Once the skeletons that had been keeping the chimera at bay were dealt with we had to contend with the chimera itself. It had the body of a jackal and the head of a snake. It managed to land a decent hit on me before I had a chance to move. After hitting me it was close enough that Tatiana and I could both reach it, and reach it we did. In short order the creature was dealt with. The others took care of the rest of the skeletons. Overall it was an easy fight, but then we only had one chimera to deal with. Those creatures hit hard.<br /> <br /> I will admit to being curious as to what the chimeras were after. According to Dana they usually guard tombs and stay at said tombs. But this time they ventured all the way to the city to find something. And given the fact that the skeletons were fending off the chimera in the slaver\u2019s place I\u2019d say there are two groups of people looking for this artifact, whatever it is, at the very least. There are probably human agents looking for it as well. We just don\u2019t know what the item is and where it is. It is possible that the missing nuns have it. If that is the case, then they are in grave danger. Those chimeras will find them and tear them apart. I am almost tempted to just let the creatures take back what they are looking for even if that means the nuns will die. I am alone in my indifference however. I believe the others want to make sure that the chimeras do not harm any more people. I suppose I should follow their example on this matter. In any case we need to collaborate on what to do next. We have time before the boat will be able to take us upriver (I maintain that it is strange that a river flows south to north) so we will have time to investigate the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Volchonok, would you stop growling at Wolfram?<br /> <br /> Yes, I know he poured the burning water into our alpha\u2019s wounds. Did you not see that the wounds then closed?<br /> <br /> Well, I know it was Wolfram\u2019s doing, foolish volchonok. The burning waters helped.<br /> <br /> What was I supposed to do? We killed the tainted ones that were hurting him as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> Very, very tainted. I can still taste the horrible juices.<br /> <br /> I did have honeyed locusts. They taste good. It made things better, somewhat.<br /> <br /> Of course I still bit them, volchonok. That was the quickest way to kill these abominations.<br /> <br /> They wanted something, Dana thinks.<br /> <br /> It was complicated and much in different languages that I don\u2019t know. There were slavers, and the nuns were trying to stop them, but then the tainted ones attacked and maybe the nuns stole the thing the tainted ones wanted? I do not know why they attacked the man who\u2019d had the keystone.<br /> <br /> That is something else entirely. Dana needs a key for this Black Pharaoh.<br /> <br /> I mentioned it, impertinent volchonok, because the place that had the key also got attacked by tainted ones. That does not mean that the others who attacked us have something to do with the tainted ones.<br /> <br /> The ones at the airport, remember? They wanted to key from Dana.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I know she did not have it. They did not know, because they didn\u2019t believe Nathan.<br /> <br /> They asked him. That is how they knew she would be arriving by plane. It perhaps has something to do with Tunisia.<br /> <br /> A human place, do not worry. It is surely not important. Those people who attacked though - they are what we will have to deal with. They wanted the key, for Lucius.<br /> <br /> I do not know who Lucius is, other than the one who paid people to attack us to get the key. Perhaps a vampire.<br /> <br /> No, he was not a tainted one. These tainted ones and the mummy thing were just something to do while we wait for the river.<br /> <br /> That is what Wolfram said the bug man was, a mummy. I was looking forward to fighting him, even if he would just come back probably. Wolfram said he had many times before.<br /> <br /> You are right, volchonok, mummies are cowards. Turning into clouds of bugs... as if we did not have enough with the bees and the scorpions and the centipedes that came from the tainted ones.<br /> <br /> And skeletons, yes, but skeletons are not bugs. They were much easier to kill than the tainted ones. Claws and teeth worked well against both, but not all of our pack have claws and teeth.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, this means there will be no running, not until we leave the city and these tainted ones. Perhaps later, after the boat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s Plans</b><br /> <br /> 28th January 1926<br /> <br /> There has been a delay in leaving for Luxor. Unfortunately, we are not sipping wine waiting.<br /> <br /> Actually, when we got off the plane, moving through the airport, we were ambushed by Arabs looking for a \u201ckeystone\u201d Dana denied having. While we argued, I shut down four rifles. Sadly, there were eight of them, plus the speaker. However, when we attacked, Laszlo blocked the shots at Dana from the four I could not shut down, and the Werewolves made short work of them, while Laszlo and Wolfram shut down the leader. Sadly, he was hired almost anonymously, by a \u201cLucius\u201d in a semi-public place. Dana, for her part, denied having the keystone with her, but did not expect the ambush, we got a call out to Nathan, and he picked us and our luggage up.<br /> <br /> So we met at the hotel. Dana and Nathan still respect and appreciate each other, but their relationship is not as close as before. Apparently her secretive and tricksy ways had eroded the trust somewhat. Nathan apparently gave our ambushers the location we would be landing in, and when Dana challenged him over doing that he just mentioned Tunisia, which she seemed to accept as a totally valid reason to send them where we would be arriving. Still, he seemed pleased we were okay.<br /> <br /> Dana has a keystone she needs to pick up for getting into the Black Pharaoh\u2019s temple. She was evasive on how she got it, except that she just happened to have it when this mission started. I love Dana, truly, but I wish she would be more honest and less evasive.<br /> <br /> We shared a room that night, as we all paired off and went to rooms. We fell asleep before long, me all curled up against her. It was nice.<br /> <br /> So the next day after breakfast the team, plus Dana but without Nathan or Nicholette, set out to get the keystone. Dana was dressed like the local Arabs, with a keffiyeh as she called it, or headress, in shining white. I did notice her garb was like the men wore, not the women. Anyway, Dana had Marek and I come inside the ramshackle establishment, and she quickly made out like Marek was her man and I her daughter. The Arab inside seemed\u2026annoyed\u2026she returned with a man, and while he got in her grill, she pulled a pistol and he backed down. Dana said she paid, but flirted to get a lower rate, and he was hoping for a payoff never promised. While Marek held him at gunpoint, she went to the vault, opened it easily, and retrieved her keystone, ignoring the money and only pausing a moment to study an artifact inside also, but ultimately leaving it. The whole thing was surreal since only Dana spoke Arabic there.<br /> <br /> We headed out, and saw some nuns speaking Polish, which Laszlo went to speak to. He had come back and was telling us about slavers, monster hunters and animal hybrids when we heard shouting and gunfire in the business Dana had left her keystone in, so we went back there and found two hybrids of lions, snakes, falcons and the like. Dana noted they were bulletproof, and tried using her was without any luck. They were indeed very bulletproof but not clawproof or fireproof, and the werewolves and Wolfram made short work of them. Wound up burning a fair amount of the inside though, and the man we had spoken to was dead when we arrived. They ejected bees and scorpions when wounded, which was unpleasant. In the end, we burned out large areas of the room to wipe out the bugs. Of course, fire always helps.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> At that point the church was our only lead, and we went there, to find some of the polish nuns standing outside horrified. The church was full of the monsters, all sorts of combinations. These were bulletproof as the last, so Dana stayed outside, and the rest of us went in. The Werewolves leapt in savagely, and Wolfram pointed his supernatural gifts. Laszlo apparently could harm them\u2026if he channels his energy he gets from punishing, but it is strenuous for him. Despite their near invulnerability, they were torn apart. Marek was badly hurt for his part, though. All of them ejected all sorts of unpleasant things, bees, scorpions, centipedes that attacked en mass. I used a Dusk Court trick I leaned to bolster my allies resistance to poison, and my Elemental contract to immolate myself and rushed into the bugs. It was a deeply unpleasant battle, but we won.<br /> <br /> We got the location the church people had found the slavers, and fell back to the hotel. Wolfram used his healing ritual on Marek. We discussed it, and began to put a picture together. Dana had seen these monsters before in and around tombs, so they are likely drawn to artifacts. Perhaps the one in the business we stopped at drew some? But the slavers found one, the church back slaver fighters took it, and the monsters followed them to the church. These people had gone for help of some Vatican demon hunters, so some may still be pursuing the artifact. Whatever it is.<br /> <br /> We resolved to raid the slaver\u2019s headquarters, and to pick up the artifact from the building we visited earlier. The latter task was simple\u2026Dana seems to have a way with safes. The former was easier than I feared. The latter was also relatively easy, but still took some work.<br /> <br /> The site being used by the slavers was a ways out from downtown Alexandria. When we got there, a pair of undead were keeping watch, some sort of animated ones. They were visible as such only for the hollow holes visible on their face, the rest hidden under the keffiyeh or behind the scarf over their mouth. Wolfram saw used Boneyard and saw five more inside, two of which seemed to be keeping a hybrid trapped below. A cowled cloaked figure was inside rumming through books and maps, guarded by the undead, with a symbol of an Egyptian creature named Ammut around their neck.<br /> <br /> We decided to charge as it looked decidedly unfriendly. The undead fell rapidly under our attacks, bullet resistant as they may be. Moving in I fired at the cloaked undead thing, and collapsed into piles of vermin and fled in every direaction, leaving robes behind. These undead too fell rapidly, and when the hybrid, no longer trapped, came up the werewolves tore it to pieces.<br /> <br /> We are looking for clues here, now, but I haven\u2019t found anything and I suspect we won\u2019t be more successful than the undead creature was.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXI</i><br /> <br /> The monsters were Amkhata, from <b>Mummy the Curse</b>. The Undead were their risen minions Ninitu. They were sort of an experiment, honestly; how difficult would they be to the group. Answer was a mix; the Werewolves plowed right through them, Wolfram and Laszlo could only really hurt them by spending resources. Lizette could not really do anything save kill the bugs with fire. So the feedback I got was mixed. At least the Ninitu and the humans proved good punching bags for them.<br /> <br /> So this was mostly side plot. It should be resolved next time. But we also get back on track next time. It\u2019s a fancy party, and we meet Lady Brackenstall. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T02:12:07-07:00","id":1145139,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to go to Egypt, where our team prepares for an expedition. A chance party changes things. A stranger and an old face.<br /> <br /> An unfortunate factor is that those most involved in the plot did not do journals. Marek did a good job of covering though. Tatiana\u2019s part was more peripheral, so for her a flash forward.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 27 January 1926<br /> <br /> This evening we switched gears and did something more social than martial. After we got back to the hotel Nathan indicated that he knew where Emma was going to be this evening. He said that she was going to be at a fancy party in town and that it might be possible for us to crash said party. Most of us acquired or borrowed clothes to wear. Nathan leant me one of his suits while Lizette went shopping for material and made outfits for Laszlo and Alla. Tatiana decided that she didn\u2019t want to go. I don\u2019t blame her for that. Social situations are not my forte but I thought it would be good if I went anyway. I felt that since this is my pack I should be there to look out for them just in case.<br /> <br /> We all arrived at the party separately so it would be more inconspicuous. Dana made a straight line for Emma and they started talking. I stayed within earshot of those two just in case things went badly. Wolfram disappeared into the crowd fairly early on, as did Alla. Those two can look after themselves so I did not feel the need to go looking for them right away, so I stayed near Dana and monitored the situation. It seemed that after a fairly short time things started going badly. Emma said that she did not trust Dana and neither did Iris. Dana said that she just wanted access to the tomb. Emma said no, that Iris had found it so she gets to go in first. Dana reminded Emma that she had the keystone that could disable many of the traps that were inside the tomb, but Emma did not seem impressed at all. She was adamant that Iris and she go in by themselves. Dana also said that she has her w\u0101s, which is what made Emma bring up the fact that neither of them trust Dana since she can control Iris with it. There were also some comments made about a double-cross on Dana\u2019s part and Iris and Emma getting captured. Dana said that she got them out of that situation too, but I don\u2019t think Emma was convinced. Things were starting to seriously decline so I decided to intervene and so I went over and asked Dana if she\u2019d like to dance. I was being a gentleman about it so Dana responded in kind and accepted my offer. I think I managed a passable Charleston.<br /> <br /> About the time that Dana and I stopped dancing, Wolfram and Laszlo came back from another room. Wolfram explained that he\u2019d been approached by a gentleman who called himself Khofu. He claimed to be an Arisen, which I believe Wolfram translates to him being a mummy. An actual one this time, not some strange servitor made of bugs. Apparently Khofu noticed us fighting the chimera, which he called Amkhatas, and was happy that we were keeping people safe from them. He also saw it as a favor to him since those creatures may have come after him at some point while he was in the city. He also said that he knew that we traveled with Dana and offered his assistance when we travel upriver. It seems Khofu can manipulate the weather to work in our favor. Wolfram then asked him about vampires in the area, thinking back to a warning we\u2019d gotten earlier this trip, and Khofu said that there was a group of Kindred calling themselves the Bak\u2019ra. They are a sect of the Mekhet clan and they have an inordinate interest in the sun. They claim to worship Aten, the sun god, and want to make it so the sun shines even at night. This seems counterproductive to me since they are Kindred and will all be inconvenienced, if not killed, by this turn of events just as their enemies will. Khofu does not believe that they have the capabilities to do this.<br /> <br /> Khofu also warned Wolfram and Laszlo that if they see a servant of Ammut that they should be careful. This sounded an awful lot like the bug guy that we saw before, and they mentioned this to the Arisen. Khofu offered again to travel with us as far as Karnak and to make sure the that weather is favorable to us while we travel. Apparently, he can make it so the river cooperates with us and he will be ready to leave by noon tomorrow. Wolfram said that he needed to talk this over with the rest of the pack first before making any promises. Later, when we all discussed this Dana thought that it was a good idea since it would ensure that we get to the tomb quicker than we would otherwise. Speed is of the essence in this situation where multiple groups are all going for the same prize. We can\u2019t stop Iris and Emma from making their way to the tomb, but we can try and get there first. <br /> <br /> While Wolfram was having his conversation with Khofu and I was keeping an eye on Dana, Alla had an adventure of her own. She ran into Izzy of all people and the two of them made their way down a hallway. Izzy it seems was after something from the host of the party, another mage that she knew, and wanted to enlist Alla\u2019s help to get it. She got Alla to charm some mortal guards into leaving their post so they could walk unhindered. They found the other mage and Izzy persuaded, by use of fire, the other mage into giving her some books that she said the Mysterium wanted her to acquire. He didn\u2019t want to give them up at first but when Izzy threatened to burn the library he capitulated. Also during this exchange there was something about Izzy claiming that Alla was the Prince of Minsk, or something like that. I\u2019m not exactly sure what that was all about.<br /> <br /> After that they came back out into the main room and we all talked. We agreed that having Khofu accompany us as far as Karnak would be advantageous to us and Wolfram made arrangements with the other man to meet him on the dock tomorrow at noon. Also during this meeting Alla asked the rest of the pack if we would mind if Izzy came with us on our trip into the desert. The rest of us didn\u2019t see a problem with that and Nathan offered to acquire extra supplies for her. Alla then invited her friend who said that she wanted to talk to us about details about the trip before she decided one way or the other. She said that she would meet us at the hotel later and we agreed. Izzy met us later and explained that the police had been called to remove her from the party because she had been investigating the kitchens looking for cannibals. I\u2019m not sure what it is with her and cannibals. It seems that she made quite the scene and she was forced to sneak out. The police were watching her hotel room and couldn\u2019t get her stuff out without getting arrested. So, she enlisted our help. Alla and Nicolette distracted the officers by telling them that they had been mugged. Alla is quite the actress, as is Nicolette. While the police were dealing with the ladies I snuck in and retrieved Izzy\u2019s belongings.<br /> <br /> I guess given her current predicament Izzy cannot stay in Alexandria so she agreed to come along with us on our trip into the desert. She didn\u2019t complain or anything and just said that she\u2019d be ready to travel by noon tomorrow. I am unsure about having Izzy along on the trip, though I do have to admit that having a talented mage along for the trip might make things easier\u2026 and more interesting. If she can conjure fire then she might be useful in a fight.<br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 27 January 1926<br /> <br /> While the rest of us were packing up this morning Lizette and Laszlo went out to reenergize themselves. To that end Lizette animated a vehicle and made it drive around the street and sidewalks scaring the daylights out of pedestrians. She gathers her energy from the fear of mortals, so this seemed a good way to go about doing it. It was a bit flashy, but effective. Laszlo was also able to gain what he needed from the spectacle. When he came back he seemed more \u201chuman\u201d than I\u2019ve ever seen him. Apparently, I\u2019ve always seen him closer to his beast than his humanity. It was an interesting change. <br /> <br /> While they were out Dana approached me, and asked to speak privately. So, we stepped aside and talked. She said that she was concerned about Nicolette. She does not trust the other woman because she has been so close to Iris in the past. She thought Nicolette might be spying for her old employer. I was not sure what to make of this. She could just be suspicious because she has a rivalry with Iris, or there might be some legitimate concern about Nicolette\u2019s intentions. She also said that she was suspicious of Izzy. It was coincidence that the elder mage was at the same party that we were and that Alla asked her to come along. The world is a big place. Dana seemed convinced that mages work by coincidence and that it could be more orchestrated than accidental. She also said repeatedly that she did not want to sow discord among the group. She said that she was honestly worried about those two ladies and their intentions and didn\u2019t trust them. She did admit during this whole conversation that she was good at the \u201cconfidence game.\u201d I was aware of this. I agreed that I didn\u2019t trust Nicolette, and Dana pointed out that we keep leaving the writer alone at our house or at the hotel. She could be doing anything while we\u2019re not looking. But she didn\u2019t want to sow discord. She repeated that. I\u2019m not sure what to make of Dana\u2019s warning. I don\u2019t think she trusts a lot of people all told. She might be being honest about her concerns regarding Nicolette and Izzy. Or she could be planting seeds for suspicion while saying that she isn\u2019t. <br /> <br /> Also, this morning Dana offered to help anyone that needed to acquire native clothes so that we could pass easier while in the desert. Native clothes are also better designed for dealing with the sand and heat it seems. So, Laszlo and I took her up on her offer and she went off in search of clothes for us. Khofu met us at the boat after we\u2019d acquired last minute supplies and we took little time in getting ready and underway. The boat that Nathan got for us is fairly large and comfortably accommodated all of us if we split into pairs.<br /> <br /> While we traveled we discussed a number of things. One of which was the fact that instead of camels we are using wallys to get us through the desert. Lizette said that she can keep them running despite the sand, so we agreed to go with the vehicles instead of the animals. I think that the workers we have arranged to hire will be using camels to travel across the desert. I believe that we will have ten men coming with us to dig and help carry stuff. I guess our only real concern is that we have enough fuel packed in our gear to get the wallys to and from the site, lest we find ourselves walking back to Karnak.<br /> <br /> Tatiana also asked a really good question. How is the hunting in the desert? Nathan said that it is slim, but there are smaller animals out there that are available to hunt. I believe that this will suit our needs, though we may be a bit on the hungry side depending on how big the animals are and how many we can catch. I do not doubt our ability to hunt, but this will be a new environment for both of us. Should make things interesting.<br /> <br /> During this conversation Dana also covered some tips about desert safety. None of us have traveled in the desert before and do not know what to expect, so Dana took it upon herself to inform us of what we should expect once we get into the desert proper. She was pretty detailed in her description and it reinforced the fact that we do in fact have a capable guide taking us to this archaeological site. I find myself looking forward to this expedition.<br /> <br /> I guess time will tell what Dana\u2019s plan is as far as Nicolette and Izzy. She says that she doesn\u2019t trust them but she has not forbidden us from taking them either. I suppose it\u2019s not really her place to tell us who we can and cannot take on this trip. We are not getting paid for this whole thing. We are doing it out of the kindness in our hearts, and because she is a friend. I suppose I should at least warn Wolfram about her concerns with Nicolette at least. I know that Lizette would not look kindly on that discussion so I will have to make sure to do it out of her earshot. I should also include Tatiana. She may be indifferent towards the writer, but she is still this pack\u2019s best defender. It would be remiss of me to leave her out of plans that may affect the safety of our pack. I\u2019m not sure whether or not I should include Alla. I know that she would not look kindly on Dana\u2019s warnings about Izzy, but she might be good to tell about concerns about Nicolette. It\u2019s just hard to decide who amongst my pack I should share these concerns with. I am not as good at reading people as I should be. I know it is a product of my general indifference when it comes to outsiders, but sometimes I feel like I should be able to rise above that. It would be advantageous to know someone\u2019s intentions by body language or how they say things. It is just something that I will have to work on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> \u201cCamels\u201d<br /> <br /> Flash forward.<br /> <br /> Walking towards the table, Sasha looked over at Tatiana moving around the kitchen in her flowing light colored clothes and strange head wrapping, a curious look in his eyes. Pyotr, ever the more impetuous one, asked, as soon as he got in the room, \u201cWhy are you wearing those weird clothes, Tanya?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI just got back from the desert, nosy one, everyone there dresses like this.\u201d Tatiana tapped him on the nose.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy?\u201d He made a face. \u201cWouldn\u2019t the fluttery bits get caught on things?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana smirked. \u201cNot if you are good. All the desert dwellers dress like this - the better to deal with the dangers all around them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The boys recognized her storytelling voice and the moved over hurriedly, their attention fully on their aunt. \u201cWhat kind of dangers?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, all kinds. Sun that will cook you in your skin. A dry wind that can strip flesh from bone.\u201d She pulled the head wrap over her mouth, making noises like a blowing wind. \u201cPoisonous bugs as big as your spread hand. Lubmering beasts the size of houses. Lizards who could gobble you up in one bite.\u201d Sasha squirmed as Tatiana tickled him.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you fight them?\u201d Pyotr grinned up at her.<br /> <br /> She struck a heroic pose. \u201cOf course! Also, monsters.\u201d She waggled her eyebrows. \u201cBulls with falcon heads. Snakes with wings and dog heads. Scorpions flowed from their wounds like blood and they vomited bees.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBees?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBees.\u201d Tatiana nodded seriously. \u201cBut even those aren\u2019t the worst.\u201d<br /> <br /> The boys looked at each other, then back at her. Sasha spoke up. \u201cWhat was the worst?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatiana\u2019s face was grave. \u201cThese creatures are taller than me - taller than I can raise my hands. Their hair is coarse and shaggy, their bodies lumpy and thick. They can drink a lake of water in a minute, and then not drink for years. Their teeth leave scars, and they spit vile globs that gum up everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are they called?\u201d Pyotr asked eagerly. Sasha, behind him, had a growing realization on his face.<br /> <br /> \u201cCamels.\u201d Tatiana\u2019s straight face held until Sasha began cracking up.<br /> <br /> After a minute or so, Pyotr looked at his brother and aunt, still laughing, with his hands on his hips. \u201cWhat? ...what?!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lizette\u2019s plans</b><br /> <br /> 29th January 1926<br /> <br /> Just a short entry this time. We are soon to arrive at Karnack.<br /> <br /> Last night, Nathan had tracked down Lady Emma Brackenstall to a social taking place in town, and the group, minus Tatiana and Nicholette, went. The evening was less successful than we hoped. Dana talked to Lady Brackenstall for a while, but they seemed only to argue. I kept a respectful distance, as Dana had suggested Lady Brackenstall might be jealous. Apparently they were unable to come to an agreement. When things seemed to be getting hostile, Marek interrupted to dance with Dana, which galling as that was I think was a good move.<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Laszlo had slipped out with a very tall African fellow, and Alla had followed Izzy off behind closed doors, to neck I presumed but apparently Izzy was taking some books from inside the house. Necking and stealing? Mayhem? Anyway, she set about searching for cannibals, her hobby, while Wolfram came to discuss what he had found.<br /> <br /> Apparently the man, Khofu, was a Mummy, which I figured were a thing. An Arisen he called himself. He was pleased about us killing the hybrids, which he called Amkhata. He offered to keep conditions favorable for us if we went down with him as bodyguards to protect him against whatever was in the slavers headquarters. He would only travel as far as our paths mutually took us. It seemed a good deal.<br /> <br /> I was in dire need of Galmour from yesterday, so went out in the morning. An animated car later, Laszlo, who was with me, and I were well re-energized.<br /> <br /> We all, Khofu included, met the boat. We hope to arrive in Karnack tonight. Dana had a long talk with Marek while I readied all the equipment we had. There was a lot of talk of cars vs. camels, and frankly, I cannot wonder if our best bet is mechanical camels. If we can access the tomb, who knows, robot camels could be our future.<br /> <br /> With a Vickers attached.<br /> <br /> And a flamethrower.<br /> <br /> Mayhem!<br /> <br /> Anyway, time to repack up. There is adventure to be had!<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXII</i><br /> <br /> Izzy got Alla to help recover books for the Mysterium, which she was a member of. She also demonstrated considerable power over forces.<br /> <br /> There was a long conversation between Dana and Nathan about Dana, when trapped at gunpoint, claiming to be pregnant and taking her sweet time telling Nathan it was a ruse. She claimed she presumed he knew, but apparently did not tell him till he asked weeks later.<br /> <br /> Other thing was Nathan and Laszlo wound up sleeping together.<br /> <br /> I think that covers it, comments and questions welcome<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T03:47:40-07:00","id":1145154,"title":"","content":"So, as it stands, the group contains:<br /> 1 Vampire<br /> 2 Werewolves<br /> 1 Mage<br /> 1Changeling<br /> 1 Sin-Eater<br /> 1 Mummy<br /> 1 Beast<br /> And an immortal<br /> (They may also have an Angel or Demon in their group somewhere as well - hard to tell with those types)<br /> And in partial opposition to 1 Demon.<br /> <br /> All you need to do is throw in a Promethean somewhere, and you'll have all the lines covered at once (Hunters are just violent humans in this analysis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T16:21:58-07:00","id":1145383,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you <i>did </i>want to include Hunter (again - the Berlin plot-line has the Lucifuge), you simple must go with the Faithful of Shulpae. Because it both ties into the newly added (albeit temporary) Mummy, but also Izzy obsession with &quot;cannibals&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T13:33:36-07:00","id":1145883,"title":"","content":"I'll look into it, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, I will be out of state and away from computer in 2 weeks, so no update for four weeks. I should still be able to check here of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T18:14:16-08:00","id":1172465,"title":"","content":"This is long delayed, but here are the most recent Golden Eagle Journals. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Marek\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> 28 January 1926<br /> <br /> We arrived in Karnak. While Dana, Tatiana and I went to town to get the lay of the land Nathan worked on getting transportation for the party. He got a couple of wallys and camels for the workers that he hired. We hired locals since none of us have a problem with non-Christians and they are actually cheaper to hire. We also figured that they might know more about the land than outsiders would. It seemed a good idea. In any case the three of us went in to town to see what was going on and found ourselves somewhat surprised. We all noticed the sheer number of soldiers in uniform and carrying rifles. There did not seem to be any police officers around, just soldiers. Dana confirmed for us that this was odd. Tatiana also asked around and found out about the local Uratha situation, which turns out to be not much of anything. There are very few Uratha in the area due to the climate and scarcity of resources. She did note that Cairo is once more in Uratha hands after being held by the Pure for one thousand years. While interesting it doesn\u2019t have much influence on our current activities. At least not yet. We headed back to where the others were and Dana overheard some locals saying something about raiders being seen in the area. I guess we will have to keep a weather eye out.<br /> <br /> When we got back we told the others what we had found out. Dana explained to the rest of us how it normally works here. In Egypt, or at least this part of Egypt, a group of soldiers can take over an area and if the actual Army doesn\u2019t kick them out then they lay claim to whatever land they are inhabiting. It\u2019s like some sort of tacit agreement on the part of the Army for the mercenaries to take over whatever town or land they want. It doesn\u2019t seem like a good idea to me, but if the Army is not strong enough to push out all would-be invaders it might be the only way that they can handle things. Fighting them would be costly if they don\u2019t have the resources to back up those fighting.<br /> <br /> Karnak is also where we said our goodbyes to Khafu. He said that some of his enemies may be active in the area so we might see him in the near future. He didn\u2019t know for sure. We wished him well and he went on his way, and we went on ours. We loaded up the wallys and camels with all the equipment, as well as Alla\u2019s crate. It\u2019s not the most dignified way to travel, but when you\u2019re a Kindred in Egypt then you have to do what you have to do. We hadn\u2019t gotten very far when we came across a checkpoint of sorts manned by men in uniform. They were not regular Army, but they were soldiers. They told us that we could not pass because of Ethiopian bandits in the area. They repeated this several times to Dana and Nathan who had gone up to talk to the guards. Nicolette translated for the rest of us. It seemed that the soldiers thought that we were trouble, and in Arabic apparently that word can translate to mean danger or threat. Negotiations were breaking down and the guards stopped talking to Dana altogether. They weren\u2019t even accepting the customary bribe, which in and of itself was odd. They really didn\u2019t want us to pass. They were hiding something. Tatiana decided that enough was enough and went forward to bring back Nathan and Dana. We all got back into the vehicles and drove around the checkpoint regardless of what the guards said. They didn\u2019t stop us, which was interesting. I was expecting them to try something. My guess is that they would send a runner ahead to warn their compatriots that we were coming. I was proven right a few moments later. A solider took off across the desert on camel so we drove slowly, and after we were out of line of sight Tatiana jumped off the vehicle and changed shape and chased after the messenger.<br /> <br /> Tatiana chased after the soldier into the desert quietly. It looked like he was on his way to an old fort. It was currently manned by several armed soldiers and there was a wally parked outside alongside some camels. She transformed into Urshal form and knocked the poor man off his camel in one blow. She then threatened him with gestures since they did not share a spoken language. She told him not to go to the fort or she would kill him. She also told him to go running back to his friends at the checkpoint. Apparently she was rather effective at communicating with the man and he took off as fast as his legs would carry him. She watched him run for a bit before she transformed back to wolf form and headed back to meet up with the rest of us. We agreed that the fort would warrant a look at some point.<br /> <br /> We eventually arrived at an old town that had been abandoned some time ago and repurposed recently by archaeologists as a staging point for their digs. The dig that we were looking for, to find Kruger, was nearby. After we set up our tents Nathan got out his maps so Tatiana could mark the location of the fort on it. Turns out that the fort was already marked on the map. Dana also mentioned, when she got back from talking to Kruger, that if there was another mummy in the area it would probably be at that fort. I had a feeling that we hadn\u2019t heard the last of that place. I expected trouble. It would seem likely to come at some point if the checkpoint guard had been heading straight for that place. It stands to reason they would eventually get up the guts to send another guy to the fort to warn them that we had passed them and traveled into the desert. With that in mind I dozed while we drove and planned to stay up tonight and stand guard. When I mentioned my intentions to the pack Wolfram agreed that it was a good idea and said that he would join me. Four eyes are better than two, and even more so when two of those eyes belong to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> **** **** ****<br /> <br /> 29 January 1926<br /> <br /> So far today has been fairly exciting. Once everyone was up Dana introduced us to Kruger who she\u2019d talked to last night. We told him about the checkpoint that we\u2019d encountered yesterday and he admitted that he been seeing soldiers in the area lately. Some of them he thought had suspicious blood stains on their clothes. He said that he wasn\u2019t sure if they were real soldiers, as in real Army, or just mercenaries. They had not been bothering him or his workers, so there\u2019s that. Dana suggested that one of us go with Kruger\u2019s workers to get supplied and see if the soldiers try and stop them or not. Or see how they react to the workers rather than a large group of foreigners traveling by wally. Dana also asked Kruger about Kindred activity in the area. He confirmed that the Bak\u2019ra are active in the nearby regions, but didn\u2019t have much more information than that. It basically just confirmed what we already knew.<br /> <br /> Once Kruger took a break to get water Dana asked if any of us could get a bird\u2019s eye view of the area so we could see the soldier\u2019s activities as well as anything else that is going on around here. Wolfram admitted that he could do it but would need to be away from the workers when he tried. See, he would have to immolate himself in order to activate his gift. Things like that remind me how glad I am that Uratha gifts are so much more straightforward than Claimed gifts. I would not want to have to set myself alight to use a gift. It apparently doesn\u2019t really hurt Wolfram to use this gift, which is good. I would not like it if my packmate ended up seriously hurting himself just for some reconnaissance.<br /> <br /> As a side note, the sun here is very hot. Of course it\u2019s hot, it\u2019s the desert, but it seems a lot hotter than summers at home. It\u2019s also very dry here and very bright. The sun seems to just reflect off the sand and it takes some getting used to. I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s the heat or the climate, but it just seems to sap the strength right out of you. It\u2019s not a pleasant feeling. It could also be that I stayed up all night, but I\u2019ve done that plenty of times so I prefer to think that it\u2019s the sun causing the problems. Lizette has also been similarly affected. She went so far as to build herself a backpack with a fan on it to blow cooler air down on her. It seems to work rather well, and makes more sense than just continuously fanning herself with something. Doing that just uses more energy and works to make you hotter in the long run. It should just be a matter of acclimating to the dry heat though, so hopefully we\u2019ll get over this discomfort soon.<br /> <br /> Shortly after our talk with Kruger some of the workers came over to talk to Dana and said that there were ghostly jackals at the dig site that was nearby. We all gathered up any weapons we wanted and headed for the dig site. Sure enough, when we arrived there were five ghostly jackals wandering around the area. They seemed to just be watching the workers there but became a little more interested when we arrived. We immediately determined that they were not ghosts or spirts, they were mortal creatures that just happened to be supernatural in appearance. They also seemed to be reflecting sunlight, which made them hard to look at for too long. Wolfram called them cryptids. Tatiana then howled, like a human pretending to be a wolf, to get Dana\u2019s attention. Said woman arrived shortly after that and the jackals immediately became interested in her. Our theory is that they were drawn to technology like we\u2019ve encountered in the past\u2026 specifically the items that are said to be connected to the Black Pharaoh. Presumably Dana had the w\u0101s in her possession and they all looked in her direction.<br /> <br /> Dana told the workers to leave and they all did. She then tried to use the w\u0101s on the jackals, to no effect. Soon after that the jackals all started heading for us, Dana in particular. We moved to stand in front of her, preparing ourselves as we did so. The ensuing fight was quick. One of the jackals tried to attack Dana, but it didn\u2019t succeed. Tatiana taught one a lesson, hurting it badly. I attacked one with my claws. It was not happy with me after that. One of them, presumably in defense of his friend, flashed a bright light in my eyes blinding me. I had to smile at that. I may not have been able to see them but my other senses took up the slack rather well and I had no problems finding my target after that. Lizette shot one with her tommy gun and Wolfram finished it off with his sword. Laszlo killed the one that I had been fighting and I took out another one that had had been injured by someone. There are plenty of details that I am missing since I was paying attention to the things in my own field of perception. Tatiana killed another one in short order and Lizette opened up with that gun of hers at the remaining one. We thought that we were done with the jackals when all of a sudden another one seemed to appear out of nowhere. It headed for Dana\u2019s w\u0101s, and grabbed it. Tatiana killed it before it could get away, and I finished off the last of the original group. We discovered after the fight was over that the jackals had come up out of the sand. They had been hiding under there and that\u2019s why the last one seemed to materialize out of thin air.<br /> <br /> After the fight, but before the workers came back, Tatiana and I each stuffed one of the jackals in a sack and brought them back to our tents. We figured that they would make for a good source of meat. Food that will do something for us is going to be hard enough to come by in the desert as it is, so I didn\u2019t see a reason to let the meat go to waste. Soon after that we all packed up our gear. We had discussed our options and felt that leaving sooner would keep Kruger and his men from any future harm. These kinds of creatures are likely to continue showing up as we travel, so there\u2019s no need to put the men in danger for no reason. At least that\u2019s how it was presented to me. I agreed that it would be a waste if the men were killed, but didn\u2019t phrase it like that when talking to the pack. I know enough to know how to phrase certain things. I don\u2019t particularly care about the workers. They are not pack, but I can acknowledge that they serve a purpose and it would be a waste of resources if they were killed when we could prevent it.<br /> <br /> Our next step is to have Wolfram use his gift to travel as a spirit would so he can get the lay of the land. We will need to do this out of the sight of Kruger and his men. I will leave this for now and record more later, after I have something to report. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tatiana\u2019s Conversations</b><br /> <br /> Volchonok, leave off pawing at that. It is fine.<br /> <br /> It was just a beast, supernatural or no. See, here in the tent it is merely white, not shining, and slightly larger than a usual jackal. It is good meat.<br /> <br /> It is good! I was worried it would be metal, since Wolfram said it was something to do with Dana\u2019s was, or the Golden Eagle. But it is meat, and nothing smells wrong with it.<br /> <br /> Yes, Dana\u2019s was. Her magic stick. They attacked when they saw it, and tried to steal it, so it was probably that. Or else they just smelled all of the strange technology on all of us and just attacked when they smelled it directly. They didn\u2019t attack any of the workers, anyway.<br /> <br /> You must not have been paying attention, volchonok. I am pretty sure the archeologist man would have mated with Dana no matter what she did, if she wanted to. But he would have been upset had his workers been killed because of us. Probably.<br /> <br /> We are not here for his workers, or for Dana to mate with him. He was supposed to know about vampires.<br /> <br /> He knew what Khofu had already said. Well, I suppose the archeologist did know for sure they were working around here, not just that they are around sometimes.<br /> <br /> Oh, the vampires will probably be fun to fight. But yes, the jackals were a good fight. I think the pack did well, though we shall have to keep in mind that they can burrow, should we see them again.<br /> <br /> I do not think we can teach Laszlo to smell better, volchonok, though it would have helped after he got blinded. He did well before that though.<br /> <br /> Back on that again? Nicolette did not think the meat was bad. She is just a foolish human who doesn\u2019t like to see people eating meat properly.<br /> <br /> Remember? They burn it first. And then use forks.<br /> <br /> I am not explaining forks again, volchonok.<br /> <br /> She did back out very quickly, it is true. Maybe she will stop trying to mate with me. Maybe when we hunt I shall save some for eating just before bed.<br /> <br /> Bah. She is a pale shadow of a nursemaid. Wearing that pink nightgown was the most interesting thing she has done since showing up and remembering that we turned into wolves once. Besides, Marek doesn\u2019t trust her.<br /> <br /> Probably because she showed up and remembered that we turned into wolves once in her sight. Or because she is compelled to write.<br /> <br /> Also, everyone she mates with dies or has something horrible happen.<br /> <br /> Yes, volchonok, I will come back, but I do not think mating with her will be worth going through that again.<br /> <br /> Usually you are happy when I will not mate with a human.<br /> <br /> Do not go changing the subject...<br /> <br /> Oh that. It is alright volchonok. Wolfram is doing it on purpose, so he can become like a spirit and fly to check on the fort, the Mountain of the Hawk.<br /> <br /> The one from last night? We were stopped by soldiers, and then we went on a run?<br /> <br /> I know you enjoyed the run, you silly headed volchonok. I ran so that I could stop the soldier from reporting us.<br /> <br /> Yes, the one who I scared into smelling bad.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t make sounds at him because he would not understand my sounds.<br /> <br /> Oh, he understood my hands.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t? Well, you are just a foolish volchonok...<br /> <br /> OK, OK, I will tell you. I told him if he went to the fort, I would kill him. And that I would watch him, and if he came back to the fort later, or anyone else did, I would kill them.<br /> <br /> Yes, all that, just with my hands.<br /> <br /> I do not know how to say let\u2019s go for a run with my hands. And we can\u2019t, not right now. Now we must pack up, and continue towards the temple. If you want, you can run alongside...<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXIII<br /> </i><br /> About two years ago, when The Golden Eagle began, we were looking at a lot of things. A lot at a different, swinging era, but also an era where women had unprecedented rights, queer people were around and more open than ever. Sewing circles, unground gay clubs. An era when PoC\u2019s had\u2026okay, it still blew for them but better than before. Then the rise of the far right, fascism, Nazism. It would bury all this for many years, until the 90s at earliest. It was a paean to that time even as we had a Nazi fighting good time. Two years ago this was easy for us, a majority female majority queer group to do.<br /> <br /> 2017 came to be a different time. White power, Nazi salutes in the streets. In my own country. I\u2019m scared. Many of us are scared. Wolfram\u2019s player noted he was playing a man watching his country go mad, now he is a man watching his country go mad. Working on the game has become very stressful for me, and there is something of an air for some of us over it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this makes it hard to run as the spectre of fascism covers Europe when we worry about it at home away from the table. This has substantially decreased the overall fun of the game. I had a highly stressful October, and the game never quite restarted. Unfortunately as of the end of the year we had to call it. . No drama contributed, in fact the same group is starting a new game soon. I apologize. This game had potential, and if real world politics had not become so horrifying, maybe it would have continued. But as is, it only adds to my and some other player\u2019s stress.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed it, folks. Sorry for the sudden end. We could do no different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a>